1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:01,668
欢迎来到本课程。
Welcome to the course.

2
00:00:02,029 --> 00:00:07,760
这是 Claude Certified Architect – Foundations 的考试，考试代码为 CCAR-F。
This is the Claude Certified Architect Foundation's exam exam code CCAR-F.

3
00:00:08,173 --> 00:00:19,044
这是 Anthropic 的首个技术认证，而且非常独特。在接下来的 10 个小时左右，我们将按照实际考查比例，涵盖所有测试内容。
Anthropex first technical certification and a genuinely unusual one. Over the next 10 hours or so, we will work through everything it tests in the proportions it actually tests them.

4
00:00:20,046 --> 00:00:25,412
包含 25 个视频、20 个教学模块和 4 套完整的模拟考试。
25 videos, 20 teaching modules, and 4 full practice exams.

5
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:30,820
在开始之前，花几分钟讲一下这门课程是如何构建的以及如何使用它。
Before we start, a few minutes on how this course was built and how to use it.

6
00:00:31,438 --> 00:00:33,892
这两点决定了你能从中学到什么。
Both of those change what you get out of it.

7
00:00:35,566 --> 00:00:43,268
我们分析了一个包含 134 道练习题的题库，以确定考试测试哪些决策以及出现的频率。
A bank of 134 practice questions was analyzed to work out which decisions this exam tests and how often.

8
00:00:43,822 --> 00:00:47,012
这项分析决定了本课程的时间分配。
That analysis decided where the time goes in this course.

9
00:00:47,726 --> 00:00:50,500
但是，那个题库里的任何题目都不会出现在这里。
But not one question from that bank appears here.

10
00:00:51,086 --> 00:00:59,172
你将看到的每一个场景都是从零开始编写的，并且所有的解释都源自当前的 Anthropic 官方文档。
Every scenario you will see was written from scratch, and every explanation is sourced from current anthropic documentation.

11
00:00:59,982 --> 00:01:01,828
这样做有一个实际的原因。
There is a practical reason for that.

12
00:01:02,574 --> 00:01:06,116
记住一道泄露的题目只能让你学会那道题。
Memorizing a leaked question teaches you that question.

13
00:01:07,118 --> 00:01:12,036
理解其背后的决策逻辑，才能让你掌握那些你从未见过的 50 道题。
Understanding the decision underneath it teaches you the 50 you have never seen.

14
00:01:13,646 --> 00:01:15,172
这是考试的结构。
Here is the shape of the exam.

15
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:18,480
60 道题，120 分钟。
60 questions, 120 minutes.

16
00:01:18,766 --> 00:01:23,040
也就是每题 2 分钟，而且由于题目很长，时间会比听起来更紧迫。
That is 2 minutes each, and it is tighter than it sounds because the questions are long.

17
00:01:23,278 --> 00:01:30,212
大多数题目是单选题，但有些是多选题，且每道题都会说明需要选择几个。
Most items are multiple choice with one right answer, but some are multiple response, and each one states how many to pick.

18
00:01:30,990 --> 00:01:34,980
评分按比例缩放至 1000 分，达到 720 分即可通过。
Scoring is scaled out of 1000 and you pass at 720.

19
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:40,804
通过 Pearson VUE 进行考试，可以选择在线监考或前往测试中心。
Deliveries through Pearson VUE, either online with a proctor or at a test center.

20
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:47,840
目前仅限 Cloud Partner Network 组织的人员参加，需要提供工作邮箱地址。
Access is currently limited to people at organizations in the Cloud Partner Network, which needs a work email address.

21
00:01:48,398 --> 00:01:50,436
该证书有效期为 12 个月。
The credential lasts 12 months.

22
00:01:50,990 --> 00:01:59,076
在预约前请自行确认费用和准入规则，因为这些内容自录制以来最有可能发生变化。
Check the fee and the access rules yourself before booking, because those are the parts most likely to have changed since this was recorded.

23
00:02:00,654 --> 00:02:02,948
关于谁适合参加这个考试。
A word on who this exam suits.

24
00:02:03,470 --> 00:02:11,460
Anthropic 建议拥有大约 6 个月使用 Claude API、agent SDK、Claude Code 和 MCP 进行实操开发的经验。
Anthropic recommends about 6 months of hands-on building with the Claude API, the agent SDK, Claude Code and MCP.

25
00:02:12,110 --> 00:02:15,044
这说法比较模糊，所以这里给出具体的含义。
That is vague, so here is what it means concretely.

26
00:02:15,694 --> 00:02:20,036
你已经从头到尾构建过一个包含真实工具调用和真实故障的智能体。
You have built an agent end-to-end with real tool calls and real failures.

27
00:02:20,942 --> 00:02:24,996
你必须解决如何停止循环以及如何恢复会话的问题。
You had to work out how to stop the loop and how to resume a session.

28
00:02:25,646 --> 00:02:29,796
你为其他人员共同参与的项目配置过 Claude Code。
You have configured Claude code for a project that other people also work on.

29
00:02:30,382 --> 00:02:34,564
你曾因为 Claude 一直选择错误的工具而重写过工具描述。
You have rewritten a tool description because Claude kept choosing the wrong tool.

30
00:02:35,054 --> 00:02:41,028
你构建过从文档中提取结构化数据的东西，并目睹过它虚构字段的情况。
You have built something that pulls structured data out of documents and watched it invent a field.

31
00:02:41,326 --> 00:02:44,400
如果你已经掌握了大部分内容，这门课程将填补你的知识空白。
If you have most of that, this course fills the gaps.

32
00:02:44,686 --> 00:02:49,892
如果你完全没基础，也要看这门课，但同时要动手做一个小项目。
If you have none of it, watch the course anyway, but build something small alongside it.

33
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:55,556
这次考试的干扰项是由实战经验丰富的专家编写的，这在题目中体现得很明显。
The distractors on this exam are written by people who have debugged these systems and it shows

34
00:02:57,006 --> 00:02:59,332
共有 5 个领域，它们的权重并不相等。
5 domains and they are not equal.

35
00:03:00,014 --> 00:03:05,412
智能体架构与编排占 27%，大约是 16 道题。
Agentic architecture and orchestration is 27%, which is roughly 16 questions.

36
00:03:06,286 --> 00:03:09,520
工具设计和模型上下文协议占 18%。
Tool design and the model context protocol is 18%.

37
00:03:10,670 --> 00:03:14,800
Claude 代码配置和提示工程各占 20%。
Lord code configuration and prompt engineering are 20% each.

38
00:03:15,342 --> 00:03:18,480
上下文管理和可靠性占 15%。
Context management and reliability is 15%.

39
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:27,300
右侧列将这些权重转换成了题目数量，因为百分比容易理解，但题数更直观。
The right-hand column converts those weights into question counts because percentages are easy to nod at and question counts are not.

40
00:03:28,142 --> 00:03:34,916
很多人没通过考试最常见的原因是：提示工程很强，就以为其他部分也能拿高分。
The most common way people fail this exam is being strong in prompt engineering and assuming that carries the rest.

41
00:03:35,406 --> 00:03:36,804
但这只占整份试卷的五分之一。
It is a fifth of the paper.

42
00:03:37,934 --> 00:03:44,324
本课程按这些比例分配时间。所以如果你按顺序学习，你就在按照考试大纲来复习。
This course allocates time in these proportions. So if you follow it in order, you are already studying to the blueprint.

43
00:03:45,966 --> 00:03:48,868
考试不会考孤立的问题。
The exam does not ask isolated questions.

44
00:03:49,390 --> 00:03:54,148
它会把你扔进一个生产环境场景，并围绕它提出一系列问题。
It drops you into a production situation and asks a series of questions about it.

45
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:59,748
题库里有 6 个这样的场景，其中 4 个是随机抽取的。
There are six of these scenarios in the pool, and you are given four chosen at random.

46
00:04:00,110 --> 00:04:03,428
一个处理退货和账单纠纷的客户支持智能体。
A customer support agent handling returns and billing disputes.

47
00:04:04,238 --> 00:04:07,172
一个团队使用 Claude Code 进行日常开发。
A team using QARD code for everyday development.

48
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:12,228
一个包含协调者和专门子智能体的多智能体研究系统。
A multi-agent research system with a coordinator and specialized subagents.

49
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:16,000
用于探索陌生代码库的开发者工具。
Developer tools for exploring unfamiliar code bases.

50
00:04:20,430 --> 00:04:25,188
以及从杂乱文档中提取干净数据的结构化提取系统。
And a structured extraction system pulling clean data out of messy documents.

51
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:29,280
你无法预知会考到哪四个，所以这门课程涵盖了全部六个场景。
You cannot guess which four you will get, so this course covers all six.

52
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:33,700
你会注意到每个场景都会在不同模块中以不同的角度反复出现。
You will notice each one recurring across modules from a different angle each time.

53
00:04:35,182 --> 00:04:39,012
这是在你开始学习前最需要知道的一件事。
Here is the single most useful thing to know before you start studying.

54
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:50,724
考试中几乎没有任何题目会问某个功能是什么。问题通常以「生产日志显示」、「调查发现」或「在测试过程中你注意到」等短语开头。
Almost nothing on this exam asks what a feature is. The questions open with phrases like production logs show or investigation reveals or during testing you notice.

55
00:04:51,374 --> 00:04:57,604
你会拿到一个故障系统和一个症状，然后被要求找出原因或者修复方法。
You are handed a broken system and a symptom and asked either what caused it or what fixes it.

56
00:04:58,190 --> 00:05:00,068
这改变了你的复习策略。
That changes how you should study.

57
00:05:00,942 --> 00:05:03,460
仅仅知道钩子存在对你没啥帮助。
Learning that hooks exist will not help you.

58
00:05:04,430 --> 00:05:05,988
以下这些内容才会对你有帮助。
Here is what will help you.

59
00:05:06,862 --> 00:05:13,508
尽管有明确指令，但仍有 3% 的情况违反规则，这是强制执行层级设置错误的一个症状。
A rule violated 3% of the time despite clear instructions is a symptom of enforcement sitting in the wrong layer.

60
00:05:14,318 --> 00:05:19,364
所以这门课程贯穿始终的逻辑是「从症状到原因」，而不是「从功能到定义」。
So this course pitches symptom to cause throughout, not feature to definition.

61
00:05:21,166 --> 00:05:28,900
第二点要了解的是，在大多数题目中，四个选项里其实有两个或三个都是可行的。
The second thing to know is that on most questions, two or three of the four options would actually work.

62
00:05:29,870 --> 00:05:32,868
区分它们的关键在于题干中的限定词。
What separates them is a qualifier in the question stem.

63
00:05:33,870 --> 00:05:41,892
如果题目提到“保证”或“防篡改”，或者“无论智能体如何提示”，那么答案就在代码或配置中。
If the question says guarantee or tamper proof, or regardless of how the agent is prompted, then the answer lives in code or configuration.

64
00:05:42,414 --> 00:05:46,148
任何表述为对模型的指令的选项，从定义上来说都是错误的。
Every option phrased as an instruction to the model is wrong by definition.

65
00:05:46,734 --> 00:05:53,540
如果提到“直接解决根本原因”，那么一个只能可靠防止症状的选项仍然是干扰项。
If it says directly addresses the root cause, then an option that reliably prevents the symptom is still a distractor.

66
00:05:55,118 --> 00:06:02,628
“最有效”和“最可靠”通常倾向于那种具有通用性的方法，而不是只针对当前情况的处理方案。
Most effective and most reliable usually favor the approach that generalizes over the one that handles the case in front of you.

67
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:08,000
把这些词看作指令而非填充词，是核心技巧。
Reading these words as instructions rather than as filler is a skin.

68
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:11,940
这是可以掌握的。而且第19个模块专门讲这个内容。
It is learnable. And module 19 is entirely about it.

69
00:06:13,582 --> 00:06:14,852
这就是整门课程的核心。
This is the whole course.

70
00:06:15,406 --> 00:06:23,268
包含一个导论、涵盖五个领域并按官方比例分配的17个模块、三个横向贯穿的模块以及4场模拟考试。
One introduction 17 modules covering the five domains in their published proportions, three cross-cutting modules and four practice exams.

71
00:06:23,854 --> 00:06:26,596
共包含25个视频，大约6个半小时的内容。
25 videos and about 6 and a half hours.

72
00:06:27,406 --> 00:06:34,660
在学习过程中，模块内包含106个实战案例，模拟考试中还有80道题目。
Along the way, there are 106 worked scenarios inside the modules and 80 more questions across the practice exams.

73
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:40,420
也就是说，总共包含186道原创题目。
That is 186 original questions in total.

74
00:06:41,294 --> 00:06:48,324
各领域的模块大小是按大纲设计的，所以你在领域1和3上花费的两个小时并非随意安排的。
The domain blocks are sized to the blueprint, so the two hours you spend on domains 1 and 3 are not arbitrary.

75
00:06:48,814 --> 00:06:52,000
因为这两个领域占你总分的47%。
They are where 47% of your score comes from.

76
00:06:53,358 --> 00:06:57,520
之所以有三个模块，是因为考试题目认为大纲里没列出来。
Three modules exist because the exam test thinks the syllabus does not list.

77
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:01,028
第18个模块把所有容易混淆的成对选项都放在一起对比。
Module 18 puts every confusable pair side by side.

78
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:08,868
比如什么时候用记忆文件，什么时候用钩子；什么时候恢复会话，什么时候派生它；以及什么时候拆分工具，或者合并两个工具。
When to use a memory file and when to use a hook, when to resume a session and when to fork it, when to split a tool and when to merge two.

79
00:07:09,678 --> 00:07:12,676
等你学到那里时，你已经理解这些概念了。
You will already understand each of those by the time you get there.

80
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:20,580
第18个模块的作用是把「理解」转化为「识别」，这是两种不同的技能，而后者在时间压力下最容易出错。
What module 18 does is turn understanding into recognition, which is a different skill and the one that faints first under time pressure.

81
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:24,132
第19个模块是关于题目如何编写的。
Module 19 is about how the questions are written.

82
00:07:24,686 --> 00:07:29,188
第20个模块是关于时效性的，这部分需要专门讲一页。
And module 20 is about currency, which needs a slide of its own.

83
00:07:30,638 --> 00:07:36,900
认证内容总是滞后于产品更新，有些地方甚至落后了大约六个月。
Certification content always trails the product and this one trails it by about six months in places.

84
00:07:37,966 --> 00:07:39,300
有四个差距非常重要。
Four gaps matter.

85
00:07:39,822 --> 00:07:42,596
首先也是最重要的，是结构化输出。
First and most important, structured output.

86
00:07:43,342 --> 00:07:51,300
考试的标准答案是：定义一个输入架构为目标形状的工具，然后从工具调用块中读取该形状。
The exam's answer is to define a tool whose input schema is your target shape. You then read the shape back out of the tool use block.

87
00:07:52,110 --> 00:07:53,412
Claude API
The Claude AP

88
00:08:01,070 --> 00:08:12,496
Claude API。它现在有一个原生的结构化输出功能，可以通过编译语法来限制生成内容。这在实际工作中是更好的答案，但在考试中却是错误答案。
The Clot AP. I now has a native structured outputs feature that constrains generation with a compiled grammar. That is a better answer at work and the wrong answer in the exam.

89
00:08:12,736 --> 00:08:17,696
第二，显示哪些记忆文件已加载的命令现在分成了两个。
Second, the command that shows which memory files are loaded has split in two.

90
00:08:18,446 --> 00:08:23,620
第三，Claude Code 现在会生成自己的记忆笔记，而指南版本早于此更新。
Third, clot code now writes its own memory notes with the guide predates.

91
00:08:23,982 --> 00:08:30,180
第四，智能体光束虽然存在，但处于实验性标志之后，不会出现在考试中。
Fourth, agent beams exist but sit behind an experimental flag and are not examinable.

92
00:08:31,918 --> 00:08:34,212
处理这些情况的规则很简单。
The rule for handling all of that is simple.

93
00:08:34,734 --> 00:08:40,164
在考场上，根据指南编写时的蓝图和文档来回答。
In the exam room, answer from the blueprint and the documentation as it stood when the guide was written.

94
00:08:40,782 --> 00:08:43,844
在你的工作岗位上，按照现在的文档内容来构建。
At your desk, build from what the documentation says today.

95
00:08:44,910 --> 00:08:49,536
只要你知道自己处于哪种模式，这两者就不会冲突。
Those two are not in conflict as long as you know which mode you are in.

96
00:08:50,062 --> 00:08:57,732
每当本课程涉及到两者不一致的地方时，都会有一张幻灯片说明变化了什么以及何时改变的。
Every time this course reaches a point where they diverge, you will get a slide that says so, with what changed and when.

97
00:08:58,286 --> 00:09:05,188
模块 20 会把它们全部汇总在一起，这样你可以在考试日前统一复习这些差异。
Module 20 gathers them all in one place at the end so you can review the gaps as a set before exam day.

98
00:09:06,478 --> 00:09:10,756
每个模块都以实战场景结束，并且遵循同样的四个步骤。
Every module ends with work scenarios and they follow the same four beats.

99
00:09:11,726 --> 00:09:14,788
你会得到一个情境、一个症状和一项限制条件。
You get a situation, a symptom, and a constraint.

100
00:09:15,854 --> 00:09:18,532
然后是问题、四个选项以及一个停顿。
Then the question and four options and a pause.

101
00:09:19,310 --> 00:09:20,836
接着，你做出最终选择。
Then you commit to an answer.

102
00:09:21,806 --> 00:09:28,772
然后是解析过程，它花在解释为什么错误选项具有诱惑力上的时间，和解释正确答案为什么正确的时间一样多。
Then the walkthrough, which spends as much time on why the wrong answers are tempting as on why the right one is right.

103
00:09:29,966 --> 00:09:35,684
第三步是大家经常跳过的一步，跳过它会让练习失去意义。
That third step is the one people skip, and skipping it wastes the exercise.

104
00:09:36,590 --> 00:09:42,500
如果你在还没做出选择的情况下就看解析，你的大脑会读到正确答案并认为它是显而易见的。
If you watch the walkthrough without having chosen, your brain reads the correct answer and files it as obvious.

105
00:09:42,976 --> 00:09:44,196
它并不明显。
It was not obvious.

106
00:09:44,416 --> 00:09:46,180
你只是从未真正测试过自己。
You just never tested yourself.

107
00:09:47,982 --> 00:09:50,628
每次都要选一个字母，即使你在瞎猜的时候也是。
Pick a letter every time, even when you are guessing.

108
00:09:51,182 --> 00:09:53,296
尤其是当你正在猜测时。
Especially when you are guessing.

109
00:09:54,510 --> 00:09:56,452
这是我实际建议遵循的路线。
Here is the route I would actually follow.

110
00:09:56,656 --> 00:10:01,732
按顺序观看模块，因为后面的内容会用到前面章节提到的词汇。
Watch the modules in order because later ones assume the vocabulary of earlier ones.

111
00:10:01,936 --> 00:10:04,260
然后认真做一次模拟考试。
Then sit practice exam one properly.

112
00:10:04,814 --> 00:10:08,416
限时进行，不暂停，不记笔记，每题两分钟。
Timed, no pausing, no notes, two minutes a question.

113
00:10:08,656 --> 00:10:11,876
然后看你的错误集中在哪里，而不是只看分数。
Then look at where your misses cluster rather than at the score.

114
00:10:12,622 --> 00:10:18,756
如果 70% 的得分集中在某个领域，这比分数均匀分布在各个领域的 70% 情况要糟糕。
A 70% concentrated in domain, one is a worse position than a 70% spread evenly.

115
00:10:19,216 --> 00:10:21,828
它还能准确告诉你哪些内容需要重看。
It also tells you exactly what to rewatch.

116
00:10:22,096 --> 00:10:26,660
然后将剩下的三场考试分在几天内进行，而不是连着做。
Then space the remaining three exams out over days rather than doing them together.

117
00:10:26,896 --> 00:10:29,476
并且对这张幻灯片上的最后一点保持诚实。
And be honest about the last point on this slide.

118
00:10:30,094 --> 00:10:33,924
重看你已经擅长的领域感觉像是真的在学习。
Rewatching the domain you are already good at feels like studying.

119
00:10:34,126 --> 00:10:36,804
分数会一直很高，但并不会带来任何进步。
The scores stay high and it moves nothing.

120
00:10:38,350 --> 00:10:40,576
在进入模块 1 之前还有最后一件事。
One last thing before module 1.

121
00:10:40,910 --> 00:10:47,524
这不是那种可以通过背诵功能列表就能通过的考试，如果你尝试这样做，情景题会让你栽跟头。
This is not an exam you can pass by memorizing a list of features, and if you try, the scenario format will punish you.

122
00:10:48,334 --> 00:10:57,376
每一道题都会给你四个选项，这些选项都是合格的工程师可能做出的选择，但题目要求你判断在特定约束下，优秀的架构师会选哪一个。
Every question hands you four options that a competent engineer might reasonably choose and asks which one a good architect would choose given this specific constraint.

123
00:10:57,616 --> 00:11:02,884
所以当你学习这门课程时，不断问自己：在这种情况下，究竟是什么因素决定了最终的选择。
So as you go through the course, keep asking yourself what in the situation made the difference.

124
00:11:03,374 --> 00:11:05,124
这个问题就是整场考试的核心。
That question is the whole exam.

125
00:11:06,030 --> 00:11:12,772
模块 1 从智能体组开始，这是所有其他内容构建的基础。到时见。
Module 1 starts with the agentic group, which is the foundation everything else is built on. See you there.

126
00:11:14,318 --> 00:11:15,492
欢迎来到模块 1。
Welcome to module 1.

127
00:11:15,776 --> 00:11:23,300
这是领域 1：智能体架构与编排，占考试总分的 27%，是分量最大的领域。
This is domain 1, agentic architecture and orchestration, which is 27% of the exam, the largest domain by some distance.

128
00:11:24,046 --> 00:11:27,844
这个第一个模块涵盖了基础知识，其他三个模块都建立在它之上。
This first module covers the foundation, the other three build on.

129
00:11:28,686 --> 00:11:32,484
包括智能体到底是什么，以及它的循环如何开始和停止。
What an agent actually is and how its loop starts and stops.

130
00:11:33,454 --> 00:11:37,060
接下来是这个领域最常提出的问题。
Then the question this domain asks more often than any other.

131
00:11:38,862 --> 00:11:41,028
你到底该不该构建一个智能体？
Should you be building an agent at all?

132
00:11:41,870 --> 00:11:43,216
这里面的内容都不是废话。
None of this is filler.

133
00:11:44,174 --> 00:11:47,492
这里提到的每一个术语，后续都会出现在题目中。
Every term introduced here shows up in a question later.

134
00:11:49,134 --> 00:11:54,176
从这里开始，因为这个领域里几乎所有的错误答案都是因为遗漏了这些内容。
Start here because almost every wrong answer in this domain comes from forgetting it.

135
00:11:54,574 --> 00:11:56,336
模型并不运行智能体。
The model does not run an agent.

136
00:11:56,526 --> 00:11:57,456
是你的代码在运行。
Your code does.

137
00:11:57,774 --> 00:12:03,364
模型一次只生成一个响应，而你应用程序中的某些逻辑决定了是否再次调用它。
The model produces one response at a time and something in your application decides whether to call it again.

138
00:12:03,822 --> 00:12:06,736
那个“某些东西”就是循环，而它是由你控制的。
That something is the loop and you own it.

139
00:12:07,216 --> 00:12:15,204
当题目描述智能体表现不佳时，在考虑修改提示词之前，先问问自己是循环中的哪一部分出了问题。
When a question describes an agent behaving badly, ask yourself which part of the loop is at fault before you reach for a prompt change.

140
00:12:15,536 --> 00:12:19,076
很多时候，问题的解决办法在于你的代码，而不是你的措辞。
Very often, the fix is in your code, not in your words.

141
00:12:20,526 --> 00:12:25,856
Anthropic 将循环描述为四个步骤，值得按照这个结构来记忆。
Anthropic describes the loop in four steps, and it is worth memorizing in that shape.

142
00:12:26,222 --> 00:12:27,492
收集上下文。
Gather context.

143
00:12:27,982 --> 00:12:28,896
采取行动。
Take action.

144
00:12:29,198 --> 00:12:30,256
验证工作。
Verify work.

145
00:12:30,926 --> 00:12:31,716
重复。
Repeat.

146
00:12:32,270 --> 00:12:36,336
收集上下文是指在模型做出决定之前，你提供给它的所有信息。
Gathering context is everything you put in front of the model before it decides.

147
00:12:36,654 --> 00:12:40,324
采取行动是指模型选择一个工具，然后由你的代码去运行它。
Taking action is the model selecting a tool and your code running it.

148
00:12:40,974 --> 00:12:47,136
验证是指根据模型之外的某些内容来检查结果，比如测试套件、架构或进行二次校验。
Verifying is checking the result against something outside the model, like a test suite or a schema or a second pass.

149
00:12:47,630 --> 00:12:49,380
然后你再进入下一个循环。
And then you go round again.

150
00:12:50,318 --> 00:12:55,012
之所以要记住这四个步骤，是因为考试题目会逐一针对它们来考查。
The reason to hold all four in your head is that exam questions attack them one at a time.

151
00:12:55,936 --> 00:13:05,700
关于智能体不该调用某个工具的问题属于「收集上下文」问题。而关于没人发现错误输出的问题则是「验证」问题。
A question about a tool the agent should not have called is a gather context question. A question about wrong output nobody caught is a verify question.

152
00:13:07,246 --> 00:13:08,336
三个要素。
Three ingredients.

153
00:13:08,576 --> 00:13:12,196
工具调用，让模型能够采取行动，而不只是进行描述。
Tool use so the model can act rather than only describe.

154
00:13:12,622 --> 00:13:22,416
对路径的自主权。也就是说，模型根据刚刚发现的信息来决定下一步。以及一个反馈循环，让结果回到上下文中并改变接下来的走向。
Autonomy over the path. So the model decides the next step based on what it just found out. And a feedback loop so results come back into context and change what happens next.

155
00:13:22,958 --> 00:13:27,556
中间这一项是判别器，也是大家最容易做错的一项。
The middle one is the discriminator, and it is the one people get wrong.

156
00:13:28,176 --> 00:13:35,428
一个每次都按固定顺序调用三个工具的系统并不是智能体，尽管它大量使用了工具。
A system that calls three tools in a fixed order every single time is not an agent, even though it uses tools heavily.

157
00:13:36,078 --> 00:13:38,180
它只是包含工具的工作流。
It is a workflow with tools in it.

158
00:13:39,022 --> 00:13:45,252
记住这个区别，因为考试会直接考查这一点，而且题目中的措辞非常微妙。
Hold on to that distinction because the exam tests it directly and the wording it uses is subtle.

159
00:13:46,894 --> 00:13:52,516
Anthropic 将此称为增强模型，它是构建其他所有内容的基础单元。
Anthropic calls this the augmented model and it is the atom that everything else is built from.

160
00:13:53,294 --> 00:13:58,020
一个能够查询信息、调用工具并记住已执行操作的模型。
A model that can look things up, call tools, and remember what it has already done.

161
00:13:58,638 --> 00:14:07,428
这个领域中的每种架构，从单次调用到运行六个子智能体的协调者，不都是由同样的模块以不同的排列方式组成的吗？
Every architecture in this domain, from a single call to a coordinator running six subagents, is that same block arranged differently?

162
00:14:08,366 --> 00:14:12,548
当题目给出一个复杂的架构时，这是一个很有用的锚点。
That is a useful anchor when a question presents an elaborate architecture.

163
00:14:13,134 --> 00:14:17,956
将其简化为有多少个增强模型块，以及谁来决定它们运行的顺序。
Reduce it to how many augmented blocks there are and who decides the order they run in.

164
00:14:19,758 --> 00:14:23,364
这是考试最看重的区别。
Here is the distinction the exam leans on hardest.

165
00:14:23,854 --> 00:14:29,412
在工作流中，模型和工具是通过你编写的预定义代码路径来编排的。
In a workflow, models and tools are orchestrated through predefined code paths that you wrote.

166
00:14:30,254 --> 00:14:37,124
在智能体中，模型动态地引导自己的过程，决定使用哪些工具以及按什么顺序使用。
In an agent, the model dynamically directs its own process, deciding which tools to use and in what order.

167
00:14:37,998 --> 00:14:42,084
工作流提供可预测性、更低的成本和更简单的调试。
Workflows give you predictability, lower cost, and easier debugging.

168
00:14:42,702 --> 00:14:46,244
当路径无法预知时，智能体能提供灵活性。
Agents give you flexibility when the path cannot be known in advance.

169
00:14:48,366 --> 00:14:51,556
底部的这个判定标准是你要带进考场去用的。
The tiebreaker at the bottom is the one to carry into the exam room.

170
00:14:51,856 --> 00:14:55,108
问问自己：你是否能在任务开始前画出流程图？
Ask whether you could draw the flowchart before the task starts.

171
00:14:56,046 --> 00:14:57,668
如果可以，那就是工作流。
If you could, it is a workflow.

172
00:14:57,934 --> 00:15:03,492
如果流程图的形状取决于第二步返回的内容，那么你就需要一个智能体。
If the shape of the flowchart depends on what step 2 comes back with, then you need an agent.

173
00:15:04,878 --> 00:15:08,900
增加第三种类型是值得的，因为考试场景会涵盖这三种情况。
It is worth adding a third shape because exam scenarios use all three.

174
00:15:09,454 --> 00:15:14,948
对话式系统在每一轮中都有人类参与来回答问题，且不需要任何外部操作。
A conversational system answers questions with a human present every turn and no external action required.

175
00:15:15,758 --> 00:15:18,724
工作流执行你设计的路径中的定义步骤。
A workflow does a defined step of a path you designed.

176
00:15:19,438 --> 00:15:21,348
智能体自行决定路径。
An agent decides the path itself.

177
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:27,696
注意随着表格向上移动，模型的职责在缩小，而你的确定性在增加。
Notice how the model's job shrinks as you move up that table and how your certainty grows.

178
00:15:27,856 --> 00:15:30,244
这种权衡就是整个设计决策的核心。
That trade is the whole design decision.

179
00:15:30,496 --> 00:15:32,612
并留意提示中的规律。
And watch for the pattern in the callout.

180
00:15:32,816 --> 00:15:39,716
场景会描述一个具有固定三步路径的案例，然后在四个选项中提供一个智能体式的解决方案。
A scenario will describe something with a fixed 3-step path, then offer an agentic solution as one of the four options.

181
00:15:40,430 --> 00:15:41,988
这听起来很高级。
It sounds sophisticated.

182
00:15:42,478 --> 00:15:46,724
但它是错误答案，而且题目中的约束条件通常会告诉你原因。
It is the wrong answer, and the question usually tells you why in the constraint.

183
00:15:48,336 --> 00:15:53,936
Anthropic 在这方面的官方指南非常直接，而且这些内容直接关系到得分。
Anthropic's published guidance on this is unusually blunt and it converts straight into marks.

184
00:15:54,576 --> 00:15:59,236
先寻找最简单的解决方案，只有在需要时才增加复杂度。
Find the simplest solution first and add complexity only when you need it.

185
00:16:00,014 --> 00:16:08,516
对于大量的应用场景，一个构建良好的包含检索和少量上下文示例的调用就完全足够了。
For a great many applications, a single well-constructed call with retrieval and a few in context examples is entirely sufficient.

186
00:16:09,198 --> 00:16:12,804
智能体系统确实能提高复杂问题的任务表现。
Agentic systems do improve task performance on hard problems.

187
00:16:13,518 --> 00:16:18,436
但它们成本更高、耗时更长，而且在出错时更难排查原因。
They also cost more, take longer, and are harder to reason about when they go wrong.

188
00:16:19,278 --> 00:16:23,972
如果路径是固定的，增加决策者只会增加变数，而不会带来任何好处。
If the path is fixed, adding a decision maker adds variance and buys you nothing.

189
00:16:25,998 --> 00:16:30,692
考试会考到你是否应该构建一个智能体，而有时正确答案就是“不”。
The exam does ask whether you should build an agent, and sometimes the correct answer is no.

190
00:16:31,374 --> 00:16:34,308
不要因为觉得这是个陷阱就犹豫不决。
Do not talk yourself out of it because it feels like a trick.

191
00:16:35,950 --> 00:16:37,348
这就是设计上的决策。
So that is the design decision.

192
00:16:37,552 --> 00:16:38,788
现在来看机制部分，
Now the mechanics,

193
00:16:39,502 --> 00:16:46,244
因为很大一部分领域一的题目是关于循环本身的，只要掌握一个领域，这些问题就很容易回答。
because a large group of domain one questions are about the loop itself, and they are very answerable once you know one field.

194
00:16:47,246 --> 00:16:48,868
这是需要记住的一句话。
Here is the sentence to carry.

195
00:16:49,230 --> 00:16:51,812
当模型说它完成了时，循环并不停止。
The loop does not stop when the model says it is done.

196
00:16:52,752 --> 00:16:56,068
只有当模型不再请求工具时，它才会停止。
It stops when the model stops asking for tools.

197
00:16:56,272 --> 00:17:02,500
这两者不是一回事，而两者之间的差距正是大量生产环境 Bug 出现的地方。
Those two are not the same thing, and the gap between them is where a surprising number of production bugs live.

198
00:17:03,982 --> 00:17:05,924
这里有一个具体的轮次示例。
Here is one turn concretely.

199
00:17:06,112 --> 00:17:10,912
你将消息数组和你的工具定义发送到 messages API。
You send the messages array and your tool definitions to the messages API.

200
00:17:11,472 --> 00:17:16,932
返回的响应包含一个名为“停止原因”的字段，它告诉你生成为什么停止。
The response comes back with a field called stop reason, which tells you why generation stopped.

201
00:17:17,392 --> 00:17:22,468
如果该字段显示为“工具调用”，说明模型想要运行工具，于是你的代码去执行它们。
If that field says tool use, the model wants tools run, so your code runs them.

202
00:17:22,990 --> 00:17:25,392
然后你向对话中添加两样东西。
You then append two things to the conversation.

203
00:17:25,646 --> 00:17:30,500
首先是助手轮次，内容与返回的一模一样，包括工具调用块。
First, the assistants turn exactly as it came back, including the tool use blocks.

204
00:17:31,054 --> 00:17:33,476
接着是一个包含工具结果的用户轮次。
Then a user turn containing the tool results.

205
00:17:34,030 --> 00:17:35,108
然后你再次调用。
Then you call again.

206
00:17:35,392 --> 00:17:40,420
只要“停止原因”等于“工具调用”，你就继续循环；当它显示为“结束轮次”时，你退出。
You keep going while stop reason equals tool use and you exit when it says end turn.

207
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:42,340
这就是整个循环。
That is the whole loop.

208
00:17:42,832 --> 00:17:47,844
它的逻辑确实这么简单，而且考试要求你掌握如此细致的细节。
It is genuinely that small and the exam expects you to know it in that much detail.

209
00:17:49,550 --> 00:17:53,712
有 7 个记录的数值，每一个都需要不同的分支处理。
7 documented values and each needs a different branch.

210
00:17:54,210 --> 00:17:56,548
“结束轮次”意味着完成，所以退出。
End turn means finished, so exit.

211
00:17:57,358 --> 00:18:00,068
工具调用意味着运行工具并返回结果。
Tool use means run tools and come back.

212
00:18:00,432 --> 00:18:03,364
最大标记数意味着输出预算耗尽了。
Max tokens means the output budget ran out.

213
00:18:04,238 --> 00:18:08,004
停止序列意味着匹配到了你自定义的其中一个停止字符串。
Stop sequence means one of your custom stop strings matched.

214
00:18:08,910 --> 00:18:14,116
最后三项是大家容易忘掉的，而它们正是智能体在生产环境中报错的地方。
The last three are the ones people forget, and they are exactly where agents break in production.

215
00:18:15,278 --> 00:18:21,540
暂停轮次发生在像网络搜索这样的服务端工具循环达到其自身的迭代限制时。
Pause turn happens when a server-side tool loop like web search hits its own iteration limit.

216
00:18:22,094 --> 00:18:24,292
你会追加响应并再次调用。
You append the response and call again.

217
00:18:25,166 --> 00:18:31,332
拒绝者意味着模型拒绝了请求，并且以正常的成功响应而非错误形式到达。
Refuser means plot declined and it arrives as a normal successful response rather than an error.

218
00:18:31,632 --> 00:18:34,244
不要自动重试相同的提示词。
Do not retry the same prompt automatically.

219
00:18:34,512 --> 00:18:40,100
而模块上下文窗口超出意味着输入加上输出溢出了窗口。
And module context window exceeded means the input plus the output overflowed the window.

220
00:18:40,352 --> 00:18:42,468
提高数值无法解决这个问题。
Raising a number will not fix that one.

221
00:18:43,472 --> 00:18:44,964
你必须减少发送的内容。
You have to send less.

222
00:18:46,638 --> 00:18:52,228
这两者在日志中看起来很像，但解决方法正好相反，所以考试喜欢把它们区分开来。
These two look similar in a log and the fixes are opposites, so the exam likes separating them.

223
00:18:52,752 --> 00:19:01,412
最大标记数意味着输出超过了你在请求中设置的上限。你可以提高那个上限，或者要求模型从停止的地方继续。
Max tokens means the output ran past the ceiling that you set in the request. You can raise that ceiling or you can ask the model to continue from where it stopped.

224
00:19:01,952 --> 00:19:03,684
输入从来不是问题所在。
The input was never the problem.

225
00:19:04,654 --> 00:19:12,228
模型上下文窗口超出意味着整个请求的输入加上输出合在一起无法放入模型的窗口中。
Model context window exceeded means the entire request input plus output together will not fit in the model's window.

226
00:19:12,846 --> 00:19:14,308
没有可以增加的数值。
There is no number to raise.

227
00:19:14,670 --> 00:19:20,032
你必须减少发送的内容，这意味着裁剪历史记录、进行总结或者拆分任务。
You have to send less, which means trimming history, summarizing, or splitting the work up.

228
00:19:20,590 --> 00:19:24,260
并且记住你的工具定义也是输入标记。
And remember that your tool definitions are input tokens too.

229
00:19:26,030 --> 00:19:30,752
在一个定义了 20 个工具的系统中，它们不是微不足道的误差。
On a system with 20 tools defined, they are not a rounding error.

230
00:19:32,110 --> 00:19:36,484
有一种特定的故障值得你能够立即识别出来。
One specific failure is worth being able to recognize instantly.

231
00:19:37,742 --> 00:19:44,036
停止原因返回为最大标记数，且最后一个内容块是一个不完整的工具调用。
Stop reason comes back as max tokens, and the last content block is a partial tool use.

232
00:19:44,750 --> 00:19:51,876
模型在编写工具输入的中途就因为预算耗尽而停止了，所以输入不完整且无法传递。
The model was partway through writing the tool's input when the budget ran out, so the input is incomplete and cannot be passed.

233
00:19:52,846 --> 00:19:57,988
需要注意的是，在不改变任何内容的情况下重试，会产生完全相同的失败。
The thing to notice is that retrying without changing anything produces exactly the same failure.

234
00:19:58,272 --> 00:20:03,908
采样不会拯救你。你要么增加预算，要么减少该次调用需要承载的内容。
Sampling is not going to rescue you. You either raise the budget or reduce what that call has to carry.

235
00:20:04,302 --> 00:20:09,188
记住这个特征，因为它会在领域 4 中以截断的提取形式出现。
And keep this shape in mind because it comes back in domain 4 with a truncated extraction.

236
00:20:10,112 --> 00:20:18,192
当题目告诉你重试会产生相同的失败时，它是在告诉你修复方法是结构性的。
When a question tells you retrying produces identical failures, it is telling you the fix is structural.

237
00:20:19,502 --> 00:20:26,916
对话数组有规则，其中两条由 API 执行，而第三条仅表现为异常行为。
The conversation array has rules and two of them are enforced by the API while the third only shows up as strange behavior.

238
00:20:27,790 --> 00:20:35,140
首先，当你追加模型的轮次时，要按接收到的原样添加，包括所有的工具调用块。
First, when you append the model's turn, append it exactly as received, tool use blocks and all.

239
00:20:35,790 --> 00:20:39,232
漏掉这些会导致数组无效并报错。
Leaving it out gives you an invalid array and an error.

240
00:20:39,872 --> 00:20:48,516
其次，紧随其后的用户轮次仅包含工具结果块，不包含其他内容。每一个都以工具调用 ID 为键进行响应。
Second, the user turn that follows contains tool result blocks and nothing else. Each one keyed by the tool use ID, it answers.

241
00:20:49,070 --> 00:20:54,660
第三点，也是最容易出错的一点：不要在工具结果旁边塞入任何有用的提示信息。
Third, and this is the one that bytes, do not tuck a helpful note in alongside the tool results.

242
00:20:55,470 --> 00:21:02,832
这会让 Claude 学会在每次工具调用后都期待用户文本，而你会莫名其妙地收到空轮次的响应。
It teaches Claude to expect user text after every tool call and you start getting empty n turn responses for no obvious reason.

243
00:21:02,992 --> 00:21:08,900
而在这一切的底层，消息 API 是无状态的。你每次都要重新发送所有内容。
And underneath all of it, the messages API is stateless. You resend everything every time.

244
00:21:10,254 --> 00:21:14,852
有 5 种会导致循环出错的方法，而考试会从这些中设计出干扰项。
5 ways to get the loop wrong and the exam builds distractors from all of them.

245
00:21:15,392 --> 00:21:21,092
通过判断响应文本来决定智能体是否完成，而不是读取停止原因字段。
Passing the response text to decide whether the agent is finished rather than reading the stop reason field.

246
00:21:21,792 --> 00:21:26,340
这是整个领域中最常见的干扰项，而且看起来总是很有道理。
That is the most common distractor in the whole domain and it always looks reasonable.

247
00:21:27,278 --> 00:21:31,236
一旦模型用不恰当的措辞表达内容时，它就会失效。
It breaks the first time the model phrases something inconveniently.

248
00:21:31,872 --> 00:21:37,380
将迭代上限作为你的停止条件，而实际上上限只是安全网而非终止符。
Using an iteration cap as your stop condition when a cap is a safety net rather than a terminator.

249
00:21:38,062 --> 00:21:41,316
在追加两个结果之前删除助手轮次。
Dropping the assistant turn before you append two results.

250
00:21:42,510 --> 00:21:44,964
在这些结果之后添加清除文本。
Adding clearing text after those results.

251
00:21:45,742 --> 00:21:53,156
以及将暂停轮次视为结束轮次，这会悄悄截断所有使用服务端工具的智能体。
And treating pause turn as though it were end turn, which quietly truncates every agent that uses a server-side tool.

252
00:21:54,830 --> 00:22:00,100
这个区别在多个模块中都涉及得分，所以值得花 10 秒钟去关注一下。
This distinction earns marks in more than one module, so it is worth 10 seconds of attention.

253
00:22:01,390 --> 00:22:06,532
循环真正的退出条件是模型不返回任何工具调用块，这会显示为结束轮次。
The loop's real exit condition is the model returning no tool use blocks, which shows up as end turn.

254
00:22:06,990 --> 00:22:09,028
这意味着 Claude 判断任务已完成。
That means Clot judge the task complete.

255
00:22:09,806 --> 00:22:11,428
其他所有内容都是护栏。
Everything else is a guardrail.

256
00:22:12,142 --> 00:22:16,432
最大轮数限制了单次调用可能进行的迭代次数。
Max turns caps how many iterations a single invocation may take.

257
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:19,844
以美元计量的最大预算限制了它可以花费的金额。
Max budget in dollars caps what it may spend.

258
00:22:20,192 --> 00:22:25,284
这两者都是由 SDK 执行而非模型执行，且两者都是保护机制。
Both are enforced by the SDK rather than by the model, and both are protections.

259
00:22:25,872 --> 00:22:28,484
重要的后果就在这个提醒中。
The important consequence is in the callout.

260
00:22:29,390 --> 00:22:32,580
当运行因为触发护栏而结束时，意味着没有任何任务完成。
When a run ends because it hit a guardrail, nothing was finished.

261
00:22:33,134 --> 00:22:38,532
将每次循环退出都视为成功的代码，会报告一个从未发生过的已完成任务。
Code that treats every loop, exit as success will report a completed task that never happened.

262
00:22:40,558 --> 00:22:42,948
模块 4 就是为了填补这个漏洞。
Module 4 is about closing that gap.

263
00:22:44,622 --> 00:22:46,340
回到那四个步骤。
Back to the four steps for a moment.

264
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:51,652
第三步在实际系统和错误的考试答案中都会被悄悄忽略。
The third one gets quietly dropped, both in real systems and in wrong exam answers.

265
00:22:52,112 --> 00:22:54,912
收集上下文和采取行动是显而易见的。
Gather context and take action are obvious.

266
00:22:55,152 --> 00:23:02,512
验证并不是因为它需要额外的调用或额外的基础设施，而且没有它时输出看起来也没问题。
Verification is not because it costs an extra call or an extra piece of infrastructure and the output looks fine without it.

267
00:23:03,022 --> 00:23:08,292
但一个没有验证的智能体是一个会产出没人检查过的、看似自信的工作的系统。
But an agent without verification is a system that produces confident work nobody has checked.

268
00:23:08,832 --> 00:23:17,156
当场景描述一个快速、廉价，但在生产环境中产生错误风险的智能体时，寻找增加检查项的选项。
When a scenario describes an agent that is fast, cheap, and wrong in ways that reach production, look for the option that adds a check.

269
00:23:18,766 --> 00:23:30,660
验证有优先顺序，考试也遵循这个顺序。首先是确定性检查，因为测试套件、架构验证器或类型检查器能以极低的成本提供无可争议的答案。
Verification has a preference order and the exam follows it. Deterministic checks first because a test suite or a schema validator or a type checker gives you an unarguable answer for almost no money.

270
00:23:31,406 --> 00:23:34,372
然后是智能体无法通过对话绕过的规则。
Then rules the agent cannot talk its way past.

271
00:23:35,310 --> 00:23:41,732
一个阻止操作的钩子，或者是在工具内部强制执行的限制，而不是在提示词中描述的限制。
A hook that blocks an action or a limit enforced inside the tool itself rather than described in a prompt.

272
00:23:42,446 --> 00:23:47,876
只有当你需要判断时，才使用带有全新上下文和明确问题的第二个模型环节。
Then only if you need judgment, a second model pass with fresh context and a narrow question.

273
00:23:48,398 --> 00:23:50,992
而底线是：根本不需要验证。
And the bottom line is not verification at all.

274
00:23:51,534 --> 00:24:01,188
询问智能体是否表现良好属于相同的上下文，这会让它在创造自己的工作时，比正常情况下更频繁地自我认同。
Asking the agent whether it did well is the same context creating its own work and it agrees with itself far more often than it should.

275
00:24:02,478 --> 00:24:05,072
这就是该理论如何转化为得分的方法。
Here is how that theory turns into marks.

276
00:24:05,392 --> 00:24:10,948
这些阶段会出现在题干中，而且在你读到任何选项之前，每一个环节都会缩小备选范围。
These phases appear in question stems, and each one narrows the field before you have read a single option.

277
00:24:13,806 --> 00:24:20,272
每个请求都遵循相同的三个步骤意味着工作流，因为固定的路径不需要决策者。
The same three steps for every request means workflow because a fixed path does not need a decision maker.

278
00:24:20,814 --> 00:24:24,548
取决于它在每一步发现的内容，这意味着智能体。
Depends on what it finds at each step means agent.

279
00:24:25,312 --> 00:24:32,356
必须是可预测且可审计的，这会引导你选择工作流或带有严格限制的智能体。
Must be predictable and auditable, pushes you towards a workflow or an agent with hard limits wrapped around it.

280
00:24:33,198 --> 00:24:42,884
诸如开放式、不熟悉，或者工程师未指定优先处理哪些模块等词汇都意味着智能体，因为没有人能提前画出那种流程图。
Words like open-ended, unfamiliar, or the engineer has not specified which modules to prioritize all mean agent, because nobody can draw that flow chart in advance.

281
00:24:44,206 --> 00:24:50,752
而「保证」或「无论提示词如何」意味着答案根本不是关于系统的架构。
And guarantee or regardless of prompting means the answer is not about the shape of the system at all.

282
00:24:51,406 --> 00:24:53,860
它是一个位于模型之外的控制机制。
It is a control sitting outside the model.

283
00:24:55,534 --> 00:25:00,292
在案例之前先记住一个核心限制，因为它贯穿整个课程。
One honest limit before the scenarios, because it recurs throughout this course.

284
00:25:00,592 --> 00:25:06,148
没有任何办法能写出一个系统提示词，让智能体 100% 的时间都去做某件事。
There is no way to write a system prompt that makes an agent do something 100% of the time.

285
00:25:06,894 --> 00:25:08,100
强调有助于辨析。
Emphasis helps.

286
00:25:08,878 --> 00:25:10,660
大写字母也有点帮助。
Capital letters help a little.

287
00:25:11,534 --> 00:25:14,756
这两者都无法让你达到「总是」，而考试也知道这一点。
Neither gets you to always, and the exam knows it.

288
00:25:15,630 --> 00:25:22,244
这里的题目通常描述一个规则，尽管有明确的指令，但在 97% 的情况下依然会失效。
Questions here often describe a rule that holds 97% of the time despite clear instructions.

289
00:25:24,302 --> 00:25:26,788
然后他们会问如何填补这个差距。
Then they ask how to close the gap.

290
00:25:27,376 --> 00:25:30,180
答案永远不是更强硬的指令。
The answer is never a firmer instruction.

291
00:25:30,830 --> 00:25:35,136
而是你代码中的一个控制机制，无论模型决定什么都会执行。
It is a control in your code that runs regardless of what the model decided.

292
00:25:35,694 --> 00:25:40,096
记住这个想法，因为它至少会决定试卷上的一个问题。
Hold that thought because it decides at least one question on every paper.

293
00:25:41,262 --> 00:25:44,356
在进入案例前先记住这五行核心要点。
Five lines to takeaway before the scenarios.

294
00:25:44,846 --> 00:25:46,436
智能体是一个循环。
An agent is a loop.

295
00:25:46,736 --> 00:25:52,260
你的代码负责运行、收集上下文、采取行动、验证、重复。
Your code owns running, gather context, take action, verify, repeat.

296
00:25:52,576 --> 00:25:57,956
当你能提前画出流程图时选择工作流，当你不能预先画出时选择智能体。
Choose a workflow when you can draw the flowchart in advance and an agent when you cannot.

297
00:25:58,638 --> 00:26:05,348
循环在停止原因为工具调用时运行，并在结束轮次时退出，你永远不会通过阅读文本来决定完成。
The loop runs while stop reason is tool use and exits on end turn, and you never decide completion by reading the text.

298
00:26:05,856 --> 00:26:11,172
最大轮数和最大预算是保护栏，所以触发其中任何一个都是失败而非完成。
Max turns and max budget are guardrains, so hitting one is a failure rather than a finish.

299
00:26:12,046 --> 00:26:19,652
提示词是说服，而代码是强制执行。因此当问题中使用「保证」这个词时，寻找那些位于模型之外的选项。
And prompts persuade while code enforces. So when a question uses the word guarantee, look for the option that lays outside the model.

300
00:26:20,014 --> 00:26:21,284
现在开始五个案例。
Five scenarios now.

301
00:26:21,536 --> 00:26:25,732
在讲解之前，每次都要选一个字母，即使是猜的时候也要选。
Pick a letter each time before the walkthrough, including when you are guessing.

302
00:26:27,470 --> 00:26:28,420
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

303
00:26:29,006 --> 00:26:34,052
一家物流公司有一个用于回答货物相关问题的智能体。
A logistics company has an agent that answers questions about shipments.

304
00:26:34,478 --> 00:26:36,932
它有四个工具，并且测试通过。
It has four tools and it tests cleanly.

305
00:26:37,518 --> 00:26:42,096
但在生产环境中，大约每 20 次调用中就会有一次不返回结果。
In production, about one call in 20 never returns.

306
00:26:42,638 --> 00:26:54,404
在智能体生成完整答案后，循环仍会持续调用 API，直到轮数限制终止运行。日志显示，这些最后的响应根本不包含工具调用，只有文本。
The loop keeps calling the AP long after the agent has produced a complete answer until the turncap aborts the run. The logs show those final responses contain no tool calls at all, just text.

307
00:26:54,816 --> 00:27:01,316
而且循环的实现逻辑是：在退出前检查响应文本中是否包含“任务完成”这几个字。
And the loop implementation checks whether the response text contains the words task complete before it exits.

308
00:27:01,696 --> 00:27:02,976
根本原因是什么？
What is the root cause?

309
00:27:03,246 --> 00:27:06,336
A. 轮数限制对于当前工作量设置得太低了。
a The turncap is set too low for the workload.

310
00:27:06,606 --> 00:27:11,396
B. 循环是根据响应文本而非停止原因字段来判断是否完成的。
B. The loop determines completion from response text rather than from the stop reason field.

311
00:27:12,142 --> 00:27:18,404
C. 智能体需要一个系统提示词，告诉它在完成时说“任务完成”。
C. The agent needs a system prompt telling it to say task complete when it finishes.

312
00:27:18,816 --> 00:27:19,136
D。
D.

313
00:27:19,694 --> 00:27:23,696
工具结果在没有前面的助手轮次的情况下被添加了。
Tool results are being appended without the preceding assistant turn.

314
00:27:24,142 --> 00:27:25,380
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

315
00:27:30,958 --> 00:27:32,496
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

316
00:27:32,910 --> 00:27:37,124
埋设的细节是：最后的响应不包含任何工具调用。
The planted detail is that the final responses contain no tool calls.

317
00:27:37,376 --> 00:27:41,216
没有工具调用意味着停止原因字段显示为“结束轮次”。
No tool calls means the stop reason field says end turn.

318
00:27:41,536 --> 00:27:46,404
API 说：“我已经告诉这个循环要退出了，但循环没在听。”
The AP, I already told this loop to exit and the loop was not listening.

319
00:27:47,022 --> 00:27:49,028
它一直在读取纯文本。
It was reading prose instead.

320
00:27:49,518 --> 00:27:55,140
选项 A 是一个很有迷惑性的干扰项，因为轮数限制确实参与其中。
Option A is the interesting distractor because the turn cap genuinely is involved.

321
00:27:56,046 --> 00:27:57,508
它是阻止程序失控的因素。
It is what stops the runaway.

322
00:27:58,094 --> 00:28:04,260
但它只是症状的限制器，而不是根本原因；提高这个限制只会让每次失败的成本更高。
But it is the limiter on the symptom, not the cause, and raising it would only make each failure more expensive.

323
00:28:05,166 --> 00:28:09,988
选项 C 实际上会降低失败率，这就是它看起来很有诱惑力的原因。
Option C would actually reduce the failure rate, which is what makes it tempting.

324
00:28:10,446 --> 00:28:17,604
但它会让正确性取决于模型是否选择特定的短语，而这正是 Bug 的所在，而不是修复方案。
It also makes correctness depend on the model choosing a particular phrase, and that is the bug rather than the fix.

325
00:28:18,542 --> 00:28:25,764
选项 D 是一个真实的错误，但它会立即且明显地报错，这与循环运行时间过长的情况不符。
Option D is a real error, but it fails immediately and loudly, which does not match a loop running too long.

326
00:28:27,342 --> 00:28:34,404
场景 2。一个团队对每一个拉取请求都进行自动化审查。它总是按同样的顺序做三件事。
Scenario 2. A team runs an automated review on every pull request. It always does the same three things in the same order.

327
00:28:34,656 --> 00:28:40,932
对照公司指南检查代码风格，扫描已知的安全模式，并确认公共函数都有文档说明。
Check style against the house guide, scan for known security patterns, and confirm that public functions are documented.

328
00:28:41,136 --> 00:28:43,236
每一部分都是独立的。
Each part is independent of the others.

329
00:28:43,982 --> 00:28:51,492
今天，一个智能体被交给所有三个检查清单，由它来决定如何推进。结果并不一致。
Today a single agent is handed all three checklists and left to decide how to proceed. Results are inconsistent.

330
00:28:51,696 --> 00:28:59,748
有时会完全跳过文档检查，审核人员无法判断缺失的项是因为代码没问题还是因为该步骤根本没运行。
Sometimes documentation is skipped entirely and reviewers cannot tell whether a missing finding means the code was clean or the step never ran.

331
00:29:00,526 --> 00:29:02,724
最合适的架构变更是什么？
What is the most appropriate design change?

332
00:29:03,214 --> 00:29:05,700
A. 对系统进行强调。
a add emphasis to the system.

333
00:29:06,446 --> 00:29:10,020
提示词要求智能体始终执行所有三个检查。
Prompt instructing the agent to always perform all three checks.

334
00:29:10,496 --> 00:29:10,736
B.
b.

335
00:29:11,470 --> 00:29:13,252
将其重构为提示词链。
Restructure it as prompt chaining.

336
00:29:13,710 --> 00:29:15,108
分为三个串行步骤。
Three sequential steps.

337
00:29:15,598 --> 00:29:18,692
每次都是独立的调用，并配有各自专注的提示词。
Each a separate call with its own focused prompt.

338
00:29:19,456 --> 00:29:19,696
C.
C.

339
00:29:20,398 --> 00:29:25,028
给智能体提供三个独立的工具，每个检查对应一个工具，让它去调用这些工具。
Give the agent three separate tools, one per check, and let it call them.

340
00:29:25,390 --> 00:29:29,924
D. 增加最大轮数，让智能体有足够的空间完成所有三项任务。
D. Increase max turns so the agent has room to complete all three.

341
00:29:30,446 --> 00:29:31,716
稍等一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

342
00:29:37,390 --> 00:29:38,468
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

343
00:29:39,056 --> 00:29:43,588
再读一遍第一段，这是一个工作流规范。
Read the first paragraph again, and it is a specification for a workflow.

344
00:29:44,016 --> 00:29:49,220
每次都要按同样的顺序执行这三件事，且它们彼此独立。
The same three things in the same order every time and independent of each other.

345
00:29:49,838 --> 00:29:56,096
智能体不需要做决策，所以交给它一个任务只会引入变数，没别的作用。
There is no decision for an agent to make, so handing it one introduces variance and nothing else.

346
00:29:56,718 --> 00:30:04,388
提示词链从你的代码中运行所有三项内容，这也能解决审核员的抱怨，因为缺失的项现在很可能意味着代码是干净的。
Prompt chaining runs all three from your code and it also fixes the reviewer's complaint because a missing finding now probably means clean code.

347
00:30:05,038 --> 00:30:11,140
选项 A 虽然减少了跳过的情况，但并没有消除它，而审核人员需要的是确定性而不是较低的失败率。
Option A reduces the skipping without eliminating it, and reviewers need certainty rather than a lower rate.

348
00:30:13,390 --> 00:30:15,936
选项 C 是最强的干扰项。
Option C is the strongest distractor.

349
00:30:16,718 --> 00:30:22,980
三个专注的工具确实比一个巨大的清单更好用，如果答案必须是智能体相关的，那选这个。
Three focus tools genuinely beat one giant checklist, and if the answer had to be agentic, this would be it.

350
00:30:23,566 --> 00:30:27,108
但路径仍然由智能体掌控，所以它仍可能跳过某一步。
But the agent still owns the path, so it can still skip a step.

351
00:30:27,438 --> 00:30:29,700
它只是降低了失败率，并没有消除风险。
It shrinks the failure without removing it.

352
00:30:30,318 --> 00:30:31,856
选项 D 解决了问题。
Option D solves the problem.

353
00:30:32,016 --> 00:30:34,016
场景从未描述过这种情况。
The scenario never described.

354
00:30:35,342 --> 00:30:36,356
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

355
00:30:37,358 --> 00:30:44,900
一个智能体通过一个接收大型结构化输入的单一工具，提取合同条款并将其写入记录系统。
An agent extracts contract terms and writes them into a record system through a single tool that takes a large structured input.

356
00:30:46,446 --> 00:30:48,452
在处理长合同时，运行失败了。
On long contracts, the run fails.

357
00:30:48,736 --> 00:30:53,444
返回的响应中，停止原因字段被设置为最大标记数。
The response comes back with the stop reason field set to max tokens.

358
00:30:53,966 --> 00:31:05,956
最后一个内容块是一个工具调用，在对象中间就被截断了。团队的重试逻辑将相同的请求重新发送了三次，但每次尝试都以同样的方式失败。
The last content block is a partial tool use cut off partway through an object. The team's retry logic resends the identical request up to three times and every attempt fails in the same way.

359
00:31:06,542 --> 00:31:08,356
最有效的修复方法是什么？
What is the most effective fix?

360
00:31:08,974 --> 00:31:12,612
a 在三次重试之间加入指数退避。
a add exponential backoff between the three retrees.

361
00:31:13,550 --> 00:31:13,776
B。
b.

362
00:31:14,254 --> 00:31:19,268
捕获传递错误，并让智能体用纯文本总结合同。
Catch the pass error and have the agent summarize the contract in prose instead.

363
00:31:19,696 --> 00:31:19,936
C。
C.

364
00:31:20,336 --> 00:31:25,156
提高最大标记数，并将非常长的合同拆分到多次工具调用中。
Raise max tokens and split very long contracts across several tool calls.

365
00:31:25,536 --> 00:31:25,776
D。
D.

366
00:31:26,350 --> 00:31:30,756
减少可用的工具数量，从而为输出留出更多预算。
Reduce the number of tools available so more of the budget is left for output.

367
00:31:31,246 --> 00:31:32,324
稍等一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

368
00:31:37,998 --> 00:31:39,376
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

369
00:31:40,206 --> 00:31:44,068
决定性的句子是“每一次尝试都以同样的方式失败”。
The deciding sentence is that every attempt fails the same way.

370
00:31:44,590 --> 00:31:46,884
这一行就排除了选项
That single line eliminates option.

371
00:31:47,598 --> 00:31:48,772
仅凭 A 是不够的。
A on its own.

372
00:31:49,294 --> 00:31:53,412
因为退避机制是针对瞬时故障的，而这种情况是确定性的。
Because back off is for transient failures, and this one is deterministic.

373
00:31:54,030 --> 00:31:57,936
每次发送相同的输入都会超出同样的预算。
The same input will overflow the same budget every time you send it.

374
00:31:58,478 --> 00:32:03,136
C 解决了实际的限制，而且后半句和前半句同样重要。
C fixes the actual constraint, and the second half matters as much as the first.

375
00:32:03,406 --> 00:32:06,564
增加预算可以解决那些刚好超出一点的合同。
Raising the budget helps the contracts that were just over.

376
00:32:07,086 --> 00:32:11,428
拆分则能处理那些会超出任何合理设置的预算的合同。
Splitting handles the ones that would overflow any budget you could reasonably set.

377
00:32:12,366 --> 00:32:17,124
选项 B 是一个危险的干扰项，因为它虽然能让错误消失。
Option B is the dangerous distractor because it makes the error go away.

378
00:32:17,646 --> 00:32:23,748
但它也放弃了记录系统所依赖的结构化输出，把明显的失败变成了隐蔽的失败。
It also abandons the structured output the record system depends on, turning a loud failure into a quiet one.

379
00:32:24,686 --> 00:32:29,136
选项 D 对标记压力有正确的直觉，但瞄错了限制点。
Option D has the right instinct about token pressure but aims it at the wrong limit.

380
00:32:29,422 --> 00:32:32,932
工具定义是输入端，最大标记数是输出端的上限。
Tool definitions are input and max tokens caps output.

381
00:32:34,638 --> 00:32:35,652
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

382
00:32:36,016 --> 00:32:38,276
一个支持智能体处理退货。
A support agent handles returns.

383
00:32:38,656 --> 00:32:44,580
它的工具包括获取客户、查询订单、处理退款和转接人工。
Its tools are get customer, lookup order, process refund, and escalate to human.

384
00:32:45,456 --> 00:32:47,940
一位客户询问如何退货。
A customer asks about returning an item.

385
00:32:48,656 --> 00:32:50,724
智能体调用“查询订单”。
The agent calls lookup order.

386
00:32:51,470 --> 00:32:58,372
结果显示该商品是 45 天前购买的，而系统提示词中的退货政策是 30 天。
The result shows the item was purchased 45 days ago against a 30-day return policy in the system prompt.

387
00:32:58,926 --> 00:33:05,124
一位同事问循环如何做出决定。即此时，是调用“处理退款”还是“转接人工”。
A colleague asks how the loop decides. At this point, whether to call process refund or escalate to human.

388
00:33:09,166 --> 00:33:10,948
这个决策是如何做出的？
How is that decision made?

389
00:33:11,886 --> 00:33:17,216
A. SDK 将工具结果与政策进行对比，并路由到正确的工具。
a The SDK compares the tool result against the policy and routes to the correct tool.

390
00:33:17,518 --> 00:33:22,896
B. 订单详情被添加到对话中，模型会推论该采取哪种行动。
B. The order details are added to the conversation and the model reasons about which action to take.

391
00:33:23,136 --> 00:33:28,164
C. 你的编排代码检查购买日期，并直接调用相应的工具。
C. Your orchestration code inspects the purchase date and calls the appropriate tool directly.

392
00:33:28,816 --> 00:33:29,136
D。
D.

393
00:33:29,710 --> 00:33:33,636
查询订单返回一个路由提示，从而决定下一次调用哪个工具。
Lookup order returns a routing hint that determines the next tool call.

394
00:33:34,382 --> 00:33:35,780
稍停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

395
00:33:41,488 --> 00:33:43,008
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

396
00:33:43,566 --> 00:33:48,420
之所以包含这个场景，是因为考试中会出现类似题目，而且人们往往会想得太复杂。
And this scenario is included because the exam asks a version of it and people overthink it.

397
00:33:48,688 --> 00:33:50,244
它看起来像是一个政策问题。
It looks like a policy question.

398
00:33:51,168 --> 00:33:54,404
但它其实是一个关于循环如何运作的定义性问题。
It is a definitional question about how the loop works.

399
00:33:55,310 --> 00:33:57,728
工具结果会被添加到对话中。
The tool result is appended to the conversation.

400
00:33:58,030 --> 00:34:03,012
模型会结合系统提示词中的政策来阅读它，并决定下一步该做什么。
The model reads it alongside the policy in the system prompt and it decides what to do next.

401
00:34:03,406 --> 00:34:05,156
这就是整个机制。
That is the entire mechanism.

402
00:34:07,470 --> 00:34:09,487
选项 A 虚构了一个功能。
Option A invents a capability.

403
00:34:09,728 --> 00:34:14,020
没有任何 SDK 会去读取你的业务规则。它只是传递消息并运行工具。
No SDK reads your business rules. It moves messages and runs tools.

404
00:34:14,574 --> 00:34:22,947
选项 C 作为一种设计并不算错，很多优秀的系统确实是这么做的。它描述的是一个工作流，而这个场景构建的是一个智能体。
Option C is not wrong as a design, and plenty of good systems do exactly that. It is a description of a workflow and the scenario built an agent.

405
00:34:23,630 --> 00:34:28,964
选项 D 会把决策放在工具内部，这就会消除在循环中加入模型的任何理由。
Option D would put the decision inside the tool, which removes the reason for having a model in the loop at all.

406
00:34:30,094 --> 00:34:34,500
注意看，这里的正确答案是列表中最合理的那个。
Notice how the right answer here is the least plever one on the list.

407
00:34:36,078 --> 00:34:40,260
场景 5，这是一个判断题，而不是诊断题。
Scenario 5, and this one is a judgment call rather than a diagnosis.

408
00:34:40,848 --> 00:34:45,603
一家媒体公司想要自动化处理进入的媒体查询的第一线分诊。
A media company wants to automate first-line triage of inbound press enquiries.

409
00:34:46,478 --> 00:34:54,340
大约 95% 的内容属于四个类别，这些类别目前已经由关键词规则正确分类，且每个类别都有固定的模板回复。
About 95% fall into four categories that a keyword rule already classifies correctly today, and each category has a fixed template reply.

410
00:34:54,688 --> 00:34:58,276
剩下的 5% 是真正异常的情况，会转交给人工处理。
The remaining 5% are genuinely unusual and go to a person.

411
00:34:59,054 --> 00:35:00,292
处理量很大，
Volume is high,

412
00:35:01,038 --> 00:35:06,852
延迟很重要，而且财务团队在询问为什么 AI 预算增加了。
latency matters, and the finance team is asking why the AI budget has grown.

413
00:35:07,598 --> 00:35:16,164
一名工程师建议用一个拥有分类、回复草稿和升级工具的智能体来替换整个系统。
An engineer proposes replacing the whole system with an agent that has tools for classification, replied rafting, and escalation.

414
00:35:17,102 --> 00:35:18,768
你应该给出什么建议？
What should you advise?

415
00:35:19,342 --> 00:35:24,868
A. 构建这个智能体，因为它可以在一个系统中处理常见情况和异常情况。
a Build the agent since it handles both the common and the unusual cases in one system.

416
00:35:25,328 --> 00:35:30,372
B. 保留针对那 95% 的规则，仅将未分类的剩余部分路由到模型。
B. Keep the rule for the 95% and route only the unclassified remainder to a module.

417
00:35:30,848 --> 00:35:35,716
C. 构建智能体，但设置最大轮数和最大预算来控制成本。
C. Build the agent but cap it with max turns and max budget to control cost.

418
00:35:36,494 --> 00:35:43,076
D. 用单次分类调用替换关键词规则，保留模板和人工升级。
D. Replace the keyword rule with a single classification call, keeping the templates and the human escalation.

419
00:35:44,174 --> 00:35:45,220
稍停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

420
00:35:50,766 --> 00:35:55,684
答案是 B，能够熟练地选出这个选项能帮你拿到实实在在的分数。
The answer is B, and getting comfortable choosing it is worth real marks.

421
00:35:56,174 --> 00:36:02,116
埋下的细节是，关键词规则已经能正确分类 95% 的流量了。
The planted detail is that a keyword rule already classifies 95% of traffic correctly.

422
00:36:02,542 --> 00:36:05,572
那里没出问题，所以不需要模型去处理。
Nothing is broken there, so nothing there needs a model.

423
00:36:06,382 --> 00:36:13,828
如果在这些流量前加一个智能体，就会给原本免费且正确的任务增加延迟和成本。
Put an agent in front of that traffic, and you have added latency and cost to work that was free and right.

424
00:36:14,448 --> 00:36:20,484
选项 C 是大多数人会选的，也是这页幻灯片上最有教育意义的错误答案。
Option C is the one most people land on, and it is the most instructive wrong answer on this slide.

425
00:36:21,006 --> 00:36:24,068
护栏只能限制一个本不该存在的设计的破坏性。
Caps limit the damage from a design that should not exist.

426
00:36:24,974 --> 00:36:27,328
它们不能让错误的架构变正确。
They do not make a wrong architecture right.

427
00:36:27,854 --> 00:36:33,060
一个在糟糕主意上提供 guardrails 的问题，是在测试你会不会接受这个主意。
A question that offers guardraise on a bad idea is testing whether you will accept the idea.

428
00:36:33,550 --> 00:36:36,452
选项 D 修补了一个没坏的东西。
Option D fixes something that is not broken.

429
00:36:37,262 --> 00:36:45,028
而选项 A 把单一系统称为更简单，这听起来像是好的架构，但实际上是在费很大劲来掩盖增加的成本。
And option A calls a single system simpler, which sounds like good architecture and is doing a lot of work to hide added cost.

430
00:36:47,086 --> 00:36:49,988
Module 2。接下来是任务分解。
Module 2. Next on task decomposition.

431
00:36:51,790 --> 00:36:52,608
Module 2。
Module 2.

432
00:36:52,878 --> 00:36:54,052
仍在领域 1。
Still in domain 1.

433
00:36:54,446 --> 00:36:57,124
上次我们确定了你是否需要使用智能体。
Last time we settled whether you need an agent at all.

434
00:36:57,646 --> 00:37:01,892
本模块假设你已经决定需要拆分工作，并探讨如何拆分。
This module assumes you have decided the work needs splitting up and asks how.

435
00:37:02,702 --> 00:37:04,608
这里有 5 种命名模式。
There are 5 name patterns.

436
00:37:04,768 --> 00:37:10,532
它们经常被混淆，而考试非常喜欢同时给出其中三种选项。
They get confused with each other constantly, and the exam is very fond of offering you three of them at once.

437
00:37:10,928 --> 00:37:17,252
到这章结束时，你应该能在读完选项之前，就从题干中辨认出正确的模式。
By the end of this, you should be able to name the right one from the question stem before you have finished reading the options.

438
00:37:18,958 --> 00:37:25,412
这是区分所有五种模式的轴，它比死记硬背五个名称更有价值。
Here is the axis that separates all five patterns, and it is worth more than memorizing the five names.

439
00:37:25,966 --> 00:37:30,244
问谁来写子任务列表，以及他们是什么时候写的。
Ask who writes the list of subtasks and ask when they write it.

440
00:37:30,958 --> 00:37:37,284
如果你在写代码时就写好了列表，那就是工作流，而哪种工作流取决于列表的形状。
If you wrote the list at the time you wrote the code, that is a workflow, and which workflow depends on the shape of the list.

441
00:37:38,062 --> 00:37:44,132
如果模型在任务运行时根据它刚刚看到的内容来生成列表，那就是智能体。
If the model writes the list while the task is running based on what it has just seen, that is an agent.

442
00:37:45,038 --> 00:37:46,848
其他情况都有详细说明。
Everything else is detailed.

443
00:37:47,182 --> 00:37:54,596
记住这个轴，这五个模式就不再是需要记忆的列表，而是带有点的维度。
Hold that axis in your head and the five patterns stop being a list to memorize and start being one dimension with points on it.

444
00:37:56,110 --> 00:37:58,980
这里是按该轴排序的五个模式。
Here are the five sorted along that axis.

445
00:37:59,502 --> 00:38:03,268
在提示词链中，你写好步骤，它们按固定顺序运行。
In prompt chaining, you write the steps and they run in a fixed order.

446
00:38:06,062 --> 00:38:12,548
在路由中，你写下几个列表，每个类别一个，模型只负责选择走哪个分支。
In routing, you write several lists, one per category, and the model only picks which branch to take.

447
00:38:13,998 --> 00:38:18,000
在并行化中，你写好列表，所有内容同时运行。
In parallelization, you write the list and everything runs at once.

448
00:38:18,542 --> 00:38:23,332
在编排工作者中，模型在运行时根据面前的输入来生成列表。
In Orchestrator Workers, the model writes the list at runtime, from the input in front of it.

449
00:38:23,822 --> 00:38:26,532
评估器优化在本质上是不同的。
An evaluator optimizer is different in kind.

450
00:38:27,694 --> 00:38:32,452
你知道步骤，但不知道它们会运行多少次，因为由一个裁判决定何时停止。
You know the steps, but not how many times they will run because a judge decides when to stop.

451
00:38:32,800 --> 00:38:36,240
注意，前三项是第一模块中所说的“工作流”。
Notice the top three are workflows in the sense from module one.

452
00:38:37,070 --> 00:38:40,292
只有第四项是直接交给模型处理的路径。
Only the fourth hands, the path to the model.

453
00:38:41,710 --> 00:38:48,868
提示词链将任务分解为一系列固定的调用，其中每一个步骤的工作范围都比整体更窄。
Prompt chaining decomposes a task into a fixed sequence of calls where each one does a narrower job than the whole.

454
00:38:49,294 --> 00:38:50,820
这种权衡是显而易见的。
The trade is explicit.

455
00:38:51,120 --> 00:38:57,572
你会增加更多次调用，整个过程也会变长，但每一次单独的调用都会变得更容易，因此也更准确。
You make more calls and the whole thing takes longer, but each individual call is easier and therefore more accurate.

456
00:38:58,350 --> 00:39:03,172
当你能够提前定义步骤，且每个步骤本身确实更简单时，就使用它。
Use it when you can name the steps in advance, and each step is genuinely simpler on its own.

457
00:39:03,470 --> 00:39:07,620
大家容易忽略的是中间的“门控”，这部分值得单独拿出来讲。
The piece people forget is the gate in the middle, which deserves its own slide.

458
00:39:09,198 --> 00:39:12,708
门控是你写在代码中、运行在步骤之间的检查点。
The gate is a check you write running between steps in your code.

459
00:39:13,006 --> 00:39:17,060
它可能用于验证架构，确认某个字段是否存在，或者去查询相关信息。
It might validate a schema, confirm a field is present, or look something up.

460
00:39:17,454 --> 00:39:24,100
有两个原因让它很有价值：它能阻止错误输出向下传递。所以第三步永远不会继承第二步的错误。
Two things make it valuable. It stops a bad output propagating. So step 3 never inherits step 2's mistake.

461
00:39:24,910 --> 00:39:26,960
而且它能为你提供可证明的覆盖范围。
And it gives you provable coverage.

462
00:39:27,246 --> 00:39:31,460
因为如果门控运行了，就说明该步骤已经执行过了，你可以这样告诉审计人员。
Because if the gate ran, then the step ran and you can tell an auditor that.

463
00:42:24,494 --> 00:42:27,940
这是考试中实际考查的机械细节。
Here is the mechanical detail the exam actually tests.

464
00:42:28,208 --> 00:42:35,140
协调者通过在单个助手响应中发出多个任务调用，来并发式地学习子代理。
A coordinator learns sub-agents concurrently by emitting several task calls inside a single assistant response.

465
00:42:35,408 --> 00:42:37,220
这就是它们之所以能并行的原因。
That is what makes them parallel.

466
00:42:37,870 --> 00:42:42,128
如果它发出一个任务调用，等待结果，然后再发出另一个。
If it emits one task call, waits for the result, then emits another.

467
00:42:42,350 --> 00:42:45,284
无论你的提示词怎么写，这种工作方式都是串行的。
The work is sequential, no matter what your prompt said.

468
00:42:45,568 --> 00:42:54,276
要求模型并行工作本身并不能产生并发，因为并发是消息结构的属性，而不是提示词内容的属性。
Asking a model to work in parallel does not by itself produce concurrency because concurrency is a property of the message shape rather than the freezing.

469
00:42:54,926 --> 00:42:56,804
还有一个需要记住的陷阱。
And one trap worth carrying forward.

470
00:42:57,486 --> 00:43:05,188
如果允许的工具列表不包含任务，协调者会思考如何委派，但最终永远不会去委派。
If the allowed tools list does not include task, the coordinator will reason about delegating and then never delegate.

471
00:43:05,710 --> 00:43:07,968
日志中不会出现任何错误。
No error appears in the logs.

472
00:43:09,326 --> 00:43:11,332
在继续之前，先说明一个明确的限制。
One honest limit before we move on.

473
00:43:11,662 --> 00:43:13,732
同时运行 12 个分析
Running 12 analyses concurrently

474
00:43:14,862 --> 00:43:18,052
而不是串行运行，能让用户等待的时间缩短到原来的约六分之一。
instead of sequentially makes the user wait about a twelfth as long.

475
00:43:19,568 --> 00:43:28,288
它并不会减少工作量，你仍然需要为 12 次分析付费，而且在实践中还会多一点，因为每个子代理都需要自己的框架上下文。
It does not reduce the work, you still pay for 12 analyses and in practice slightly more because each sub agent needs its own framing context.

476
00:43:28,814 --> 00:43:38,288
所以并行化是解决延迟问题的，而不是成本问题。如果题干说财务团队希望降低账单费用，那么“并行化”就是一个干扰项。
So parallelization answers latency questions and never cost questions. If a STEM says the finance team wants the bill reduced, parallelization is a distractor.

477
00:43:38,528 --> 00:43:43,396
如果它说一个关键案例耗时超过 3 分钟，那么“并行化”就是正确答案。
If it says a landmark case takes over 3 minutes, parallelization is the answer.

478
00:43:45,070 --> 00:43:50,468
编排工作者在图表上看起来像并行化，但其实是完全不同的东西。
Orchestrator workers looks like parallelization on a diagram and is a different thing entirely.

479
00:43:51,054 --> 00:44:00,548
一个核心模型读取实际请求，确定这项特定任务需要哪些子任务，进行委派，然后汇总返回的内容。
A central model reads the actual request, works out what subtasks this particular job needs, delegates them, and then synthesizes what comes back.

480
00:44:03,758 --> 00:44:07,088
这些子任务的列表并不是写在你的代码里的。
The list of subtasks is not written in your code.

481
00:44:07,534 --> 00:44:10,528
它是在运行时生成的，且针对每个输入都不一样。
It is produced at runtime and it differs for every input.

482
00:44:10,862 --> 00:44:12,836
最后那句话就是核心区别。
That last sentence is the whole distinction.

483
00:44:13,230 --> 00:44:18,404
这也是这个领域最容易混淆的一对概念，所以它有专门的一页幻灯片。
It is also the most commonly confused pair in this domain, so it gets a slide of its own.

484
00:44:19,694 --> 00:44:23,716
判定标准在底部，是一个单一问题。
The tiebreaker is at the bottom and it is a single question.

485
00:44:25,010 --> 00:44:28,228
你会先看到输入之前就写好子任务列表吗？
Would you write the list of subtasks before seeing the input?

486
00:44:29,102 --> 00:44:36,196
如果选“是”，那就是并行化，你应该在代码中保留这种可预测且可测试的分离。
If yes, you have parallelization and you should keep the split in your code where it is predictable and testable.

487
00:44:37,134 --> 00:44:44,740
如果选“否”，因为简单的请求需要一个工作节点而复杂的需要六个，那么你就需要编排器来做决策。
If no, because a simple request needs one worker and a complicated one needs six, then you need an orchestrator to decide.

488
00:44:45,486 --> 00:44:47,888
注意那些能揭示这一点的关键词。
Watch for the phrase that gives this away instance.

489
00:44:48,686 --> 00:44:52,612
“查询分发多样且不断演变”是编排器的术语。
Query distribution is diverse and evolving is orchestrator language.

490
00:44:53,358 --> 00:44:59,204
“文档包含12个先例”是并行化的术语。
The document contains 12 precedents, is parallelization language.

491
00:45:00,526 --> 00:45:02,884
在白板上，架构是一样的。
Same architecture on a whiteboard.

492
00:45:03,182 --> 00:45:05,220
但在考试中，答案是不一样的。
Different answer on the exam.

493
00:45:06,926 --> 00:45:10,308
评估器优化是在循环中加入一个评论者。
Evaluator optimizer puts a critic in the loop.

494
00:45:10,702 --> 00:45:16,036
第一次调用生成候选结果，第二次调用根据你设定的标准进行评估。
One call generates a candidate and a second evaluates it against criteria you stated.

495
00:45:16,846 --> 00:45:22,500
评论者提供反馈，如此循环往复，直到评估器满意或达到上限为止。
The critic feeds back and round it goes until the evaluator is satisfied or you hit a cap.

496
00:45:23,470 --> 00:45:29,156
这是五种模式中唯一一种在编写时无法确定将进行多少次调用的。
It is the only one of the five where you do not know at author time how many calls you will make.

497
00:45:30,062 --> 00:45:32,608
这就是为什么它始终需要一个上限的原因。
That is exactly why it always needs a cap.

498
00:45:33,518 --> 00:45:37,568
如果没有限制，你就造出了一个直到你的预算耗尽才会停止的东西。
Without one, you have built something that can run until your budget notices.

499
00:45:39,278 --> 00:45:42,212
在引入评论者之前，必须满足两个条件。
Two conditions have to hold before a critic is worth it.

500
00:45:42,528 --> 00:45:49,008
你必须能够明确判定标准，因为如果没有具体内容可查，评估器只会产生一些讨好人的废话。
You must be able to state the criteria because an evaluator with nothing concrete to check just produces agreeable noise.

501
00:45:49,328 --> 00:45:55,620
而且迭代必须有明显的帮助，也就是说第二稿确实更好，且你能证明这一点。
And iteration must measurably help, meaning a second draft really is better and you can demonstrate it.

502
00:45:56,334 --> 00:46:05,540
在两种情况下，它不是正确的工具：当确定性检查即可满足时，因为架构验证器或测试套件更便宜且不会产生争议。
Two situations where it is a wrong tool. When a deterministic check would do, because a schema validator or a test suite is cheaper and cannot be argued with.

503
00:46:06,222 --> 00:46:13,380
以及当同一个模型在相同上下文中对自己的工作进行评分时，这不叫评估，这叫共识。
And when it is the same model grading its own work in the same context, which is not evaluation, it is agreement.

504
00:46:14,288 --> 00:46:20,836
这对应了模块1中的验证顺序，考试内容在这方面是一致的。
This mirrors the verification ordering from module 1, and the exam is consistent about it.

505
00:46:22,286 --> 00:46:26,212
有时没有固定的模式适用，而题干会明确告诉你。
Sometimes no fixed pattern fits, and the stem tells you plainly.

506
00:46:27,918 --> 00:46:31,300
工程师还没有指定要优先处理哪些模块。
The engineer has not specified which modules to prioritize.

507
00:46:32,014 --> 00:46:36,804
通过路由、中间件、业务逻辑和数据库来追踪这个错误。
Trace this error through routing, middleware, business logic, and the database.

508
00:46:37,710 --> 00:46:41,216
代码库有800个文件，而且没人读过它们。
The code base has 800 files and nobody has read them.

509
00:46:41,806 --> 00:46:46,576
在所有这些情况下，你接下来看什么都取决于你刚刚发现了什么。
In every one of those, what you look at next depends on what you just found.

510
00:46:46,736 --> 00:46:49,696
所以任何人都无法提前写好列表。
So no list can be written in advance by anyone.

511
00:46:49,856 --> 00:46:54,244
那就是让智能体在探索过程中生成自己的子任务。
That is when you let the agent generate its own subtasks as it explores.

512
00:46:54,736 --> 00:46:59,776
给它工具，给它轮数限制，并给它一个外部标准来核对。
Give it tools, give it a turn limit, and give it something external to check against.

513
00:47:00,336 --> 00:47:05,156
不要强行把这五种模式中的一种套用到真正开放式的任务上。
Do not force one of the five patterns onto genuinely open-ended work.

514
00:47:06,798 --> 00:47:10,816
存在一种折中方案，考试题目喜欢这种，但考生往往会忽略它。
There is a middle ground that exam questions like and candidates forget.

515
00:47:11,056 --> 00:47:16,644
固定的链式调用能提供可证明的覆盖范围，但在结构上对你写出的步骤之外的内容视而不见。
A fixed chain gives you provable coverage but is structurally blind to anything outside the steps you wrote.

516
00:47:17,358 --> 00:47:26,372
例如，HAPER 文件审查无法发现仅存在于两个文件交互中的错误，无论提示词写得多么好。
HAPER file review, for instance, cannot see a bug that only exists in the interaction between two files, no matter how good the prompt is.

517
00:47:26,862 --> 00:47:29,610
无限制的智能体能看到它，但可能会跑题。
An unbounded agent can see it but might wander.

518
00:47:30,542 --> 00:47:33,540
介于两者之间的是有轮数限制的智能体任务。
In between sits the turn limited agentic task.

519
00:47:34,350 --> 00:47:38,736
模型获得了工具，因此它可以读取文件并搜索代码库。
The model gets tools, so it can read files and search the code base.

520
00:47:39,918 --> 00:47:44,644
它会跟随线索走到任何地方，但仅限固定的轮数。
It follows the thread wherever it goes, but only for a fixed number of turns.

521
00:47:45,230 --> 00:47:50,148
这种模式作为正确答案出现的频率比它的名气还要高。
That shape shows up as a correct answer more often than its reputation suggests.

522
00:47:51,886 --> 00:47:58,468
分解并非免费，了解其成本是识别题目是否提供过多分解的关键。
Decomposition is not free and knowing its cost is how you recognize when a question is offering you too much of it.

523
00:48:00,558 --> 00:48:04,932
每一个边界都是一次往返，除非各部分是并发执行的，否则延迟会增加。
Every boundary is a round trip, so latency grows unless the pieces are concurrent.

524
00:48:05,838 --> 00:48:09,604
每个部分都需要自己的框架上下文，因此 token 也会增加。
Every piece needs framing context of its own, so tokens grow too.

525
00:48:10,656 --> 00:48:17,508
信息会在衔接处丢失，因为第二步没传递的内容，第三步根本无法使用。
Information gets lost at the seams because whatever step 2 does not pass along, step 3 simply cannot use.

526
00:48:17,856 --> 00:48:19,524
而且调试也会变得更难。
And debugging gets harder.

527
00:48:19,856 --> 00:48:25,412
因为六个组件各自失败很少会累加成一个系统频繁故障。
Since six components each failing rarely add up to one system, failing regularly.

528
00:48:26,096 --> 00:48:30,948
衔接处是最昂贵的，而领域 5 的大部分内容就是关于修复这些衔接的。
The seams are the expensive one, and most of domain 5 is about repairing them.

529
00:48:31,950 --> 00:48:38,148
只有当某个步骤独立执行时真正变得更容易时才进行分解，而不是因为架构图看起来更酷。
Decompose when a step is genuinely easier alone, not because the architecture diagram looks more impressive.

530
00:48:39,534 --> 00:48:43,556
这张表是该模块的浓缩版，值得停下来看一下。
This table is the module in one screen and it is worth pausing on.

531
00:48:44,238 --> 00:48:49,828
左侧的每个短语都会出现在题干中，且每一个都指向特定的一个模式。
Each phrase on the left appears in exam stems and each one points at exactly one pattern.

532
00:48:50,734 --> 00:48:53,444
每次都是相同的三个步骤，意味着链式调用。
The same three steps every time means chaining.

533
00:48:54,894 --> 00:48:59,776
我们无法判断一个步骤是否运行，这也意味着链式调用，特别是针对门控。
We cannot tell if a step ran means chaining as well, specifically for the gate.

534
00:49:00,686 --> 00:49:04,932
优化一条路径会损害另一条路径，意味着路由或拆分提示词。
Tuning one path degrades another means routing or split prompts.

535
00:49:05,422 --> 00:49:08,004
这些任务是独立的，意味着分区。
These tasks are independent means sectioning.

536
00:49:10,222 --> 00:49:13,060
我们总是漏掉真正的问题，意味着投票机制。
We keep missing genuine issues means voting.

537
00:49:13,776 --> 00:49:17,444
多样且不断变化的查询分布，意味着编排器。
Diverse and evolving query distribution means an orchestrator.

538
00:49:18,638 --> 00:49:22,468
并且取决于它在每一步中发现的内容，意味着智能体任务。
And depends on what it discovers at each step means agentic.

539
00:49:23,374 --> 00:49:28,900
大多数题目只埋入其中一个点，在阅读选项前就找出来能帮你节省一分钟。
Most questions plant exactly one of these, and finding it before you read the option saves you a minute.

540
00:49:30,286 --> 00:49:32,096
接下来是 5 行核心要点。
5 lines to carry forward.

541
00:49:32,494 --> 00:49:38,340
询问谁在什么时间编写子任务列表，因为这个维度区分了本模块中的所有模式。
Ask who writes the subtask list and when, because that one axis separates every pattern in this module.

542
00:49:38,816 --> 00:49:43,460
对于固定的步骤使用链式调用，并记住门控往往是选择它的真正原因。
Use chaining for fixed steps, and remember the gate is often the real reason to choose it.

543
00:49:44,846 --> 00:49:48,836
独立意味着为了速度采用分段并行，并为了召回率采用投票机制。
Independent means parallel with sectioning for speed and voting for recall.

544
00:49:49,780 --> 00:49:56,356
并行化是拆分你写好的列表，而编排器是在运行时根据输入来生成列表。
Parallelization splits a list you wrote, While an orchestrator writes the list at runtime from the input.

545
00:49:56,656 --> 00:50:02,788
而且并行性能节省墙钟时间，但永远不能降低成本。所以它只适用于回答延迟相关的问题。
And parallelism buys wall clock time and never buys cost. So it answers latency questions only.

546
00:50:03,438 --> 00:50:04,804
现在有 7 个场景。
7 scenarios now.

547
00:50:05,776 --> 00:50:11,652
其中几个会同时给你三个模式供选择，这正是考试的考法。
Several of them put three patterns in front of you at once, which is exactly what the exam does.

548
00:50:13,326 --> 00:50:14,244
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

549
00:50:14,766 --> 00:50:21,732
一个法律研究系统通过协调者将文档分析任务分派给子代理，来分析法院判决。
A legal research system analyses court judgments with a coordinator delegating document analysis to a subagent.

550
00:50:22,176 --> 00:50:24,964
普通案例大约需要 15 秒。
An ordinary case takes about 15 seconds.

551
00:50:25,710 --> 00:50:33,540
引用 12 个先例的里程碑式判决需要 3 分钟以上，因为子代理是一个接一个地处理它们。
A landmark judgment citing 12 precedents takes over 3 minutes because the subagent works through them one after another.

552
00:50:34,096 --> 00:50:36,004
用户放弃了请求。
Users abandon the request.

553
00:50:36,974 --> 00:50:45,540
团队希望降低延迟，但协调者仍必须能够监控进度，并在单个先例分析出错时进行调试。
The team wants the latency down, but the coordinator must still be able to monitor progress and debug individual precedent analysis when they go wrong.

554
00:50:46,254 --> 00:50:47,936
最有效的改进是什么？
What is the most effective change?

555
00:50:48,176 --> 00:50:53,252
a. 让单个子代理在一个更大的提示词中处理所有 12 个先例。
a Have the single subagent process all 12 precedents in one larger prompt.

556
00:50:54,062 --> 00:50:54,336
b。
b.

557
00:50:54,862 --> 00:51:01,508
让协调者生成并行分析的子智能体，每个处理一部分，然后进行汇总。
Have the coordinator spawn parallel analysis subagents, each handling a subset, then aggregate.

558
00:51:01,966 --> 00:51:07,140
c. 分析引用最多的三个先例，并注明其余内容被省略。
C. Analyze the three most cited precedents and note that the rest were omitted.

559
00:51:07,616 --> 00:51:07,856
B。
B.

560
00:51:08,176 --> 00:51:11,216
将分析移至消息批处理中。
Move the analysis to the message batches.

561
00:51:12,078 --> 00:51:13,764
使用 API 以降低成本。
API to reduce cost.

562
00:51:14,126 --> 00:51:15,204
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

563
00:51:20,622 --> 00:51:22,352
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

564
00:51:22,958 --> 00:51:29,348
先例之间互不依赖，所以这是分段处理，而且 12 个并发分析所需的时间与一个差不多。
Precedents do not depend on one another, so this is sectioning, and 12 concurrent analyses take roughly as long as one.

565
00:51:29,998 --> 00:51:35,012
但看看这个问题的构造方式，它有两个约束条件，第二个才是有趣的。
But look at how the question is built because it has two constraints, and the second is the interesting one.

566
00:51:36,334 --> 00:51:39,072
选项 A 确实解决了延迟问题。
Option A genuinely fixes the latency.

567
00:51:49,518 --> 00:51:58,564
关于监控和调试单个先例分析的句子是为了排除掉这个选项，因为合并后的单一提示词只会给出一个不透明的结果。
The sentence about monitoring and debugging individual precedent analysis is there to eliminate it because a single merged prompt gives you one opaque result.

568
00:51:59,072 --> 00:52:04,836
选项 C 通过不做工作来解决时间问题，但在法律工具中，这比慢还要糟糕。
Option C fixes the timing by not doing the work, which in a legal tool is worse than being slow.

569
00:52:05,646 --> 00:52:10,692
选项 D 回答了一个没人问的成本问题，而且批处理会让等待时间变长。
Option D answers a cost question nobody asked, and batch would make the wait longer.

570
00:52:12,142 --> 00:52:14,308
场景 2：生产环境。
Scenario 2 A production.

571
00:52:19,534 --> 00:52:23,300
API 返回不规律的 500 错误。
AP I returns intermittent 500 errors.

572
00:52:23,886 --> 00:52:32,272
原因可能出在请求路由、中间件、业务逻辑或数据库层，但没人知道具体在哪。
The cause could be in request routing, in middleware, in the business logic or in the database layer, and nobody knows which.

573
00:52:32,686 --> 00:52:36,512
一名工程师要求一个带有代码工具的智能体去找出问题。
An engineer asks an agent with code-based tools to find it.

574
00:52:37,070 --> 00:52:41,604
一位同事建议将调查过程硬编码为四个固定的步骤。
A colleague proposes hard coding the investigation as four fixed steps.

575
00:52:42,062 --> 00:52:48,004
检查路由，然后是中间件，接着是业务逻辑，最后是数据库。
Check routing, then middleware, then business logic, then the database.

576
00:52:52,686 --> 00:52:56,132
哪种任务分解方法最有效？
What task decomposition approach is most effective?

577
00:52:56,526 --> 00:53:03,524
a. 让智能体根据每一步发现的情况动态生成调查子任务。
a Have the agent generate investigation subtasks dynamically based on what it finds at each step.

578
00:53:03,982 --> 00:53:04,192
b.
b.

579
00:53:04,592 --> 00:53:08,036
按顺序将这四个固定的层级检查作为提示词链来运行。
Run the four fixed layer checks as a prompt chain in order.

580
00:53:09,006 --> 00:53:12,868
C. 并行运行这四个层的检查并汇总结果。
C. Run the four layer checks in parallel and aggregate the findings.

581
00:53:13,454 --> 00:53:18,340
D. 根据 HTTP 状态码将错误路由到专门的子代理。
D. Route the error to a specialized subagent based on the HTTP status code.

582
00:53:18,958 --> 00:53:20,132
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

583
00:53:25,838 --> 00:53:27,072
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

584
00:53:27,312 --> 00:53:30,820
这个场景是故意与模块 1 中的一个场景配对的。
And this scenario is deliberately paired with one from module 1.

585
00:53:31,392 --> 00:53:33,956
在那里，一个拉取请求审查也做了同样的操作。
There, a pull request review did the same.

586
00:53:34,272 --> 00:53:37,828
每次进行三个独立的检查并使用提示词链是正确的。
Three independent checks every time and prompt chaining was correct.

587
00:53:38,798 --> 00:53:42,724
这里的结构看起来很相似，也是四个层级名称，但链式调用是错误的。
Here the shape looks similar, four name layers and chaining is wrong.

588
00:53:43,712 --> 00:53:45,508
区别在于依赖关系。
The difference is dependency.

589
00:53:46,432 --> 00:53:48,452
调试是基于发现驱动的。
Debugging is discovery driven.

590
00:53:49,134 --> 00:53:57,220
在中间件中发现的堆栈追踪会改变你要去查看哪个数据库调用，没有任何作者能提前写好那部分内容。
A stack trace found in middleware changes which database call you go and look at, and no author can write that part in advance.

591
00:53:59,278 --> 00:54:08,432
选项 B 孤立地检查四个层级，无法在它们之间跟踪线索，而且在找到答案时也无法提前停止。
Option B checks four layers in isolation and cannot follow a thread between them and it cannot stop early when it finds the answer.

592
00:54:08,974 --> 00:54:11,792
选项 C 让这种盲目性变得更快。
Option C makes the same blindness faster.

593
00:54:12,206 --> 00:54:15,172
并行处理只会让分解变快，而不会变得更聪明。
Parallel makes a decomposition quicker, never smarter.

594
00:54:15,552 --> 00:54:21,316
选项 D 没有可分类的依据，因为 500 只告诉你出了问题，没告诉你出在哪。
Option D has nothing to classify on because a 500 tells you something failed and not where.

595
00:54:23,022 --> 00:54:31,952
场景 3 A 研究协调者将任务委派给一个网络搜索子代理和一个文档分析子代理。两者都不需要对方的输出。
Scenario 3 A research coordinator delegates to a web search sub agent and a document analysis subagent. Neither needs the other's output.

596
00:54:32,142 --> 00:54:35,684
它们阅读不同的来源，之后再合并他们的发现。
They read different sources and their findings are merged afterwards.

597
00:54:36,622 --> 00:54:44,068
追踪显示协调者发出网络搜索的任务调用，等待结果，然后发出文档分析的任务调用。
Traces show the coordinator emits a task call for web search, waits for the result, then emits a task call for document analysis.

598
00:54:44,462 --> 00:54:46,084
总耗时是两者的总和。
Total time is the sum of both.

599
00:54:46,894 --> 00:54:51,396
系统提示词已经指示协调者并行运行独立的调研。
The system prompt already instructs the coordinator to run independent research in parallel.

600
00:54:52,032 --> 00:54:55,460
系统应该如何修改才能并发运行这些任务？
How should the system be changed to run these concurrently?

601
00:54:55,854 --> 00:55:02,308
a. 强化系统提示词指令，强调并行执行是必须的而非可选的。
a strengthen the system prompt instruction, adding that parallel execution is required rather than optional.

602
00:55:02,766 --> 00:55:07,716
b. 让协调者在单条响应消息中同时发出两个任务调用。
b. Structure the coordinator to emit both task calls in a single response message.

603
00:55:08,462 --> 00:55:08,752
C。
C.

604
00:55:09,262 --> 00:55:13,872
将两个子代理合并为一个，以便在单次处理中完成搜索和分析。
Merge the two sub agents into one that searches an analysis in a single pass.

605
00:55:14,510 --> 00:55:19,524
d. 增加最大轮数，给协调者留出足够的空间来发出两个调用。
D. Raise max turns so the coordinator has room to issue both calls.

606
00:55:21,582 --> 00:55:22,820
稍等，我们来做决定。
Pause and decide.

607
00:55:28,270 --> 00:55:30,016
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

608
00:55:30,656 --> 00:55:34,084
隐藏的考点是场景描述的最后一句话。
The planted detail is the last sentence of the scenario.

609
00:55:34,862 --> 00:55:39,780
系统提示词中已有相关指令，但实际表现仍不正确。
The system prompt already contains the instruction and the behavior is still wrong.

610
00:55:40,590 --> 00:55:50,404
每当题干提到指令已存在但执行不严谨时，这句话的作用就是排除掉那些试图去优化或重写指令的选项。
Whenever a stem tells you the instruction exists and is being followed loosely, that sentence exists to eliminate every option that writes a better instruction.

611
00:55:51,214 --> 00:55:55,844
选项 A 就是那种情况，也是大多数人的首选。
Option A is that option and it is the one most people pick.

612
00:55:56,576 --> 00:56:03,876
并发源于单条助手响应中同时出现两个工具调用。因此，这是消息本身的特性，而非强调强度的体现。
Concurrency comes from two tool calls appearing in a single assistant response. So it is a property of the message and not of emphasis.

613
00:56:04,496 --> 00:56:13,056
选项 C 虽然通过移除架构解决了表面问题，但也破坏了支撑双子代理架构的上下文隔离。
Option C makes the symptom disappear by deleting the architecture and it also destroys the context isolation that made two subagents worth having.

614
00:56:13,582 --> 00:56:18,340
选项 D 解决了一个根本没成瓶颈的限制，因为这两个调用原本就是并行发出的。
Option D fixes a constraint that was never binding since both calls were issued.

615
00:56:21,486 --> 00:56:22,500
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

616
00:56:23,086 --> 00:56:25,892
一个研究助理负责处理多种不同类型的工作任务。
A research assistant serves a mixed workload.

617
00:56:26,286 --> 00:56:28,612
有些查询只是简单的单行事实核实。
Some queries are one-line factual lookups.

618
00:56:28,896 --> 00:56:33,764
而其他的则需要联网搜索、文档分析以及整合来自十多个源头的综合信息。
Others need web search, document analysis, and synthesis across a dozen sources.

619
00:56:34,096 --> 00:56:38,436
随着用户挖掘出更多新玩法，各种不同类型的查询层出不穷。
New kinds of query keep appearing as users find new uses for the tool.

620
00:56:39,406 --> 00:56:43,492
目前，每一个查询都需要跑完完整的 4 个子代理流水线。
Today, every query runs the full 4 Subagent pipeline.

621
00:56:43,696 --> 00:56:48,388
所以简单的查询也要耗费 40 秒，而且成本和复杂的查询一样高。
So simple lookups take 40 seconds and cost as much as complex ones.

622
00:56:49,294 --> 00:56:52,484
处理这些不同复杂度要求的最佳方案是什么？
What is the most effective way to handle the varying complexity?

623
00:56:53,518 --> 00:56:59,684
a. 增加长度阈值。这样字数少于 15 个的查询就会直接进入单次调用。
a add a length threshold. So queries under 15 words skip straight to a single call.

624
00:57:00,496 --> 00:57:00,816
b。
b.

625
00:57:01,102 --> 00:57:05,380
b. 构建两条固定的流水线（简单型和复杂型），并根据关键词匹配进行分流。
Build two fixed pipelines, simple and complex, and root by keyword match.

626
00:57:06,016 --> 00:57:11,108
c. 让协调者去评估每个查询，并决定该调用哪些子代理。
C. Have the coordinator assess each query and decide which subagents to invoke for it.

627
00:57:11,598 --> 00:57:14,564
d. 同时并行运行全部四个子代理。
D. Run all four subagents in parallel.

628
00:57:15,182 --> 00:57:17,412
这样即便复杂查询也能快速返回结果。
So even complex queries return quickly.

629
00:57:17,998 --> 00:57:19,172
稍等，我们来做决定。
Pause and decide.

630
00:57:24,782 --> 00:57:29,668
正确答案是 C，而选项 B 是那个容易让人产生困惑的陷阱题。
The answer is C and option B is the one worth arguing with.

631
00:57:30,096 --> 00:57:34,576
采用关键词路由的两个固定流水线是一个非常合理的架构设计。
Two fixed pipelines with keyword routing is a perfectly good design.

632
00:57:34,896 --> 00:57:40,416
在类别稳定的系统中，这种设计在成本和可预测性上优于编排器。
In a system with stable categories, it would beat an orchestrator on cost and predictability.

633
00:57:40,656 --> 00:57:44,868
导致这个方案失败的词是「不断出现的新查询类型」。
The phrase that kills it is that new kinds of query keep appearing.

634
00:57:45,678 --> 00:57:52,580
你今天写的任何关键词列表到下个月就过时了，而且每种新查询类型都会在不知不觉中进入错误的路径。
Any keyword list you write today is out of date next month, and every new query type silently takes the wrong branch.

635
00:57:53,806 --> 00:58:00,356
「多样化且不断演变」是编排器的语言，因为子任务列表必须来自查询，而不是从你的代码中产生。
Diverse and evolving is orchestrator language because the subtask list has to come from the query rather than from your code.

636
00:58:00,846 --> 00:58:06,896
选项 A 用长度作为复杂度的代称，并对比所有的 EUA。
Option A uses length as a proxy for complexity and compare all EUA.

637
00:58:07,296 --> 00:58:10,468
我草稿里有六个词，而且需要包含所有内容。
I ag drafts is six words and needs everything.

638
00:58:10,976 --> 00:58:11,616
选项
Option

639
00:58:13,518 --> 00:58:19,524
D 在不增加成本的情况下降低了延迟，并且仍运行三个子智能体。根本不需要查表。
D cuts latency without cutting cost and still runs three sub agents. A lookup never needed.

640
00:58:21,134 --> 00:58:22,148
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

641
00:58:22,734 --> 00:58:27,216
对拉取请求中的每个更改文件进行自动审查。
An automated review runs on each change file in a pull request.

642
00:58:27,502 --> 00:58:31,396
针对每个文件进行一次调用，包含文件内容和相关的标准。
One call per file with the file contents and the teen standards.

643
00:58:32,494 --> 00:58:34,916
它在处理单文件问题时表现良好。
It performs well on single file issues.

644
00:58:35,790 --> 00:58:43,300
但评估发现，跨文件的错误占到了经过审查的拉取请求中生产事故的 35%。
But an evaluation finds that cross-file bugs account for 35% of production incidents from reviewed pull requests.

645
00:58:44,334 --> 00:58:46,436
这种审查几乎无法发现这些错误。
The review catches almost none of them.

646
00:58:47,854 --> 00:58:51,556
例如在签名更改后未更新的调用者
Examples are a caller not updated after a signature change

647
00:58:52,206 --> 00:58:55,216
或者两个模块之间断裂的契约。
or a contract broken between two modules.

648
00:58:55,822 --> 00:58:58,564
对审查设计最有效的改进是什么？
What is the most effective change to the review design?

649
00:59:00,142 --> 00:59:05,124
a. 在每个单文件审查调用中包含所有更改文件的内容。
a Include every change files contents in each per file review call.

650
00:59:05,646 --> 00:59:12,196
b. 将其重新设计为一个限制轮次的智能体任务，模型可以读取文件并搜索代码库。
b. Redesign it as a turn-limited agentic task where the model can read files and search the code base.

651
00:59:13,070 --> 00:59:13,376
C。
C.

652
00:59:13,934 --> 00:59:18,308
在系统提示词中添加指令，要求在审查每个文件时考虑跨文件的影响。
Add a system prompt instruction to consider cross file impacts when reviewing each file.

653
00:59:19,616 --> 00:59:19,856
D。
D.

654
00:59:20,430 --> 00:59:24,612
增加第二个针对每个文件的处理步骤，专门关注跨文件问题。
Add a second per file pass focused specifically on crossfile concerns.

655
00:59:26,286 --> 00:59:27,620
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

656
00:59:33,358 --> 00:59:45,392
答案是 B。核心思路是这种分解在结构上是盲目的，而不是提示词写得不好。当你的工作单元是一个文件时，两个文件之间的错误不可能出现在任何一个单位中。
The answer is B. The key idea is that this decomposition is structurally blind rather than badly prompted. When your unit of work is one file, a bug between two files cannot appear inside any unit.

657
00:59:45,614 --> 00:59:47,632
无论怎么修改指令都无法改变这一点。
No amount of instruction changes that.

658
00:59:47,872 --> 00:59:50,212
选项 C 是最明显的例证。
Option C is the clearest illustration.

659
00:59:50,958 --> 00:59:54,112
在调用时，物理上并没有另一个文件在它面前。
The call physically does not have the other file in front of it.

660
00:59:54,446 --> 00:59:58,948
让它去考虑跨文件的影响，是要求它去推理那些它根本看不到的东西。
Telling it to consider cross file impact asks it to reason about something it cannot see.

661
00:59:59,598 --> 01:00:02,564
选项 B 对同样的盲区付出了双倍代价。
Option B pays twice for the same blindness.

662
01:00:03,502 --> 01:00:06,272
选项 A 是一个考虑周全但错误的答案。
Option A is the thoughtful wrong answer.

663
01:00:06,766 --> 01:00:12,644
包含每一个变更文件在很大程度上是有帮助的，直到巨大的拉取请求耗尽上下文窗口为止。
Including every change file does help until a large pull request exhausts the context window.

664
01:00:12,832 --> 01:00:15,844
它仍然会漏掉那些不属于变更范围的调用者。
It also still misses callers that were not part of the change.

665
01:00:16,352 --> 01:00:23,844
选项 B 让模型能够顺着特征追踪到任何使用它的地方，包括未变动的文件，而轮数限制则能确保其在范围内。
Option B lets the model follow a signature to wherever it is used, including untouched files, and the turn limit keeps it bounded.

666
01:00:25,326 --> 01:00:26,592
场景 6。
Scenario 6.

667
01:00:26,912 --> 01:00:34,052
一名研究协调者刚刚完成了一个完整的流水线，并将其所有发现保存在上下文中。它返回了一份报告。
A research coordinator has just completed a full pipeline and holds all the findings in its context. It returns a report.

668
01:00:34,670 --> 01:00:36,992
用户随后提出了三个简短的后续问题。
The user then asks three short follow-ups.

669
01:00:37,262 --> 01:00:39,652
用两句话概括第二部分。
Summarize the second section in two sentences.

670
01:00:40,112 --> 01:00:41,636
哪个来源提到了这一点？
Which source said that?

671
01:00:42,542 --> 01:00:45,444
并为非技术读者重写结论。
And revert the conclusion for a non-technical reader.

672
01:00:46,030 --> 01:00:51,876
目前每个后续问题都会生成一个全新的综合子代理，在回答之前重新阅读这些发现。
Each follow-up currently spawns a fresh synthesis subagent which rereads the findings before answering.

673
01:00:52,590 --> 01:00:56,356
用户抱怨这些后续问题的响应速度比原始报告还要慢。
Users complain the follow-ups are slower than the original report was.

674
01:00:56,878 --> 01:01:00,196
提高后续问题响应时间最有效的方法是什么？
What is the most effective way to improve follow-up response time?

675
01:01:01,134 --> 01:01:06,788
a. 让协调者直接从现有的上下文中回答简单的后续问题。
a Have the coordinator answer straightforward follow-ups directly from its existing context.

676
01:01:07,246 --> 01:01:07,472
b。
b.

677
01:01:07,918 --> 01:01:12,352
c. 缓存综合子代理的输出，以便从缓存中提供重复请求的服务。
Cache the synthesis subagents output so repeat requests are served from cache.

678
01:01:12,846 --> 01:01:17,380
d. 为所有三个后续问题并行生成综合子代理。
C. Spawn the synthesis subagents for all three follow-ups in parallel.

679
01:01:17,934 --> 01:01:23,332
e. 在生成子代理时传递简化的摘要，而不是完整的发现内容。
D. Pass a condensed summary rather than the full findings when spawning the subagent.

680
01:01:24,718 --> 01:01:26,180
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

681
01:01:31,790 --> 01:01:37,156
答案是 A，之所以包含它是因为考试奖励那些知道何时不需要委派任务的知识点。
The answer is A and it is included because the exam rewards knowing when not to delegate.

682
01:01:37,552 --> 01:01:45,732
协调者已经把这些发现保存在上下文中了。为了去读取你当前正持有内容而生成一个子代理纯属多余开销。
The coordinator already has the findings in its context. Spawning a subagent to read read what you are currently holding is pure overhead.

683
01:01:46,574 --> 01:01:49,632
这就是为什么后续问题的处理比报告本身还要慢的原因。
That is why the follow-ups are slower than the report itself.

684
01:01:50,254 --> 01:02:00,452
选项 C 是给那些刚学过并行化的人设下的陷阱，因为三个同时运行的无用子代理依然是三个无用的子代理。
Option C is the trap for anyone who has just learned about parallelization because three unnecessary subagents running concurrently are still three unnecessary subagents.

685
01:02:01,152 --> 01:02:08,324
选项 B 误判了情况，因为每个后续问题都是不同的问题，没有任何重复内容可以缓存。
Option B misreads the situation since each follow-up is a different question and there is nothing repeated to cache.

686
01:02:09,262 --> 01:02:16,932
选项 D 让错误的运算变便宜了，同时却丢失了关于来源问题的关键细节。
Option D makes the wrong operation cheaper while losing exactly the detail that the question about sources needs.

687
01:02:18,670 --> 01:02:24,228
将子代理保留给那些需要隔离或新上下文容量的工作。
Reserve subagents for work that needs isolation or fresh context capacity.

688
01:02:25,806 --> 01:02:26,916
场景 7。
Scenario 7.

689
01:02:27,470 --> 01:02:34,276
一次安全扫描审查合并的代码，检查注入缺陷、不安全的反序列化以及密钥泄露。
A security scan reviews merged code for injection flaws, unsafe deserialization, and secret leakage.

690
01:02:34,752 --> 01:02:40,708
单次调优良好的扫描能找出约 70% 的问题，这些问题随后被人工审计员确认。
A single well-tuned pass finds about 70% of the issues a human auditor later confirms.

691
01:02:41,614 --> 01:02:43,712
团队的优先目标是召回率。
The team's priority is recall.

692
01:02:44,622 --> 01:02:47,072
漏掉一个漏洞的代价很高。
A missed vulnerability is expensive.

693
01:02:47,502 --> 01:02:54,116
他们有足够的审核人力来处理误报，而且由于扫描是每晚运行一次，延迟不是问题。
They have spare reviewer capacity to triage false positives, and latency is not a concern because the scan runs nightly.

694
01:02:55,470 --> 01:02:57,348
哪种改变最能提高召回率？
What change most improves recall?

695
01:02:57,712 --> 01:03:02,212
a. 用不同的提示词多次运行扫描，并取所有结果的并集。
a run the scan several times with different framings and take the union of findings.

696
01:03:03,232 --> 01:03:06,272
b. 将扫描分为三个连续的步骤。
b. Split the scan into three sequential steps.

697
01:03:06,432 --> 01:03:08,272
每类漏洞对应一个步骤。
One per vulnerability class.

698
01:03:08,592 --> 01:03:13,508
c. 添加一个评估环节来审查结果并剔除低置信度的项。
C. Add an evaluator pass that reviews the findings and removes low confidence ones.

699
01:03:13,966 --> 01:03:17,892
d. 根据文件语言将每个文件分配给专门的扫描器。
D. Root each file to a specialized scanner based on its language.

700
01:03:18,382 --> 01:03:19,556
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

701
01:03:25,454 --> 01:03:30,372
答案是 A，有趣的是场景是如何为你提供依据的。
The answer is A, and the interesting part is how the scenario licenses it.

702
01:03:30,894 --> 01:03:32,228
这里埋了三个细节。
Three details are planted.

703
01:03:32,590 --> 01:03:34,244
召回率是首要任务。
Recall is the priority.

704
01:03:34,798 --> 01:03:37,376
有足够的审核人力来处理误报。
There is spare reviewer capacity for false positives.

705
01:03:37,710 --> 01:03:39,136
而且延迟不重要。
And latency does not matter.

706
01:03:39,470 --> 01:03:43,428
投票机制成本高且干扰多，所以通常很难证明其合理性。
Voting is expensive and noisy, so it is normally hard to justify.

707
01:03:44,270 --> 01:03:49,316
这三句话排除了所有反对意见，而这些正是题目提示你选择 A 的依据。
Those three sentences remove every objection, which is the question telling you to pick it.

708
01:03:49,998 --> 01:03:57,636
选项 C 是需要警惕的，因为评估环节听起来像是增加了严谨性，但它实际上是朝着相反的方向运作。
Option C is the one to be careful with, because an evaluator pass sounds like added rigor and it works in the opposite direction.

709
01:03:58,382 --> 01:04:05,092
剔除低置信度的结果是通过舍弃内容来提高精确率，而团队要求的是召回率。
Removing low confidence findings raises precision by discarding things, and the team asked for recall.

710
01:04:06,030 --> 01:04:13,060
选项 B 是真正的分区，虽然有一点帮助，但每个步骤仍会在其类别中漏掉内容。
Option B is genuine sectioning and does help a little, but each pass still misses within its own class.

711
01:04:15,406 --> 01:04:17,776
选项 D 是在某一个维度上进行专业化。
Option D specializes on a dimension.

712
01:04:18,094 --> 01:04:19,652
题干中没有任何信息指向
Nothing in the stem points at

713
01:04:20,558 --> 01:04:24,260
模块 3，接下来是协调者和子智能体。
Module 3 next on coordinators and subagents.

714
01:04:25,838 --> 01:04:28,292
模块 3 依然在领域内
Module 3 and still domain

715
01:04:30,126 --> 01:04:36,804
1. 模块 2 以编排工作者结束，其中模型在运行时决定子任务列表。
1. Module 2 ended with orchestrator workers where a model decides the subtask list at runtime.

716
01:04:37,326 --> 01:04:39,748
这个模块是关于接下来会发生什么。
This module is about what happens next.

717
01:04:40,526 --> 01:04:48,932
协调者如何真正进行委派，子智能体能看到什么或不能看到什么，以及委派失败且无人察觉的特定方式。
How the coordinator actually delegates, what a subagent can and cannot see, and the specific ways delegation fails without anyone noticing.

718
01:04:50,478 --> 01:04:57,252
多智能体研究系统是六个考试场景之一。所以如果你抽到这个内容，它肯定会出现在考题中。
The multi-agent research system is one of the six exam scenarios. So this material is guaranteed to appear if you draw it.

719
01:04:58,176 --> 01:05:01,348
它还会出现在开发者生产力场景中。
It also shows up inside the developer productivity scenario.

720
01:05:01,870 --> 01:05:03,076
请全神贯注。
What your full attention.

721
01:05:04,494 --> 01:05:12,196
先从心理模型开始，因为几乎所有的子代理错误都是披着语法外壳的心理模型错误。
Start with the mental model because almost every sub-agent mistake is a mental model mistake wearing a syntax costume.

722
01:05:12,496 --> 01:05:17,636
子代理不是一个函数调用，也不是共享你工作空间的助手。
A subagent is not a function call and it is not a helper that shares your workspace.

723
01:05:18,416 --> 01:05:27,748
它是一个独立的智能体实例，运行在拥有自己对话历史、上下文窗口、工具权限，甚至可能有不同模型的环境中。
It is a separate agent instance running its own conversation with its own context window, its own tool permissions, and potentially its own model.

724
01:05:28,416 --> 01:05:30,308
它看不到你看到的内容。
It does not see what you have seen.

725
01:05:30,766 --> 01:05:32,388
它不知道你掌握的信息。
It does not know what you know.

726
01:05:32,576 --> 01:05:35,908
所有它需要的东西都必须有意识地交给它。
Everything it needs has to be handed to it deliberately.

727
01:05:36,654 --> 01:05:39,076
记住这一点，大部分模型逻辑都遵循这个原则。
Hold that and most of this model follows.

728
01:05:40,558 --> 01:05:46,244
这里有四个原因，作为一个列表去学习很有价值，因为考试题目往往取决于哪一个适用。
Four reasons and they are worth learning as a list because exam questions turn on which one applies.

729
01:05:46,816 --> 01:05:54,336
上下文隔离。这样子代理可以读取 50 个文件并返回一个摘要，而父智能体的上下文保持整洁。
Context isolation. So a subagent can read 50 files and return one summary while the parent's context stays clean.

730
01:05:54,830 --> 01:06:00,996
并行性，让独立的工作能在最慢的部分耗时内完成，而不是所有步骤时间的总和。
Parallelism, so independent work finishes in the time of the slowest piece rather than the sum.

731
01:06:01,550 --> 01:06:03,204
专门的指令。
Specialized instructions.

732
01:06:03,598 --> 01:06:11,236
这样数据库迁移专家就能携带详细知识，而这些内容在主智能体的提示词中可能会变成纯粹的干扰信息。
So a database migration expert can carry detailed knowledge that would be pure noise in the main agent's prompt.

733
01:06:11,982 --> 01:06:13,216
还有工具限制。
And tool restriction.

734
01:06:13,456 --> 01:06:16,356
这样审核者可以阅读所有内容，但不会写任何东西。
So a reviewer can read everything and write nothing.

735
01:06:16,910 --> 01:06:19,268
第一个才是真正关键的。
The first is the one that genuinely matters.

736
01:06:19,822 --> 01:06:23,140
如果非必要的话，其他三个你可以通过其他方式实现。
The other three you could achieve other ways if you had to.

737
01:06:23,918 --> 01:06:26,176
但隔离是做不到的。
Isolation you cannot.

738
01:06:27,470 --> 01:06:29,284
这是具体的运作机制。
Here is the mechanism concretely.

739
01:06:29,616 --> 01:06:34,404
协调者调用带有子代理类型的智能体工具并提供提示词。
The coordinator calls the agent tool with a subagent type and a prompt.

740
01:06:36,622 --> 01:06:44,816
Claude 代码或 SDK 会启动那个子代理，它会开始一段包含所给提示词的全新上下文对话。
Clawed code or the SDK spins up that subagent, which starts a fresh conversation containing the prompt it was given.

741
01:06:45,358 --> 01:06:51,908
它调用它拥有的任何工具来完成工作，而所有这些交互都留在它自己的上下文窗口内。
It does its work calling whatever tools it has, and all of that traffic stays inside its own context window.

742
01:06:52,494 --> 01:06:56,096
然后它的最终消息作为工具结果返回给父智能体。
Then its final message comes back to the parent as the tool result.

743
01:06:56,526 --> 01:06:57,924
仅仅是那一条消息。
Just that one message.

744
01:06:58,684 --> 01:07:00,964
父智能体永远看不到中间步骤。
The parent never sees the intermediate steps.

745
01:07:01,604 --> 01:07:03,744
有些人有时会把这理解为一种限制。
People sometimes read that as a limitation.

746
01:07:04,814 --> 01:07:06,464
但这正是核心目的。
It is the entire point.

747
01:07:07,284 --> 01:07:13,244
这就是让协调者的上下文保持足够整洁，从而在第 40 轮时仍能做出正确决策的原因。
That is what keeps the coordinator's context clean enough to still be making good decisions on turn 40.

748
01:07:14,944 --> 01:07:22,052
全新上下文意味着真正的全新，而子代理拿不到的东西比人们预想的要多。
Fresh context means genuinely fresh, and the list of things a subagent does not get is longer than people expect.

749
01:07:22,384 --> 01:07:28,452
它没有对话历史，所以它不知道用户要求了什么或者已经决定了什么。
It has no conversation history, so it does not know what the user asked or what has already been decided.

750
01:07:28,974 --> 01:07:34,304
它没有读过主线程读取的文件，所以如果它需要这些文件，它必须重新读取。
It has not read the files, the main thread read, so if it needs them, it reads them again.

751
01:07:34,464 --> 01:07:39,908
而且至关重要的一点是，它看不到同级子代理发现的内容。它们之间没有共享内存。
And critically, it cannot see what a sibling subagent found. There is no shared memory between them.

752
01:07:40,224 --> 01:07:44,100
从父级到子级的唯一通道就是智能体调用中的提示词。
The only channel from parent to child is the prompt in the agent call.

753
01:07:44,846 --> 01:07:49,572
如果某个事实没写进那个提示词，子代理就没有这个信息。
If a fact is not written into that prompt, the subagent does not have it.

754
01:07:50,190 --> 01:07:55,012
在这一领域中，在提示词中传递发现结果是出现频率最高的正确答案之一。
Pass findings in the prompt is one of the most repeated correct answers in this domain.

755
01:07:56,302 --> 01:07:58,148
还有另一种值得了解的情况。
There is a second flavor worth knowing.

756
01:07:58,704 --> 01:08:05,444
全新的子代理仅从你给它的提示词开始，这是最大程度的隔离，也是默认设置。
A fresh subagent starts from nothing but the prompt you gave it, which is maximum isolation and the default.

757
01:08:05,998 --> 01:08:09,860
派生子代理则从父级到那一刻为止的对话内容开始。
A forked subagent starts from the parent's conversation at that point.

758
01:08:10,064 --> 01:08:14,020
所以它已经拥有了上下文，你不需要重复任何内容。
So it already has the context and you do not have to restate anything.

759
01:08:14,990 --> 01:08:19,011
代价是你在每一次派生中都要为这些上下文付费。
The trade is that you pay for that context in every fork.

760
01:08:19,982 --> 01:08:24,676
当你想要从同一个位置探索两种不同的方法时，使用派生子代理。
Use a fork when you want to explore two different approaches from the same position.

761
01:08:25,486 --> 01:08:29,188
当工作内容可以真正分离时，使用全新的子代理。
Use a fresh subagent when the work is genuinely separable.

762
01:08:30,062 --> 01:08:32,996
注意这个提醒，因为它经常误导考生。
And note the callout because it catches people.

763
01:08:33,966 --> 01:08:36,420
派生改变的是进入子代理的内容。
Fork changes what goes into the subagent.

764
01:08:37,344 --> 01:08:39,716
它永远不会改变产出的内容。
It never changes what comes out.

765
01:08:40,064 --> 01:08:43,076
无论哪种方式，只有最终消息会返回。
Only the final message returns either way.

766
01:08:44,366 --> 01:08:47,332
这个单一的事实重新定义了什么是委派。
That single fact reframes what delegation is.

767
01:08:47,854 --> 01:08:51,363
你不是在与一个参加过会议的同事共享工作。
You are not sharing work with a colleague who has been sitting in the meeting.

768
01:08:52,206 --> 01:09:00,162
你是在为一个从未见过你项目、不能向你提问，且无论如何都会产出结果的承包商编写简报。
You are writing a brief for a contractor who has never seen your project, cannot ask you a question, and will produce something either way.

769
01:09:01,102 --> 01:09:05,667
Anthropic 在构建他们自己的多智能体研究系统时发现了这一点。
Anthropic found exactly this when they built their own multi-agent research system.

770
01:09:06,957 --> 01:09:14,948
模糊的子代理指令导致了重复工作、由于每个子代理都假设有另一个在处理而产生的漏洞，以及没人需要的搜索。
Vague subagent instructions produced duplicated work, gaps where each subagent assumed another was covering something, and searches nobody needed.

771
01:09:15,822 --> 01:09:18,627
解决方法不是更好的模型，而是更好的简报。
The fix was not a better model, it was better briefs.

772
01:09:20,142 --> 01:09:21,584
那么，简报里包含什么内容？
So, what goes in the brief?

773
01:09:21,774 --> 01:09:28,131
目标必须表述得足够明确，以至于两个子代理不会同时认为该任务属于自己。
The objective stated narrowly enough that two subagents cannot both believe it belongs to them.

774
01:09:28,558 --> 01:09:33,667
你需要的输出格式，因为那个最终消息就是你将获得的全部内容。
The output format you need back because that final message is everything you will get.

775
01:09:34,573 --> 01:09:40,996
任何早期工作的上下文或发现都必须完整重述，因为子代理无法自行去挖掘它们。
Any context or findings from earlier work restated in full because the subagent cannot rip them up.

776
01:09:41,710 --> 01:09:47,268
边界，即明确不在范围内的内容，以及要从哪些来源或目录进行工作。
Boundaries, meaning what is explicitly out of scope and which sources or directories to work from.

777
01:09:48,109 --> 01:09:51,428
以及在多个工具功能重叠时，应优先使用哪个工具的指导。
And a steer on which tools to prefer if several overlap.

778
01:09:52,304 --> 01:10:00,740
当场景描述子代理重复彼此的工作，或者报告中出现明显的漏洞时，原因几乎总是出在这里。
When a scenario describes subagents duplicating each other's work or a report with an obvious hole in it, the cause is almost always here.

779
01:10:02,414 --> 01:10:06,052
这揭示了本次考试中所有多智能体系统的结构。
That gives you the shape of every multi-agent system on this exam.

780
01:10:06,958 --> 01:10:08,580
即星型拓扑。
A hub and spoke.

781
01:10:09,454 --> 01:10:13,412
协调者掌握目标、计划和所有结果。
The coordinator holds the goal, the plan, and all the results.

782
01:10:14,350 --> 01:10:19,172
它根据目前掌握的信息，为每个子代理分派一个提示词。
It delegates outward one prompt per subagent written from what it currently knows.

783
01:10:20,046 --> 01:10:23,364
结果会传回给协调者，且只能交给协调者。
Results come back to the coordinator and only to the coordinator.

784
01:10:24,302 --> 01:10:33,572
综合是在那里进行的，因为那是所有发现汇聚的唯一地方。要记住强调框里的那句话：子代理之间从不互相通信。
And synthesis happens there because that is the only place findings ever meet. The line in the call out is the one to memorize. Subagents never message each other.

785
01:10:33,904 --> 01:10:41,508
如果第二个子代理需要第一个子代理找到的东西，协调者会读取第一个结果并将其写入到第二个提示词中。
If the second subagent needs something, the first one found, the coordinator reads the first result and writes it into the second prompt.

786
01:10:42,304 --> 01:10:43,844
没有其他路径。
There is no other route.

787
01:10:45,358 --> 01:10:52,068
现在来看同时运行多个子代理的机制，因为这是考试的常考点。
Now, the mechanics of running subagents at the same time because this is a favorite exam target.

788
01:10:53,774 --> 01:10:59,536
并发源于协调者在单个助手响应中发出多个智能体调用。
Concurrency comes from the coordinator emitting several agent calls inside a single assistant response.

789
01:10:59,790 --> 01:11:01,572
这就是全部机制。
That is the entire mechanism.

790
01:11:02,350 --> 01:11:06,244
如果它发起一个调用，等待结果，然后再发起另一个。
If it makes one call, waits for the result, then makes another.

791
01:11:06,606 --> 01:11:09,348
无论提示词怎么写，那都是串行。
That is sequential no matter how the prompt is worded.

792
01:11:10,126 --> 01:11:17,444
仅仅指令模型并行工作并不会改变响应的结构。而且底部的隐性故障值得记住。
Instructing the model to work in parallel does not change the response shape on its own. And the quiet failure at the bottom is worth remembering.

793
01:11:18,382 --> 01:11:23,460
如果代理工具不在允许的工具列表中，协调者会思考如何分派任务。
If the agent tool is not in the allowed tools list, the coordinator will reason about delegating.

794
01:11:24,206 --> 01:11:25,956
它甚至可能会描述这种分派。
It may even describe the delegation.

795
01:11:26,478 --> 01:11:27,940
但它永远不会真正去执行。
It never actually does it.

796
01:11:29,614 --> 01:11:33,216
四种故障模式，它们之所以重要是因为强调框里提到的原因。
Four failure modes, and the reason they matter is in the call out.

797
01:11:33,870 --> 01:11:35,652
这些情况中没有一个会报错。
Not one of them raises an error.

798
01:11:36,014 --> 01:11:39,684
子代理涵盖相同内容意味着目标重叠了。
Sub-agents covering the same ground means the objectives overlapped.

799
01:11:40,142 --> 01:11:44,356
缺失的主题意味着每个子代理都以为别人会处理它。
A missing topic means every sub agent assumed someone else had it.

800
01:11:45,262 --> 01:11:50,948
一个接一个运行的子代理意味着协调者在每次响应中只发出一个智能体调用。
Subagents running one after another means the coordinator is emitting one agent call per response.

801
01:11:51,296 --> 01:11:57,764
而一个只谈论分派但不去执行的协调者，意味着该代理工具不在其允许列表中。
And a coordinator that talks about delegating without doing it means the agent tool is not in its allowed list.

802
01:11:58,478 --> 01:12:09,636
这些看起来都像是运作中的系统，只是产出的结果略显平庸，这正是为什么考试题目将它们描述为“令人困惑”而非“损坏”。
Each of these looks like a working system, producing slightly disappointing output, which is exactly why exam scenarios describe them as puzzling rather than broken.

803
01:12:11,022 --> 01:12:15,620
还有一个协调者的职责，这是大家经常忽略的。
One more coordinator responsibility, and it is the one people forget.

804
01:12:16,654 --> 01:12:25,316
当结果返回时，协调者的工作不仅是把它们拼接起来，还要阅读它们并询问还有什么缺失。
When results come back, the coordinator's job is not only to stitch them together, it is to read them and ask what is still missing.

805
01:12:26,446 --> 01:12:32,068
然后根据第一轮发现的内容，为这些缺口生成更多子代理的提示词。
Then spawn further subagents for those gaps with prompts informed by what the first round found.

806
01:12:32,976 --> 01:12:42,244
这就是为什么子任务列表不能在编写时就写死的根本原因。这也是真正的编排器与带有额外步骤的并行化之间的区别。
This is precisely why the subtask list cannot be written at author time. It is also the difference between a real orchestrator and parallelization with extra steps.

807
01:12:42,656 --> 01:12:48,804
如果你的系统只运行一轮子代理、汇总并停止，那就是并行化。
If your system fires one round of subagents, aggregates, and stops, you have parallelization.

808
01:12:49,422 --> 01:12:53,776
只要拆分正确，这没问题，而且你最好能确定这一点。
Which is fine as long as the split was right and you had better be sure of that.

809
01:12:55,086 --> 01:12:59,268
这个对比决定了不止一道考题，所以请花点时间理解一下。
This comparison decides more than one exam question, so give it a moment.

810
01:13:04,110 --> 01:13:06,436
当工作需要独立窗口时，再进行分派。
Delegate when the work needs its own window.

811
01:13:06,976 --> 01:13:10,404
当探索产生出的内容你并不想要保留时。
When exploration generates output you do not want to keep.

812
01:13:10,656 --> 01:13:13,348
当父级上下文已经开始退化时。
When the parent's context is already degrading.

813
01:13:13,616 --> 01:13:19,140
当任务需要不同的工具，或者多个部分确实是独立的时。
When the task needs different tools, when several pieces are genuinely independent.

814
01:13:19,694 --> 01:13:23,364
如果父级已经持有所需内容，就直接在行内处理。
Do it in line when the parent already holds what is needed.

815
01:13:24,622 --> 01:13:30,020
是一项小工作，或者是针对当前就在上下文中的发现提出的后续问题。
A small piece of work or a follow-up question about findings that are sitting in context right now.

816
01:13:30,816 --> 01:13:33,540
这个陷阱是常见的套路。
The trap in the call out is the common one.

817
01:13:34,542 --> 01:13:41,508
为了让协调者已经持有的内容重新读一遍而派生子智能体，会消耗一轮往返和一次全新上下文加载。
Spawning a subagent to reread something the coordinator already holds costs a round trip and a fresh context load.

818
01:13:42,126 --> 01:13:43,616
这毫无好处。
It buys you nothing.

819
01:13:44,942 --> 01:13:50,948
多智能体系统成本很高，考试要求你大致了解这些成本。
Multi-agent systems are expensive, and the exam expects you to know roughly how expensive.

820
01:13:51,456 --> 01:13:57,892
Anthropic 报告他们自己的研究系统消耗的 token 是普通对话交互的 15 倍左右。
Anthropic reported their own research system using around 15 times the tokens of an ordinary chat interaction.

821
01:13:58,256 --> 01:14:02,436
每个子智能体在执行任何有用工作之前，都要支付加载成本。
Every subagent also pays a loading cost before it does any useful work.

822
01:14:03,246 --> 01:14:07,108
而且并行性能节省墙钟时间，但永远不能节省支出。
And parallelism buys you wall clock time and never buys you spend.

823
01:14:07,456 --> 01:14:12,388
同时运行的六个子智能体所花费的成本，与按顺序运行的六个完全一样。
Six subagents running concurrently cost exactly what six running in sequence would cost.

824
01:14:12,656 --> 01:14:17,764
所以当题目要求你降低成本时，增加子智能体几乎绝不是正确答案。
So when a question asks you to reduce cost, adding subagents is almost never the answer.

825
01:14:18,016 --> 01:14:20,976
但当它要求你降低延迟时，可能就是。
When it asks you to reduce latency, it might be.

826
01:14:21,422 --> 01:14:23,428
读一下题干里用了哪个词。
Read which word the stem used.

827
01:14:25,038 --> 01:14:27,696
在题目中会出现的四个配置细节。
Four configuration details that turn up in questions.

828
01:14:27,936 --> 01:14:33,028
首先，除非你明确设置，否则子智能体会继承主智能体的模型。
First, a subagent inherits the lead agents model unless you set one explicitly.

829
01:14:33,294 --> 01:14:37,668
所以一个廉价驱动的子智能体可能会在静默状态下运行在你最昂贵的模型上。
So a cheap drive subagent can silently run on your most expensive model.

830
01:14:38,382 --> 01:14:43,044
其次，工具限制是真正的控制手段，而不是建议。
Second, tool restriction is a genuine control rather than a suggestion.

831
01:14:44,016 --> 01:14:50,948
只给读工具权限的子智能体无法进行写入，无论你怎么提示它，这使其成为一种强制执行机制。
A subagent given only read tools cannot write, no matter how it is prompted, and that makes it an enforcement mechanism.

832
01:14:51,982 --> 01:14:58,416
第三，你可以限制每个子智能体的轮次，达到上限时会返回部分输出，由父级来处理。
Third, you can cap turns per subagent, and hitting that cap returns partial output the parent has to handle.

833
01:14:58,958 --> 01:15:04,164
第四，Claude 通过读取描述字段来决定调用哪个子智能体。
Fourth, Claude decides which subagent to invoke by reading its description field.

834
01:15:04,974 --> 01:15:09,044
把那个描述写成「在……情况下使用」，而不是作为一个职位名称。
Write that description as use this when rather than as a job title.

835
01:15:10,926 --> 01:15:15,424
这是一个版本核查，因为有两个内容在考试指南发布后发生了变化。
A currency check because two things here have moved since the exam guide was written.

836
01:15:15,664 --> 01:15:23,556
派生子智能体的工具以前叫 task，在 clot 代码 2.1.63 版本中被重命名为 智能体。
The tool that spawns subagents was called task and was renamed to agent in plot code version 2.1.63.

837
01:15:24,366 --> 01:15:30,464
旧的 task 引用仍作为别名有效，所以你会在不同时期的文档中看到这两个名称。
Old task references still work as aliases, so you will see both names in documentation from different periods.

838
01:15:30,894 --> 01:15:32,164
它们是同一种机制。
They are the same mechanism.

839
01:15:32,590 --> 01:15:34,084
而且嵌套限制放宽了。
And nesting has softened.

840
01:15:35,374 --> 01:15:41,412
考试的答案是子智能体不能派生子智能体，只提供一层平行的扇出。
The exam answer is that subagents cannot spawn subagents, giving you one flat level of fan out.

841
01:15:42,224 --> 01:15:49,220
目前的文档描述嵌套深度为5，但关于哪些类型的子代理能获得工具，报告说法不一。
Current documentation describes nesting to a depth of 5, though reports differ on which subagent types actually get the tool.

842
01:15:49,584 --> 01:15:52,740
在考试中，回答任务并只选一层。
On the exam, answer task and answer one level.

843
01:15:53,184 --> 01:15:55,556
同级通信完全没有变化。
Sibling communication has not changed at all.

844
01:15:55,918 --> 01:15:57,060
目前还是没有任何（的）。
There still is not any.

845
01:15:58,606 --> 01:16:02,052
如果你只能记住本模块的一句话，就记这一句。
If you remember one sentence from this module, make it that one.

846
01:16:02,478 --> 01:16:05,380
子代理知道的一切内容都是你写在它的提示词里的。
Everything a subagent knows you wrote into its prompt.

847
01:16:05,806 --> 01:16:08,864
你从它那里学到的一切都必须包含在一个返回消息中。
Everything you learn from it has to fit into one return message.

848
01:16:09,024 --> 01:16:14,340
这两个约束之间的关系解释了失败原因、成本以及大部分的设计决策。
Those two constraints between them explain the failures, the costs, and most of the design decisions.

849
01:16:15,184 --> 01:16:20,932
当题目描述子代理做错事时，去问它的提示词里写了什么。
When a question describes a subagent doing the wrong thing, ask what was in its prompt.

850
01:16:21,344 --> 01:16:27,492
当它描述协调者遗漏内容时，去问子代理在回复中能容纳下什么。
When it describes a coordinator missing something, ask what the subagent was able to fit in its reply.

851
01:16:29,198 --> 01:16:31,204
就在场景描述的前五行。
Five lines before the scenarios.

852
01:16:31,504 --> 01:16:38,756
子代理是一个拥有独立上下文窗口的独立对话，隔离是创建它的主要原因。
A subagent is a separate conversation with its own context window, and isolation is the main reason to spawn one.

853
01:16:39,246 --> 01:16:45,604
它不继承任何内容，所以提示词是唯一的输入通道，最后的消息是唯一的输出通道。
It inherits nothing, so the prompt is the only channel in and the final message is the only channel out.

854
01:16:46,414 --> 01:16:53,028
结构是星型拓扑，协调者负责在同级之间传递发现结果，因为它们无法直接通话。
The shape is hub and spoke, with the coordinator carrying findings between siblings because they cannot talk.

855
01:16:53,806 --> 01:16:59,620
并发源于一个助手响应中的多个智能体调用，而不是靠礼貌请求。
Concurrency comes from several agent calls in one assistant response rather than from asking nicely.

856
01:17:00,526 --> 01:17:03,940
而且子代理能节省墙钟时间和上下文余量。
And subagents buy wall clock time and context headroom.

857
01:17:04,270 --> 01:17:05,104
从不产生额外成本。
Never cost.

858
01:17:06,158 --> 01:17:10,820
现在有六个场景，其中两个看起来像委派问题但并不是。
Six scenarios now, and two of them look like delegation problems but are not.

859
01:17:12,078 --> 01:17:13,828
每次都坚持选一个字母。
Commit to a letter every time.

860
01:17:15,502 --> 01:17:16,544
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

861
01:17:16,784 --> 01:17:27,140
一个研究系统有一个协调者，它派生了四个专门的子代理：一个网络搜索智能体、一个学术论文智能体、一个数据分析智能体和一个报告生成器。
A research system has a coordinator that spawns four specialized subagents a web search agent, an academic paper agent, a data analysis agent, and a report generator.

862
01:17:27,534 --> 01:17:33,668
报告生成器生成的报告总是漏掉数据分析智能体发现的内容。
The report generator consistently produces reports that leave out findings the data analysis agent uncovered.

863
01:17:34,382 --> 01:17:41,028
日志确认了数据分析子代理已成功完成，并向协调者返回了详细结果。
The logs confirmed the data analysis subagent, completed successfully, and returned a detailed result to the coordinator.

864
01:17:41,550 --> 01:17:48,004
报告生成器紧接着响应提示词：针对研究问题生成一份综合报告。
The report generator responds straight afterwards with the prompt Generate a Comprehensive Report on the Research Question.

865
01:17:48,814 --> 01:17:49,988
根本原因是什么？
What is the root cause?

866
01:17:50,894 --> 01:17:56,804
a. 报告生成器需要更长的轮数限制，以便有时间收集分析结果。
a. The report generator needs a longer turn cap so it has time to gather the analysis.

867
01:17:57,550 --> 01:18:03,812
b 数据分析子代理应该直接将它的发现发送给报告生成器。
b The data analysis subagent should message the report generator directly with its findings.

868
01:18:05,024 --> 01:18:05,264
C。
C.

869
01:18:05,904 --> 01:18:10,660
协调者没有将分析结果包含在报告生成器的提示词中。
The coordinator is not including the analysis findings in the report generator's prompt.

870
01:18:11,344 --> 01:18:11,664
D。
D.

871
01:18:12,206 --> 01:18:16,064
报告生成器的模型太小，无法进行全面的综合。
The report generator's model is too small for comprehensive synthesis.

872
01:18:16,366 --> 01:18:17,412
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

873
01:18:22,784 --> 01:18:24,132
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

874
01:18:24,464 --> 01:18:27,812
注意题干完整引用了报告生成器的提示词。
Notice that the stem quotes the report generators prompt in full.

875
01:18:27,984 --> 01:18:30,944
这是刻意为之的，也是埋下的关键细节。
That is deliberate and it is the planted detail.

876
01:18:31,184 --> 01:18:37,904
提示词要求对研究问题生成一份全面的报告，但其中根本不包含任何调查结果。
The prompt says generate a comprehensive report on the research question and it contains no findings whatsoever.

877
01:18:38,382 --> 01:18:44,452
由于提示词是父级到子级的唯一通道，报告生成器从未看到过分析内容。
Since the prompt is the only channel from parent to child, the report generator has never seen the analysis.

878
01:18:44,704 --> 01:18:50,852
选项 B 是最具启发性的错误答案，因为它描述了一个并不存在的机制。
Option B is the most instructive wrong answer because it describes a mechanism that does not exist.

879
01:18:51,406 --> 01:18:53,476
子智能体之间没有直接联系。
Subagents have no root to each other.

880
01:18:54,414 --> 01:19:01,024
选项 A 给子代理提供了更多轮次去搜索一个永远不会包含它要找的内容的上下文。
Option A gives the subagent more turns to search a context that will never contain what it is looking for.

881
01:19:01,264 --> 01:19:08,516
选项 D 将信息问题归咎于能力问题，而更大的模型也会同样可靠地忽略这些结果。
Option D blames capability for an information problem, and a larger model will omit the same findings just as reliably.

882
01:19:10,126 --> 01:19:11,268
场景 2
Scenario 2

883
01:19:11,982 --> 01:19:17,444
一个协调者负责处理需要三个独立调查线索的研究请求。
A coordinator handles research requests needing three independent lines of inquiry.

884
01:19:17,966 --> 01:19:22,372
每一项都是真正可分离的，且任何一项都不依赖于另一项的输出。
Each is genuinely separable and none depends on another's output.

885
01:19:23,054 --> 01:19:31,204
系统提示词要求：将独立的调研任务委派给子智能体，并尽可能并行运行。
The system prompt says Delegate independent research tasks to sub agents and run them in parallel wherever possible.

886
01:19:32,110 --> 01:19:38,180
追踪显示协调者发出一个智能体调用，等待结果，再发出下一个，以此类推。
Traces show the coordinator issuing one agent call, waiting for the result, issuing the next, and so on.

887
01:19:38,830 --> 01:19:41,892
总耗时大约是团队预期的三倍。
Total time is about three times what the team expected.

888
01:19:42,478 --> 01:19:46,628
代理工具在允许的工具列表中，且每个子智能体都正确完成了任务。
The agent tool is in allowed tools and each subagent completes correctly.

889
01:19:47,502 --> 01:19:49,764
什么样的改变能让它们并发运行？
What change makes them run concurrently?

890
01:19:50,734 --> 01:19:57,316
a. 在系统提示词中加入更强硬的措辞，说明并行执行是必须的而非可选的。
a Add stronger wording to the system prompt, stating that parallel execution is required rather than optional.

891
01:19:57,856 --> 01:19:58,096
b。
b.

892
01:19:58,496 --> 01:20:03,748
调整协调者的结构，使所有三个智能体调用都在单次助手响应中发出。
Structure the coordinator so all three agent calls are emitted in a single assistant response.

893
01:20:04,176 --> 01:20:04,416
C。
C.

894
01:20:04,974 --> 01:20:09,380
增加轮数限制，让协调者有空间发出所有三个调用。
Increase the turn cap so the coordinator has room to issue all three calls.

895
01:20:10,286 --> 01:20:10,496
D。
D.

896
01:20:11,086 --> 01:20:15,908
将三条调查线索合并到一个具有更广泛任务要求的子智能体中。
Merge the three lines of enquiry into one subagent with a broader brief.

897
01:20:16,782 --> 01:20:17,828
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

898
01:20:23,566 --> 01:20:25,296
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

899
01:20:26,094 --> 01:20:29,444
题干在第二段就给了你排除干扰项的线索。
The stem hands you the eliminator in its second paragraph.

900
01:20:30,094 --> 01:20:35,364
系统提示词已经包含了该指令，但行为依然错误。
The system prompt already contains the instruction and the behavior is still wrong.

901
01:20:36,590 --> 01:20:43,236
当题目告诉你存在一条指令且正在被松散地执行时，那句话存在的目的只有一个。
When a question tells you an instruction exists and is being followed loosely, that sentence is there for one purpose.

902
01:20:44,142 --> 01:20:47,376
它排除了所有写出更优指令的选项。
It rules out every option that writes a better instruction.

903
01:20:47,616 --> 01:20:51,108
选项 A 就是那个选项，也是最常见的错误答案。
Option A is that option and it is the popular wrong answer.

904
01:20:51,376 --> 01:20:54,256
并发是响应形状的一个属性。
Concurrency is a property of the response shape.

905
01:20:54,734 --> 01:21:01,380
在一个助手中包含三个智能体调用，在同一轮执行，且每个包含一个调用的三个响应永远不会发生。
Three agent calls in one assistant, turn execute together, and three responses each containing one call never will.

906
01:21:02,414 --> 01:21:06,852
选项 C 被追踪信息排除，因为所有三个调用都已发出。
Option C is ruled out by the trace since all three calls were issued.

907
01:21:07,278 --> 01:21:15,172
选项 D 通过删除架构解决了时序问题，但它抛弃了你为了获得上下文隔离而创建子代理所获得的成果。
Option D solves the timing problem by deleting the architecture and it throws away the context isolation you spawned sub-agents to get.

908
01:21:16,686 --> 01:21:17,604
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

909
01:21:17,856 --> 01:21:29,348
一个基于代码的探索智能体使用子代理来调查不同的模块。在一次大规模调查中，协调者的上下文填满了，其后续的决策明显变差。
A code-based exploration agent uses subagents to investigate different modules. During a large investigation, the coordinator's own context fills up and its later decisions become noticeably worse.

910
01:21:31,374 --> 01:21:33,060
审查显示了两点。
Review shows two things.

911
01:21:34,062 --> 01:21:43,136
协调者将目前发现的所有内容的完整副本传递给每个子代理，而每个子代理返回其探索的完整转录记录，
The coordinator passes each subagent a full copy of everything found so far, and each subagent returns a complete transcript of its exploration,

912
01:21:43,376 --> 01:21:46,820
包括每一次文件迭代，然后由协调者保留这些内容。
including every file iterate, which the coordinator then keeps.

913
01:21:47,374 --> 01:21:49,060
最有效的改变是什么？
What is the most effective change?

914
01:21:49,902 --> 01:21:57,188
a. 让子代理仅返回它们的结论，并仅向每个新子代理传递与其任务相关的发现。
a Have subagents return only their conclusions and pass each new subagent only the findings relevant to its task.

915
01:21:57,742 --> 01:22:01,796
b. 将协调者的模型升级到具有更大上下文窗口的模型。
b. Increase the coordinator's model to one with a larger context window.

916
01:22:02,478 --> 01:22:06,724
C. 减少子代理的数量，从而减少返回的材料。
C. Reduce the number of subagents so less material comes back.

917
01:22:07,456 --> 01:22:07,776
D。
D.

918
01:22:08,416 --> 01:22:13,828
让每个子代理将其转录记录写入文件，并给协调者提供路径。
Have each subagent write its transcript to a file and give the coordinator the paths.

919
01:22:15,566 --> 01:22:16,932
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

920
01:22:22,350 --> 01:22:23,524
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

921
01:22:24,016 --> 01:22:30,308
这个场景之所以值得加入，是因为团队在架构上做了正确的事情，然后又把它搞砸了。
What makes this scenario worth including is that the team did the right thing architecturally and then undid it.

922
01:22:31,216 --> 01:22:37,316
他们为了上下文隔离而创建了子代理，然后却在两个端都破坏了这种隔离。
They spawned subagents for context isolation, then defeated that isolation at both ends.

923
01:22:38,190 --> 01:22:43,844
将目前发现的所有内容推送到每个子代理中，又把所有的转录记录拉回到上方。
Pushing everything found so far down into each subagent and pulling every transcript back up.

924
01:22:44,174 --> 01:22:48,100
选项 A 修复了两个方向的问题，而这正是当前情况所需要的。
Option A fixes both directions, which is what the situation needs.

925
01:22:48,654 --> 01:22:54,916
选项 D 是真正良好的实践，它出现在领域 5 中，但它只解决了向上泄漏的问题。
Option D is genuinely good practice and it appears in domain 5, but it only fixes the upward leak.

926
01:22:55,502 --> 01:22:59,300
协调者仍然在向下传递其完整的历史记录。
The coordinator is still shipping its entire history downwards.

927
01:22:59,758 --> 01:23:05,540
选项 B 在不改变增长率的情况下争取时间，而更大的窗口也会以同样的速度耗尽。
Option B buys time without changing the growth rate and a bigger window fins at the same speed.

928
01:23:06,094 --> 01:23:11,776
选项 C 通过减少调查量来减少上下文，这并不是一种修复。
Option C reduces context by doing less investigation, which is not a fix.

929
01:23:13,134 --> 01:23:20,388
场景 4 一个协调者委派给五个子代理，每个子代理调查市场研究问题的一个方面。
Scenario 4 A coordinator delegates to five sub agents, each investigating one aspect of a market research question.

930
01:23:22,094 --> 01:23:23,972
给每个人的简报只有一行。
The brief to each is a single line.

931
01:23:24,320 --> 01:23:27,620
深入研究这个主题并报告你的发现。
Research this topic thoroughly and report what you find.

932
01:23:27,920 --> 01:23:30,564
最终报告有两个反复出现的问题。
The final reports have two recurring problems.

933
01:23:31,374 --> 01:23:35,716
三个子智能体独立研究了相同的监管背景。
Three subagents independently research the same regulatory background.

934
01:23:36,270 --> 01:23:40,900
而且客户端特别询问的一个话题，在任何一个子智能体的输出中都没有出现。
And a topic the client specifically asked about appears in no subagent's output at all.

935
01:23:41,518 --> 01:23:43,236
最有效的修复方法是什么？
What is the most effective fix?

936
01:23:43,950 --> 01:23:47,620
a. 添加第六个专门负责缺失主题的子智能体。
a add a sixth subagent dedicated to the missing topic.

937
01:23:48,494 --> 01:23:48,720
b.
b.

938
01:23:49,040 --> 01:23:55,520
给每个子智能体一个明确的目标、明确的非范围界限以及要求的输出格式。
Give each subagent a narrow objective, explicit out-of-scope boundaries, and the required output format.

939
01:23:55,840 --> 01:24:00,132
c. 让协调者在综合过程中对重叠部分进行去重。
C. Have the coordinator deduplicate the overlapping sections during synthesis.

940
01:24:00,720 --> 01:24:05,828
d. 串行运行这五个子智能体，以便每个智能体都能看到前一个智能体涵盖的内容。
D. Run the five subagents sequentially so each can see what the previous one covered.

941
01:24:07,406 --> 01:24:08,420
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

942
01:24:14,190 --> 01:24:15,172
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

943
01:24:15,520 --> 01:24:19,076
这里的关键点是发现这两个症状其实是同一个缺陷导致的。
The key move here is spotting that the two symptoms are the same defect.

944
01:24:20,078 --> 01:24:25,860
工作重叠和话题缺失，都是因为没有人被明确告知哪些内容属于他们负责，哪些不属于。
Overlapping work and a missing topic both happen because nobody was told precisely what was theirs and what was not.

945
01:24:28,014 --> 01:24:30,148
明确的目标可以解决重叠问题。
Narrow objectives fix the overlap.

946
01:24:30,894 --> 01:24:34,020
明确的非范围界限可以解决遗漏问题。
Explicit out-of-scope boundaries fix the gap.

947
01:24:34,478 --> 01:24:36,548
一个改动同时解决了两个症状。
One change both symptoms.

948
01:24:38,606 --> 01:24:43,716
选项 D 是个有趣的干扰项，因为串行执行听起来似乎会有帮助。
Option D is the interesting distractor because sequential execution feels like it would help.

949
01:24:44,334 --> 01:24:45,124
但它没用。
It cannot.

950
01:24:45,902 --> 01:24:49,120
无论以何种顺序，子智能体都无法看到彼此的工作内容。
Subagents cannot see each other's work in any order.

951
01:24:49,280 --> 01:24:53,060
所以你得到的只是一个速度变慢、但依然存在同样两个问题的系统。
So all you have bought is a slower system with the same two problems.

952
01:24:53,710 --> 01:24:57,476
选项 A 只补上了这个缺口，却留下了下一个问题。
Option A patches this gap and leaves the next one.

953
01:24:57,710 --> 01:25:01,508
而选项 C 虽然隐藏了重复，却完全忽略了整个缺失的内容。
And option C hides the duplication while ignoring the whole entirely.

954
01:25:03,150 --> 01:25:04,164
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

955
01:25:04,974 --> 01:25:09,060
一个技术支持团队运行一个调查故障的智能体。
A support engineering team runs an agent that investigates incidents.

956
01:25:10,350 --> 01:25:16,644
它会派生出子智能体来读取日志、查询指标并搜索操作手册库，而且效果很好。
It spawns subagents to read logs, query metrics, and search the runbook repository, and it works well.

957
01:25:17,358 --> 01:25:19,076
该团队希望降低成本。
The team wants to reduce cost.

958
01:25:19,982 --> 01:25:27,434
他们的提议是让三个子智能体并发运行而不是串行运行，他们预计这能减少约三分之二的费用。
Their proposal is to run the three subagents concurrently rather than sequentially, which they expect will cut the bill by about two-thirds.

959
01:25:28,080 --> 01:25:30,276
目前延迟不是问题。
Latency is not currently a problem.

960
01:25:30,720 --> 01:25:35,076
故障是在后台调查的，结果会在第二天早上进行审查。
Incidents are investigated in the background and results are reviewed the next morning.

961
01:25:37,614 --> 01:25:38,788
你应该告诉他们什么？
What should you tell them?

962
01:25:39,758 --> 01:25:48,000
a. 并发不会降低成本，所以考虑为子智能体选择更便宜的模型，或者缩减任务范围以减少读取量。
a concurrency will not reduce cost, so consider a cheaper model for the subagents or narrower briefs that read less.

963
01:25:48,480 --> 01:25:48,800
b.
b.

964
01:25:49,262 --> 01:25:55,588
这个估算大致正确，因为并发执行可以在三个子智能体之间共享上下文加载。
The estimate is roughly right because concurrent execution shares context loading across the three subagents.

965
01:25:56,480 --> 01:25:56,800
c.
C.

966
01:25:57,280 --> 01:26:02,244
只有当子智能体使用相同的工具时，并发才会降低成本。
Concurrency reduces cost only if the subagents use the same tools.

967
01:26:02,926 --> 01:26:03,200
d.
D.

968
01:26:03,918 --> 01:26:06,372
将三个子智能体合并为一个
Merge the three subagents into one

969
01:26:07,246 --> 01:26:09,284
以消除两个上下文加载。
to eliminate two context loads.

970
01:26:10,222 --> 01:26:11,524
稍停并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

971
01:26:17,134 --> 01:26:19,040
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

972
01:26:19,790 --> 01:26:28,800
这个场景是在考查你是否已经内化了「并行性与成本无关」这一知识点。六个子智能体同时运行的成本是多少？
This scenario is a check on whether you have internalized that parallelism and cost are unrelated. Six subagents running at once cost exactly what?

973
01:26:29,166 --> 01:26:33,860
六个按顺序运行的成本也是一样的，因为 token 数量并不受调度影响。
Six running in sequence cost because the token count does not care about scheduling.

974
01:26:34,414 --> 01:26:37,060
第三段话是埋下的干扰细节。
The third paragraph is the planted detail.

975
01:26:38,030 --> 01:26:43,492
延迟不是问题，所以并发带来的唯一好处对这个团队来说毫无价值。
Latency is not a problem, so the single thing concurrency does buy is worth nothing to this team.

976
01:26:44,430 --> 01:26:48,388
选项 B 虚构了一个并不存在的共享机制。
Option B invents a sharing mechanism that does not exist.

977
01:26:49,120 --> 01:26:54,800
选项 C 是那种听起来很专业、似乎是真的，但纯属编造的答案。
Option C is the kind of answer that sounds technical enough to be true and is simply made up.

978
01:26:55,342 --> 01:27:00,388
选项 D 确实能减少两个上下文加载，它是最强的干扰项。
Option D would genuinely save two context loads and it is the strongest distractor.

979
01:27:01,550 --> 01:27:06,116
它还会破坏隔离性，而且题干从未暗示设计有误。
It also trades away the isolation and the stem never suggested the design was wrong.

980
01:27:07,822 --> 01:27:09,040
场景 6。
Scenario 6.

981
01:27:09,454 --> 01:27:13,252
这是一个领域 1 的问题，预演了领域 2 和领域 3 的内容。
And it is a domain 1 question that previews domain 2 and domain 3.

982
01:27:14,830 --> 01:27:17,380
一个代码审查智能体正在进行扩展。
A code review agent is being extended.

983
01:27:17,902 --> 01:27:23,396
团队想要一个能够审查更改中的安全问题并报告发现结果的子代理。
The team wants a subagent that reviews changes for security issues and reports what it finds.

984
01:27:24,014 --> 01:27:28,452
无论如何提示，它都绝不能修改文件。
It must never be able to modify files regardless of how it is prompted.

985
01:27:29,294 --> 01:27:39,076
一名工程师建议在子代理的系统提示词开头加上：你是一个只读审查者，在任何情况下都不得编辑、写入或删除文件。
One engineer suggests a system prompt for the subagent beginning. You are a read-only reviewer, Never edit, write or delete files under any circumstances.

986
01:27:39,520 --> 01:27:42,244
强制执行这一要求最可靠的方法是什么？
What is the most reliable way to enforce this?

987
01:27:42,734 --> 01:27:48,772
a. 使用建议的系统提示词，并在 clot.md 中添加约束作为强化。
a Use the suggested system prompt and add the constraint to clot.md as reinforcement.

988
01:27:49,440 --> 01:27:49,760
b.
b.

989
01:27:50,318 --> 01:27:54,756
定义该子代理时仅包含只读工具，这样它的工具集中根本就没有写入工具。
Define the subagent with only read tools so write tools are not in its tool set at all.

990
01:27:55,200 --> 01:28:00,996
c. 让协调者检查子代理的输出，并拒绝任何文件修改。
C. Have the coordinator inspect the subagent's output and reject any file modifications.

991
01:28:01,440 --> 01:28:01,760
D.
D.

992
01:28:02,222 --> 01:28:06,244
将子代理的轮数限制设为 1，让它没有机会执行写入操作。
Run the subagent with the turn cap set to 1 so it has no opportunity to write.

993
01:28:06,638 --> 01:28:07,716
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

994
01:28:13,358 --> 01:28:18,752
答案是 B，这是模块 0 中关于限定条件的课程派上用场了。
The answer is B, and this is the qualifier lesson from Module 0 paying off.

995
01:28:19,374 --> 01:28:23,364
「无论如何提示」这个短语排除了其他选项。
The phrase regardless of how it is prompted eliminates options.

996
01:28:23,822 --> 01:28:27,652
在读完之前，A 以及任何其他基于提示词形状的答案都可以排除。
A and any other prompt shaped answer before you have finished reading them.

997
01:28:28,590 --> 01:28:35,236
如果要求是“无论如何提示”，那么从定义上讲，没有任何提示能满足这个条件。
If the requirement is stated as regardless of prompting, then by definition, no prompt satisfies it.

998
01:28:35,982 --> 01:28:41,124
选项 B 有效，因为子代理如果没有某个工具，就无法调用该工具。
Option B works because a tool the subagent does not have is a tool it cannot call.

999
01:28:41,806 --> 01:28:46,564
无论面对什么样的指令、任何越狱手段，还是任何搞混了的审核员，这一点都成立。
That holds under any instruction, any jailbreak, and any confused reviewer.

1000
01:28:47,470 --> 01:28:55,588
选项 C 是事后检测。更糟糕的是，协调者只能看到最终消息，所以它根本看不到写入操作。
Option C is detection after the event. And worse, the coordinator only ever sees the final message. So it would not even see the write.

1001
01:28:57,006 --> 01:28:59,524
选项 D 误解了什么是“轮次”。
Option D misunderstands what a turn is.

1002
01:29:00,654 --> 01:29:06,084
一个轮次就足够调用写入工具了，而且这也会让需要读取多个文件的审核员感到困惑。
One turn is plenty to call a write tool, and it also breaks a reviewer that needs to read several files.

1003
01:29:06,958 --> 01:29:07,844
模块 4。
Module 4.

1004
01:29:08,814 --> 01:29:12,100
接下来，讲关于会话和保证结果的内容。
Next, on sessions and guaranteed outcomes.

1005
01:29:13,422 --> 01:29:16,132
模块 4，是领域 1 的最后一个部分。
Module 4, the last of domain 1.

1006
01:29:16,462 --> 01:29:18,692
这是两个相关联的组成部分。
Two halves and they belong together.

1007
01:29:19,072 --> 01:29:20,772
第一部分是会话。
The first is sessions.

1008
01:29:21,072 --> 01:29:26,148
它包含什么内容，你如何返回到第 1 步，以及为什么有时返回并不是正确的做法。
What they hold, how you return to 1, and why returning is sometimes the wrong move.

1009
01:29:26,592 --> 01:29:29,668
第二部分解决了在模块 1 中开启的一个话题。
The second half closes a thread opened in module 1.

1010
01:29:30,542 --> 01:29:37,380
我们当时说过，触发护栏是失败而非结束，而且模型之外的某些东西必须能识别出这种区别。
We said then that hitting a guardrail is a failure rather than a finish, and that something outside the model has to notice the difference.

1011
01:29:37,902 --> 01:29:39,748
本模块就是构建那个“东西”。
This module builds that something.

1012
01:29:40,654 --> 01:29:46,272
到最后，你应该能够毫不犹豫地回答任何包含“保证”这个词的问题。
By the end, you should be able to answer any question containing the word guarantee without hesitating.

1013
01:29:47,566 --> 01:29:53,156
从定义开始，因为这个领域里一半的错误答案都是因为过度解读导致的。
Start with the definition because half the wrong answers in this area come from overreading it.

1014
01:29:53,582 --> 01:29:58,432
会话是智能体在工作过程中积累的对话历史。
A session is the conversation history the agent accumulated while it worked.

1015
01:29:58,862 --> 01:30:05,732
包括你的提示词、它执行的每一次工具调用、返回的每一个工具结果，以及它给出的每一个回复。
Your prompt, every tool call it made, every tool result that came back, and every response it gave.

1016
01:30:06,192 --> 01:30:09,700
它会自动写入磁盘，以便你可以返回到之前的状态。
It is written to disk automatically, so you can return to it.

1017
01:30:10,032 --> 01:30:12,484
它不是什么，是你的系统快照。
What it is not is a snapshot of your system.

1018
01:30:12,992 --> 01:30:18,052
这种区别听起来很琐碎，直到它决定一个问题的答案时，这个区别就变得至关重要了。
The distinction sounds pedantic right up until it decides a question, which it does.

1019
01:30:19,598 --> 01:30:23,492
具体来说，会话按顺序保存完整的消息数组。
Concretely, a session holds the full message array in order.

1020
01:30:24,192 --> 01:30:28,992
每一个提示词、每一个响应、每一次工具调用和每一个工具结果。
Every prompt, every response, every tool call, and every tool result.

1021
01:30:31,150 --> 01:30:36,868
SDK 会在过程中将其写入磁盘，作为项目目录下的一个转录记录文件。
The SDK writes it to disk as it goes, as a transcript file under the project directory.

1022
01:30:37,902 --> 01:30:41,924
查询是项目感知的，这比听起来要重要得多。
Lookup is project aware, which matters more than it sounds.

1023
01:30:42,862 --> 01:30:47,140
如果你从不同的目录运行 resume 命令，就不会形成会话。
Run the resume command from a different directory and the session is not formed.

1024
01:30:47,472 --> 01:30:50,340
而且转录记录保存在创建它的机器上。
And the transcript lives on the machine that created it.

1025
01:30:51,246 --> 01:30:55,844
全新的 CI 工作节点或临时容器根本不知道它的存在。
A fresh CI worker or an ephemeral container has no knowledge of it at all.

1026
01:30:57,518 --> 01:31:00,164
最后一点会在本模块的后面再次出现。
That last point comes back later in this module.

1027
01:31:01,838 --> 01:31:04,228
这就是容易误导考生的区别点。
Here is the distinction that catches people.

1028
01:31:04,622 --> 01:31:06,672
会话保留对话内容。
Sessions persist the conversation.

1029
01:31:06,912 --> 01:31:08,868
它们不保留文件系统。
They do not persist the file system.

1030
01:31:09,550 --> 01:31:15,712
如果智能体在会话期间写入了文件，那个写入操作已经保存在磁盘上并保持不变。
If the agent wrote to a file during a session, that write is already on disk and it stays there.

1031
01:31:15,952 --> 01:31:20,804
恢复会话会让智能体记住它做过那个更改。
Resuming the session gives the agent its memory of having made that change.

1032
01:31:21,646 --> 01:31:24,100
它既不会撤销这个操作，也不会重新执行。
It does not undo it and it does not redo it.

1033
01:31:24,526 --> 01:31:31,076
如果你想对实际的文件更改进行快照并还原，那是检查点机制，这是一个完全独立的机制。
If you want to snapshot and revert actual file changes, that is checkpointing, which is a completely separate mechanism.

1034
01:31:31,534 --> 01:31:32,900
把这个术语读两遍。
Read the call out twice.

1035
01:31:33,390 --> 01:31:37,764
恢复操作是恢复编辑记忆，而不是提供撤销编辑的能力。
Resuming restores memory of editing, never the ability to un-edit.

1036
01:31:39,406 --> 01:31:44,196
有四种启动方式，考试要求你根据场景在这些选项中做出选择。
Four ways to begin, and the exam expects you to pick between them from a scenario.

1037
01:31:45,006 --> 01:31:50,084
Continue 或 dash C 会恢复当前目录中最近的会话。
Continue or dash C resumes the most recent session in the current directory.

1038
01:31:50,670 --> 01:31:54,212
这是在你今早继续昨晚中断的地方时使用的快捷命令。
That is the quick one for carrying on this morning where you stopped last night.

1039
01:31:55,086 --> 01:31:58,468
Resume 通过 ID 或名称来获取特定的会话。
Resume takes a specific session by ID or by name.

1040
01:31:58,832 --> 01:32:02,112
值得记住的一点是，它只负责恢复。
And the thing worth remembering is that it only ever resumes.

1041
01:32:02,272 --> 01:32:03,780
它从不创建新会话。
It never creates a session.

1042
01:32:04,366 --> 01:32:07,876
Fork 会话 从某一点开始恢复并写入到一个新会话中。
Fork session resumes from a point and writes into a new session.

1043
01:32:08,432 --> 01:32:11,556
保留原始的 ID，让原有的内容保持不变。
ID, leaving the original exactly as it was.

1044
01:32:13,198 --> 01:32:15,524
而运行 plain 则会给你一个全新的开始。
And running plane gives you a clean slate.

1045
01:32:16,432 --> 01:32:23,684
在启动时给你的会话命名，因为三个月后在操作手册中看到一串原始的 UID 是没有任何意义的。
Name your sessions when you start them because a raw U UID in a runbook three months later tell you nothing.

1046
01:32:25,326 --> 01:32:28,592
分叉是为了从同一个位置探索两条路径。
Forking is for exploring two paths from one position.

1047
01:32:28,974 --> 01:32:35,072
当你深入在一个会话中，想要尝试一个冒险的替代方案，且不想丢失当前进度时。
You are deep in a session, you want to try a risky alternative, and you do not want to lose the thread you are on.

1048
01:32:35,392 --> 01:32:41,152
进行分叉并进行实验，如果搞砸了，原始内容仍保留在另一个不同的会话中。
Fork, experiment, and if it goes badly, the original is still there with a different session.

1049
01:32:41,486 --> 01:32:43,876
它的 ID 和历史记录都不会被破坏。
ID and its history untouched.

1050
01:32:44,814 --> 01:32:46,912
两者都可以独立恢复。
Both remain separately resumable.

1051
01:32:47,072 --> 01:32:49,072
注意与之前相同的注意事项。
Note the same caveat as before.

1052
01:32:49,486 --> 01:32:52,740
分叉（Fork）是让对话分支化，而不是文件系统。
Forking branches the conversation and not the file system.

1053
01:32:52,910 --> 01:32:56,516
并注意最后一点，因为它是一个极具误导性的干扰项。
And note the last point because it is a distractor waiting to happen.

1054
01:32:56,832 --> 01:33:01,828
分叉会继承父级历史，因此对于缓解上下文压力毫无帮助。
A fork inherits the parent's history, so it does nothing at all for context pressure.

1055
01:33:03,374 --> 01:33:08,032
现在是尴尬的部分，也就是领域 1 交给领域 5 的地方。
Now the awkward part, and this is where domain 1 hands over to domain 5.

1056
01:33:08,238 --> 01:33:10,436
继续（Resume）能让你保留之前的所有内容。
Resuming gives you everything from before.

1057
01:33:11,214 --> 01:33:13,796
这是它的卖点，但同时也是问题所在。
That is the selling point, and it is also the problem.

1058
01:33:16,526 --> 01:33:21,604
因为这些历史记录描述的是获取数据时的世界状态。
The tune results in that history describe the world as it was when they were fetched.

1059
01:33:22,126 --> 01:33:25,860
假设你的同事从那时起合并了三个拉取请求（Pull Request）。
Say a colleague has merged three pull requests since then.

1060
01:33:26,352 --> 01:33:33,124
智能体现在是基于一个已不存在的仓库快照进行推理，而且它无法得知这一点。
The agent is now reasoning from a snapshot of a repository that no longer exists and it cannot know that.

1061
01:33:33,582 --> 01:33:35,620
它会非常有信心，但结果是错误的。
It would be confident and it would be wrong.

1062
01:33:37,390 --> 01:33:40,996
有四件事会过时，而第四点正是这种做法危险的原因。
Four things go stale, and the fourth is the reason this is dangerous.

1063
01:33:41,774 --> 01:33:43,552
几小时前读取的文件内容。
File contents read hours ago.

1064
01:33:43,632 --> 01:33:47,268
所以智能体相信旧版本，因为它确实只能看到那个版本。
So the agent believes the old version because that is genuinely what it can see.

1065
01:33:48,750 --> 01:33:50,436
查询结果和 API。
Query results and AP.

1066
01:33:51,014 --> 01:33:53,988
高响应数据在获取的那一刻就被冻结了。
High responses frozen at the moment they were fetched.

1067
01:33:54,478 --> 01:34:01,380
还有它基于这些数据得出的结论，它仍会坚持这些结论。问题出在最后一行。
And its own conclusions, which it drew from that data, and still holds. The problem is the last line.

1068
01:34:01,934 --> 01:34:06,468
转录记录中没有任何内容是以模型能识别为有意义的时间戳标注的。
Nothing in the transcript is timestamped in a way the model treats as meaningful.

1069
01:34:07,472 --> 01:34:11,152
周二的工具结果看起来和一秒钟前的结果一模一样。
A tool result from Tuesday looks exactly like one from a second

1070
01:34:11,152 --> 01:34:14,116
智能体无法分辨它们之间的区别。
ago. The agent cannot tell them apart.

1071
01:34:15,054 --> 01:34:18,628
只有你知道过去了多少时间，以及哪些内容发生了变化。
Only you know how much time has passed and what has moved.

1072
01:34:20,270 --> 01:34:21,348
所以，做出决定。
So the decision.

1073
01:34:21,934 --> 01:34:24,674
当连贯性比实时性更重要时，选择继续（Resume）。
resume when continuity matters more than freshness.

1074
01:34:25,234 --> 01:34:30,054
变化很小，间隔很短，且推理链条值得完整保留。
Little has changed, the gap was short, and the chain of reasoning is worth keeping whole.

1075
01:34:31,086 --> 01:34:34,788
当准确性更重要时，通过注入摘要来开启新会话（Start fresh）。
Start fresh with an injected summary when accuracy matters more.

1076
01:34:35,632 --> 01:34:41,508
在你离开期间世界发生了变化，那些过时的工具结果会误导智能体。
The world moved while you were away, and those stale tool results would actively mislead the agent.

1077
01:34:41,872 --> 01:34:48,548
在新建会话的情况下，你带过去的是你的结论而非原始历史，这虽然牺牲了一些细节，但换取了准确性。
In the fresh case, you carry across your conclusions rather than the raw history, which costs you nuance and buys you correctness.

1078
01:34:49,966 --> 01:34:52,100
决定权在于一个问题。
The tiebreaker is one question.

1079
01:34:53,198 --> 01:34:54,884
“我不在的时候，有什么变动吗？”
What changed while I was gone?

1080
01:34:55,758 --> 01:34:56,900
如果答案是“没变”，那就选择继续（Resume）。
Nothing means resume.

1081
01:34:57,454 --> 01:35:00,868
某些内容意味着开启一个携带你现有知识的新会话。
Something means a fresh session carrying what you know now.

1082
01:35:02,510 --> 01:35:07,620
如果你选择这种新路径，摘要就在发挥实效，所以值得好好去写。
If you go the fresh route, the summary is doing real work, so it is worth writing properly.

1083
01:35:08,272 --> 01:35:12,900
带上决策及其背后的原因，而不是产生这些决策的讨论过程。
Carry the decisions and the reasons behind them, not the discussion that produced them.

1084
01:35:14,606 --> 01:35:17,188
带上描述为“当前状态”的内容。
Carry the current state described as current.

1085
01:35:17,312 --> 01:35:21,092
这样智能体就不会在新的外壳中继承过时的信息。
So the agent is not inheriting a stale picture in a new wrapper.

1086
01:35:22,062 --> 01:35:25,732
带上仍未解决的内容、已被排除的内容以及排除的原因。
Carry what is still open and what was ruled out and why.

1087
01:35:26,192 --> 01:35:30,244
否则，它会热心地建议你已经拒绝过的方案。
Because otherwise, it will helpfully suggest the thing you already rejected.

1088
01:35:30,702 --> 01:35:32,964
并且不要把转录记录粘贴回去。
And do not paste the transcript back in.

1089
01:35:33,518 --> 01:35:39,428
如果你这样做，就相当于手动重建了续传，并导入了你试图摆脱的所有过时素材。
If you do, you have rebuilt resume by hand and imported all the stale material you were trying to escape.

1090
01:35:41,038 --> 01:35:46,084
有一个实用的领域值得了解，因为 CI 本身就是一个独立的考试场景。
One practical area worth knowing because CI is an exam scenario in its own right.

1091
01:35:46,672 --> 01:35:48,996
会话转录记录是本地文件。
Session transcripts are local files.

1092
01:35:49,472 --> 01:35:56,996
新的 CI 工作节点没有任何这些文件，而且容器在重启时会丢失它们，除非主目录被挂载为卷。
A fresh CI worker has none of them, and a container loses them on restart unless the home directory is mounted as a volume.

1093
01:35:58,030 --> 01:36:04,996
如果你打算通过程序方式恢复，请在第一次运行结束时从结构化输出中获取会话 ID。
If you intend to resume programmatically, capture the session ID from the structured output when the first run finishes.

1094
01:36:05,550 --> 01:36:10,212
若要在不同的宿主上继续，要么移动转录记录文件，要么连接一个会话存储。
To resume on a different host, either move the transcript file or attach a session store.

1095
01:36:12,366 --> 01:36:15,744
存储会将转录记录镜像到两个宿主都能访问的地方。
A store mirrors transcripts somewhere both hosts can reach.

1096
01:36:16,366 --> 01:36:18,404
并且不要依赖 CI 中的 continue 命令。
And do not lean on continue in CI.

1097
01:36:19,086 --> 01:36:23,844
对于一个 90 秒前才创建的机器来说，这个目录中“最近的会话”毫无意义。
Most recent session in this directory means nothing on a machine that was created 90 seconds ago.

1098
01:36:25,454 --> 01:36:26,660
这就是会话。
That is sessions.

1099
01:36:26,944 --> 01:36:35,876
现在是第二部分，也是更有价值的一部分。到目前为止的所有内容都假设智能体的运行已经结束，而你正在决定如何回到那个点。
Now the second half, and it is the more valuable one. Everything so far assumes the agent's run ended and you are deciding how to come back to it.

1100
01:36:36,144 --> 01:36:39,584
更难的问题是，你如何知道它是否真的正常结束了。
The harder question is how you know it ended properly at all.

1101
01:36:40,206 --> 01:36:45,764
这就是模块 1 中关于“终止符”和“守卫栏”的区别转化为架构的地方。
This is where module 1's distinction between a terminator and a guardrain turns into architecture.

1102
01:36:46,064 --> 01:36:49,220
这也是几乎出现在每一份试卷上的问题类型。
It is also a question shape that appears on nearly every paper.

1103
01:36:50,702 --> 01:36:55,204
运行有六种结束方式，只有第一种意味着工作真正完成了。
Six ways a run can end and only the first means the work is actually done.

1104
01:36:55,854 --> 01:37:00,384
“结束轮次”，即 Claude 没有产生任何工具调用，这才是真正的完成。
End turn, where clot produced no tool calls, is a genuine completion.

1105
01:37:00,814 --> 01:37:04,612
“轮数限制”触发，意味着它在执行过程中耗尽了迭代次数。
The turn cap firing means it ran out of iterations part way through.

1106
01:37:04,784 --> 01:37:08,388
“预算限制”触发，意味着它在执行过程中耗尽了资金。
The budget cap firing means it ran out of money part way through.

1107
01:37:09,104 --> 01:37:12,644
执行过程中的错误，意味着工具超时或调用失败。
An error during execution means a tool through or a call failed.

1108
01:37:13,104 --> 01:37:21,092
“拒绝”意味着 Claude 拒绝了请求。记住模块 1 的内容：这作为正常的成功响应返回，而不是作为一个错误。
A refusal means clot declined. And remember from module 1 that this arrives as a normal successful response rather than an error.

1109
01:37:21,504 --> 01:37:26,020
而“上下文窗口填满”意味着根本没有空间放置下一轮的内容。
And the context window filling means there was simply nowhere to put the next turn.

1110
01:37:26,478 --> 01:37:27,424
把通话带出来。
Lead the call out.

1111
01:37:28,398 --> 01:37:30,724
这六种情况中有五种会导致工作没完成。
Five of those six leave work unfinished.

1112
01:37:31,246 --> 01:37:37,316
所以，如果代码只读取“循环退出且任务成功”，就会把五种失败的情况误报为成功。
So code that reads loop exited as task succeeded will report five kinds of failure as success.

1113
01:37:38,958 --> 01:37:40,100
所以你要给它套个包装。
So you wrap it.

1114
01:37:40,878 --> 01:37:42,624
在设置了上限的情况下运行智能体。
Run the agent with cap set.

1115
01:37:43,214 --> 01:37:48,944
当它返回时，去判断它是如何结束的，读取结构化结果而不是纯文本。
When it comes back, classify how it ended, reading the structured result rather than the prose.

1116
01:37:49,390 --> 01:37:51,844
然后决定这个结局意味着什么。
Then decide what that ending means.

1117
01:37:52,464 --> 01:37:55,940
是完成、重试、继续还是上报给人工处理。
Complete, retry, resume, or escalate to a person.

1118
01:37:56,910 --> 01:38:04,964
并且要确保每条路径都有明确的终点，不能让任何交互在没人接手的情况下悄悄结束。
And make sure every one of those paths terminates somewhere definite so that no interaction can end quietly with nobody holding it.

1119
01:38:05,614 --> 01:38:11,492
这个包装层的作用就是把一个“通常能完成”的智能体变成一个“总有明确结果”的系统。
That wrapper is what converts an agent that usually finishes into a system that always ends somewhere.

1120
01:38:12,110 --> 01:38:16,420
它不能放在智能体内部，因为智能体本身就是可能失败的东西。
It cannot live inside the agent because the agent is the thing that might have failed.

1121
01:38:17,998 --> 01:38:21,892
这个对比是领域一中最具通用性的内容。
This comparison is the single most reusable thing in domain one.

1122
01:38:24,590 --> 01:38:27,300
保证可以存在于提示词中，也可以存在于代码中。
A guarantee can live in the prompt or in the code.

1123
01:38:28,782 --> 01:38:30,692
在提示词里，它是“说服”。
In the prompt, it is persuasion.

1124
01:38:31,310 --> 01:38:33,668
如果你无法解决问题，就必须上报。
Always escalate if you cannot resolve.

1125
01:38:35,214 --> 01:38:36,452
这在大多数情况下有效。
Works most of the time.

1126
01:38:37,006 --> 01:38:39,744
“大部分时间有效”正是陷阱所在。
Working most of the time is exactly the trap.

1127
01:38:40,304 --> 01:38:45,156
它恰恰会在智能体感到困惑时失效，而那正是你最需要它的时候。
It fails precisely when the agent is confused, which is when you needed it.

1128
01:38:45,584 --> 01:38:47,652
在代码里，它是“强制执行”。
In the code, it is enforcement.

1129
01:38:48,144 --> 01:38:55,460
无论智能体表现如何，无论过程如何演变，每次调用后都会运行的检查。
A check that runs after every invocation, whether the agent behaved or not, independent of how anything was phased.

1130
01:38:56,174 --> 01:38:58,628
它是可测试的，你可以把它展示给审计人员看。
It is testable and you can show it to an auditor.

1131
01:38:59,566 --> 01:39:06,148
当题干中使用“保证”这个词时，在阅读任何提示词选项前，所有的提示词方案就都被排除掉了。
When a STEM uses the word guarantee, every prompt shape option is eliminated before you have read them.

1132
01:39:07,954 --> 01:39:10,694
强制执行可以存在的四个位置。
Four places enforcement can actually sit.

1133
01:39:12,590 --> 01:39:20,996
在编排包装器中，在每次运行后进行检查，这是最通用的答案，也是针对结果问题时的正确做法。
In the orchestration wrapper, checking after every run, which is the most general answer and the right one when the question is about outcomes.

1134
01:39:21,934 --> 01:39:28,356
在工具本身内部，比如一个带自动核查限制的退款工具，无论智能体怎么想，都无法绕过。
Inside the tool itself, so a refund tool that checks its own limit cannot be top passed no matter what the agent believes.

1135
01:39:28,910 --> 01:39:34,084
在一个触发事件的钩子上，无论智能体的意图如何，它都能拦截操作。
In a hook which fires on an event regardless of what the agent intended and can block the action.

1136
01:39:34,862 --> 01:39:43,076
或者在工具集中，因为智能体没有权限使用的工具就是它不具备的能力，这只是看起来像个位置而已。
Or in the tool set, since a tool the agent does not have is a capability it does not have, and one place that only looks like a place.

1137
01:39:43,918 --> 01:39:49,732
Clot.md 和系统提示词都属于上下文，而上下文是“说服”而非“强制”。
Clot.md and the system prompt are both context, and context persuades rather than enforces.

1138
01:39:51,438 --> 01:39:53,156
还有一个包装层的职责。
One more wrapper responsibility.

1139
01:39:53,582 --> 01:39:57,156
一个中途失败的运行可能已经执行了不可逆的操作。
A run that failed halfway may already have done something irreversible.

1140
01:39:57,966 --> 01:40:01,636
退款已发出，票据已创建，邮件也已发送。
The refund went out, the ticket was created, the email was sent.

1141
01:40:02,062 --> 01:40:07,584
会话转录记录了发生了什么，这正是为什么继续执行比重新开始更安全的原因。
The session transcript records that it happened, which is exactly why resuming is safer than restarting.

1142
01:40:08,142 --> 01:40:14,624
从零开始盲目重试会把所有步骤都再跑一遍，包括那些已经成功的步骤。
A blind retry from a clean slate will happily do the whole thing again, including the parts that succeeded.

1143
01:40:14,864 --> 01:40:21,668
所以要么选择继续执行，让智能体看到它已经做了什么，要么就让你的有副作用的工具具备幂等性。
So either resume so the agent can see what it already did or make your side effecting tools idempotent.

1144
01:40:21,904 --> 01:40:23,588
这样重复操作就不会造成危害。
So a repeat is harmless.

1145
01:40:24,494 --> 01:40:30,884
“重试整个任务”听起来是个安全的答案，但只有在没有任何内容有副作用的情况下才真正安全。
Retry the whole task is a safe sounding answer that is only actually safe when nothing has side effects.

1146
01:40:32,494 --> 01:40:37,904
这就是模式识别：如果没有变化且我们想继续，就选“继续执行”。
Here is the pattern recognition. Nothing has changed and we want to carry on means resume.

1147
01:40:38,384 --> 01:40:43,428
如果智能体闲置时有内容被合并，就意味着需要带上当前摘要的“新会话”。
Something was merged while the agent was idle means a fresh session with a current summary.

1148
01:40:44,174 --> 01:40:47,524
在不丢失当前线程的情况下尝试备选方案，意味着“分支（fork）”。
Try an alternative without losing this thread means fork.

1149
01:40:48,334 --> 01:40:52,944
每次都使用全新的 CI 容器，意味着根本不存在任何会话。
A fresh CI container every time means no session exists at all.

1150
01:40:53,184 --> 01:40:56,804
所以你要捕获并传递 ID 或者挂载一个存储。
So you capture and pass the ID or attach a store.

1151
01:40:58,990 --> 01:41:05,216
确保每场对话最终都能解决或上报，这是编排层的功能，绝不是提示词的作用。
Guarantee every conversation ends resolved or escalated means the orchestration layer, never a prompt.

1152
01:41:05,856 --> 01:41:12,164
而在轮数限制处停止的运行，意味着你的代码必须对这些未完成的工作进行分类并采取行动。
And a run that stopped at the turn cap means unfinished work that your code has to classify and act on.

1153
01:41:12,942 --> 01:41:18,660
关于会话的问题，几乎总是取决于描述两次运行之间发生了什么的那个句子。
Session questions almost always turn on one sentence describing what happened between the two runs.

1154
01:41:20,366 --> 01:41:21,988
用 5 行代码来关闭领域。
5 lines to close domain.

1155
01:41:22,670 --> 01:41:27,812
1. 会话是磁盘上的对话历史，而不是文件系统的快照。
1. A session is conversation history on disk and not a snapshot of your file system.

1156
01:41:28,206 --> 01:41:34,884
对于最近的选“继续”，针对有名称的选“继续执行”，要分支选“分支”，记住，“继续执行”永远不会创建新内容。
Continue for the most recent, resume for a named one, fork to branch, and remember, resume never creates.

1157
01:41:35,456 --> 01:41:39,876
当没有任何变动时选择“继续执行”，当有变动时带上摘要开始新会话。
Resume when nothing moved and start fresh with a summary when something did.

1158
01:41:40,754 --> 01:41:47,364
在运行可能结束的六种情况中，有五个会导致工作未完成。所以要对结尾进行分类，而不是去猜测。
five of the six ways a run can end Leave work unfinished. So classify the ending rather than assuming it.

1159
01:41:47,616 --> 01:41:53,536
保证机制存在于代码中，因为提示词和记忆文件属于上下文，而上下文起的是说服作用。
And guarantees live in code because prompts and memory files are context and context persuades.

1160
01:41:54,256 --> 01:41:58,084
现在是 5 个场景。然后我们进入领域 2 和工具设计。
5 scenarios now. Then we move into domain 2 and tool design.

1161
01:41:59,790 --> 01:42:00,676
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

1162
01:42:01,262 --> 01:42:06,692
一个智能体正与一名工程师共同进行大规模重构，已经持续了 2 小时。
An agent has been working through a large refactor with an engineer for 2 hours.

1163
01:42:07,534 --> 01:42:09,316
工程师去吃午饭了。
The engineer breaks for lunch.

1164
01:42:09,934 --> 01:42:15,140
在他不在的时候，一位同事合并了一个分支，更改了四个函数的签名。
While they are away, a colleague merges a branch that changes the signatures of four functions.

1165
01:42:15,790 --> 01:42:18,244
这些是智能体已经阅读并思考过的内容。
The agent has already read and reasoned about.

1166
01:42:19,086 --> 01:42:23,940
工程师回来了并想继续工作，而剩余的工作依赖于那四个函数。
The engineer returns and wants to continue, and the remaining work depends on those four functions.

1167
01:42:24,942 --> 01:42:27,012
最可靠的继续方式是什么？
What is the most reliable way to continue?

1168
01:42:27,502 --> 01:42:31,940
a. 继续执行会话，让智能体保留对重构的完整理解。
a resume the session so the agent keeps its full understanding of the refactor.

1169
01:42:32,736 --> 01:42:32,976
b。
b.

1170
01:42:33,456 --> 01:42:37,988
继续执行会话，并要求智能体在继续之前重新阅读那四个文件。
Resume the session and ask the agent to reread the four files before continuing.

1171
01:42:38,766 --> 01:42:38,976
C。
C.

1172
01:42:39,694 --> 01:42:44,452
开启一个包含已做决策和当前代码状态摘要的新会话。
Start a fresh session with a summary of decisions made and the current state of the code.

1173
01:42:45,454 --> 01:42:50,244
D。为了保留合并前的版本以便对比。
D. For the session so the pre-merge version is preserved for comparison.

1174
01:42:51,566 --> 01:42:52,708
稍停一下，做决定。
Pause and decide.

1175
01:42:58,414 --> 01:42:59,536
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

1176
01:42:59,776 --> 01:43:05,284
埋设的短语是「在他们不在场时」，它的作用是告诉你上下文不再符合现实情况。
The planted phrase is while they were away, which exists to tell you the context no longer matches reality.

1177
01:43:05,616 --> 01:43:09,412
选项 B 是最强的干扰项，值得好好理解一下。
Option B is the strongest distractor and worth understanding properly.

1178
01:43:09,696 --> 01:43:13,572
重新读取文件确实会将当前内容放入对话中。
Rereading the files does put current content into the conversation.

1179
01:43:14,416 --> 01:43:19,364
但由于会话是仅追加的，旧内容也会留在那里。
It also leaves the old content sitting there because a session is append only.

1180
01:43:19,776 --> 01:43:26,308
智能体现在持有四个函数的两个版本，且没有任何标记说明哪个是当前的，它可能会基于其中任何一个进行推理。
The agent now holds two versions of four functions with nothing marking which is current, and it may reason from either.

1181
01:43:26,894 --> 01:43:30,116
这可以说比选项 A 中那种清晰的失败情况还要糟糕。
That is arguably worse than the clean failure in option A.

1182
01:43:31,022 --> 01:43:36,996
选项 D 将陈旧的历史记录复制到第二个会话中，让你得到两份错误的画面。
Option D copies the stale history into a second session, giving you two copies of the wrong picture.

1183
01:43:37,742 --> 01:43:42,884
选项 C 则抛弃了陈旧读取，只把决策带到下一步。
Option C leaves the stale reads behind and carries only the decisions forward.

1184
01:43:44,462 --> 01:43:45,668
场景 2。
Scenario 2.

1185
01:43:46,574 --> 01:43:49,028
一个支持智能体负责处理账单查询。
A support agent resolves billing queries.

1186
01:43:49,870 --> 01:43:56,516
政策要求每一场对话都必须以解决问题或升级到人工客服结束，没有任何例外。
Policy requires that every conversation ends either resolved or escalated to a human with no exceptions.

1187
01:43:56,816 --> 01:44:00,420
系统提示词用强硬的措辞清晰地说明了这一点。
The system prompt states this clearly and in strong terms.

1188
01:44:04,142 --> 01:44:08,196
生产数据表明，97% 的对话正确结束。
Production data shows 97% of conversations end correctly.

1189
01:44:09,166 --> 01:44:18,976
剩下的 3% 在智能体发出最终消息后就结束了，没有进行升级，导致客户既没得到解决也没收到工单。
The remaining 3% end with the agent producing a final message and no escalation, leaving the customer with no resolution and no ticket.

1190
01:44:19,296 --> 01:44:26,084
调查显示，这些情况是智能体认为自己解决了问题但实际上并未解决的情况。
Investigation shows these are cases where the agent believed it had resolved the issue but had not.

1191
01:44:28,174 --> 01:44:30,692
什么方法能最可靠地填补这一差距？
What most reliably closes the gap?

1192
01:44:31,566 --> 01:44:37,444
a. 通过明确需要升级的情况示例来强化系统提示词。
a strengthen the system prompt with explicit examples of situations requiring escalation.

1193
01:44:37,966 --> 01:44:44,516
b. 在每场对话后增加一个编排检查，对任何未标记为已解决的交互进行升级。
b. Add an orchestration check after each conversation that escalates any interaction not marked resolved.

1194
01:44:44,976 --> 01:44:50,948
C. 在 plot.m d 中添加一条规则：只要智能体不确定就必须进行升级。
C. Add a rule to plot.m d requiring escalation whenever the agent is uncertain.

1195
01:44:51,726 --> 01:44:51,936
D。
D.

1196
01:44:52,526 --> 01:44:56,644
降低智能体选择进行升级的置信度阈值。
Lower the confidence threshold at which the agent chooses to escalate.

1197
01:44:57,134 --> 01:44:58,212
稍停一下，做决定。
Pause and decide.

1198
01:45:03,822 --> 01:45:05,156
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1199
01:45:05,440 --> 01:45:09,316
题干的最后一句起到了关键作用，但很容易被忽略过去。
The last sentence of the stem does the work and it is easy to skim past.

1200
01:45:09,680 --> 01:45:12,836
这些情况是智能体认为自己已经解决了问题的情况。
These are cases where the agent believed it had resolved the issue.

1201
01:45:13,280 --> 01:45:20,580
这一个事实同时排除了 A、C 和 D，因为这三项都依赖于智能体识别出它并不知道的故障。
That single fact eliminates A, C, and D together because all three depend on the agent recognizing a failure it does not know it is having.

1202
01:45:21,358 --> 01:45:23,680
选项 D 最具启发性。
Option D is the most instructive.

1203
01:45:23,920 --> 01:45:30,980
降低升级阈值只有在智能体不确定时才有用，而从定义上讲，这些智能体是很有把握的。
Lowering the escalation threshold only helps when the agent is uncertain, and by definition, these agents were confident.

1204
01:45:32,526 --> 01:45:36,516
选项 B 有效是因为它根本不会询问智能体任何内容。
Option B works because it never asks the agent anything.

1205
01:45:37,294 --> 01:45:43,428
它在对话后运行，检查交互是否被标记为已解决，如果没有，则进行升级。
It runs after the conversation, checks whether the interaction is marked, resolved, and escalates it if not.

1206
01:45:45,262 --> 01:45:50,480
选项 C 也在一个并非硬编码的部署中寻求 Claude Code 机制。
Option C also reaches for a clot code mechanism in a deployment that is not clothed code.

1207
01:45:51,854 --> 01:45:52,868
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

1208
01:45:53,120 --> 01:46:00,324
一个夜间任务运行一个智能体，对前一天的错误报告进行分诊，且每次运行都在全新的 CI 容器中进行。
A nightly job runs an agent that triages the previous day's error reports and each run happens on a fresh CI container.

1209
01:46:00,814 --> 01:46:08,452
团队希望每晚的运行都能记住前一晚得出的结论，这样重复出现的错误就能被识别出来，而不是从头开始重新调查。
The team wants each night's run to remember what it concluded the night before, so recurring errors are recognized rather than reinvestigated from scratch.

1210
01:46:09,200 --> 01:46:12,004
他们在命令中添加了 continue 标志。
They have added the continue flag to the command.

1211
01:46:12,400 --> 01:46:15,236
但每次运行仍然表现得像第一次运行一样。
Every run still behaves as though it is the first.

1212
01:46:17,646 --> 01:46:19,588
为什么？他们应该改用什么方法？
Why? And what should they do instead?

1213
01:46:20,494 --> 01:46:25,220
A. Continue 只在交互式模式下有效，所以请使用带会话的 resume。
A. Continue only works interactively, so use resume with the session.

1214
01:46:25,680 --> 01:46:26,916
改为用 ID。
ID instead.

1215
01:46:27,790 --> 01:46:35,620
b. 容器磁盘上没有之前的会话，所以请持久化转录记录或会话存储，或者在文件中传递结论。
b. The container has no prior session on disk, so persist the transcript or a session store or carry conclusions forward in a file.

1216
01:46:36,160 --> 01:46:42,340
C. 会话在 24 小时后过期，所以到任务运行时，前一晚的会话已经消失了。
C. Sessions expire after 24 hours, so the previous night session is gone by the time the job runs.

1217
01:46:42,960 --> 01:46:43,280
D。
D.

1218
01:46:43,680 --> 01:46:49,636
Continue 要求会话必须正常结束，而 CI 运行正被 轮数限制 强制终止。
Continue needs the session to have ended cleanly and C I runs are being terminated by the turncap.

1219
01:46:51,118 --> 01:46:52,132
暂停一下，思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1220
01:46:57,806 --> 01:46:58,884
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1221
01:46:59,310 --> 01:47:03,520
「一个全新的 CI 容器」这个短语就是整个问题的核心。
The phrase a fresh C I container is the entire question.

1222
01:47:03,680 --> 01:47:14,340
会话转录记录是机器上的文件，而这台机器昨天并不存在，所以没有任何内容可以继续。选项 A 是最强的干扰项，因为它有一半是对的。
Session transcripts are files on a machine, and this machine did not exist yesterday, so there is nothing to continue. Option A is the strongest destructor because it is half-right.

1223
01:47:15,022 --> 01:47:23,332
Resume 会读取特定的 ID 而不是去猜测，但它仍然读取本地转录记录，而这个容器根本没有任何转录记录。
Resume does take a specific ID rather than guessing, but it still reads a local transcript, and this container has no transcripts at all.

1224
01:47:23,982 --> 01:47:29,892
要让 A 生效，你还必须移动文件或连接一个存储，而这正是 B 所说的。
To make A work, you would also have to move the file or attach a store, which is what B says.

1225
01:47:30,318 --> 01:47:33,284
选项 C 和 D 都虚构了行为。
Options C and D both invent behavior.

1226
01:47:34,062 --> 01:47:42,404
注意它们都提供了一种听起来合理的机制，但都没有解释为什么第二次运行仍被当作第一次运行。
Notice how both offer a mechanism that sounds plausible and neither explains why even the second run behaves as a first run.

1227
01:47:44,174 --> 01:47:45,060
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

1228
01:47:45,486 --> 01:47:47,920
一个智能体处理供应商发票。
An agent processes supplier invoices.

1229
01:47:48,314 --> 01:47:54,692
Kit 验证发票，将其记录在账本中并发出付款，而支付操作不是幂等的。
Kit validates the invoice, records it in the ledger and issues payment and Payment is not idempotent.

1230
01:47:55,040 --> 01:47:57,252
其中一次运行在过程中失败了。
One run failed part way through.

1231
01:47:57,600 --> 01:48:03,620
发票已验证并记录，但在支付前网络错误中断了运行。
The invoice was validated and recorded, then a network error interrupted the run before payment.

1232
01:48:04,558 --> 01:48:10,276
编排层的重试逻辑会携带相同的输入从头开始任务。
The orchestration layers retry logic starts the task again from the beginning with the same input.

1233
01:48:10,862 --> 01:48:14,084
团队现在正在调查重复的账本条目。
The team is now investigating duplicate ledger entries.

1234
01:48:14,320 --> 01:48:16,400
最合适的修改是什么？
What is the most appropriate change?

1235
01:48:16,750 --> 01:48:21,668
a 增加更长的超时时间，降低网络错误导致运行中断的概率。
a add a longer timeout so network errors are less likely to interrupt a run.

1236
01:48:22,702 --> 01:48:29,668
b 继续失败的会话而不是重新开始，并让有副作用的工具具有幂等性。
b Resume the failed session rather than restarting and make the side effecting tools idem potent.

1237
01:48:30,478 --> 01:48:35,012
c 将整个任务封装在数据库事务中，一旦失败就回滚。
C. Wrap the whole task in a database transaction that rolls back on failure.

1238
01:48:35,758 --> 01:48:40,324
d 让智能体在记录之前检查是否存在已有的账本条目。
d Have the agent check for an existing ledger entry before recording one.

1239
01:48:41,326 --> 01:48:42,340
稍停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

1240
01:48:48,014 --> 01:48:49,264
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1241
01:48:49,966 --> 01:48:54,304
这个场景的核心在于检查应该放在哪里以及相关的选项。
This scenario is really about where a check belongs and options.

1242
01:48:54,958 --> 01:48:57,380
B 和 D 的思路都是正确的。
B and D are both the right idea.

1243
01:48:58,254 --> 01:49:06,628
选项 D 要求智能体在记录前检查现有条目，这取决于智能体是否记得去查。
Option D asks the agent to check for an existing ledger entry before recording one, which works whenever the agent remembers.

1244
01:49:07,502 --> 01:49:13,316
选项 B 将同样的检查放入工具内部，无论智能体是否考虑到它都会执行。
Option B puts the same check inside the tool where it runs whether the agent thought of it or not.

1245
01:49:14,702 --> 01:49:19,652
这就是本模块前面提到的针对有副作用操作的强制执行原则。
That is the enforcement principle from earlier in this module applied to a side effect.

1246
01:49:20,462 --> 01:49:27,748
选项 B 的前半部分更好，因为继续会话能让智能体看到已完成的操作，而不是从零开始。
Option B also has the better first half, since resuming lets the agent see what it already did rather than starting cold.

1247
01:49:28,270 --> 01:49:35,876
选项 C 对有数据库背景的人很有吸引力，但支付是外部调用，没有对应的事务规则支持。
Option C is tempting to anyone with a database background, but the payment is an external call and no transaction rules that back.

1248
01:49:36,686 --> 01:49:41,984
选项 A 只是减少了遇到问题的频率，并没有解决问题本身。
Option A reduces how often you hit the problem and does nothing about the problem.

1249
01:49:43,278 --> 01:49:44,384
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

1250
01:49:44,590 --> 01:49:50,564
一个智能体执行隔夜数据对账，调用时设有 30 次的轮数限制和预算限制。
An agent performs overnight data reconciliation invoked with a turn cap of 30 and a budget cap.

1251
01:49:51,150 --> 01:50:00,164
只要调用返回时不抛出异常，编排包装器就会将运行记录为成功，并在跟踪系统中标记对账完成。
The orchestration wrapper logs a run as successful whenever the invocation returns without throwing an exception and then marks the reconciliation complete in the tracking system.

1252
01:50:01,102 --> 01:50:07,652
审计人员发现，在一些被标记为完成的对账中，大约有三分之一的记录从未被检查过。
An auditor has found reconciliations marked complete where roughly a third of the records were never examined.

1253
01:50:09,678 --> 01:50:10,884
根本原因是什么？
What is the root cause?

1254
01:50:11,502 --> 01:50:14,692
a 轮数限制对于如此大量的记录来说太低了。
a The turn cap is too low for the volume of records.

1255
01:50:15,184 --> 01:50:15,424
B。
B.

1256
01:50:15,918 --> 01:50:21,156
包装器将任何非异常的返回都视为成功，包括因达到限制而中止的运行。
The wrapper treats any non-exception return as success, including runs aborted by the caps.

1257
01:50:22,064 --> 01:50:22,384
C。
C.

1258
01:50:22,864 --> 01:50:26,692
应该指示智能体在未完成时进行报告。
The agent should be instructed to report when it has not finished.

1259
01:50:27,104 --> 01:50:31,620
d 对账任务应拆分到多个较小的调用中。
D. Reconciliation should be split across several smaller invocations.

1260
01:50:32,224 --> 01:50:33,700
稍停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

1261
01:50:39,406 --> 01:50:43,236
答案是 B，它解决了我们在第一模块中讨论的内容。
The answer is B, and it closes the thread we opened in module 1.

1262
01:50:43,886 --> 01:50:47,076
触发护栏并不算错误，也不算完成。
Hitting a guardrail is not an error and it is not a completion.

1263
01:50:47,310 --> 01:50:50,884
它是第三种结果，而这个封装器只识别两种。
It is a third outcome, and this wrapper only knows about 2.

1264
01:50:51,886 --> 01:50:57,156
因轮数限制而中止的运行会正常返回，不抛出任何内容，并被标记为已完成。
A run aborted by the turn cap returns normally, throws nothing and gets marked complete.

1265
01:50:58,064 --> 01:51:03,044
选项 A 是真正有贡献的，也是大家常选的答案。
Option A is genuinely contributing and it is the answer people pick.

1266
01:51:03,374 --> 01:51:10,468
但提高上限只会改变静默失败返回的频率，因为封装器仍然无法区分“完成”和“停止”。
But raising the cap only moves the volume at which the silent failure returns because the wrapper still cannot tell finish from stopped.

1267
01:51:10,864 --> 01:51:15,556
选项 C 要求一个已经没有剩余轮次来生成报告的运行提供报告。
Option C asks for a report from a run that has no turn left in which to make one.

1268
01:51:16,366 --> 01:51:24,996
选项 D 减少了触发限制的频率，而每个较小的运行仍会将受限的终止记录为成功。
Option D reduces how often a cap fires while each smaller run still records a capped abode as a success.

1269
01:51:25,664 --> 01:51:27,460
这部分内容结束了。
That closes domain 1.

1270
01:51:28,622 --> 01:51:29,572
领域 2
Domain 2

1271
01:51:30,222 --> 01:51:31,908
接下来是工具设计。
Next on tool design.

1272
01:51:33,774 --> 01:51:37,348
欢迎来到领域 2，即工具设计和 MCP 集成。
Welcome to domain 2, tool design and MCP integration.

1273
01:51:38,830 --> 01:51:41,796
占考试的 18%，大约有 11 道题。
18% of the exam, roughly 11 questions.

1274
01:51:42,382 --> 01:51:50,944
本模块是三个中的第一个，涵盖工具本身。即 Claude 在决定调用哪一个工具以及如何构建参数时所读取的内容。
This module is the first of three and it covers the tools themselves. What Claude reads when it decides which one to call and how to shape the parameters.

1275
01:51:51,502 --> 01:51:56,036
然后是拆分或合并的决策，考试会从两个方向来考查这一点。
Then the split or merge decision, which the exam tests in both directions.

1276
01:51:57,198 --> 01:51:58,756
开始前先提醒一下。
A warning before we start.

1277
01:51:59,662 --> 01:52:04,324
这些内容在你看的时候觉得显而易见，但在时间压力下却会变得很难。
This material feels obvious while you watch it and turns out to be hard under time pressure.

1278
01:52:04,704 --> 01:52:07,908
错误选项都是那些理智的工程师会做的事情。
The wrong answers are all things a sensible engineer would do.

1279
01:52:09,422 --> 01:52:10,692
这是基础知识。
Here is the foundation.

1280
01:52:11,284 --> 01:52:13,024
Claude 看不到你的具体实现。
Claude does not see your implementation.

1281
01:52:13,264 --> 01:52:22,148
它看不到你的测试、类型，或者你为了解释边缘情况而留下的注释。它只看到一个名称、一段描述和一个参数架构。
It does not see your tests, your types, or the comment you left explaining the edge case. It sees a name, a description, and a parameter schema.

1282
01:52:22,670 --> 01:52:24,132
这就是全部的交互界面。
That is the whole interface.

1283
01:52:24,784 --> 01:52:30,564
所以如果一个场景说 Claude 调用了错误的工具，或者传递了奇怪的参数，或者忽略了一个工具。
So a scenario says Clot called the wrong tool or passed an odd argument or ignored a tool.

1284
01:52:30,864 --> 01:52:32,464
首先看你写的文本。
Look first at the text you wrote.

1285
01:52:32,782 --> 01:52:34,244
Anthropic 把这一点说明得很清楚。
Anthropic put it plainly.

1286
01:52:34,544 --> 01:52:36,292
工具描述就是提示词。
Tool descriptions are prompts.

1287
01:52:36,622 --> 01:52:41,476
名称、描述和参数文档中的每一个词都在塑造行为。
Every word in the name, the description and the parameter documentation shapes behavior.

1288
01:52:42,958 --> 01:52:50,436
Anthropic 发布了五项原则，它们与考试考查的内容几乎完全吻合，所以值得作为参考框架。
Anthropic publishes five principles and they map almost exactly onto what the exam tests, so they are worth using as a frame.

1289
01:52:51,598 --> 01:52:58,724
选择正确的工具，意味着选择少数几个高杠杆的工具，而不是把你手头有的每个端点都套个薄薄的包装。
Choose the right tools, meaning a few high-leverage ones rather than a thin wrapper around every endpoint you happen to have.

1290
01:52:59,310 --> 01:53:00,228
给它们加上命名空间。
Namespace them.

1291
01:53:00,526 --> 01:53:03,748
这样智能体就不会在两个相似的选项中犹豫不决。
So the agent is not guessing between two similar neighbors.

1292
01:53:04,174 --> 01:53:09,380
返回有意义的上下文，也就是人类可读的字段，而不是原始标识符。
Return meaningful context, meaning human readable fields, rather than raw identifiers.

1293
01:53:09,824 --> 01:53:16,932
然后智能体需要进行查询，并通过合理的默认值、过滤、分页和截断来优化 Token 使用。
The agent then has to look up, optimize for tokens with sensible defaults, filtering, pagination, and truncation.

1294
01:53:17,550 --> 01:53:21,156
并且对描述进行提示词工程处理，因为它本身就是一个提示词。
And prompt engineer the description because it is a prompt.

1295
01:53:21,424 --> 01:53:26,372
本模块中的每一个问题都是这五个要点在不同场景下的变体。
Every question in this module is one of those five varying a scenario.

1296
01:53:27,918 --> 01:53:29,104
那么，第一个要点是什么？
So, what goes in one?

1297
01:53:29,550 --> 01:53:32,036
用一句清晰的话说明工具的功能。
What the tool does in a clear sentence.

1298
01:53:32,544 --> 01:53:39,492
何时使用它：描述时应基于智能体所处的场景，而不是底层机制。
When to use it, describe in terms of the situation the agent will be in rather than the mechanism underneath.

1299
01:53:40,304 --> 01:53:44,624
何时不使用它，以及至关重要的一点是，该用哪个工具代替。
When not to use it, and crucially, which tool to use instead.

1300
01:53:45,134 --> 01:53:49,744
它返回什么：让智能体在调用之前就能规划下一步。
What it returns so the agent can plan its next step before it even calls.

1301
01:53:49,984 --> 01:53:56,784
如果工具执行了破坏性或不可逆的操作，必须有明确的标记，因为智能体无法从名称中推断出这一点。
And an explicit flag if the tool does something destructive or irreversible, because the agent cannot infer that from a name.

1302
01:53:57,024 --> 01:53:59,876
大多数描述缺失的正是第三点。
The line most descriptions are missing is the third one.

1303
01:54:00,784 --> 01:54:06,692
「何时不使用」是真正防止错误选择的关键，但几乎没人去写它。
When not to use this is what actually prevents wrong selection, and almost nobody writes it.

1304
01:54:08,078 --> 01:54:10,064
这里是具体的区别。
Here is the difference concretely.

1305
01:54:10,414 --> 01:54:14,788
「检索数据库」是一个真实陈述，但却是个没用的描述。
Searches the database is a true statement and a useless description.

1306
01:54:15,566 --> 01:54:22,052
给智能体这样的描述，它会为了任何数据类请求去调用它，包括那些它根本无法回答的问题。
An agent given that will call it for anything data shaped, including questions it cannot possibly answer.

1307
01:54:22,304 --> 01:54:25,892
然后它才会从空结果中意识到自己犯了错。
It then works out from the empty result that it made a mistake.

1308
01:54:26,574 --> 01:54:32,420
第二个版本说明了它搜索什么、基于什么键值，以及数据追溯到多远。
The second version says what it searches, what it keys on, and how far back the data goes.

1309
01:54:32,704 --> 01:54:37,636
它还指明了处理特定已知订单时该用哪个工具，并说明了哪些内容被排除在外。
It also names the tool to use for a single known order and says what is excluded.

1310
01:54:38,094 --> 01:54:41,732
同样的代码，同样的架构，但完全不同的行为。
Same code, same schema, and completely different behavior.

1311
01:54:42,064 --> 01:54:44,900
这就是本模块核心内容的总结表。
That is the whole lesson of this module in one table.

1312
01:54:46,544 --> 01:54:48,624
命名比你想象的更重要。
Names matter more than they should.

1313
01:54:48,864 --> 01:54:59,428
清晰胜过巧妙。如果工具集中包含「获取用户」和「获取用户」，智能体就像在抛硬币，再多的描述也救不了场。
Distinct beats clever. If a tool set contains get user and fetch user, the agent is effectively flipping a coin and no amount of description will fully rescue that.

1314
01:54:59,918 --> 01:55:09,284
当你有多个来源时，按领域划分命名空间，比如「财务_查询支出」，让智能体在读到任何描述之前就知道它属于哪个范畴。
When you have several sources, namespace by domain, so finance get expenses tells the agent where it lives before it reads a word of description.

1315
01:55:09,838 --> 01:55:11,204
注意第三点。
And note the third point.

1316
01:55:11,694 --> 01:55:16,164
重叠的工具是选择问题，而不是文档问题。
Overlapping tools are a selection problem rather than a documentation problem.

1317
01:55:17,024 --> 01:55:21,264
解决方法是消除重叠，而不是多写点字去解释它。
The fix is to remove the overlap, not to write more words about it.

1318
01:55:21,646 --> 01:55:25,124
Anthropic 提供的参数示例值得记住。
Anthropic's own parameter example is worth memorizing.

1319
01:55:25,424 --> 01:55:28,900
称之为「用户_ID」，而不是「用户」。
Call it user underscore ID, not user.

1320
01:55:30,446 --> 01:55:41,380
参数是虚构信息的起点，所以要设计它们以消除猜测。尽可能使用枚举，因为枚举能让无效值变得不可能，而不仅仅是不太可能。
Parameters are where fabrication starts, so design them to make guessing unnecessary. Enumerate whatever you can because an enum makes an invalid value impossible rather than merely unlikely.

1321
01:55:41,934 --> 01:55:49,124
描述每个字段及其格式。例如，起始位要求符合 ISO8601 并给出一个示例。
Describe each field including its format. So start bit says ISO8601 with an example.

1322
01:55:49,934 --> 01:55:56,612
将“必填”视为严格必填，而对于智能体可能缺失的任何内容，都应设为可选并提供合理的默认值。
Treat required as genuinely required and make anything the agent might not have optional with a sensible default.

1323
01:55:57,024 --> 01:55:59,300
第四点是核心要点。
That fourth point is the one to carry.

1324
01:55:59,854 --> 01:56:06,244
如果一个必填字段是智能体根本无法获知的信息，那就是在诱导它去编造内容，而它一定会照做。
A required field the agent cannot possibly know is an invitation to invent one and it will accept the invitation.

1325
01:56:07,086 --> 01:56:12,804
当场景描述中出现虚构参数时，先看架构定义再看提示词。
When a scenario describes fabricated arguments, look at the schema before you look at the prompt.

1326
01:56:14,222 --> 01:56:16,260
这一行重塑了整个领域的逻辑。
This line reframes the whole domain.

1327
01:56:16,784 --> 01:56:21,344
普通的 API 设计是两个确定性系统之间的契约。
Ordinary API design is a contract between two deterministic systems.

1328
01:56:21,584 --> 01:56:25,412
你调用一个获取纽约天气的接口，每次都会得到相同的行为。
Call you get weather with New York and you get the same behavior every time.

1329
01:56:27,374 --> 01:56:32,708
而工具则是你的确定性系统与一个完全非确定性用户之间的契约。
A tool is a contract between your deterministic system and a user that is not deterministic at all.

1330
01:56:33,664 --> 01:56:37,828
它无法向你询问澄清问题，无论如何它都会执行操作。
It cannot ask you a clarifying question and it will do something either way.

1331
01:56:38,734 --> 01:56:45,188
因此，工具必须采用防御性设计、提供丰富的文档，并能容忍合理的错误。
So, tools have to be defensively designed, richly documented, and forgiving of reasonable mistakes.

1332
01:56:46,062 --> 01:56:51,812
直接把现有的 API 接口搬过来就叫它“工具集”，是最常见的设计错误。
Porting your existing API surface and calling it a tool set is the single most common design error.

1333
01:56:52,590 --> 01:56:53,924
而且考试内容也涵盖了这一点。
And the exam knows it.

1334
01:56:55,662 --> 01:56:59,748
现在，考试会从两个维度来考查这个决策，这也是它变难的原因。
Now the decision the exam tests in both directions, which is what makes it hard.

1335
01:57:01,646 --> 01:57:04,196
当一个工具承担多个任务时，进行拆分。
Split when one tool is doing several jobs.

1336
01:57:05,454 --> 01:57:12,004
判断标准是：存在用于在不同行为间切换的模式参数，或者描述中必须反复强调某些内容。
The signs are a mode parameter selecting between behaviors and a description that has to say or repeatedly.

1337
01:57:12,878 --> 01:57:16,864
此外，还包括智能体选择了错误的模式，或者不同的任务需要不同的权限。
Also, an agent picking the wrong mode and jobs needing different permissions.

1338
01:57:17,198 --> 01:57:26,788
当多个工具总是被一起调用时，进行合并。判断标准是：智能体为了得到一个答案而连续调用三个接口，且每个结果仅作为下一个输入的环节。
Merge when several tools are always called together. The signs are the agent chaining three calls to get one answer, with each result useful only as input to the next.

1339
01:57:27,630 --> 01:57:32,196
中间结果会消耗上下文，而且步骤过多会导致链条悄悄断裂。
Intermediate results eat context, and a drop step breaks the chain quietly.

1340
01:57:34,030 --> 01:57:37,156
平局时的判定标准是：询问一次成功的操作看起来是什么样的。
The tiebreaker is to ask what one successful use looks like.

1341
01:57:37,550 --> 01:57:39,780
如果总是需要三次调用，就意味着要合并。
Always three calls means merge.

1342
01:57:40,430 --> 01:57:42,532
如果三个行为中只有一个是需要的，就意味着要拆分。
One of three behaviors means split.

1343
01:57:44,174 --> 01:57:47,236
有一种特定的合并情况经常出现，值得专门提出来。
One specific merge case comes up often enough to name.

1344
01:57:47,808 --> 01:57:55,076
智能体调用“查询客户”，从结果中读出一个 ID，然后用这个 ID 调用“获取订单”。
The agent calls search customer, reads an ID out of the result, then calls get orders with that ID.

1345
01:57:55,950 --> 01:58:02,468
为了回答一个问题需要三次交互和往返，而且上下文里还堆着一个毫无贡献的标识符。
Three turns and a round trip to answer one question, plus an identifier sitting in context contributing nothing.

1346
01:58:03,406 --> 01:58:10,500
更好的做法是让“获取订单”接受电子邮件地址或公司名称，并在内部进行查询。
The better shape is for get orders to accept an email address or a company name and do the lookup internally.

1347
01:58:10,928 --> 01:58:15,748
当它返回结果时，同时提供可读的字段和标识符。
And when it returns, give back the readable field alongside the identifier.

1348
01:58:17,358 --> 01:58:22,404
这样智能体就可以谈论“ACME 有限公司”，而不是一个 UUID。
Then the agent can talk about ACME Limited rather than a UUID.

1349
01:58:23,502 --> 01:58:25,604
背后的原则很简单。
The principle underneath is short.

1350
01:58:26,574 --> 01:58:31,474
让工具接收智能体拥有的信息，而不是你的数据库想要的信息。
Make the tool take what the agent has, not what your database wants.

1351
01:58:33,006 --> 01:58:36,068
响应的逻辑设计必须像输入一样经过深思熟虑。
Responses need designing as deliberately as inputs.

1352
01:58:36,814 --> 01:58:43,748
返回结构化数据，而不是格式化的文本，因为智能体只是在传递这些数据，没人会去欣赏你的表格边框。
Return structured data rather than formatted prose because the agent is passing it and nobody is admiring your table borders.

1353
01:58:44,878 --> 01:58:51,108
在标识符旁边包含人类可读的字段，这样就不需要为了描述发生了什么而进行后续通话了。
Include human readable fields next to identifiers so no follow-up call is needed just to describe what happened.

1354
01:58:52,014 --> 01:58:59,396
只返回必要的内容，并提供详细信息或格式参数，以便智能体在需要时可以索要更多内容。
Return only what is needed and offer a detail or format parameter so the agent can ask for more when it wants it.

1355
01:59:00,174 --> 01:59:03,364
并且要抵制那种认为“返回所有内容就是慷慨”的本能。
And resist the instinct that returning everything is generous.

1356
01:59:03,758 --> 01:59:04,580
那并不慷慨。
It is not.

1357
01:59:04,928 --> 01:59:09,092
如果不加询问就返回所有内容，就是在代替智能体去处理它并不需要的上下文。
It is pending the agent's context on its behalf without asking.

1358
01:59:10,094 --> 01:59:16,848
Claude 代码默认在 25,000 个 token 处截断工具响应，这个默认值是有原因的。
Clot code truncates tool responses at 25,000 tokens by default, and that default exists for a reason.

1359
01:59:17,614 --> 01:59:22,564
Anthropic 用通讯录来解释这一点，这是我见过的最清晰的版本。
Anthropic uses an address book to explain this, and it is the clearest version I know.

1360
01:59:22,990 --> 01:59:29,124
传统的程序可以非常廉价地逐个扫描联系人列表，因为内存是充足的。
A traditional program can scan a list of contacts one at a time very cheaply because memory is abundant.

1361
01:59:29,838 --> 01:59:35,044
而调用一个返回所有联系人的工具的智能体，必须逐个 token 地阅读每一个。
An agent that calls a tool returning all contacts has to read every one, token by token.

1362
01:59:35,886 --> 01:59:39,492
它在并不在意的对象上消耗了有限的上下文。
It spends its limited context on people it does not care about.

1363
01:59:39,808 --> 01:59:43,728
那就像是翻通讯录时从第一页开始读到每一页。
That is searching an address book by reading each page from the top.

1364
01:59:44,110 --> 01:59:49,060
人类和智能体的通用做法是直接跳到相关的页面。
The natural approach for humans and agents alike is to skip to the relevant page.

1365
01:59:49,902 --> 01:59:55,460
因此，优先选择搜索而非列出，并构建具有过滤功能的工具，而不是简单倾倒数据的工具。
So prefer search over listing and build tools that filter rather than tools that dump.

1366
01:59:57,134 --> 02:00:05,252
在实践中，这意味着四件事：合理的默认限制，比如除非智能体要求，否则只给 50 个结果。
In practice, that means four things Sensible default limits, so 50 results rather than everything unless the agent asks.

1367
02:00:07,328 --> 02:00:13,444
分页、范围选择和过滤，以便分块处理庞大的结果集。
Pagination, range selection, and filters so a large result set can be approached in pieces.

1368
02:00:14,638 --> 02:00:19,268
带有明确指令的截断，告诉智能体如何获取剩余内容。
Truncation that comes with instructions telling the agent how to fetch the rest.

1369
02:00:20,174 --> 02:00:26,276
以及一个能够引导智能体进行多次小范围定向搜索、而非一次性大范围搜索的描述。
And a description that actively steers towards many small targeted searches rather than one broad one.

1370
02:00:27,022 --> 02:00:28,608
这种提醒非常关键。
The callout is the clap.

1371
02:00:29,262 --> 02:00:35,076
静默截断会将部分答案变成错误答案，因为智能体根本不知道情况。
Truncating silently turns a partial answer into a wrong answer because the agent has no idea.

1372
02:00:35,502 --> 02:00:37,188
它只看到了第一页。
It only saw the first page.

1373
02:00:38,894 --> 02:00:43,428
你添加的每个工具都会带来两种成本，而问题往往会利用这两点。
Two costs come with every tool you add, and questions exploit both.

1374
02:00:43,918 --> 02:00:45,252
第一是金钱。
The first is money.

1375
02:00:45,710 --> 02:00:50,980
每一个工具定义都是每次请求中的输入 token，而不是仅在开始时计算一次。
Every tool definition is input tokens on every single request, not once at the start.

1376
02:00:51,808 --> 02:00:58,468
大量的 MCP 服务器可能会在智能体读到用户问题之前就消耗掉数万个 token。
A large collection of MCP servers can consume tens of thousands of tokens before the agent has read the user's question.

1377
02:00:59,342 --> 02:01:01,412
第二项成本是准确性。
The second cost is accuracy.

1378
02:01:02,286 --> 02:01:09,604
随着工具集的增加，选择质量会下降，因为每一个额外的工具都是可能导致混淆的干扰项。
Selection quality degrades as the tool set grows because every extra tool is another neighbor to be confused with.

1379
02:01:10,638 --> 02:01:15,044
这就是为什么在这次考试中，添加另一个工具往往不是正确答案的原因。
Which is why adding another tool is so often the wrong answer on this exam.

1380
02:01:15,918 --> 02:01:19,204
每一次增加都会增加你未来发起的所有请求的负担。
Each addition taxes every request you will ever make.

1381
02:01:20,910 --> 02:01:22,020
一张货币纸币。
A currency note.

1382
02:01:25,422 --> 02:01:31,012
考试中针对臃肿工具集的对策是整合，而这依然是很好的建议。
The exam's answer to a bloated tool set is consolidation, and that is still good advice.

1383
02:01:32,462 --> 02:01:36,452
变化的是 Anthropic 增加了一项工具搜索功能。
What has changed is that Anthropic added a tool search capability.

1384
02:01:36,974 --> 02:01:43,396
智能体加载单个搜索工具，并按需获取定义，而不是预先加载所有内容。
The agent loads a single search tool and pulls in definitions on demand rather than holding everything upfront.

1385
02:01:44,302 --> 02:01:52,484
Anthropic 报告称此举显著节省了上下文并提升了准确性。在考试中，选“整合”。
Anthropic reported large context savings and measurable accuracy improvements from it. On the exam, answer consolidate.

1386
02:01:53,216 --> 02:01:56,068
在实际工作中，要知道存在延迟加载这种方案。
At work, know that deferred loading exists.

1387
02:01:56,814 --> 02:01:59,748
注意第三行，因为这是核心点。
And note the third row because it is the point.

1388
02:02:00,176 --> 02:02:04,420
按需加载并不意味着让庞大且重叠的工具集变成一个好主意。
On demand loading does not make a sprawling overlapping tool set a good idea.

1389
02:02:05,376 --> 02:02:06,916
它只是让这个做法成本更低一些。
It just makes it cheaper.

1390
02:02:08,334 --> 02:02:12,996
最常见的结构性错误是直接套用现有的 API。
The most common structural mistake is porting an existing API.

1391
02:02:13,870 --> 02:02:16,804
端点是围绕你的数据模型组织的。
Endpoints are organized around your data model.

1392
02:02:17,742 --> 02:02:22,656
工具应该围绕智能体实际被要求执行的任务来组织。
Tools should be organized around the tasks the agent is actually asked to do.

1393
02:02:23,136 --> 02:02:32,228
每个端点套一个薄包装会导致产生 40 个高度重叠且需要频繁链式调用的工具，这在所有我们讨论过的维度上都很昂贵。
A thin wrapper per endpoint gives you 40 tools with heavy overlap and constant chaining, which is expensive in every sense we have discussed.

1394
02:02:32,576 --> 02:02:37,604
相反，应该从真实的流程出发，构建该工作流所需的少量工具。
Start instead from a real workflow and build the handful of tools that workflow needs.

1395
02:02:38,734 --> 02:02:42,020
然后进行原型设计、在真实任务上测试并不断优化。
Then prototype, test on realistic tasks, and refine.

1396
02:02:43,054 --> 02:02:46,692
Anthropic 关于评估的指导非常实用。
Anthropic's guidance on evaluation is refreshingly practical.

1397
02:02:47,376 --> 02:02:53,764
3 到 5 个真实案例就足够了，因为效应量越大，所需的样本量就越小。
3 to 5 real cases is enough because the larger the effect size, the smaller the sample you need to see it.

1398
02:02:55,374 --> 02:02:57,215
本模块的模式识别。
Pattern recognition for this module.

1399
02:02:57,518 --> 02:03:08,484
“调用错误的工具”意味着要检查描述以及与相邻工具的重叠情况；“传递不存在的值”意味着要查看架构中是否存在智能体无法获知的必填字段。
Calls the wrong tool means look at the description and at overlap with its neighbors. Passes values that do not exist means look at the schema for a required field the agent cannot know.

1400
02:03:09,390 --> 02:03:14,976
“回答一个问题需要三次调用”，意味着合并或在工具内部解析标识符。
Three calls to answer, one question means merge or resolves the identifier inside the tool.

1401
02:03:15,150 --> 02:03:20,016
“选择错误的模式”，意味着拆分，因为一个工具承担了多项工作。
Picks the wrong mode, means split because one tool is doing several jobs.

1402
02:03:20,256 --> 02:03:24,644
“在几次工具调用后上下文变满”，意味着响应设计问题。
Context filling up after a few tool calls means response design.

1403
02:03:25,390 --> 02:03:32,496
“根本不使用该工具”。通常意味着描述没有涵盖智能体能识别出的当前情况。
And never uses the tool at all. Usually means the description does not describe a situation the agent recognizes it is in.

1404
02:03:32,736 --> 02:03:39,012
注意，几乎每一个症状都指向的是描述或架构，而不是系统提示词。
Notice that almost every symptom points at the description or the schema rather than at the system prompt.

1405
02:03:40,590 --> 02:03:41,508
五行。
5 lines.

1406
02:03:41,776 --> 02:03:47,780
描述就是接口，所以要说明它做什么、何时使用、何时不使用以及返回什么内容。
The description is the interface, so say what it does, when to use it, when not to, and what comes back.

1407
02:03:48,256 --> 02:03:52,708
虚构的参数是架构缺陷，所以永远不要要求智能体提供它无法获知的信息。
Fabricated arguments are a schema fault, so never require what the agent cannot know.

1408
02:03:53,294 --> 02:03:58,500
当成功使用总是需要三次调用时选择合并，当一个工具具有三种行为时选择拆分。
Merge when a successful use is always three calls, and split when one tool has three behaviors.

1409
02:03:59,406 --> 02:04:06,660
像设计输入一样仔细地设计响应，即结构化、过滤、可读，并根据指令进行截断。
Design the response as carefully as the input, meaning structured, filtered, readable, and truncated with instructions.

1410
02:04:07,502 --> 02:04:13,188
记住，每一个工具定义都会在 Token 消耗和选择准确性上增加请求成本。
And remember every tool definition taxes every request in tokens and in selection accuracy.

1411
02:04:14,158 --> 02:04:15,588
现在有七个场景
Seven scenarios now

1412
02:04:16,416 --> 02:04:23,716
其中有两个关于拆分或合并的决策指向相反的方向。看哪个细节决定了走向。
and two of them are the split or merge decision pointing in opposite directions. Watch which detail flips it.

1413
02:04:25,422 --> 02:04:26,404
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

1414
02:04:26,656 --> 02:04:28,416
一个支持智能体有两个工具。
A support agent has two tools.

1415
02:04:28,656 --> 02:04:32,132
查询订单的描述是“检索订单信息”。
Lookup order is described as retrieves order information.

1416
02:04:33,838 --> 02:04:36,644
搜索订单的描述是“搜索订单”。
Search orders is described as searches orders.

1417
02:04:39,470 --> 02:04:47,556
在生产环境中，当客户提供特定订单号时，智能体经常调用“搜索订单”，然后自行过滤结果。
In production, the agent frequently calls search orders when the customer has quoted a specific order number, then filters the results itself.

1418
02:04:48,336 --> 02:04:52,416
它偶尔会用客户邮箱去调用“查询订单”，但这会失败。
It occasionally calls lookup order with a customer email which fails.

1419
02:04:52,576 --> 02:04:57,380
团队的提议是在系统提示词中添加指导，解释在什么情况下使用哪个工具。
The team's proposal is to add guidance to the system prompt explaining which tool to use when.

1420
02:04:58,016 --> 02:04:59,908
哪种修复最有效？
What is the most effective fix?

1421
02:05:00,334 --> 02:05:03,428
A. 按建议在系统提示词中添加指导。
a add the guidance to the system prompt as proposed.

1422
02:05:04,096 --> 02:05:04,336
B。
B.

1423
02:05:04,782 --> 02:05:10,180
重写两个描述，说明每个工具接收什么、返回什么，以及何时使用另一个。
Rewrite both descriptions to state what each takes, what each returns, and when to use the other.

1424
02:05:10,736 --> 02:05:11,056
C。
C.

1425
02:05:11,534 --> 02:05:16,004
将两个工具合并为一个，该工具既可接受订单号也可接受搜索查询。
Merge the two tools into one that accepts either an order number or a search query.

1426
02:05:16,622 --> 02:05:20,256
D. 删除“搜索订单”，只保留一个工具。
D. Remove search orders so only one tool remains.

1427
02:05:21,262 --> 02:05:22,656
停一下，做决定。
Pause and decide.

1428
02:05:28,398 --> 02:05:30,080
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1429
02:05:30,640 --> 02:05:35,460
题干中引用了两个描述，这是提醒你要仔细阅读它们的信号。
Both descriptions are quoted in the stem, which is your cue to read them properly.

1430
02:05:36,000 --> 02:05:38,916
“检索订单信息”和“搜索订单”。
Retrieves order information and searches orders.

1431
02:05:39,598 --> 02:05:41,444
两者都没说明它们接收什么参数。
Neither says what it accepts.

1432
02:05:41,840 --> 02:05:46,852
所以智能体无法知道一个是接收订单号，另一个是接收查询内容。
So the agent has no way to know one takes an order number and the other takes a query.

1433
02:05:47,726 --> 02:05:53,920
选项 A 是热门选择，它并不是错的，只是不合适。
Option A is the popular choice and it is not wrong so much as misplaced.

1434
02:05:54,720 --> 02:05:59,492
系统提示词中的选择指导离决策点太远了。
Selection guidance in the system prompt sits far away from the point of selection.

1435
02:05:59,760 --> 02:06:03,428
而且你还得为以后添加的每一个工具重复这个操作。
You would also have to repeat the exercise for every tool you ever add.

1436
02:06:04,206 --> 02:06:12,676
选项 C 将两个真正不同的任务（带有不同输入）合并在了一起，这正是你以后需要拆分开来的“模式混淆”。
Option C merges two genuinely different jobs with different inputs, which creates exactly the mode confusion you would later have to split apart.

1437
02:06:14,510 --> 02:06:19,556
选项 D 删除了一些智能体在不知道订单号时所需的职能。
Option D deletes the capability the agent needs whenever no order number is known.

1438
02:06:20,846 --> 02:06:21,796
场景 2。
Scenario 2.

1439
02:06:22,094 --> 02:06:26,660
一个提取智能体有一个名为“创建工单”的工具，包含必填参数。
An extraction agent has a tool called Create Ticket with required parameters.

1440
02:06:27,150 --> 02:06:32,580
标题、描述、优先级、负责人、ID 和部门代码。
Title, Description, Priority, Assignee, ID, and Department Code.

1441
02:06:33,038 --> 02:06:39,652
用户报告称，工单出现的分配人虽然看起来像真的，但其实是错误的，而且部门代码根本不存在。
Users report tickets appearing with plausible but incorrect assignees and department codes that do not exist.

1442
02:06:40,560 --> 02:06:45,092
智能体无法直接访问员工信息或部门列表。
The agent has no access to the staff directly or the department list.

1443
02:06:45,360 --> 02:06:48,548
标题和描述始终是准确的。
The title and description are consistently accurate.

1444
02:06:49,166 --> 02:06:50,436
根本原因是什么？
What is the root cause?

1445
02:06:51,360 --> 02:06:55,268
A. 模型在产生幻觉，需要降低采样温度。
a The model is hallucinating and needs a lower temperature.

1446
02:06:56,110 --> 02:06:56,320
B。
B.

1447
02:06:56,878 --> 02:07:01,988
B. 分配人 ID 和部门代码是必填项但未绑定，所以智能体编造了数值。
Assignee ID and department code are required but unurban, so the agent invents values.

1448
02:07:02,480 --> 02:07:06,116
C. 工具描述没有解释什么是部门代码。
C. The tool description does not explain what a department code is.

1449
02:07:06,510 --> 02:07:10,948
D. 智能体需要一个系统提示词指令，要求它绝不要猜测参数值。
D. The agent needs a system prompt instruction never to guess parameter values.

1450
02:07:11,280 --> 02:07:12,484
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1451
02:07:17,966 --> 02:07:19,600
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1452
02:07:20,160 --> 02:07:22,980
题干的最后一行在起微妙的作用。
The last line of the stem is doing quiet work.

1453
02:07:24,302 --> 02:07:30,980
标题和描述始终准确，而这两个字段正是智能体能从输入中获取到的唯一两个字段。
Title and description are consistently accurate, and those are precisely the two fields the agent can derive from the input.

1454
02:07:31,520 --> 02:07:35,172
那两个失败的字段，恰好就是它没有来源的两个字段。
The two failing fields are exactly the two it has no source for.

1455
02:07:36,080 --> 02:07:47,680
这种对比排除了任何关于模型普遍不可靠的解释，从而排除选项 A。选项 D 是最有趣的错误答案，因为它建立了一个直接的矛盾。
That contrast rules out any explanation about the model being generally unreliable, which kills option A. Option D is the most interesting wrong answer because it sets up a direct contradiction.

1456
02:07:47,840 --> 02:07:52,036
架构规定这个字段是必填项，而指令要求不要猜测。
The schema says this field is required and the instruction says do not guess.

1457
02:07:52,686 --> 02:07:57,060
智能体无法同时满足这两个条件，而由于架构属于结构性约束，所以它优先遵循架构。
The agent cannot satisfy both, and the schema wins because it is structural.

1458
02:07:57,390 --> 02:08:00,324
要么把这些字段设为可选，要么给智能体一个查询工具。
Make those fields optional or give the agent a lookup tool.

1459
02:08:01,134 --> 02:08:04,900
选项 C 把“信息缺失”和“信息不明确”混淆了。
Option C confuses missing information with unclear information.

1460
02:08:06,510 --> 02:08:07,460
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

1461
02:08:07,760 --> 02:08:11,204
一个房产研究智能体负责回答有关房源的问题。
A property research agent answers questions about listings.

1462
02:08:11,440 --> 02:08:15,396
以这个问题为例：Mill 路上的公寓的议会税等级是多少？
Take the question What is the council tax band for the flat on Mill Road?

1463
02:08:15,600 --> 02:08:21,732
它调用 search properties，从结果中读取房产 ID，然后调用 get property 获取详情。
It calls search properties, reads the property ID from the result, then calls get property for details.

1464
02:08:22,318 --> 02:08:27,120
它从中读取地方当局 ID，然后调用 get tax band。
It reads the local authority ID from that, then calls get tax band.

1465
02:08:28,878 --> 02:08:30,436
每个问题需要三次往返请求。
Three round trips per question.

1466
02:08:31,150 --> 02:08:34,884
追踪显示这些中间标识符从未被用于其他任何用途。
Traces show the intermediate identifiers are never used for anything else.

1467
02:08:35,630 --> 02:08:37,348
最有效的改进是什么？
What is the most effective change?

1468
02:08:38,638 --> 02:08:42,080
a. 并行运行这三个调用以降低延迟。
a run the three calls in parallel to reduce latency.

1469
02:08:42,880 --> 02:08:51,108
b. 提供一个接收房产描述或地址并返回税级、在内部处理标识符的工具。
b. Provide a tool that takes a property description or address and returns the tax band resolving identifiers internally.

1470
02:08:51,760 --> 02:08:52,000
C。
C.

1471
02:08:52,718 --> 02:08:54,852
缓存中间标识符。
Cache the intermediate identifiers.

1472
02:08:55,840 --> 02:08:58,212
这样重复提问时就可以跳过查询了。
So repeated questions skip the lookups.

1473
02:08:58,800 --> 02:08:59,040
D。
D.

1474
02:08:59,758 --> 02:09:03,364
添加一个系统提示词示例，展示正确的三个调用序列。
Add a system prompt example showing the correct three call sequence.

1475
02:09:05,262 --> 02:09:06,436
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1476
02:09:12,224 --> 02:09:13,572
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1477
02:09:14,224 --> 02:09:15,748
有两个细节暴露了答案。
Two details give it away.

1478
02:09:15,984 --> 02:09:21,860
成功的情况总是相同的。就是三个调用，而且中间标识符绝不会用于其他任何用途。
Success is always the same. Three calls and the intermediate identifiers are never used for anything else.

1479
02:09:22,304 --> 02:09:29,284
这两点结合起来说明这个序列不是智能体要做出的决策，而是底层逻辑，而底层逻辑应该放在工具内部。
Together, those say the sequence is not a decision. The agent is making, it is plumbing, and plumbing belongs inside the tool.

1480
02:09:29,934 --> 02:09:34,180
选项 A 值得思考一下，因为它根本不可行，而不只是不够理想。
Option A is worth pausing on because it is impossible, not merely suboptimal.

1481
02:09:34,446 --> 02:09:40,516
每次调用都需要上一个调用产生的标识符。所以这是一个链式过程，链式过程无法并行化。
Each call needs an identifier, the previous call produced. So this is a chain and chains cannot be parallelized.

1482
02:09:40,944 --> 02:09:44,932
能立刻识别出这一点就是一种模块化能力，这里体现了两种技能的优势。
Recognizing that instantly is a module, two skills paying off here.

1483
02:09:45,744 --> 02:09:50,436
选项 C 只解决了关于给定房产的第二个问题。
Option C helps only the second question about a given property.

1484
02:09:50,830 --> 02:09:56,164
选项 D 是在要求智能体去做它本来就已经在正确执行的事情。
Option D pitches the agent to do the thing it is already doing correctly.

1485
02:09:57,710 --> 02:09:58,692
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

1486
02:09:59,054 --> 02:10:01,824
一个文档工具被定义为「管理文档」。
A document tool is defined as manage document.

1487
02:10:01,984 --> 02:10:09,636
它有一个必填的 action 参数，接受 read、update、delete 和 share，还有 15 个其他用于不同操作的参数。
It has a required action parameter accepting read, update, delete, and share, plus 15 other parameters used by different actions.

1488
02:10:10,030 --> 02:10:11,332
有两个问题反复出现。
Two problems recur.

1489
02:10:11,504 --> 02:10:16,388
智能体有时在用户只提问时，却调用了 action update。
The agent sometimes calls it with action update when the user only asked a question.

1490
02:10:16,878 --> 02:10:21,664
而且安全团队无法在不授予删除权限的情况下仅授予读取权限。
And the security team cannot grant read access without also granting delete.

1491
02:10:22,478 --> 02:10:24,132
最合适的修改是什么？
What is the most appropriate change?

1492
02:10:25,006 --> 02:10:30,628
a 将其拆分为独立的工具，每个操作一个工具，且每个工具只包含它自己的参数。
a Split it into separate tools, one per action, each with only its own parameters.

1493
02:10:31,104 --> 02:10:36,144
B. 添加一个确认参数，在执行 update 和 delete 时必须设为 true。
B. Add a confirmation parameter that must be set to true for update and delete.

1494
02:10:37,038 --> 02:10:37,264
C。
C.

1495
02:10:37,806 --> 02:10:41,024
改进描述，解释每种操作在什么情况下应该被使用。
Improve the description to explain when each action should be used.

1496
02:10:41,344 --> 02:10:41,664
D。
D.

1497
02:10:41,998 --> 02:10:45,744
添加一个钩子，拦截用户未要求的删除操作。
Add a hook that blocks delete actions the user did not ask for.

1498
02:10:45,998 --> 02:10:47,172
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1499
02:10:52,814 --> 02:10:58,304
答案是 A， giveaway 是两个症状源于同一个原因。
The answer is A, and the giveaway is that there are two symptoms with one cause.

1500
02:10:58,606 --> 02:11:06,660
错误的模式选择和无法划定的权限边界，都是因为四个任务挤在一个工具里导致的后果。
Wrong mode selection and a permissions boundary that cannot be drawn are both consequences of four jobs living in one tool.

1501
02:11:07,470 --> 02:11:15,492
拆分可以解决这两个问题，因为这样能更可靠地选择特定的工具，且权限将变为针对每个工具，而不是全有或全无。
Splitting fixes both because distinct tools are selected more reliably and permissions become per tool rather than all or nothing.

1502
02:11:18,254 --> 02:11:20,932
选项 C 只解决了第一个症状。
Option C addresses only the first symptom.

1503
02:11:21,614 --> 02:11:26,148
选项 D 是真正的强制执行，这通常是强力选项。
Option D is genuine enforcement, which is normally the strong answer.

1504
02:11:26,894 --> 02:11:34,788
但它针对的是删除操作，而题干中的选择问题是更新，而且它没能解决权限问题。
But it is aimed at delete while the stem selection problem is update and it leaves the permissions issue untouched.

1505
02:11:36,078 --> 02:11:39,684
从原则上讲，选项 B 是需要警惕的一个。
Option B is the one to be suspicious of on principle.

1506
02:11:40,526 --> 02:11:44,836
确认参数是由你正试图限制的同一个智能体设置的。
A confirmation parameter is set by the same agent you are trying to constrain.

1507
02:11:45,262 --> 02:11:46,916
所以它根本不算一种控制手段。
So it is not a control at all.

1508
02:11:48,590 --> 02:11:49,540
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

1509
02:11:49,966 --> 02:11:58,852
一个基于代码的智能体有一个名为“列出文件”的工具，该工具会返回仓库中的所有文件路径，而该仓库大约有 800 个文件。
A code-based agent has a tool called list files that returns every file path in the repository and the repository has around 800 files.

1510
02:11:59,790 --> 02:12:08,708
工程师报告说，在进行两到三次工具调用后，智能体开始遗忘对话早期的细节，其回答变得模糊。
Engineers report that after two or three tool calls, the agent starts forgetting details from earlier in the conversation and its answers become vaguer.

1511
02:12:09,582 --> 02:12:13,732
团队正在考虑切换到一个具有更大上下文窗口的模型。
The team is considering moving to a model with a larger context window.

1512
02:12:14,638 --> 02:12:15,908
你应该推荐什么？
What should you recommend?

1513
02:12:17,070 --> 02:12:20,708
a 按计划切换到更大的上下文窗口。
a move to the larger context window as planned.

1514
02:12:21,198 --> 02:12:28,580
b 用支持模式匹配并返回带默认限制的路径的搜索工具来替换“列出文件”。
b Replace list files with a search tool that accepts a pattern and returns matching paths with a default limit.

1515
02:12:29,614 --> 02:12:33,444
c 让智能体在接收到文件列表后进行总结。
C. Have the agent summarize the file list after receiving it.

1516
02:12:34,126 --> 02:12:39,584
d 在开始时调用一次“列出文件”，并指示智能体重复使用该结果。
d. Call list files once at the start and instruct the agent to reuse the result.

1517
02:12:40,686 --> 02:12:42,020
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1518
02:12:47,790 --> 02:12:51,908
答案是 B，这是将地址簿具体化的做法。
The answer is B and it is the address book made concrete.

1519
02:12:53,198 --> 02:12:59,204
一个返回 800 个路径的工具会迫使智能体去阅读所有这些路径，只为了找到那三个重要的。
A tool that returns 800 paths forces the agent to read all of them to find the three that matter.

1520
02:13:01,070 --> 02:13:06,020
选项 A 只是买了个更大的硬盘，并没有改变你正在阅读每一页的事实。
Option A buys a bigger disk without changing the fact that you are reading every page.

1521
02:13:06,542 --> 02:13:08,356
选项 C 是一个微妙的陷阱。
Option C is the subtle one.

1522
02:13:09,326 --> 02:13:17,360
接收后总结没用，因为完整的列表在进入的一瞬间就已经进入上下文了，而且摘要只是在它之上增加的额外 token。
Summarizing after receiving cannot help because the full list entered context the moment it arrived and the summary is additional tokens on top of it.

1523
02:13:18,286 --> 02:13:22,884
选项 D 确实比重复调用要好，这就是它具有诱惑力的原因。
Option D is genuinely an improvement over calling it repeatedly, which is why it tempts.

1524
02:13:23,694 --> 02:13:28,420
但 800 个路径仍会留在整个会话的上下文中。
But 800 paths still sit in context for the rest of the session.

1525
02:13:28,910 --> 02:13:31,652
只有 B 能从源头上阻止这些信息的堆砌。
Only B stops the dump at source.

1526
02:13:33,326 --> 02:13:34,500
场景 6。
Scenario 6.

1527
02:13:35,040 --> 02:13:40,452
一个集成接口自动生成了 40 个工具，每个列表端点对应一个。
An integration exposes 40 tools generated automatically one per list endpoint.

1528
02:13:40,974 --> 02:13:42,000
许多工具的功能重叠。
Many overlap.

1529
02:13:42,670 --> 02:13:48,160
“获取用户”、“获取用户资料”和“获取用户详情”都返回重叠的数据。
Get user, get user profile, and fetch user details all return overlapping data.

1530
02:13:48,750 --> 02:13:55,556
智能体经常选择一个返回几乎正确信息的工具，然后再调用另一个来获取缺失的字段。
The agent frequent key selects a tool that returns almost the right information, then calls another to get the missing field.

1531
02:13:56,000 --> 02:13:58,692
即使是简单的请求，Token 成本也很高。
Token costs are high even on simple requests.

1532
02:13:58,880 --> 02:14:02,980
一位工程师建议为所有 40 个工具编写更详细的描述。
One engineer proposes writing much more detailed descriptions for all 40.

1533
02:14:04,240 --> 02:14:06,244
哪种方法最有效？
What is the most effective approach?

1534
02:14:07,086 --> 02:14:11,108
a. 编写详细的描述，因为描述就是接口。
a Write the detailed descriptions since the description is the interface.

1535
02:14:11,680 --> 02:14:11,920
b.
b.

1536
02:14:12,320 --> 02:14:16,964
识别智能体实际执行的工作流，并为其构建一小组工具。
Identify the workflows the agent actually performs and build a small set of tools for them.

1537
02:14:17,360 --> 02:14:17,680
c.
C.

1538
02:14:18,000 --> 02:14:23,076
d. 保留所有 40 个，但在系统提示词中指示智能体优先使用 get user。
Keep all 40, but instruct the agent in the system prompt to prefer get user.

1539
02:14:23,854 --> 02:14:24,080
e.
D.

1540
02:14:24,400 --> 02:14:28,900
将这 40 个工具分布到多个 MCP 服务器上，以减轻单个服务器的负载。
Split the 40 tools across several MCP servers to reduce per server load.

1541
02:14:29,742 --> 02:14:30,852
稍停一下，做决定。
Pause and decide.

1542
02:14:36,238 --> 02:14:37,284
答案是 b。
The answer is B.

1543
02:14:37,680 --> 02:14:42,596
选项 a 值得注意，因为它利用了本模块的教学点作为诱饵。
Option A deserves attention because it uses this module's own lesson as bait.

1544
02:14:43,790 --> 02:14:48,356
描述确实是接口，更好的描述确实会有帮助。
The description really is the interface, and better descriptions really do help.

1545
02:14:49,230 --> 02:15:01,120
但它们无法解决真正重叠的工具问题，因为这种模糊性存在于工具本身而非文字中。而且无论这些定义写什么，40 个定义依然会增加每次请求的负担。
What they cannot do is separate tools that genuinely overlap because the ambiguity is in the tools rather than in the words. And 40 definitions still tax every request, whatever they say.

1546
02:15:01,518 --> 02:15:03,588
根本原因在第一行就提到了。
The root cause is named in the first line.

1547
02:15:04,558 --> 02:15:12,996
每个 REST 接口对应一个工具是典型的 API 反模式，解决办法是从智能体实际执行的工作流入手。
One tool per rest endpoint is the ported API anti-pattern, and the fix is to start from the workflows the agent actually performs.

1548
02:15:13,998 --> 02:15:22,756
选项 d 值得注意，因为它听起来像个合理的错误选项。无论这些定义来自哪个服务器，它们都会加载到同一个上下文中。
Option D is worth noting as a plausible sounding non-answer. All those definitions load into the same context regardless of which server they came from.

1549
02:15:24,014 --> 02:15:25,156
场景 7。
Scenario 7.

1550
02:15:25,518 --> 02:15:28,640
一个财务智能体有一个名为 Get Transactions 的工具。
A finance agent has a tool called Get Transactions.

1551
02:15:28,880 --> 02:15:34,880
它的描述是：返回交易集，若要获取完整历史，请将 include all 设置为 true。
Its description reads Returns Transactions set include all to true for the complete history.

1552
02:15:35,278 --> 02:15:43,108
在几乎每次调用中，智能体都会将 include all 设置为 true，从而检索出多层记录来回答关于上个月的问题。
The agent sets include all to true on nearly every call, retrieving several layers of records to answer questions about last month.

1553
02:15:43,950 --> 02:15:46,532
该工具没有默认限制，也没有日期过滤。
The tool has no default limit and no date filter.

1554
02:15:46,960 --> 02:15:48,804
成本是预估值的 4 倍。
Costs are 4 times the estimate.

1555
02:15:49,998 --> 02:15:51,620
最有效的改进是什么？
What is the most effective change?

1556
02:15:52,334 --> 02:15:57,636
a. 在系统提示词中指示智能体除非必要否则避免将 include all 设置为 true。
a instruct the agent in the system prompt to avoid setting include all unless necessary.

1557
02:15:58,574 --> 02:16:06,564
b. 添加日期范围参数和合理的默认限制，并描述在何种情况下才适合获取完整历史。
b Add date range parameters and a sensible default limit and describe when the full history is appropriate.

1558
02:16:07,054 --> 02:16:07,360
c.
C.

1559
02:16:08,078 --> 02:16:10,596
完全移除 include all 参数。
Remove the include all parameter entirely.

1560
02:16:11,118 --> 02:16:11,360
d.
D.

1561
02:16:11,630 --> 02:16:15,044
将响应截断到最近的 50 条交易。
Truncate the response to the most recent 50 transactions.

1562
02:16:16,110 --> 02:16:17,188
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1563
02:16:22,990 --> 02:16:24,624
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1564
02:16:26,094 --> 02:16:30,660
这里的关键点是注意到智能体正在按逻辑运行。
The important move here is noticing that the agent is behaving rationally.

1565
02:16:31,726 --> 02:16:38,340
该工具没有日期过滤功能，所以要确保涵盖上个月，唯一的办法就是请求所有内容。
The tool has no date filter, so the only way to be certain of covering last month is to ask for everything.

1566
02:16:39,214 --> 02:16:45,092
选项 A 让它停止执行唯一能保证正确答案的操作，且没有提供替代方案。
Option A tells it to stop doing the one thing that guarantees a correct answer without offering an alternative.

1567
02:16:45,424 --> 02:16:49,348
选项 C 移除了一些问题确实需要的处理能力。
Option C removes the capability some questions legitimately need.

1568
02:16:49,664 --> 02:16:54,948
选项 B 是危险的，它对应到本模块前面提到的截断警告。
Option B is the dangerous one and it is a callback to the truncation warning earlier in the module.

1569
02:16:55,822 --> 02:17:04,004
在没有任何提示的情况下将交易截断到 50 条，意味着智能体认为它看到了所有内容，并基于部分信息自信地做出回答。
Truncating to 50 transactions with no indication that it happened means the agent believes it saw everything and answers confidently from a partial view.

1570
02:17:04,464 --> 02:17:07,748
这把一个成本问题变成了一个正确性问题。
That converts a cost problem into a correctness problem.

1571
02:17:09,870 --> 02:17:10,436
模块
Module

1572
02:17:11,692 --> 02:17:14,340
6. 下一节是关于工具结果和错误。
6. Next on tool results and errors.

1573
02:17:16,206 --> 02:17:17,183
第 6 模块。
Module 6.

1574
02:17:17,424 --> 02:17:17,904
继续。
Still.

1575
02:17:18,638 --> 02:17:19,522
领域 2。
Domain 2.

1576
02:17:22,093 --> 02:17:27,075
第 5 模块是关于如何调用正确的工具并带上正确的参数。
Module 5 was about getting the right tool called with the right arguments.

1577
02:17:28,142 --> 02:17:32,804
这个模块是关于当它失败时会发生什么，而在这次考试中，这种情况往往是大多数情况。
This module is about what happens when it fails, which on this exam is most of the time.

1578
02:17:33,422 --> 02:17:34,308
还是分为两个部分。
Two halves again.

1579
02:17:35,054 --> 02:17:40,066
首先，两种类型的工具故障，以及为什么把它们同等对待会破坏智能体。
First, the two kinds of tool failure and why treating them the same breaks agents.

1580
02:17:41,038 --> 02:17:46,852
其次是强制执行，这是当提示词不够好时，规则真正该属于的地方。
Second, enforcement, which is where a rule actually belongs when a prompt is not good enough.

1581
02:17:47,502 --> 02:17:54,084
这后半部分非常重要，因为它涉及的原则在另外三个领域中也会决定相关问题的答案。
That second half is worth disproportionate marks because the same principle decides questions in three other domains.

1582
02:17:55,790 --> 02:17:56,548
从这里开始。
Start here.

1583
02:17:58,316 --> 02:18:04,066
当你设计错误信息时，你的直觉是为凌晨三点查看日志的开发人员编写内容。
When you design an error, your instinct is to write for a developer reading a log at 3 in the morning.

1584
02:18:05,358 --> 02:18:07,428
但在这种情况下，那种直觉是错误的。
That instinct is wrong in this context.

1585
02:18:08,110 --> 02:18:15,843
工具错误的主要阅读者是模型，它将完全根据你写的内容来决定下一步该做什么。
The primary reader of a tool error is the model and it will decide what to do next based entirely on what you wrote.

1586
02:18:16,718 --> 02:18:20,224
所以问题不在于信息在技术上是否准确。
So the question is not whether the message is technically accurate.

1587
02:18:20,654 --> 02:18:24,964
问题在于智能体是否能读懂它，并据此判断如何采取不同的行动。
The question is whether an agent could read it and work out what to do differently.

1588
02:18:25,772 --> 02:18:29,412
本模块前半部分几乎所有内容都源于此点。
Almost everything else in the first half of this module follows from that.

1589
02:18:31,084 --> 02:18:35,204
MCP 定义了两种类型的故障，这种区分是刻意为之的。
MCP defines two kinds of failure and the distinction is deliberate.

1590
02:18:35,598 --> 02:18:40,708
协议错误是一个带有代码的 JSON RPC 错误对象。
A protocol error is a JSON RPC error object with a code.

1591
02:18:41,325 --> 02:18:46,180
工具不存在或者请求格式错误，导致没有任何内容运行。
The tool does not exist or the request was malformed, so nothing ran.

1592
02:18:46,958 --> 02:18:48,804
模型通常根本看不到它。
The model usually never sees it.

1593
02:18:49,998 --> 02:18:52,132
而工具执行错误则是不同的情况。
A tool execution error is different.

1594
02:18:53,070 --> 02:18:58,052
工具存在，请求有效，工具运行了但失败了。
The tool existed, the request was valid, the tool ran and it failed.

1595
02:18:58,316 --> 02:19:05,442
这种情况会返回一个正常的成功结果，只是 isError 标志设为 true，模型会将其作为内容读取。
That comes back as a normal successful result with the isError flag set to true and the model reads it as content.

1596
02:19:05,998 --> 02:19:08,260
之所以要区分这两者，原因就在于后续的处理。
The reason for the split is in the callout.

1597
02:19:08,781 --> 02:19:11,492
有一种故障是模型可以采取措施处理的。
One kind of failure the model can do something about.

1598
02:19:12,270 --> 02:19:13,763
另一种它则无法处理。
The other it cannot.

1599
02:19:14,190 --> 02:19:16,704
因为请求本身的结构就是坏的。
Because the request structure itself was broken.

1600
02:19:18,126 --> 02:19:19,396
这是分类规则。
Here is the sorting rule.

1601
02:19:19,758 --> 02:19:22,724
不存在的工具名称属于协议错误。
A tool name that does not exist is a protocol error.

1602
02:19:23,182 --> 02:19:26,436
在协议层面格式错误的请求也是协议错误。
A request malformed at the protocol level is a protocol error.

1603
02:19:27,308 --> 02:19:30,308
表中的其他所有情况都属于工具执行错误。
Everything else in this table is a tool execution error.

1604
02:19:30,958 --> 02:19:33,028
参数通过输入校验失败。
A parameter that failed validation.

1605
02:19:33,486 --> 02:19:36,784
上游 API 返回 500。
An upstream AP returning a 500.

1606
02:19:37,358 --> 02:19:40,132
业务规则拒绝了该操作。
A business rule rejecting the operation.

1607
02:19:40,686 --> 02:19:42,244
数据库被锁定。
A locked database.

1608
02:19:42,624 --> 02:19:48,356
这些情况全部属于 isError 为 true，因为工具运行了，模型可以针对它们做出响应。
All of those are is error true because the tool ran and the model can respond to them.

1609
02:19:48,846 --> 02:19:51,428
最后一项的重要性比看起来要大。
And the last row matters more than it looks.

1610
02:19:51,744 --> 02:19:55,140
搜索结果为空并不算错误。
A search that matched nothing is not an error at all.

1611
02:19:55,504 --> 02:19:58,564
它是一个恰好为空的成功结果。
It is a successful result that happens to be empty.

1612
02:20:00,302 --> 02:20:06,308
输入校验值得单独拿出来讲，因为这是开发者最容易搞错的地方。
Validation deserves its own slide because it is where implementations most often get this wrong.

1613
02:20:08,206 --> 02:20:13,444
如果你把错误的参数报告为协议错误，模型只会收到一个通用的失败提示。
If you report a bad parameter as a protocol error, the model receives a generic failure.

1614
02:20:14,638 --> 02:20:20,036
它看不出是哪个字段错了或者正确的格式是什么，所以它没法自我修正。
It does not see which field was wrong or what the correct format is, so it cannot correct itself.

1615
02:20:20,622 --> 02:20:22,948
它会重复同样的调用并再次失败。
It retrieves the same call and fails again.

1616
02:20:24,046 --> 02:20:28,100
将其报告为 isError 为 true，模型就能读到错误信息了。
Report the same thing as is error true and the model reads the message.

1617
02:20:29,294 --> 02:20:35,364
它会看到数量字段需要整数但收到了单词 5，然后用数字再次调用。
It sees that quantity expected an integer and received the word 5, then calls again with a number.

1618
02:20:36,462 --> 02:20:39,620
规范中明确澄清了这一点。
The specification was clarified explicitly on this point.

1619
02:20:40,398 --> 02:20:43,236
输入校验属于工具执行错误。
Input validation is a tool execution error.

1620
02:20:43,568 --> 02:20:48,068
搞错了就会让一个能自我修正的智能体变成卡死的智能体。
Getting it wrong converts a self-correcting agent into a stuck one.

1621
02:20:49,550 --> 02:20:50,608
那么，里面该填什么内容？
So what goes in one?

1622
02:20:51,054 --> 02:20:52,004
出了什么问题？
What went wrong?

1623
02:20:52,334 --> 02:20:54,628
用通俗易懂的语言，而不是代码编号。
In plain language rather than a code number.

1624
02:20:55,088 --> 02:20:57,188
是哪个字段或输入导致了错误？
Which field or input caused it?

1625
02:20:57,806 --> 02:21:00,452
因为指出具体的字段是解决问题的一半。
Because naming the field is half the fix.

1626
02:21:00,814 --> 02:21:03,716
包含预期的格式以及一个具体的示例。
The expected format with a concrete example.

1627
02:21:04,014 --> 02:21:06,916
例如：开始日期必须是“年-月-日”格式。
So start date must be year-month-day.

1628
02:21:07,246 --> 02:21:08,196
这里就是一个例子。
And here is one.

1629
02:21:09,038 --> 02:21:14,532
还有下一步该怎么做，包括如果当前工具真的没用时，该调用哪个工具。
And what to do next, including which tool to reach for, if this one genuinely cannot help.

1630
02:21:14,848 --> 02:21:17,412
不应该放入的内容是堆栈追踪。
What does not go in is a stack trace.

1631
02:21:17,808 --> 02:21:22,276
内部路径和数据库详情对这里没人有帮助，还会泄露大量信息。
Internal paths and database details help nobody here and leak a great deal.

1632
02:21:23,502 --> 02:21:28,164
把错误写成指令，因为阅读者是一个正在选择下一步动作的智能体。
Write the error as an instruction because the reader is an agent choosing its next move.

1633
02:21:29,742 --> 02:21:31,168
在一个表格中进行对比。
The contrast in one table.

1634
02:21:31,568 --> 02:21:34,688
“错误，输入无效”这句话描述得非常准确。
Error, invalid input is perfectly accurate.

1635
02:21:34,848 --> 02:21:37,124
但它没给智能体提供任何可操作的信息。
It also gives the agent nothing to act on.

1636
02:21:37,248 --> 02:21:43,204
于是它会重复同样的调用，做出相同的尝试，最终放弃或者开始胡编乱造。
So it retalies the same call, feigns identically, and eventually gives up or starts inventing values.

1637
02:21:43,982 --> 02:21:51,888
第二条信息指明了字段、说明了要求的格式、展示了实际接收的内容，并给出了示例。
The second message names the field, states the required format, shows what was actually received, and gives an example.

1638
02:21:52,334 --> 02:21:55,204
智能体重新格式化后，在下一次调用中成功了。
The agent reformats and succeeds on the next call.

1639
02:21:55,566 --> 02:21:56,932
两条信息都是正确的。
Both messages are true.

1640
02:21:57,422 --> 02:21:58,688
但只有一条是有用的。
Only one is useful.

1641
02:21:58,926 --> 02:22:01,924
在这场考试中，准确性并不是衡量标准。
On this exam, accuracy is never the standard.

1642
02:22:02,286 --> 02:22:03,808
可操作性才是。
Actionability is.

1643
02:22:05,422 --> 02:22:10,288
并非所有错误都应该被直接返回给智能体，而且智能体无法可靠地分辨哪些是哪种类型。
Not every error should be retrieved and the agent cannot reliably tell which is which from pros.

1644
02:22:10,862 --> 02:22:18,128
像速率限制、超时和 503 这样的瞬时故障，可能在 10 秒后就成功了。所以这种情况用退避策略来重试。
Transient failures like rate limits, timeouts, and a 503 might well succeed in 10 seconds. So retrieve with back-off.

1645
02:22:18,894 --> 02:22:26,820
像输入错误、权限缺失或违反业务规则等确定性失败，会一直以同样的方式失败。因此重试纯属浪费。
Deterministic failures like a bad input, a missing permission, or a business rule violation will fail identically forever. So retrying is pure waste.

1646
02:22:27,278 --> 02:22:34,148
解决方法是在人类可读的消息旁边，用类别或“可重试”标志来明确其结构类型。
The fix is to say which it is structurally with a category or a retryable flag alongside the human readable message.

1647
02:22:35,022 --> 02:22:38,448
记住这个考点，因为它是一个经常出现的考试信号。
And remember the call out because it is a recurring exam signal.

1648
02:22:38,608 --> 02:22:43,972
当题干说每次尝试都以同样的方式失败时，它是在告诉你这个故障是确定性的。
When a stem says every attempt fails the same way, it is telling you the failure is deterministic.

1649
02:22:45,518 --> 02:22:47,332
这是一个值得摒弃的旧习惯。
One habit worth unlearning.

1650
02:22:48,302 --> 02:22:53,892
当工具返回“错误为真”时，直觉往往是捕获它并在客户端代码中处理。
When a tool returns is error true, the instinct is to catch it in client code and handle it there.

1651
02:22:54,606 --> 02:22:55,488
要抵制这种做法。
Resist that.

1652
02:22:55,886 --> 02:23:01,380
将错误内容作为工具结果返回给模型，让它去判断该如何处理。
Pass the error content back to the model as the tool result and let it reason about what to do.

1653
02:23:02,350 --> 02:23:06,148
盲目重试会发送相同的请求并得到同样的失败。
A blind retry resents the same request and gets the same failure.

1654
02:23:06,734 --> 02:23:11,460
有根据的重试意味着模型已经读到了错误原因，并做出相应的调整。
An informed retry means the model has read what went wrong and changes something.

1655
02:23:12,110 --> 02:23:12,996
并且要设上限。
And cap it.

1656
02:23:13,774 --> 02:23:20,772
尝试两次或三次后就该升级处理了，因为没有限制的自我修正循环会导致成本失控。
Two or three attempts then escalate because an uncapped self-correction loop is a cost incident waiting to be discovered.

1657
02:23:22,254 --> 02:23:23,780
这一条很容易考到人。
This one catches people.

1658
02:23:24,558 --> 02:23:27,076
一个没有任何匹配结果的搜索也是成功的。
A search that matched nothing has succeeded.

1659
02:23:27,408 --> 02:23:30,208
它回答了问题，只是答案是“无”。
It answered the question and the answer was none.

1660
02:23:30,638 --> 02:23:38,596
如果将其报告为错误，智能体就会尝试重试、重新表述、再次重试，并最终判定工具损坏而绕过它。
Report it as an error and the agent will retry, rephrase, retry again, and eventually decide the tool is broken and root around it.

1661
02:23:39,086 --> 02:23:41,828
相反，应该返回一个带有少量上下文的空结果。
Instead, return an empty result with a little context.

1662
02:23:42,286 --> 02:23:44,644
搜索了什么内容？以及哪些操作可以扩大搜索范围？
What was searched and what might widen it?

1663
02:23:45,038 --> 02:23:47,888
在这些日期之间没有找到该客户的记录。
No results found for that customer between those dates.

1664
02:23:48,206 --> 02:23:49,508
尝试扩大查询范围。
Try broadening the range.

1665
02:23:49,806 --> 02:23:52,804
这是一个能够完成有用工作的成功结果。
That is a successful result doing useful work.

1666
02:23:53,550 --> 02:23:55,716
同样的逻辑也适用于真实的零值。
And the same holds for a legitimate zero.

1667
02:23:56,654 --> 02:24:00,708
“无未支付账单”是一个事实，而不是一个失败。
No outstanding invoices is a fact rather than a failure.

1668
02:24:02,350 --> 02:24:05,668
关于安全的一点简短说明，因为考试内容涉及到了这一点。
A short security note because the exam does touch it.

1669
02:24:06,048 --> 02:24:11,524
堆栈跟踪、内部文件路径和数据库详情不应该出现在错误信息中。
Stack traces, internal file paths, and database details do not belong in an error.

1670
02:24:11,982 --> 02:24:15,940
这些文本会进入模型的上下文，甚至可能直接展示给用户。
That text lands in the model's context and often in front of a user.

1671
02:24:16,208 --> 02:24:20,580
同样，也不要区分“不存在的记录”和“你可能看不到的记录”。
Nor does the distinction between a record that does not exist and one you may not see.

1672
02:24:21,518 --> 02:24:25,444
揭示两者的区别会让攻击者能够枚举你的数据。
Revealing which is which lets someone enumerate your data.

1673
02:24:25,998 --> 02:24:32,676
不要将未经清洗的上游错误传递过来，因为供应商写的任何内容现在都会出现在你的对话中。
And do not pass upstream errors through unsanitized because whatever the vendor wrote is now in your conversation.

1674
02:24:33,550 --> 02:24:36,388
只包含足够执行操作的信息，不多也不少。
Include enough to act on and nothing more.

1675
02:24:37,326 --> 02:24:43,076
错误文本也是工具输出，所有在正常响应中需要清洗的内容，在这里同样适用。
Error text is tool output, and everything you would sanitize in a normal response applies here too.

1676
02:24:44,750 --> 02:24:45,796
这就是关于错误的处理。
That is errors.

1677
02:24:46,926 --> 02:24:48,132
现在是强制执行部分。
Now enforcement.

1678
02:24:48,560 --> 02:24:56,548
这一部分比长度显示的更重要，因为它涉及的原则决定了五个领域中的四个。
This half is worth more marks than its length suggests because the same principle decides questions in four of the five domains.

1679
02:24:57,262 --> 02:24:58,916
这个问题表述起来很简单。
The question is simple to state.

1680
02:24:59,470 --> 02:25:02,660
当你需要某些规则生效时，你应该把规则放在哪里？
When you need something to be true, where do you put the rule?

1681
02:25:03,662 --> 02:25:07,748
这里有四个候选位置，但实际上只有三个是有效的。
There are four candidate places, and only three of them actually work.

1682
02:25:09,294 --> 02:25:12,420
这四个位置在表格中已经为你分类好了。
Four places and the table sorts them for you.

1683
02:25:13,710 --> 02:25:16,100
系统提示词提供的是说服力。
The system prompt gives you persuasion.

1684
02:25:16,750 --> 02:25:18,244
它大部分时候有效，
It works most of the time

1685
02:25:18,958 --> 02:25:21,924
但在智能体感到困惑时就会失效，
and it fails exactly when the agent is confused,

1686
02:25:22,574 --> 02:25:23,844
而那正是你最需要它的时候。
which is when you needed it.

1687
02:25:24,720 --> 02:25:32,228
Clot.md 和其他记忆文件提供的内容是一样的，因为它们是通过不同路径加载到同一个窗口的上下文。
Clot.md and other memory files give you the same thing because they are context loaded into the same window by a different route.

1688
02:25:32,880 --> 02:25:38,660
在工具内部提供的是强制执行，因为无论智能体意图如何，检查都会在每次调用时运行。
Inside the tool gives you enforcement because the check runs on every call, whatever the agent intended.

1689
02:25:39,662 --> 02:25:45,828
而钩子或权限规则提供的是来自工具外部的强制执行，它们会在事件触发时运行并能够进行拦截。
And a hook or a permission rule gives you enforcement from outside the tool firing on the event and able to block it.

1690
02:25:46,958 --> 02:25:48,548
前两个属于上下文。
The top two are context.

1691
02:25:49,102 --> 02:25:50,564
后两个属于代码。
The bottom two are code.

1692
02:25:51,342 --> 02:25:53,700
只有代码能提供保证。
Only code guarantees anything.

1693
02:25:54,958 --> 02:25:59,908
这里把区别具体化了，注意答案不是非此即彼。
Here is the distinction made concrete and note that the answer is not either or.

1694
02:26:01,006 --> 02:26:06,880
在工具描述中要求超过500的退款需要审批，这确实很有用。
Putting refunds above 500 require approval in the tool description is genuinely useful.

1695
02:26:07,040 --> 02:26:11,140
它能帮助智能体做出正确的决策，并降低失败率。
It helps the agent make good decisions and it lowers the failure rate.

1696
02:26:12,014 --> 02:26:18,436
但它仍然是一句描述，而描述可能会被逻辑绕过去，你不能把它作为一种控制手段展示给审计员看。
It is still a sentence, and a sentence can be reasoned past, and you cannot show it to an auditor as a control.

1697
02:26:19,566 --> 02:26:26,244
把检查放在工具内部意味着无论提示词、措辞或用户输入了什么内容，它都会在每次调用时运行。
Putting the check inside the tool means it runs on every call regardless of prompting, phrasing, or anything a user typed.

1698
02:26:27,086 --> 02:26:27,876
两者都要做。
Do both.

1699
02:26:28,750 --> 02:26:32,484
描述防止尝试行为，而检查防止结果发生。
The description prevents the attempt and the check prevents the outcome.

1700
02:26:33,040 --> 02:26:35,012
只有后者才是保证。
Only the second one is a guarantee.

1701
02:26:36,480 --> 02:26:39,440
在实践中，工具内部的强制执行看起来是这样的。
Practically, tool internal enforcement looks like this.

1702
02:26:39,790 --> 02:26:44,388
在采取行动前进行验证，并返回明确的错误信息，而不是抛出异常。
Validate before acting and return a clear is error rather than throwing an exception.

1703
02:26:45,120 --> 02:26:49,316
在工具内部检查授权，而不是在描述它的提示词中去检查。
Check authorization inside the tool rather than in the prompt describing it.

1704
02:26:50,000 --> 02:26:54,436
尽可能让副作用变得无害，这样重复操作也不会产生影响。
Make side effects inimputent where you can, so a repeat is harmless.

1705
02:26:55,342 --> 02:27:01,572
并限制工具能做的事情。这样限制就是能力的属性，而不是针对任何特定请求的限制。
And cap what the tool can do. So the limit is a property of the capability rather than of any particular request.

1706
02:27:03,150 --> 02:27:06,468
最后一点会误导很多人，所以记好它。
The last point catches a lot of people, so hold on to it.

1707
02:27:06,720 --> 02:27:11,920
一个被设为 true 的确认参数是由你试图去约束的那个智能体设置的。
A confirmed equals true parameter is set by the same agent you are trying to constrain.

1708
02:27:12,430 --> 02:27:15,780
由模块控制的标志位根本不算是一种控制手段。
A flag the module controls is not a control at all.

1709
02:27:17,134 --> 02:27:27,844
有时工具并不是合适的地方，有两个常见原因：你并不拥有它，因为它是一个你仅仅在使用的第三方 MCP 服务器。
Sometimes the tool is not the right place, and there are two common reasons. You do not own it because it is a third-party MCP server you are simply consuming.

1710
02:27:28,320 --> 02:27:35,844
或者规则跨越了多个工具，比如“永远不要写入生产环境”，这必须适用于任何执行写入操作的工具。
Or the rule spans several tools, like never write to production, which has to hold whichever tool is doing the writing.

1711
02:27:36,430 --> 02:27:40,708
在这两种情况下，控制逻辑是向外扩展而非向后退缩。
In both cases, the control moves outward rather than backward.

1712
02:27:41,038 --> 02:27:48,292
权限规则会彻底移除该功能，而钩子会在事件触发时执行，并可以检查和拦截它。
A permission rule removes the capability entirely, and a hook fires on the event and can inspect and block it.

1713
02:27:48,974 --> 02:27:51,556
第9模块涵盖了这两点。
Module 9 covers both properly.

1714
02:27:52,142 --> 02:27:53,860
原则没有改变。
The principle is unchanged.

1715
02:27:54,766 --> 02:28:00,900
如果工具不是由你修改的，就应该将控制逻辑上移一层，而不是退回到提示词中。
If the tool is not yours to modify, move the control up a layer rather than retreating into the prompt.

1716
02:28:02,414 --> 02:28:03,588
模式识别。
Pattern recognition.

1717
02:28:03,982 --> 02:28:11,844
重试产生相同的错误意味着是确定性的。所以要修复输入或结构，而不是修改重试策略。
Redrying produces identical failures means deterministic. So fix the input or the structure rather than the retree policy.

1718
02:28:13,006 --> 02:28:17,988
智能体在调用失败后放弃，意味着错误信息没提供任何可操作的提示。
The agent gives up after a failed call means the error told it nothing actionable.

1719
02:28:18,862 --> 02:28:26,212
重复使用相同的错误值进行调用，意味着验证被报告为协议错误，或者消息内容毫无用处。
Repeatedly calling with the same bad value means validation is being reported as a protocol error or the message is useless.

1720
02:28:28,398 --> 02:28:34,820
当没有任何匹配项时判定工具损坏，意味着空结果正被报告为错误。
Deciding the tool is broken when nothing matches means empty results are being reported as errors.

1721
02:28:35,470 --> 02:28:45,936
无论提示词如何，绝不能超过某项限制，这意味着在工具内部或钩子中。而我们无法修改第三方服务器，意味着是钩子或权限规则。
Must never exceed something, regardless of prompting, means inside the tool or a hook. And we cannot modify the third-party server means a hook or a permission rule.

1722
02:28:46,126 --> 02:28:50,084
最后这两行是整个考试中价值最高的模式。
Those last two rows are the highest value pattern on the whole exam.

1723
02:28:51,662 --> 02:28:52,576
5行。
5 lines.

1724
02:28:52,816 --> 02:28:57,284
协议错误是针对损坏请求的，其他所有情况都是错误。
Protocol errors are for broken requests and everything else is is error.

1725
02:28:57,456 --> 02:28:59,876
这样模型就能读到它并进行自我修正。
So the model can read it and correct itself.

1726
02:29:00,176 --> 02:29:04,804
将错误写成指令，标明字段、格式，
Write errors as instructions, naming the field, the format,

1727
02:29:05,710 --> 02:29:07,908
一个示例以及下一步操作。
an example, and the next step.

1728
02:29:08,814 --> 02:29:13,856
说明失败是否可以重试，因为智能体无法从纯文本中推断出这一点。
Say whether a failure is retrieable because the agent cannot infer that from prose.

1729
02:29:14,254 --> 02:29:20,420
空结果是一个成功的结果，如果将其报告为错误，就会破坏智能体对工具的信任。
An empty result is a success, and reporting it as an error destroys the agent's trust in the tool.

1730
02:29:21,326 --> 02:29:29,092
描述是用来劝导的，而工具、钩子和权限是用来强制执行的。所以“保证”这个词总是指向第二组。
And descriptions persuade while tools, hooks, and permissions enforce. So the word guarantee always points at the second group.

1731
02:29:29,776 --> 02:29:31,268
现在有七个场景。
Seven scenarios now.

1732
02:29:31,950 --> 02:29:36,644
三个关于错误设计的，三个关于强制执行的，还有一个两者都不是的。
Three on error design, three on enforcement, and one that is neither.

1733
02:29:38,286 --> 02:29:39,204
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

1734
02:29:39,566 --> 02:29:42,256
一个 MCP 服务器提供了一个预订工具。
An MCP server exposes a booking tool.

1735
02:29:42,416 --> 02:29:46,736
当日期参数以错误的格式到达时，服务器抛出异常。
When a date parameter arrives in the wrong format, the server raises an exception.

1736
02:29:46,976 --> 02:29:50,884
SDK 将其转换为 JSON RPC 错误。
The SDK converts that into a JSON RPC error.

1737
02:29:51,406 --> 02:29:56,612
生产环境的追踪显示，智能体用同样的错误日期调用该工具多达五次。
Production traces show the agent calling the tool with the same malformed date up to five times.

1738
02:29:57,614 --> 02:30:01,376
随后它放弃了任务，并告诉用户预订不可用。
It then abandons the task and tells the user booking is unavailable.

1739
02:30:02,030 --> 02:30:04,548
用户提供的日期是下周二。
The date the user supplied was next Tuesday.

1740
02:30:05,198 --> 02:30:06,340
根本原因是什么？
What is the root cause?

1741
02:30:06,766 --> 02:30:10,180
a. 智能体在调用工具之前应该解析相对日期。
a. The agent should parse relative dates before calling the tool.

1742
02:30:11,054 --> 02:30:16,740
b. 验证失败被报告为协议错误，所以智能体根本看不到哪里出了问题。
b. The validation failure is reported as a protocol error so the agent never sees what was wrong.

1743
02:30:17,136 --> 02:30:21,348
c. 重试限制太低，导致智能体无法收敛到有效的日期。
C. The rectory limit is too low for the agent to converge on a valid date.

1744
02:30:21,856 --> 02:30:22,176
d。
D.

1745
02:30:22,542 --> 02:30:24,836
工具应该接受自然语言日期。
The tool should accept natural language dates.

1746
02:30:25,326 --> 02:30:26,404
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1747
02:30:31,982 --> 02:30:33,696
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1748
02:30:36,334 --> 02:30:40,452
关键点在于智能体连续五次发送同一个格式错误的日期。
The tell is that the agent sends the same malformed date five times.

1749
02:30:40,816 --> 02:30:48,336
完全相同的重复意味着它在尝试之间没学到任何东西，而它之所以没学到东西是因为协议错误根本没传达给它。
Identical repeats mean it learned nothing between attempts and it learned nothing because a protocol error never reaches it.

1750
02:30:48,910 --> 02:30:51,296
按原样报告相同的失败作为错误。
Report the same failure as is error.

1751
02:30:51,662 --> 02:30:57,056
正确，并包含指出字段和格式的提示信息，智能体会在第二次调用时重新格式化。
True with a message naming the field and the format and the agent reformats on the second call.

1752
02:30:57,296 --> 02:31:01,508
选项 C 是一个常见的错误答案，这一点需要明确说明。
Option C is the popular wrong answer and it is worth being clear about.

1753
02:31:01,870 --> 02:31:06,660
五次相同的尝试不会收敛到任何结果，所以第六次才会改变。
Five identical attempts do not converge on anything, so a sixth changes.

1754
02:31:07,790 --> 02:31:08,260
无。
Nothing.

1755
02:31:09,294 --> 02:31:17,572
选项 D 对这个特定的输入有效，但没能解决根本的隐蔽性问题。因此下一个错误值仍会以同样隐蔽的方式失败。
Option D would work for this particular input and leaves the underlying invisibility untouched. So the next bad value fails the same silent way.

1756
02:31:18,126 --> 02:31:21,988
选项 A 要求智能体去猜测一个没人告诉过它的格式。
Option A asks the agent to guess a format nobody told it.

1757
02:31:23,696 --> 02:31:35,204
场景 2。退款工具的说明是处理客户退款。超过 500 的退款需要经理批准，不得直接发放。
Scenario 2. A refund tool is documented as issues a customer refund. Refunds above 500 require manager approval and must not be issued directly.

1758
02:31:35,726 --> 02:31:40,388
在 6 个月内，有 11 笔超过 500 的退款被直接发放了。
Over 6 months, 11 refunds above 500 were issued directly.

1759
02:31:41,294 --> 02:31:48,416
审查显示，在每种情况下，客户都给出了看似合理的理由，而且系统提示词中也说明了限制。
Review shows the agent had been given plausible reasons by customers in each case, and the system prompt also states the limit.

1760
02:31:48,656 --> 02:31:52,096
合规团队需要证明这种情况不应该发生。
The compliance team needs to demonstrate that this cannot happen.

1761
02:31:52,398 --> 02:31:54,176
哪项符合要求？
What satisfies the requirement?

1762
02:31:54,510 --> 02:31:59,908
a 将限制也添加到 clot.md 中，让它出现在三个地方。
a add the limit to clot.md as well so it appears in three places.

1763
02:32:00,878 --> 02:32:09,540
b 在工具中拒绝超过 500 英镑的金额，并返回一个引导智能体前往审批流程的错误。
b reject amounts over 500 pounds inside the tune, returning an error that directs the agent to the approval tune.

1764
02:32:10,286 --> 02:32:10,496
c。
C.

1765
02:32:11,278 --> 02:32:17,444
增加一个 requires_approval 参数，对于超过 500 的金额，智能体必须将其设为 true。
Add a requires approval parameter that the agent must set to true for amounts over 500.

1766
02:32:18,350 --> 02:32:18,576
d。
d.

1767
02:32:19,136 --> 02:32:24,356
在系统提示词中添加几个简短示例，展示超过限制时的正确拒绝情况。
Add few short examples to the system prompt showing correct refusals above the limit.

1768
02:32:24,878 --> 02:32:26,084
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1769
02:32:31,694 --> 02:32:33,072
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1770
02:32:33,550 --> 02:32:35,140
两个短语决定了结果。
Two phrases decide it.

1771
02:32:35,552 --> 02:32:46,020
给出了合理的理由，告诉你故障模式是劝说并证明这种情况不会发生，同时告诉你某个速率不可接受。这两点共同排除了所有由文字组成的选项。
Given plausible reasons, tells you the failure mode is persuasion and demonstrate that this cannot happen, tells you a rate is not acceptable. Together they eliminate every option made of words.

1772
02:32:47,886 --> 02:32:49,956
选项 A 是需要注意的那个。
Option A is the one to notice.

1773
02:32:50,894 --> 02:32:55,748
增加第三遍同样的句子并不能提供更多保护，而且也没用。
Adding a third copy of the same sentence feels like more protection and is not.

1774
02:32:56,046 --> 02:32:59,460
这三项都落在同一个上下文窗口中，同样具有争议性。
All three land in the same context window, equally arguable.

1775
02:32:59,872 --> 02:33:02,628
选项 C 是本模块前面提到的陷阱。
Option C is the trap from earlier in the module.

1776
02:33:02,894 --> 02:33:07,300
智能体设置的参数是由你试图限制的那个智能体来设置的。
A parameter the agent sets is set by the agent you are trying to constrain.

1777
02:33:08,014 --> 02:33:14,084
选项 D 确实提高了速率，而且合规团队并没有要求更好的速率。
Option D genuinely improves the rate, and the compliance team did not ask for a better rate.

1778
02:33:15,726 --> 02:33:16,832
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

1779
02:33:17,166 --> 02:33:19,812
一个研究智能体使用了一个文档搜索工具。
A research agent uses a document search tool.

1780
02:33:20,032 --> 02:33:26,372
当查询没有匹配到任何文档时，该工具会返回一个读取失败、无匹配文档的错误。
When a query matches no documents, the tool returns an error reading Search failed, no matching documents.

1781
02:33:26,752 --> 02:33:32,324
工程师注意到在结果为空后，智能体会连续进行三到四次范围越来越广的搜索。
Engineers notice the agent runs three or four progressively broader searches after an empty result.

1782
02:33:33,134 --> 02:33:36,964
随后它在整个会话中都不再使用搜索工具，而是从记忆中回答。
It then stops using the search tool for the session and answers from memory.

1783
02:33:37,518 --> 02:33:39,204
最有效的修改是什么？
What is the most effective change?

1784
02:33:39,790 --> 02:33:45,188
a. 返回一个成功的空结果，说明查询了什么内容并建议如何扩大范围。
a return a successful empty result, stating what was searched and suggesting how to broaden it.

1785
02:33:45,646 --> 02:33:45,872
b。
b.

1786
02:33:46,446 --> 02:33:51,140
在系统提示词中告知智能体，空搜索是正常的，不是故障。
Instruct the agent in the system, prompt that empty searches are normal and not failures.

1787
02:33:52,046 --> 02:33:56,324
c. 让工具在没有任何匹配时自动扩大查询范围。
C. Have the tool automatically broaden the query when nothing matches.

1788
02:33:56,782 --> 02:34:01,124
d. 隐藏错误并返回一个不带消息的空数组。
D. Suppress the error and return an empty array with no message.

1789
02:34:02,094 --> 02:34:03,364
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1790
02:34:09,070 --> 02:34:10,272
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

1791
02:34:10,542 --> 02:34:12,740
关键点在于症状的后半部分。
The giveaway is the second half of the symptom.

1792
02:34:13,152 --> 02:34:19,268
智能体完全停止使用搜索工具，在报告了多次故障后，这是合理的行为。
The agent stops using the search tool altogether, which is rational behavior after several reported failures.

1793
02:34:20,174 --> 02:34:27,716
它判定该工具不可靠并绕过它，现在它从记忆中回答，这比空结果要糟糕得多。
It concluded the tool was unreliable and routed around it, and now it is answering from memory, which is far worse than an empty result.

1794
02:34:28,974 --> 02:34:33,604
选项 B 具有启发性，因为它要求智能体去不信任它自己的工具。
Option B is instructive because it asks the agent to disbelieve its own tool.

1795
02:34:33,998 --> 02:34:41,444
工具提示失败，而提示词却说当它显示失败时请忽略，这是一个逻辑不通的要求。
The tool says failed and the prompt says ignore that when it says failed, which is an incoherent thing to ask.

1796
02:34:42,126 --> 02:34:49,764
选项 C 剥夺了智能体区分精确匹配和扩大范围后的匹配的能力，这恰好掩盖了它需要的界限。
Option C removes the agent's ability to distinguish an exact match from a widened one, which hides exactly the boundary it needs.

1797
02:34:50,510 --> 02:34:55,812
选项 D 对了一半，而空结果中的上下文才是决定性的区别。
Option D is half right and context in the empty result is what makes the difference.

1798
02:34:57,550 --> 02:34:58,532
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

1799
02:34:59,022 --> 02:35:03,844
一个智能体集成了一个第三方 MCP 服务器来对接支付提供商。
An agent integrates a third-party MCP server for a payments provider.

1800
02:35:04,686 --> 02:35:06,244
团队有一项硬性规定。
The team has a hard rule.

1801
02:35:06,702 --> 02:35:10,724
在变更窗口之外，不得对生产环境调用任何工具。
No tool may be called against the production environment outside a change window.

1802
02:35:11,246 --> 02:35:15,972
该 MCP 服务器由供应商维护，无法修改。
The MCP server is maintained by the vendor and cannot be modified.

1803
02:35:16,910 --> 02:35:20,420
它提供了 8 个工具，其中 4 个会影响生产环境。
It exposes 8 tools, 4 of which can affect production.

1804
02:35:20,814 --> 02:35:24,996
目前的方法是在系统提示词中列出变更窗口的时间。
The current approach is a system prompt instruction listing the change window times.

1805
02:35:25,582 --> 02:35:27,716
哪种强制执行方式最可靠？
What is the most reliable enforcement?

1806
02:35:28,302 --> 02:35:33,700
a. 使用一个钩子来检查对这些工具的调用，并在窗口外拦截它们。
a A hook that inspects calls to those tools and blocks them outside the window.

1807
02:35:34,222 --> 02:35:39,396
b. 分叉供应商的 MCP 服务器，并在每个受影响的工具中加入检查。
b. Fork the vendor's MCP server and add the check inside each affected tool.

1808
02:35:39,792 --> 02:35:40,032
C。
C.

1809
02:35:40,462 --> 02:35:44,132
强化系统提示词，并在每次请求中包含当前时间。
Strengthen the system prompt and include the current time in every request.

1810
02:35:44,512 --> 02:35:44,752
D。
D.

1811
02:35:45,326 --> 02:35:48,516
从允许的工具中永久移除这四个保护性工具。
Remove the four protection tools from allowed tools permanently.

1812
02:35:49,934 --> 02:35:51,172
稍停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

1813
02:35:56,686 --> 02:35:57,828
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

1814
02:35:58,254 --> 02:36:06,832
这个案例的价值在于有两个选项都是真正的强制执行。所以仅靠“劝导还是强制”这条规则是不够的。
What makes this scenario useful is that two options are genuine enforcement. So the persuade versus enforce rule is not enough on its own.

1815
02:36:07,854 --> 02:36:15,748
选项 D 移除了该功能，绝对可靠，而且是永久性的，这会把变更窗口和其他所有东西都挡掉。
Option D removes the capability and is absolutely reliable, and it is also permanent, which blocks the change window along with everything else.

1816
02:36:16,622 --> 02:36:20,996
这里的规则是基于时间的，权限是开启或关闭的。
The rule here is conditional on time and permissions are on or off.

1817
02:36:21,312 --> 02:36:26,724
钩子可以评估条件并做出判断，这正是时间窗口所需要的。
Hooks can evaluate a condition and decide which is exactly what a time window needs.

1818
02:36:29,024 --> 02:36:37,412
选项 B 在技术上可行，但会让你被迫永远去维护一个分叉的供应商产品，而且题干已经排除了这个选项。
Option B would work technically and commits you to maintaining a fork of a vendor product forever and the STEM rules it out anyway.

1819
02:36:38,286 --> 02:36:44,228
选项 C 给出了智能体遵守规则所需的信息，但并没有强制执行合规性。
Option C gives the agent what it needs to comply without making compliance mandatory.

1820
02:36:45,824 --> 02:36:47,108
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

1821
02:36:47,726 --> 02:36:50,852
一个库存工具调用了一个仓库 API。
An inventory tool calls a warehouse API.

1822
02:36:51,264 --> 02:36:56,580
当该 API 受到速率限制时，它会返回 HTTP 429。
When that API is rate limited, it returns HTTP 429.

1823
02:36:57,024 --> 02:37:00,644
当 SKU 不存在时，它会返回 404。
When a SKU does not exist, it returns 404.

1824
02:37:01,006 --> 02:37:05,476
该工具将两者都报告为错误：true，仓库查询失败。
The tool reports both as is error true, warehouse lookup failed.

1825
02:37:05,998 --> 02:37:11,300
编排层会对任何失败的工具调用进行三次重试，并采用指数退避。
The orchestration layer retries any failed tool call three times with exponential backoff.

1826
02:37:12,686 --> 02:37:14,628
速率限制导致的失败通常可以恢复。
Rate limit failures usually recover.

1827
02:37:15,086 --> 02:37:20,612
未知 SKU 导致的失败会消耗三次重试机会和大量时间，智能体才会继续下一步。
Unknown SKU failures consume three retries and a lot of time before the agent moves on.

1828
02:37:21,646 --> 02:37:23,492
最有效的改进是什么？
What is the most effective change?

1829
02:37:24,398 --> 02:37:27,504
a. 将重试次数从 3 次减少到 1 次。
a reduce the retry count from 3 to 1.

1830
02:37:28,014 --> 02:37:33,188
b. 在错误中通过可重试标志和说明原因的消息来区分这两者。
b. Distinguish the two in the error with a retryable flag and a message naming the cause.

1831
02:37:33,710 --> 02:37:39,332
C. 将未知的 SKU 报告为协议错误，以便重试逻辑跳过它们。
C. Report unknown SKUs as a protocol error so the retry logic skips them.

1832
02:37:39,824 --> 02:37:40,064
D。
D.

1833
02:37:40,462 --> 02:37:43,780
增加退避间隔，让重试的成本降低。
Increase the back-off interval so retries are less costly.

1834
02:37:44,398 --> 02:37:45,316
稍停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

1835
02:37:51,054 --> 02:37:52,164
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1836
02:37:52,464 --> 02:38:01,924
结构性问题在于两种截然不同的故障共用了同一个错误信息，这导致两者被迫共用同一种重试策略。
The structural problem is that two genuinely different failures are wearing the same error, which forces a single retry policy onto both.

1837
02:38:03,790 --> 02:38:04,384
选项
Option

1838
02:38:06,510 --> 02:38:09,892
A 展示了为什么调整策略行不通。
A shows why tuning the policy cannot work.

1839
02:38:10,624 --> 02:38:17,988
减少到一次重试对未知 SKU 有帮助，但会损害限流情况，而后者才是真正需要重试的情况。
Dropping to one retry helps the unknown SKU and hurts the rate yamit, which is the case that actually needed retrying.

1840
02:38:18,478 --> 02:38:20,516
你只是用一种失败换取另一种失败。
You are trading one failure for another.

1841
02:38:21,742 --> 02:38:24,548
选项 D 只是让浪费的重试变慢了。
Option D just makes the wasted retries slower.

1842
02:38:25,326 --> 02:38:33,892
选项 C 很诱人，因为它确实绕过了重试逻辑，但它在两方面都是错误的。工具存在并运行了，所以它不是协议错误。
Option C is tempting because it does root around the retry logic and it is wrong on two counts. The tool exists and ran, so it is not a protocol error.

1843
02:38:34,510 --> 02:38:40,704
误用协议错误还会把信息从模型中隐藏掉，而这正是本模块警告要避免的情况。
Misusing protocol errors also hides the message from the model, which is what this module warns against.

1844
02:38:41,998 --> 02:38:43,104
场景 6。
Scenario 6.

1845
02:38:43,344 --> 02:38:48,708
一个数据流水线的智能体调用了一个转换工具，该工具在处理格式错误的行时偶尔会失败。
A data pipeline agent calls a transformation tool that occasionally fails on malformed rows.

1846
02:38:49,104 --> 02:38:53,796
工具返回了错误，并带有明确的、指明出错行和列的信息。
The tool returns his error with a clear message naming the offending row and column.

1847
02:38:54,704 --> 02:39:01,956
客户端代码捕获到该错误，记录下来，并向智能体返回一个通用的「转换不可用」字符串作为工具结果。
The client code catches that error, logs it, and returns a generic transformation unavailable string to the agent as the tool result.

1848
02:39:02,384 --> 02:39:06,468
智能体总是放弃整个文件，而不是跳过那行错误的行。
The agent consistently abandons the file rather than skipping the bad row.

1849
02:39:07,424 --> 02:39:08,772
根本原因是什么？
What is the root cause?

1850
02:39:09,710 --> 02:39:14,436
a. 智能体需要关于如何处理转换失败的指令。
a The agent needs instructions on how to handle transformation failures.

1851
02:39:14,944 --> 02:39:20,644
b. 在模型看到之前，客户端代码就把一个可操作的错误替换成了通用的错误。
b. The client code replaces an actionable error with the generic one before the model sees it.

1852
02:39:21,422 --> 02:39:21,664
C。
C.

1853
02:39:22,064 --> 02:39:26,224
转换工具应该自动跳过格式错误的行。
The transformation tool should skip malformed rows automatically.

1854
02:39:26,766 --> 02:39:29,060
D. 该错误应该是协议错误。
D. The error should be a protocol error.

1855
02:39:29,326 --> 02:39:31,264
这样智能体就会将其视为致命错误。
So the agent treats it as fatal.

1856
02:39:31,504 --> 02:39:32,836
稍停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

1857
02:39:38,464 --> 02:39:39,908
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1858
02:39:40,384 --> 02:39:44,388
这个场景之所以存在，是因为工具本身没问题。
And this scenario exists because the tool is not at fault.

1859
02:39:45,358 --> 02:39:50,212
有人写出了一个真正好的错误信息，指明了行和列。
Somebody wrote a genuinely good error, naming the row and the column.

1860
02:39:50,702 --> 02:39:55,332
然后客户端代码就把那个信息扔掉，换成了「转换不可用」。
And then the client code threw that away and substituted transformation unavailable.

1861
02:39:56,142 --> 02:40:01,924
智能体放弃该文件，因为面对没有任何细节的错误时，放弃是唯一合理的反应。
The agent abandons the file because abandoning is the only sensible response to an error with no detail in it.

1862
02:40:02,574 --> 02:40:03,172
选项。
Option.

1863
02:40:05,422 --> 02:40:12,644
A 不可行，因为没有指令能补偿智能体从未接收到的信息。它不知道是哪一行失败了。
A cannot work because no instruction compensates for information the agent never receives. It does not know which row failed.

1864
02:40:13,136 --> 02:40:15,748
从原则上讲，选项 C 不值得选择。
Option C is worth resisting on principle.

1865
02:40:16,366 --> 02:40:21,188
在数据流水线中静默跳过格式错误的行会掩盖正确性问题。
Silently skipping malformed rows in a data pipeline hides a correctness problem.

1866
02:40:21,742 --> 02:40:27,044
而选项 D 则走向了完全错误的方向，保证智能体看到的信息更少。
And option D moves in exactly the wrong direction, guaranteeing the agent sees even less.

1867
02:40:28,686 --> 02:40:29,828
场景 7。
Scenario 7.

1868
02:40:31,086 --> 02:40:34,500
一个面向客户的智能体调用了一个内部信用工具。
A customer-facing agent calls an internal credit tool.

1869
02:40:35,246 --> 02:40:38,532
当调用者缺乏权限时，工具返回此内容：
When the caller lacks permission, the tool returns this.

1870
02:40:39,022 --> 02:40:45,188
拒绝访问，账号 88213 存在但需要 credit admin 角色。
Access denied account 88213 exists but requires role credit admin.

1871
02:40:45,902 --> 02:40:51,524
在 check limit 时，查询失败于信用数据库内部端口 5432。
Query failed at credit DB internal port 5432 in check limit.

1872
02:40:52,430 --> 02:41:00,324
安全审查删除了错误文本中的部分内容，因为智能体在向客户解释为何无法提供帮助时，经常会重复这些内容给客户。
A security review has flat the error text because the agent frequently repeats parts of it to the customer when explaining why it cannot help.

1873
02:41:01,966 --> 02:41:03,268
应该如何修改？
What should change?

1874
02:41:03,616 --> 02:41:07,524
a. 指令要求智能体永远不要向客户重复工具的错误文本。
a instruct the agent never to repeat tool error text to customers.

1875
02:41:08,256 --> 02:41:08,496
b。
b.

1876
02:41:08,896 --> 02:41:16,708
对错误进行清洗，说明操作不被允许并告知下一步该做什么，而不包含内部细节或存在信息披露。
Sanitize the error to state that the operation is not permitted and what to do next without internal detail or existence disclosure.

1877
02:41:17,136 --> 02:41:21,124
c. 返回一个协议错误，使文本永远不会到达智能体。
C. Return a protocol error so the text never reaches the agent.

1878
02:41:21,710 --> 02:41:26,756
d. 完全移除错误消息，并返回内容为空的错误。
D. Remove the error message entirely and return is error with empty content.

1879
02:41:27,854 --> 02:41:28,964
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1880
02:41:34,734 --> 02:41:35,844
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1881
02:41:36,336 --> 02:41:41,252
这条消息中泄露了两个独立的信息，而大多数人只发现了一个。
Two separate things leak in that message and most people spot only one.

1882
02:41:45,262 --> 02:41:50,788
明显的泄露是基础设施细节，即宿主、端口和函数名称。
The obvious leak is the infrastructure detail, the host, the port, and the function name.

1883
02:41:51,534 --> 02:42:00,164
更隐蔽的一点是，这条消息确认了账号 88213 的存在，而这正是导致枚举攻击的区分点。
The subtler one is that the message confirms account 88213 exists, which is exactly the distinction that enables enumeration.

1884
02:42:00,654 --> 02:42:06,596
选项 A 将两者都留在上下文中，且智能体和客户之间只有一条提示词作为隔阂。
Option A leaves both in context, with a single prompt standing between them and the customer.

1885
02:42:07,534 --> 02:42:11,044
这是换了种形式的「说服而非强制」的错误。
That is the persuade versus enforce mistake in a new costume.

1886
02:42:11,662 --> 02:42:16,420
选项 C 和 D 通过破坏所有信息来解决泄露问题。
Options C and D solve disclosure by destroying all information.

1887
02:42:16,878 --> 02:42:21,668
这虽然安全但没用，会让你回到场景 1 中那种卡住的智能体状态。
That is safe and useless, and it takes you back to the stuck agent from scenario 1.

1888
02:42:22,190 --> 02:42:26,052
b 保留了信息的可用性，并剔除了不该出现的内容。
b keeps the message actionable and strips what should not be there.

1889
02:42:26,976 --> 02:42:30,656
接下来是模块 7，关于 MCP 本身。
Module 7 next on MCP itself.

1890
02:42:32,334 --> 02:42:34,532
模块 7 结束，领域 2。
Module 7 closes, domain 2.

1891
02:42:35,150 --> 02:42:37,828
第5和第6模块是关于通用的工具。
Modules 5 and 6 were about tools in general.

1892
02:42:38,254 --> 02:42:41,476
这一个则是专门关于模型上下文协议的。
This one is about the model context protocol specifically.

1893
02:42:41,856 --> 02:42:49,856
服务端暴露什么内容、客户端反向暴露什么、如何在 Claude Code 中连接，以及配置保存在哪里。
What a server exposes, what the client exposes back, how you connect one in Claude Code, and where the configuration lives.

1894
02:42:50,336 --> 02:42:57,092
这里的词汇量比前两个模块多，但判断逻辑少，所以题目往往更清晰。
There is more vocabulary here than in the last two modules and less judgment, so the questions tend to be cleaner.

1895
02:42:57,456 --> 02:43:01,764
只要正确掌握基础概念，就能轻松拿到几分。
Learn the primitives properly, and a handful of marks come almost free.

1896
02:43:03,118 --> 02:43:15,216
首先是 MCP 的用途，因为有些场景会把它当作解决某些它根本无法解决的问题的方案。MCP 是连接模型与外部系统的开放协议。
First, what MCP is for because scenarios sometimes offer it as a solution to problems it does not solve. MCP is an open protocol for connecting models to external systems.

1897
02:43:15,376 --> 02:43:18,180
它是基于 JSON RPC 2.0 构建的。
It is built on JSON RPC 2.0.

1898
02:43:18,496 --> 02:43:20,548
它带给你的是标准化。
What it buys you is standardization.

1899
02:43:21,134 --> 02:43:26,564
别人写的服务端可以与你的客户端配合工作，而你写的服务端也能与任何人的客户端配合。
A server someone else wrote works with your client, and a server you write works with anyone's client.

1900
02:43:27,182 --> 02:43:29,668
但它并不提供功能上的增强。
What it does not buy you is capability.

1901
02:43:30,798 --> 02:43:35,524
用 MCP 包装一个糟糕的工具，只会得到一个更容易分享的糟糕工具。
Wrapping a bad tool in MCP gives you a bad tool that is easier to share.

1902
02:43:36,686 --> 02:43:40,196
第5和第6模块的所有内容依然适用。
Everything from modules 5 and 6 still applies.

1903
02:43:41,934 --> 02:43:45,956
架构包含三个层级，考试要求你准确命名它们。
The architecture has three layers and the exam expects you to name them.

1904
02:43:46,446 --> 02:43:52,356
宿主是应用程序，比如 Claude Code、桌面应用或你基于 SDK 构建的自己的智能体。
The host is the application, so Cloud Code, the desktop app, or your own agent built on the SDK.

1905
02:43:52,656 --> 02:43:56,804
客户端是一个连接，且每个宿主为每个服务端持有一个客户端。
The client is a connection and the host holds one client per server.

1906
02:43:57,646 --> 02:44:01,376
服务端是提供功能的进程或服务。
The server is the process or service that exposes capabilities.

1907
02:44:01,616 --> 02:44:10,404
在底层，传输层负责传递消息，对于本地进程使用标准输入输出，对于远程内容则使用可流式的 HTTP。
And underneath, a transport carries the messages, either standard input and output for a local process or streamable HTTP for something remote.

1908
02:44:10,990 --> 02:44:14,436
注意这个强调，因为它对安全相关的题目很重要。
Note the call out because it matters for the security questions.

1909
02:44:15,278 --> 02:44:22,148
宿主位于模型和每个服务端之间，它决定了模型能看到哪些功能。
The host sits between the model and every server and it decides which capabilities the model ever sees.

1910
02:44:23,726 --> 02:44:28,576
服务端提供三种东西，第三列是大家经常忽略的部分。
A server exposes three things, and the third column is the part people skip.

1911
02:44:29,102 --> 02:44:33,060
工具是具有类型输入的操作，由模型决定何时调用。
Tools are actions with typed inputs, and the model decides when to call one.

1912
02:44:33,710 --> 02:44:40,868
资源是可以通过 URI 访问的只读数据，由应用程序附加或由用户拉取。
Resources are read only data addressed by a URI, and they get attached by the application or pulled in by the user.

1913
02:44:41,774 --> 02:44:46,148
提示词是带有参数的可用的模板，由用户来选择。
Prompts are usable templates with parameters and the user chooses them.

1914
02:44:46,574 --> 02:44:53,348
所以同一个服务端提供的东西中，有模型驱动的、应用驱动的，还有用户驱动的。
So the same server offers something the model drives, something the application drives, and something the user drives.

1915
02:44:53,776 --> 02:44:59,172
这个领域几乎所有的混淆都源于忘记了这三者中哪一个在主导。
Almost every confusion in this area comes from forgetting which of the three is in charge.

1916
02:45:00,416 --> 02:45:03,492
这是本模块中最关键的一对易混淆概念。
This is the confusion pair that matters most in this module.

1917
02:45:03,856 --> 02:45:11,620
资源是带有 URI 和声明的 MIME 类型的只读数据，是被刻意拉入上下文的，而不是被调用的。
A resource is read-only data with a URI and a declared MIME type pulled into context deliberately rather than called.

1918
02:45:12,366 --> 02:45:20,356
架构、配置文件、可用内容的目录；而工具执行逻辑并可能改变某些内容。
A schema, a configuration file, a catalog of what is available, a tool executes logic and may change something.

1919
02:45:21,262 --> 02:45:27,940
它有类型输入架构，由模型选择，且会消耗一个轮次和一次往返。
It has a typed input schema, is selected by the model and costs a turn and a round trip.

1920
02:45:29,102 --> 02:45:30,692
判定标准很简单。
The tiebreaker is short.

1921
02:45:31,246 --> 02:45:35,236
如果智能体在做出任何决定之前就需要知道相关信息，那它就是一项资源。
If the agent needs to know it before it can decide anything, that is a resource.

1922
02:45:35,726 --> 02:45:38,372
如果智能体需要去执行某项操作，那它就是一个工具。
If the agent needs to do it, that is a tool.

1923
02:45:39,406 --> 02:45:42,500
搞混这两者会导致双向的成本增加。
Getting this backwards is expensive in both directions.

1924
02:45:44,046 --> 02:45:49,476
资源仅在少数特定情况下适用，而第一种情况正是考试中常考的。
Resources earn their place in a few specific situations, and the first is the one the exam likes.

1925
02:45:50,158 --> 02:45:55,972
如果一个智能体为了弄清楚有哪些可用功能而进行多次工具调用，那它就是在进行昂贵的侦查。
An agent that makes several tool calls purely to discover what exists is doing expensive reconnaissance.

1926
02:45:56,256 --> 02:45:59,140
把目录放入资源中，它就会消失。
Put a catalog in a resource and that disappears.

1927
02:46:00,107 --> 02:46:02,052
模式和约定也属于这一类。
Shimas and conventions belong here too.

1928
02:46:02,990 --> 02:46:07,588
数据库结构、有效的状态值、命名规则。
The database structure, the valid status values, the naming rules.

1929
02:46:08,096 --> 02:46:14,148
任何稳定且被频繁引用的内容都属于此类，因为一次性获取比每次提问时都去抓取要高效。
So does anything stable that gets referenced repeatedly because fetching it once beats.

1930
02:46:14,547 --> 02:46:15,887
每问一次就抓取一次。
Fetching it per question.

1931
02:46:15,918 --> 02:46:27,172
不属于这一类的是庞大且多变的数据，因为挂载资源无论智能体最终是否需要它，都会消耗上下文。
What does not belong is large, volatile data, because attaching a resource spends context whether or not the agent turns out to need it.

1932
02:46:28,686 --> 02:46:32,260
提示词是人们常忽略的基础要素。
Prompts are the primitive people forget exists.

1933
02:46:32,656 --> 02:46:41,696
服务器发布带有参数的可重用模板，在 Claude 代码中，这些会体现为名为 MCP 的斜杠命令。
A server publishes reusable templates with parameters, and in clawed code, those surface as slash commands named MCP,

1934
02:46:41,856 --> 02:46:43,936
然后是服务器，接着是提示词。
then the server, then the prompt.

1935
02:46:44,462 --> 02:46:46,948
关键属性在第三行。
The important property is in the third line.

1936
02:46:47,536 --> 02:46:49,412
用户选择提示词。
The user chooses a prompt.

1937
02:46:50,382 --> 02:46:56,356
模型不会决定去调用它，这使得提示词与工具有本质区别。
The model does not decide to invoke one, which makes prompts fundamentally different from tools.

1938
02:46:57,006 --> 02:47:00,388
它们适用于标准化团队经常重复请求的内容。
They are good for standardizing a request a team makes constantly.

1939
02:47:00,656 --> 02:47:03,748
这样每个人都能获得正确的结构，而无需记住细节。
So everyone gets the right structure without remembering it.

1940
02:47:04,686 --> 02:47:11,844
当场景描述人们每天都要手动输入相同的繁琐请求时，这属于提示词类型而非工具类型。
When a scenario describes people typing the same awkward request by hand every day, that is prompt shaped rather than tool-shaped.

1941
02:47:13,198 --> 02:47:19,140
MCP 是双向的，这会让那些把它当成插件格式的人感到意外。
MCP is bidirectional, which surprises people who think of it as a plugin format.

1942
02:47:19,696 --> 02:47:23,492
客户端向服务器暴露三个基础要素。
The client exposes three primitives back to the server.

1943
02:47:24,206 --> 02:47:32,416
采样允许服务器请求宿主模型的补全，这样服务器就可以在没有自己的 API
Sampling lets a server ask the host's model for a completion so a server can use the model without having its own WI

1944
02:47:32,576 --> 02:47:33,216
key 的情况下使用模型。
key.

1945
02:47:33,710 --> 02:47:36,804
引导允许服务器向用户索要输入。
Elicitation lets a server ask the user for input.

1946
02:47:37,166 --> 02:47:42,404
它在操作过程中缺失，用户可以选择接受、拒绝或取消。
It is missing mid-operation and the user can accept, decline, or cancel.

1947
02:47:43,310 --> 02:47:47,972
规则允许客户端告诉服务器它被允许在哪些文件系统边界内工作。
Rules let the client tell the server which file system boundaries it is allowed to work within.

1948
02:47:48,622 --> 02:47:50,084
记住这三个名称。
Learn these three by name.

1949
02:47:50,976 --> 02:47:54,532
它们是简单的考点，且只出现在某些特定问题中。
They are cheap marks and they only appear as recoil questions.

1950
02:47:56,110 --> 02:47:58,084
三种传输方式和一个简单的规则。
Three transports and a simple rule.

1951
02:47:58,416 --> 02:48:02,532
标准输入输出是用于作为本地进程运行的服务。
Standard input and output is for a server running as a local process.

1952
02:48:02,736 --> 02:48:11,876
它是默认选项，可以在离线状态下工作且不涉及网络。可流式的 HTTP 用于远程服务器，是目前托管服务的标准方式。
It is the default, it works offline and no network is involved. Streamable HTTP is for remote servers and is the current standard for anything hosted.

1953
02:48:12,462 --> 02:48:19,396
ServerSent Events 是较旧的远程传输方式，仍受支持，但现有的服务器正在从中迁移。
ServerSent Events is the older remote transport, still supported, with existing servers migrating away from it.

1954
02:48:20,142 --> 02:48:22,404
提示框里的规则就是你需要的全部内容。
The rule in the callout is all you need.

1955
02:48:22,656 --> 02:48:25,604
本地进程意味着标准输入和输出。
A local process means standard input and output.

1956
02:48:26,158 --> 02:48:32,644
URL 意味着 HTTP。除非供应商明确告诉你它使用的是 ServerSent Events。
A URL means HTTP. Unless the vendor specifically tells you it uses server cent events.

1957
02:48:34,254 --> 02:48:38,500
有三个范围，考试会考查其中的区别。本地是默认选项。
Three scopes and the exam cares about the difference. Local is the default.

1958
02:48:38,688 --> 02:48:51,728
它存在于你的主配置中，以项目路径作为键。所以只有你在这个项目中可以使用，其他人不行。项目范围会在项目根目录写入一个 mcp.json 文件，然后你将其提交到版本控制中。
It lives in your home configuration keyed by project path. So it is you in this project and nobody else. Project scope writes a.mcp.json file at the project root, which you commit to version control.

1959
02:48:52,526 --> 02:48:58,372
任何克隆该仓库的人都会获得相同的服务器，并在第一次使用时收到授权提示。
Anyone who clones the repository gets the same servers with an approval prompt the first time.

1960
02:48:59,214 --> 02:49:05,668
用户范围也存在于你的主配置中，但它是全局生效的，因此它会跟随你进入每一个项目。
User scope also lives in your home configuration but applies globally, so it follows you into every project.

1961
02:49:06,542 --> 02:49:13,284
当场景要求整个团队自动获得该功能时，答案是项目范围和已提交的文件。
When a scenario says the whole team should get this automatically, the answer is project scope and a committed file.

1962
02:49:14,926 --> 02:49:19,168
一旦连接到服务器，你就会获得三个句柄，每个基础组件对应一个。
Once a server is connected, you get three handles, one per primitive.

1963
02:49:19,694 --> 02:49:26,436
工具会以类似 mcp 双下划线 服务端 双下划线 工具 的名称显示给模型。
Tools appear to the model with names like umcp double underscore server double underscore tool.

1964
02:49:26,928 --> 02:49:30,756
提示词会以相同的格式作为斜杆命令显示给用户。
Prompts appear to the user as slash commands in the same shape.

1965
02:49:31,598 --> 02:49:34,500
资源通过 @ 提及被引入到提示词中。
Resources are pulled into a prompt with an act mention.

1966
02:49:35,406 --> 02:49:38,276
最后一行解释了为什么命名规范不是琐碎的知识。
And the last line is why the naming convention is not trivia.

1967
02:49:38,688 --> 02:49:47,008
那个全限定工具名称是你写在钩子匹配器或权限规则中的内容。它能让你允许或阻止特定的 MCP 工具。
That fully qualified tool name is what you write in a hoop matcher or a permission rule. It lets you allow or block one specific MCP tool.

1968
02:49:47,328 --> 02:49:51,076
模块 6 的强制执行课程需要这种格式才能投入使用。
Module 6's enforcement lesson needs this shape to be usable.

1969
02:49:52,366 --> 02:49:54,528
会出现一些操作限制。
A few operational limits come up.

1970
02:49:54,990 --> 02:50:01,028
MCP 工具输出在达到 10,000 个 token 时会发出警告，默认上限是 25,000。
MCP tool output warns at around 10,000 tokens and is capped at 25,000 by default.

1971
02:50:01,454 --> 02:50:06,020
如果服务器确实返回更多内容，你可以提高这个限制，但在操作前先停下来思考一下。
You can raise that if a server legitimately returns more, but pause before you do.

1972
02:50:06,574 --> 02:50:11,300
启动和单次调用的超时时间也可以配置，支持全局或按服务器配置。
Startup and per call timeouts are configurable too, globally or per server.

1973
02:50:12,078 --> 02:50:14,564
最后一点是与考试相关的。
And the last point is the exam-relevant one.

1974
02:50:14,928 --> 02:50:21,188
一个每次调用都返回 40,000 个 token 的服务器是一个工具设计问题，而不是配置问题。
A server returning 40,000 tokens on every call is a tool design problem, not a configuration problem.

1975
02:50:21,648 --> 02:50:29,220
为了容纳臃肿的响应而提高上限是在处理警报而非火灾，模块 5 已经告诉你该怎么做。
Raising the cap to accommodate a bloated response is treating the alarm rather than the fire, and module 5 told you what to do instead.

1976
02:50:30,862 --> 02:50:32,036
一个设计决策。
1 design decision.

1977
02:50:32,368 --> 02:50:34,244
对于通用系统，选择采用。
For a common system, adopt.

1978
02:50:34,528 --> 02:50:45,636
你正在集成的功能几乎肯定已经有维护良好的服务器了。它已经处理好了身份验证、分页和错误处理，你可以直接继承这些修复。
There is almost certainly a maintained server for the thing you are integrating. It has already dealt with authentication, pagination, and error handling, and you inherit the fixes.

1979
02:50:48,590 --> 02:50:50,276
当它是你的专属系统时，才选择自行构建。
Build when it is your system.

1980
02:50:51,214 --> 02:50:56,100
内部服务，除了你之外没人有针对你组织的特定工作流。
Internal services, nobody else has workflow specific to your organization.

1981
02:50:56,558 --> 02:51:01,956
在模块 5 中描述的那种，需要对工具粒度进行控制的情况。
Cases where you need control over the tool granularity in the way module 5 described.

1982
02:51:02,478 --> 02:51:05,476
要明确，构建是长期的承诺。
Just be clear that building is a long-term commitment.

1983
02:51:06,446 --> 02:51:14,020
你是在承担维护服务器的责任，而考试有时会提供“自行构建”作为解决“采用现成方案”所带来的问题的重磅选项。
You are signing up to maintain a server and the exam sometimes offers building your own as a heavyweight answer to a problem adoption solves.

1984
02:51:15,726 --> 02:51:16,928
一个简短的信任提示。
A short trust note.

1985
02:51:17,550 --> 02:51:25,668
你安装的服务器可以暴露它喜欢的任何工具以及对应的描述，而这些描述会变成模型上下文中的指令。
A server you install can expose any tools it likes with any descriptions it likes, and those descriptions become instructions in your model's context.

1986
02:51:26,190 --> 02:51:31,140
这就是为什么项目范围内的服务器在团队成员第一次遇到它们时，会提示要求批准。
That is why project scope servers prompt for approval the first time a team member encounters them.

1987
02:51:32,078 --> 02:51:38,500
这也是为什么限制供应商服务器意味着使用钩子或权限规则，而不是修改服务器本身。
It is also why constraining a vendor server means a hook or a permission rule rather than a change to the server.

1988
02:51:38,848 --> 02:51:43,268
那是模块 6 的场景 4，值得记住。
That was module 6's scenario, 4, and it is worth carrying forward.

1989
02:51:44,174 --> 02:51:49,188
如果工具不是由你来修改的，那么强制执行就会上移一层，而不是放在提示词里。
If the tool is not yours to modify, the enforcement moves up a layer rather than into a prompt.

1990
02:51:50,688 --> 02:51:53,668
一个货币检查，这一项需要注意。
A currency check, and this one needs care.

1991
02:51:54,208 --> 02:51:57,796
三种服务器原语保持不变，可以放心学习。
The three server primitives are unchanged and safe to learn.

1992
02:51:58,222 --> 02:52:00,048
客户端方面还不那么确定。
The client side is less settled.

1993
02:52:03,214 --> 02:52:10,084
一个 2026 年的候选版本提议对路由、采样和日志进行弃用，并给出了很长的移除窗口。
A 2026 release candidate proposes deprecating routes, sampling and logging with a long removal window.

1994
02:52:10,528 --> 02:52:20,964
它还提议通过移除初始握手来使协议变得无状态。这是候选版本而非发布的行为，而且弃用窗口大约有一年。
It also proposes making the protocol stateless by removing the initialized handshake. That is a release candidate rather than ship behavior, and deprecation windows run about a year.

1995
02:52:21,408 --> 02:52:26,564
在考试中，关于采样、路由和引导，回答“有状态”。
On the exam, answer sampling, routes and elicitation, and answer stateful.

1996
02:52:27,310 --> 02:52:29,924
要了解发展的方向
Know the direction of travel

1997
02:52:30,798 --> 02:52:35,492
这样你在阅读规范时就不会感到困惑。
so the specification does not confuse you when you read it.

1998
02:52:37,006 --> 02:52:41,924
模式识别，而本模块的版本非常机械化。
Pattern recognition and this module's version is unusually mechanical.

1999
02:52:44,878 --> 02:52:49,860
仅仅为了找出什么可用而进行多次调用，意味着包含目录的资源。
Several calls just to find out what exists means. A resource holding a catalog.

2000
02:52:50,382 --> 02:52:55,908
整个团队都能自动获取到，意味着项目范围和已提交的配置文件。
The whole team should get this automatically, means project scope and a committed configuration file.

2001
02:52:56,782 --> 02:53:02,720
团队每天输入相同的请求，意味着作为斜杠命令出现的 MCP 提示词。
The team types the same request every day, means an MCP prompt surfaced as a slash command.

2002
02:53:02,990 --> 02:53:06,212
服务器在本地运行，意味着标准输入输出。
The server runs locally, means standard input and output.

2003
02:53:07,438 --> 02:53:12,644
我们无法修改供应商的服务器，意味着对全限定工具名称使用钩子或权限规则。
We cannot modify the vendor server, means a hook or a permission rule on the fully qualified tool name.

2004
02:53:13,520 --> 02:53:17,540
而一个需要模型总结某些内容的服务器，意味着采样。
And a server that needs the model to summarize something means sampling.

2005
02:53:18,094 --> 02:53:22,628
这些是变体场景的召回问题，所以词汇量就是整场考试的关键。
These are recall questions varying scenarios, so the vocabulary is the whole test.

2006
02:53:24,174 --> 02:53:26,244
五行内容来结束领域工具。
Five lines to close domain tool.

2007
02:53:26,800 --> 02:53:34,148
服务器分别提供模型驱动、应用驱动和用户驱动的工具、资源和提示词。
Servers expose tools, resources, and prompts which are model-driven, application-driven, and user-driven respectively.

2008
02:53:34,926 --> 02:53:41,124
客户端反向提供采样、路由和引导，因为协议是双向运行的。
Clients expose sampling, routes, and elicitation back because the protocol runs in both directions.

2009
02:53:41,680 --> 02:53:46,436
如果智能体需要知道某些信息，就是资源；如果它需要执行某些操作，就是工具。
Resource if the agent needs to know something, tool if it needs to do something.

2010
02:53:47,040 --> 02:53:55,556
本地范围是 U，项目范围是仓库，用户范围是你无处不在的身份，而项目范围是团队共享的已提交文件。
Local scope is U, Project Scope is the repository, user scope is you everywhere, and project scope is the committed file the team shares.

2011
02:53:56,240 --> 02:54:00,228
MCP 标准化了连接，但并不能修复设计糟糕的工具。
An MCP standardizes the connection without fixing a badly designed tool.

2012
02:54:01,134 --> 02:54:02,500
现在有五个场景。
Five scenarios now.

2013
02:54:03,022 --> 02:54:05,124
接下来是领域三和云端代码。
Then domain three and cloud code.

2014
02:54:06,670 --> 02:54:07,588
场景一。
Scenario 1.

2015
02:54:07,982 --> 02:54:11,812
一个分析智能体通过 MCP 服务器连接到数据库。
An analytics agent connects to a database through an MCP server.

2016
02:54:15,086 --> 02:54:18,404
为了回答任何问题，它首先调用“列出表”。
To answer any question, it first calls list tables.

2017
02:54:19,470 --> 02:54:23,200
然后它会调用两到三次“描述表”来找到正确的列。
Then it calls describe table two or three times to find the right columns.

2018
02:54:23,360 --> 02:54:24,772
最后再运行查询。
Then finally runs the query.

2019
02:54:25,550 --> 02:54:28,160
架构大约每年变动两次。
The schema changes roughly twice a year.

2020
02:54:28,686 --> 02:54:35,108
工程师报告说，简单的提问需要四到五个次工具调用，且成本高于预期。
Engineers report that simple questions take four or five tool calls and that costs are higher than expected.

2021
02:54:36,686 --> 02:54:38,372
最有效的改进是什么？
What is the most effective change?

2022
02:54:39,950 --> 02:54:45,540
A. 将“列出表”和“描述表”合并为一个能一次返回所有信息的工具。
a merge list tables and describe table into one tool that returns everything at once.

2023
02:54:46,702 --> 02:54:52,612
B. 将架构作为 MCP 资源暴露，以便在智能体规划查询前就包含在上下文中。
B. Expose the schema as an MCB resource so it is in context before the agent plans a query.

2024
02:54:53,040 --> 02:54:53,360
C。
C.

2025
02:54:53,774 --> 02:54:58,564
D. 在智能体的系统提示词中缓存架构，并每年手动更新两次。
Cache the schema in the agent system prompt and update it manually twice a year.

2026
02:54:59,182 --> 02:55:02,244
D. 将表列表添加到查询工具的描述中。
D. Add the table list to the query tool's description.

2027
02:55:03,440 --> 02:55:04,772
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2028
02:55:10,158 --> 02:55:11,680
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2029
02:55:11,920 --> 02:55:13,988
有两个细节结合在一起，揭示了答案。
Two details combined to give it away.

2030
02:55:14,382 --> 02:55:17,476
架构每年变动两次，所以它是稳定的。
The schema changes twice a year, so it is stable.

2031
02:55:17,742 --> 02:55:26,340
而且智能体在规划任何查询之前都需要它。所以它需要在前期提供。稳定且需要提前提供的特征就是“资源”。
And the agent needs it before it can plan any query. So it is required up front. Stable plus required upfront is the resource signature.

2032
02:55:26,830 --> 02:55:31,012
选项 A 是一个真正的改进，也是最强的干扰项。
Option A is a genuine improvement and the strongest distractor.

2033
02:55:31,566 --> 02:55:35,460
将三次调用合并为一次正是模块 5 教给你的做法。
Merging three calls into one is exactly what module 5 told you to do.

2034
02:55:35,854 --> 02:55:39,940
它仍在运行时去探索一些智能体本就可以直接获知的信息。
It is still discovering at runtime something the agent could simply have known.

2035
02:55:40,878 --> 02:55:50,852
选项 C 通过手动操作达到类似效果，但如果有人忘记更新就会在第一次就失败。服务端已经知道架构并可以将其发布。
Option C achieves a similar effect by hand and breaks the first time someone forgets to update it. The server already knows the schema and could publish it.

2036
02:55:51,280 --> 02:55:55,684
选项 D 误用了描述字段，因为描述是用来说明如何使用工具的。
Option B misuses the description, which is for how to use a tool.

2037
02:55:57,326 --> 02:55:58,436
场景二。
Scenario 2.

2038
02:55:58,800 --> 02:56:03,300
一个平台团队为他们的内部部署系统构建了一个 MCP 服务器。
A platform team has built an MCP server for their internal deployment system.

2039
02:56:03,840 --> 02:56:13,508
他们希望团队中的每个工程师在克隆仓库时都能自动配置好，而不需要每个人都运行安装命令。
They want every engineer on the team to have it configured automatically when they clone the repository without each person running a setup command.

2040
02:56:14,382 --> 02:56:20,400
一个独立的服务器，比如个人笔记工具，应该跟随工程师跨越他们所有的项目。
A separate server, a personal note-taking tool, should follow one engineer across all their projects.

2041
02:56:20,640 --> 02:56:22,480
应该使用哪种范围？
Which scope should be used?

2042
02:56:22,830 --> 02:56:26,180
a. 两者都设为用户范围，这样它们始终可用。
a Both at user scope so they are always available.

2043
02:56:26,702 --> 02:56:31,364
b. 部署服务器设为项目范围，笔记工具设为用户范围。
b Deployment server at project scope and note taking server at user scope.

2044
02:56:32,080 --> 02:56:37,508
c. 部署服务器设为本地范围，笔记工具设为项目范围。
C Deployment server at local scope and note taking server at project scope.

2045
02:56:38,000 --> 02:56:38,320
d.
D.

2046
02:56:38,798 --> 02:56:40,100
两者都设为项目范围。
Both at project scope.

2047
02:56:40,334 --> 02:56:42,564
这样配置就能纳入版本控制了。
So the configuration is version controlled.

2048
02:56:43,150 --> 02:56:44,260
停下来思考一下并做决定。
Pause and decide.

2049
02:56:49,870 --> 02:56:55,620
答案是 B，这是一个套在特定场景下的定义性问题。
The answer is B, and this is a definitional question with a scenario wrapped around it.

2050
02:56:56,334 --> 02:57:06,320
两个需求分别对应两个维度。所有克隆此仓库的人都属于项目维度。所以应该是项目范围和提交到代码库的配置文件。
Two requirements sit on two different axes. Everyone who clones this repository is the project axis. So project scope and a committed configuration file.

2051
02:57:06,830 --> 02:57:12,260
这一个人的所有项目属于用户维度，所以是用户范围。
This one person across all their projects is the user axis, so user scope.

2052
02:57:12,686 --> 02:57:19,652
选项 A 不符合第一个要求，因为用户范围是针对个人的，每个工程师仍需手动添加。
Option A fails the first requirement because user scope is per person and every engineer would still have to add it.

2053
02:57:20,238 --> 02:57:23,428
选项 C 在两个方面都完全反了。
Option C is exactly backwards on both counts.

2054
02:57:24,270 --> 02:57:31,812
选项 D 有点微妙，因为版本控制配置听起来是良好的实践，而且它适用于部署服务器。
Option D is the interesting one because version control configuration sounds like good practice and it is for the deployment server.

2055
02:57:33,774 --> 02:57:38,756
但如果应用到个人笔记工具上，就会把某人的偏好强加给整个团队。
Applied to a personal note-taking tool, it pushes somebody's preferences onto the whole team.

2056
02:57:40,270 --> 02:57:41,284
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

2057
02:57:41,710 --> 02:57:47,396
一个事件响应团队在他们的可观测性平台中使用 Claude Code 和一个 MCP 服务器。
An incident response team uses clod code with an MCP server for their observability platform.

2058
02:57:47,760 --> 02:57:51,012
每次发生故障时，工程师都要输入一段很长的请求。
Every incident, an engineer types out a long request.

2059
02:57:51,822 --> 02:58:01,348
“提取指定服务的最后一堆错误，按类型分组，与最近的部署关联，并将结果格式化为事件摘要。”
Pull the last tower of errors for a named service, group them by type, correlate with recent deploys, and format the result as an incident summary.

2060
02:58:01,934 --> 02:58:06,212
不同工程师使用的措辞各不相同，输出格式也不统一。
The wording varies between engineers and the output format is inconsistent.

2061
02:58:06,958 --> 02:58:09,348
最合适的解决方案是什么？
What is the most appropriate solution?

2062
02:58:09,838 --> 02:58:14,084
a. 在服务端添加一个执行整个序列的工具。
a Add a tool to the server that performs the whole sequence.

2063
02:58:14,542 --> 02:58:20,900
b. 发布一个包含服务名称的 MCP 提示词，让它显示为斜杠命令。
b publish an MCP prompt taking the service name so it appears as a slash command.

2064
02:58:21,838 --> 02:58:22,080
c.
C.

2065
02:58:22,638 --> 02:58:27,300
在 clot.md 中添加标准措辞，让每个人都使用相同的表述。
Add the standard wording to clot.md so everyone uses the same phrasing.

2066
02:58:27,840 --> 02:58:28,080
d.
D.

2067
02:58:28,480 --> 02:58:31,460
将事件摘要格式作为资源暴露出来。
Expose the incident summary format as a resource.

2068
02:58:33,806 --> 02:58:34,884
停下来思考一下并做决定。
Pause and decide.

2069
02:58:40,590 --> 02:58:41,732
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2070
02:58:41,998 --> 02:58:47,012
强调中的规则是需要记住的，因为它清晰地划分了这两个基本要素。
The rule in the call out is the one to take away because it separates the two primitives cleanly.

2071
02:58:47,598 --> 02:58:50,180
人类重复某事时需要提示词。
A human repeating something wants a prompt.

2072
02:58:50,480 --> 02:58:52,932
模型重复某事时需要工具。
A model repeating something wants a tool.

2073
02:58:53,422 --> 02:58:57,124
这里是人在重复，所以它属于提示词类型。
Here the repetition is human, so it is prompt shaped.

2074
02:58:57,998 --> 02:59:01,476
选项 A 是最强的干扰项，而且它确实可行。
Option A is the strongest distractor and it does work.

2075
02:59:02,926 --> 02:59:11,204
但它硬编码了一个调查序列，而工程师通常会根据情况调整这个序列，且它去除了智能体关于接下来该看什么的判断。
It also hard codes an investigation sequence that engineers legitimately vary and removes the agent's judgment about what to look at next.

2076
02:59:11,920 --> 02:59:20,400
选项 C 是上下文而非指令。所以工程师仍需记住具体的措辞，而这正是他们容易出错的地方。
Option C is context rather than a command. So engineers still have to remember the phrasing which is the thing they are getting wrong.

2077
02:59:21,200 --> 02:59:26,564
选项 D 解决了格式一致性的问题，并保留了所有的输入内容。
Option D addresses format consistency and leaves all the typing in place.

2078
02:59:28,206 --> 02:59:29,220
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

2079
02:59:29,520 --> 02:59:34,500
一个团队想要将他们的智能体与一个广泛使用的问题追踪器集成。
A team wants to integrate their agent with a widely used issue tracker.

2080
02:59:34,990 --> 02:59:43,012
厂商已经发布了一个维护良好的 MCP 服务器，并处理好了身份验证和分页。
There is a maintained MCP server for it published by the vendor with authentication and pagination already handled.

2081
02:59:43,950 --> 02:59:52,196
一名工程师提议改用自建服务器，理由是他们只需要四个操作，而厂商的服务器提供了 30 个工具。
An engineer proposes building an in-house server instead, arguing that they only need four operations while the vendor server exposes 30 tools.

2082
02:59:52,814 --> 02:59:55,680
该团队没有能力进行持续维护。
The team has no capacity for ongoing maintenance.

2083
02:59:56,110 --> 02:59:57,348
你应该给出什么建议？
What should you advise?

2084
02:59:58,030 --> 03:00:04,004
a. 构建自建服务器，因为四个专注的工具比 30 个重叠的工具表现更好。
a Build the in-house server since four focus tools will outperform 30 overlapping ones.

2085
03:00:04,560 --> 03:00:04,800
b。
b.

2086
03:00:05,486 --> 03:00:09,892
采用厂商提供的服务器，并限制智能体可以使用的工具。
Adopt the vendor server and restrict which of its tools the agent may use.

2087
03:00:10,400 --> 03:00:10,640
C。
C.

2088
03:00:11,214 --> 03:00:15,876
c. 原样采用厂商的服务器，因为更多的工具能给智能体提供更多选择。
Adopt the vendor server as is since more tools give the agent more options.

2089
03:00:16,782 --> 03:00:21,284
d. 构建自建服务器并贡献给厂商。
d Build the in-house server and contribute it back to the vendor.

2090
03:00:22,382 --> 03:00:23,652
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2091
03:00:29,294 --> 03:00:35,108
答案是 B，这个场景考察的是区分正确的诊断和错误的对策。
The answer is B, and this scenario rewards separating a correct diagnosis from a wrong prescription.

2092
03:00:35,744 --> 03:00:41,828
工程师的观点是对的，30 个工具确实是个问题，原因正如模块 5 所述。
The engineer is right that 30 tools is a problem for exactly the reasons module 5 gave.

2093
03:00:42,144 --> 03:00:47,492
每一个定义都会消耗资源，随着邻近选项增多，每一次请求和选择的质量都会下降。
Every definition taxes, every request and selection degrades as neighbors multiply.

2094
03:00:48,430 --> 03:00:50,628
他们错误的地方在于解决办法。
Where they go wrong is the fix.

2095
03:00:51,534 --> 03:00:54,820
你不需要拥有一个服务器就能获得精简的工具集。
You do not need to own a server to get a narrow tool set.

2096
03:00:55,470 --> 03:01:03,904
限制智能体可用的工具，可以在保留厂商提供的身份验证、分页等功能的同时，
Restricting which tools the agent may use gives you the same four tool surface while keeping the vendor's authentication, pagination,

2097
03:01:04,064 --> 03:01:05,252
以及未来的修复更新的同时，提供同样的四个工具界面。
and future fixes.

2098
03:01:05,998 --> 03:01:13,636
决定性的句子是“团队没有能力进行持续维护”，这排除了两个构建选项。
The deciding sentence is that the team has no capacity for ongoing maintenance, which rules out both build options.

2099
03:01:16,974 --> 03:01:17,424
选项
Option

2100
03:01:18,414 --> 03:01:22,596
C 忽略了工程师正确识别出的一个真实问题。
C Ignores a real problem the engineer correctly identified.

2101
03:01:23,758 --> 03:01:25,028
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

2102
03:01:25,504 --> 03:01:32,036
一个文档处理 MCP 服务器需要在其工具之一中对长文档进行摘要。
A document processing MCP server needs to summarize long documents as part of one of its tools.

2103
03:01:32,624 --> 03:01:36,260
团队正在决定服务器应如何获取这些摘要。
The team is deciding how the server should obtain those summaries.

2104
03:01:36,864 --> 03:01:42,180
他们不希望持有独立的 API 密钥，也不想管理自己的速率限制。
They would prefer not to hold a separate API key and not to manage their own rate limits.

2105
03:01:43,024 --> 03:01:47,780
他们也不希望客户去配置使用哪种摘要模型。
They also do not want customers configuring which summarization model to use.

2106
03:01:48,144 --> 03:01:50,704
哪种 MCP 能力符合要求？
Which MCP capability fits.

2107
03:01:50,944 --> 03:01:59,812
A. 引导（引导），要求用户提供摘要。B. 采样（Sampling），通过客户端请求宿主模型生成内容。
a elicitation asking the user to supply a summary. B. Sampling requesting a completion from the host model through the client.

2108
03:02:00,144 --> 03:02:04,196
C. 根目录（Roots），授予服务器访问模块上下文的权限。
C. Roots granting the server access to the module's context.

2109
03:02:05,024 --> 03:02:05,344
D。
D.

2110
03:02:05,744 --> 03:02:10,180
一个包含文档的资源，让智能体自行进行摘要。
A resource containing the document so the agent summarizes it itself.

2111
03:02:11,182 --> 03:02:12,420
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

2112
03:02:18,190 --> 03:02:19,664
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2113
03:02:20,064 --> 03:02:24,740
第二段中的三个约束几乎准确地描述了采样。
The three constraints in the second paragraph describe sampling almost exactly.

2114
03:02:25,344 --> 03:02:32,228
无需独立 API 密钥，无需管理自己的速率限制，且不要求客户配置模型。
No separate API key, no rate limits of their own, and no model configuration pushed on to customers.

2115
03:02:32,718 --> 03:02:37,508
采样之所以存在，就是为了让服务器能够借用宿主模型，而不是自带模型。
Sampling exists so a server can borrow the host model rather than bringing its own.

2116
03:02:38,414 --> 03:02:43,172
选项 A 混淆了两个涉及“索取内容”的客户端原语。
Option A confuses the two client primitives that involve asking for something.

2117
03:02:43,694 --> 03:02:48,068
引导是向用户提问，而没有用户想被要求去写摘要。
Elicitation asks the user and no user wants to be asked to write the summary.

2118
03:02:49,422 --> 03:02:53,284
选项 C 虚构了一个定义，而根目录具有文件系统的边界。
Option C invents a definition and roots have file system boundaries.

2119
03:02:54,190 --> 03:02:56,388
从某种意义上说，选项 D 是可行的。
Option D would work in a sense.

2120
03:02:56,864 --> 03:03:04,100
但它会将摘要操作移入主对话中，而这恰恰是该服务器结构旨在避免的上下文成本。
It also moves summarization into the main conversation, which is exactly the context cost the server was structured to avoid.

2121
03:03:04,622 --> 03:03:05,604
到此结束。
That closes.

2122
03:03:05,984 --> 03:03:10,596
接下来是领域 2、领域 3 以及 Claude Code 配置。
Domain 2, domain 3 next, and Claude Code Configuration.

2123
03:03:12,334 --> 03:03:16,624
欢迎来到领域 3，Claude Code 配置与工作流。
Welcome to domain 3, Claude Cody Configuration and Workflows.

2124
03:03:16,864 --> 03:03:21,924
占考试的 20%，大约有 12 道题，由 4 个模块涵盖。
20% of the exam, roughly 12 questions, and 4 modules to cover it.

2125
03:03:22,702 --> 03:03:24,804
第一个模块是关于配置的。
This first one is about configuration.

2126
03:03:25,582 --> 03:03:34,020
涉及记忆文件存放的位置、它们的组合方式、设置层级的分布，以及如何确定实际加载的内容。
Where memory files live, how they combine, where the settings hierarchy sits, and how to work out what actually loaded.

2127
03:03:35,950 --> 03:03:45,060
这个模块中有一个非常令人意外的事实，很多公开资料都搞错了。所以当我们讲到拼接幻灯片时请注意。
There is one genuinely surprising fact in this module that a lot of published material gets wrong. So pay attention when we reach the concatenation slide.

2128
03:03:46,350 --> 03:03:51,024
从分工开始，因为它决定了本模块中比任何其他内容更多的题目。
Start with the division of labour, because it decides more questions than anything else in this module.

2129
03:03:51,264 --> 03:03:58,244
设置文件控制 Claude 被允许做什么、可以调用哪些工具、可以触碰哪些路径以及触发哪些钩子。
Settings files control what Claude is permitted to do, which tools it may call, which paths it may touch, which hooks fire.

2130
03:03:58,990 --> 03:04:01,284
记忆文件决定 Claude 知道什么。
Memory files control what Claude knows.

2131
03:04:02,158 --> 03:04:07,332
你的约定、你的架构，以及更改特定目录的原因。
Your conventions, your architecture, the reason a particular directory is changed.

2132
03:04:08,238 --> 03:04:13,028
两种不同的任务，两种不同的机制，以及两种截然不同的保证。
Two different jobs, two different mechanisms, and two very different guarantees.

2133
03:04:13,742 --> 03:04:21,828
第6模块已经告诉过你哪一个是强制执行，哪一个是说服；本模块将告诉你每一项分别存放在哪里。
Module 6 already told you which of those is enforcement and which is persuasion. This module tells you where each one lives.

2134
03:04:41,390 --> 03:04:48,196
目录记忆，即 clod.md，位于子目录中，并在该目录下工作时加载。
Directory memory, a clod.md, sitting inside a subdirectory which loads when work happens there.

2135
03:04:49,070 --> 03:04:59,984
以及在 clot.local.md 中的个人项目记忆，它被 gitignore 了，所以属于你个人。Claude 会向上遍历目录树读取这些文件，这样单仓项目就可以为每个组件携带一个。
And personal project memory in clot.local.md, which is gitignored so it stays yours. Clot reads these up the directory tree so a monorepo can carry one per component.

2136
03:05:00,590 --> 03:05:05,476
保持父级文件精简，因为你上方的所有内容都会在每个会话中加载。
Keep the parent files light because everything above you loads every session.

2137
03:05:06,926 --> 03:05:09,200
到这一页时请放慢速度。
Here is the slide to slow down for.

2138
03:05:09,600 --> 03:05:12,548
记忆文件被拼接进上下文。
Memory files are concatenated into context.

2139
03:05:12,846 --> 03:05:14,372
它们不属于优先级链。
They are not a precedence chain.

2140
03:05:14,798 --> 03:05:21,924
大量的公开资料告诉你，更具体的规则胜出，或者项目层级的覆盖用户层级。
A great deal of published material tells you that more specific wins or that project level overrides user level.

2141
03:05:22,958 --> 03:05:25,348
官方文档并没有这么说。
The official documentation does not say that.

2142
03:05:25,966 --> 03:05:33,600
在同一层级时，Claude.local.md 会被追加在 Claude.md 之后，这是加载顺序而非优先级。
Claude.local.md is appended after Claude.md at the same level, that is load order rather than precedence.

2143
03:05:33,902 --> 03:05:36,932
最后读取到某项内容并不意味着它能在冲突中胜出。
Reading something last does not make it win a contradiction.

2144
03:05:37,200 --> 03:05:41,380
因此，当两个记忆文件不一致时，结果是不可预测的。
So when two memory files disagree, the outcome is not guaranteed.

2145
03:05:42,160 --> 03:05:44,932
工程上的解决方案是消除矛盾。
The engineering answer is to remove the contradiction.

2146
03:05:45,200 --> 03:05:49,636
如果你需要一个确定的胜出者，那么这条规则根本就不该出现在记忆文件中。
If you need a guaranteed winner, that rule does not belong in a memory file at all.

2147
03:05:51,150 --> 03:05:54,320
把两者并排对比，设计逻辑就清晰了。
Put the two side by side and the design becomes obvious.

2148
03:05:54,560 --> 03:06:05,956
记忆文件是拼接的上下文，没有官方定义的冲突解决机制。因此矛盾会导致不可预测的结果，解决方法就是停止自相矛盾。
Memory files are concatenated context with no documented conflict resolution. So contradictions resolve unpredictably, and the fix is to stop contradicting yourself.

2149
03:06:06,510 --> 03:06:08,996
设置文件是一个严格的优先级链。
Settings files are a strict precedence chain.

2150
03:06:09,200 --> 03:06:15,556
五个层级从低到高合并，托管策略始终胜出，且每一层内部都有明确的规则。
Five layers merge from low to high with managed policy always winning and a defined rule inside each layer.

2151
03:06:16,270 --> 03:06:19,012
这就是为什么强制执行存在于设置中的原因。
That is exactly why enforcement lives in settings.

2152
03:06:19,982 --> 03:06:25,508
它是两种机制中唯一一个在“谁胜出”这个问题上有明确答案的机制。
It is the only one of the two mechanisms with a defined answer to the question which one wins.

2153
03:06:26,190 --> 03:06:32,004
第6模块关于说服和强制执行的所有内容，都有这个底层逻辑作为支撑。
Everything module 6 said about persuasion and enforcement has this as its underlying reason.

2154
03:06:33,294 --> 03:06:34,560
那么，什么该放进其中一个呢？
So what goes in one?

2155
03:06:34,880 --> 03:06:43,840
约定和标准，意味着命名、结构、测试方法、提交信息格式、架构，以及具体到
Conventions and standards, meaning naming, structure, the testing approach, the commit message format, architecture, and specifically

2156
03:06:44,000 --> 03:06:50,020
背后的原因。因为知道为什么某个目录很特殊，比仅仅知道它很特殊更有价值。
the reasons behind it. Because knowing why a directory is strange is worth more than knowing that it is.

2157
03:06:50,862 --> 03:06:56,836
那些不通过观察就能发现的命令，比如如何运行测试或启动开发服务端。
Commands that are not obvious from looking around, like how to run the tests or start the development server.

2158
03:06:57,230 --> 03:07:04,388
判断整个文件好坏的一个标准是：问问一个能力出众的新同事在还没读任何资料的第一天需要什么。
A good filter for the whole file is to ask what a competent new colleague would need on day one before they had read anything.

2159
03:07:05,198 --> 03:07:06,564
另外有两样东西要排除在外。
And two things stay out.

2160
03:07:07,086 --> 03:07:08,676
显然，是密钥。
Secrets, obviously.

2161
03:07:09,582 --> 03:07:13,252
还有硬性规则，因为记忆文件无法强制执行这些规则。
And hard rules, because a memory file cannot enforce one.

2162
03:07:14,830 --> 03:07:18,180
记忆文件可以通过添加路径引用来导入其他文件。
Memory files can import others with an add path reference.

2163
03:07:18,606 --> 03:07:25,924
相对路径是根据执行导入的文件来解析的，而不是你的工作目录，这在嵌套设置中常让人困惑。
Relative paths resolve from the file doing the importing, not from your working directly, which trips people up in nested setups.

2164
03:07:26,254 --> 03:07:28,228
关键的成本在于第二行。
The important cost is the second line.

2165
03:07:29,038 --> 03:07:35,396
所有被导入的内容都会在每个会话中加载到上下文中，所以导入并不是懒加载引用。
Everything imported loads into context every session, so an import is not a lazy reference.

2166
03:07:37,360 --> 03:07:44,900
在工作目录之外解析的导入会在第一次时触发审批开关，这是一个合理的安全措施。
Imports that resolve outside your working directory trigger an approval dial-off the first time, which is a sensible safety measure.

2167
03:07:45,902 --> 03:07:47,492
还有一个加号符号
And an add symbol

2168
03:07:48,686 --> 03:07:54,276
在代码块或代码片段中的加号不会被视为导入，所以示例是安全的。
inside a code block or code span is not treated as an import, so examples are safe.

2169
03:07:55,438 --> 03:07:56,900
仔细读一下这个调用。
Read the call out carefully.

2170
03:07:58,574 --> 03:08:03,044
将大文件拆分为多个导入只是重新组织了加载内容，并没有减少内容量。
Splitting a big file into imports reorganizes what loads without reducing it.

2171
03:08:04,494 --> 03:08:09,060
路径范围规则才是真正减少上下文的机制。
Path-scoped rules are the mechanism that genuinely reduces context.

2172
03:08:09,680 --> 03:08:20,964
位于 .claude 规则目录下的文件会在其前置元数据中声明它们适用的路径。只有当工作涉及这些路径时才会加载，而不是在每个会话中都加载。
Files under the.claude rules directory declare in their front matter which paths they apply to. They load when work touches those paths rather than on every session.

2173
03:08:21,646 --> 03:08:24,260
与之相对的是导入，它们总是会被加载。
Contrast that with imports which always load.

2174
03:08:25,166 --> 03:08:31,396
这是针对单仓项目的答案，在这种情况下，前端惯例在后端工作中只是干扰项。
This is the answer for a monorepo where front-end conventions are noise during back-end work.

2175
03:08:32,160 --> 03:08:38,852
它也适用于任何一个巨大的记忆文件对于当前任务基本无关的项目。
It also suits any project where one enormous memory file is mostly irrelevant to today's task.

2176
03:08:40,800 --> 03:08:47,588
当场景中抱怨记忆文件变得难以管理时，通常需要的正是路径范围。
When a scenario complains that the memory file has grown unmanageable, path scoping is usually what it wants.

2177
03:08:49,358 --> 03:08:52,996
clot.local.md 用于每个项目的私有偏好设置。
Clot.local.md is for private per project preferences.

2178
03:08:53,582 --> 03:08:58,852
你的沙箱、URL、测试数据、端口以及你的开发服务器运行的端口。
Your sandbox, URL, your test data, the port, your development server runs on.

2179
03:08:59,246 --> 03:09:03,940
它是 gitignore，这就是重点所在，因为除了你之外没人需要知道你的本地端口。
It is gitignode, which is the entire point because nobody else needs your local ports.

2180
03:09:04,430 --> 03:09:05,988
陷阱在第三行。
The trap is in the third line.

2181
03:09:06,638 --> 03:09:11,332
gitignode 文件仅存在于你创建它的工作树中。
A gitignode file exists only in the work tree where you created it.

2182
03:09:11,982 --> 03:09:17,604
如果你在同一个仓库的多个工作树之间切换，你就需要维护多个同步的副本。
Work across several work trees of the same repository and you have several copies to keep in step.

2183
03:09:17,920 --> 03:09:24,612
解决方法是将内容保存在你的主目录中并进行导入。这样一个文件就能服务于所有的检出。
The fix is to keep the content in your home directory and import it. So one file serves every checkout.

2184
03:09:25,550 --> 03:09:30,244
当有人说在一种检出下可行而在另一种下不行时，通常就是这个原因。
When someone says it works in one checkout and not the other, this is usually why.

2185
03:09:32,014 --> 03:09:34,404
现在来看具有明确行为的链条。
Now the chain that does have defined behavior.

2186
03:09:34,926 --> 03:09:35,972
有五个层级。
Five layers.

2187
03:09:37,102 --> 03:09:40,996
最底层是你的用户设置，即个人默认设置。
At the bottom, your user settings, which are personal defaults.

2188
03:09:41,582 --> 03:09:47,040
在那之上是提交到仓库的项目设置，它们会覆盖你的默认设置。
Above that, project settings committed to the repository, which override your defaults.

2189
03:09:47,662 --> 03:09:53,028
再往上是项目本地设置，即针对你机器特定环境对共享项目文件的覆盖。
Above that, project local settings, which are your machine specific overrides of the shared project file.

2190
03:09:54,702 --> 03:09:57,700
最上方是单次调用的命令行标志。
Above that, command line flags for a single invocation.

2191
03:09:59,054 --> 03:10:03,492
而在最顶层是企业托管策略，下方的任何设置都无法放宽它。
And at the top, enterprise managed policy, which nothing below can relax.

2192
03:10:05,262 --> 03:10:07,428
最后一个就是安全方面的答案。
That last one is the security answer.

2193
03:10:08,334 --> 03:10:16,740
如果你的组织在托管层拒绝了某项功能，任何用户、项目或本地设置都无法允许它，这是有意为之的。
If your organization denies something at the managed layer, no user, project, or local setting can permit it, and that is deliberate.

2194
03:10:18,382 --> 03:10:21,392
在任何单一层级中，都有第二条规则。
Inside any single layer, there is a second rule.

2195
03:10:21,646 --> 03:10:25,252
权限分为三种模式：允许、拒绝和请求。
Permissions come in three modes allow, deny and ask.

2196
03:10:25,614 --> 03:10:27,620
而最严格的匹配规则将获胜。
And the strictest matching rule wins.

2197
03:10:30,478 --> 03:10:33,636
拒绝优于请求，请求优于允许。
Deny beats ask and ask beats allow.

2198
03:10:35,246 --> 03:10:39,632
所以，在同一个文件中添加一个允许规则，无法挽救你在该文件中已经拒绝的内容。
So adding an allow rule cannot rescue something you denied in the same file.

2199
03:10:40,174 --> 03:10:45,732
要在你自己的机器上覆盖项目层级的拒绝，必须在你的项目本地设置中加入允许。
To override a project level deny on your own machine, the allow goes into your project local settings.

2200
03:10:46,382 --> 03:10:48,324
那完全属于更高的层级。
That is a higher layer entirely.

2201
03:10:49,806 --> 03:10:53,060
这里结合了两条规则，考试也会同时考查这两点。
Two rules combine here and the exam tests both.

2202
03:10:53,934 --> 03:10:58,596
层级向下覆盖，而在同一个层级内，最严格的匹配规则获胜。
Layers override downwards, and inside a layer, the strictest match wins.

2203
03:11:00,302 --> 03:11:05,604
在实践中，大多数团队设置的最高价值权限是关于读取环境文件的自定义设置。
In practice, the highest value permission most teams set is a DIY on reading environment files.

2204
03:11:06,030 --> 03:11:10,884
它能确保敏感信息不会进入模型的上下文，而且在审计时你可以明确指出这一点。
It keeps secrets out of the model's context in a way you can point at during an audit.

2205
03:11:11,406 --> 03:11:16,196
「拒绝」意味着功能的移除，所以没有提示词、没有推理、也没有例外。
Denny is a capability removal, so there is no prompt and no reasoning and no exception.

2206
03:11:17,070 --> 03:11:23,524
「请求」是针对那些有时正确的操作，即引入人工参与，而不是直接拦截。
Ask is for actions that are sometimes right, putting a human in the loop rather than blocking outright.

2207
03:11:23,918 --> 03:11:27,300
还要记住模块 6 第四个场景中的限制条件。
And remember the limitation from module 6's fourth scenario.

2208
03:11:27,918 --> 03:11:29,380
权限要么开启，要么关闭。
Permissions are on or off.

2209
03:11:29,870 --> 03:11:34,852
如果你的规则取决于时间或文件的内容，你就需要一个钩子。
If your rule is conditioned on the time of day or the contents of a file, you need a hook.

2210
03:11:36,334 --> 03:11:40,100
这是一个常出现在调试场景中的操作细节。
One operational detail that shows up as a debugging scenario.

2211
03:11:40,846 --> 03:11:46,948
大多数设置会自动重新加载，因此权限更改或新的钩子在你保存文件后就会立即生效。
Most settings reload automatically, so a permissions change or a new hook applies as soon as you save the file.

2212
03:11:47,886 --> 03:11:54,884
少数设置仅在启动时读取一次，包括模型和输出风格。所以修改这些内容直到下一个会话才会生效。
A few are read once at startup, including the model and the output style. So changing those does nothing until the next session.

2213
03:11:57,422 --> 03:12:03,972
当有人说他们改了但没反应时，通常就是这两者之一。重启就能解决问题。
When somebody says I changed it and nothing happened, it is usually one of those two. And the restart resolves it.

2214
03:12:04,814 --> 03:12:08,836
而 ClaudeDoctor 会告诉你你的设置文件是否被读取。
And ClaudeDoctor tells you whether your settings file is being read at all.

2215
03:12:09,152 --> 03:12:12,420
这能区分是设置错误还是根本就没有加载。
That distinguishes a wrong setting from one that never loaded.

2216
03:12:13,870 --> 03:12:17,792
有四种查看当前情况的方法，它们分别回答不同的问题。
Four ways to see what is going on, and they answer different questions.

2217
03:12:18,222 --> 03:12:25,572
Slash 上下文 会报告哪些记忆文件实际加载到了这个会话中，当你需要确认某个文件是否生效时，用这个命令。
Slash context reports which memory files actually loaded into this session, which is the one to use when you are verifying that a file is live.

2218
03:12:25,872 --> 03:12:29,892
Slash memory 列出你的记忆文件位置并打开它们供编辑。
Slash memory lists your memory file locations and opens them for editing.

2219
03:12:30,638 --> 03:12:37,252
Slash status 显示版本、会话 ID、模型以及哪些设置源处于激活状态。
Slash status shows the version, the session ID, the model, and which settings sources are active.

2220
03:12:37,472 --> 03:12:41,348
而 ClaudeDoctor 则检查你的配置是否被读取。
And Clot Doctor checks whether your configuration is being read at all.

2221
03:12:41,872 --> 03:12:43,204
注意这个提示。
Note the callout.

2222
03:12:44,174 --> 03:12:45,828
这两个命令都不加载任何内容。
Neither command loads anything.

2223
03:12:46,670 --> 03:12:52,868
配置会根据所在位置自动加载，而这些命令仅用于报告当前状态。
Configuration loads automatically based on where it sits, and these commands only report on it.

2224
03:12:54,158 --> 03:12:57,732
这是开头提到的货币项标志，现在加上详细说明。
The currency item flag back in the introduction, now with the detail.

2225
03:12:58,254 --> 03:13:03,428
在编写考试指南时，slash memory 是显示已加载哪些记忆文件的命令。
When the exam guide was written, slash memory was the command that showed you which memory files were loaded.

2226
03:13:04,366 --> 03:13:06,468
当前的 Claude 代码将这项任务拆分了。
Current clawed code splits that job.

2227
03:13:32,352 --> 03:13:36,996
以及与 cross 工具 agents.md 规范的互操作性。
And interoperability with the cross tool agents.md convention.

2228
03:13:37,422 --> 03:13:39,044
这两个都不在考核范围内。
Neither is examinable.

2229
03:13:40,686 --> 03:13:41,892
模式识别。
Pattern recognition.

2230
03:13:42,352 --> 03:13:48,676
“无论 Claude 如何决定都必须生效”意味着设置或钩子，绝不是记忆文件。
Must hold regardless of what Claude decides means settings or a hook, never a memory file.

2231
03:13:49,230 --> 03:13:50,980
整个团队都应该掌握这一点。
The whole team should get this.

2232
03:13:51,392 --> 03:13:56,612
这意味着项目级文件、记忆或设置，取决于它是属于知识还是权限。
Means a project level file, memory, or settings, depending on whether it is knowledge or permission.

2233
03:13:57,550 --> 03:14:01,028
“仅限我的机器且未提交”意味着其中一个本地文件。
Just my machine and not committed means one of the local files.

2234
03:14:01,294 --> 03:14:05,312
“记忆文件变得难以管理”意味着部分范围的规则。
The memory file has become unmanageable, means part scoped rules.

2235
03:14:05,806 --> 03:14:12,228
“两个文件内容不一致”意味着拼接，没有确定的胜者。应将规则移动到具有明确行为的地方。
Two files say different things, means concatenation, no guaranteed winner. Move the rule somewhere with defined behavior.

2236
03:14:12,814 --> 03:14:18,884
“IT 策略不得被覆盖”意味着企业管理层。
And IT policy must not be overridable, means the enterprise managed layer.

2237
03:14:19,470 --> 03:14:22,724
几乎每一行最终都指向一个问题。
Almost every row comes down to one question.

2238
03:14:24,302 --> 03:14:27,044
“这是否需要被知晓或强制执行？”
Does this need to be known or enforced?

2239
03:14:28,686 --> 03:14:29,632
5 行。
5 lines.

2240
03:14:30,382 --> 03:14:39,876
设置是 Claude 能做什么，而记忆文件是 Claude 应该知道什么。记忆文件是拼接而非排序，所以冲突时没有确定的胜者。
Settings are what clot can do and memory files are what clot should know. Memory files are concatenated rather than ranked, so contradictions have no guaranteed winner.

2241
03:14:40,974 --> 03:14:47,556
设置有五个层级，管理策略始终在最顶层；而在任何层级内部，拒绝优于询问，询问优于允许。
Settings have five layers with managed policy always on top, and inside any layer deny, beats ask beats allow.

2242
03:14:48,462 --> 03:14:58,148
导入总是加载，而路径范围的规则才是真正减少上下文的内容，slash 上下文 会告诉你哪些已加载，因为你运行的操作不会触发加载。
Imports always load while path scoped rules are what actually reduce context and slash context tells you what loaded because nothing you run causes loading.

2243
03:14:58,670 --> 03:15:04,356
现在有五个场景，其中一个完全取决于拼接这一事实。所以要记住这一点。
Five scenarios now, and one of them turns entirely on the concatenation fact. So keep it in mind.

2244
03:15:05,774 --> 03:15:06,692
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

2245
03:15:07,150 --> 03:15:12,868
一个团队项目 Clod.md 说始终使用四个空格缩进。
A teens project, Clod.mb, says always use four space indentation.

2246
03:15:13,326 --> 03:15:18,756
一名工程师的个人级别 Claude.md 说始终使用两个空格缩进。
One engineer's user level, Claude.md, says always use two space indentation.

2247
03:15:19,726 --> 03:15:27,712
该工程师报告说，Claude 大多数时候用四个空格，偶尔用两个，有时在同一个文件中混合使用两者。
That engineer reports that Claude uses four spaces, most of the time, two spaces occasionally, and once mixed both within a single file.

2248
03:15:27,952 --> 03:15:30,692
他们希望项目标准能够可靠地生效。
They want the project standard to apply reliably.

2249
03:15:31,758 --> 03:15:33,072
他们该怎么做？
What should they do?

2250
03:15:33,902 --> 03:15:38,372
a 选项，因为项目级记忆会覆盖用户级记忆。
a nothing since project level memory overrides user level memory.

2251
03:15:38,512 --> 03:15:40,612
所以，四个空格已经胜出了。
So four spaces already wins.

2252
03:15:40,912 --> 03:15:48,352
b. 从用户的 clot.md 中删除冲突规则，并通过钩子或格式化程序强制执行格式。
b. Remove the conflicting rule from the user clot.md and enforce formatting with a hook or a formatter.

2253
03:15:48,672 --> 03:15:53,892
C. 将四个空格规则移入 clot.local.md，以便最后读取。
C. Move the four space rule into clot.local.md so it is read last.

2254
03:15:54,862 --> 03:15:55,072
D。
D.

2255
03:15:55,712 --> 03:16:01,316
在项目文件中添加更强硬的措辞，例如“此项覆盖任何个人偏好”。
Add stronger wording to the project file, such as this overrides any personal preference.

2256
03:16:02,766 --> 03:16:03,876
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2257
03:16:09,582 --> 03:16:10,832
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2258
03:16:11,152 --> 03:16:13,124
症状描述就是关键线索。
The symptom description is the giveaway.

2259
03:16:13,472 --> 03:16:18,628
大部分时间用四个空格，偶尔用两个，甚至有时在同一个文件中两种都出现。
Four spaces most of the time, two occasionally, and once both in one file.

2260
03:16:19,232 --> 03:16:21,956
这并不是覆盖规则该有的表现。
That is not what an override rule looks like.

2261
03:16:22,798 --> 03:16:32,036
覆盖规则应该产生一致的行为，而这种情况是两个相互矛盾的指令同时存在于同一个上下文窗口中，且没有任何机制来裁决它们之间的冲突。
An override produces consistent behavior, and this is a signature of two contradictory instructions sitting in the same context window with nothing deciding between them.

2262
03:16:32,398 --> 03:16:38,756
选项 A 是一种文档从未明确说明过、且实际表现也已推翻的假设。
Option A is the belief the documentation never actually states, and the observed behavior disproves it anyway.

2263
03:16:39,534 --> 03:16:46,724
选项 C 将加载顺序与优先级混淆了，并且它把团队标准放在了一个个人的 Git 节点文件中。
Option C confuses load order with precedence and it puts a team standard in a personal giting node file.

2264
03:16:47,072 --> 03:16:51,492
选项 B 强化了两个相互矛盾的指令中的其中一个。
Option B adds emphasis to one of two contradictory instructions.

2265
03:16:51,982 --> 03:16:53,828
B 同时涵盖了这两个方面。
B does both halves.

2266
03:16:54,032 --> 03:16:57,860
消除矛盾，然后将格式化规则移到有明确结果的地方。
Remove the contradiction, then move formatting somewhere with a defined outcome.

2267
03:16:59,470 --> 03:17:00,356
场景 2。
Scenario 2.

2268
03:17:00,878 --> 03:17:06,052
一个单仓项目有一个大约 900 行的 clot.md 文件。
A monorepo has a single clot.md of about 900 lines.

2269
03:17:06,352 --> 03:17:13,060
它涵盖了 React 前端、Python 服务、Terraform 基础设施和数据流水线。
It covers the React front end, the Python services, the Terraform infrastructure, and the data pipeline.

2270
03:17:13,742 --> 03:17:23,076
工程师报告称，在开始任何工作之前就会消耗大量的上下文，并且 Claude 有时会将前端规范应用于 Python 文件。
Engineers report that a large amount of context is consumed before any work begins and that clot sometimes applies front-end conventions to Python files.

2271
03:17:23,534 --> 03:17:29,412
一名工程师建议将其拆分为四个文件，并从根目录的 clot.md 中导入它们。
One engineer proposes splitting it into four files and importing them all from the root clot.md.

2272
03:17:30,382 --> 03:17:32,132
最有效的改变是什么？
What is the most effective change?

2273
03:17:33,102 --> 03:17:38,308
a 按建议将内容拆分为四个文件，并从根文件中导入。
a split into four files and import them from the root file as proposed.

2274
03:17:40,032 --> 03:17:47,652
b 在 .Claude 规则 目录下拆分为路径范围规则，这样每个规则仅在工作涉及相关路径时才加载。
b Split into pathscoped rules under the.clot rules directory so each loads only when work touches its paths.

2275
03:17:48,622 --> 03:17:54,832
C. 将前端和基础设施部分移入 clot.local.md。
C. Move the front end and infrastructure sections into clot.local.md.

2276
03:17:55,790 --> 03:18:00,292
d. 添加一行指令，要求 Claude 只应用相关的部分。
d. Add a line instructing plot to apply only the relevant section.

2277
03:18:00,654 --> 03:18:01,956
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2278
03:18:07,470 --> 03:18:14,720
答案是 B，而选项 A 是一个值得警惕的干扰项，因为这是大多数人实际会做的做法。
The answer is B, and option A is the distractor worth dwelling on because it is what most people actually do.

2279
03:18:14,960 --> 03:18:22,468
将 900 行内容拆分为四个导入文件会让仓库更易于阅读，但不会改变加载的内容。
Splitting 900 lines into four imported files makes the repository tidier to read and changes nothing about what loads.

2280
03:18:23,214 --> 03:18:28,356
所有四个导入项在每个会话中都会解析到上下文，因此 Token 消耗是一样的。
All four imports resolve into context every session, so the token cost is identical.

2281
03:18:28,800 --> 03:18:35,748
路径范围在本质上不同，因为规则声明了它们适用的路径，并且仅在工作涉及这些路径时才加载。
Path scoping is different in kind because the rules declare which paths they apply to and load only when work touches them.

2282
03:18:36,686 --> 03:18:39,044
注意这两个症状的起因是相同的。
Notice that both symptoms have the same cause.

2283
03:18:39,918 --> 03:18:45,956
上下文成本以及 Claude 将 React 规范应用于 Python，都是因为所有内容都在一直加载。
The context cost and Claude applying React conventions to Python both come from everything being loaded all the time.

2284
03:18:47,694 --> 03:18:51,076
选项 D 要求模型忽略它面前已经存在的内容。
Option D asks the model to ignore what is already in front of it.

2285
03:18:52,846 --> 03:18:53,920
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

2286
03:18:54,318 --> 03:18:57,120
一个团队的项目设置文件禁止了 bash curl。
A team's project settings file denies bash curl.

2287
03:18:57,280 --> 03:19:02,560
一名工程师确实需要在本地测试沙盒时使用 curl。API。
One engineer legitimately needs curl for local testing against a sandbox. API.

2288
03:19:03,566 --> 03:19:08,900
他们在同一个项目设置文件中添加了一个允许 bash curl 的规则，但没有任何效果。
They add an allow rule for bash curl to the same project settings file and it has no effect.

2289
03:19:09,774 --> 03:19:14,436
他们无法更改团队政策，也不想提交一个影响所有人的更改。
They cannot change the team's policy and do not want to commit a change that affects everyone.

2290
03:19:14,800 --> 03:19:15,812
他们该怎么做？
What should they do?

2291
03:19:16,160 --> 03:19:20,292
a. 改在项目设置的本地文件中添加允许规则。
a add the allow rule to the project settings local file instead.

2292
03:19:20,720 --> 03:19:25,124
b. 在其主目录中的用户设置文件中添加允许规则。
b. Add the allow rule to their user settings file in their home directory.

2293
03:19:25,934 --> 03:19:26,160
C。
C.

2294
03:19:26,560 --> 03:19:29,412
D. 从项目设置文件中移除拒绝规则。
Remove the denay rule from the project settings file.

2295
03:19:30,000 --> 03:19:32,868
D. 在 plot.local.m 中添加注释。
D. Add a note to plot.local.m.

2296
03:19:33,280 --> 03:19:33,440
D。
D.

2297
03:19:33,840 --> 03:19:36,484
解释该工程师被允许使用 curl。
Explaining that curl is permitted for this engineer.

2298
03:19:37,230 --> 03:19:38,404
停顿并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

2299
03:19:44,080 --> 03:19:48,000
答案是 A，这个场景同时测试了两个规则。
The answer is A and this scenario tests both rules at once.

2300
03:19:48,240 --> 03:19:53,636
工程师的允许操作失败了，因为在任何单一层级中，最严格的匹配规则优先。
The engineer's allow failed because inside any single layer, the strictest match wins.

2301
03:19:54,160 --> 03:19:58,596
同一文件中的拒绝规则无论位于何处，都会覆盖他们的允许规则。
A deny in the same file beats their allow wherever in the file it sits.

2302
03:19:58,960 --> 03:20:02,724
要解决这个问题，意味着需要向上移动一个层级，而不是写一个更强力的规则。
Getting past it means moving up a layer other than writing a louder rule.

2303
03:20:03,406 --> 03:20:09,476
项目本地设置位于项目设置之上且不会被提交，因此它符合题干中的两个约束条件。
Project local settings sit above project settings and are not committed, so it satisfies both constraints in the stem.

2304
03:20:10,030 --> 03:20:15,460
选项 B 完全走向了错误的方向，因为用户设置是五个层级中最低的一层。
Option B moves in the wrong direction entirely since user settings are the lowest layer of the five.

2305
03:20:15,840 --> 03:20:17,956
选项 C 被题干排除。
Option C is ruled out by the stem.

2306
03:20:18,862 --> 03:20:24,036
选项 D 是配置逻辑中「说服」与「强制执行」之间的错误。
Option D is the persuade versus enforce error in configuration clothing.

2307
03:20:24,654 --> 03:20:26,660
记忆文件无法授予权限。
A memory file cannot grant a permission.

2308
03:20:28,078 --> 03:20:29,060
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

2309
03:20:29,518 --> 03:20:35,844
一名工程师在他们的项目 clot.md 中添加了一条规则，并报告说 Claude 完全忽略了它。
An engineer adds a rule to their project, clot.md, and reports that Claude is ignoring it entirely.

2310
03:20:36,686 --> 03:20:38,788
他们已经重新启动了两次会话。
They have restarted the session twice.

2311
03:20:39,662 --> 03:20:42,500
一位同事问他们是怎么知道文件正在加载的。
A colleague asks how they know the file is being loaded.

2312
03:20:43,342 --> 03:20:47,040
工程师说他们能在磁盘上看到包含该规则的文件。
The engineer says they can see the file on disk with the rule in it.

2313
03:20:47,662 --> 03:20:49,060
正确的下一步是什么？
What is the right next step?

2314
03:20:49,440 --> 03:20:54,692
a 运行 /上下文 并检查本会话加载的记忆文件列表。
a run slash context and check the list of memory files that loaded this session.

2315
03:20:55,406 --> 03:20:59,108
b 运行 /memory 将文件加载到会话中。
b run slash memory to load the file into the session.

2316
03:20:59,694 --> 03:21:00,000
C。
C.

2317
03:21:00,398 --> 03:21:03,396
更强力地重申规则并再次重启。
Restate the rule more forcefully and restart again.

2318
03:21:03,950 --> 03:21:04,240
D。
D.

2319
03:21:04,526 --> 03:21:06,480
将规则移动到用户级别
Move the rule to the user level

2320
03:21:07,431 --> 03:21:09,860
claw.md，该文件加载更可靠。
claw.md, which loads more reliably.

2321
03:21:11,840 --> 03:21:13,280
稍停并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

2322
03:21:18,638 --> 03:21:19,588
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

2323
03:21:20,160 --> 03:21:24,804
工程师已确认文件存在于磁盘上，并假设它已被加载。
The engineer has verified that the file exists on disk and assumed that it loaded.

2324
03:21:25,120 --> 03:21:26,532
而这两者是完全不同的情况。
And those are different games.

2325
03:21:30,011 --> 03:21:37,540
Slash 上下文 可以报告本会话实际加载了什么，从而区分出“规则被忽略”和“文件从未加载”。
Slash context reports what actually loaded this session, Which separates the rule is being ignored from the file, never loaded.

2326
03:21:38,446 --> 03:21:42,724
这两者对应的修复方法截然不同。因此，先进行诊断是核心目的。
Those two have opposite fixes. So diagnosing first is the whole point.

2327
03:21:45,038 --> 03:21:49,604
选项 B 包含了本模块警告过的误区。
Option B contains the misconception this module warned about.

2328
03:21:50,894 --> 03:21:57,060
没有任何操作能按需加载记忆文件，因为加载是自动的，而命令仅用于报告情况。
Nothing loads a memory file on demand because loading is automatic and the commands only report on it.

2329
03:21:57,838 --> 03:22:04,036
选项 C 跳过了诊断，如果文件从未加载，那么措辞强弱就毫无意义。
Option C skips diagnosis, and if the file never loaded, then the wording could not matter less.

2330
03:22:04,814 --> 03:22:10,308
选项 D 虚构了不同层级之间并不存在的可靠性差异。
Option D invents a reliability difference between hierarchy levels that does not exist.

2331
03:22:12,014 --> 03:22:13,120
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

2332
03:22:13,422 --> 03:22:21,092
一个受监管的机构必须确保公司任何地方的云端代码会话都无法读取匹配 .pem 或 .key 的文件。
A regulated organization must guarantee that no cloud code session anywhere in the company can read files matching.pem or.key.

2333
03:22:21,360 --> 03:22:23,716
它还必须向审计员证明这一点。
It must also demonstrate this to an auditor.

2334
03:22:24,560 --> 03:22:32,644
工程团队控制自己的仓库和设置文件，且一些工程师在本地使用了危险的跳过权限标志。
Engineering teams control their own repositories and their own settings files, and some engineers use the dangerously skipped permissions flag locally.

2335
03:22:33,360 --> 03:22:35,268
哪种做法符合要求？
What satisfies the requirement?

2336
03:22:35,680 --> 03:22:40,484
a 在强制执行代码审查的情况下，在每个项目设置文件中添加拒绝规则。
a A deny rule in every project settings file when forced by code review.

2337
03:22:40,880 --> 03:22:41,120
b。
b.

2338
03:22:41,678 --> 03:22:46,000
在通过 IP 部署的企业级管理设置文件中添加拒绝规则。
A deny rule in the enterprise managed settings file deployed by IP.

2339
03:22:46,720 --> 03:22:46,960
C。
C.

2340
03:22:47,440 --> 03:22:52,772
在全组织范围的 Claude.md 中加入禁止访问密钥材料的一行指令。
A line in the organization wide Claude.md forbidding access to key material.

2341
03:22:53,710 --> 03:22:53,920
D。
D.

2342
03:22:54,318 --> 03:22:58,724
通过设置脚本分发到每位工程师用户设置中的一条拒绝规则。
A deny rule in each engineer's user settings distributed by a setup script.

2343
03:22:59,150 --> 03:23:00,324
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2344
03:23:06,030 --> 03:23:07,776
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2345
03:23:08,718 --> 03:23:11,268
题干中的三个短语都指向同一个方向。
Three phrases in the stem all point the same way.

2346
03:23:12,046 --> 03:23:16,036
确保在公司任何地方都生效，并且能向审计员展示出来。
Guarantee anywhere in the company and demonstrate to an auditor.

2347
03:23:16,622 --> 03:23:23,940
企业管理层是唯一的。下层任何设置都不能放宽限制，这使其成为政策底线，也是唯一站得住脚的答案。
The enterprise managed layer is the only one. Nothing below can relax, which makes it the policy floor and the only defensible answer.

2348
03:23:24,816 --> 03:23:29,700
选项 D 是最强的干扰项，因为设置脚本听起来像是覆盖了全范围。
Option D is the strongest distractor because a setup script feels like coverage.

2349
03:23:30,016 --> 03:23:41,412
但用户设置是五个层级中的最低层。因此任何项目或本地设置都会覆盖它。选项 A 依赖于公司所有仓库中没有任何人会遗忘。
But user settings are the lowest of the five layers. So any project or local setting overrides them. Option A relies on nobody ever forgetting across every repository in the company.

2350
03:23:42,318 --> 03:23:50,212
选项 C 是一个记忆文件，只是拼接的上下文，没有保证的结果，也没法给审计员看。
Option C is a memory file which is concatenated context with no guaranteed outcome and nothing you could show an auditor.

2351
03:23:50,958 --> 03:23:51,908
模块 9。
Module 9.

2352
03:23:52,622 --> 03:23:55,236
接下来是关于扩展 Claude Code 的内容。
Next, on extending clot code.

2353
03:23:57,006 --> 03:23:58,176
模块 9。
Module 9.

2354
03:23:58,510 --> 03:24:01,796
模块 8 涵盖了被加载的配置。
Module 8 covered configuration that is loaded.

2355
03:24:02,606 --> 03:24:08,644
这一部分涵盖的是运行中的配置、技能、斜杆命令、钩子和插件。
This one covers configuration that runs, skills, slash commands, hooks and plugins.

2356
03:24:09,550 --> 03:24:11,616
两个问题涵盖了所有内容。
Two questions organize all of it.

2357
03:24:12,046 --> 03:24:14,660
是谁调用这个东西，它能拒绝吗？
Who invokes this thing and can it refuse?

2358
03:24:15,438 --> 03:24:18,660
搞清楚这两点，整个领域就清晰了。
Get those two straight and the whole area falls into place.

2359
03:24:19,536 --> 03:24:26,896
本模块还将构建我之前在模块 6 和模块 8 中承诺过两次的条件强制执行。
This module also finally builds the conditional enforcement I have promised you twice now in module 6 and module 8.

2360
03:24:27,056 --> 03:24:30,276
那就是钩子部分，它非常关键。
That is the hooks half and it is worth real marks.

2361
03:24:31,982 --> 03:24:40,816
四个扩展点和一列核心内容。技能可以由你调用，由 Claude 调用，或者两者皆可，由你决定。
Four extension points and one column that matters. A skill can be invoked by you, by Claude, or by both, and you decide which.

2362
03:24:42,158 --> 03:24:46,340
斜杆命令是功能较少的、由你调用的技能。
A slash command is a skill with fewer features invoked by you.

2363
03:24:46,894 --> 03:24:52,580
钩子不被任何人调用，因为它是在事件发生时触发的，无论是否有人想要它。
A hook is invoked by nobody because it fires on an event whether anyone wanted it to or not.

2364
03:24:53,422 --> 03:24:56,484
而插件是一个包含其他三者的包。
And a plugin is a package containing the other three.

2365
03:24:57,070 --> 03:24:58,468
看最后一列。
Look at the last column.

2366
03:24:59,246 --> 03:25:00,772
只有钩子可以拦截。
Only hooks can block.

2367
03:25:01,326 --> 03:25:06,532
其他所有内容都是指令，这意味着其他所有内容都是说服。
Everything else is instructions, which means everything else is persuasion.

2368
03:25:07,534 --> 03:25:12,548
这就是模块 6 的规则到了领域 3，只是换了套衣服。
That is module 6's rule arriving in domain 3 wearing different clothes.

2369
03:25:14,286 --> 03:25:20,100
有一项核心内容需要在任何其他内容之前说明，因为它会改变你阅读这些材料的方式。
One currency item needs stating before anything else because it reshapes how you read this material.

2370
03:25:20,336 --> 03:25:26,948
当考试指南编写时，斜杆命令和技能是两个独立的概念。此后它们合并成了一个系统。
When the exam guide was written, slash commands and skills were separate concepts. They have since merged into one system.

2371
03:25:27,726 --> 03:25:34,724
一个位于 .claude 命令目录下的 deploy.md 文件，以及一个在 .prompt skills 目录下作为技能的 技能.md。
A file at .claude commands, deploy.md, and a skill at.plod skills deploy as skill.md.

2372
03:25:36,462 --> 03:25:38,052
两者都会创建 /deploy 命令。
Both create slash deploy.

2373
03:25:38,798 --> 03:25:40,676
现有的命令文件仍可正常工作。
Existing command files keep working.

2374
03:25:41,806 --> 03:25:45,060
技能是推荐的存放位置，并且在名称冲突时具有优先权。
Skills are the recommended location and they win a name collision.

2375
03:25:45,966 --> 03:25:56,068
在考试中，按照指南的要求：重复提示词用命令，复杂的工作流用技能。我提到的关于技能的所有内容都适用于两者。
On the exam, treat them as the guide does with commands for repeated prompts and skills for richer workflows. Everything I say about skills applies to both.

2376
03:25:57,294 --> 03:26:03,044
一个技能是一个包含 技能.md 文件以及所需支持文件的文件夹。
A skill is a folder containing a skill.md file plus whatever supporting files it needs.

2377
03:26:03,502 --> 03:26:05,856
模板、示例、脚本等。
Templates, examples, scripts.

2378
03:26:06,176 --> 03:26:11,396
在该文件内部，是 Claude 在技能激活时遵循的 Markdown 指令。
Inside that file, markdown instructions that Claude follows when the skill is active.

2379
03:26:11,950 --> 03:26:19,236
还有 YAML 前置内容字段，用于控制谁可以调用它、它可以调用哪些工具以及在何处运行。
Also YAM, L front matter, controlling who may invoke it, which tools it may use, and where it runs.

2380
03:26:42,638 --> 03:26:44,548
有 6 个前置内容字段值得了解。
6 front matter fields worth knowing.

2381
03:26:45,134 --> 03:26:48,036
Name 是必填项，并成为斜杆命令。
Name is required and becomes the slash command.

2382
03:26:49,486 --> 03:26:52,324
Description 是必填项，它不是文档说明。
Description is required and it is not documentation.

2383
03:26:52,686 --> 03:26:53,636
它是描述性文本。
It is the text.

2384
03:26:54,926 --> 03:26:59,300
Claude 在决定是否加载该技能时，会根据你的意图进行匹配。
Claude matches against your intent when deciding whether to load the skill.

2385
03:26:59,662 --> 03:27:02,308
所以要把它写成一个场景，而不是一个标题。
So write it as a situation rather than a title.

2386
03:27:03,182 --> 03:27:06,464
Disable 模型调用 意味着只有你可以触发它。
Disable model invocation means only you can trigger it.

2387
03:27:06,734 --> 03:27:09,572
User invocable false 意味着只有 Claude 可以触发。
User invocable false means only Claude can.

2388
03:27:09,904 --> 03:27:13,124
Allowed 工具 限制了该技能可以使用的工具。
Allowed tools restricts which tools the skill may use.

2389
03:27:13,504 --> 03:27:17,604
而 上下文分叉 会在隔离的子代理中运行该技能。
And context fork runs the skill in an isolated subagent.

2390
03:27:18,510 --> 03:27:19,876
接下来的三张幻灯片。
The next three slides.

2391
03:27:21,582 --> 03:27:25,988
仔细看最后那三张，因为每一项都会涉及考题。
Take the last three of those properly because each one decides questions.

2392
03:27:27,534 --> 03:27:30,596
默认情况下，你和 Claude 都可以调用任何技能。
By default, both you and Claude can invoke any skill.

2393
03:27:30,944 --> 03:27:35,972
你输入斜杠加名称，当它符合你的意图时，Claude 会自动加载它。
You type slash and the name, and Claude loads it automatically when it matches your intent.

2394
03:27:37,390 --> 03:27:39,652
两个前置内容字段，把其中一个关掉。
Two front matapes, turn one of those off.

2395
03:27:40,464 --> 03:27:48,164
Disable 模型调用 意味着 Claude 不会自行触发它，这对于任何具有真实副作用的操作都是你想要的。
Disable model invocation means Claude will never trigger it by itself, which is what you want for anything with real side effects.

2396
03:27:48,544 --> 03:27:50,820
部署、发布、发送。
Deploying, releasing, sending.

2397
03:27:51,824 --> 03:27:53,092
这样你就保留了手动触发权。
You keep the trigger.

2398
03:27:53,504 --> 03:27:56,196
User invocable false 是相反的情况。
User invocable false is the opposite.

2399
03:27:57,102 --> 03:28:05,860
不会暴露斜杆命令，只有 Claude 能加载它，这适用于你希望自动执行且不需要任何人输入任何内容的常规操作。
No slash command is exposed and only Claude can load it, which suits conventions you want followed automatically without anyone typing anything.

2400
03:28:06,446 --> 03:28:10,704
思考哪种调用者会产生问题，然后把那个选项关掉。
Ask which invoker would be a problem and switch that one off.

2401
03:28:12,078 --> 03:28:16,740
「允许工具」同时做了三件事，而考试考查的是其中的两项。
Allow tools is doing three things at once and the exam cares about two of them.

2402
03:28:17,351 --> 03:28:21,828
它起到了限制作用，也就是说在技能激活期间，Claude 只能使用列出的工具。
It restricts, so while the skill is active, Claude may use only the tools listed.

2403
03:28:27,184 --> 03:28:27,424
而且
And

2404
03:28:27,424 --> 03:28:31,780
它缩小了上下文，因为只有这些工具定义会被包含进来。
it shrinks context because only those tool definitions get included.

2405
03:28:32,064 --> 03:28:35,584
第四行提到的后果才是考试考查的内容。
The consequence in the fourth line is the examinable one.

2406
03:28:35,854 --> 03:28:43,492
一个仅被赋予读取工具、没有写入权限的研究技能，无论它的指令怎么写，或者任何人要求它做什么，它都无法执行写入操作。
A research skill given read tools only cannot write, no matter what its instructions say or what anyone asks it to do.

2407
03:28:44,206 --> 03:28:46,724
这是能力范围限制，而不是提示。
That is capability scoping rather than a hint.

2408
03:28:46,944 --> 03:28:52,196
这和第三模块中限制子代理工具集时的原则是一样的。
And it is the same principle as restricting a subagent's tool set back in module 3.

2409
03:28:54,064 --> 03:28:59,716
上下文分叉是在一个具有独立上下文窗口的隔离子代理中运行该技能。
Context fork runs the skill inside an isolated subagent with its own context window.

2410
03:29:00,384 --> 03:29:06,948
所有冗长的中间输出都留在分叉中，主对话接收到的是结果而非过程。
All the verbose intermediate output stays in the fork and the main conversation receives the result rather than the working.

2411
03:29:07,664 --> 03:29:11,524
这意味着第三模块的所有内容在这里都适用且无需更改。
Which means everything from module 3 applies here unchanged.

2412
03:29:12,494 --> 03:29:20,944
分叉技能不继承任何对话历史，因此它必须被编写成完全自包含的，只有它的最终结果
A fork skill inherits no conversation history, so it must be written to be entirely self-contained, and only its final result

2413
03:29:21,104 --> 03:29:21,744
会被传回。
comes back.

2414
03:29:22,094 --> 03:29:30,884
将其用于基于代码的分析、头脑风暴、研究，以及任何会产生大量你不想要的内容且会弄乱主线程的情况。
Use it for code-based analysis, brainstorming, research, and anything else that generates a lot of material you do not want, cluttering the main thread.

2415
03:29:31,790 --> 03:29:36,612
如果没有它，所有这些输出都会直接进入你的上下文窗口。
Without it, all of that output flows straight into your context window.

2416
03:29:38,254 --> 03:29:39,024
这就是 skills。
That is skins.

2417
03:29:39,504 --> 03:29:43,076
现在是钩子，这张幻灯片上的句子就是核心概念。
Now hooks and the sentence on this slide is the whole idea.

2418
03:29:44,910 --> 03:29:51,396
到目前为止，领域 3 中的所有内容都是某种形式的指令，Claude 会读取并在不同程度上遵循这些指令。
Everything so far in domain 3 has been instructions of one kind or another, which Claude reads and follows to varying degrees.

2419
03:29:53,518 --> 03:29:55,652
钩子在性质上是不同的。
A hook is different in kind.

2420
03:29:56,462 --> 03:30:04,868
它是一个处理程序，Claude Code 会在生命周期的固定点自动运行它，而且 Claude 不决定是否运行它。
It is a handler that Claude code runs automatically at a fixed point in its lifecycle, and Claude does not decide whether it runs.

2421
03:30:05,104 --> 03:30:14,212
它不是被请求执行的。这是包裹在非确定性智能体外层的确定性层，也是领域 3 中所有保证所在的地方。
It is not asked. This is the deterministic layer wrapped around a non deterministic agent, and it is where every guarantee in domain 3 ends up living.

2422
03:30:15,758 --> 03:30:19,556
参考文档涵盖了大约 30 种钩子事件，而且这个数字还在增加。
The reference documents around 30 hook events and the number keeps growing.

2423
03:30:19,952 --> 03:30:22,020
所以不要试图去背诵这个列表。
So do not try to memorize the list.

2424
03:30:22,446 --> 03:30:24,992
5. 承担几乎所有的实际工作。
5. Carry almost all real work.

2425
03:30:25,710 --> 03:30:31,620
工具使用前在任何工具调用之前触发，并可以拦截它，这使其成为强制执行点。
Pre-tool use fires before any tool call and can block it, which makes it the enforcement point.

2426
03:30:32,494 --> 03:30:37,956
工具使用后在工具成功后触发，无法拦截，因为工具已经运行了。
Post tool use fires after a tool succeeds and cannot block because the tool already ran.

2427
03:30:38,991 --> 03:30:43,204
提示词提交在你提交提示词时触发，并可以拒绝它。
Use a prompt submit fires when you submit a prompt and can reject it.

2428
03:30:43,918 --> 03:30:50,020
停止在 Claude 完成一个响应、轮次时触发，并且可以拒绝让它停止，从而强制执行更多工作。
Stop fires when Claude finishes a response, turn and can refuse to let it stop, forcing more work.

2429
03:30:50,862 --> 03:30:55,588
会话开始在开始和恢复时触发，仅作为信息提供。
And session start fires at the beginning and again on resume and is informational.

2430
03:30:56,878 --> 03:31:01,604
钩子通过标准输入接收 JSON，并通过退出代码进行响应。
Hooks receive JSON on standard input and answer through exit codes.

2431
03:31:01,966 --> 03:31:04,112
零允许，且调用继续进行。
Zero allows and the call proceeds.

2432
03:31:04,366 --> 03:31:10,244
两个会拦截可能导致阻塞的事件，而你写入标准错误的内容会作为原因反馈给 Claude。
Two blocks on the events that can block and whatever you wrote to standard error goes back to Claude as the reason.

2433
03:31:10,798 --> 03:31:12,356
还有一个根本不会拦截任何内容。
And one blocks nothing at all.

2434
03:31:13,326 --> 03:31:16,516
这是人们在使用钩子时犯的最大错误。
That is the single biggest mistake people make with hooks.

2435
03:31:16,974 --> 03:31:22,272
一个是传统的 Unix 失败代码，直觉告诉我们它应该意味着停止。
One is the conventional Unix failure code, and every instinct says it should mean stop.

2436
03:31:22,512 --> 03:31:23,364
但它并不代表停止。
It does not.

2437
03:31:23,712 --> 03:31:26,084
这就导致了第四行的警告。
Which leads to the warning in the fourth line.

2438
03:31:26,958 --> 03:31:33,892
一个从未测试过的护栏比没有护栏更糟糕，因为你已经不再关注它原本该拦截的东西了。
A guardrail you never tested is worse than no guardrail because you have stopped watching for the thing it was supposed to catch.

2439
03:31:35,552 --> 03:31:38,532
这两个工具生命周期事件划分得很清晰。
The two tool lifecycle events split cleanly.

2440
03:31:39,150 --> 03:31:40,992
工具使用前是预防性的。
Pre-tool use is prevention.

2441
03:31:41,262 --> 03:31:48,672
它能看到工具名称以及 Claude 即将传递的准确参数，并且在执行前就停止调用。
It sees the tool name and the exact arguments Claude is about to pass, and exiting tool stops the call before it happens.

2442
03:31:48,974 --> 03:31:50,628
所有的护栏都属于这一类。
Every guardrail belongs here.

2443
03:31:52,142 --> 03:31:55,652
值得知道的一个限制是，它无法重写参数。
One limitation worth knowing is that it cannot rewrite the arguments.

2444
03:31:56,622 --> 03:31:59,716
它只能拒绝，然后 Claude 会重新组织表述。
It can only refuse and then Claude reformulates.

2445
03:32:17,072 --> 03:32:17,392
如果
If

2446
03:32:17,392 --> 03:32:20,324
题目要求“阻止”，那就是工具使用前。
a question says prevent, that is pre-tool use.

2447
03:32:21,262 --> 03:32:28,260
如果它说“每当写入文件时，也要运行格式化程序”，那就是工具使用后。
If it says whenever a file is written, also run the formatter, that is post tool use.

2448
03:32:29,870 --> 03:32:31,072
有 4 个限制。
4 limitations.

2449
03:32:31,312 --> 03:32:38,912
钩子不能调用工具或斜杆命令，因为它们仅通过退出代码和输出流进行通信，没有其他方式。
Hooks cannot call tools or slash commands because they communicate through exit codes and output streams and nothing else.

2450
03:32:39,374 --> 03:32:45,636
工具使用前无法修改参数。既然 Claude 正准备传递这些参数，那么拦截路径就是你唯一的手段。
Pre-tool use cannot modify the arguments. Claude is about to pass, so the block path is your only lever.

2451
03:32:46,592 --> 03:32:51,076
Stop 在每次响应结束时都会触发，而不仅仅是在任务完成时。
Stop fires at the end of every response rather than only a task completion.

2452
03:32:51,312 --> 03:32:55,044
所以你在那里构建的任何门控都必须能够容忍在任务中途停止的情况。
So any gate you build there has to tolerate stopping mid task.

2453
03:32:55,792 --> 03:32:57,572
还有一个诚实的提醒。
And a honest one at the bottom.

2454
03:32:58,112 --> 03:33:04,036
钩子只能涵盖你预先想到的情况，这使得它们更像是一个策略层，而不是安全网。
Hooks only cover the cases you thought of in advance, which makes them a policy layer rather than a safety net.

2455
03:33:04,910 --> 03:33:10,852
在钩子中使用正则表达式不应该成为 Claude 与你的生产数据库之间唯一的屏障。
A regular expression in a hook should not be the only thing standing between Claude and your production database.

2456
03:33:12,430 --> 03:33:15,364
有一项属性值得单独记忆。
One property is worth memorizing on its own.

2457
03:33:15,982 --> 03:33:18,916
钩子会收紧权限，且永远不会放宽权限。
Hooks tighten permissions and they never loosen them.

2458
03:33:19,790 --> 03:33:23,396
即使有人已经开始操作，工具使用前的拒绝依然有效。
A pre-tool use deny holds even when someone has started.

2459
03:33:23,982 --> 03:33:27,076
Claude Code 在一种绕过权限提示的模式下运行。
Claude code in a mode that bypasses permission prompts.

2460
03:33:27,950 --> 03:33:32,900
这是一个刻意的设计决策，也是让钩子作为一种控制手段变得可靠的原因。
That is a deliberate design decision and it is what makes hooks defensible as a control.

2461
03:33:33,872 --> 03:33:36,352
它还告诉你钩子不能做什么。
It also tells you what a hook cannot do.

2462
03:33:36,592 --> 03:33:40,676
你不能利用钩子来授予权限规则已经禁止的功能。
You cannot use one to grant a capability that permissions have denied.

2463
03:33:40,912 --> 03:33:45,892
所以，如果题目提供钩子作为允许某项操作的手段，那么这个选项就是错误的。
So if a question offers a hook as a way of permitting something, that option is wrong.

2464
03:33:47,470 --> 03:33:52,992
这就是模块 6 的第四个场景建立起来、并由模块 8 承诺完成的对应关系。
This is the pair that module 6's fourth scenario set up and module 8 promised to finish.

2465
03:33:53,152 --> 03:33:55,140
权限规则是“开”或“关”。
A permission rule is on or off.

2466
03:33:55,566 --> 03:34:00,676
允许、拒绝或请求，与工具匹配时没有任何逻辑和条件。
Allow, deny or ask matched against the tool with no logic and no conditions.

2467
03:34:01,632 --> 03:34:04,772
它成本低、是声明式的，且易于审计。
It is cheap and declarative and easy to audit.

2468
03:34:05,326 --> 03:34:08,068
而且只要规则被标记，它就是正确的默认选择。
And it is a right default whenever the rule is flagged.

2469
03:34:08,846 --> 03:34:10,116
钩子可以做决策。
A hook can decide.

2470
03:34:11,312 --> 03:34:14,596
它能看到参数、路径和当前时间。
It sees the arguments, the path, and the current time.

2471
03:34:15,118 --> 03:34:19,140
它运行实际的代码，并且可以评估你能够表达的任何内容。
It runs actual code and it can evaluate anything you can express.

2472
03:34:20,142 --> 03:34:24,324
所以当规则包含权限无法表述的条件时，就选择钩子。
So reach for it when the rule is conditional in a way a permission cannot state.

2473
03:34:24,622 --> 03:34:26,912
“严禁读取环境文件”是一项权限。
Never read environment files is a permission.

2474
03:34:27,214 --> 03:34:29,312
“严禁在变更范围外写入生产环境”。
Never write to production outside the change.

2475
03:34:29,582 --> 03:34:30,660
“窗口”是一个钩子。
Window is a hook.

2476
03:34:32,142 --> 03:34:34,532
插件本身不增加任何功能。
Plugins add no capability of their own.

2477
03:34:34,926 --> 03:34:43,204
插件是一个包含技能、钩子、子智能体和 MCB 服务器配置的包，作为一个可安装单元进行分发。
A plugin is a package containing skills, hooks, subagents, and MCB server configuration distributed as one installable unit.

2478
03:34:43,630 --> 03:34:46,564
这种访问属于“分发”而非“功能”。
The access is distribution rather than capability.

2479
03:34:47,502 --> 03:34:56,612
如果相同的发布工作流被复制粘贴到五个客户端代码库中，那么它应该属于插件，由插件来处理发现和更新。
If the same release workflow is copy-pasted into five client codebases that belongs in a plugin where discovery and updates are handled for you.

2480
03:34:57,390 --> 03:35:05,604
如果工作流仅针对一个代码库（比如你们团队特定的测试运行器），那它就保留在仓库中的项目级别。
If the workflow is specific to one codebase, like your team's particular test runner, it stays as a project scale in the repository.

2481
03:35:06,032 --> 03:35:12,740
当场景提到多个仓库和重复的配置时，插件就是要求的答案。
When a scenario mentions several repositories and duplicated configuration, plugins are the answer it wants.

2482
03:35:14,350 --> 03:35:17,700
这是到目前为止整个领域 3 的决策表。
The decision table for the whole of domain 3 so far.

2483
03:35:18,144 --> 03:35:22,980
“Plot 应该始终知道某事”意味着记忆文件或范围化的规则。
Plot should always know something means a memory file or a path scoped rule.

2484
03:35:23,424 --> 03:35:28,036
“按需运行的重复请求”意味着作为斜杠命令调用的技能。
A repeated request run on demand means a skill invoked as a slash command.

2485
03:35:28,544 --> 03:35:32,964
“包含步骤、资源和工具限制的工作流”意味着带有允许工具列表的技能。
A workflow with steps, assets, and tool limits means a skill with allowed tools.

2486
03:35:33,870 --> 03:35:37,476
“复杂的任务”意味着具有上下文分叉的技能。
A noisy task means a skill with context fork.

2487
03:35:37,870 --> 03:35:41,956
“某些操作必须在每次工具调用时发生”意味着工具使用后钩子。
Something must happen on every tool call means a post-tool use hook.

2488
03:35:42,624 --> 03:35:45,028
“某些情况绝不能发生”意味着权限。
Something must never happen means a permission.

2489
03:35:45,664 --> 03:35:47,844
或者是一个工具使用前钩子。
Deny or a pre-tool use hook.

2490
03:35:48,224 --> 03:35:51,664
并且在多个仓库中采用相同的设置，意味着插件。
And the same setup across many repositories means a plugin.

2491
03:35:52,622 --> 03:35:54,468
检查要求中的动词。
Check the verb in the requirement.

2492
03:35:55,374 --> 03:35:56,868
Should 是一个技能。
Should is a skill.

2493
03:35:57,504 --> 03:35:59,556
Must 是一个钩子或权限。
Must is a hook or a permission.

2494
03:36:01,102 --> 03:36:02,180
货币汇总。
The currency summary.

2495
03:36:02,734 --> 03:36:06,980
指南编写时，命令和技能是分开的，后来合并了。
Commands and skills were separate when the guide was written and have since merged.

2496
03:36:07,344 --> 03:36:12,100
两者现在都产生相同的斜杠命令。所以根据指南给出的答案并不算错。
Both still produce the same slash command. So a guide data answer is not wrong.

2497
03:36:12,384 --> 03:36:17,412
钩子事件的数量从几个增加到大约 30 个，且列表仍在增加。
Hook events numbered a handful and now run to around 30, with the list still growing.

2498
03:36:18,446 --> 03:36:22,704
这就是为什么本模块教你 5 个核心点，而不是给出一个完整的目录。
That is why this module taught you 5 rather than a catalog.

2499
03:36:23,214 --> 03:36:30,564
而且皮肤现在可以在前置元数据中携带自己的钩子，并限制在该技能的生命周期内，而指南完全没有涵盖这一点。
And skins can now carry their own hooks in front matter, scoped to that skill's lifetime, which the guide does not cover at all.

2500
03:36:32,430 --> 03:36:34,944
在考试中，按指南的框架来回答。
Answer the guide's framing on the exam.

2501
03:36:35,502 --> 03:36:40,612
这些变化不会让旧答案变错，只会让它变得不完整。
None of these developments make an older answer incorrect, only incomplete.

2502
03:36:42,062 --> 03:36:42,864
5 行。
5 lines.

2503
03:36:43,104 --> 03:36:48,864
皮肤是带有前置元数据指令，只有名称和描述会在使用前产生上下文。
Skins are instructions with front matter, and only the name and description cause context until one is used.

2504
03:36:49,166 --> 03:36:55,824
允许工具既有限制作用也有预先批准，而上下文分叉则隔离工作并仅返回结果。
Allow tools both restricts and pre-approves, while context fork isolates the work and returns only the result.

2505
03:36:56,622 --> 03:36:59,492
钩子是根据事件触发的，而不是基于 clot 的决策。
Hooks fire on events rather than on plot's decision.

2506
03:36:59,758 --> 03:37:02,660
退出两个块，而退出一个块则不影响任何内容。
Exit two blocks and exit one blocks nothing.

2507
03:37:03,886 --> 03:37:07,652
工具使用前阻止，而工具使用后响应且无法撤销。
Pre-tool use prevents while post-tool use reacts and cannot undo.

2508
03:37:08,334 --> 03:37:13,380
权限是扁平化的规则，钩子是条件性的，而插件是关于分发的。
And permissions are flat rules, hooks are conditional ones, and plugins are about distribution.

2509
03:37:14,382 --> 03:37:20,708
现在有五个场景，其中两个看起来几乎一样，但需要的钩子却相反。
Five scenarios now and two of them look almost identical while wanting opposite hooks.

2510
03:37:22,446 --> 03:37:23,364
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

2511
03:37:23,726 --> 03:37:30,980
一个团队要求 Claude 编写或编辑的每个 Python 文件在提交前都必须使用他们的标准格式化程序进行格式化。
A team requires that every Python file Claude writes or edits is formatted with their standard formatter before it is committed.

2512
03:37:31,502 --> 03:37:35,984
该规则目前存在于 Claude.mb 中，合规率约为 90%。
The rule currently lives in Claude.mb and compliance is roughly 90%.

2513
03:37:37,070 --> 03:37:41,540
当 Claude 进行多文件更改时，有时会跳过格式化步骤。
When Claude is deep in a multifile change, it sometimes skips the formatting step.

2514
03:37:41,902 --> 03:37:43,524
他们希望每次都执行此操作。
They want it to happen every time.

2515
03:37:43,822 --> 03:37:45,956
而且他们不希望 Claude 必须去记住这一点。
And they do not want Claude to have to remember.

2516
03:37:46,766 --> 03:37:47,940
他们应该实施什么？
What should they implement?

2517
03:37:48,398 --> 03:37:53,220
a. 在写入和编辑时增加一个工具使用前钩子，拦截未格式化的内容。
a a pre-tool use hook on write and edit that blocks unformatted content.

2518
03:37:54,126 --> 03:37:58,596
b. 在写入和编辑时增加一个工具使用后钩子，运行格式化程序。
b a post tool use hook on write and edit that runs the formatter.

2519
03:37:59,024 --> 03:37:59,344
C。
C.

2520
03:37:59,694 --> 03:38:04,544
一个名为 slash format 的皮肤，让 Claude 在编辑文件后调用它。D。
A skin called slash format that Claude invokes after editing files. D.

2521
03:38:04,910 --> 03:38:08,420
一条权限规则，规定除非内容已格式化，否则不允许写入。
A permissions rule denying write unless the content is formatted.

2522
03:38:08,944 --> 03:38:10,276
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2523
03:38:15,982 --> 03:38:16,836
答案是
The answer is

2524
03:38:18,926 --> 03:38:19,184
B。
B.

2525
03:38:19,664 --> 03:38:22,464
需要内化的区别在于强调点。
The distinction to internalize is in the call out.

2526
03:38:23,054 --> 03:38:24,740
这个要求是附加性的。
This requirement is additive.

2527
03:38:26,030 --> 03:38:28,708
每当写入文件时，也要运行格式化程序。
Whenever a file is written, also run the formatter.

2528
03:38:29,358 --> 03:38:32,260
它不是禁止性条款，所以没有什么可以阻止的。
It is not a prohibition, so there is nothing to prevent.

2529
03:38:33,582 --> 03:38:39,684
工具使用后钩子在写入后触发，运行格式化程序，而且 Claude 不需要去记住它。
Post tool use fires after the write, runs the formatter, and Claude never has to remember.

2530
03:38:40,590 --> 03:38:46,944
选项 A 是一个很有趣的错误答案，因为“拦截”是更强力的机制，人们往往会倾向于选择它。
Option A is the interesting wrong answer because blocking is the more powerful mechanism and people reach for it.

2531
03:38:47,184 --> 03:38:53,988
在这里，它把一个简单的格式化操作变成了一个拦截、重新表述和重试的过程，却没有任何好处。
Here it turns a one-step formatting operation into a block, a reformulation and a retry for no benefit.

2532
03:38:54,766 --> 03:39:00,004
选项 C 把决定权留给了 Claude，而这正是他们已经面临的 10% 的失败率。
Option C keeps the decision with Claude, which is the 10% failure they already have.

2533
03:39:00,464 --> 03:39:04,836
选项 D 要求检查内容权限，但他们无法做到这一点。
Option D asks permissions to inspect content, which they cannot do.

2534
03:39:06,414 --> 03:39:07,424
场景 2。
Scenario 2.

2535
03:39:07,694 --> 03:39:16,164
同一团队还要求：在任何情况下，都不允许 plod 对任何名称包含 plod 的环境执行数据库迁移命令。
The same team also requires that plod never runs a database migration command against any environment whose name contains plod under any circumstances.

2536
03:39:17,742 --> 03:39:22,500
迁移命令通过 bash 运行，环境名称作为参数出现在命令字符串中。
Migration commands run through bash and the environment appears as a flag in the command string.

2537
03:39:23,022 --> 03:39:26,980
一些工程师在跳过权限提示的情况下运行 plod 代码。
Some engineers run plod code with permission prompts bypassed.

2538
03:39:27,344 --> 03:39:28,624
他们应该实现什么？
What should they implement?

2539
03:39:28,864 --> 03:39:34,660
a. 在 bash 上设置一个工具使用后钩子，当检测到生产环境迁移时发出警报。
a A post tool use hook on bash that alerts when a production migration is detected.

2540
03:39:35,104 --> 03:39:40,864
b. 在 bash 上设置一个工具使用前钩子，检查命令并在匹配时退出。
b a pre tool use hook on bash that inspects the command and exits two on a match.

2541
03:39:41,184 --> 03:39:43,972
C. 在 bash 上设置权限拒绝规则。
C. A permissions deny rule on bash.

2542
03:39:44,878 --> 03:39:50,436
D. 使用 clot.md 规则，因为团队已经严格遵守他们的惯例。
D a clot.md rule since the team already follows their conventions closely.

2543
03:39:50,990 --> 03:39:52,388
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2544
03:39:58,048 --> 03:40:01,732
答案是 B，这就是我警告过你们的那对情况。
The answer is B, and this is the pair I warned you about.

2545
03:40:02,062 --> 03:40:04,740
同样的团队，同样的工具，相反的答案。
Same team, same tools, opposite answer.

2546
03:40:06,670 --> 03:40:13,380
区别在于场景 1 是附加性的，而这个是禁止性的。所以只有预防措施才有效。
The difference is that scenario 1 was additive, and this one is a prohibition. So prevention is the only thing that works.

2547
03:40:14,158 --> 03:40:20,928
选项 A 是陷阱，它很好地说明了为什么工具使用后不能作为护栏。
Option A is the trap, and it is a good illustration of why post tool use cannot be a guardrail.

2548
03:40:21,166 --> 03:40:26,628
迁移已经执行了，所以你的警报只是在提醒你当前正在发生的故障。
The migration has already run, so your alert is a notification about the outage you are currently having.

2549
03:40:27,534 --> 03:40:31,044
选项 C 说明了为什么权限并不总是足够的。
Option C shows why permissions are not always enough.

2550
03:40:31,918 --> 03:40:37,252
它们匹配的工具相同，而直接拒绝 bash 会移除所有合法的命令。
They match on the tool and denying bash outright would remove every legitimate command.

2551
03:40:37,710 --> 03:40:39,684
而且题干的最后一行很重要。
And the last line of the stem matters.

2552
03:40:40,654 --> 03:40:44,836
即使权限提示被绕过，工具使用前拒绝依然有效。
A pre-tool use deny holds even when permission prompts are bypassed.

2553
03:40:46,574 --> 03:40:47,492
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

2554
03:40:47,886 --> 03:40:52,548
一名工程师编写了一个技能，用于审计代码库中未使用的依赖项。
An engineer has written a skill that audits a code base for unused dependencies.

2555
03:40:52,768 --> 03:41:04,388
它读取包文件、在仓库中执行 grep，并生成一份简短的报告。它能运行，但运行它会导致大量的文件列表和 grep 输出填满上下文窗口。
It reads package files, greps across the repository, and produces a short report. It works, but running it fills a large portion of the context window with file listings and grep output.

2556
03:41:04,814 --> 03:41:12,048
之后，Claude 在工程师实际正在处理的任务上的表现明显变差。报告本身只有大约 15 行。
Afterwards, Claude is noticeably worse at the task the engineer was actually working on. The report itself is about 15 lines.

2557
03:41:12,208 --> 03:41:14,212
最有效的更改是什么？
What is the most effective change?

2558
03:41:14,862 --> 03:41:18,048
A. 在技能的前置元数据中添加上下文分叉。
a add context fork to the skin's front matter.

2559
03:41:18,528 --> 03:41:21,572
B. 将允许的工具列表仅限制为读取和 grep。
B add allowed tools listing only read and grep.

2560
03:41:22,414 --> 03:41:22,688
C。
C.

2561
03:41:23,168 --> 03:41:26,212
添加禁用模型调用，使其运行频率降低。
Add disable model invocation so it runs less often.

2562
03:41:26,702 --> 03:41:29,988
D. 将该技能移入插件中，以便单独加载。
D. Move the skill into a plugin so it loads separately.

2563
03:41:30,382 --> 03:41:31,364
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2564
03:41:37,102 --> 03:41:38,448
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

2565
03:41:39,088 --> 03:41:41,668
关键线索就在题干的最后一行。
The signature is in the last line of the stem.

2566
03:41:43,118 --> 03:41:46,368
大量的中间工作过程，却只有 15 行的结果。
A great deal of intermediate working and a 15-line result.

2567
03:41:47,182 --> 03:41:50,724
这种比例正是上下文分叉存在的意义所在。
That ratio is precisely what context fork exists for.

2568
03:41:51,182 --> 03:41:56,004
因为探索过程发生在隔离的窗口中，只有报告会被传回。
Since the exploration happens inside an isolated window and only the report comes back.

2569
03:41:56,782 --> 03:42:05,668
选项 B 是最强的干扰项，因为限制允许工具确实可以通过裁剪包含的工具定义来减少上下文。
Option B is the strongest distractor because allowed tools genuinely does reduce context by trimming which tool definitions are included.

2570
03:42:06,446 --> 03:42:11,488
但它对 grep 输出本身毫无影响，而那才是真正占用空间的地方。
It does nothing about the grep output itself, which is where the volume actually is.

2571
03:42:12,110 --> 03:42:18,660
选项 C 虽然能降低问题的发生频率，但工程师还是想运行这个技能。
Option C reduces how often the problem occurs and the engineer wants to run this skill.

2572
03:42:19,662 --> 03:42:25,828
选项 D 将分发与上下文混淆了，这是一种值得注意的、经常出现的干扰项模式。
Option D confuses distribution with context, which is worth noticing as a recurring distractor shape.

2573
03:42:27,502 --> 03:42:28,452
场景 4
Scenario 4

2574
03:42:29,326 --> 03:42:35,364
一个平台团队维护着一个在 11 个服务仓库中通用一致的发布工作流。
A platform team maintains a release workflow used identically across 11 service repositories.

2575
03:42:35,568 --> 03:42:40,996
它由三个技能、一个工具使用前钩子和一个 MCP 服务器配置组成。
It consists of three skins, a pre-tool use hook and an MCP server configuration.

2576
03:42:41,742 --> 03:42:45,728
目前它被复制粘贴到每个仓库的 .clot 目录中。
Today it is copy-pasted into each repository's.plot directory.

2577
03:42:46,158 --> 03:42:51,492
更新需要提交 11 个拉取请求，且已有三个仓库已过时。
Updates require 11 pull requests and three repositories are already out of date.

2578
03:42:52,334 --> 03:42:59,044
他们该怎么做？a. 将其移至用户级配置，以便每个工程师在任何地方都能使用它。
What should they do? a move it to user level configuration so each engineer has it everywhere.

2579
03:42:59,408 --> 03:43:03,428
b. 将其打包成插件并安装到每个仓库中。
b package it as a plugin and install it in each repository.

2580
03:43:04,142 --> 03:43:04,368
C。
C.

2581
03:43:04,814 --> 03:43:10,020
把它放入共享仓库，并在每个 clot.md 中通过 at-path 引用来导入。
Put it in a shared repository and import it with an add path reference from each clot.md.

2582
03:43:10,608 --> 03:43:10,928
D。
D.

2583
03:43:11,342 --> 03:43:13,828
将其移动到企业管理的设置文件中。
Move it into the enterprise managed settings file.

2584
03:43:14,318 --> 03:43:15,332
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2585
03:43:21,070 --> 03:43:24,928
答案是 B，题干在第一段就给出了提示。
The answer is B and the STEM hands it to you in the first paragraph.

2586
03:43:25,168 --> 03:43:32,260
三个技能、一个钩子和 MCP 服务器配置，这几乎就是插件的定义。
Three skills a hook and MCP server configuration is the definition of a plugin almost word for word.

2587
03:43:32,768 --> 03:43:39,204
选项 C 是值得好好理解的一个，因为导入是真实存在的机制，而且感觉像是共享。
Option C is the one worth understanding properly because imports are a real mechanism and they feel like sharing.

2588
03:43:39,822 --> 03:43:44,208
at-path 导入会将记忆文件内容拉入上下文。
An at path import pulls memory file content into context.

2589
03:43:44,494 --> 03:43:51,652
它既不分发钩子，也不分发 MCP 配置，所以它只能涵盖这组选项中的三分之一。
It does not distribute a hook and it does not distribute MCP configuration, so it would cover perhaps a third of this bundle.

2590
03:43:52,814 --> 03:43:56,484
选项 A 把问题从 11 个仓库转移到了每一个工程师身上。
Option A moves the problem from 11 repositories to every engineer.

2591
03:43:57,230 --> 03:44:04,708
选项 D 试图用政策层来解决分发问题，这在正确的规模下选错了工具。
Option D reaches for the policy layer to solve a distribution problem, which is the wrong tool at the right scale.

2592
03:44:06,222 --> 03:44:07,204
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

2593
03:44:07,758 --> 03:44:10,788
一个团队有一个部署到预发布环境的技能。
A team has a skill that deploys to staging.

2594
03:44:11,118 --> 03:44:13,668
它有副作用，且耗时约 4 分钟。
It has side effects and takes about 4 minutes.

2595
03:44:14,254 --> 03:44:22,180
工程师报告说，Claude 有时会在解析类似「这能在预发布环境运行吗？」这样的问题后，自动将其视为部署请求并执行该技能。
Engineers report that Lord sometimes invokes it on its own after interpreting a question like Would this work on staging as a request to deploy?

2596
03:44:22,926 --> 03:44:26,116
他们仍希望能够通过斜杠命令来手动运行它。
They still want to be able to run it themselves with a slash command.

2597
03:44:26,446 --> 03:44:27,888
正确的配置是什么？
What is the correct configuration?

2598
03:44:28,142 --> 03:44:37,408
a 设置 user_invocable 为 false。b 设置 disable_model_invocation 为 true。c 添加一个阻止部署命令的预工具使用钩子。
a set user invocable false. b set disable model invocation true. C. Add a pre tool use hook that blocks the deploy command.

2599
03:44:37,728 --> 03:44:38,048
D。
D.

2600
03:44:38,368 --> 03:44:41,412
重写描述，让 Claude 匹配它的频率降低。
Rewrite the description so Cloud matches it less often.

2601
03:44:41,888 --> 03:44:43,620
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2602
03:44:48,942 --> 03:44:58,020
答案是 B。两个名称相似但含义相反的前置内容字段，而场景明确告诉了你要移除哪种调用者。
The answer is B Two front matter fields with similar names and opposite meanings, and the scenario tells you exactly which invoker to remove.

2603
03:44:58,894 --> 03:45:02,692
Claude 不应该触发它，而工程师应该保留他们的斜杠命令。
Claude should not trigger it and the engineer should keep their slash command.

2604
03:45:03,950 --> 03:45:06,020
禁用模型调用可以同时做到这两点。
Disable model invocation does both.

2605
03:45:06,926 --> 03:45:16,932
选项 A 是同类字段但指向相反的方向。它会移除斜杆命令，并让 Claude 成为唯一的调用者，同时破坏了两个要求。
Option A is the same field family pointing the other way. It removes the slash command and leaves Claude as the only invoker, failing both requirements at once.

2606
03:45:17,616 --> 03:45:27,524
选项 C 是模块中关于强制执行的教训被误用了，因为钩子无法判断是工程师还是 Claude 发起了部署。所以它会把两者都拦截掉。
Option C is the module's enforcement lesson misapplied since a hook cannot tell whether the engineer or Claude initiated the deploy. So it would block both.

2607
03:45:27,936 --> 03:45:31,620
选项 D 在要求根本不存在的情况下降低了匹配率。
Option D lowers a match rate when the requirement is never.

2608
03:45:32,256 --> 03:45:36,068
模块 10，接下来是关于使用 Claude Code 的内容。
Module 10, next on working with Claude Code.

2609
03:45:37,262 --> 03:45:38,212
模块 10。
Module 10.

2610
03:45:38,656 --> 03:45:42,116
模块 8 和 9 是关于配置 Claude Code 的。
Modules 8 and 9 were about configuring clod code.

2611
03:45:42,414 --> 03:45:43,776
这一部分是关于如何使用它。
This one is about using it.

2612
03:45:44,078 --> 03:45:49,636
计划模式，什么时候该跳过它，以及如何进行迭代，让智能体能判断出自己是否成功。
Plan mode, when to skip it and how to iterate so that the agent can tell whether it has succeeded.

2613
03:45:50,606 --> 03:45:58,404
这里的配置语法较少，更多是考查判断力，这意味着这些问题很难靠记忆来回答，但很容易通过推理来解答。
There is less configuration syntax here and more judgment, which means the questions are harder to answer by recall and easier to answer by reasoning.

2614
03:45:59,886 --> 03:46:01,636
有两个核心概念占据了大部分的分数。
Two ideas carry most of the marks.

2615
03:46:02,542 --> 03:46:05,764
计划模式是一个权限边界，而不是一种提示词工程风格。
Plan mode is a permission boundary rather than a style of prompting.

2616
03:46:06,702 --> 03:46:09,988
而且验证过程需要模型之外的干预。
And verification needs something outside the model.

2617
03:46:11,406 --> 03:46:14,816
首先从大多数关于计划模式的描述所忽略的事实开始。
Start with the fact that most descriptions of plan mode miss.

2618
03:46:15,216 --> 03:46:19,616
它不是一种提示词风格，也不是一种要求它先思考的礼貌请求。
It is not a prompting style and it is not a polite request to think first.

2619
03:46:20,096 --> 03:46:24,932
它是 Claude Code 的权限模式之一，且它的权限是只读的。
It is one of Clot code's permission modes and its permission is reads only.

2620
03:46:25,710 --> 03:46:32,196
修改操作在工具层被拦截了，所以即使 Claude 认为这样做会有帮助，它在计划阶段也无法写入文件。
Edits are blocked at the tool layer so Claude cannot write a file while planning, even if it decides that would be helpful.

2621
03:46:32,736 --> 03:46:37,696
这一个区别就让计划模式从一种生产力习惯变成了一种控制手段。
That single distinction converts plan mode from a productivity habit into a control.

2622
03:46:38,542 --> 03:46:43,940
它属于与权限和钩子同类的范畴，而不是和写得好的提示词放在一起。
It belongs in the same category as permissions and hooks, not alongside a well-written prompt.

2623
03:46:45,582 --> 03:46:48,580
Anthropic 教授的工作流包含四个阶段。
The workflow Anthropic Teaches has four phases.

2624
03:46:49,198 --> 03:46:54,724
探索：Claude 在提出任何建议之前，先阅读相关代码并建立理解。
Explore, where Claude reads the relevant code and builds an understanding before proposing anything.

2625
03:46:55,630 --> 03:46:56,016
计划
Plan

2626
03:46:56,814 --> 03:46:59,812
在此阶段它会生成一个你可以审阅并修改的方案。
where it produces an approach you can review and revise.

2627
03:47:01,198 --> 03:47:04,612
编码：它根据核准的计划进行实现。
Code where it implements against the approved plan.

2628
03:47:05,518 --> 03:47:08,804
以及带上描述性信息的提交和拉取请求。
And commit with a descriptive message and a pull request.

2629
03:47:09,262 --> 03:47:14,820
计划模式涵盖了前两个阶段。它的价值在于提前提醒，这一点值得直白地说明。
Plan mode covers the first two phases. The value is in the call out and it is worth saying plainly.

2630
03:47:15,278 --> 03:47:20,164
你可以在任何东西产生之前提出异议，这是成本最低的异议时机。
You get to disagree before anything exists, which is the cheapest possible moment to disagree.

2631
03:47:21,550 --> 03:47:23,556
有四种进入方式和两种退出方式。
Four ways in and two ways out.

2632
03:47:24,398 --> 03:47:30,736
Shift 和 Tab 可以切换不同的权限模式，比如从默认模式到接受修改，再到计划模式。
Shift and tap cycles through the permission modes, so default, then accept edits, then plan.

2633
03:47:31,662 --> 03:47:35,940
输入 /plan 会在不改变整个会话的情况下，为单次提示词进入该模式。
Slash plan enters it for a single prompt without flipping the whole session.

2634
03:47:36,590 --> 03:47:39,108
权限模式标志位会在开始时就将整个会话置于该模式中。
The permission mode flag starts a session in it.

2635
03:47:39,886 --> 03:47:46,340
设置默认值会让整个项目首先进入计划模式，这是在必须始终进行规划的场景下应选择的选项。
A settings default makes an entire project plan first, which is the one to reach for where planning should always happen.

2636
03:47:46,816 --> 03:47:53,924
退出时，核准一个计划会自动退出计划模式，并进入你核准选项所描述的任何模式。
Coming out, approving a plan exits plan mode automatically and moves you into whichever mode your approval option describes.

2637
03:47:54,574 --> 03:48:01,092
再次按下 Shift 和 Tab 会在不核准的情况下退出，因为进入该模式并不意味着你必须产出一个计划。
And pressing shift and tab again leaves without approving because entering does not commit you to producing a plan.

2638
03:48:02,862 --> 03:48:06,436
现在是决策环节，Anthropic 为此提供了一个判断标准。
Now the decision and anthropic gives you a sentence for it.

2639
03:48:07,694 --> 03:48:11,812
如果你能用一句话准确描述出差异，那就跳过计划。
If you could describe the exact diff in one sentence, skip the plan.

2640
03:48:12,718 --> 03:48:16,164
比如修复拼写错误、添加日志行或重命名变量。
Fixing a typo, adding a log line, renaming a variable.

2641
03:48:16,622 --> 03:48:21,136
对于那些情况，计划纯属额外开销，而且制定计划的时间比修改还要长。
For those, planning is pure overhead and the plan takes longer than the change.

2642
03:48:21,742 --> 03:48:28,740
记住这句话的原文，因为考试确实会考到是否使用计划模式，而“不使用”是一个正确的答案。
Learn that sentence as it is written because the exam does ask whether to use plan mode and no is a real answer.

2643
03:48:29,294 --> 03:48:37,156
对简单任务过度规划浪费的时间，和对复杂任务规划不足浪费的时间是一样的，题目会考查这两个方向。
Over planning a simple task wastes time exactly as much as under planning a complex one does, and the questions test both directions.

2644
03:48:38,894 --> 03:48:40,708
就像表格里展示的一样，这是同样的决策逻辑。
The same decision as a table.

2645
03:48:41,056 --> 03:48:47,588
当修改涉及多个文件、不确定采用什么方法或者代码不熟悉时，就使用计划。
Plan when the change touches several files, when you are unsure of the approach, or when the code is unfamiliar.

2646
03:48:48,078 --> 03:48:53,284
此外，当涉及生产路径或迁移，或者指令模糊不清时，也要用计划。
Also when production paths or migrations are involved or the instruction is ambiguous.

2647
03:48:54,030 --> 03:48:59,716
如果是单个文件且有明显的修改，或者方法已经确定时，就直接开始。
Go straight in when it is one file and one obvious edit or when the approach is not in question.

2648
03:49:00,270 --> 03:49:05,216
还有一种情况是：你上周刚写过这段代码，或者正在对一些小问题进行快速迭代。
Also, when you wrote the code last week or you are iterating tightly on something small.

2649
03:49:05,518 --> 03:49:09,988
有三种力量推动我们去使用计划：不确定性、广度和风险。
Three forces push towards planning uncertainty, breadth, and risk.

2650
03:49:10,510 --> 03:49:11,716
另外有两个因素反对使用计划。
Two push against it.

2651
03:49:12,526 --> 03:49:14,148
那就是清晰度和规模小。
Clarity and smallness.

2652
03:49:15,118 --> 03:49:20,324
这个领域中几乎所有的题目，都是这五行内容加上具体案例的变体。
Almost every question in this area is one of those five rows with a story attached.

2653
03:49:21,902 --> 03:49:25,284
这种对比是该模块对你现在掌握的“何时使用”模式的一种总结。
This comparison is the module's version of a pattern you now know when.

2654
03:49:25,678 --> 03:49:28,768
计划模式是一个边界。在工具层，编辑操作是被拦截的。
Plan mode is a boundary. Edits are blocked at the tool layer.

2655
03:49:28,928 --> 03:49:31,088
Claude 不会自动开始执行代码实现。
Clot cannot quietly start implementing.

2656
03:49:31,374 --> 03:49:35,204
审批是一个明确的门控，而计划是你可以查阅的一个产物。
Approval is an explicit gate and the plan is an artifact you can review.

2657
03:49:36,302 --> 03:49:38,948
要求 Claude 先制定计划是一个请求。
Asking Clot to make a plan first is a request.

2658
03:49:39,598 --> 03:49:45,572
这个请求通常会被遵循，偶尔也不会。这种情况下没有门控，响应会直接进入编辑环节。
It is usually obeyed and occasionally not. There is no gate and the response flows straight on into edits.

2659
03:49:45,998 --> 03:49:48,644
对于低风险的工作，这种请求完全没问题。
For low stakes work, the request is perfectly fine.

2660
03:49:49,008 --> 03:49:56,356
当场景描述为智能体在任何人同意之前就开始编辑时，正确答案是“边界”，而不是更强硬的请求。
When a scenario says the agent started editing before anyone agreed, the approach, the answer is the boundary, not a firmer request.

2661
03:49:57,870 --> 03:50:01,636
把计划当作一个真正的产物，而不仅仅是一个形式。
Treat the plan as a real artifact rather than a formality.

2662
03:50:02,606 --> 03:50:08,516
计划会写入磁盘，因此它们能经受住压缩和会话重启，这在长周期的任务中非常重要。
Plans are written to disk so they survive compaction and session restarts, which matters on a long piece of work.

2663
03:50:09,038 --> 03:50:10,436
在批准之前先进行修改。
Revise before you approve.

2664
03:50:10,958 --> 03:50:16,036
增加步骤、删除步骤或更改顺序，因为目前还没有任何操作发生，修改是免费的。
Add steps, remove steps, change the order because nothing has happened yet and revision is free.

2665
03:50:16,942 --> 03:50:21,412
这就是整个练习的重点，正如强调的那样，值得明确说明。
That is the point of the whole exercise and it is worth stating as the call out does.

2666
03:50:22,030 --> 03:50:24,676
在计划阶段进行纠偏只需要花费一句话。
Course correcting during planning costs you a sentence.

2667
03:50:25,358 --> 03:50:28,420
在执行后进行纠偏则需要重写。
Course correcting after implementation costs a rewrite.

2668
03:50:29,230 --> 03:50:38,608
对于重大功能，计划能提供很好的拉取请求描述，因为审核者可以同时看到意图和实现细节。
And on a significant feature, the plan makes a good pull request description because reviewers can see intent alongside implementation.

2669
03:50:39,950 --> 03:50:45,348
现在是这个模块的另一半内容，关于智能体如何知道自己成功了。
Now the other half of the module, which is about how the agent knows it has succeeded.

2670
03:50:46,030 --> 03:50:49,092
这句话是整个主题如此重要的原因。
This sentence is the reason the whole topic matters.

2671
03:50:49,710 --> 03:50:57,796
如果模型外部没有任何东西来检查工作，那么可用的唯一验证手段就是模型对自身输出的判断。
If there is nothing outside the model to check the work, the only verifier available is the model's own judgment about its own output.

2672
03:50:58,702 --> 03:51:06,724
这种判断并不差，但随着上下文窗口填满，它的效果就会下降，而这正是长会话中容易受损的一环。
That judgment is not terrible, but it degrades as the context window fills, and it is exactly the thing that is compromised on a long session.

2673
03:51:07,470 --> 03:51:13,188
所以目标是给循环提供一个无论工作多久都能保持准确的判定源。
So the goal is to give the loop an oracle that stays accurate no matter how long you have been working.

2674
03:51:14,894 --> 03:51:17,636
这是本模块中最有用的单一习惯。
Here is the most useful single habit in this module.

2675
03:51:18,222 --> 03:51:25,668
在给定 Bug 描述的情况下，Claude 必须推断出具体的故障点，而成功的判断是基于阅读代码并形成主观意见。
Given a description of a bug, Claude has to infer the exact failure, and success gets judged by reading the code and forming an opinion.

2676
03:51:26,638 --> 03:51:31,044
在给出一个失败的测试用例时，故障是明确且可复现的。
Given a failing test, the failure is unambiguous and reproducible.

2677
03:51:31,566 --> 03:51:36,996
成功意味着通过运行（变绿），而不是一种主观判断，而且循环会基于证据而终止。
Success is a green run rather than an opinion, and the loop terminates on evidence.

2678
03:51:37,710 --> 03:51:42,532
测试用例还能作为回归保护保留下来，而描述永远做不到这一点。
The test also stays behind as a regression guard, which the description never does.

2679
03:51:43,502 --> 03:51:45,860
这个要点是需要带到考试中的内容。
The callout is the thing to carry into the exam.

2680
03:51:46,734 --> 03:51:50,608
失败的测试将「这看起来对吗？」转换成了「它通过了吗？」。
A failing test converts does this look right into, did it pass?

2681
03:51:50,862 --> 03:51:53,828
而这两个问题具有不同的可靠性。
And those are different questions with different reliability.

2682
03:51:55,246 --> 03:51:56,644
实际中的循环操作。
The loop in practice.

2683
03:51:57,491 --> 03:52:01,871
先写测试，或者让 Claude 写一个能复现问题的测试。
Write the test first, or ask Claude to write one that reproduces the problem.

2684
03:52:02,382 --> 03:52:07,076
在修复任何内容之前，确认它失败了，并且是由于正确的原因而失败。
Confirm it fails and fails for the right reason before anything gets fixed.

2685
03:52:09,168 --> 03:52:11,812
让 Claude 去实现，然后运行测试套件。
Let Claude implement, then run the suite.

2686
03:52:12,718 --> 03:52:16,004
把实际的错误信息反馈回去，而不是用文字描述它们。
Feed the actual failures back rather than describing them.

2687
03:52:16,398 --> 03:52:19,812
因为原始输出比你的总结更能作为证据。
Because the raw output is better evidence than your summary of it.

2688
03:52:20,782 --> 03:52:25,508
而且当测试套件变绿时循环就会结束，这是一个事实而非判断。
And the loop ends when the suite is green, which is a fact rather than a judgment.

2689
03:52:25,998 --> 03:52:28,608
如果这个模式看起来很熟悉，那它确实是这样的。
If that shape looks familiar, it should.

2690
03:52:29,134 --> 03:52:35,396
这是模块核心：收集、思考、验证、重复，并将验证步骤具体化。
This is module once, Gather, hat, verify, repeat with the verification step made concrete.

2691
03:52:37,038 --> 03:52:39,460
同样的技巧可以推广到测试之外的场景。
The same trick generalizes past tests.

2692
03:52:40,718 --> 03:52:49,220
在前端工作中，给 Claude 一个设计模型和一种获取截图的方法。这样它就能对比输出与目标并进行迭代。
On front-end work, give Claude a design mock and a way to take a screenshot. It can then compare its output against the target and iterate.

2693
03:52:50,158 --> 03:52:57,188
Anthropic 报告称这种循环能带来 2 到 3 倍的质量提升，对于这么简单的方法来说，这是一个巨大的效果。
Anthropic reports that loop producing a 2 3 times improvement in quality, which is a large effect for something so simple.

2694
03:52:57,648 --> 03:53:03,652
在数据工作中，对输出进行断言优于描述输出应该长什么样。
On data work, an assertion on the output beats a description of what the output should look like.

2695
03:53:04,398 --> 03:53:11,524
在基础设施方面，一个可以与预期状态进行对比的计划或预演也能起到同样的作用。
On infrastructure, a plan or a dry run that can be diffed against the intended state does the same job.

2696
03:53:13,518 --> 03:53:15,236
这个模式永远不会改变。
The pattern never changes.

2697
03:53:16,302 --> 03:53:19,364
一个模型外部返回通过或失败的结果。
Something outside the model that returns pass or fail.

2698
03:53:20,942 --> 03:53:22,756
输入端的 4 个习惯。
4 habits on the input side.

2699
03:53:23,118 --> 03:53:31,716
当需求模糊时，要求 Claude 在编写任何内容之前先对你进行采访，因为提问的成本低于错误实现的代价。
When a requirement is fuzzy, ask Lord to interview you before writing anything because questions cost less than a wrong implementation.

2700
03:53:32,590 --> 03:53:41,892
使用加号符号引用特定文件作为当前上下文的一部分，而不是将它们添加到记忆文件中，并在标注中注明这种区别。
Reference specific files with an add symbol for one of context rather than adding them to a memory file and note the distinction in the call-out.

2701
03:53:43,022 --> 03:53:48,996
添加引用适用于当前对话，而记忆文件适用于所有对话。
An add reference is for this conversation and a memory file is for every conversation.

2702
03:53:49,998 --> 03:53:57,252
当你有一个可用的参考时就粘贴它，因为 clot 在处理具体示例时比抽象描述效果更好。
Paste a working reference when you have one since plot does better with a concrete example than an abstract description.

2703
03:53:57,710 --> 03:54:03,908
当多个问题纠缠在一起时，按照依赖顺序来修复它们，而不是按你发现它们的顺序。
And when several issues are tangled, fix them in dependency order rather than in the order you happen to notice them.

2704
03:54:05,550 --> 03:54:09,156
有一种反模式值得特别提出来，因为它看起来像是良好的实践。
One anti-pattern is worth naming because it looks like good practice.

2705
03:54:09,614 --> 03:54:15,236
不要用一个拒绝正在进行中的工作的钩子，在实现过程中去拦截编辑或写入。
Do not block edit or write part way through an implementation with a hook that rejects work in progress.

2706
03:54:16,142 --> 03:54:24,036
在写入时拦截会破坏多步骤推理，因为 Claude 会丢失当前序列的位置，必须重新构建。
Blocking at write time breaks multi-step reasoning because Claude loses track of where it was in the sequence and has to reconstruct it.

2707
03:54:24,718 --> 03:54:29,444
让它完成，然后用工具使用后钩子或提交前检查来验证。
Let it finish, then validate with a post-tool use hook or a pre-commit check.

2708
03:54:30,318 --> 03:54:32,772
注意它是如何与模块行并列的。
Note how this sits alongside module line.

2709
03:54:33,550 --> 03:54:39,620
禁止性条款属于工具使用前，而格式或风格规则不属于禁止性条款。
Prohibitions do belong in pre-tool use and a formatting or style rule is not a prohibition.

2710
03:54:40,750 --> 03:54:44,996
预防措施应该放在任务的边界处，而不是在任务中间。
Prevention belongs at the boundary of a task rather than in the middle of one.

2711
03:54:46,734 --> 03:54:47,808
模式识别。
Pattern recognition.

2712
03:54:48,048 --> 03:54:54,180
在任何人同意之前就开始编辑。这种做法意味着计划模式，即边界而非形式或指令。
Started editing before anyone agreed. The approach means plan mode, the boundary rather than a form or instruction.

2713
03:54:54,528 --> 03:55:02,628
单行更改意味着跳过计划。没人能判断是否真的修复了，这意味着需要外部检查，通常是失败的测试。
A one-line change means skip the plan. Nobody can tell whether it is actually fixed, means an external check, usually a failing test.

2714
03:55:03,408 --> 03:55:08,196
一个包含多个文件的陌生代码库，意味着每次都必须使用计划模式。
An unfamiliar code base with a multi-file de factor means plan mode every time.

2715
03:55:08,528 --> 03:55:13,961
在大型更改中途丢失进度，说明你应该寻找一个在任务中途拦截错误的钩子。
Losing track partway through a large change should make you look for a hook blocking rights mid-task.

2716
03:55:14,528 --> 03:55:18,628
而模糊的需求意味着让 Claude 先提问。
And an ambiguous requirement means have Claude ask questions first.

2717
03:55:19,470 --> 03:55:20,928
规模和确定性。
Size and certainty.

2718
03:55:21,088 --> 03:55:25,221
决定哪些是规划问题，证据决定哪些是迭代问题。
Decide the planning questions and evidence decides the iteration ones.

2719
03:55:26,734 --> 03:55:28,228
一个简短的货币检查。
A short currency check.

2720
03:55:28,608 --> 03:55:33,156
进入计划模式的考试时代答案是 Shift 和 Tab。
The exam era answer for entering plan mode is Shift and Tab.

2721
03:55:33,408 --> 03:55:38,884
现在还有其他几种路径，包括斜杠命令和设置默认值。
There are now several other routes in, including a slash command and a settings default.

2722
03:55:39,328 --> 03:55:42,500
规划期间运行的内容现在变得更加微妙。
What runs during planning is now more nuanced.

2723
03:55:42,798 --> 03:55:46,852
读取操作和只读命令集在无需提示的情况下即可执行。
Reads and a read-only command set proceed without prompting.

2724
03:55:47,758 --> 03:55:52,804
在提供自动模式的地方，其他 shell 命令可以交给分类器处理，而不是中断你的操作。
Where auto mode is available, other shell commands can go to a classifier instead of stopping you.

2725
03:55:53,902 --> 03:56:00,260
在 2026 年期间，付费计划的新会话默认权限模式变为自动模式。
An auto mode became the default permission mode for new sessions on paid plans during 2026.

2726
03:56:00,750 --> 03:56:02,852
这些都不会改变可考查的核心内容。
None of that changes the examinable core.

2727
03:56:03,630 --> 03:56:07,172
计划模式是只读的，编辑在工具层被拦截。
Plan mode is read only and edits are blocked at the tool layer.

2728
03:56:08,622 --> 03:56:09,648
5 行。
5 lines.

2729
03:56:10,254 --> 03:56:18,820
计划模式是一种权限模式，因此编辑是在工具层被拦截而非不建议执行。如果你能用一句话描述差异，就跳过计划。
Plan mode is a permission mode, so edits are blocked at the tool layer rather than discouraged. If you could describe the diff in one sentence, skip the plan.

2730
03:56:19,088 --> 03:56:24,868
不确定性、广度和风险倾向于使用规划，而清晰度和小型化则倾向于直接进入。
Uncertainty, breadth and risk favor planning while clarity and smallness favor going straight in.

2731
03:56:25,550 --> 03:56:29,408
失败的测试会让「这看起来对吗？」变成「它通过了吗？"
A failing test turns does this look right into Did it pass?

2732
03:56:29,728 --> 03:56:37,476
而且在没有外部判定源的情况下，智能体会根据自己的判断来评估工作，而这种判断随着会话变长就会不断下降。
And without an external oracle, the agent grades its own work using judgment that degrades exactly as the session gets long.

2733
03:56:38,286 --> 03:56:44,324
现在有五个场景，其中有两个关于是否采用计划模式的决策指向了相反的方向。
Five scenarios now, and two of them are the plan or not decision pointing in opposite directions.

2734
03:56:46,030 --> 03:56:46,884
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

2735
03:56:48,334 --> 03:56:52,928
一名工程师要求 Claude Code 给一个内部 API 添加速率限制。
An engineer asks Claude Code to add rate limiting to an internal API.

2736
03:56:53,088 --> 03:56:54,660
这个代码库对他们来说是全新的。
The code base is new to them.

2737
03:56:55,086 --> 03:57:01,060
这次更改会涉及中间件层、配置架构、三个根处理程序以及测试套件。
The change will touch the middleware layer, the configuration schema, three root handlers, and the test suite.

2738
03:57:01,646 --> 03:57:03,968
Claude 开始立即编辑文件。
Claude begins editing files immediately.

2739
03:57:04,526 --> 03:57:11,396
20 分钟后，工程师意识到它把速率限制器放错了层级，必须撤销这些操作。
Twenty minutes later, the engineer realizes it has put the rate limiter in the wrong layer and the work has to be unpicked.

2740
03:57:12,046 --> 03:57:13,828
他们想防止这种情况再次发生。
They want to prevent this recurring.

2741
03:57:14,382 --> 03:57:15,492
他们应该改动什么？
What should they change?

2742
03:57:16,302 --> 03:57:18,884
a 在 plot.m 中添加一行。
a add a line to plot.m.

2743
03:57:19,438 --> 03:57:22,788
d 告诉 Claude 在做出更改前先提议一个方案。
d Telling Claude to propose an approach before making changes.

2744
03:57:23,488 --> 03:57:23,728
b。
b.

2745
03:57:24,334 --> 03:57:29,316
对于这类变动，使用计划模式，并在开始执行前批准该计划。
Use plan mode for changes of the shape and approve the plan before implementation begins.

2746
03:57:29,728 --> 03:57:34,052
c. 在提示词中要求 Claude 在开始前解释它的方法。
C. Ask Claude to explain its approach in the prompt before it starts.

2747
03:57:34,528 --> 03:57:34,768
d。
D.

2748
03:57:35,406 --> 03:57:39,236
添加一个工具调用前的钩子，在存在计划文件之前阻止编辑。
Add a pre tool use hook blocking edit until a plan file exists.

2749
03:57:39,854 --> 03:57:40,964
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2750
03:57:46,638 --> 03:57:47,684
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2751
03:57:48,110 --> 03:57:51,588
第一段同时包含了三个计划触发点。
The first paragraph contains three planning triggers at once.

2752
03:57:52,526 --> 03:57:59,364
代码库不熟悉、更改涉及多个文件，且最终的方法也存在争议。
The code base is unfamiliar, the change touches several files, and the approach turned out to be arguable.

2753
03:58:00,208 --> 03:58:09,636
计划模式正是为这种组合而设计的机制，而且至关重要的一点是，编辑在获得批准前会被拦截，而不仅仅是受到劝阻。
Plan mode is the mechanism built for exactly that combination, and crucially, the edits are blocked until approval rather than merely discouraged.

2754
03:58:11,982 --> 03:58:18,884
选项 D 是一个有趣的错误答案，因为它追求强制执行，而这门课程教导我们要优先考虑这种做法。
Option D is the interesting wrong answer because it leaches for enforcement, which this course has trained you to prefer.

2755
03:58:19,808 --> 03:58:22,180
但它是糟糕的强制执行。
It is enforcement aimed badly.

2756
03:58:23,054 --> 03:58:30,276
在任务中途拦截编辑的钩子会中断正在进行的权利，从而破坏了它本应保护的多步推理。
A hook blocking edit interrupts rights mid-task, which breaks the multi-step reasoning it was supposed to protect.

2757
03:58:31,374 --> 03:58:36,688
选项 A 和 C 是在两个地方提出了相同的请求，且两者都没有效果。
Options A and C are the same request in two places and neither gets anything.

2758
03:58:37,550 --> 03:58:38,436
场景 2。
Scenario 2.

2759
03:58:40,270 --> 03:58:44,388
同一位工程师现在在设置中将计划模式设为项目的默认值。
The same engineer now sets plan mode as the project default in settings.

2760
03:58:45,294 --> 03:58:52,100
在接下来的一个星期里，重命名一个变量、添加一行日志以及修正一个拼写错误，每一个操作都会生成一个包含三段内容的计划。
Over the following week, renaming a variable, adding a log line, and correcting a typo each produce a three paragraph plan.

2761
03:58:52,368 --> 03:58:54,212
他们必须阅读并批准每一个。
They have to read and approve every one.

2762
03:58:55,150 --> 03:58:58,180
他们估计每天产生的额外工作量大约是几分钟。
They estimate the overhead at several minutes a day.

2763
03:58:58,528 --> 03:58:59,620
他们该怎么做？
What should they do?

2764
03:59:00,366 --> 03:59:04,388
a. 保留默认设置，因为有计划总是比没计划更安全。
a keep the default since planning is always safer than not planning.

2765
03:59:04,928 --> 03:59:10,448
b. 移除默认设置，并针对值得进行规划的更改，有意识地进入计划模式。
b. Remove the default and enter plan mode deliberately for changes that warrant it.

2766
03:59:10,990 --> 03:59:16,132
c. 保留默认设置，但指示 QARD 为小的更改生成更短的计划。
C. Keep the default but instruct QARD to produce shorter plans for small changes.

2767
03:59:16,622 --> 03:59:20,288
d. 完全移除计划模式，并依靠审查差异。
D. Remove plan mode entirely and rely on reviewing the diff.

2768
03:59:20,814 --> 03:59:21,988
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2769
03:59:27,662 --> 03:59:30,244
答案是 b，这就是这一对题。
The answer is B and this is the pair.

2770
03:59:30,768 --> 03:59:36,036
同样的工程师，同样的工具，但因为更改的大小发生了变化，所以答案相反。
Same engineer, same tool, opposite answer because the size of the change flipped.

2771
03:59:37,934 --> 03:59:42,852
选项 a 是大多数人默认采取的立场，它把规划当成免费的。
Option A is the position most people default to and it treats planning as free.

2772
03:59:43,470 --> 03:59:44,292
它并不是免费的。
It is not.

2773
03:59:45,102 --> 03:59:51,748
Anthropic 的官方指南明确指出，如果你能用一句话描述差异，就应该跳过计划。
Anthropic's own guidance is explicit that if you could describe the diff in one sentence, you should skip the plan.

2774
03:59:52,430 --> 04:00:00,516
选项 d 过度修正到了问题场景中，即之前描述的情况，而那个工程师确实需要为速率限制器进行规划。
Option D overcorrects into the problem scenario, one described, and that engineer genuinely needed planning for the rate limiter.

2775
04:00:01,326 --> 04:00:08,196
选项 c 是一个折中方案，它保留了审批步骤，而这正是大部分摩擦所在的地方。
Option C is the compromise that keeps the approval step, which is where most of the friction actually lives.

2776
04:00:10,062 --> 04:00:16,516
注意考试会测试这两个方向，并期望你能从容地对不需要的计划说“不”。
Notice that the exam will test both directions and expects you to be comfortable saying no to planning.

2777
04:00:18,190 --> 04:00:19,268
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

2778
04:00:19,758 --> 04:00:22,084
一个团队报告了一个间歇性 Bug。
A team reports an intermittent bug.

2779
04:00:22,288 --> 04:00:26,608
在某些条件下，一个定时任务会处理两次相同的记录。
Under some conditions, a scheduled job processes the same record twice.

2780
04:00:26,928 --> 04:00:30,692
他们向 Claude code 描述了症状并要求它修复。
They describe the symptom to Claude code and ask it to fix it.

2781
04:00:31,168 --> 04:00:34,532
Claude 进行了一项合理的更改并报告问题已解决。
Claude makes a plausible change and reports the issue resolved.

2782
04:00:34,768 --> 04:00:36,580
两天后，问题再次出现。
Two days later it recurs.

2783
04:00:37,390 --> 04:00:40,848
这种情况已经伴随三种不同的更改发生了三次。
This has now happened three times with three different changes.

2784
04:00:41,088 --> 04:00:43,728
他们工作流程中最有效的改进是什么？
What is the most effective change to how they work?

2785
04:00:44,174 --> 04:00:47,808
a. 给 Claude 提供更多关于问题发生条件的细节。
a give Claude more detail about the conditions under which it occurs.

2786
04:00:48,142 --> 04:00:54,052
b. 编写一个能重现重复处理问题的测试，并在修复前要求该测试失败。
b. Write a test that reproduces the double processing and require it to fail before any fix.

2787
04:00:54,798 --> 04:00:55,008
c。
C.

2788
04:00:55,568 --> 04:00:59,428
使用计划模式，以便在实施前审查方案。
Use plan mode so the approach is reviewed before implementation.

2789
04:01:00,046 --> 04:01:04,228
d. 在接受修复之前，要求 Claude 解释为什么它的修复是有效的。
D. Ask Claude to explain why its fix works before accepting it.

2790
04:01:04,910 --> 04:01:06,020
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2791
04:01:11,790 --> 04:01:12,868
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2792
04:01:13,408 --> 04:01:17,156
需要注意的短语是：Claude 报告问题已解决。
The phrase to notice is that Claude reports the issue resolved.

2793
04:01:17,648 --> 04:01:23,812
这是模型自我评估，没有任何外部因素在核查，而且它现在已经连续失败三次了。
That is self-assessment with nothing outside the model checking it, and it has now failed three times running.

2794
04:01:24,528 --> 04:01:31,008
选项 D 是最具误导性的错误答案，因为要求解释听起来像是某种验证。
Option D is the most instructive wrong answer because asking for an explanation feels like verification.

2795
04:01:31,566 --> 04:01:32,368
但事实并非如此。
It is not.

2796
04:01:32,718 --> 04:01:40,388
对错误的修复给出自信的解释正是这个团队已经收到过三次的内容，第四次同样会让人信以为真。
A confident explanation of a wrong fix is precisely what this team has already received three times, and a fourth will be equally convincing.

2797
04:01:40,848 --> 04:01:47,844
选项 A 用更多的文字重复了失败的方法。选项 C 则是在审查一个没人知道是错误的方法。
Option A repeats the method that failed with more words. Option C would review an approach nobody knew was wrong.

2798
04:01:48,366 --> 04:01:53,412
只有 B 引入了模型之外的、能够返回事实的东西。
Only B introduces something outside the model that can return a fact.

2799
04:01:54,830 --> 04:01:55,908
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

2800
04:01:56,750 --> 04:02:00,548
一名工程师要求 Claude Code 清理报告模块。
An engineer asks Claude code to clean up the reporting module.

2801
04:02:01,230 --> 04:02:09,828
Claude 花费了 15 分钟进行更改，重命名函数、提取辅助工具、重新排列方法并重写注释。
Claude spends 15 minutes making changes, renaming functions, extracting helpers, reordering methods, rewriting comments.

2802
04:02:10,414 --> 04:02:12,420
但这些都不是工程师想要的。
None of it is what the engineer wanted.

2803
04:02:12,782 --> 04:02:16,324
他们的本意是移除三个未使用的报告类型。
They had meant remove the three unused report types.

2804
04:02:17,134 --> 04:02:19,248
他们希望避免这种不匹配的情况。
They want to avoid this kind of mismatch.

2805
04:02:19,598 --> 04:02:21,636
最有效的习惯是什么？
What is the most effective habit to adopt?

2806
04:02:22,094 --> 04:02:32,132
a. 当请求含义模糊时，让 Claude 在执行前提出澄清问题。b. 添加一个 clot.md 部分，定义对该团队而言“清理”意味着什么。
a have Claude ask clarifying questions before implementing when a request is open-ended. b add a clot.md section defining what cleanup means for this team.

2807
04:02:32,910 --> 04:02:33,168
C。
C.

2808
04:02:33,488 --> 04:02:37,540
始终使用计划模式，这样误解就会在计划阶段暴露出来。
Always use plan mode so the misunderstanding surfaces in the plan.

2809
04:02:38,062 --> 04:02:38,368
d。
d.

2810
04:02:38,768 --> 04:02:42,020
在接受更改之前更仔细地检查差异。
Review the diff more carefully before accepting changes.

2811
04:02:43,726 --> 04:02:44,836
停下来思考并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

2812
04:02:50,542 --> 04:02:55,204
答案是 A，而选项 C 足够接近，值得详细解释一下。
The answer is A, and option C is close enough to deserve a proper explanation.

2813
04:02:55,840 --> 04:03:04,868
计划模式确实能让这种误解暴露出来，因为计划中会描述重命名和提取操作，工程师就会提出异议。
Plan Mode genuinely would have surfaced this misunderstanding because the plan would have described renaming and extracting, and the engineer would have objected.

2814
04:03:05,710 --> 04:03:16,000
A 比 C 更好的原因是选项 C 中包含了“始终”这个词，这会导致陷入场景 2 中的过度规划陷阱。这里的根本问题是歧义而非计划不足。
What makes A better is the word always in option C, which walks into the over planning trap from scenario 2. The root problem here is ambiguity rather than planning.

2815
04:03:16,160 --> 04:03:20,260
两个澄清问题无需任何流程就能在几秒钟内发现问题。
Two clarifying questions would have caught it in seconds without any process at all.

2816
04:03:20,750 --> 04:03:30,052
选项 B 只解决了一个短语，下一个模糊请求仍会使用不同的词汇。选项 D 则是在浪费了 15 分钟后才发现问题。
Option B fixes one phrase and the next vague request will use a different one. Option D catches the problem after 15 wasted minutes.

2817
04:03:31,630 --> 04:03:32,612
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

2818
04:03:33,198 --> 04:03:41,092
一个团队在写入和编辑时使用了 pre-tour 钩子，如果文件包含待办事项注释就会被拒绝，以保持代码库整洁。
A team has a pre-tour use hook on write and edit that rejects any file containing a to-do comment to keep the code base clean.

2819
04:03:41,774 --> 04:03:50,720
工程师报告称，在涉及多个文件的重大更改中，clot 会变得混乱，有时会退回到之前的步骤或丢失对已完成内容的追踪。
Engineers report that during large multifile changes, plot gets confused, sometimes reverting to earlier steps or losing track of what it has already

2820
04:03:50,720 --> 04:03:54,020
在单文件编辑时，它运行正常。
done. It works fine on single file edits.

2821
04:03:54,480 --> 04:03:58,084
在典型的重大变更过程中，该钩子会触发多次。
The hook fires several times during a typical large change.

2822
04:03:59,310 --> 04:04:01,700
根本原因是什么？他们应该怎么做？
What is the root cause and what should they do?

2823
04:04:02,734 --> 04:04:04,868
A. 上下文窗口正在填满。
a The context window is filling.

2824
04:04:05,040 --> 04:04:07,748
所以对于大型变更，使用上下文分叉。
So use context fork for large changes.

2825
04:04:08,654 --> 04:04:10,240
B. 阻塞写入。
b blocking writes.

2826
04:04:10,400 --> 04:04:15,760
任务中途中断了多步骤推理。因此应将检查移至工具使用后或提交前。
Mid-task breaks multi-step reasoning. So move the check to post tool use or pre-commit.

2827
04:04:16,560 --> 04:04:19,780
C. 钩子太慢，所以将其设为异步。
C. The hook is too slow, so make it asynchronous.

2828
04:04:20,910 --> 04:04:25,796
D. Claude 需要在 Claude.md 中加入待办事项规则，这样它就会停止编写这些内容。
D Claude needs the to-do rule in Claude.md, so it stops writing them.

2829
04:04:28,750 --> 04:04:29,860
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

2830
04:04:35,600 --> 04:04:37,360
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2831
04:04:37,678 --> 04:04:42,880
关键的判断细节是：单文件编辑没问题，但多文件更改有问题。
The deciding detail is that single file edits are fine and multi-file changes are not.

2832
04:04:43,054 --> 04:04:50,880
这排除了任何关于数量或上下文的解释，因为如果窗口是问题所在，单文件编辑也会出现性能下降。
That rules out any explanation about volume or context because a single file edit would degrade too if the window were the problem.

2833
04:04:51,726 --> 04:04:59,840
不同之处在于，多文件更改是一个序列，每一次被拒绝的写入都会中断它，导致 Claude
What differs is that a multi-file change is a sequence and every rejected write interrupts it, leaving clot

2834
04:05:00,000 --> 04:05:01,828
不得不重新构建它进行到了哪一步。
to reconstruct where it had got to.

2835
04:05:03,662 --> 04:05:11,140
选项 A 是最强的干扰项，因为大型变更中确实存在上下文压力，但它无法解释与钩子触发之间的相关性。
Option A is the strongest distractor because context pressure is real on large changes and it does not explain the correlation with the hook firing.

2836
04:05:12,014 --> 04:05:15,684
选项 C 在保留表象的同时去除了控制。
Option C removes the control while keeping the appearance of one.

2837
04:05:16,080 --> 04:05:18,596
模块 11，接下来是 Claude Code。
Module 11 next clod code.

2838
04:05:19,200 --> 04:05:20,932
在 CI 和 C D。
In CI and C D.

2839
04:05:22,542 --> 04:05:23,876
模块 11 结束。
Module 11 closes.

2840
04:05:24,270 --> 04:05:28,324
领域 3，在没有人的流水线中运行 Claude Code。
Domain 3, clod code in a pipeline with no human present.

2841
04:05:29,070 --> 04:05:31,920
这本身就是六个考试场景之一。
This is one of the six exam scenarios in its own right.

2842
04:05:32,080 --> 04:05:35,300
所以如果你去考，你会从这些材料中看到好几个问题。
So if you draw it, you will get several questions from this material.

2843
04:05:36,718 --> 04:05:41,120
核心思路很简单，它能解释我们将要查看的每一个标志。
The organizing idea is simple and it explains every flag we will look at.

2844
04:05:41,646 --> 04:05:42,500
交互式。
Interactive.

2845
04:05:43,054 --> 04:05:50,980
Claude Code 有人在不察觉的情况下承担三项工作。无头模式下的 Claude Code 则没有。因此，这三项工作必须移入配置中。
Clot code has a human doing three jobs without noticing. Headless clot code does not. So those three jobs have to move into configuration.

2846
04:05:51,360 --> 04:05:53,316
这里的每一项都属于那三项中的一项。
Everything here is one of those three.

2847
04:05:54,894 --> 04:06:00,260
当你与 Claude Code 进行交互式操作时，你是在不经意间承担着三项工作。
When you sit with Claude Code interactively, you are doing three jobs without thinking about them.

2848
04:06:00,942 --> 04:06:04,708
通过批准或拒绝每项操作来授予权限。
Granting permission by approving or refusing each action.

2849
04:06:05,454 --> 04:06:09,636
通过判断工作是否完成且质量合格来判定完成情况。
Judging completion by deciding whether the work is finished and any good.

2850
04:06:10,574 --> 04:06:17,892
以及通过察觉它是否在循环、走错路或开始消耗超出预期的成本来监控问题。
And watching for trouble by noticing when it loops or takes a wrong turn or starts costing more than you expected.

2851
04:06:18,958 --> 04:06:22,020
去掉人工参与后，这三项都变成了配置。
Take the human away and all three become configuration.

2852
04:06:22,574 --> 04:06:24,900
而且重要的后果在于最后一行。
And the important consequence is the last line.

2853
04:06:25,934 --> 04:06:29,860
如果你没配置其中一项任务，它就根本不会执行。
If you have not configured one of those jobs, it is not being done at all.

2854
04:06:30,766 --> 04:06:33,280
没人会默默帮你补位。
Nobody is quietly covering for you.

2855
04:06:34,638 --> 04:06:37,040
这六个标志位涵盖了几乎所有的内容。
Six flags carry almost all of it.

2856
04:06:37,611 --> 04:06:41,791
Dash p 是打印模式，它在非交互模式下运行一次并退出。
Dash p is print mode which runs once non-interactively and exits.

2857
04:06:42,414 --> 04:06:51,204
输出格式 JSON 会给你一个机器可读的对象，包含结果、成本、耗时、会话 ID 和停止原因。
Output format JSON gives you a machine readable object containing the result, the cost, the duration, the session ID, and the stop reason.

2858
04:06:52,910 --> 04:06:55,108
最大轮数限制了智能体的步骤。
Max turns caps the agentic steps.

2859
04:06:56,110 --> 04:06:59,844
以美元计价的最大预算限制了该次调用的支出。
Max budget in dollars caps the spend for that invocation.

2860
04:07:00,302 --> 04:07:05,156
允许工具定义了工具范围以及它不能调用或做到的内容。
Allow tools defines the tool surface and what it cannot call it cannot do.

2861
04:07:05,998 --> 04:07:09,188
追加系统提示词会在默认设置中添加指令。
An append system prompt adds instructions to the default.

2862
04:07:09,902 --> 04:07:11,652
还有一项值得了解的机制。
One more mechanic worth knowing.

2863
04:07:12,494 --> 04:07:17,988
管道标准输入在提示词之前变成上下文，这就是差异信息进入运行过程的方式。
Piped standard input becomes context before the prompt, which is how a diff gets into the run.

2864
04:07:19,584 --> 04:07:23,716
输出格式值得单独用一页来讲，因为这个选择会产生后果。
Output format deserves its own slide because the choice has consequences.

2865
04:07:24,174 --> 04:07:30,724
文本输出是纯文本，对人类来说没问题，但对解析器来说很差，且不能作为决策的基础。
Text output is prose, which is fine for a human and poor for a parser and useless as the basis for a decision.

2866
04:07:31,246 --> 04:07:36,068
JSON 会提供结果以及元数据，包括成本和停止原因。
JSON gives you the result together with metadata, including the cost and the stop reason.

2867
04:07:36,910 --> 04:07:43,300
这个停止原因是你的流水线用来判断结束状态的，这是模块 4 中关于构建系统的课程内容。
That stop reason is how your pipeline classifies the ending, which is module 4's lesson arriving in a build system.

2868
04:07:43,584 --> 04:07:48,388
这也是如果你后续阶段需要继续执行时，捕获会话 ID 的地方。
And this is also where you capture the session ID if a later stage needs to resume.

2869
04:07:49,870 --> 04:07:50,944
看这个特别提醒。
Read the call-out.

2870
04:07:51,694 --> 04:07:58,340
只消耗优点信息的流水线就丢弃了所有关于运行如何结束的必要信息。
A pipeline consuming only the pros has thrown away everything it needed to know about how the run ended.

2871
04:07:59,726 --> 04:08:05,220
两个名字相似但效果迥异的标志，考试会考查其中的区别。
Two similarly name flags with very different effects, and the exam does test the difference.

2872
04:08:05,664 --> 04:08:15,428
追加系统提示词会在 Claude Code 的默认设置之上添加你的指令。因此关于工具使用、安全和环境的内置指导都会保留。
Append system prompt adds your instructions on top of Claude Code's default. So the built-in guidance about tool usage, safety, and the environment all stays.

2873
04:08:16,302 --> 04:08:24,100
替换系统提示词会彻底移除默认内容，包括那些你不知道存在的片段，然后你就得负责全部内容了。
Replace system prompt removes the default entirely, including the parts you did not know were there, and you become responsible for all of it.

2874
04:08:24,544 --> 04:08:29,316
追加几乎总是你的首选，特别是在没有人监控的流水线中。
Append is almost always what you want, particularly in a pipeline where nobody is watching.

2875
04:08:29,984 --> 04:08:33,424
替换是用于有意识且经过测试的自定义。
Replace is for deliberate tested customization.

2876
04:08:33,870 --> 04:08:39,460
两个替换标志是互斥的，而追加可以与其中任何一个结合使用。
The two replace flags are mutually exclusive and append can be combined with either.

2877
04:08:41,198 --> 04:08:47,908
这一页讲的是精确性而非趣味性，但它很重要，因为题目会利用这种混淆点。
This slide is precision rather than excitement, and it is worth it because questions exploit the confusion.

2878
04:08:48,691 --> 04:08:52,772
Claude.md 作为用户消息添加到默认系统提示词之后。
Claude.md is added as a user message following the default system prompt.

2879
04:08:53,518 --> 04:08:57,188
追加系统提示词是追加到系统提示词本身。
Append system prompt appends to the system prompt itself.

2880
04:08:58,126 --> 04:09:02,852
它们两个都不会修改 Claude Code 的默认提示词，只有替换标志才会这样做。
Neither of them edits Claude code's default prompt and only the replace flag does that.

2881
04:09:03,184 --> 04:09:09,028
这三个机制在请求中处于不同的位置，所以它们不能互换。
Three mechanisms occupying three different positions in the request, which is why they are not interchangeable.

2882
04:09:10,030 --> 04:09:12,132
注意流水线的最后一行。
And note the last line for a pipeline.

2883
04:09:13,024 --> 04:09:16,644
你的记忆文件在每次运行中都会被读取。
Your memory file is read on every single run.

2884
04:09:16,864 --> 04:09:21,504
所以在繁忙的仓库中，这是一个真实的持续成本。
So on a busy repository, it is a real recurring cost.

2885
04:09:23,182 --> 04:09:28,164
轮数限制代替了监控问题的真人，而且第一行有个陷阱。
Caps replace the human watching for trouble, and there is a trap in the first line.

2886
04:09:30,094 --> 04:09:35,844
在打印模式下，最大轮数没有默认限制，所以如果你省略这个标志，就完全没有上限。
In print mode, max turns has no default limit, so if you omit the flag, there is no ceiling at all.

2887
04:09:37,006 --> 04:09:42,340
3 到 8 轮适合大多数审查任务，足以让系统在不犹豫的情况下完成阅读和推理。
3 to 8 turns suits most review tasks, which is enough to read and reason without wondering.

2888
04:09:43,118 --> 04:09:49,348
以美元计价的最大预算限制了每次调用的支出，它是当轮次便宜但耗时较长时的最后防线。
Max budget in dollars cap spent per invocation and is the backstop for when turns are cheap but long.

2889
04:09:49,824 --> 04:09:53,476
再加上一个工作流层级的超时作为第二个独立的保障。
And add a workflow level timeout as a second independent layer.

2890
04:09:54,478 --> 04:09:56,580
这个提示是实用的见解。
The callout is the practical insight.

2891
04:09:57,550 --> 04:10:07,424
成本超支几乎总是源于某个范围定义不明确的任务需要比预期多得多的迭代，而不是因为运行次数过多。
Cost overruns almost always come from one badly scoped task needing far more iterations than anyone expected, rather than from the number of runs.

2892
04:10:08,704 --> 04:10:13,344
权限是三个人工环节中的第一个，这里有一个特定的坑。
Permissions are the first of the three human jobs, and there is a specific gotcha.

2893
04:10:13,824 --> 04:10:19,524
在普通的无头模式运行中，权限请求钩子不会触发，因为没有人在那等待提示。
Permission request hooks do not fire in a plain headless run because there is nobody to prompt.

2894
04:10:20,238 --> 04:10:26,436
所以真正起作用的控制手段是允许使用的工具和预工具使用钩子，它们无论如何都会触发。
So the controls that do work are allowed tools and pre-tooled use hooks, which fire regardless.

2895
04:10:27,406 --> 04:10:33,584
对于只读审查，允许读取、grip 和 glob，不要允许任何写入或执行 shell 命令的操作。
For a read-only review, allow read, grip, and glob and nothing that writes or runs shell commands.

2896
04:10:33,744 --> 04:10:40,292
跳过权限标志仅适用于隔离的临时容器，绝不能用于任何重要的机器。
The skip permissions flag belongs only in an isolated ephemeral container and never on a machine that matters.

2897
04:10:40,624 --> 04:10:42,468
这个提示是核心原则。
The callout is the principle.

2898
04:10:43,310 --> 04:10:49,188
权限提示曾是一个控制点，移除人工环节就会移除它，除非你特意去替换它。
The permission prompt was a control, and removing the human removes it unless you replace it deliberately.

2899
04:10:50,830 --> 04:10:56,836
现在是第二个人工环节：判断是否完成，这也是流水线经常出错的地方。
Now, the second human job, judging completion, and this is where pipelines go quietly wrong.

2900
04:10:57,104 --> 04:11:04,996
无头模式运行可能以状态码 0 退出，产生空结果或无关结果，并被下游的所有环节记录为成功。
A headless run can exit with status 0, produce an empty or irrelevant result, and be recorded as a success by everything downstream.

2901
04:11:05,806 --> 04:11:10,404
没人会注意到这一点，因为流水线的初衷就是不需要有人盯着。
Nobody notices because the whole point of the pipeline was that nobody is watching.

2902
04:11:10,704 --> 04:11:13,188
这是模块 4 的确定性结果。
This is module 4's guaranteed outcomes.

2903
04:11:13,870 --> 04:11:17,156
构建系统中的问题，而解决方法是相同的。
Problem in a build system, and the fix is the same one.

2904
04:11:17,664 --> 04:11:23,492
你的流水线必须对运行如何结束进行分类，而不是假设只要没崩溃就意味着成功。
Your pipeline has to classify how the run ended rather than assuming that not crashing means it worked.

2905
04:11:25,102 --> 04:11:26,436
所以要正确地进行分类。
So classify properly.

2906
04:11:26,830 --> 04:11:31,492
从 JSON 中读取停止原因，而不是仅依赖于退出码。
Read the stop reason out of the JSON rather than relying on the exit code alone.

2907
04:11:32,622 --> 04:11:35,812
达到轮数限制属于“关于”而非“完成”。
Hitting the turn cap is an about rather than a completion.

2908
04:11:36,494 --> 04:11:40,292
审查是不完整的，绝不能当作最终结果发布。
The review is partial and must not be posted as if it were final.

2909
04:11:41,326 --> 04:11:46,176
带有零退出码的空结果是一个失败，你的流水线必须将其视为失败。
An empty result with a zero exit is a failure and your pipeline has to treat it as one.

2910
04:11:46,574 --> 04:11:52,612
当任何一种情况发生时，让该阶段失败或标记给人工处理，绝不要把部分结果发布为完成结果。
And when either happens, fail the stage or flag it for a human but never publish a partial result as a finished one.

2911
04:11:53,070 --> 04:11:55,076
这些又是模块 4 的三种结尾。
Those are module 4's three endings again.

2912
04:11:55,536 --> 04:11:57,636
完成、受限、报错。
Finished, capped, errored.

2913
04:11:58,496 --> 04:12:03,908
一个只知道通过和失败的流水线会把这三者混为一谈。
A pipeline that knows only pass and fail collapses all three.

2914
04:12:05,518 --> 04:12:10,564
第三个人工任务是监控问题，而这个版本在 CI 中最为重要。
The third human job is watching for trouble, and here is the version that matters most in CI.

2915
04:12:11,136 --> 04:12:17,252
如果编写代码的同一个会话也在进行审查，那么审核者会承载在编写过程中做出的所有假设。
If the same session that wrote the code also reviews it, the reviewer holds every assumption made during writing.

2916
04:12:17,776 --> 04:12:21,476
它看到的是它原本想写出的代码，而不是实际存在的代码。
It sees the code it meant to write rather than the code that is there.

2917
04:12:22,350 --> 04:12:26,820
它认同自己的推理，并完全忽略掉它误解的部分。
It agrees with its own reasoning and misses precisely what it misunderstood.

2918
04:12:27,758 --> 04:12:35,780
一个新的会话只看到差异和标准，不记得任何选择背后的原因，并且按原样阅读代码。
A fresh session sees only the diff and the standards, has no memory of why any choice was made, and reads the code as written.

2919
04:12:36,782 --> 04:12:39,364
它对推理过程的无知并不是一种限制。
Its ignorance of the reasoning is not a limitation.

2920
04:12:40,302 --> 04:12:45,764
这正是核心目的，也是你能获得的、最接近第二双眼睛的审查方式。
It is the entire point and it is the closest thing you get to a second pair of eyes.

2921
04:12:47,406 --> 04:12:53,828
自动审查的一个实际问题值得关注，因为考试中会将其作为一种场景来考查。
One practical problem with automated review deserves attention because the exam frames it as a scenario.

2922
04:12:54,254 --> 04:13:00,516
一个事无巨细报错的审核者会被忽略，而且一旦团队开始略读，真正的发现也会被略过。
A reviewer that flags everything gets ignored, and once the team is skimming, the real findings get skimmed too.

2923
04:13:00,942 --> 04:13:02,020
有四点可以帮助解决这个问题。
Four things help.

2924
04:13:02,414 --> 04:13:05,056
给它提供你的标准，而不仅仅是差异。
Give it your standards rather than only the diff.

2925
04:13:05,966 --> 04:13:12,388
明确说明哪些内容不在范围内，这样风格上的偏好就不会伪装成安全问题出现。
State explicitly what is out of scope so style opinions do not turn up dressed as security findings.

2926
04:13:12,736 --> 04:13:18,096
要求给出严重程度评级，并让流水线只发布超过阈值的内容。
Ask for a severity rating and have the pipeline post only above a threshold.

2927
04:13:18,510 --> 04:13:22,724
这样做是将过滤逻辑放在代码中，而不是交给模型去判断相关性。
That puts the filtering in code rather than in the model's judgment about relevance.

2928
04:13:23,470 --> 04:13:29,124
而且在大规模代码库中，几个专项审查的效果优于一个通用审查。
And on a large code base, several focus reviews outperform one general.

2929
04:13:29,696 --> 04:13:30,116
1。
1.

2930
04:13:31,886 --> 04:13:36,452
增加一个简短的安全部分，因为 CI 执行器是一个目标丰富的环境。
A short security section because a CI runner is a target-rich environment.

2931
04:13:37,006 --> 04:13:39,696
API 密钥来自仓库密钥。
The API key comes from a repository secret.

2932
04:13:39,982 --> 04:13:43,620
千万不要在工作流中硬编码它，也不要通过命令行传递。
Never hardcode it in the workflow and never pass it on the command line.

2933
04:13:44,302 --> 04:13:48,196
命令行上的密钥会出现在进程列表和日志中。
A key on the command line shows up in the process list and in logs.

2934
04:13:49,102 --> 04:13:54,084
禁止读取环境文件，这样存在于执行器中的凭据就永远不会传给模型。
Deny reading environment files, so credentials present in the runner never reach the model.

2935
04:13:54,734 --> 04:13:58,660
从子进程上下文中清除敏感的环境变量。
Scrub sensitive environment variables from the sub-process context.

2936
04:14:00,782 --> 04:14:03,332
并在最后一行保留通用假设。
And hold the general assumption in the last line.

2937
04:14:04,174 --> 04:14:11,428
CI 执行器充满了凭据，所以要假设智能体能看到所有你没有刻意排除的内容。
A CI runner is full of credentials, so assume the agent can see anything you have not deliberately excluded.

2938
04:14:13,134 --> 04:14:15,684
这是一个关键点，而且是个很好的切入点。
One currency item and it is a good one.

2939
04:14:16,270 --> 04:14:25,956
现在有一个裸模式标志，它会跳过对钩子、技能、插件、MCP 服务器、自动记忆和 clot.md 的自动发现。
There is now a bare flag which skips auto discovery of hooks, skills, plugins, MCP servers, auto memory, and clot.mb.

2940
04:14:26,542 --> 04:14:27,972
原因是为了确定性。
The reason is determinism.

2941
04:14:28,302 --> 04:14:35,076
如果没有它，队友的本地钩子或项目的 MCP 配置可能会改变你的流水线行为。
Without it, a teammate's local hooks or a project MCP configuration can change what your pipeline does.

2942
04:14:35,566 --> 04:14:38,096
这正是构建过程中不希望出现的情况。
That is exactly what you do not want from a build.

2943
04:14:38,286 --> 04:14:44,336
在“裸模式”下，身份验证必须来自 API 密钥或密钥辅助程序，而不是钥匙串。
Under bear mode, authentication has to come from an API key or a key helper rather than the keychain.

2944
04:14:44,590 --> 04:14:46,980
Anthropic 建议在脚本调用时使用它。
Anthropic recommends it for scripted calls.

2945
04:14:47,216 --> 04:14:50,564
它不可被审查，而且是工作中的正确答案。
It is not examinable and it is the right answer at work.

2946
04:14:51,982 --> 04:14:53,124
模式识别。
Pattern recognition.

2947
04:14:53,456 --> 04:14:55,216
流水线无法解析。
The pipeline cannot parse.

2948
04:14:55,534 --> 04:14:58,656
结果意味着输出格式。JSun。
The result means output format. JSun.

2949
04:15:00,256 --> 04:15:04,976
某次拉取请求的成本飙升，意味着轮数和预算限制。
Cost spiked on one pull request means turn and budget caps.

2950
04:15:06,158 --> 04:15:11,364
在评审期间开始修改文件，意味着允许的工具被限制为只读。
It started modifying files during a review means allowed tools restricted to read only.

2951
04:15:12,270 --> 04:15:17,732
即使不完整也发布评论，意味着在发布前要识别停止原因。
Reviews posted even when incomplete means classify the stop reason before publishing.

2952
04:15:18,318 --> 04:15:24,580
评审漏掉了它引入的 Bug，意味着需要一个新的会话，而不是作者编写代码的那个会话。
The review misses the bugs it introduced, means a fresh session rather than the authoring one.

2953
04:15:25,198 --> 04:15:29,156
还有开发者忽略评论的情况，意味着严重程度阈值、
And developers ignoring the comments means severity thresholds,

2954
04:15:29,806 --> 04:15:32,132
范围限制以及团队标准。
scope limits, and team standards.

2955
04:15:33,038 --> 04:15:39,556
将每一行映射回三个人类任务之一，整个模块就会简化成你能掌握的内容。
Map each row back to one of the three human jobs, and the whole module compresses into something you can hold.

2956
04:15:41,070 --> 04:15:42,532
还有 5 行就结束了。
5 lines to close.

2957
04:15:43,054 --> 04:15:43,888
领域 3。
Domain 3.

2958
04:15:44,048 --> 04:15:49,220
无头模式移除了人工干预，因此权限、完成情况和警惕性都变成了配置问题。
Headless removes the human, so permission, completion, and vigilance all become configuration.

2959
04:15:50,190 --> 04:15:55,268
JSON 输出格式会提供停止原因，而仅仅的退出码无法提供。
Output format JSON gives you the stop reason which the exit code alone does not.

2960
04:15:56,078 --> 04:16:02,436
追加系统提示词是增加内容，而替换系统提示词会删除所有内容，包括你依赖的部分。
Append system prompt adds while replace system prompt removes everything, including the parts you are relying on.

2961
04:16:02,608 --> 04:16:11,492
在打印模式下，轮数限制没有默认值，达到该限制会导致中止而非完成。而且新会话的评审效果优于编写代码的那个会话。
In print mode, the turncap has no default and hitting it is an abort rather than a completion. And a fresh session reviews better than the session that wrote the code.

2962
04:16:12,078 --> 04:16:15,968
现在有五个场景。然后是领域 4 和提示工程。
Five scenarios now. Then domain 4 and prompt engineering.

2963
04:16:17,358 --> 04:16:18,528
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

2964
04:16:18,688 --> 04:16:26,180
一个团队对每个拉取请求运行自动评审，并把结果作为拉取请求评论发布。
A team runs an automated review on every pull request with claw-p, posting the result as a pull request comment.

2965
04:16:27,502 --> 04:16:33,328
在大型拉取请求中，评论有时会中途断开或只涵盖前两个文件。
On large pull requests, the comment sometimes stops mid-sentence or covers only the first two files.

2966
04:16:33,646 --> 04:16:35,876
工作流每次都报告成功。
The workflow reports success every time.

2967
04:16:36,622 --> 04:16:42,820
JSON 输出显示的停止原因表明已达到轮数限制，且该限制设置为 3。
The JSON output shows a stop reason indicating the turn cap was reached and the cap is set to 3.

2968
04:16:43,310 --> 04:16:44,580
他们应该修改什么？
What should they change?

2969
04:16:46,574 --> 04:16:50,500
a 移除轮数限制，以便大型评审能够完整运行。
a remove the turncap so large reviews can run to completion.

2970
04:16:50,928 --> 04:16:55,684
b 提高上限，并让工作流在发布前检查停止原因。
b Raise the cap and have the workflow check the stop reason before posting.

2971
04:16:56,526 --> 04:17:00,740
C. 切换到文本输出，让评论读起来更自然。
C. Switch to text output so the comment reads more naturally.

2972
04:17:01,390 --> 04:17:04,260
D. 将大型拉取请求拆分为较小的请求。
D. Split large pull requests into smaller ones.

2973
04:17:04,910 --> 04:17:06,148
稍停一下，做决定。
Pause and decide.

2974
04:17:11,854 --> 04:17:13,328
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2975
04:17:15,470 --> 04:17:19,876
这里有两个独立的故障，而最强的选项涵盖了这两点。
There are two separate faults here, and the strongest answer addresses both.

2976
04:17:20,494 --> 04:17:26,884
对于大型审查来说，上限设得太低，且工作流将被截断的运行结果当作已完成的任务发布。
The cap is too low for large reviews, and the workflow publishes a capped run as though it were a finished one.

2977
04:17:27,822 --> 04:17:34,128
选项 A 解决了第一个问题但让第二个问题变糟，而且它还会陷入没有默认上限的情况。
Option A fixes the first and makes the second worse, and it also walks into the no default cap.

2978
04:17:34,862 --> 04:17:38,128
在打印模式中移除该标志后，将完全没有任何上限。
Remove the flag in print mode, and there is no ceiling at all.

2979
04:17:38,286 --> 04:17:41,604
所以你用被截断的审查换取了无限制的成本。
So you have traded truncated reviews for unbounded cost.

2980
04:17:42,478 --> 04:17:48,132
选项 C 丢弃了停止原因，而这是该团队今天能够诊断出问题的唯一线索。
Option C throws away the stop reason, which is the only reason this team can diagnose the problem today.

2981
04:17:48,878 --> 04:17:53,188
选项 D 是良好的实践，但它会让这种静默成功完全保留下来。
Option D is good practice that leaves the silent success entirely intact.

2982
04:17:54,702 --> 04:17:55,568
场景 2。
Scenario 2.

2983
04:17:55,808 --> 04:17:59,684
一名工程师希望 CI 审查者表现得像安全专家一样。
An engineer wants the CI reviewer to behave as a security specialist.

2984
04:17:59,888 --> 04:18:02,564
他们添加了一个替换系统提示词的标志：
They add a replace system prompt flag reading.

2985
04:18:02,875 --> 04:18:08,155
“你是一名安全工程师，检查差异中的漏洞并以 JSON 格式报告结果。”
you are a security engineer, review the diff for vulnerabilities and report findings as JSON.

2986
04:18:09,038 --> 04:18:12,228
更改后，审查质量大幅下降。
After the change, review quality drops sharply.

2987
04:18:13,166 --> 04:18:20,996
Claude 忽略了仓库的惯例，偶尔在审查期间尝试编辑文件，且文件导航变得紊乱。
CROD ignores the repository's conventions, occasionally attempts to edit files during a review, and its file navigation becomes erratic.

2988
04:18:22,048 --> 04:18:24,928
提示词文本本身是正确且写得很好的。
The prompt text itself is correct and well written.

2989
04:18:25,230 --> 04:18:26,212
出了什么问题？
What went wrong?

2990
04:18:26,830 --> 04:18:30,852
a. 提示词需要更多关于仓库惯例的细节。
a The prompt needs more detail about the repository's conventions.

2991
04:18:31,726 --> 04:18:31,968
b。
b.

2992
04:18:32,448 --> 04:18:39,492
替换系统提示词删除了 Claude Code 的默认指令，包括工具指导和安全上下文。
Replace system prompt removed clot code's default instructions, including tool guidance and safety context.

2993
04:18:39,968 --> 04:18:43,812
C. 模型太小，无法胜任安全审查工作。
C. The model is too small for security review work.

2994
04:18:44,302 --> 04:18:49,348
D. claude.md 在无头模式下未被加载。
D clot.m D is not being loaded in headless mode.

2995
04:18:49,870 --> 04:18:51,140
稍停一下，做决定。
Pause and decide.

2996
04:18:56,878 --> 04:19:01,316
答案是 B，这种诊断技巧非常值得借鉴。
The answer is B and the diagnostic technique is worth taking away.

2997
04:19:01,648 --> 04:19:04,260
三个无关的症状同时出现。
Three unrelated symptoms appeared at once.

2998
04:19:04,608 --> 04:19:10,596
忽略惯例、在只读任务中尝试编辑、以及紊乱的文件导航。
Ignored conventions, attempted edits during a read-only task, and erratic file navigation.

2999
04:19:11,168 --> 04:19:15,972
一个薄弱的提示词不会同时导致三个无关的退化问题。
A single weak prompt does not produce three unrelated regressions simultaneously.

3000
04:19:16,910 --> 04:19:24,644
移除默认系统提示词则会，因为工具使用指导、安全指令和环境上下文都会同时消失。
Removing a default system prompt does, because tool usage guidance, safety instructions, and environment context all vanish together.

3001
04:19:26,222 --> 04:19:32,068
题干也告诉我们提示词本身写得很好，这是为了防止你去纠结措辞问题。
The stem also tells you the prompt text itself is well written, which is there to stop you blaming the wording.

3002
04:19:32,448 --> 04:19:34,948
修复方法应该是追加而不是替换。
The fix is append rather than replace.

3003
04:19:35,822 --> 04:19:41,476
选项 D 只解释了三个症状中的一个，这是个很好的排查习惯。
Option D explains only one of the three symptoms, which is a good habit to check for.

3004
04:19:42,766 --> 04:19:43,748
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

3005
04:19:44,142 --> 04:19:46,372
一个流水线为某个功能生成代码。
A pipeline generates code for a feature.

3006
04:19:46,688 --> 04:19:54,180
然后，在同一个会话中，它要求 Claude 在发起拉取请求前，对照团队标准来审查自己的工作。
Then, in the same session, it asks Claude to review its own work against the team's standards before opening a pull request.

3007
04:19:54,894 --> 04:19:56,996
审查结果一直都是正面的。
The reviews are consistently positive.

3008
04:19:57,902 --> 04:20:06,372
随后人工审查员发现了自动审查未提及的问题，其中有几个是由于误读现有接口导致的。
Human reviewers subsequently find issues the automated review did not mention and several of them stem from a misreading of an existing interface.

3009
04:20:06,688 --> 04:20:09,444
团队希望自动审查能识别出这些问题。
The team wants the automated review to catch these.

3010
04:20:09,808 --> 04:20:11,780
最有效的修改是什么？
What is the most effective change?

3011
04:20:12,128 --> 04:20:16,004
a. 给审查步骤提供一个更长、更详细的清单。
a give the review step a longer, more detailed checklist.

3012
04:20:16,622 --> 04:20:16,848
b。
b.

3013
04:20:17,358 --> 04:20:21,732
在仅能看到差异和标准的独立会话中运行审查。
Run the review in a separate session that sees only the diff and the standards.

3014
04:20:22,288 --> 04:20:22,608
C。
C.

3015
04:20:23,008 --> 04:20:27,076
d. 增加审查步骤的轮数限制，以便它能更仔细地检查。
Increase the turn cap for the review step so it can look more carefully.

3016
04:20:27,694 --> 04:20:27,968
D。
D.

3017
04:20:28,654 --> 04:20:32,644
要求审查步骤更加严厉，并假设代码是错误的。
Ask the review step to be more critical and assume the code is wrong.

3018
04:20:33,262 --> 04:20:34,436
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3019
04:20:40,174 --> 04:20:41,824
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3020
04:20:42,224 --> 04:20:47,664
埋设的细节是：遗漏的问题源于对现有接口的误读。
The planted detail is that the missed issues stem from a misreading of an existing interface.

3021
04:20:47,824 --> 04:20:51,460
这一个环节就同时排除了 A、C 和 D。
That single phase eliminates A, C and D together.

3022
04:20:51,664 --> 04:20:57,252
这三个选项都要求审查者在保留导致 Bug 的那个误解的前提下，去更努力地工作。
All three ask the reviewer to work harder while holding the very misunderstanding that caused the bugs.

3023
04:20:57,998 --> 04:21:04,132
它会自信地勾选每一个清单项目，因为在那个误读的逻辑里，代码是正确的。
It will tick every checklist item confidently because from inside that misreading the code is correct.

3024
04:21:04,464 --> 04:21:12,484
只有全新的会话才能打破这个循环，因为它没有之前的推理记忆，并且会按代码实际写法而非预期意图来读取代码。
Only a fresh session breaks the loop since it has no memory of the reasoning and reads the code as written rather than as intended.

3025
04:21:13,264 --> 04:21:18,704
选项 D 最具诱惑力，因为变得更严厉听起来像是增加了严谨性。
Option D is the most seductive because being more critical sounds like rigor.

3026
04:21:19,118 --> 04:21:21,540
它改变的是语气，而不是信息量。
It changes tone rather than information.

3027
04:21:23,054 --> 04:21:24,164
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

3028
04:21:24,494 --> 04:21:36,452
一个自动审查者在每个拉取请求中发布 15 到 40 条评论。大部分是风格偏好、命名建议和关于代码的观察。拉取请求并未变动。
An automated reviewer posts between 15 and 40 comments per pull request. Most are stylistic preferences, naming suggestions, and observations about code. The pull request did not touch.

3029
04:21:37,230 --> 04:21:45,764
开发人员开始在不阅读的情况下直接合并机器人的评论，上个月就这样漏掉了一个真实的 SQL 注入问题。
Developers have started collapsing the bot's comments without reading them, and last month, a genuine SQL injection finding was missed this way.

3030
04:21:47,022 --> 04:21:49,284
团队希望审查内容能被再次阅读。
The team wants the reviewer to be read again.

3031
04:21:49,584 --> 04:21:51,428
哪种改动最有效？
What is the most effective change?

3032
04:21:52,142 --> 04:21:57,956
a 让审核者为每个发现分配严重程度，并只发布高风险的关键项。
a Have the reviewer assign a severity to each finding and post only high-end critical ones.

3033
04:21:58,414 --> 04:22:02,084
b 降低轮数限制，使其产生的评论更少。
b. Reduce the turn cap so it produces fewer comments.

3034
04:22:03,024 --> 04:22:03,344
C。
C.

3035
04:22:04,014 --> 04:22:06,724
在提示词中要求审核者不要过于吹毛求疵。
Ask the reviewer to be less pedantic in the prompt.

3036
04:22:07,424 --> 04:22:07,664
D。
D.

3037
04:22:08,494 --> 04:22:11,844
将完整的审查内容作为文件附件发布，而不是作为评论。
Post the full review as a file attachment instead of comments.

3038
04:22:13,390 --> 04:22:14,628
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3039
04:22:20,270 --> 04:22:21,744
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

3040
04:22:22,064 --> 04:22:26,532
之所以优选 A 而非 C，是因为过滤是在流水线中进行的。
The reason to prefer it over option. C is where the filtering happens.

3041
04:22:26,784 --> 04:22:31,780
要求模型减少吹毛求疵，会将决策权交给模型的判断。
Asking the model to be less pedantic puts the decision inside the model's judgment.

3042
04:22:32,142 --> 04:22:35,844
而正是这种判断导致了目前产生的 40 条评论。
That judgment is the thing currently producing 40 comments.

3043
04:22:36,654 --> 04:22:41,764
要求进行严重程度评级并在流水线中过滤，是将决策权交给代码。
Asking for a severity rating and filtering in the pipeline puts the decision in code.

3044
04:22:42,144 --> 04:22:47,012
你可以对其进行微调，而且关键的发现不会被命名建议淹没。
You can tune it, and a critical finding cannot be crowded out by naming suggestions.

3045
04:22:48,942 --> 04:22:54,692
选项 B 是根据位置而非重要性来丢失信息，这是随机的。
Option B loses findings by position rather than by importance, which is arbitrary.

3046
04:22:55,470 --> 04:23:01,892
选项 D 只是在多点一次点击的情况下保留同样数量的内容，这让忽略它变得更容易而不是更难。
Option D keeps the same volume behind an extra click, which makes ignoring it easier rather than harder.

3047
04:23:03,566 --> 04:23:04,516
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

3048
04:23:04,784 --> 04:23:10,980
一个 IT 作业在 GitHub Actions 容器中运行 clot-p 来分诊失败的测试。
An IT job runs plot-p in a GitHub Actions container to triage failing tests.

3049
04:23:11,344 --> 04:23:16,132
它被调用时允许使用的工具包括 read、grep、glob 和 bash。
It is invoked with allowed tools read, grep, glob, and bash.

3050
04:23:16,784 --> 04:23:19,504
安全审查提出了两个问题。
A security review raises two concerns.

3051
04:23:20,046 --> 04:23:29,476
运行器的环境包含部署凭据，且该作业之前曾运行过一个将环境文件内容读取到上下文中的 bash 命令。
The runner's environment contains deployment credentials, and the job has previously run a bash command that read an environment file into its context.

3052
04:23:30,062 --> 04:23:32,676
该任务确实需要运行测试套件。
The job genuinely needs to run the test suite.

3053
04:23:33,326 --> 04:23:34,244
他们应该怎么做？
What should they do?

3054
04:23:34,784 --> 04:23:37,540
a 从允许的工具中移除 bash。
a remove bash from allowed tools.

3055
04:23:38,254 --> 04:23:47,204
b 禁止读取环境文件，从子进程中清除敏感的环境变量，并将 bash 的范围限制在测试命令上。
b Deny reading environment files, scrub sensitive environment variables from the subprocess, and keep bash scope to the test command.

3056
04:23:47,664 --> 04:23:47,904
C。
C.

3057
04:23:48,384 --> 04:23:53,060
添加一个 clod.md，规定规则让 Claude 永远不要读取凭证文件。
Add a clod.md, rule instructing clot never to read credential files.

3058
04:23:53,454 --> 04:23:58,148
D. 由于容器是临时的，使用跳过权限标志。
D. Use the skip permissions flag since the container is ephemeral.

3059
04:24:05,806 --> 04:24:06,820
答案是
The answer is

3060
04:24:07,470 --> 04:24:07,744
B。
B.

3061
04:24:08,622 --> 04:24:13,824
选项 A 是一个诱人的简单修复，但它会移除该任务存在的目的所需要的核心功能。
Option A is the tempting simple fix and it removes the capability the job exists to use.

3062
04:24:14,094 --> 04:24:17,668
题干告诉我们，它确实需要运行测试套件。
The stem tells you it genuinely needs to run the test suite.

3063
04:24:18,510 --> 04:24:26,276
选项 C 是一个记忆文件，试图阻止 shell 命令读取文件，这是用劝导去代替强制执行的功能。
Option C is a memory file trying to stop a shell command from reading a file, which is persuasion attempting to do enforcement's job.

3064
04:24:26,894 --> 04:24:30,404
选项 D 值得思考一下，因为「临时」听起来让人很放心。
Option D deserves a moment because ephemeral sounds reassuring.

3065
04:24:30,798 --> 04:24:32,324
但这和「保存」不是一回事。
It is not the same as save.

3066
04:24:32,814 --> 04:24:36,420
临时容器限制了漏洞持续存在的时间。
An ephemeral container limits how long a compromise persists.

3067
04:24:37,326 --> 04:24:42,624
它无法解决任务运行时环境中存在的凭据问题，而这正是泄露发生的时候。
It does nothing about credentials sitting in the environment while the job runs, which is when the leak happens.

3068
04:24:42,958 --> 04:24:46,052
B 选项包含了 3 层强制控制，并能保证任务正常运行。
B layers 3 enforce controls and keeps the job working.

3069
04:24:46,382 --> 04:24:47,780
这就涵盖了领域 3。
That closes domain 3.

3070
04:24:50,830 --> 04:24:51,616
领域 4。
Domain 4.

3071
04:24:51,918 --> 04:24:55,012
接下来是提示工程和结构化输出。
Next on prompt engineering and structured output.

3072
04:24:56,462 --> 04:25:00,292
欢迎来到领域 4：提示工程和结构化输出。
Welcome to domain 4, prompt engineering and structured output.

3073
04:25:00,736 --> 04:25:04,612
占考试的 20%，大约有 12 道题，包含 3 个模块。
20% of the exam, roughly 12 questions, 3 modules.

3074
04:25:05,582 --> 04:25:09,124
第一个模块是关于如何从提示词中获得可靠的判断。
This first one is about getting reliable judgment out of a prompt.

3075
04:25:09,806 --> 04:25:13,188
包括决策、分类、评估和审查。
Deciding, classifying, assessing, reviewing.

3076
04:25:13,774 --> 04:25:17,732
下一个模块是关于结构化数据，第三个是关于成本和规模。
The next module is about structured data, and the third is about cost and scale.

3077
04:25:18,096 --> 04:25:20,256
这是一个适用于整个领域的警告。
A warning that applies to this whole domain.

3078
04:25:20,576 --> 04:25:27,108
提示工程是大家普遍认为自己已经掌握了答案的领域，也是干扰项最具有迷惑性的地方。
Prompt engineering is the area where everyone assumes they already know the answers, and it is where the distractors are most plausible.

3079
04:25:27,694 --> 04:25:29,220
处理案例时要放慢点。
Slow down on the scenarios.

3080
04:25:30,702 --> 04:25:32,548
从诊断立场开始。
Start with the diagnostic stance.

3081
04:25:32,816 --> 04:25:36,420
当提示词表现不佳时，本能反应是加大力度。
When a prompt underperforms, the instinct is to push harder.

3082
04:25:36,816 --> 04:25:40,100
增加强调、加粗大写、加上「关键」这个词。
Add emphasis, add capitals, add the word critical.

3083
04:25:40,526 --> 04:25:45,252
这种直觉假设模型不够努力，但事实几乎从不是这样。
That instinct assumes the model is not trying hard enough, and it almost never is.

3084
04:25:46,158 --> 04:25:53,668
实际发生的情况是，因为你没有准确表达你的意思，所以模型无法准确理解你的意图。
What is actually happening is that the model does not know precisely what you meant because you did not say precisely what you meant.

3085
04:25:53,936 --> 04:25:59,716
因此，有效的做法几乎总是变得更具体，而不是更强硬。
So the productive move is nearly always to be more specific rather than more forceful.

3086
04:26:00,590 --> 04:26:06,212
仅凭这个思维转变，就能回答大量领域 4 的题目。
That single reframe answers a surprising number of domain 4 questions on its own.

3087
04:26:07,502 --> 04:26:12,068
Anthropic 的指导建议以三个前提条件开头，这些非常值得认真对待。
Anthropic's guidance opens with three prerequisites and they are worth taking seriously.

3088
04:26:12,622 --> 04:26:18,916
明确成功的定义，要足够具体，让两个人都能就给出的输出是否符合要求达成共识。
Define what success looks like concretely enough that two people would agree on whether a given output met it.

3089
04:26:19,822 --> 04:26:26,372
建立一种针对该定义进行测试的方法，这可以简单到只包含几个已知答案的真实案例。
Build a way to test against that definition, which can be as small as a handful of real cases with known answers.

3090
04:26:26,990 --> 04:26:29,988
然后写出第一稿，并根据这些测试进行改进。
Then write a first draft and improve it against the tests.

3091
04:26:30,862 --> 04:26:37,444
如果没有这三点，你就是在盲目优化，而且任何改动看起来都像是改进，因为你根本没法判断。
Without those three, you are optimizing blind, and every change will feel like an improvement because you have no way of telling.

3092
04:26:38,350 --> 04:26:43,332
提示工程比微调要便宜得多，但前提是你得能判断出它是否奏效。
Prompt engineering is far cheaper than fine-tuning, but only if you can tell whether it worked.

3093
04:26:44,576 --> 04:26:52,772
Anthropic 按顺序发布这些技术，从广泛有效的到专门的，这个顺序就是建议。
Anthropic publishes these techniques in order, from the broadly effective to the specialized, and the order is the advice.

3094
04:26:54,382 --> 04:26:57,924
清晰直接是第一步，也是最大的杠杆。
Be clear and direct is first, and it is the largest lever.

3095
04:26:58,734 --> 04:26:59,936
接下来是示例。
Then examples.

3096
04:27:00,176 --> 04:27:03,876
当格式不一致或任务需要判断时。
When the format is inconsistent or the task needs judgment.

3097
04:27:04,750 --> 04:27:09,060
接着是让 Claude 进行思考，当存在值得明确执行的推理步骤时。
Then letting Claude think when there are reasoning steps worth doing explicitly.

3098
04:27:09,582 --> 04:27:13,860
接着是结构化提示词，当指令和数据开始混淆时。
Then structuring the prompt when instructions and data are getting confused with each other.

3099
04:27:15,662 --> 04:27:18,276
接着是用于语气和框架的角色或系统提示词。
Then a role or system prompt for tone and framing.

3100
04:27:19,822 --> 04:27:22,884
接着是预填充，用以控制输出的开头。
Then prefilling to control how the output starts.

3101
04:27:23,790 --> 04:27:27,216
最后是链式调用，当一个提示词承担的任务太多时。
And finally chaining when one prompt is doing too much.

3102
04:27:27,502 --> 04:27:30,308
按这个列表从上往下做，而不是从底部开始。
Work down that list rather than starting at the bottom.

3103
04:27:31,982 --> 04:27:35,936
有一个方法不在这个列表中，它的缺失是刻意为之的。
One approach is missing from that list and its absence is deliberate.

3104
04:27:36,256 --> 04:27:38,212
强调并不是一种技术。
Emphasis is not a technique.

3105
04:27:38,702 --> 04:27:46,500
用大写字母写“务必彻底”，或者加上“非常重要”等词，或重复三次指令，只能产生微弱且不可靠的效果。
Writing be thorough in capitals or adding the words very important or repeating an instruction three times does something small and unreliable.

3106
04:27:47,470 --> 04:27:50,596
这些都不会告诉模型任何它原本不知道的信息。
None of it tells the model anything it did not already know.

3107
04:27:51,438 --> 04:27:53,136
“彻底”并不是一个明确的标准。
Thorough is not a defined standard.

3108
04:27:53,486 --> 04:28:00,324
当某个场景描述一个团队已经强化了两次措辞但问题依然存在时，说明措辞从来就不是问题所在。
When a scenario describes a team that has strengthened the wording twice and still has the problem, the wording was never the issue.

3109
04:28:01,006 --> 04:28:04,256
提示词缺少的是信息量，而不是字数。
The prompt is missing information rather than volume.

3110
04:28:05,518 --> 04:28:09,508
这是决定更多领域 4 题目的关键对比点。
Here is the contrast that decides more domain 4 questions than any other.

3111
04:28:09,696 --> 04:28:13,636
“仔细检查这段代码”在每次运行中都有不同的含义。
Review this code carefully means something slightly different on every run.

3112
04:28:14,862 --> 04:28:20,708
覆盖范围取决于模型注意到了什么，你无法区分它是漏掉了还是做出了判断。
Coverage varies with whatever catches the model's attention, and you cannot distinguish a miss from a judgment call.

3113
04:28:21,614 --> 04:28:23,748
加上“不同”这个词就会改变结果。
Adding the word vary changes.

3114
04:28:24,206 --> 04:28:25,188
不要用那些。
None of that.

3115
04:28:25,856 --> 04:28:28,452
命名类别可以解决覆盖范围问题。
Naming the categories fixes coverage.

3116
04:28:28,846 --> 04:28:35,204
检查 SQL 注入、缺失的权限检查以及未处理的错误路径。
Check for SQL injection, missing authorization checks, and unhandled error paths.

3117
04:28:35,886 --> 04:28:42,532
这能保证每次检查的内容一致，漏掉时有明显的缺口，并且方便添加新类别。
That gives the same sweep every time, a visible gap when something is missed, and somewhere to add a category.

3118
04:28:43,246 --> 04:28:47,716
明确的标准并不会让模型变得更聪明。
Explicit criteria do not make the model cleverer.

3119
04:28:48,334 --> 04:28:49,828
它们能让结果可重复。
They make it repeatable.

3120
04:28:51,438 --> 04:28:54,148
当你编写标准时，要写成具有普适性的内容。
When you write criteria, write them to generalize.

3121
04:28:55,182 --> 04:29:01,796
描述属性而非具体实例，比如写“超过审批限制的金额”，而不是“600磅的案例”
Describe the property rather than the instance, so amounts above the approval limit rather than the 600 pound case.

3122
04:29:04,046 --> 04:29:10,500
明确说明哪些内容不在范围内，就像明确包含的内容一样，因为没说明的排除项会被包含进来
State what is out of scope as explicitly as what is in it because unstated exclusions get included.

3123
04:29:11,406 --> 04:29:18,148
给出约束背后的原因，因为当 Claude 知道规则在保护什么时，它能更好地遵循规则
Give the reason behind the constraint since Claude follows a rule considerably better when it knows what the rule is protecting.

3124
04:29:18,608 --> 04:29:20,484
别忘了底部的警告
And remember the warning at the bottom.

3125
04:29:21,166 --> 04:29:27,524
根据一个错误案例编写的规则只能修复那个特定的例子，下一个故障可能会以不同的形式出现
A rule written from one bad example fixes exactly that example, and the next failure will be shaped differently.

3126
04:29:28,302 --> 04:29:35,076
这就是为什么在这场考试中，最有效的选项通常是具有普适性的答案
That is why most effective on this exam usually means the answer that generalizes.

3127
04:29:36,366 --> 04:29:44,285
本模块中的第二个重大决策是：当输出格式不一致或任务涉及判断时，选择使用示例
The second big decision in this module reach for examples when the output format is inconsistent or the task is a judgement call

3128
04:29:44,528 --> 04:29:46,212
这些情况很难用语言准确描述
hard to pin down in words.

3129
04:29:46,510 --> 04:29:51,268
还有在需要演示如何处理边缘情况或者语气很重要的时候
Also when edge cases need a demonstrated resolution or when tone matters.

3130
04:29:52,046 --> 04:29:58,368
当规则确实是硬性规定，或者需要确保覆盖范围完整且可核查时，选择明确的准则
Reach for explicit criteria when the rule genuinely is a rule or coverage needs to be complete and checkable.

3131
04:29:58,608 --> 04:30:03,620
还有在边界可以清晰表述，或者你需要审计模型接收到的指令时
Also when the boundary can be stated in words or you need to audit what the model was told.

3132
04:30:05,550 --> 04:30:08,452
这个判定标准值得作为一个句子背下来
The tiebreaker is worth memorizing as a sentence.

3133
04:30:09,088 --> 04:30:13,220
示例适用于那些比定义更易于演示的事情
Examples are for things easier to demonstrate than to define.

3134
04:30:13,550 --> 04:30:17,284
准则适用于那些比演示更易于定义的事情
Criteria for things easier to define than to demonstrate.

3135
04:30:18,798 --> 04:30:21,488
如果你决定使用示例，就得正确地使用它们
If you do use examples, use them properly.

3136
04:30:21,648 --> 04:30:26,404
通常提供 3 到 5 个就够了，多样性比数量重要得多
3 to 5 is usually enough and diversity matters far more than quantity.

3137
04:30:27,694 --> 04:30:35,876
至少包含一个困难案例并展示如何解决它，因为正是这些边界情况才是教学的关键所在
Include at least one hard case and show how it resolves because the boundary is where the teaching actually happens.

3138
04:30:36,462 --> 04:30:42,308
如果示例看起来都一模一样，就会教会模型一个狭隘的规则，模型随后会以过高的置信度去执行这个规则
Examples that all look alike teach a narrow rule that the model then applies with unwarranted confidence.

3139
04:30:42,894 --> 04:30:50,925
别忘了，每次调用都会消耗输入标记。所以长篇的示例集是持续性的成本，而不是一次性的支出
And remember, they cost input tokens on every single call. So a long example set is a real recurring expense rather than a one-off.

3140
04:30:52,622 --> 04:30:55,524
这种警示是值得识别的一种故障模式
The call out is the failure mode worth recognizing.

3141
04:30:55,982 --> 04:31:02,468
如果一组示例中不包含任何困难情况，就会让模型认为不存在困难情况
An example set containing no difficult case teaches the model that there are no difficult cases.

3142
04:31:04,046 --> 04:31:07,716
现在来看这个在这一领域产生一些非常有趣问题的权衡问题
Now the trade-off that produces some of the most interesting questions in this domain.

3143
04:31:08,302 --> 04:31:14,116
一个要求两件不同事情的提示词，通常的效果都会比两个分别要求一件事情的提示词差
A prompt asking for two different things will usually do both worse than two prompts, each asking for one.

3144
04:31:14,926 --> 04:31:17,700
这与其说是能力限制，不如说是注意力问题
This is not a capability limit so much as an attention.

3145
04:31:18,574 --> 04:31:19,076
1
1.

3146
04:31:20,046 --> 04:31:27,108
模型在平衡两组指令，而具体的详细指令会与广泛的一般性指令产生竞争
The model is balancing two sets of instructions and a specific detailed instruction competes with a broad general one.

3147
04:31:27,950 --> 04:31:34,916
典型的症状是：特定的任务完成得很好，但通用的处理就很浅显；或者反过来
The typical symptom is that the specific job gets done well and the general sweep gets shallow or the reverse.

3148
04:31:35,726 --> 04:31:41,348
对其中任何一侧增加强调，只是改变了哪一部分会失败
Adding emphasis to whichever half is using simply swaps which half loses.

3149
04:31:42,894 --> 04:31:48,196
过载提示词的特征值得学习，因为一旦你掌握了它，这种现象就非常明显
The signature of an overloaded prompt is worth learning because it is unmistakable once you know it.

3150
04:31:48,528 --> 04:31:53,060
它会让其中一半做得很好，另一半做得很敷衍，而且哪一部分出问题在不同运行中是不确定的
It does one half well and the other half thinly, and which half varies between runs.

3151
04:31:53,518 --> 04:31:59,236
强化弱项会导致强项变差，这是一种诊断结果而非巧合。
Strengthening the weak half makes the strong half worse, which is a diagnosis rather than a coincidence.

3152
04:31:59,982 --> 04:32:08,292
不同类别的发现会互相挤占空间而不是叠加，因此总量基本不变，只是比例在变化。
And findings from one category crowd out another instead of adding to it so the total volume stays roughly constant while the mix shifts.

3153
04:32:08,688 --> 04:32:12,708
解决方法是分成两次调用，每项任务都有明确的指令，最后再合并。
The fix is two calls, each with a narrow brief combined afterwards.

3154
04:32:13,326 --> 04:32:20,996
当题干说“我们改进了一项，但另一项变差了”时，这是领域 4 中最明确的信号。
When a stem says, We improved one thing and another got worse, that is the clearest signal in domain 4.

3155
04:32:22,608 --> 04:32:29,636
拆分并非免费，所以要清楚权衡：它会增加调用次数、延迟以及一些编排代码。
Splitting is not free, so be honest about the trade. It costs more calls, more latency, and some orchestration code.

3156
04:32:30,094 --> 04:32:36,100
但它换来的是每次调用只负责一个任务，因此每个环节都能独立进行调优、测试和衡量。
What it buys is that each call has a single job, so each can be tuned, tested, and measured on its

3157
04:32:36,128 --> 04:32:45,328
它还能提供诊断功能，因为你可以看到是哪个阶段失败了，而不是去猜测合并后的提示词中哪一部分出了问题。
own. It also buys you diagnosis because you can see which stage failed rather than guessing which half of a combined prompt went wrong.

3158
04:32:45,998 --> 04:32:52,260
只要可靠性比延迟更重要时，这种做法就值得采用，而在这次考试中，大部分情况都是如此。
It is worth it whenever reliability matters more than latency, which on this exam is most of the time.

3159
04:32:53,230 --> 04:33:00,708
注意，这是来自提示工程领域的模块 2 的提示词链，而不是架构方面的。
And note that this is module 2's prompt chaining arriving from the prompt engineering side rather than the architecture side.

3160
04:33:02,318 --> 04:33:05,968
这是一个贯穿整个领域 4 和领域 5 的模式。
Here is a pattern that recurs right through domain 4 and domain 5.

3161
04:33:06,348 --> 04:33:11,908
要求模型只报告它有把握的内容，是将阈值放入其自身的判断中。
Telling the model to report only what it is confident about puts the threshold inside its own judgment.

3162
04:33:12,430 --> 04:33:16,740
这种阈值会在不同运行中变化，且所有被过滤掉的内容对你来说都是不可见的。
That threshold moves between runs and everything suppressed is invisible to you.

3163
04:33:17,580 --> 04:33:22,687
要求它报告所有内容并附带置信度评分，是将阈值作为数字放入你的代码中。
Asking it to report everything with a confidence score puts the threshold in your code as a number.

3164
04:33:22,956 --> 04:33:27,876
每一个结果都是可见且被记录的，你可以根据实际结果来调整截断值。
Every finding is visible and recorded, and you can tune the cutoff against real outcomes.

3165
04:33:28,288 --> 04:33:33,474
低置信度的项会进入人工审核，而不是被静默丢弃。
Low confidence items root to human review rather than being silently discarded.

3166
04:33:34,366 --> 04:33:36,128
核心原则就在这个强调点上。
The principle is the callout.

3167
04:33:36,448 --> 04:33:39,972
要求模型进行过滤会隐藏它丢弃的内容。
Asking the model to filter hides what it discarded.

3168
04:33:41,294 --> 04:33:44,804
对于歧义，有两种合理的处理方式和一种糟糕的。
Ambiguity has two reasonable responses and one bad one.

3169
04:33:45,198 --> 04:33:51,088
当歧义较小且假设容易验证时，说明你的假设并继续执行。
State the assumption and carry on when the ambiguity is minor and the assumption is easy to check.

3170
04:33:51,248 --> 04:33:53,634
这样读者可以在一秒钟内纠正它。
The reader can then correct it in a second.

3171
04:33:53,968 --> 04:33:59,428
当选择会实质性改变输出，且选错会导致工作白费时，才去提问。
Ask when the choice materially changes the output and getting it wrong would waste the work.

3172
04:34:00,142 --> 04:34:06,756
你不该做的是在开始前提出三个问题，那是审问而非澄清。
What you should not do is ask three questions before starting, which is an interrogation rather than a clarification.

3173
04:34:07,404 --> 04:34:10,288
要记住的准则就在这个强调点里。
And the line to carry into the exam is in the call out.

3174
04:34:10,928 --> 04:34:15,364
最差的选项永远是那个基于未说明假设而继续进行的选项。
The worst option is always the one that proceeds on an unstated assumption.

3175
04:34:15,918 --> 04:34:19,396
所以，要么明确陈述，要么提问，而不是默默猜测。
So both stating and asking be it guessing quietly.

3176
04:34:20,608 --> 04:34:22,468
关于审核环节有两点。
Two things about review passes.

3177
04:34:22,687 --> 04:34:29,220
针对每个问题进行单独的审核，优于为了应对提示词过载而让一个环节涵盖所有内容。
A separate pass per concern beats one pass covering everything for the overloaded prompt reasons we just went through.

3178
04:34:29,408 --> 04:34:36,580
要求 Claude 在宣布任务完成前明确核实自己的工作是有帮助的，这也是 Anthropic 推荐的。
And asking Claude to verify its own work explicitly before declaring a task complete does help, which Anthropic recommends.

3179
04:34:37,518 --> 04:34:39,684
但要清楚它到底有多少帮助。
But be clear about how much it helps.

3180
04:34:39,968 --> 04:34:47,968
在同一个上下文内进行自我验证是最弱的一种形式，因为同样的逻辑在给自己打分，它更倾向于认同自己。
Self-verification inside the same context is the weakest form because the same reasoning is grading itself and it agrees more than it

3181
04:34:47,968 --> 04:34:52,128
应该。重新过一遍或者进行确定性检查效果更好。
should. A fresh pass or a deterministic check is stronger.

3182
04:34:52,366 --> 04:34:54,660
强调时的顺序值得保留。
The ordering in the call out is worth holding.

3183
04:34:55,630 --> 04:35:00,932
确定性检查，然后是全新上下文，接着是自我审查，最后是没有任何操作。
Deterministic check, then fresh context, then self-review, then nothing.

3184
04:35:02,348 --> 04:35:08,386
故障排除地图，因为问题的领域通常是寻找对应技术的症状。
A troubleshooting map because domain for questions are usually a symptom looking for a technique.

3185
04:35:09,008 --> 04:35:14,436
格式多变意味着要使用示例或者预填充回复的开头。
Format keeps varying means examples or prefilling the start of the response.

3186
04:35:14,928 --> 04:35:20,900
不同运行之间的覆盖范围不一，意味着要用具体的类别名称而不是质量形容词。
Coverage varies between runs means named categories rather than a quality adjective.

3187
04:35:21,774 --> 04:35:27,556
在困难案例中推理错误，意味着让它在回答前逐步思考。
Reasoning is wrong on hard cases, means letting it think step by step before answering.

3188
04:35:28,846 --> 04:35:32,612
指令和数据混淆，意味着要对提示词进行结构化处理。
Instructions and data getting confused means structuring the prompt.

3189
04:35:33,486 --> 04:35:35,076
这样它们就能清晰分离。
So they are clearly separated.

3190
04:35:36,973 --> 04:35:38,116
改进了一件事，
Improving one thing.

3191
04:35:38,734 --> 04:35:42,206
却导致另一件事变差，这意味着要拆分成两个提示词。
Degrading another means split into two prompts.

3192
04:35:42,702 --> 04:35:46,756
还有你从未发现的情况，意味着要打分并进行下游过滤。
And findings you never see means score and filter downstream.

3193
04:35:47,086 --> 04:35:51,300
要根据症状匹配技术，而不是去用你喜欢的那种。
Match the symptom to the technique rather than reaching for the one you like.

3194
04:35:52,812 --> 04:35:57,008
货币注释：两种技术并没有消失，只是变得没那么核心了。
A currency note Two techniques have softened rather than disappeared.

3195
04:35:57,248 --> 04:36:02,340
结构化标签曾是区分指令和数据的核心推荐做法。
Structural tags were once a headline recommendation for separating instructions from data.

3196
04:36:02,608 --> 04:36:10,468
目前的指导建议说，现代模型在没有这些标签的情况下也能很好处理结构，但在处理大型嵌入文档时它们仍然有用。
Current guidance says modern models handle structure well without them, though they remain useful with large embedded documents.

3197
04:36:10,956 --> 04:36:19,168
大量的角色提示也经历了同样的转变，现在的建议是先从明确清晰的指令开始，而不是构建复杂的角色设定。
Heavy role prompting has moved the same way, and the advice now is to start with explicit clear instructions rather than an elaborate persona.

3198
04:36:19,328 --> 04:36:25,314
而且目前的指导更强调这些技术会消耗 token，因此应当在确实必要时才使用。
And current guidance is more insistent that these techniques cause tokens and should justify themselves.

3199
04:36:25,568 --> 04:36:27,778
在考试中，要按照指南的框架来回答。
On the exam, answer the guide's framing.

3200
04:36:28,608 --> 04:36:32,036
没有任何一种技术变错了，只是不再是核心支撑手段了。
Neither technique became wrong, only less load-bearing.

3201
04:36:33,486 --> 04:36:34,687
5行。
5 lines.

3202
04:36:35,008 --> 04:36:39,556
当提示词表现不佳时，要更具体一些，而不是用语气强硬点。
When a prompt underperforms, be more specific rather than more forceful.

3203
04:36:39,886 --> 04:36:44,964
具体的类别名称能解决覆盖范围问题，而像“仔细”和“彻底”这样的形容词不行。
Named categories fix coverage, while adjectives like careful and thorough do not.

3204
04:36:45,408 --> 04:36:51,300
对于那些比定义更容易展示的内容使用示例，对于相反的情况则使用标准。
Use examples for what is easier to show than to define, and criteria for the reverse.

3205
04:36:52,174 --> 04:36:54,692
一个提示词承担两个任务会导致两项工作都变差。
One prompt doing two jobs does both worse.

3206
04:36:55,246 --> 04:36:59,140
而且“改进了一件事而另一项变差”就是拆分的信号。
And we improved one thing and another got worse is the signal to split.

3207
04:36:59,568 --> 04:37:02,372
先手动打分，然后再进行下游过滤。
Handscore everything, then filter downstream.

3208
04:37:02,894 --> 04:37:05,955
因为让模型直接去过滤会隐藏它丢弃的内容。
Because a model asked to filter hides what it discarded.

3209
04:37:06,862 --> 04:37:12,484
现在有六个场景，其中两个提供的更强提示词作为具有诱惑力的错误选项。
Six scenarios now, and two of them offer a stronger prompt as the tempting wrong answer.

3210
04:37:14,188 --> 04:37:15,044
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

3211
04:37:15,598 --> 04:37:20,706
一个合同审查提示词写着：请仔细且全面地审查此合同。
A contract review prompt says, Review this contract carefully and thoroughly.

3212
04:37:21,100 --> 04:37:23,728
识别出任何有风险或异常的条款。
Identify any risky or unusual terms.

3213
04:37:23,982 --> 04:37:25,380
务必极其细致。
Be extremely diligent.

3214
04:37:26,254 --> 04:37:36,324
在一百份合同中，模型能稳定发现异常的付款条款，有时会提到责任上限，但从未提醒过自动续约条款。
Across a hundred contracts, the model finds unusual payment terms reliably, mentions liability cap sometimes, and has never once flagged an automatic renewal clause.

3215
04:37:37,838 --> 04:37:42,980
团队已经强化了两次措辞。哪种改动最有效？
The team has strengthened the wording twice already. What is the most effective change?

3216
04:37:43,918 --> 04:37:49,154
a. 进一步强化措辞，并加上续约条款特别重要的提示。
a strengthen the wording further and add that renewal clauses are especially important.

3217
04:37:49,488 --> 04:37:55,428
b. 用具体的条款类别清单替换形容词，包括自动续约。
b. Replace the adjectives with a named list of clause categories to check, including automatic renewal.

3218
04:37:55,854 --> 04:37:59,108
c. 添加三份带有正确审查结果的示例合同。
C. Add three example contracts with their correct reviews.

3219
04:38:00,044 --> 04:38:04,928
d. 使用更大的模型，因为合同审查是一项高要求的任务。
D. Use a larger model since contract review is a demanding task.

3220
04:38:05,248 --> 04:38:06,402
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3221
04:38:12,044 --> 04:38:13,184
答案是 b。
The answer is the.

3222
04:38:14,318 --> 04:38:16,516
关键点在于“从未”这个词。
The tell is the phrase never once.

3223
04:38:17,998 --> 04:38:26,383
如果模型在处理续约条款时遇到困难，它有时会发现它们；而“从未”意味着该内容完全不在定义的范围内。
A model that struggled with renewal clauses would find them sometimes, and never is the signature of something being outside the defined scope entirely.

3224
04:38:26,990 --> 04:38:35,204
选项 a 是团队已经尝试过两次的方法，它只是修补了一个类别，但没改变导致遗漏的根本机制。
Option A is what the team has already tried twice and it also patches one category while leaving the mechanism that lost it in place.

3225
04:38:37,070 --> 04:38:42,596
选项 c 是最强的干扰项，因为示例确实能改善判断和格式。
Option C is the strongest distractor because examples do improve judgment and format.

3226
04:38:43,470 --> 04:38:48,196
但它们无法保证涵盖那些恰好没出现在示例中的类别。
But they cannot guarantee coverage of a category the examples happen not to include.

3227
04:38:49,774 --> 04:38:52,706
选项 d 把范围问题归咎于模型能力不足。
Option D blames capability for a scope problem.

3228
04:38:53,454 --> 04:38:58,723
明确分类能将模糊的搜索转变为可以扩展的固定清单。
Naming the categories converts a variable sweep into a fixed checklist you can extend.

3229
04:39:00,078 --> 04:39:00,944
场景 2。
Scenario 2.

3230
04:39:01,104 --> 04:39:08,324
一个审查提示词要求 Claude 在单次调用中同时检查代码是否符合 12 点风格指南，并识别安全漏洞。
A review prompt asks Claude to both check code against a 12-point style guide and identify security vulnerabilities in a single call.

3231
04:39:08,718 --> 04:39:15,605
当团队强调安全性时，风格方面的发现明显减少；随后他们再次强调风格时，安全方面的发现又减少了。
When the team emphasized security, style findings dropped noticeably. When they later re-emphasized style, security findings dropped.

3232
04:39:16,526 --> 04:39:21,252
每次审查的总发现数量基本保持不变。这两个问题对他们来说同等重要。
Total findings per review stayed roughly constant. Both concerns matter equally to them.

3233
04:39:21,486 --> 04:39:22,340
他们该怎么做？
What should they do?

3234
04:39:22,704 --> 04:39:26,062
a. 平等强调两者，并接受目前的平衡状态。
a emphasize both equally and accept the current balance.

3235
04:39:26,304 --> 04:39:31,330
b. 分两次调用，一次查风格，一次查安全，然后合并结果。
B. Run two calls, one for style and one for security and merge the results.

3236
04:39:32,044 --> 04:39:32,304
c.
C.

3237
04:39:32,686 --> 04:39:38,212
先要求检查安全，再检查风格。这样在注意力最集中时完成安全检查。
Ask for security first and style second. So security is done while attention is fresh.

3238
04:39:38,670 --> 04:39:40,784
d. 增加最大 token 数。
D. Increase max tokens.

3239
04:39:40,944 --> 04:39:43,652
这样就有空间容纳两个类别的发现了。
So there is room for findings from both categories.

3240
04:39:44,014 --> 04:39:45,220
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3241
04:39:50,926 --> 04:39:51,972
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3242
04:39:52,304 --> 04:39:57,220
埋设的细节是：在比例变化的同时，总发现数量基本保持不变。
The planted detail is that total findings stayed roughly constant while the mix shifted.

3243
04:39:58,254 --> 04:40:00,548
那句单一的话就排除了该选项。
That single sentence rules out option.

3244
04:40:01,806 --> 04:40:05,956
选 D，因为并没有发生截断，而且它证实了诊断结果。
D because nothing was being truncated and it confirms the diagnosis.

3245
04:40:06,958 --> 04:40:09,764
两个任务在争夺有限的注意力。
Two jobs are competing for the same finite attention.

3246
04:40:10,734 --> 04:40:15,556
选项 A 值得提出来，因为它正是大多数团队最终妥协的选择。
Option A is worth naming because it is what most teams settle for.

3247
04:40:15,744 --> 04:40:21,444
它接受了一种权衡而非消除竞争，且双方类别都维持在平庸的水平。
It accepts a trade rather than removing it, and both categories stay mediocre by agreement.

3248
04:40:21,984 --> 04:40:29,828
选项 C 重新排列了竞争顺序但并未结束竞争，所以无论哪个问题排在第二位，最终都会得到剩下的部分。
Option C reorders the competition without ending it, so whichever concern goes second still gets whatever is left.

3249
04:40:30,624 --> 04:40:36,484
拆分是唯一能消除而非重新分配竞争的选项。
Splitting is the only option that removes the competition rather than redistributing it.

3250
04:40:37,966 --> 04:40:38,884
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

3251
04:40:39,184 --> 04:40:47,268
一个支持分诊提示词将进入的消息分为六个类别。这些类别定义明确且互不重叠。
A support triage prompt classifies incoming messages into six categories. The categories are clearly defined and mutually exclusive.

3252
04:40:47,662 --> 04:40:49,344
准确率为 91%。
Accuracy is 91%.

3253
04:40:50,064 --> 04:40:53,796
错误集中在那些真正处于模糊地带的消息中。
The errors are concentrated in genuinely borderline messages.

3254
04:40:54,382 --> 04:40:57,796
一个既是账单投诉又是取消威胁的案例。
A billing complaint that is also a cancellation threat.

3255
04:40:58,574 --> 04:41:01,092
一个表述为功能请求的 Bug 报告。
A bug report phrased as a feature request.

3256
04:41:02,384 --> 04:41:06,244
团队希望提高这些模糊案例的准确率。
The team wants to improve accuracy on those borderline cases.

3257
04:41:07,054 --> 04:41:08,644
哪种方法最可能有帮助？
What is most likely to help?

3258
04:41:09,230 --> 04:41:16,900
a. 添加几个带有正确分类和简短理由的模糊消息示例。
a add few short examples of borderline messages with their correct classifications and brief reasoning.

3259
04:41:17,424 --> 04:41:17,744
b。
b.

3260
04:41:18,222 --> 04:41:21,412
重写六个类别的定义，使其更加精确。
Rewrite the six category definitions to be even more precise.

3261
04:41:21,824 --> 04:41:22,064
C。
C.

3262
04:41:22,318 --> 04:41:24,740
增加一个名为“模糊”的第七个类别。
Add a seventh category called ambiguous.

3263
04:41:25,326 --> 04:41:30,212
d. 指示模型对可能符合两个类别的消息更加谨慎。
D. Instruct the model to be more careful with messages that could fit two categories.

3264
04:41:31,022 --> 04:41:32,228
稍停并决定。
Pause and decide.

3265
04:41:37,824 --> 04:41:45,028
答案是 A，这被刻意与场景 1 配对，在场景 1 中，标准优于示例。
The answer is A, and this is deliberately paired with scenario 1, where criteria beat examples.

3266
04:41:45,424 --> 04:41:48,036
区别在于失败的类型不同。
The difference is what kind of failure it is.

3267
04:41:49,166 --> 04:41:55,524
场景 1 是范围失败，即某个类别从未被命名过，而命名它就是解决方法。
Scenario 1 was a scope failure where a category had never been named and naming it was the fix.

3268
04:41:56,462 --> 04:42:04,708
这是一个边界失败，其中类别很清晰，难点在于决定两个清晰的类别中哪一个适用。
This is a boundary failure where the categories are clear and the difficulty is deciding which of two clear categories applies.

3269
04:42:05,264 --> 04:42:11,332
那属于判断问题，而判断比定义更容易展示。所以示例胜出。
That is a judgment call, and judgment is easier to demonstrate than to define. So examples win.

3270
04:42:12,238 --> 04:42:16,388
选项 B 只是在优化题干已经告诉你很清晰的定义。
Option B sharpens definitions that the stem tells you are already clear.

3271
04:42:17,358 --> 04:42:21,252
选项 C 创建了一个没人有处理流程的类别。
Option C creates a bucket nobody has a process for.

3272
04:42:21,806 --> 04:42:23,844
选项 D 只是一个形容词。
Option D is an adjective.

3273
04:42:25,326 --> 04:42:26,276
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

3274
04:42:26,926 --> 04:42:34,436
为了避免让审核人员负担过重，一份文档分析提示词要求仅报告高度置信的发现。
A document analysis prompt ends with only report findings you are highly confident about to avoid overwhelming reviewers.

3275
04:42:35,470 --> 04:42:40,644
审计发现，在模型报告为空的几份文件中，实际上存在多个重大问题。
An audit finds that several material issues were present in documents where the model reported nothing.

3276
04:42:41,230 --> 04:42:44,352
没有任何记录显示模型考虑并舍弃了哪些内容。
There is no record of what it considered and discarded.

3277
04:42:44,974 --> 04:42:49,316
审核人员表示，他们宁可看到不确定的发现，也不愿漏掉真实的发现。
Reviewers say they would rather see uncertain findings than miss real ones.

3278
04:42:50,254 --> 04:42:51,268
该如何修改？
What should change?

3279
04:42:51,790 --> 04:42:56,272
a. 将提示词中的置信度门槛降低到“合理置信”。
a lower the confidence bar in the prompt to reasonably confident.

3280
04:42:56,782 --> 04:42:56,992
b。
b.

3281
04:42:57,710 --> 04:43:03,472
报告所有发现并附带置信度评分，并在流水线中根据调整后的阈值进行过滤。
Report all findings with a confidence score and filter in the pipeline against a tuned threshold.

3282
04:43:04,014 --> 04:43:04,272
C。
C.

3283
04:43:04,782 --> 04:43:08,112
移除置信度指令，以便报告所有内容。
Remove the confidence instruction so everything is reported.

3284
04:43:08,432 --> 04:43:08,752
D。
D.

3285
04:43:09,230 --> 04:43:13,188
要求模型解释它为何舍弃了低置信度的发现。
Ask the model to explain why it discarded low confidence findings.

3286
04:43:13,902 --> 04:43:15,300
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3287
04:43:20,974 --> 04:43:22,592
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3288
04:43:23,054 --> 04:43:30,820
需要注意的句子是“没有记录显示模型考虑并舍弃了什么”，因为这个盲点才是问题的核心。
The sentence to notice is that there is no record of what the model considered and discarded because that blind spot is the actual problem.

3289
04:43:33,934 --> 04:43:34,432
选项分析
Options

3290
04:43:35,758 --> 04:43:38,752
A 和 D 都将过滤逻辑留在模型内部。
A and D both leave the filtering inside the model.

3291
04:43:39,152 --> 04:43:43,748
A 只是把一个隐形的阈值移动到了另一个稍微不同的隐形位置。
A moves an invisible threshold to a slightly different invisible place.

3292
04:43:44,272 --> 04:43:53,284
D 要求模型报告它已经默默做出的抑制决策，这比什么都没有好一点，但比不进行过滤要可靠得多。
D asks the model to report on a suppression decision it already made silently, which is better than nothing and considerably less reliable than not suppressing.

3293
04:43:54,062 --> 04:43:59,396
选项 C 通过重新制造原本为了防止而设计的“信息过载”来解决遗漏问题。
Option C fixes the misses by recreating the overwhelm the instruction was written to prevent.

3294
04:44:00,270 --> 04:44:06,884
只有 B 能提供记录、可调节的数值，并为不确定的发现提供去向。
Only B gives you a record, a tuneable number, and somewhere for uncertain findings to go.

3295
04:44:08,494 --> 04:44:09,636
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

3296
04:44:10,672 --> 04:44:14,340
一名工程师要求智能体为董事会总结季度业绩。
An engineer asks an agent to summarize the quarterly results for the board.

3297
04:44:14,752 --> 04:44:17,348
该智能体生成了一份两页的叙述性摘要。
The agent produces a two-page narrative summary.

3298
04:44:18,352 --> 04:44:21,732
工程师想要的是包含数字的半页要点。
The engineer wanted half a page of bullet points with figures.

3299
04:44:22,192 --> 04:44:25,636
他们再次提出更具体的请求，并得到了想要的内容。
They ask again more specifically and get what they wanted.

3300
04:44:26,606 --> 04:44:31,940
这种模式在许多不同用户提出的各种开放式请求中反复出现。
This pattern repeats across many different open-ended requests from many different users.

3301
04:44:32,782 --> 04:44:34,500
最好的通用修复方案是什么？
What is the best general fix?

3302
04:44:35,552 --> 04:44:42,020
A. 在系统提示词中添加默认输出格式，包含半页内容、要点和数字。
a add a default output format to the system prompt, half a page, bullets, figures included.

3303
04:44:42,766 --> 04:44:48,432
B. 让智能体在生成长输出前，先说明其对范围和格式的假设。
B. Have the agent state its assumptions about scope and format before producing long output.

3304
04:44:48,752 --> 04:44:52,964
C. 让智能体在每次请求前提出三个澄清问题。
C. Have the agent ask three clarifying questions before every request.

3305
04:44:54,190 --> 04:44:57,284
D. 添加几个简短的优质摘要示例。
D. Add few short examples of good summaries.

3306
04:44:58,030 --> 04:44:59,044
稍停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

3307
04:45:04,718 --> 04:45:06,112
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3308
04:45:06,672 --> 04:45:14,340
关键的判断词是：这种情况在许多不同用户的多种开放式请求中反复出现。
The deciding phrase is that this repeats across many different open-ended requests from many different users.

3309
04:45:14,926 --> 04:45:17,540
这排除了选项 A 和 D。
That rules out options A and D together.

3310
04:45:18,192 --> 04:45:25,552
因为这两个选项只针对特定摘要进行了修复，且对后续不同形式的请求没有帮助。
Because both fix summarization specifically and neither helps the next request, which will be a different shape.

3311
04:45:26,094 --> 04:45:28,292
选项 C 是过度纠正。
Option C is the overcorrection.

3312
04:45:29,198 --> 04:45:34,820
在大多数并不模糊的情况下，强加三个问题到每一次请求中。
Imposing three questions on every request when most of them are not ambiguous.

3313
04:45:35,246 --> 04:45:37,028
这样会导致到处产生摩擦。
So the friction lands everywhere.

3314
04:45:37,646 --> 04:45:46,352
陈述假设只需要一行，适用于各种类型的请求，并让用户在生成两页内容前有机会修正方向。
Stating assumptions costs a single line, generalizes across request types, and gives the user a chance to correct course before two

3315
04:45:46,512 --> 04:45:47,524
在写出两页内容之前。
pages have been written.

3316
04:45:48,334 --> 04:45:50,180
而且它是四个选项中最省成本的。
It is also the cheapest of the four.

3317
04:45:51,694 --> 04:45:52,900
场景 6。
Scenario 6.

3318
04:45:53,232 --> 04:45:59,684
一个提示词要求 Claude 提取政策文件中所有对客户施加义务的条款。
A prompt asks Claude to extract every clause in a policy document that imposes an obligation on the customer.

3319
04:46:00,334 --> 04:46:04,068
然后它必须按五分制对每项义务的严重程度进行评分。
It must then rate each obligation severity on a five-point scale.

3320
04:46:05,550 --> 04:46:08,676
当省略严重程度评分时，提取召回率很高。
Extraction recall is high when severity ratings are omitted.

3321
04:46:09,614 --> 04:46:17,220
当要求评分时，好几项义务完全丢失了，而提取出来的那些则被一致地评了分。
When ratings are requested, several obligations go missing entirely and the ones extracted are rated consistently.

3322
04:46:18,510 --> 04:46:20,004
团队需要这两项内容。
The team needs both.

3323
04:46:21,454 --> 04:46:23,472
最有效的做法是什么？
What is the most effective approach?

3324
04:46:24,005 --> 04:46:30,512
A. 在两个独立的调用中分别请求提取和评分，将提取出的条款输入到第二个调用中。
A. ask for extraction and rating in two separate calls, feeding the extracted clauses into the second.

3325
04:46:31,118 --> 04:46:36,004
B. 要求模型先提取所有内容，然后在同一个响应中进行评分。
b ask the model to extract everything first, then rate within the same response.

3326
04:46:36,366 --> 04:46:40,740
C. 强调无论评分工作量如何，都不应遗漏任何义务。
C. Emphasize that no obligation should be missed regardless of rating effort.

3327
04:46:41,072 --> 04:46:45,508
D. 将严重程度量表缩减到三分，以减轻评分负担。
D. Drop the severity scale to three points to reduce the rating burden.

3328
04:46:46,032 --> 04:46:47,332
稍停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

3329
04:46:53,248 --> 04:46:54,688
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

3330
04:46:55,022 --> 04:47:00,804
而选项 B 是一个值得理解的干扰项，因为它确实是一个部分有效的修复方案。
And option B is the distractor worth understanding because it is genuinely a partial fix.

3331
04:47:02,286 --> 04:47:07,780
要求模型在评分前先完成提取是有帮助的，因为它把召回任务提前到了前面。
Asking the model to extract fully before rating does help since it front loads the recall task.

3332
04:47:08,718 --> 04:47:15,204
两个任务仍在一个回复中运行并共享同一个注意力预算，所以召回率仍会下降，只是降幅变小了。
Both jobs still live inside one response and share one attention budget, so recall still degrades, just less.

3333
04:47:15,488 --> 04:47:18,128
分成两次调用可以完全消除这种竞争。
Two calls remove the competition entirely.

3334
04:47:18,368 --> 04:47:21,668
提取任务获得一个高召回率的独立调用。
Extraction gets a call to itself with high recall.

3335
04:47:22,048 --> 04:47:24,836
评分任务在固定的列表上进行一次调用。
Rating gets a call to itself on a fixed list. The

3336
04:47:25,488 --> 04:47:28,772
这种配对是在你的代码中完成的，而不是在模型的注意力中。
pairing happens in your code rather than in the model's attention.

3337
04:47:29,328 --> 04:47:29,892
选项
Option

3338
04:47:30,608 --> 04:47:36,452
C 选项明确了哪一半受影响，而 D 选项在不消除竞争的情况下缩小了竞争范围。
C swabs which half suffers, and option D shrinks the competition without ending it.

3339
04:47:37,870 --> 04:47:38,461
模块。
Module.

3340
04:47:38,461 --> 04:47:41,636
接下来是关于架构的第 13 章。
13 next on schemas.

3341
04:47:43,342 --> 04:47:46,724
第 13 模块，这是本课程中最长的模块。
Module 13, and this is the longest module in the course.

3342
04:47:47,088 --> 04:47:55,300
结构化数据提取是六个考试场景之一，其中的题目非常具体，因此很容易拿分。
Structured data extraction is one of the six exam scenarios, and the questions in it are unusually concrete, which makes them winnable.

3343
04:47:56,174 --> 04:47:56,848
两个部分。
Two halves.

3344
04:47:57,870 --> 04:48:05,124
第一，你如何获得符合规范的输出，这是整个课程中最大的知识差距所在。
First, how you get schema conformant output at all, which is where the biggest currency gap in the whole course lives.

3345
04:48:05,582 --> 04:48:12,836
第二，你如何设计架构让模型停止虚构内容，这才是得分的关键点。
Second, how you design a schema so the model stops inventing things, which is where most of the marks actually are.

3346
04:48:14,382 --> 04:48:16,420
这是整个模块的框架。
Here is the framing for the whole module.

3347
04:48:16,878 --> 04:48:22,756
当提取系统虚构数据时，直觉是增加一条指令告诉它不要这样做。
When an extraction system invents data, the instinct is to add an instruction telling it not to.

3348
04:48:23,088 --> 04:48:24,608
这几乎从来不起作用。
That almost never works.

3349
04:48:24,878 --> 04:48:27,652
而理解其中的原因正是这个领域的关键。
And understanding why is the key to this domain.

3350
04:48:28,174 --> 04:48:33,008
如果你的架构规定某个字段是必填项，模型就必须为它生成内容。
If your schema says a field is required, the model must produce something for it.

3351
04:48:33,550 --> 04:48:38,928
当文档中不包含该信息时，产出内容就意味着虚构内容。
When the document does not contain that information, producing something means inventing something.

3352
04:48:39,168 --> 04:48:41,092
是架构制造了这种压力。
The schema created the pressure.

3353
04:48:41,328 --> 04:48:43,620
所以修复方案应该在架构上着手。
So the schema is where the fix goes.

3354
04:48:44,366 --> 04:48:48,644
虚构往往是设计缺陷，而非模型的故障。
Fabrication is a design fault far more often than it is a model fault.

3355
04:48:50,318 --> 04:48:53,700
四个层级，每一层都能消除一类错误。
Four rungs and each one removes a class of failure.

3356
04:48:54,990 --> 04:49:02,916
要求提供 JSON 的礼貌提示通常有效，但在大规模应用时会有百分之几的失败率，而在高频场景下，这就是大量的错误记录。
Asking polite key for JSON usually works and fails several percent of the time at scale, which at high volume is a lot of broken records.

3357
04:49:03,328 --> 04:49:09,732
JSON 模式保证你获得有效的 JSON，但不能保证它符合你的结构。
JSON mode guarantees you get valid JSON and guarantees nothing about whether it matches your shape.

3358
04:49:10,574 --> 04:49:18,084
定义一个输入架构为目标结构的工具，并强制使用工具选择，这是考试的标准答案，也是一个很好的方案。
Defining a tool whose input schema is your target shape and forcing it with Tool choice is the exam's answer and it is a good one.

3359
04:49:19,470 --> 04:49:26,596
而语法约束生成会将你的架构编译成正式的语法，这样模型就不会输出任何可能破坏结构的字符。
And grammar constraint generation compiles your schema into a formal grammar so the model cannot emit a character that would break it.

3360
04:49:27,470 --> 04:49:29,668
无效输出并没有被抑制。
Invalid output is not discouraged.

3361
04:49:30,254 --> 04:49:31,648
这是无法达到的。
It is unreachable.

3362
04:49:33,102 --> 04:49:39,044
有必要具体说明一下「仅提示词输出JSON」为什么会失败，因为这些失败情况都很常见。
It is worth being specific about how prompt only JSON fails because the failures are mundane.

3363
04:49:39,790 --> 04:49:44,420
在对象周围加上 Markdown 围栏，因为它看起来像代码，而且模型在试图提供帮助。
Markdown fences around the object because it looks like code and the model is being helpful.

3364
04:49:45,102 --> 04:49:47,236
在它之前或之后加一句友好的话。
A friendly sentence before or after it.

3365
04:49:48,142 --> 04:49:54,020
字段被重命名，或者与你在散文中描述的结构略有不同的嵌套方式。
A field renamed or nested slightly differently from the shape you described in prose.

3366
04:49:54,382 --> 04:50:00,964
还有当输出配额耗尽时，在对象中间发生的截断，这我们在模块 1 中遇到过。
And truncation part way through an object when the output budget runs out, which we met in module 1.

3367
04:50:01,934 --> 04:50:08,868
这些情况都不是罕见到可以忽略的，因为一百万条记录中的 1% 就是 10,000 个错误。
None of these are rare enough to ignore at volume because 1% of a million records is 10,000 broken ones.

3368
04:50:09,168 --> 04:50:13,252
一旦生成受到约束，所有这些问题都会在解码层消失。
All of them vanish at the decoding layer once generation is constrained.

3369
04:50:14,862 --> 04:50:19,012
把这句话按原样记下来，因为这是考试要求的答案。
Learn this sentence as written because it is the answer the exam wants.

3370
04:50:19,328 --> 04:50:23,492
定义一个输入架构正是你想要得到的形状的工具。
Define a tool whose input schema is exactly the shape you want back.

3371
04:50:24,046 --> 04:50:26,372
通过工具选择强制模型调用它。
Force the model to call it with tool choice.

3372
04:50:27,054 --> 04:50:31,044
然后从工具调用块中读取你的数据，而不是从文本中读取。
Then read your data out of the tool use block rather than out of the text.

3373
04:50:31,950 --> 04:50:33,808
你实际上根本没有在调用工具。
You are not really calling a tool at all.

3374
04:50:33,968 --> 04:50:37,156
你是在借用工具机制，因为它自带一个架构。
You are borrowing the tool mechanism because it comes with a schema.

3375
04:50:37,408 --> 04:50:39,172
模型经过训练去遵循它。
The model is trained to respect.

3376
04:50:39,408 --> 04:50:42,884
这比在散文中描述相同的形状要可靠得多。
That is far more reliable than describing the same shape in prose.

3377
04:50:43,168 --> 04:50:46,756
这是长期以来的标准技术，而且依然有效。
That has been the standard technique for a long time and it still works.

3378
04:50:48,462 --> 04:50:52,836
这是考试和产品之间最大的差距。所以这里是完整的表述。
This is the largest gap between the exam and the product. So here it is in full.

3379
04:50:53,328 --> 04:50:58,116
考试中关于保证架构符合性的答案就是工具技术。
The exam's answer to guaranteed schema conformance is the tool technique.

3380
04:50:58,608 --> 04:51:03,780
API 现在提供原生的结构化输出，通常有两种形式。
The API now has native structured outputs generally available in two forms.

3381
04:51:04,686 --> 04:51:12,004
一种是约束 Claude 说话内容的输出配置格式，另一种是约束 Claude 如何调用工具的工具上的严格标志。
An output configuration format that constrains what Claude says and a strict flag on a tool that constrains how Claude calls it.

3382
04:51:12,590 --> 04:51:14,564
两者都使用了语法约束采样。
Both use grammar constraint sampling.

3383
04:51:15,342 --> 04:51:17,648
它们解决不同的问题，并且可以结合使用。
They solve different problems and they combine.

3384
04:51:17,808 --> 04:51:23,812
这样智能体就可以调用具有保证有效参数的工具，并返回结构化的最终答案。
So an agent can call tools with guaranteed valid arguments and return a structured final answer.

3385
04:51:24,494 --> 04:51:30,308
而且模块 12 列出的预填充技术在最新的模型上不再受支持了。
And pre filling which module 12 listed as a technique is no longer supported on the latest models.

3386
04:51:32,046 --> 04:51:37,380
即使是在最高级别，也有限制，了解这些可以防止产生虚假的安全感。
Even at the top rung, there are limits, and knowing them prevents a false sense of safety.

3387
04:51:37,632 --> 04:51:45,860
语法约束可以强制类型、必填字段、枚举、嵌套以及不包含额外属性。因此，形状是真正得到保证的。
A glamour can enforce types, required fields, enums, nesting, and the absence of extra properties. So the shape is genuinely guaranteed.

3388
04:51:46,734 --> 04:51:52,932
它无法强制数值范围、字符串长度或递归，因为支持的架构关键字只是一个子集。
It cannot enforce numeric bounds, string lengths, or recursion because the supported schema keywords are a subset.

3389
04:51:53,312 --> 04:52:00,548
而且它肯定无法强制业务规则，比如结束日期必须在开始日期之后，或者总计必须等于各项内容的总和。
And it certainly cannot enforce business rules like an end date falling after a start date or a total matching the sum of the line items.

3390
04:52:01,152 --> 04:52:03,236
所以你仍然需要一个验证层。
So you still need a validation layer.

3391
04:52:04,046 --> 04:52:07,268
语法负责处理结构，而你的代码负责处理含义。
The grammar handles shape and your code handles meaning.

3392
04:52:08,206 --> 04:52:11,620
约束解码是重新分配你的精力，而不是消除这些努力。
Constraint decoding moves your effort rather than removing it.

3393
04:52:13,262 --> 04:52:16,672
这就引出了本模块中更重要的一半内容。
Which brings us to the more important half of this module.

3394
04:52:16,942 --> 04:52:20,900
到目前为止的所有内容都在保证你的输出具有正确的结构。
Everything so far guarantees that your output has the right shape.

3395
04:52:22,414 --> 04:52:24,804
但这些都不保证数值是真实的。
None of it guarantees the values are true.

3396
04:52:25,792 --> 04:52:33,604
一条记录可能通过所有的架构检查，解析正常，却包含一个从未被发放过的发票号码。
A record can pass every schema check, parse cleanly, and contain an invoice number nobody ever issued.

3397
04:52:34,542 --> 04:52:39,140
这就是那种会进入生产环境的错误，因为它在整个流水线中看起来都正确无误。
That is the failure that reaches production because it looks correct all the way through the pipeline.

3398
04:52:39,792 --> 04:52:42,884
所以本模块的其余部分是关于设计架构。
So the rest of this module is about designing the schema.

3399
04:52:43,072 --> 04:52:47,204
这样模型就不会在第一步就被迫去虚构数值。
So the model is not pushed into inventing values in the first place.

3400
04:52:48,814 --> 04:52:53,028
架构决策中价值最高的一项是：哪些字段是必填的。
The single highest value schema decision is which fields are required.

3401
04:52:55,726 --> 04:53:02,432
当一个字段确实出现在每一份文档中，且能保证该键一定会存在时，设为“必填”才是正确的。
Required is correct when the field genuinely appears in every document and it guarantees the key will exist.

3402
04:53:03,406 --> 04:53:09,444
当数据缺失时，“必填”意味着模型必须填入点什么，而“填入点什么”就意味着虚构。
When the data is absent, required means the model has to put something there, and something means invention.

3403
04:53:10,432 --> 04:53:16,324
这是提取系统中造成虚构最常见的原因，且差距非常大。
That is the commonest cause of fabrication in extraction systems by a wide margin.

3404
04:53:17,678 --> 04:53:21,284
可选或可为空可以让缺失状态变得可表达。
Optional or nullable makes absence expressible.

3405
04:53:21,614 --> 04:53:23,908
这样“不存在”就成了一个有效的答案。
So not present becomes a valid answer.

3406
04:53:24,398 --> 04:53:27,204
这样下游的所有环节都能区分出“缺失”和“错误”。
And everything downstream can tell missing from wrong.

3407
04:53:27,886 --> 04:53:30,404
当数据存在时，这样做不会给你带来任何额外成本。
It costs you nothing when the data is there.

3408
04:53:31,374 --> 04:53:34,692
只有在确实始终存在的字段上才标记为必填。
Mark required only what is genuinely always present.

3409
04:53:36,110 --> 04:53:40,676
一个字段可以表示“无内容”有三种方式，它们代表的意思不同。
There are three ways for a field to carry nothing, and they mean different things.

3410
04:53:41,198 --> 04:53:45,700
Null 表示该字段适用于此记录，但值不在文档中。
Null says the field applies to this record and the value is not in the document.

3411
04:53:46,254 --> 04:53:50,340
省略键意味着该字段根本不适用于这类记录。
Omitting the key says the field does not apply to this kind of record at all.

3412
04:53:51,232 --> 04:53:54,756
空字符串则两者都不是，而且它是这三种情况中最糟糕的一种。
An empt string says neither, and it is the worst of the three.

3413
04:53:55,072 --> 04:53:59,072
因为它看起来像是数据，任何后续处理它的代码都会被误导。
It looks like data to every piece of code that touches it afterwards.

3414
04:53:59,312 --> 04:54:04,740
选择一种规范，记录下来，并让下游代码依赖于这个约定，而不是去猜测。
Pick one convention, document it, and make downstream code rely on it rather than guess.

3415
04:54:05,678 --> 04:54:13,828
“未说明”和“不适用”是截然不同的事实，如果架构无法区分它们，就会造成信息丢失。
Not stated and not applicable are genuinely different facts, and a schema that cannot tell them apart has lost information.

3416
04:54:15,534 --> 04:54:17,700
枚举非常强大，但它们有一个陷阱。
Enums are powerful and they have a trap.

3417
04:54:18,382 --> 04:54:25,380
枚举让无效值变得不可能，而不仅仅是不太可能，这正是你想要的。
An enum makes an invalid value impossible rather than merely unlikely, which is exactly what you want.

3418
04:54:26,094 --> 04:54:32,996
陷阱在于，封闭的枚举会强迫模型在现实情况不符合任何选项时，仍必须从你的成员中选一个。
The trap is that a closed enum forces the model to pick one of your members even when reality fits none of them.

3419
04:54:33,614 --> 04:54:37,860
一个特殊案例就会变成被错误分类的情况，而且没人能发现。
An unusual case becomes a miscategorized one and nobody finds out.

3420
04:54:38,192 --> 04:54:43,204
增加另一个成员并配合一个自由文本的详情字段，模型就可以诚实地表达了。
Add another member together with a free text detail field and the model can be honest instead.

3421
04:54:43,472 --> 04:54:50,244
细节字段随后会充当你的路线图，因为读取其他值可以告诉你下一个该把哪个成员添加到枚举中。
The detail field then doubles as your roadmap because reading the other values tells you which member to add to the enum next.

3422
04:54:51,598 --> 04:54:53,124
要求提供置信度。
Ask for confidence.

3423
04:54:53,870 --> 04:54:59,652
为每个记录或重要的字段提供一个置信度字段，并将其与数值并列放置。
A confidence field per record or per field for the ones that matter, sitting alongside the value.

3424
04:55:00,238 --> 04:55:05,828
这就是模块 12 的报告：将“所有内容”和“下游过滤”规则应用于提取过程。
That is module 12's report, everything and filter downstream rule applied to extraction.

3425
04:55:06,702 --> 04:55:13,872
增加一个计算出的标志位来判断记录是否需要审核，这样路由就是代码中的规则，而不是模型中的判断。
Add a computed flag for whether a record needs review, so routing is a rule in your code rather than a judgment in the model.

3426
04:55:14,112 --> 04:55:16,260
并且要对最后一点保持现实。
And be realistic about the last point.

3427
04:55:16,942 --> 04:55:24,580
置信度分数并非开箱即用就能校准的，所以只有在你针对带标签的数据集调整了阈值后，这个数字才有意义。
Confidence scores are not calibrated out of the box, so the number itself is only meaningful once you have tuned a threshold against a labeled set.

3428
04:55:25,232 --> 04:55:27,332
模块 17 会妥善涵盖这一点。
Module 17 covers that properly.

3429
04:55:27,552 --> 04:55:30,468
低置信度数值路由到人工处理是非常有用的。
A low confidence value route to a human is useful.

3430
04:55:30,752 --> 04:55:33,028
而静默忽略掉的字段则没用。
A silently omitted one is not.

3431
04:55:34,574 --> 04:55:38,596
有一种特定的架构形状值得记住它的名称，因为考试会用到它。
One schema shape is worth knowing by name because the exam uses it.

3432
04:55:39,342 --> 04:55:41,348
真实的文档往往自相矛盾。
Real documents contradict themselves.

3433
04:55:41,646 --> 04:55:46,340
修正后的合同、修订的账单、补充条款等通常附在末尾。
Amended contracts, revised invoices, addenda appendic to the end.

3434
04:55:46,894 --> 04:55:51,872
一个字段有两个不同的值，且两者都真实存在。
Two different values for one field and both of them genuinely appear.

3435
04:55:52,398 --> 04:55:59,460
单一的标量字段会迫使模型选择其中一个并静默丢弃另一个，而你永远不知道是哪一个被丢弃了。
A single scalar field forces the model to pick one and discard the other silently, and you will never know which.

3436
04:55:59,872 --> 04:56:07,076
相反，将其建模为一个列表，每个条目携带其数值、生效日期或来源。
Model it as a list instead, with each entry carrying its value and its effective date or its source.

3437
04:56:07,872 --> 04:56:15,012
然后让下游代码来决定哪一个适用，因为那是业务规则，而不是提取决策。
Then let downstream code decide which one applies because that is a business rule rather than an extraction decision.

3438
04:56:15,472 --> 04:56:18,116
没有任何提示词能修复结构错误的字段。
No prompt fixes a field that is the wrong shape.

3439
04:56:19,758 --> 04:56:22,724
两个 schema check 几乎无法解决任何问题。
Two schematrix catch errors for almost nothing.

3440
04:56:23,214 --> 04:56:26,992
提取声明的总额，并单独提取各项明细。
Extract the stated total and separately extract the line items.

3441
04:56:27,310 --> 04:56:29,316
然后在你自己的代码中进行对比。
Then compare them in your own code.

3442
04:56:29,838 --> 04:56:31,460
不匹配就是一个信号。
A mismatch is a signal.

3443
04:56:31,982 --> 04:56:35,396
这可能是一个提取错误，也可能是文档本身的真实错误。
It might be an extraction error or a genuine error in the document,

3444
04:56:36,046 --> 04:56:37,860
无论哪种情况都值得关注。
and either is worth knowing about.

3445
04:56:38,830 --> 04:56:43,492
其次，在任何需要验证的地方，要求提供数值的同时提供源文本。
Second, ask for the source text alongside a value wherever verification matters.

3446
04:56:43,982 --> 04:56:48,836
这样人工人员可以在几秒钟内检查可疑字段，而不需要重新打开文档。
A human can then check a suspicious field in seconds instead of reopening the document.

3447
04:56:49,072 --> 04:56:55,236
这两者起作用的原理是一样的：它们创造了冗余，而冗余正是让错误变得可见的原因。
Both work for the same reason. They create redundancy, and redundancy is what makes errors visible.

3448
04:56:55,758 --> 04:56:59,076
这就是实现在架构内部的验证。
This is verification living inside the schema.

3449
04:57:00,814 --> 04:57:04,708
规范化属于提取阶段，原因就在刚才提到的说明中。
Normalization belongs at extraction time, and the reason is in the call out.

3450
04:57:07,278 --> 04:57:15,460
在字段描述中注明格式。这样日期会以标准格式返回，金额作为小数，货币作为独立的代码。
State the format in the field description. So dates come back in a standard form, amounts as decimal numbers, and currency as a separate code.

3451
04:57:16,142 --> 04:57:18,532
把每个数值和它的单位分开。
Separate every value from its unit.

3452
04:57:19,310 --> 04:57:24,580
字符串里的磅号和逗号不是数字，会导致下游环节处理出错。
A pound sign and a comma inside a string is not a number, and somebody downstream will pass it badly.

3453
04:57:25,038 --> 04:57:31,332
在提取时就做这些操作，而不是事后处理，因为模型能看到上下文，而正则表达式不行。
Do this at extraction rather than afterwards, because the model can see the surrounding context and a regular expression cannot.

3454
04:57:32,078 --> 04:57:38,276
模型知道 3/4 这种写法在英国文档里是日期，而在美国文档里则是三月。
The model knows that a date written 3 slash 4 is able in a British document and March in an American one.

3455
04:57:39,918 --> 04:57:43,012
验证需要一个循环，有两种构建方法。
Validation needs a loop, and there are two ways to build it.

3456
04:57:43,534 --> 04:57:52,836
盲目重试会发送相同的请求。这样模型在多次尝试中学不到任何东西，而确定性的失败会以三倍的成本重复三次。
Blind retry resents the same request. So the model learns nothing between attempts and a deterministic failure repeats exactly 3 times at 3 times the cost.

3457
04:57:53,646 --> 04:57:58,756
有信息的重试会将验证错误传回，并标明是哪个字段出了什么问题。
Informed retry sends the validation error back, naming the field and what was wrong.

3458
04:57:59,152 --> 04:58:03,236
模型随后可以修正那个特定数值，循环就会收敛。
The model can then correct that specific value and the loop converges.

3459
04:58:04,590 --> 04:58:10,532
限制在 2 到 3 次尝试，然后升级处理，因为没有上限的纠错循环会导致成本超支。
Cap it at 2 or 3 attempts and then escalate because an uncapped correction loop is a cost incident.

3460
04:58:11,534 --> 04:58:17,092
这是模块 6 的错误设计课程出现在领域 4 中，逻辑是一样的。
This is module 6's error design lesson arriving in domain 4 and it is the same shape.

3461
04:58:18,446 --> 04:58:20,708
用于提取的模式识别。
Pattern recognition for extraction.

3462
04:58:21,166 --> 04:58:27,556
“看似合理但不存在的值”意味着模型无法获知的必填字段。所以把它设为可为空。
Plausible values that do not exist means a required field the model cannot know. So make it nullable.

3463
04:58:27,982 --> 04:58:31,940
“被强制归入错误类别”意味着一个没有逃生路径的枚举。
Forced into the wrong category means an enum with no escape hatch.

3464
04:58:32,494 --> 04:58:37,892
“修改后的值被静默丢失”意味着你原本需要带有效日期的列表，却用了标量。
The amended value is silently lost means a scalar where you needed a list with effective dates.

3465
04:58:38,798 --> 04:58:44,164
“符合 JSON 规范但数字错误”意味着合规不等于准确。所以增加交叉检查。
Valid JSON with wrong numbers means conformance is not accuracy. So add a cross-check.

3466
04:58:44,718 --> 04:58:50,596
“重试产生相同的失败”意味着应该把验证错误传回，而不是发送同样的请求。
Retrying producing the same failure means send the validation error back rather than the same request.

3467
04:58:51,822 --> 04:58:57,380
“无法区分缺失和零”意味着你需要为 null、省略和空值建立约定。
And cannot tell missing from zero means you need a convention for null, omitted, and empty.

3468
04:58:58,352 --> 04:59:01,312
几乎每一行都在指向架构。
Almost every row points at the schema.

3469
04:59:02,734 --> 04:59:03,552
5 行。
5 lines.

3470
04:59:03,792 --> 04:59:09,232
考试的答案是一个工具，其输入架构是你的目标形状，并强制使用工具选择。
The exam's answer is a tool whose input schema is your target shape, forced with tool choice.

3471
04:59:09,392 --> 04:59:14,212
语法能保证形状但不能保证含义，所以保留验证层。
A grammar guarantees shape and cannot guarantee meaning, so keep a validation layer.

3472
04:59:14,672 --> 04:59:19,712
模型无法获知的必填字段实际上是要求它去编造。
Required fields the model cannot know are effectively an instruction to fabricate.

3473
04:59:20,334 --> 04:59:27,428
枚举需要增加另一个成员，矛盾的文档需要用列表，且数值需要将单位分开。
Enums need another member, contradictory documents need a list, and values need their units kept separate.

3474
04:59:27,950 --> 04:59:32,580
并通过返回错误来重试，设置上限，然后升级处理。
And retry by sending the error back, capped, then escalate.

3475
04:59:33,454 --> 04:59:34,756
现在有 7 个场景。
7 scenarios now.

3476
04:59:35,598 --> 04:59:40,484
三个关于架构设计，两个关于 retry 循环，两个关于可靠性阶梯。
Three on schema design, two on the retree loop, and two on the reliability ladder.

3477
04:59:42,192 --> 04:59:43,300
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

3478
04:59:43,632 --> 04:59:52,512
一个发票提取系统返回一个包含供应商名称、发票编号、总金额、采购订单参考和到期日的架构，
An invoice extraction system returns a schema with supplier name, invoice number, total amount, purchase order reference, and due date,

3479
04:59:52,672 --> 04:59:53,476
全部都是必填项。
all required.

3480
04:59:53,712 --> 04:59:57,220
大约每五张发票中就有一张没有采购订单参考。
About one invoice in five has no purchase order reference.

3481
04:59:57,806 --> 05:00:03,684
对于这些情况，提取出的值是一个看起来像参考号、但实际上在文档中任何地方都没出现过的值。
For those, the extracted value is a plausible looking reference that appears nowhere in the document.

3482
05:00:04,110 --> 05:00:08,260
提示词已经说明了：不要猜测不存在的值。
The prompt already says, Do not guess values that are not present.

3483
05:00:08,910 --> 05:00:10,628
最有效的修复方法是什么？
What is the most effective fix?

3484
05:00:11,086 --> 05:00:17,472
a. 加强指令，并增加一个没有采购订单参考号的发票示例。
a strengthen the instruction and add an example of an invoice with no purchase order reference.

3485
05:00:17,966 --> 05:00:24,004
b. 将采购订单参考字段设为可为空，并在描述中说明 null 表示不存在。
b make the purchase order reference nullable and state in its description that null means not present.

3486
05:00:24,352 --> 05:00:24,592
C。
C.

3487
05:00:24,992 --> 05:00:28,772
后处理以检测那些在源文本中未出现的引用。
Post process to detect references that do not appear in the source text.

3488
05:00:29,232 --> 05:00:29,392
D。
D.

3489
05:00:29,872 --> 05:00:32,644
降低采样温度，让模型减少“创造性”发挥。
Lower the temperature so the model is less creative.

3490
05:00:34,446 --> 05:00:35,652
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3491
05:00:41,390 --> 05:00:42,436
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3492
05:00:43,214 --> 05:00:50,852
题干的最后一行是排除干扰项的关键，它起到了和模块 5 中那个“已知存在但无法获取”的场景相同的作用。
The last line of the stem is the eliminator, and it is doing the same job as the required but unknowable scenario back in module 5.

3493
05:00:51,278 --> 05:00:55,908
提示词已经要求不要猜测，这意味着你面临一个直接冲突。
The prompt already says do not guess, which means you have a direct conflict.

3494
05:00:56,302 --> 05:01:00,036
架构定义说明该字段是必填项，所以必须生成一个值。
The schema says this field is required, so produce a value.

3495
05:01:00,942 --> 05:01:03,204
而提示词又说不要虚构。
The prompt says do not invent.

3496
05:01:03,470 --> 05:01:08,068
模型无法同时满足这两个要求，而架构定义在结构上具有更高优先级。
The model cannot satisfy both, and the schema wins because it is structural.

3497
05:01:08,656 --> 05:01:12,324
选项 A 只是在强化那个冲突中处于劣势的一方。
Option A adds emphasis to the losing side of that conflict.

3498
05:01:13,582 --> 05:01:18,468
选项 D 值得提一下，因为“温度”是一个常见的干扰项，但在这种情况下是错误的。
Option D is worth naming because temperature is a popular answer and it is wrong here.

3499
05:01:19,278 --> 05:01:21,456
模型仍然必须填补这个字段。
The model still has to fill the field.

3500
05:01:21,966 --> 05:01:24,452
降低温度只会让它更一致地去填充这个值。
It will just fill it more consistently.

3501
05:01:25,870 --> 05:01:33,252
场景 2。一个合同提取架构中，有“终止通知天数”字段，定义为单个整数。
Scenario 2. A contract extraction schema has a termination notice days field defined as a single integer.

3502
05:01:34,478 --> 05:01:36,452
几份合同经过了修订。
Several contracts have been amended.

3503
05:01:37,456 --> 05:01:42,336
原条款是 30 天，补充协议将其改为 90 天。
The original states 30 days and an addendum changes it to 90.

3504
05:01:42,862 --> 05:01:48,484
提取出的值有时是 30，有时是 90，且没有任何提示表明这两个数值同时存在。
The extracted value is sometimes 30 and sometimes 90, with no indication that both exist.

3505
05:01:48,816 --> 05:01:51,844
法律部门需要知道这两个数值以及哪一个是当前的。
Legal need to know both values and which is current.

3506
05:01:52,496 --> 05:01:53,696
应该做出什么修改？
What should change?

3507
05:01:54,030 --> 05:01:58,340
a. 指示模型始终优先选择最新修订中的数值。
a instruct the model to always prefer the value from the most recent amendment.

3508
05:01:59,246 --> 05:02:05,936
b. 将该字段建模为条目列表，每个条目包含数值、生效日期和来源引用。
b. Model the field as a list of entries, each with a value, an effective date, and a source reference.

3509
05:02:06,256 --> 05:02:09,216
c. 添加一个用于记录修订后数值的第二个字段。
C. Add a second field for the amended value.

3510
05:02:09,456 --> 05:02:13,220
d. 在整数旁边增加一个“是否已修订”的布尔值标记。
D. Add a Boolean has been amended, flag alongside the integer.

3511
05:02:13,614 --> 05:02:14,788
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3512
05:02:20,496 --> 05:02:22,176
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3513
05:02:22,638 --> 05:02:28,496
法律要求同时知道这两个值，这排除了所有只选一个并舍弃另一个的选项。
Legal need to know both values, which eliminates every option that picks one and discards the other.

3514
05:02:28,750 --> 05:02:37,956
选项 A 明确做了这一点，但它还要求模型去裁定哪项修订生效，这是一个法律问题，而不是提取问题。
Option A does that explicitly and it also asks the model to arbitrate which amendment governs, which is a legal question rather than an extraction.

3515
05:02:38,670 --> 05:02:45,924
1. 选项 C 是最强的干扰项，因为它保留了两个值，但它只适用于恰好一种情况的修订。
1. Option C is the strongest distractor because it does keep both and it only works for exactly one amendment.

3516
05:02:46,176 --> 05:02:52,100
被修改过两次的合同会破坏这种结构，而且你现在有两个不同格式的字段里存着同一个事实。
A contract amended twice breaks it, and you now have the same fact living in two differently shaped fields.

3517
05:02:52,496 --> 05:02:56,416
选项 D 告诉你某些东西丢失了，但没告诉你是什么丢了。
Option D tells you something was lost without telling you what.

3518
05:02:57,070 --> 05:03:02,020
这个字段的结构不对，无论你怎么正确填充它都无法解决这个问题。
The field was the wrong shape, and no amount of populating it correctly fixes that.

3519
05:03:03,502 --> 05:03:04,452
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

3520
05:03:04,736 --> 05:03:11,556
一个支持工单分类器使用包含六个类别的枚举，定义为一个没有其他选项的封闭集。
A support ticket classifier uses an enum with six categories, defined as a closed set with no other option.

3521
05:03:12,238 --> 05:03:18,084
审计发现，新型问题类型总是被分配到最接近的其中一个类别中。
An audit finds that novel issue types are consistently assigned to whichever of the six is nearest.

3522
05:03:18,894 --> 05:03:26,180
有一类关于新推出的功能的新投诉，在有人注意到之前，连续六周都被归类为账单问题。
A new class of complaint about a recently launched feature and for six weeks classified as billing before anyone noticed.

3523
05:03:27,054 --> 05:03:29,828
团队希望能更早地发现新的问题类型。
The team wants to catch new issue types earlier.

3524
05:03:30,286 --> 05:03:32,100
最有效的改进是什么？
What is the most effective change?

3525
05:03:32,942 --> 05:03:36,416
a. 为他们目前已知的问题类型添加类别。
a Add categories for the issue types they know about now.

3526
05:03:37,166 --> 05:03:42,016
b. 添加另一个带有必填自由文本描述的成员，并审查那些维基页面。
b. Add another member with a required free text description and review those wiki.

3527
05:03:42,736 --> 05:03:46,788
C. 添加一个置信度评分，并审查低置信度的分类。
C. Add a confidence score and review low confidence classifications.

3528
05:03:47,216 --> 05:03:50,820
D. 删除枚举，允许使用自由文本类别。
D. Remove the enum and allow free text categories.

3529
05:03:51,694 --> 05:03:52,900
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3530
05:03:58,574 --> 05:04:06,116
答案是 B，而选项 C 也值得认真考虑，因为置信度评分通常是一个很强的答案。
The answer is B, and option C deserves a proper hearing because confidence scoring is usually a strong answer.

3531
05:04:06,496 --> 05:04:07,812
再读一遍题干。
Read the stem again.

3532
05:04:11,630 --> 05:04:20,484
新问题总是被分配到最接近的类别中，而且那类新的投诉在六周内都被误判为账单问题。
Novel issues are consistently assigned to whichever category is nearest, and the new complaint class ran for six weeks as billing.

3533
05:04:21,454 --> 05:04:25,008
那是确定的错误分类，而不是不确定性。
That is confident misclassification rather than uncertainty.

3534
05:04:25,168 --> 05:04:27,748
所以置信度阈值无法识别出这种情况。
So a confidence threshold would not have caught it.

3535
05:04:28,398 --> 05:04:30,788
另一个成员改变了问题的性质。
Another member changes the shape of the problem.

3536
05:04:31,470 --> 05:04:39,172
新问题会作为独立类别显现出来，而不是隐藏在现有类别中，而且描述字段会告诉你接下来要添加什么。
The novel issue becomes visible as a category rather than hiding inside an existing one, and the description field tells you what to add next.

3537
05:04:41,166 --> 05:04:43,140
选项 A 只是在修补过去的问题。
Option A fixes the past.

3538
05:04:43,918 --> 05:04:47,236
选项 D 抛弃了枚举所提供的保证。
Option D throws away the guarantee the enum was giving you.

3539
05:04:48,814 --> 05:04:49,764
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

3540
05:04:50,158 --> 05:04:54,372
一个提取流水线会根据 JSON 架构验证每一条记录。
An extraction pipeline validates every record against a JSON schema.

3541
05:04:54,670 --> 05:05:00,292
当验证失败时，它会在记录失败前将相同的请求重新发送最多 3 次。
When validation fails, it resends the identical request up to 3 times before logging a failure.

3542
05:05:00,782 --> 05:05:06,928
分析显示，当一条记录失败时，三次重试都以完全相同的方式失败。
Analysis shows that when a record fails, all three retrees fail in exactly the same way.

3543
05:05:07,470 --> 05:05:14,148
最常见的错误是日期字段显示为 Q3 2026，而架构要求提供完整的日期。
The most common failure is a date field arriving as Q3 2026 where the schema requires a full date.

3544
05:05:15,054 --> 05:05:19,460
这些记录的重试成本是成功路径成本的三倍。
Retree costs are three times the successful path cost on those records.

3545
05:05:20,814 --> 05:05:22,244
应该做出什么改变？
What should change?

3546
05:05:23,246 --> 05:05:28,740
a. 将验证错误连同重试一起发回，并标明字段名称和要求的格式。
a send the validation error back with the retree, naming the field and the required format.

3547
05:05:29,454 --> 05:05:29,728
b。
b.

3548
05:05:30,094 --> 05:05:31,876
将重试次数增加到 5 次。
Increase the retry count to 5.

3549
05:05:32,208 --> 05:05:36,288
c. 放宽架构以接受作为字符串的部分日期。选 B。
C. Loosen the schema to accept partial dates as strings. B.

3550
05:05:36,654 --> 05:05:39,268
在重试之间加入指数退避。
Add exponential backoff between the retries.

3551
05:05:39,728 --> 05:05:40,900
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3552
05:05:46,414 --> 05:05:50,020
答案是 A，到现在这个逻辑应该是自动化的。
The answer is A, and by now the signal should be automatic.

3553
05:05:50,288 --> 05:05:57,888
三次重试都以完全相同的方式失败，这意味着它是确定性的，也就是说重试策略无法解决问题。
All three retwees fail in exactly the same way, which means deterministic, which means no retree policy fixes it.

3554
05:05:58,190 --> 05:06:03,428
因此排除选项 D，而选项 B 会增加相同结果的成本。
Option D is ruled out for that reason, and option B multiplies the cost of the same outcome.

3555
05:06:04,334 --> 05:06:06,436
选项 C 是危险的。
Option C is the dangerous one.

3556
05:06:07,118 --> 05:06:10,208
放宽架构确实会让错误消失。
Loosening the schema does make the error disappear.

3557
05:06:10,448 --> 05:06:16,164
但如果接受 Q3 2026 到达字段中，下游系统仍会将其视为日期处理。
By accepting Q3 2026 into a field, something downstream will treat as a date.

3558
05:06:16,462 --> 05:06:24,772
这把一个明显的失败变成了隐蔽的错误。将错误发回给模型能提供它缺失的关键信息，即知道哪里出错了。
That converts a loud failure into a quiet one. Sending the error back gives the model the one thing it was missing, which is knowing what was wrong.

3559
05:06:26,126 --> 05:06:27,168
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

3560
05:06:27,408 --> 05:06:29,796
一个团队正在提取财务摘要。
A team extracts financial summaries.

3561
05:06:30,128 --> 05:06:35,012
每条记录都通过了架构验证，且每个字段的类型都是正确的。
Every record passes schema validation and every field has the right type.

3562
05:06:35,630 --> 05:06:43,652
抽查发现，在约 4% 的记录中，报告的总额与提取出的明细项总和不符。
A spot check finds that in roughly 4% of records, the reported total does not match the sum of the extracted line items.

3563
05:06:44,558 --> 05:06:48,068
因为验证通过了，所以之前没人去检查。
Nobody had been checking because validation was green.

3564
05:06:48,494 --> 05:06:50,564
他们希望能够自动捕捉到这些问题。
They want to catch these automatically.

3565
05:06:55,182 --> 05:06:57,444
最有效的改变是什么？
What is the most effective change?

3566
05:06:58,222 --> 05:07:04,740
a. 使用语法约束的结构化输出，以严格执行架构。
a use grammar constrained structured outputs so the schema is strictly enforced.

3567
05:07:05,488 --> 05:07:05,728
B。
B.

3568
05:07:06,318 --> 05:07:12,068
同时提取声明的总额和明细项，并在代码中进行比对并标记不匹配的情况。
Extract both the stated total and the line items and compare them in code flagging mismatches.

3569
05:07:12,528 --> 05:07:12,848
C。
C.

3570
05:07:13,248 --> 05:07:15,620
为总额字段添加更严格的类型。
Add a stricter type for the total field.

3571
05:07:16,142 --> 05:07:19,748
D. 要求模型在返回结果前核对一遍算术计算。
D. Ask the model to double check its arithmetic before returning.

3572
05:07:20,208 --> 05:07:21,508
稍停并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

3573
05:07:27,248 --> 05:07:28,768
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3574
05:07:29,088 --> 05:07:38,688
埋下的细节是：所有记录都已经通过了带正确类型的架构验证，这一事实同时排除了选项 A 和 C。
The planted detail is that every record already passes schema validation with correct types, and that single fact eliminates options A and C together.

3575
05:07:38,848 --> 05:07:42,052
这两个选项都只是强化了一个已经在正常工作的架构。
Both strengthen a schema that is already doing its job.

3576
05:07:42,768 --> 05:07:46,020
这是本模块前面提到的那个幻灯片的具体案例。
This is the slide from earlier in the module made concrete.

3577
05:07:46,894 --> 05:07:53,604
语法保证结构且无法表达业务规则，而“总计等于各项之和”就是一个业务规则。
A grammar guarantees shape and cannot express a business rule, and total equals the sum of the line items is a business rule.

3578
05:07:56,366 --> 05:08:05,828
选项 D 很诱人，因为算术看起来可以核查，但在同一上下文中进行自我验证是最弱的一种形式，且在失败时不会产生任何记录。
Option D is tempting because arithmetic feels checkable, but self-verification in the same context is the weakest form and it produces no record when it fails.

3579
05:08:06,350 --> 05:08:09,860
只有 B 能创建出你的代码可以执行的冗余逻辑。
Only B creates redundancy your code can act on.

3580
05:08:11,534 --> 05:08:12,580
场景 6。
Scenario 6.

3581
05:08:16,046 --> 05:08:18,564
正在构建一个新的提取服务。
A new extraction service is being built.

3582
05:08:19,022 --> 05:08:27,844
Teen 代码原型要求模型返回符合此结构的 JSON，并将一个示例对象粘贴到提示词中。
The teens prototype asks the model to return the result as JSON matching this structure and pastes an example object into the prompt.

3583
05:08:28,142 --> 05:08:29,924
在低流量情况下，它运行良好。
At low volume, it works.

3584
05:08:30,862 --> 05:08:36,048
在 50,000 份文档的负载测试中，大约有 900 个响应无法通过。
In a load test of 50,000 documents, around 900 responses could not be passed.

3585
05:08:36,654 --> 05:08:42,564
Markdown 围栏、一段前导词，以及在少数情况下，一个重命名字段。
Markdown fences, a preamble sentence, and in a handful of cases, a rename field.

3586
05:08:43,406 --> 05:08:45,732
团队正在决定发布前的处理方案。
The team is deciding what to do before launch.

3587
05:08:46,702 --> 05:08:48,548
最合适的更改是什么？
What is the most appropriate change?

3588
05:08:49,262 --> 05:08:55,116
A. 添加一个正则表达式，在传递前进行清理步骤以去除围栏和前导词。
a add a regular expression, cleanup step that strips fences and preamble before passing.

3589
05:08:55,790 --> 05:09:00,836
B. 将目标结构定义为工具输入架构，并利用工具选择强制执行。
B. Define the target shape as a tool input schema and force it with tool choice.

3590
05:09:01,390 --> 05:09:06,916
C. 在提示词中用大写字母加上“仅返回 JSON，不要其他文本”。
C. Add return only JSON with no other text to the prompt in capital letters.

3591
05:09:07,726 --> 05:09:07,968
D。
D.

3592
05:09:08,718 --> 05:09:12,128
对任何无法通过的响应重试最多三次。
Retry any unpassable response up to three times.

3593
05:09:12,398 --> 05:09:13,732
稍停并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

3594
05:09:19,374 --> 05:09:20,420
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3595
05:09:20,768 --> 05:09:24,580
注意这种故障是如何呈现的，因为它具有典型特征。
Notice how the failure presents because it is characteristic.

3596
05:09:24,848 --> 05:09:28,740
在低流量时运行良好，但在高负载下崩溃。
It works fine at low volume and falls apart under load.

3597
05:09:29,008 --> 05:09:33,348
当你处理足够的文档并能看到数据时，这就是百分比失败率的真实样貌。
That is what a percentage failure rate looks like once you run enough documents to see it.

3598
05:09:34,766 --> 05:09:38,148
选项 A 是许多团队会采用的务实做法。
Option A is the pragmatic answer many teams reach for.

3599
05:09:38,990 --> 05:09:44,836
它解决了三种故障类别中的两种，不影响重命名字段，但现在你需要维护一个解析器。
It handles two of the three failure classes, leaves rename fields untouched, and you now maintain a parser.

3600
05:09:45,486 --> 05:09:50,852
选项 D 将设计问题视为瞬时的，而检索失败的概率大致相同。
Option D treats the design problem as a transient one and the retrieves fail at roughly the same rate.

3601
05:09:51,248 --> 05:09:54,148
选项 C 是强调重点，这是模块 12 处理的内容。
Option C is emphasis, which module 12 dealt with.

3602
05:09:54,926 --> 05:10:00,100
将数据从纯文本中移出并放入架构中，可以一次性解决所有三类问题。
Moving the shape out of prose and into a schema removes all three classes at once.

3603
05:10:01,614 --> 05:10:07,236
场景 7 中，一个物流提取架构中的重量字段被定义为字符串。
Scenario 7 A logistics extraction schema has a weight field defined as a string.

3604
05:10:07,888 --> 05:10:14,436
源文档将重量写成 2.5 千克、5 磅或 2500 克。
Source documents write weights as 2.5 kilograms, 5 pounds, or 2500 grams.

3605
05:10:15,950 --> 05:10:20,964
在下游，一个服务会解析这些字符串，将重量与运输阈值进行对比。
Downstream, a service parses these strings to compare weights against shipping thresholds.

3606
05:10:21,968 --> 05:10:27,716
今年已经出错了三次，其中两次是磅单位，一次是带逗号的数值。
It has been wrong three times this year, twice on pounds and once on a value written with a comma.

3607
05:10:28,048 --> 05:10:29,888
团队希望停止这种情况。
The team wants this to stop.

3608
05:10:30,254 --> 05:10:31,328
应该做出什么改变？
What should change?

3609
05:10:31,568 --> 05:10:35,044
a. 改进下游解析器以处理更多格式。
a improve the downstream parser to handle more formats.

3610
05:10:35,728 --> 05:10:36,048
b.
b.

3611
05:10:36,368 --> 05:10:41,860
在提取时，提取出数值重量，并提供一个独立的、经过归一化的单位枚举。
Extract a numeric weight value and a separate weight unit enum normalized at extraction time.

3612
05:10:42,608 --> 05:10:42,848
C.
C.

3613
05:10:43,248 --> 05:10:46,308
指示模型始终将重量转换为千克。
Instruct the model to always convert weights to kilograms.

3614
05:10:47,088 --> 05:10:47,408
D.
D.

3615
05:10:47,758 --> 05:10:51,396
增加验证规则，拒绝解析器无法读取的重量。
Add a validation rule rejecting weights the parser cannot read.

3616
05:10:52,622 --> 05:10:53,668
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3617
05:10:59,374 --> 05:11:01,568
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3618
05:11:02,414 --> 05:11:05,380
核心原则是：在上下文所在的地方进行归一化。
The principle is normalize where the context is.

3619
05:11:06,254 --> 05:11:13,668
在提取时，模型可以看到数字旁边的单位、文档、惯例以及周围的文本。
At extraction time, the model can see the unit written next to the number, the documents, conventions, and the surrounding text.

3620
05:11:14,702 --> 05:11:19,364
等到下游解析器拿到字符串时，所有这些信息都消失了，它只能靠猜。
By the time a downstream parser gets a string, all of that is gone and it is guessing.

3621
05:11:20,334 --> 05:11:22,448
选项 C 是一个非常接近但错误的选项。
Option C is the interesting near miss.

3622
05:11:25,550 --> 05:11:28,452
转换为千克确实能提供一个可比对的数字。
Converting to kilograms does give a comparable number.

3623
05:11:29,235 --> 05:11:35,652
但它也会丢弃原始信息，并要求模型在后台进行单位换算，导致错误无法修复。
It also discards the original and asks the model to do unit arithmetic invisibly, so an error is unrecoverable.

3624
05:11:36,654 --> 05:11:42,948
将数值与单位分离可以保留两者。让模型负责读取，让你的代码来做数学计算。
Separating value from unit keeps both. Let's the model do the reading and your code do the maths.

3625
05:11:47,310 --> 05:11:48,324
模块 14。
Module 14.

3626
05:11:49,198 --> 05:11:51,396
接下来是成本和规模。
Next on cost and scale.

3627
05:11:53,166 --> 05:11:55,108
模块 14 结束。
Module 14 closes.

3628
05:11:55,886 --> 05:11:57,604
领域 4。
Domain 4.

3629
05:11:58,126 --> 05:12:05,872
这是课程中最短的一个模块，也是最容易回答的，因为决策很明确且数据是公开的。
This is the shortest module in the course and one of the most answerable because the decisions are concrete and the numbers are published.

3630
05:12:06,126 --> 05:12:10,308
批处理、截断、缓存和模型选择。
Batch processing, truncation, caching, and model choice.

3631
05:12:11,214 --> 05:12:17,220
其中有一个核心问题贯穿始终。如果你从这个模块中只能记住一点，那就是这个问题。
One question sits underneath most of it. And if you take nothing else from this module, take that question.

3632
05:12:17,632 --> 05:12:19,524
是否有人在等待这个答案？
Is anybody waiting for this answer?

3633
05:12:19,872 --> 05:12:25,316
考试中几乎所有的成本和延迟问题，都是由 STEM 的回答来决定的。
Almost every cost and latency question on the exam is decided by how the STEM answers it.

3634
05:12:26,958 --> 05:12:31,396
这是决策规则，而且建议按这种逻辑去记忆。
Here is the decision rule, and it is worth learning in exactly this shape.

3635
05:12:33,422 --> 05:12:40,452
如果用户正盯着屏幕等待结果，你就需要同步调用，且延迟是硬性限制。
If a user is staring at a screen waiting for the result, you need a synchronous call and latency is a hard constraint.

3636
05:12:41,070 --> 05:12:48,420
如果用户提交了任务并继续操作，或者因为是夜间任务根本没人实时提交，那么延迟就不是约束条件。
If a user submitted a task and moved on, or nobody submitted it at all because it is a nightly job, latency is not a constraint.

3637
05:12:48,878 --> 05:12:51,140
在这种情况下，你是在为没人需要的速度买单。
You are then paying for speed nobody needs.

3638
05:12:51,630 --> 05:12:54,180
Anthropic 对这个问题的定义与之类似。
Anthropic's own framing of the question is similar.

3639
05:12:54,894 --> 05:12:59,428
该响应在 24 小时内送达是否可以接受？
Would it be acceptable for this response to arrive within 24 hours?

3640
05:13:00,942 --> 05:13:02,212
核心数据如下。
The headline numbers.

3641
05:13:02,958 --> 05:13:08,036
输入和输出 Token 的标准费率均减免 50%。
50% of standard rates applied to both input and output tokens.

3642
05:13:08,846 --> 05:13:14,660
折扣是无条件的，因此没有达到数量门槛的要求，哪怕只有 10 个请求的一组批处理也能享受。
The discount is unconditional, so there is no volume threshold to reach, and a batch of 10 requests gets it.

3643
05:13:15,278 --> 05:13:20,516
周转时间最长为 24 小时，但大多数批处理会在几分钟到几小时内完成。
Turnaround is up to 24 hours, with most batches finishing in minutes to hours.

3644
05:13:21,454 --> 05:13:29,604
要按最坏情况来预估预算，而不是按典型情况。每批次最多可提交 100,000 个请求或 256 MB 的数据。
Budget for the worst case rather than the typical one. You can submit up to 100,000 requests or 256 MB per batch.

3645
05:13:30,158 --> 05:13:34,436
每个请求都有一个自定义 ID，结果会关联回该 ID。
Each request carries a custom ID and results are keyed back to it.

3646
05:13:35,342 --> 05:13:39,652
结果以 JSON 行格式送达，并保留 29 天。
Results arrive as JSON lines and stay available for 29 days.

3647
05:13:41,358 --> 05:13:43,204
有 4 个值得了解的运营细节。
4 operational details worth knowing.

3648
05:13:43,630 --> 05:13:49,604
没有 Webhook，因此你需要轮询状态，你的流水线必须按此逻辑构建，而不是依赖回调。
There are no webhooks, so you poll for status and your pipeline has to be built for that rather than for a callback.

3649
05:13:50,030 --> 05:13:55,524
结果在 29 天后过期，因此在批处理完成后应立即将其复制到你自己的存储中。
Results expire after 29 days, so copy them into your own storage as soon as the batch completes.

3650
05:13:56,302 --> 05:14:00,352
自定义 ID 是将结果匹配回记录的方法。
The custom IDE is how you match a result back to a record.

3651
05:14:00,814 --> 05:14:05,312
把它作为内部标识符，而不是行号，因为行号可能会变动。
Make it your internal identifier rather than a row number because rows move.

3652
05:14:05,552 --> 05:14:12,912
取消操作是尽力而为的，这意味着已经在处理中的请求仍可能完成，并且你仍需为其付费。
And cancellation is best effort, meaning requests already in flight may still complete and you will still be billed for them.

3653
05:14:13,678 --> 05:14:19,172
批处理是一个异步系统，并承担所有异步系统的相关义务。
Batch is an asynchronous system with all of an asynchronous system's obligations.

3654
05:14:20,512 --> 05:14:25,060
如果处理得当，批处理内部的失败情况表现是合理的。
Failures inside a batch behave sensibly if you handle them properly.

3655
05:14:25,614 --> 05:14:32,260
每个结果都会被单独标记为成功或错误，因此一个错误的请求不会导致整个批次失败。
Each result is individually marked succeeded or errored, so one bad request does not take down the batch.

3656
05:14:32,814 --> 05:14:36,356
在行级别处理错误，并且仅重新提交失败的部分。
Handle errors at the row level and resubmit only the failures.

3657
05:14:37,294 --> 05:14:44,004
为了修复 40 个错误而重新处理 10,000 条成功的记录是纯粹的浪费，而且考试会考到这一点。
Reprocessing 10,000 successful records to fix 40 errors is pure waste, and the exam does ask that.

3658
05:14:44,558 --> 05:14:51,332
超过 24 小时窗口且过期请求不会被构建，也不会产生结果，因此需要重新提交。
A request that expires past the 24 hour window is not built and also produces no result, so it needs resubmitting.

3659
05:14:52,590 --> 05:14:54,912
并且要接受批处理带来的真实成本。
And accept the real cost of batching.

3660
05:14:55,374 --> 05:15:01,540
错误会在数小时后批量送达，因此你会失去同步调用所提供的即时反馈。
Errors arrive hours later in bulk, so you lose the immediate feedback a synchronous call gives you.

3661
05:15:03,182 --> 05:15:06,436
一旦提出问题，这两列的区别就很明确了。
The two columns are unambiguous once you ask the question.

3662
05:15:06,862 --> 05:15:15,673
批处理适用于：批量任务、夜间作业、回填、批量分类、评估、离线分析、审核队列
Batch suits, nightly jobs, batfills, bulk classification, evaluations, offline analysis, moderation queues,

3663
05:15:15,872 --> 05:15:16,868
以及数据标注。
and data labeling.

3664
05:15:17,646 --> 05:15:22,980
同步模式适用于实时对话，或者客户要求立即得到回复的任何情况。
Synchronous is for anything in a live conversation or a customer expecting a reply now.

3665
05:15:23,854 --> 05:15:28,228
还有那些需要在决定下一步之前获取上一个结果的智能体循环。
Also an agent loop that needs each result before deciding the next step.

3666
05:15:28,942 --> 05:15:33,540
注意这个“调用”词汇，因为它排除了人们有时会选错的那个选项。
And note the call out because it rules out an answer people sometimes reach for.

3667
05:15:34,382 --> 05:15:37,092
智能体循环不能在批处理上运行。
An agentic loop cannot run on batch.

3668
05:15:37,646 --> 05:15:43,492
每一步都依赖于前一个结果，所以每步耗时 24 小时的并不是更慢的系统。
Every step depends on the previous result, so a 24 hour turnaround per step is not a slower system.

3669
05:15:45,006 --> 05:15:46,116
它根本就不是一个系统。
It is not a system.

3670
05:15:47,712 --> 05:15:51,204
这个领域最强有力的答案通常会拒绝这种非黑即白的二选一。
The strongest answers in this area often refuse the binary.

3671
05:15:51,472 --> 05:15:53,860
大多数工作并不是全部都很紧急。
Most workloads are not uniformly urgent.

3672
05:15:54,192 --> 05:15:59,076
只有少数情况确实需要立即回复，其余的都可以等到过夜后再处理。
A minority genuinely needs a reply immediately, and the rest could wait overnight.

3673
05:15:59,392 --> 05:16:03,908
把它们一视同仁意味着要么为所有任务支付高昂费用，要么让所有任务都延迟。
Treating them identically means overpaying for all of them or delaying all of them.

3674
05:16:04,526 --> 05:16:10,724
将紧急的部分走同步路径，剩下的交给批处理，这就是一个拥有两条路径的系统。
Route the urgent slice synchronously and send the remainder to batch, which is one system with two paths.

3675
05:16:11,310 --> 05:16:16,484
决定走哪条路径的规则通常成本很低，而且往往根本不需要模型参与。
The rule deciding which path something takes is usually cheap and often does not need a model at all.

3676
05:16:17,294 --> 05:16:23,172
而节省的成本取决于有多少比例的任务可以等待，在实践中，这通常是大部分任务。
And the saving scales with how much of your volume can wait, which in practice is usually most of it.

3677
05:16:24,590 --> 05:16:28,656
要牢记这个区别，因为考试会故意模糊这两者的界限。
Keep this distinction keen because the exam blurs it deliberately.

3678
05:16:29,038 --> 05:16:36,196
并行处理能为你节省时间，但永远不会给你提供折扣，这是第三模块关于子智能体的课程内容。
Running things in parallel buys you all clock time and never buys you a discount, which is module 3's lesson about subagents.

3679
05:16:36,718 --> 05:16:39,780
批处理能给你提供折扣，但会消耗你的时间成本。
Batch buys you a discount and costs you all clock time.

3680
05:16:40,782 --> 05:16:44,772
它们的作用方向相反，并不是互相可以替代的。
They pull in opposite directions and they are not substitutes for one another.

3681
05:16:45,056 --> 05:16:49,572
所以当题干要求你降低成本时，并行性就不是答案。
So when a STEM asks you to reduce cost, parallelism is not the answer.

3682
05:16:49,856 --> 05:16:53,572
当它要求你降低延迟时，批处理就不是答案。
When it asks you to reduce latency, batch is not the answer.

3683
05:16:53,936 --> 05:16:57,636
在看选项之前，先读清楚问题中实际使用的词汇。
Read which word the question actually used before you look at the options.

3684
05:16:59,246 --> 05:17:02,564
提示词缓存是另一个杠杆，并且它可以与批处理叠加使用。
Prompt caching is the other lever and it stacks with batching.

3685
05:17:03,056 --> 05:17:09,956
许多调用可能共享一个长前缀，比如系统提示词、参考文档或一组示例。
Many calls may share a long prefix such as a system prompt, a reference document, or a set of examples.

3686
05:17:10,414 --> 05:17:15,012
这个前缀可以被缓存并重复利用，而不是按全额费用重新发送。
That prefix can be cached and reused rather than resent at full rate.

3687
05:17:15,950 --> 05:17:23,268
读取缓存的成本比全新的输入标记要低得多，尽管你最初写入缓存时仍需付费。
Cache reads cost considerably less than fresh input tokens, though you do pay to write the cache in the first place.

3688
05:17:23,616 --> 05:17:30,816
它可以在批处理中运行，且批处理折扣也适用于缓存定价。因此这两项节省可以叠加。
It works inside a batch and the batch discount applies to the cash pricing too. So the two savings compound.

3689
05:17:32,110 --> 05:17:34,148
限制条件在最后一行。
The limitation is in the last line.

3690
05:17:35,118 --> 05:17:38,576
每次调用都会变动的前缀无法被缓存。
A prefix that changes on every call caches.

3691
05:17:39,790 --> 05:17:40,356
无。
Nothing.

3692
05:17:41,934 --> 05:17:47,616
截断出现在这里，是因为它既是成本和规模问题，也是机制问题。
Truncation comes back here because it is a cost and scale question as much as a mechanics.

3693
05:17:47,982 --> 05:17:48,452
1。
1.

3694
05:17:49,678 --> 05:17:56,833
停止原因为“最大标记数”意味着输出超过了你设定的上限，任何结构化输出都会在中间断开。
A stop reason of max tokens means the output ran past the ceiling you set and any structured output is cut off mid structure.

3695
05:17:57,853 --> 05:18:01,796
完全相同的重发也会以同样的方式失败，因为它是确定性的。
Resending identically fails identically because it is deterministic.

3696
05:18:02,670 --> 05:18:05,572
当输出仅略微超出时，增加预算。
Raise the budget when the output was only just over.

3697
05:18:06,030 --> 05:18:11,940
当没有合理的预算能容纳任务时，拆分工作，分段提取后再合并。
Split the work when no reasonable budget would accommodate it, extracting in sections and combining afterwards.

3698
05:18:12,814 --> 05:18:19,652
并且要将其与“上下文窗口超出”区分开来，后者是整个请求太大，其解决方法正好相反。
And keep it distinct from the context window being exceeded, which is the whole request being too large and has the opposite fix.

3699
05:18:20,430 --> 05:18:24,900
提高上限可以处理接近失败的情况，拆分则处理其余情况。
Raising a ceiling handles near misses and splitting handles the rest.

3700
05:18:26,606 --> 05:18:29,956
五个杠杆，大致按它们影响程度排序。
Five levers, roughly in order of how much they move.

3701
05:18:30,446 --> 05:18:35,492
对可以等待的工作进行批处理，这本质上是调度上的改变，价格减半。
Batch the work that can wait, which is half price for what amounts to a scheduling change.

3702
05:18:37,102 --> 05:18:39,460
当公共前缀稳定时，使用缓存。
Cache the shared prefix when it is stable.

3703
05:18:40,462 --> 05:18:41,604
减少发送量。
Send less.

3704
05:18:41,966 --> 05:18:49,444
记住工具定义、示例和对话历史在每一次调用中都是输入标记。
Remembering that tool definitions, examples, and conversation history are all input tokens on every single call.

3705
05:18:51,886 --> 05:18:57,828
根据任务匹配模型，因为分类步骤不需要你最强大的模型。
Match the model to the task because a classification step does not need your most capable model.

3706
05:18:58,286 --> 05:19:01,456
并且正确界定任务范围，这是大家最容易忽略的一点。
And scope task properly, which is the one people miss.

3707
05:19:02,446 --> 05:19:05,924
成本超支很少是因为运行次数多。
Cost overruns rarely come from the number of runs.

3708
05:19:06,256 --> 05:19:11,876
它们源于一个定义模糊的任务在大家都预期只需三次时循环了 30 次。
They come from one badly scoped task iterating 30 times when everyone expected three.

3709
05:19:13,550 --> 05:19:24,516
模式识别。次日审核、每晚审核或回填，这些都意味着批处理，因为没人需要立即等待。客户在等待回复才意味着同步。
Pattern recognition. Reviewed the next morning, nightly, or backfill all mean batch because nobody is waiting. The customer is waiting for a reply means synchronous.

3710
05:19:24,910 --> 05:19:30,020
大多数请求都可以等待，但有些不行，这意味着要按紧急程度进行路由，而不是二选一。
Most requests can wait, but some cannot means route by urgency rather than choosing one.

3711
05:19:30,798 --> 05:19:37,412
在选项中通过并行执行来降低成本意味着并行并不减少成本。所以去别处找。
Reduce cost with parallel execution among the options means parallelism does not reduce cost. So look elsewhere.

3712
05:19:37,776 --> 05:19:44,388
在中间截断且重试失败一致意味着最大标记数。所以增加它或拆分工作。
Truncated midJ Sun with retrees failing identically means max tokens. So raise it or split the work.

3713
05:19:44,656 --> 05:19:49,028
而 10,000 次中失败了 40 次，意味着对失败项进行重提交，而不是批处理。
And 40 of 10,000 failed means resubmit the failures rather than the batch.

3714
05:19:49,936 --> 05:19:52,036
找到关于“谁在等待”的那句话。
Find the sentence about who is waiting.

3715
05:19:52,416 --> 05:19:54,852
它比任何其他因素都能决定更多情况。
It decides more of these than anything else.

3716
05:19:56,270 --> 05:19:57,536
最后 5 行。
5 lines to close.

3717
05:19:57,870 --> 05:19:58,660
领域 4。
Domain 4.

3718
05:19:59,726 --> 05:20:05,636
批处理在提供最多 24 小时的耐心换取时，无条件提供 50% 的折扣。
Batch gives 50% off unconditionally in exchange for up to 24 hours of patience.

3719
05:20:06,256 --> 05:20:11,908
询问谁在等待，如果没有人就是批处理，如果屏幕后面有人就是同步。
Ask who is waiting because nobody means batch and a person on a screen means synchronous.

3720
05:20:12,496 --> 05:20:17,936
智能体循环不能使用批处理，因为每一步都需要上一步的结果。
An agenticoop cannot use batch since each step needs the previous result.

3721
05:20:18,894 --> 05:20:27,296
并行处理可以节省时间，批处理可以节省成本，而缓存配合批处理并重试失败的任务，而不是直接提交整个批次
Parallelism buys time while batch buys money and caching stacks with batch and resubmit the failures rather than the batch

3722
05:20:27,536 --> 05:20:29,540
因为错误是按行记录的。
because errors are recorded per row.

3723
05:20:29,998 --> 05:20:31,456
现在有五个场景。
Five scenarios now.

3724
05:20:31,758 --> 05:20:34,852
接下来是领域五和上下文管理。
Then domain five and context management.

3725
05:20:36,590 --> 05:20:37,700
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

3726
05:20:38,222 --> 05:20:43,936
一个合规团队每月处理约 40,000 份文件用于政策分类。
A compliance team processes around 40,000 documents each month for policy classification.

3727
05:20:44,176 --> 05:20:47,588
分析师会在每周一的例会上审查结果。
Results are reviewed by analysts during their weekly Monday meeting.

3728
05:20:48,174 --> 05:20:55,108
目前的流水线将每份到达的文件都作为同步请求发送，且每月的账单已成为一个问题。
The pipeline currently sends every document as a synchronous request as it arrives and the monthly bill has become a concern.

3729
05:20:55,470 --> 05:20:59,172
在周一审查之前，不会使用任何单个文件的结果。
No individual document result is used before the Monday review.

3730
05:20:59,918 --> 05:21:01,764
最有效的改进是什么？
What is the most effective change?

3731
05:21:02,222 --> 05:21:05,124
A. 通过消息队列发送文档。
a send the documents through the message patches.

3732
05:21:05,742 --> 05:21:06,736
API。
API.

3733
05:21:07,536 --> 05:21:07,776
B
B

3734
05:21:08,654 --> 05:21:12,740
并行处理文档以减少总处理时间。
Process the documents in parallel to reduce total processing time.

3735
05:21:13,376 --> 05:21:16,900
C. 为所有分类切换到较小的模型。
C. Switch to a smaller model for all classifications.

3736
05:21:17,390 --> 05:21:17,616
D。
D.

3737
05:21:18,350 --> 05:21:21,604
减少最大 token 数，使回复更短。
Reduce max tokens so responses are shorter.

3738
05:21:22,606 --> 05:21:23,908
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

3739
05:21:29,678 --> 05:21:30,948
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

3740
05:21:31,406 --> 05:21:35,652
题干的最后一行在提示核心工作点，而且表述得非常明确。
The last line of the stem is doing the work and it is unusually explicit.

3741
05:21:36,256 --> 05:21:46,948
“周一审查前不使用任何单个结果”这句话直白地说明了延迟对该团队没有价值。他们目前正在为没人需要的速度支付全额费用。
No individual result is used before the Monday review, which says in plain terms that latency has no value to this team. They are currently paying full price for speed nobody uses.

3742
05:21:47,822 --> 05:21:53,696
选项 B 是典型的误区。他们用同样的成本去购买并不需要的实时响应时间。
Option B is the classic confusion. Buying wall clock time they do not need at exactly the same cost.

3743
05:21:53,936 --> 05:21:55,616
选项 C 可能行得通。
Option C might well work.

3744
05:21:55,856 --> 05:22:03,268
但它在没有证据的情况下用准确性换取成本。虽然小模型可能够用，但题干中没有任何信息表明他们测试过它。
It also trades accuracy for cost with no evidence. The smaller model is adequate and nothing in the stem suggests they tested it.

3745
05:22:04,078 --> 05:22:11,044
选项 D 针对的是输出 token，而在分类任务中，这部分仅占支出的极小一部分。
Option D-targets output tokens, which on a classification task are a small fraction of the spend.

3746
05:22:12,654 --> 05:22:13,540
场景 2。
Scenario 2.

3747
05:22:13,870 --> 05:22:17,700
一个客户支持产品在实时聊天组件中回答问题。
A customer support product answers questions in a live chat widget.

3748
05:22:18,542 --> 05:22:24,260
中位响应时间为 2.4 秒，且客户在超过约 8 秒无响应后会退出对话。
Median response time is 2.4 seconds and customers abandon the chat beyond about 8 seconds.

3749
05:22:24,846 --> 05:22:30,244
财务团队注意到了批处理 API 的 50% 折扣，并询问为什么没在使用。
The finance team has noticed the batch API's 50% discount and ask why it is not being used.

3750
05:22:31,136 --> 05:22:34,180
每月处理量约为 200,000 次对话。
Volume is around 200,000 conversations per month.

3751
05:22:34,416 --> 05:22:35,780
你应该如何回答？
How should you respond?

3752
05:22:36,603 --> 05:22:41,572
A. 批处理不能用于实时聊天，因此考虑在共享系统上使用提示词缓存。
A. Batch cannot be used for live chat, so consider prompt caching on the shared system.

3753
05:22:42,158 --> 05:22:44,649
针对简单查询，使用更短的提示词和更小的模型。
Prompt and a smaller model for simple queries.

3754
05:22:44,649 --> 05:22:45,703
B。
B.

3755
05:22:46,416 --> 05:22:50,724
对这些对话使用批处理，因为大多数在几分钟内就能完成。
Use batch for the conversations since most complete within minutes anyway.

3756
05:22:51,598 --> 05:22:56,580
C. 在非高峰时段使用批处理，那时客户不太可能在等待。
C. Use batch during off-peak hours when customers are less likely to be waiting.

3757
05:22:57,376 --> 05:23:03,236
D. 将每段对话拆分，第一条消息采用同步模式，其余的采用批处理。
D. Split each conversation so the first message is synchronous and the rest are batched.

3758
05:23:05,230 --> 05:23:06,404
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

3759
05:23:12,142 --> 05:23:18,340
答案是 A。选项 B 是一个值得纠结的干扰项，因为它包含的陈述是正确的。
The answer is A, and option B is the distractor worth dwelling on because the claim inside it is true.

3760
05:23:19,950 --> 05:23:22,020
大多数批处理确实能在几分钟内完成。
Most batches do finish in minutes.

3761
05:23:23,086 --> 05:23:30,372
但它仍然是错误的，因为你应该根据服务水平协议来设计，而不是根据中位数，而该协议是 24 小时。
It is still wrong because you design against the service level agreement rather than the median, and the agreement is 24 hours.

3762
05:23:31,310 --> 05:23:36,292
一个在 8 秒后就会流失客户的聊天系统，根本无法承受几分钟，更不用说几个小时了。
A chat that loses customers after 8 seconds cannot absorb minutes, let alone hours.

3763
05:23:36,576 --> 05:23:41,924
选项 C 误解了非高峰时段的含义，因为那些客户仍然在等待。
Option C misunderstands what off-peak means since those customers are still waiting.

3764
05:23:42,542 --> 05:23:45,700
选项 D 把紧急程度搞反了。
Option D has the urgency backwards.

3765
05:23:47,598 --> 05:23:52,484
注意是什么让 A 成为一个强有力的答案，而不仅仅是一个拒绝。
And notice what makes A a strong answer rather than merely a refusal.

3766
05:23:53,358 --> 05:23:58,596
它拒绝了错误的手段，并提供了两个符合延迟限制工作负载的方案。
It says no to the wrong lever and offers two that fit a latency bound workload.

3767
05:24:00,014 --> 05:24:00,900
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

3768
05:24:01,422 --> 05:24:05,572
一个包含 12000 条记录的文档提取批处理已完成。
A document extraction batch of 12,000 records completes.

3769
05:24:07,150 --> 05:24:15,492
结果显示有 11840 条成功，160 条出错，大部分是在异常长的文档上。
The results find shows 11,840 succeeded and 160 errored, mostly on unusually long documents.

3770
05:24:16,366 --> 05:24:23,172
一名工程师建议在提高最大标记数后重新提交整个批处理，以保持流水线简单。
An engineer proposes resubmitting the entire batch after raising max tokens to keep the pipeline simple.

3771
05:24:23,758 --> 05:24:26,148
每条记录的处理成本大致相同。
Each record costs roughly the same to process.

3772
05:24:26,830 --> 05:24:28,368
他们应该怎么做？
What should they do instead?

3773
05:24:28,814 --> 05:24:34,084
a. 按照建议重新提交整个批处理，因为简单是值得付出的成本。
a resubmit the whole batch as proposed since simplicity is worth the cost.

3774
05:24:34,766 --> 05:24:42,852
b. 仅重新提交匹配特定 ID 的那 160 条失败记录，并使用更高的最大标记数。
b resubmit only the 160 failed records matched by custom ID with the higher max tokens.

3775
05:24:43,342 --> 05:24:43,648
C。
C.

3776
05:24:44,142 --> 05:24:48,324
将整个流水线切换为同步请求，以便立即发现错误。
Switch the whole pipeline to synchronous requests so errors surface immediately.

3777
05:24:48,878 --> 05:24:49,168
D。
D.

3778
05:24:49,803 --> 05:24:54,528
为未来的批处理提高最大标记数，并接受这 160 条记录的损失。
Raise max tokens for future batches and accept the loss of these 160 records.

3779
05:24:54,768 --> 05:24:55,940
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

3780
05:25:01,326 --> 05:25:03,088
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3781
05:25:03,488 --> 05:25:14,212
而且这组数据比任何论证都更有说服力。重新提交整个批处理意味着为了修复 160 条记录，而去重新处理 11,840 条成功的记录。
And the arithmetic makes the point better than any argument. Resubmitting the whole batch reprocesses 11,840 successful records to fix 160.

3782
05:25:16,206 --> 05:25:21,220
这大约是为稍微简单一点的代码而付出的多余成本的 74 倍。
That is roughly 74 times the necessary cost for slightly simpler code.

3783
05:25:21,934 --> 05:25:23,888
系统里确实有逐行的错误报告。
Per row error reporting exists precisely.

3784
05:25:24,046 --> 05:25:29,956
所以你可以选择性地重新提交，而且因为有自定义 ID，你可以把结果对应回记录中。
So you can resubmit selectively and the custom ID exists so you can match results back to records.

3785
05:25:30,894 --> 05:25:32,740
不使用这两项才是错误的做法。
Not using either is the mistake.

3786
05:25:33,358 --> 05:25:39,488
选项 C 为了提高 1.3% 部分内容的错误可见性，导致整个工作负载的成本翻倍。
Option C doubles the price of the entire workload to improve error visibility on 1.3% of it.

3787
05:25:40,014 --> 05:25:44,484
选项 D 则会默默丢失 160 份文档。
Option D quietly loses 160 documents.

3788
05:25:45,870 --> 05:25:46,848
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

3789
05:25:47,150 --> 05:25:58,884
一个内部工具用于回答关于大型政策手册的问题。每个请求都会发送包含约 9 万个最大标记数的完整手册，后面跟着一个简短的问题。该手册大约每年变动两次。
An internal tool answers questions about a large policy handbook. Every request sends the full handbook about 90,000 tokens followed by a short question. The handbook changes roughly twice a year.

3790
05:25:59,726 --> 05:26:04,644
每天大约有 3,000 个问题，用户期望在几秒钟内得到回复。
Around 3,000 questions are asked per day and users expect an answer within a few seconds.

3791
05:26:05,230 --> 05:26:07,328
输入标记数的费用占了账单的大头。
Input token costs dominate the bill.

3792
05:26:07,630 --> 05:26:09,316
最有效的改进是什么？
What is the most effective change?

3793
05:26:09,742 --> 05:26:12,036
a. 将工作负载转移到批处理中。
a move the workload to the batch.

3794
05:26:12,288 --> 05:26:14,500
为了获得 50% 折扣而使用的 API。
API for the 50% discount.

3795
05:26:15,342 --> 05:26:21,860
b. 对手册前缀进行缓存，这样重复的问题就会从缓存中读取，而不是重新发送。
b. Cache the handbook prefix so repeated questions read from the cache instead of resending it.

3796
05:26:22,448 --> 05:26:22,688
C。
C.

3797
05:26:23,342 --> 05:26:26,436
对手册进行总结，然后发送摘要。
Summarize the handbook and send the summary instead.

3798
05:26:27,088 --> 05:26:27,408
D。
D.

3799
05:26:27,808 --> 05:26:30,244
减少响应的最大标记数。
Reduce max tokens on the response.

3800
05:26:30,766 --> 05:26:32,196
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

3801
05:26:37,902 --> 05:26:42,368
答案是 B，而且题干中的每一个细节都是缓存信号。
The answer is B and every detail in the stem is a caching signal.

3802
05:26:42,528 --> 05:26:46,020
长达 9 万个标记数的大型前缀。
A large prefix at 90,000 tokens.

3803
05:26:46,446 --> 05:26:48,292
每年变动两次的稳定性。
Stable changing twice a year.

3804
05:26:48,878 --> 05:26:52,196
因为每个请求都发送相同的手册，所以它是共享的。
Shared since every request sends the same handbook.

3805
05:26:52,750 --> 05:26:55,428
每天 3000 个问题意味着高频重复使用。
High reuse at 3000 questions a day

3806
05:26:56,206 --> 05:26:57,828
而且后面跟着的是一个简短的问题。
and a short question after it.

3807
05:26:58,766 --> 05:27:00,260
这就是教科书式的案例。
That is the textbook case.

3808
05:27:01,230 --> 05:27:08,932
选项 A 被一句话就排除掉了，因为用户要求在几秒内得到回复，而批处理唯一要求的条件就是耐心。
Option A is ruled out by a single phrase because users expect an answer within a few seconds and the one thing batch requires is patience.

3809
05:27:09,408 --> 05:27:18,468
选项 C 是一个很有趣的干扰项，因为总结确实能减少标记数，但它也会丢掉政策回答所依赖的准确措辞。
Option C is the interesting near miss because summarizing genuinely reduces tokens and it also discards exact wording which policy answers depend on.

3810
05:27:19,470 --> 05:27:22,852
选项 D 只针对了账单中较小的一部分。
Option D targets the smaller half of the bill.

3811
05:27:24,302 --> 05:27:25,604
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

3812
05:27:26,208 --> 05:27:29,796
一个审核系统正在审查用户提交的内容。
A moderation system reviews user-submitted content.

3813
05:27:30,638 --> 05:27:37,764
大约 8% 的提交内容被上游规则标记为可能紧急，必须在几分钟内处理。
About 8% of submissions are flagged by an upstream rule as potentially urgent and must be actioned within minutes.

3814
05:27:38,510 --> 05:27:43,588
剩下的 92% 是常规内容，由人工团队在第二天进行审核。
The remaining 92% are routine and are reviewed by a human team the following day.

3815
05:27:44,526 --> 05:27:49,892
目前所有内容都通过同步请求处理，每月处理量为 500,000 条。
Everything currently goes through synchronous requests at a volume of 500,000 items per month.

3816
05:27:51,086 --> 05:27:54,596
团队被要求在不减慢紧急路径的情况下降低成本。
The team has been asked to reduce cost without slowing the urgent path.

3817
05:27:55,662 --> 05:27:56,612
他们该怎么做？
What should they do?

3818
05:27:57,693 --> 05:28:00,164
A，将所有内容移至批处理
A, Move everything to the batch.

3819
05:28:00,846 --> 05:28:04,048
API 并接受紧急项目的延迟。
API and accept the delay on urgent items.

3820
05:28:04,448 --> 05:28:04,768
b。
b.

3821
05:28:05,198 --> 05:28:11,044
保持 8% 的紧急内容为同步，并将剩下的 92% 通过批处理
Keep the urgent 8% synchronous and send the remaining 92% through the batch.

3822
05:28:11,438 --> 05:28:12,260
API。
API.

3823
05:28:12,718 --> 05:28:12,928
C。
C.

3824
05:28:13,614 --> 05:28:17,252
保持所有内容为同步，并全程使用较小的模型。
Keep everything synchronous and use a smaller model throughout.

3825
05:28:17,888 --> 05:28:18,208
D。
D.

3826
05:28:18,862 --> 05:28:24,516
将紧急项目在夜间进行批处理，并在白天同步处理常规项目。
Batch the urgent items overnight and process routine items synchronously during the day.

3827
05:28:25,102 --> 05:28:26,212
稍等一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

3828
05:28:31,936 --> 05:28:38,116
答案是 B，它之所以特别强有力，是因为其中一个很容易被忽略的细节。
The answer is B, and what makes it particularly strong is a detail that is easy to skim past.

3829
05:28:38,734 --> 05:28:45,092
上游规则已经标记了紧急项目，所以分类已经完成，路由决策不消耗额外成本。
An upstream rule already flags the urgent items, so the sorting is done and the routing decision costs nothing.

3830
05:28:46,030 --> 05:28:52,976
500,000 项工作中的 92% 成本减半，且紧急路径未受影响。
92% of a 500,000 item workload moves to half price and the urgent path is untouched.

3831
05:28:53,230 --> 05:28:55,940
这完全符合题目要求的约束条件。
That satisfies the constraint exactly as written.

3832
05:28:56,846 --> 05:29:00,196
选项 A 直接违反了明确的要求。
Option A violates the stated requirement outright.

3833
05:29:01,102 --> 05:29:06,176
选项 C 在最需要准确性的紧急审核中牺牲了质量。
Option C applies a quality trade to urgent moderation, which is the one place accuracy matters most.

3834
05:29:06,336 --> 05:29:13,700
而选项 D 正好反了过来，这值得注意，因为在快速做题时，反过来的答案听起来也挺像那么回事。
And option D is precisely reversed, which is worth noticing because a reversed answer reads plausibly when you are moving fast.

3835
05:29:14,542 --> 05:29:16,388
这就结束了领域 4。
That closes domain 4.

3836
05:29:17,742 --> 05:29:20,164
接下来是关于上下文的领域 5。
Domain 5 next on context.

3837
05:29:21,966 --> 05:29:25,572
欢迎来到领域 5，上下文管理和可靠性。
Welcome to domain 5, context management and reliability.

3838
05:29:26,286 --> 05:29:27,940
占考试的 15%，
15% of the exam,

3839
05:29:28,846 --> 05:29:31,556
大约 9 道题，三个模块。
roughly 9 questions, three modules.

3840
05:29:32,622 --> 05:29:36,196
这是最小的领域，也是考生最常在考题中寻找套路的领域。
It is the smallest domain and the one candidates most often scheme.

3841
05:29:36,814 --> 05:29:40,656
这让它成为一个可以捡回别人丢分的得分点。
That makes it a good place to pick up marks other people are dropping.

3842
05:29:41,198 --> 05:29:44,292
第一个模块是关于上下文窗口本身的。
This first module is about the context window itself.

3843
05:29:44,750 --> 05:29:49,003
包含什么内容、空间具体怎么分配，以及随着填充而发生的变化。
What goes in it, where the space actually goes, and what happens as it fills.

3844
05:29:50,638 --> 05:29:55,108
有两个事实起到了核心作用，而且这两个事实听起来并不直观。
Two facts do most of the work and both are less obvious than they sound.

3845
05:29:56,526 --> 05:30:01,412
第一个事实是：模型的 API 没有记忆。
The first fact is that the message's API has no memory.

3846
05:30:01,742 --> 05:30:07,748
它不记得你上一个请求、上上个请求，或者任何关于你对话的内容。
It does not remember your last request or the one before or anything about your conversation.

3847
05:30:08,526 --> 05:30:11,812
每一轮，你的代码都会把整个历史记录重新发送一遍。
Every turn, your code sends the whole history again.

3848
05:30:12,782 --> 05:30:20,740
系统提示词、每一个工具定义、每一条消息、每一个工具结果，每次都要全部发送。
The system prompt, every tool definition, every message, every tool result, all of it every time.

3849
05:30:21,294 --> 05:30:27,012
如果某些内容不在请求中，那么对于模型来说，这些内容就不存在。
If something is not in the request, it does not exist as far as the model is concerned.

3850
05:30:27,822 --> 05:30:32,496
这就是为什么上下文管理是一个工程问题，而不是模型问题。
That is why context management is an engineering problem rather than a model problem.

3851
05:30:32,816 --> 05:30:35,172
这也解释了后续大部分的内容。
And it explains most of what follows.

3852
05:30:36,654 --> 05:30:38,884
每一条请求都包含五个部分。
Five things go into every request.

3853
05:30:39,310 --> 05:30:42,500
系统提示词，在每一轮中都是固定的且计费的。
The system prompt, fixed and paid for on every turn.

3854
05:30:43,182 --> 05:30:47,908
你的工具定义，同样是固定的，无论智能体是否使用它们都会计费。
Your tool definitions, also fixed and paid for whether the agent uses them or not.

3855
05:30:49,742 --> 05:30:51,780
记忆文件和其他加载的上下文
Memory files and other loaded context

3856
05:30:52,494 --> 05:30:54,916
每会话加载一次，并在每一轮中重新发送。
loaded once per session and resent every turn.

3857
05:30:55,630 --> 05:31:02,980
对话历史，随着每次交流而增长；以及工具结果，这是增长最快的部分。
Conversation history, which grows with every exchange, and tool results, which grow fastest of all.

3858
05:31:03,790 --> 05:31:10,976
固定部分决定了你的底线，所以一个拥有 40 个工具定义的系统从开始对话时就已经占据了一定的空间。
The fixed parts set your floor so a system with 40 tool definitions starts every conversation already carrying weight.

3859
05:31:11,502 --> 05:31:18,404
增长的部分决定了会话在不得不做出妥协之前实际能运行多久。
The growing parts decide how long the session can actually run before something has to give.

3860
05:31:19,694 --> 05:31:24,260
Anthropic 发布了一个实操案例，让这些比例变得不容置疑。
Anthropec published a worked example that puts the proportions beyond argument.

3861
05:31:24,782 --> 05:31:32,256
一个正在阅读一系列文档的调研智能体，在五轮对话中累计了 335,000 个 token 的上下文。
A research agent reading a corpus of documents accumulated 335,000 tokens of context across five turns.

3862
05:31:32,750 --> 05:31:36,176
其中，文件读取结果占了约 96%。
Of that, file read results accounted for about 96%.

3863
05:31:37,454 --> 05:31:39,856
智能体实际的推理过程不到 2%。
The agent's actual reasoning was under 2%.

3864
05:31:40,430 --> 05:31:50,816
思考一下这一点，因为它重塑了整个问题。当人们担心上下文时，通常考虑的是对话长度。但对话几乎从来不是问题所在。
Sit with that for a moment because it reframes the whole problem. When people worry about context, they usually think about conversation length. The conversation is almost never the issue.

3865
05:31:50,976 --> 05:31:52,804
智能体读到了什么内容才是问题所在。
What the agent read is the issue.

3866
05:31:54,190 --> 05:31:55,844
那么 token 都去哪了？
So where do the tokens go?

3867
05:31:56,558 --> 05:32:04,484
工具结果占据了主导地位，因为每一个结果都会完整进入上下文，无论是文件读取、数据库查询还是搜索结果。
Tool results dominate because each one lands in context whole, whether it is a file read, a database query, or a search response.

3868
05:32:05,390 --> 05:32:14,404
Bard's tools 是最严重的过失项，尤其是任何列出内容而非搜索的内容，这就像是模块 5 中通讯录问题从另一个方向出现。
Burbo's tools are the worst offenders, particularly anything that lists rather than searches, which is module 5's address book problem arriving from the other direction.

3869
05:32:15,022 --> 05:32:22,148
工具定义是每一轮对话中固定的费用，而消息本身很少成为问题。
Tool definitions are a standing charge on every turn of every conversation, and the messages themselves are rarely the problem.

3870
05:32:23,054 --> 05:32:30,340
所以当你进行优化时，要优化进入窗口的内容，而不是在窗口里说的话。
So when you are optimizing, optimize what enters the window rather than what gets said in it.

3871
05:32:31,630 --> 05:32:35,588
第二个事实没那么广为人知，但它更重要。
The second fact is less widely known and it matters more.

3872
05:32:35,982 --> 05:32:40,932
宣传的上下文窗口是一个硬性限制，而不是保证全程的高质量。
The advertised context window is a hard limit, not a promise of quality throughout.

3873
05:32:41,422 --> 05:32:49,764
模型有一个有效窗口，明显比实际小得多；超过大约 12.8 万个 token 后，注意力就会开始下降。
Models have an effective window that is meaningfully smaller and beyond roughly 128,000 tokens, attention starts to degrade.

3874
05:32:50,702 --> 05:32:55,204
技术上存在于窗口中的信息，其权重会按比例降低。
Information technically present in the window receives proportionally less weight.

3875
05:32:55,790 --> 05:33:01,540
所以那种简单的模型——即在达到限制前一切正常，一旦超过就全变差的逻辑——是错误的。
So the naive model, where you are fine until you hit the limit and then you are not, is wrong.

3876
05:33:02,766 --> 05:33:09,732
质量是在任何东西崩溃之前就开始逐渐下降的，这正是这种故障难以察觉的原因。
Quality declines gradually and well before anything breaks, which is precisely why the failure is hard to notice.

3877
05:33:11,408 --> 05:33:16,004
性能退化有明显的特征，考试中也会一致地描述这种情况。
Degradation has a recognizable shape, and the exam describes it consistently.

3878
05:33:16,288 --> 05:33:20,740
它会遗忘窗口中仍然存在的一个早期约束条件。
It forgets a constraint from earlier that is still technically present in the window.

3879
05:33:21,008 --> 05:33:23,780
它后期的决策比早期的决策更差。
Its later decisions are worse than its earlier ones.

3880
05:33:24,526 --> 05:33:29,764
它会重复已经做过的工作，或者与之前得出的结论相矛盾。
It repeats work it has already done or contradicts a conclusion it previously reached.

3881
05:33:30,062 --> 05:33:38,500
而且没有任何报错。没有异常、没有警告、也没有日志记录，只是系统在悄悄地变笨。
And nothing errors. There is no exception, no warning, and no log line, just a system quietly becoming less good at its job.

3882
05:33:39,406 --> 05:33:46,608
当题干提到随着会话进行答案变得模糊，或者后期的决策明显变差时，指的就是这种情况。
When a STEM says the answers get vaguer as the session goes on or later decisions become noticeably worse, that is, this.

3883
05:33:48,302 --> 05:33:52,932
有两种机制来管理当前窗口内的内容，它们丢失的东西不同。
Two mechanisms manage what is inside the current window and they lose different things.

3884
05:33:53,328 --> 05:33:58,368
工具结果清除会成批移除过时的工具调用及其结果。
Tool result clearing removes stale tool calls and their results wholesale.

3885
05:33:58,990 --> 05:34:07,524
这些内容就彻底消失了，除非有东西再次去获取它，而且这不消耗推理成本，所以它是最轻量级的选项。
The content is simply gone until something fetches it again and it costs no inference, which makes it the lightest touch option available.

3886
05:34:08,142 --> 05:34:13,444
压缩会将整个转录记录通过模型处理，并用摘要替换之前的轮次。
Compaction runs the whole transcript through the model and replaces the prior turns with a summary.

3887
05:34:14,222 --> 05:34:20,516
核心内容以压缩形式保留下来，但逐字细节会丢失，而且这需要消耗一次推理调用。
The substance survives in compressed form and the verbatim detail does not, and it costs you an inference call.

3888
05:34:21,390 --> 05:34:23,236
这个关键区别值得记住。
The tiebreaker is worth holding.

3889
05:34:24,174 --> 05:34:26,948
清除操作利用了内容，但保留了可重新获取的属性。
Clearing uses the content but keeps it refetchable.

3890
05:34:27,534 --> 05:34:30,724
压缩保留了核心内容，但丢失了准确的措辞。
Compaction keeps the substance and loses the exact wording.

3891
05:34:32,494 --> 05:34:36,676
压缩是有损的，了解它是如何损耗的很重要。
Compaction is lossy and it is worth knowing how it is lossy.

3892
05:34:37,134 --> 05:34:39,812
与任务核心相关的宏观事实会被保留下来。
High-level facts central to the task survive.

3893
05:34:41,294 --> 05:34:44,740
关键数字、主要实体、主要的对比。
Key figures, the main entities, the major comparisons.

3894
05:34:45,518 --> 05:34:54,768
丢失的是模糊的细节，比如附录表中的一个单元格、当时没人注意的一个统计数据，或者某事的精确措辞。
What gets lost is obscure specifics, like a cell in an appendix table, a statistic nobody flagged at the time, or the exact phasing of something.

3895
05:34:55,086 --> 05:34:57,380
而真正的危险在于第三点。
And the real danger is in the third line.

3896
05:34:57,998 --> 05:35:05,860
激进的压缩会丢失那些直到后期才显现出重要性的上下文，这是最难测试出的损失类型。
Aggressive compaction loses context whose importance only becomes apparent later, which is the hardest kind of loss to test for.

3897
05:35:06,638 --> 05:35:14,768
Anthropic 关于编写压缩提示词的建议是：首先最大化召回率，捕捉所有相关内容，
Anthropith's advice on writing a compaction prompt is to maximize recall first, capturing everything relevant,

3898
05:35:15,054 --> 05:35:19,236
然后再通过迭代去除多余内容来提高精确度。
then iterate to improve precision by removing what is superfluous.

3899
05:35:20,848 --> 05:35:23,728
第三种机制在性质上不同。
The third mechanism is different in kind.

3900
05:35:24,128 --> 05:35:27,812
它不是管理窗口内的内容，而是把东西移到窗口之外。
Instead of managing what is in the window, move things out of it.

3901
05:35:28,208 --> 05:35:35,172
草稿本文件在磁盘上存储发现、决策和进度，完全处于上下文窗口之外。
A scratch pad file holds findings, decisions, and progress on disk entirely outside the context window.

3902
05:35:35,648 --> 05:35:40,132
智能体在过程中将其写入，并仅读取它需要的部分。
The agent writes to it as it goes and reads back only the parts it needs.

3903
05:35:41,006 --> 05:35:42,980
两个特性让这种方式非常强大。
Two properties make this powerful.

3904
05:35:43,566 --> 05:35:48,516
因为它从未出现在转录记录中，所以不会受到压缩的影响。
It survives compaction because it was never in the transcript to be compacted in the first place.

3905
05:35:49,006 --> 05:35:53,252
而且它还能跨越会话存在，这是“清除”和“记忆”之间的核心区别。
And it survives the session, which is the real difference between clearing and memory.

3906
05:35:54,766 --> 05:35:57,924
“清除”和“压缩”是管理窗口内部的内容。
Clearing and compaction manage what is inside the window.

3907
05:35:58,798 --> 05:36:01,348
“外部记忆”是将内容移到窗口之外。
External memory moves things out of it.

3908
05:36:02,766 --> 05:36:04,100
所以，这是设计上的选择。
So the design choice.

3909
05:36:04,528 --> 05:36:10,980
保留在上下文中的内容可以完整地立即使用，且保留原始措辞。
Keeping something in context makes it immediately available in full detail with the exact wording preserved.

3910
05:36:13,328 --> 05:36:18,276
但它也会在后续每一轮中消耗 Token，并且容易受到压缩的影响。
It also costs tokens on every subsequent turn and it is vulnerable to compaction.

3911
05:36:18,830 --> 05:36:26,404
将其写入磁盘在读取前不消耗任何费用，能跨越压缩和会话，且需要有意识地去读取。
Writing it to disk costs nothing until it is read, survives both compaction and the session, and requires a deliberate read to use.

3912
05:36:27,118 --> 05:36:32,420
它的效果也取决于实际写下了什么。作为决胜因素，启发式方法非常有用。
It is also only as good as what was actually written down. The tiebreaker is a useful heuristic.

3913
05:36:33,328 --> 05:36:38,276
保留下个决策需要的，并记录下后续决策可能需要的。
Keep what the next decision needs and write down what a later decision might need.

3914
05:36:40,398 --> 05:36:44,676
大多数系统搞反了，为了以防万一而保留所有内容。
Most systems get this backwards and keep everything just in case.

3915
05:36:46,126 --> 05:36:49,188
一种良好的习惯比任何压缩策略都有效。
One habit is worth more than any compaction strategy.

3916
05:36:49,710 --> 05:36:54,848
冗长的工具结果会完整到达，并在整个会话中保持完整。
A verbose tool result arrives whole and then stays whole for the rest of the session.

3917
05:36:55,088 --> 05:36:58,852
提取事实并仅保留这些内容可以节省大量空间。
Pulling the facts out and keeping only those is a large saving.

3918
05:36:59,408 --> 05:37:04,708
更好的是，修改工具让它返回三个字段而不是 3000 个 Token。
Better still, fix the tool so it returns three fields rather than 3000 tokens.

3919
05:37:05,568 --> 05:37:16,932
这就是模块 5 的响应设计在承担上下文管理的功能。最棒的是，让代码去处理中间输出，只将处理后的结果传回模型。
That is module 5's response design doing double duty as context management. And best of all, let code consume the intermediate output and pass only the processed result back to the model.

3920
05:37:17,248 --> 05:37:20,932
最省钱的 Token 永远是那些根本不进入窗口的。
The cheapest token is always the one that never enters the window at all.

3921
05:37:22,318 --> 05:37:25,764
模块 3 涵盖了作为一种架构的子代理。
Module 3 covered sub-agents as an architecture.

3922
05:37:27,342 --> 05:37:32,228
从领域 5 的角度来看，它们是一种上下文策略，且往往是可用的最强手段。
From Domain 5's side, they are a context strategy and often the strongest one available.

3923
05:37:33,262 --> 05:37:40,352
子代理有自己的窗口，因此它读取的任何内容都留在其中，只有它的最终消息会返回给父级。
A subagent has its own window, so whatever it reads stays inside it, and only its final message returns to the parent.

3924
05:37:40,942 --> 05:37:50,660
庞大的探索过程变成了一个简短的摘要。Anthropic 自己的研究系统中的子代理向主智能体返回的通常是 1 到 2000 个 Token。
A very large exploration becomes a short summary. Anthropic's own research system has sub-agents returning roughly 1 to 2000 tokens, each to the lead agent.

3925
05:37:51,118 --> 05:37:53,988
这极大地压缩了它们所阅读的内容。
That is a dramatic compression of whatever they read.

3926
05:37:54,958 --> 05:37:58,756
这不是免费的，因为你需要支付往返请求和加载新上下文的费用。
It is not free since you pay a round trip and a fresh context load.

3927
05:37:59,712 --> 05:38:04,996
但它仍然比把所有这些材料放入主窗口要便宜得多。
It is still frequently much cheaper than letting all that material into the main window.

3928
05:38:06,503 --> 05:38:07,283
就像一种货币。
A currency note.

3929
05:38:07,792 --> 05:38:17,604
当考试指南编写时，管理拥挤的窗口意味着手动总结并保留自己的草稿本文件，这些技术依然完全有效。
When the exam guide was written, managing a filling window meant summarizing manually and keeping your own scratch pad files, and those techniques remain entirely valid.

3930
05:38:18,158 --> 05:38:22,592
从那时起，平台已经为同样的工作提供了原生功能。
Since then, the platform has grown first-party primitives for the same jobs.

3931
05:38:23,150 --> 05:38:29,540
当智能体接近极限时，自动清除缩放工具调用和结果的上下文编辑。
Context editing that automatically clears scale tool calls and results as an agent approaches its limits.

3932
05:38:30,032 --> 05:38:32,580
用于跨会话状态的记忆工具。
A memory tool for state that outlives a session.

3933
05:38:32,912 --> 05:38:36,356
并且 Claude 代码在接近窗口顶部时会自动进行压缩。
And clawed code autocompacts as it nears the top of the window.

3934
05:38:38,830 --> 05:38:41,348
在考试中，请选择手动处理的技术方案。
On the exam, answer with the manual techniques.

3935
05:38:41,998 --> 05:38:47,300
要了解这些基础功能的存在，以免被文档内容误导。
Know that the primitives exist so the documentation does not confuse you.

3936
05:38:48,814 --> 05:38:49,872
模式识别。
Pattern recognition.

3937
05:38:50,222 --> 05:38:53,392
随着会话进行，回答变得越来越模糊，这意味着出现了性能下降。
Answers getting vaguer as the session goes on means degradation.

3938
05:38:53,472 --> 05:38:55,044
所以要减少窗口中的内容。
So reduce what is in the window.

3939
05:38:55,392 --> 05:39:01,188
在几次工具调用后出现上下文填充，意味着需要优化工具响应设计，而不是换更大的模型。
Context filling after a few tool calls means tool response design rather than a bigger model.

3940
05:39:01,614 --> 05:39:05,796
遗忘了之前的决策，意味着需要进行总结或将决策写入文件。
Forgetting a decision from earlier means summarize or write decisions to a file.

3941
05:39:06,638 --> 05:39:11,172
切换到更大的窗口后问题依然存在，这意味着是结构性问题。
We move to a larger window and it still happens. Means the problem is structural.

3942
05:39:11,630 --> 05:39:16,388
生成了没人需要的输出，意味着需要使用子代理或分支计划。
Exploration generating output nobody needs means a subagent or a forked schedule.

3943
05:39:16,750 --> 05:39:21,860
需要下周才用的信息而不是下一轮就用的，意味着要用外部记忆而非上下文。
And needing something next week rather than next turn means external memory rather than context.

3944
05:39:22,254 --> 05:39:24,013
关键点就在提示词中。
The line to hold is in the callout.

3945
05:39:25,038 --> 05:39:28,868
更大的窗口只能争取时间，永远无法改变填充率。
A bigger window buys time and never changes the fill rate.

3946
05:39:30,254 --> 05:39:31,588
第 5 条。
5. Lines.

3947
05:39:35,854 --> 05:39:41,988
API 是无状态的，所以每一轮都会重新发送所有内容，窗口里的任何东西都不是免费的。
The API is stateless, so everything is resent every turn and nothing in the window is free.

3948
05:39:42,352 --> 05:39:47,908
工具结果占据了几乎全部。所以要优化进入的内容，而不是优化的表达内容。
Tool results are almost all of it. So optimize what enters rather than what gets said.

3949
05:39:48,272 --> 05:39:53,508
有效窗口比宣传的还要小，而且性能下降是无声的。
The effective window is smaller than the advertised one, and degradation is silent.

3950
05:39:54,414 --> 05:40:00,516
清除会丢失内容但保留可重新获取性，而压缩能保留核心内容但会损失细节。
Clearing loses content while keeping it refetchable, and compaction keeps substance while losing detail.

3951
05:40:00,912 --> 05:40:05,508
并保留下一项决策所需的内容，记录下后续决策可能需要的点。
And keep what the next decision needs, writing down what a later decision might need.

3952
05:40:07,438 --> 05:40:13,312
现在有五个场景，其中有两个提供了更大的上下文窗口作为诱人的错误选项。
Five scenarios now, and two of them offer a bigger context window as the tempting wrong answer.

3953
05:40:14,670 --> 05:40:15,552
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

3954
05:40:15,758 --> 05:40:19,792
一个研究智能体从语料库中读取文档来回答分析师的问题。
A research agent reads documents from a corpus to answer analyst questions.

3955
05:40:20,206 --> 05:40:25,124
追踪显示其上下文在五轮内达到了 300,000 个 token。
Traces show its context reaching 300,000 tokens within five turns.

3956
05:40:25,742 --> 05:40:30,500
分解上下文后，文件读取结果占据了绝大部分。
Breaking the context down, file read results account for the overwhelming majority.

3957
05:40:31,278 --> 05:40:33,988
而对话本身只有几千个 token。
And the conversation itself is a few thousand tokens.

3958
05:40:34,926 --> 05:40:38,916
团队计划切换到一个具有更大上下文窗口的模型。
The team is planning to move to a model with a larger context window.

3959
05:40:39,726 --> 05:40:41,028
你应该提供什么建议？
What should you advise?

3960
05:40:41,934 --> 05:40:46,884
a 因为语料库确实很大，所以更大的窗口是正确的选择。
a The larger window is the right move since the corpus is genuinely large.

3961
05:40:47,312 --> 05:40:55,312
b 通过减少读取量、从已读内容中提取事实或将阅读任务委派给子智能体来处理这 5 个读取结果。
b address the 5 read results by reading less, extracting facts from what is read or delegating reading to subagents.

3962
05:40:55,712 --> 05:40:59,972
C. 缩短系统提示词并减少工具定义的数量。
C. Shorten the system prompt and reduce the number of tool definitions.

3963
05:41:00,846 --> 05:41:04,112
d 每隔几轮总结一次对话历史。
d summarize the conversation history every few turns.

3964
05:41:04,352 --> 05:41:05,872
稍停一下，做出决定。
Pause and decide.

3965
05:41:11,278 --> 05:41:12,688
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

3966
05:41:13,008 --> 05:41:22,244
题干刻意给了你这种细分，原因是选项 C 和 D 虽然都是合理的优化方案，但针对的组件错误了。
The STEM hands you the breakdown deliberately, and the reason is that options C and D are both genuinely sensible optimizations aimed at the wrong component.

3967
05:41:22,528 --> 05:41:28,548
缩短系统提示词和精简工具定义只能节省百分之几的 token。
Shortening the system prompt and trimming tool definitions does save tokens on a couple of percent of the total.

3968
05:41:29,294 --> 05:41:33,412
对只有几千个 token 的对话进行总结，节省的更少。
Summarizing a conversation that is a few thousand tokens saves less still.

3969
05:41:33,888 --> 05:41:42,608
选项 A 是这个领域中反复出现的干扰项，需要记住的表述是：更大的窗口提供了空间，但不会改变填充率。
Option A is the recurring distractor in this domain, and the phrasing to remember is that a bigger window buys headroom without changing the fill rate.

3970
05:41:42,768 --> 05:41:45,828
5 轮变成 8 轮，结构完全相同。
5 turns becomes 8, and the structure is identical.

3971
05:41:46,448 --> 05:41:50,468
只有 B 针对的是真正消耗窗口的组件。
Only B attacks the component that is actually consuming the window.

3972
05:41:51,950 --> 05:41:52,964
场景 2。
Scenario 2.

3973
05:41:53,198 --> 05:41:56,388
一个智能体正在处理长篇的技术支持会话。
An agent handles long technical support sessions.

3974
05:41:57,006 --> 05:42:01,668
在会话初期，它正确应用了用户提到的特定于客户的限制条件。
Early in a session, it correctly applies a customer-specific constraint the user mentioned.

3975
05:42:02,126 --> 05:42:06,276
该客户使用的是旧版方案，无法使用新的 API。
The customer is on a legacy plan and cannot use the new API.

3976
05:42:06,766 --> 05:42:09,924
到第 40 轮左右时，它推荐了新 API。
Around 40 turns in, it recommends the new API.

3977
05:42:10,542 --> 05:42:17,092
限制条件仍存在于对话历史中，且没有任何内容被截断。任何时候都没有报错。
The constraint is still present in the conversation history and nothing was truncated. No error was raised at any point.

3978
05:42:18,030 --> 05:42:19,044
发生了什么？
What is happening?

3979
05:42:19,968 --> 05:42:24,868
a 当上下文窗口溢出时，该限制条件被静默丢弃了。
a The constraint was silently dropped when the context window overflowed.

3980
05:42:25,806 --> 05:42:31,556
B. 随着窗口填满，注意力会下降，因此早期出现的信息在后期获得的权重较低。
B. Attention degrades as the window fills, so information present early receives less weight later.

3981
05:42:32,014 --> 05:42:35,524
C. 模型不支持在用户消息中声明的限制条件。
C. The model does not support constraints stated in user messages.

3982
05:42:36,206 --> 05:42:40,676
D. 对话历史没有重新发送，导致早期轮次丢失。
D. The conversation history is not being resent, so early turns are missing.

3983
05:42:42,670 --> 05:42:43,684
稍停一下，做出决定。
Pause and decide.

3984
05:42:49,422 --> 05:42:53,444
答案是 B，而且题干给出了特征中的全部三个部分。
The answer is B, and the stem gives you all three parts of the signature.

3985
05:42:55,502 --> 05:42:59,428
限制条件仍然存在，没有内容被截断，且没有报错。
The constraint is still present, nothing was truncated, and no error was raised.

3986
05:43:00,174 --> 05:43:03,140
这个组合排除了所有机械性的解释。
That combination rules out every mechanical explanation.

3987
05:43:03,790 --> 05:43:05,968
选项 A 会导致报错。
Option A would produce an error.

3988
05:43:06,542 --> 05:43:11,588
选项 D 会导致丢失早期轮次的所有内容，而不仅仅是一个限制条件。
Option D would lose everything from early turns rather than one constraint.

3989
05:43:12,206 --> 05:43:18,180
选项 C 被前 30 多轮的情况推翻了，因为在那期间它正确应用了限制条件。
Option C is disproved by the first 30 odd turns, where it applied the constraint correctly.

3990
05:43:18,990 --> 05:43:21,060
剩下的解释就是性能退化。
What remains is degradation.

3991
05:43:22,030 --> 05:43:28,804
从技术上讲，这些信息仍在窗口内，但随着窗口填满，它们获得的权重会按比例降低。
The information is technically in the window and receiving proportionally less weight as the window fills.

3992
05:43:29,358 --> 05:43:36,100
这种故障是隐蔽且逐渐发生的，这就是为什么人们往往在被坑了之后才去针对它做设计。
That failure is silent and gradual, which is why people design against it only after it has bitten them.

3993
05:43:37,806 --> 05:43:38,928
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

3994
05:43:39,168 --> 05:43:44,772
一个运行时间很长的分析智能体在持续数小时的会话中达到了上下文限制。
A long-running analysis agent hits its context limit during multi-hour sessions.

3995
05:43:45,168 --> 05:43:47,140
团队实施了压缩。
The team implements compaction.

3996
05:43:47,566 --> 05:43:53,092
当达到 token 阈值时，转录记录会被总结，并使用该摘要重新启动会话。
At a token threshold, the transcript is summarized and the session reinitiated with the summary.

3997
05:43:53,568 --> 05:43:54,528
它起作用了。
It works.

3998
05:43:55,374 --> 05:44:03,568
但分析师报告称，在压缩后，之前提到的特定数字会丢失，比如某个样本量，
But analysts report that specific figures cited earlier go missing after a compaction, a particular sample size,

3999
05:44:03,728 --> 05:44:05,168
或者带脚注的注意事项。
a footnoted caveat.

4000
05:44:05,518 --> 05:44:07,808
总体结论保持完整。
The overall conclusions survive intact.

4001
05:44:08,014 --> 05:44:10,052
最合适的对策是什么？
What is the most appropriate response?

4002
05:44:10,448 --> 05:44:14,500
a. 提高压缩阈值，让它触发得少一些。
a Lays the compaction threshold so it fires less often.

4003
05:44:15,568 --> 05:44:15,888
b。
b.

4004
05:44:16,368 --> 05:44:22,116
在发现关键数据和注意事项时就将它们写入文件，以便它们能保留在转录记录之外。
Write key figures and caveats to a file as they are found so they survive outside the transcript.

4005
05:44:23,008 --> 05:44:23,328
C。
C.

4006
05:44:23,886 --> 05:44:27,172
禁用压缩，并接受达到上下文限制的情况。
Disable compaction and accept hitting the context limit.

4007
05:44:27,982 --> 05:44:31,460
D. 指示压缩提示词保留所有内容。
D. Instruct the compaction prompt to preserve everything.

4008
05:44:31,790 --> 05:44:32,932
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4009
05:44:38,638 --> 05:44:40,448
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

4010
05:44:41,582 --> 05:44:44,996
这个场景之所以有意义，是因为并没有东西坏掉。
What makes this scenario useful is that nothing is broken.

4011
05:44:45,774 --> 05:44:52,388
结论保留而模糊的细节消失，正是压缩功能的官方预期行为。
Conclusion surviving while obscure specifics disappear is precisely how compaction is documented to behave.

4012
05:44:53,358 --> 05:44:57,988
团队看到的是正确的行为，但他们需要另一种机制来处理他们关心的内容。
The team is seeing correct behavior and needs a different mechanism for what they care about.

4013
05:44:58,894 --> 05:45:05,008
选项 D 是值得思考的，因为「保留所有内容」听起来像是一个合理的指令。
Option D is the one worth thinking through because preserve everything sounds like a reasonable instruction.

4014
05:45:05,168 --> 05:45:11,684
一个能保留所有内容的摘要其实就是转录记录本身，而不会压缩的压缩就不是压缩。
A summary that preserves everything is just the transcript, and compaction that does not compress is not compaction.

4015
05:45:12,334 --> 05:45:19,076
在发现关键数据时将其写入文件，就能让它们处于转录记录之外，从而不受压缩的影响。
Writing key figures to a file as they are found puts them outside the transcript where compaction cannot reach them.

4016
05:45:19,598 --> 05:45:22,532
那是记忆机制，而不是压缩。
That is the memory mechanism rather than the compaction.

4017
05:45:23,246 --> 05:45:23,748
1。
1.

4018
05:45:25,454 --> 05:45:26,404
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

4019
05:45:26,688 --> 05:45:30,212
一个基于代码的智能体在回答关于大型仓库的问题。
A code-based agent answers questions about a large repository.

4020
05:45:30,528 --> 05:45:36,996
为了回答任何问题，它都会调用一个工具来返回目录中每个文件的完整内容，然后对其进行推理。
To answer anything, it calls a tool that returns the full contents of every file in a directory, then reasons over them.

4021
05:45:37,518 --> 05:45:42,244
在问了三四个问题后，它的上下文几乎就满了，回答质量明显变差。
After three or four questions, its context is nearly full and answers become noticeably worse.

4022
05:45:43,182 --> 05:45:48,528
团队之前已经换过一次更大的模型，这让问题推迟了大约两个问题左右。
The team has already moved to a larger model once, which delayed the problem by about two questions.

4023
05:45:48,768 --> 05:45:51,428
大多数问题只涉及一到两个文件。
Most questions concern one or two files.

4024
05:45:51,728 --> 05:45:53,700
哪种改变最有效？
What is the most effective change?

4025
05:45:54,478 --> 05:45:57,348
a. 切换到更大的上下文窗口。
a Move to an even larger context window.

4026
05:45:58,254 --> 05:46:04,612
b. 用搜索和定向读取来替换目录转储工具，这样只有相关文件才会进入上下文。
b. Replace the directory dump tool with search and targeted read so only relevant files enter context.

4027
05:46:05,166 --> 05:46:07,972
C. 在每个问题后对文件内容进行总结。
C. Summarize the file contents after each question.

4028
05:46:08,686 --> 05:46:11,556
D. 每个问题后都开启一个新的会话。
D. Start a fresh session after every question.

4029
05:46:12,174 --> 05:46:13,220
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4030
05:46:18,926 --> 05:46:20,608
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

4031
05:46:21,008 --> 05:46:32,228
题干在这里提供了一个很友好的信息，即记录了失败的实验。他们已经换过大模型并赢得了大约两个问题的空间，这能让你准确判断出第三次变动能带来多少收益。
The STEM does something generous here by recording the failed experiment. They already moved to a larger model and bought about two questions, which tells you precisely what a third move would buy.

4032
05:46:32,688 --> 05:46:36,676
选项 C 是一个微妙的陷阱，并且在整个课程中反复出现。
Option C is the subtle one and it recurs across this course.

4033
05:46:37,486 --> 05:46:48,292
事后总结没用，因为工具返回结果的那一刻全文就已经进入上下文了，而总结只是堆叠在上面的额外 token。
Summarizing after the fact cannot help because the full contents entered context the moment the tool returned, and the summary is additional tokens sitting on top.

4034
05:46:49,326 --> 05:46:55,428
选项 D 通过放弃连续性来解决上下文问题，因此每个问题都从零开始。
Option D solves context by throwing away continuity, so every question starts from nothing.

4035
05:46:56,334 --> 05:47:03,076
只有 B 能从源头阻止数据堆积，而且题干最后一行告诉我们大多数问题只需要一到两个文件。
Only B stops the dump at source, and the last line of the stem tells you that most questions need one or two files.

4036
05:47:04,718 --> 05:47:05,728
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

4037
05:47:06,126 --> 05:47:08,676
一个智能体正在执行多步骤的迁移审计。
An agent performs a multi-step migration audit.

4038
05:47:10,094 --> 05:47:15,940
第 4 步需要在第 1 步做出的决策，以及在第 2 步发现的受影响模块列表。
Step 4 needs a decision made in step 1 and a list of affected modules discovered in step 2.

4039
05:47:16,718 --> 05:47:24,868
团队希望即使在触发压缩的超长审计中，或者跨越多个会话的审计中，这套流程也能可靠运行。
The team wants this to work reliably even on very long audits where compaction will fire and across audits that span more than one session.

4040
05:47:25,248 --> 05:47:27,716
目前，所有内容都存在于对话中。
Currently, everything lives in the conversation.

4041
05:47:28,494 --> 05:47:30,084
他们应该采用什么方案？
What should they implement?

4042
05:47:30,958 --> 05:47:36,740
a. 提高压缩阈值，让早期步骤在转录记录中保留更久。
a increase the compaction threshold so the early steps stay in the transcript longer.

4043
05:47:37,168 --> 05:47:43,524
B. 每完成一个步骤就将决策和结果写入状态文件，并在后续步骤中从中读取。
B. Write decisions and findings to a state file as each step completes and read from it in later steps.

4044
05:47:43,888 --> 05:47:47,972
C. 在每一个后续提示词中重复第一步的决定。
C. Repeat the step one decision in every subsequent prompt.

4045
05:47:48,654 --> 05:47:48,928
D。
D.

4046
05:47:49,518 --> 05:47:53,668
将每个步骤作为子代理运行，使其上下文保持隔离。
Run each step as a subagent so its context stays isolated.

4047
05:47:55,566 --> 05:47:56,900
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4048
05:48:02,478 --> 05:48:07,364
答案是 B，题干设定的两个要求极大地缩小了范围。
The answer is B and the stem sets two requirements that narrow it sharply.

4049
05:48:07,648 --> 05:48:13,924
它必须能在长审计中经受住压缩的影响，并且必须能跨越超过一个会话的审计运行。
It has to survive compaction within a long audit and it has to survive across audits spanning more than one session.

4050
05:48:14,478 --> 05:48:16,836
只有外部状态能同时满足这两个条件。
Only external state satisfies both.

4051
05:48:19,662 --> 05:48:23,716
选项 A 只解决了第一个问题，完全忽略了第二个。
Option A addresses the first and ignores the second entirely.

4052
05:48:24,558 --> 05:48:31,460
选项 C 仅适用于你预先知道的那个决策，无法应对那些你无法预测的发现。
Option C works for the one decision you knew about in advance and does not scale to findings you cannot predict.

4053
05:48:32,110 --> 05:48:38,116
选项 D 是陷阱，因为子代理是一种上下文策略，而在这种情况下它们会让情况变得更糟。
Option D is the trap because subagents are a context strategy and here they make things worse.

4054
05:48:38,702 --> 05:48:43,968
正如模块 3 所确立的，子代理不继承任何内容。所以看第 4 步。
Subagents inherit nothing as module 3 established. So step 4.

4055
05:48:44,208 --> 05:48:47,364
作为子代理运行时，它能看到的甚至比现在还要少。
Running as a subagent would see even less than it does now.

4056
05:48:48,046 --> 05:48:49,796
模块 16。下一题。
Module 16. Next.

4057
05:48:51,470 --> 05:48:52,420
模块 16。
Module 16.

4058
05:48:52,688 --> 05:48:59,648
模块 15 是关于作为容器的上下文窗口。这一部分是关于在长会话中内容的变化。
Module 15 was about the context window as a container. This one is about what happens to the contents over a long session.

4059
05:48:59,808 --> 05:49:04,676
它还涉及编码智能体中最大的上下文来源，即探索代码库。
It is also about the largest source of context in a coding agent which is exploring a code base.

4060
05:49:05,168 --> 05:49:06,340
再次分为两个部分。
Two halves again.

4061
05:49:06,958 --> 05:49:12,164
第一个是陈旧长度，这与容量是一个不同的问题，需要不同的对策。
The first is stale length, which is a different problem from volume and needs a different fix.

4062
05:49:12,688 --> 05:49:19,396
第二个是“搜索优先”的探索模式，这是解决一系列考试问题的答案。
The second is the search first exploration pattern, which is the answer to a whole family of exam questions.

4063
05:49:21,136 --> 05:49:25,828
在长会话中会积累两个问题，且这两个问题经常被混淆。
Two problems accumulate in a long session and they are routinely confused.

4064
05:49:26,096 --> 05:49:28,356
容量是指进入窗口的内容过多。
Volume is too much having entered the window.

4065
05:49:28,686 --> 05:49:36,100
它表现为回答模糊以及遗忘约束，解决方法是减少进入的内容、进行总结或委派任务。
It shows up as vaguer answers and forgotten constraints, and the fix is to reduce what enters, summarize, or delegate.

4066
05:49:37,038 --> 05:49:40,580
陈旧性是指内容进入窗口后，外部世界发生了变化。
Staleness is the world having changed since something entered the window.

4067
05:49:41,166 --> 05:49:47,492
它表现得完全不同，即基于一个不再存在的现实版本给出自信的回答。
It shows up quite differently as confident answers based on a version of reality that no longer exists.

4068
05:49:48,526 --> 05:49:52,260
解决方法是刷新，或者根据你现在掌握的信息重新开始。
The fix is to refresh or to start again with what you know now.

4069
05:49:53,102 --> 05:49:55,076
容量随着会话长度而增加。
Volume grows with the length of the session.

4070
05:49:56,046 --> 05:49:58,852
陈旧性随着你上次查看以来的间隔而增加。
Staleness grows with the gap since you last looked.

4071
05:50:00,430 --> 05:50:07,972
这是导致陈旧性难以修复的机制，值得深入理解，因为它会产生一个反直觉的答案。
Here is the mechanism that makes staleness hard to fix, and it is worth understanding properly because it produces a counterintuitive answer.

4072
05:50:08,846 --> 05:50:10,660
对话是仅追加的。
A conversation is append only.

4073
05:50:11,150 --> 05:50:14,436
没有办法追溯到历史记录中去更新某些内容。
There is no way to reach back into the history and update something.

4074
05:50:15,342 --> 05:50:19,296
每一条新信息都会排在旧信息之后，且两者都会保留。
Every new piece of information lands after the old one and both remain.

4075
05:50:19,536 --> 05:50:24,804
因此，当文件发生变化而你要求智能体重新读取时，你并没有替换掉旧内容。
So when a file has changed and you ask the agent to read it again, you have not replaced the old contents.

4076
05:50:25,230 --> 05:50:26,724
你只是添加了第二个版本。
You have added a second version.

4077
05:50:27,150 --> 05:50:31,492
智能体现在持有两个版本，且转录记录中没有任何标记能标明哪一个是当前的。
The agent is now holding two, and nothing in the transcript marks which one is current.

4078
05:50:33,102 --> 05:50:36,260
因此，重新读取有一个人们意想不到的故障模式。
So rereading has a failure mode that people do not expect.

4079
05:50:36,656 --> 05:50:40,016
旧内容仍然留在同一个对话的前面。
The old contents are still sitting earlier in the same conversation.

4080
05:50:40,256 --> 05:50:45,412
没有任何标记显示它们已被废弃，所以这两个读取对模型来说都具有同等的权威性。
Nothing marks them as superseded, so both reads look equally authoritative to the model.

4081
05:50:45,776 --> 05:50:49,636
它可能会从其中任何一个去推理，而且不会告诉你它用了哪一个。
It may reason from either and it will not tell you which one it used.

4082
05:50:50,478 --> 05:51:00,292
最后这一句是让人不舒服的地方。这可能比完全不重新读取还要糟糕，因为你现在认为上下文是最新的，并据此信任输出结果。
And the last line is the uncomfortable part. This is arguably worse than not rereading at all because you now believe the context is current and you will trust the output accordingly.

4083
05:51:00,576 --> 05:51:04,164
重新读取只是增加了一个版本，它永远不会删除旧版本。
Rereading adds a version, it never removes one.

4084
05:51:05,742 --> 05:51:09,380
这里有三种正确刷新内容的方法，按成本从低到高排列。
Three ways to refresh properly in increasing order of cost.

4085
05:51:10,030 --> 05:51:17,156
说明发生了什么变化，并明确指出之前的读取已被废弃，这样新信息就是被明确陈述的，而不是含糊暗示的。
Say what changed and say explicitly that the earlier read is superseded, so the newness is stated rather than implied.

4086
05:51:17,934 --> 05:51:24,976
指明具体的文件名称，因为列出三个部分比含糊地说“有些东西变了”要有用得多。
Name the specific files because three parts is far more useful than a vague statement that some things have changed.

4087
05:51:25,550 --> 05:51:32,740
清除陈旧的工具结果，这样就能移除旧版本，而不仅仅是利用第15模块中的机制让它在排名上落后。
Clear the stale tool results, which removes the old version rather than merely outranking it using the mechanism from module 15.

4088
05:51:33,296 --> 05:51:40,004
或者当大量内容变动时，用一个摘要来重新开始，这是最干净的选择，但代价是会丢失积累的细节。
Or start fresh with a summary when a great deal has moved, which is the cleanest option and costs you the accumulated detail.

4089
05:51:40,910 --> 05:51:45,316
准确指出哪些文件发生了变化，这种方法成本低且有效。
Naming exactly which files changed is cheap and effective.

4090
05:51:46,958 --> 05:51:47,684
所以选哪一种？
So which one?

4091
05:51:48,142 --> 05:51:53,828
当只有少量内容变动时，在原位刷新；你知道具体变了哪些，而其余的上下文仍值得保留。
Refresh in place when a few things moved, you know exactly which and the rest of the context is still worth keeping.

4092
05:51:54,382 --> 05:51:58,948
明确说明之前的读取已陈旧，列出文件名称，然后继续。
State plainly that the earlier red is stale, name the files and carry on.

4093
05:51:59,854 --> 05:52:08,772
当大量内容变动、间隔时间过长，或者陈旧的读取太多无法一一列举时，重新开始。
Start again when a lot moved or when the gap was long or when there are simply too many stale reads to enumerate.

4094
05:52:09,710 --> 05:52:12,548
注入一份关于决策和当前状态的摘要。
Inject a summary of decisions and current state.

4095
05:52:13,243 --> 05:52:16,484
接受细节的损失，换取确定性。
Accept the loss of detail And buy certainty.

4096
05:52:17,166 --> 05:52:21,252
判定标准是一个你可以在两秒钟内诚实回答的问题。
The tiebreaker is a question you can answer honestly in two seconds.

4097
05:52:22,062 --> 05:52:24,132
你能列出哪些变动了吗？
Can you list what changed?

4098
05:52:24,718 --> 05:52:29,636
如果你不确定哪里变了，这种不确定性本身就是答案。
If you are not sure what changed, that uncertainty is itself the answer.

4099
05:52:31,374 --> 05:52:40,036
第4模块介绍了移交摘要，这里值得深入强调一下，因为排除掉的内容和包含的内容同样重要。
Module 4 introduced the handoff summary and it is worth sharpening here because the exclusions matter as much as the inclusions.

4100
05:52:40,496 --> 05:52:47,332
包含决策及其背后的原因，这样新会话就不会再去争论已经解决的问题了。
Include the decisions and the reasons behind them so the new session does not relitigate settled questions.

4101
05:52:48,736 --> 05:52:51,396
包含描述为“当前”的状态。
Include current state described as current.

4102
05:52:52,256 --> 05:52:58,980
包含仍未解决的内容和已被排除的内容，否则它会贴心地把已经被你拒绝过的选项再次提出来。
Include what is still open and what was ruled out because otherwise it will helpfully propose the option you already rejected.

4103
05:52:59,726 --> 05:53:04,004
排除工具结果，因为那些正是你想要摆脱的陈旧内容。
Exclude the tool results since those are precisely the stale material you are escaping.

4104
05:53:04,878 --> 05:53:13,092
并且排除转录记录，因为把它们贴回来只是在手动重组问题，并带入所有你试图抛弃的内容。
And exclude the transcript because pasting it back rebins the problem by hand and imports everything you are trying to leave behind.

4105
05:53:14,382 --> 05:53:18,820
现在是第二部分，这直接源于第15模块的核心要点。
Now the second half and it follows directly from module 15's headline number.

4106
05:53:19,216 --> 05:53:27,940
一个编程智能体的上下文绝大部分是由大量读取组成的，因此最重要的技能是在理解代码的同时减少这些读取的数量。
A coding agent's context is overwhelmingly made of 5Z red, so the skill that matters most is reading fewer of them while still understanding the code.

4107
05:53:28,526 --> 05:53:30,308
Claude Code 就是围绕这一点构建的。
Claude code is built around this.

4108
05:53:31,182 --> 05:53:34,948
它并不维护你代码的持久索引或向量数据库。
It does not maintain a persistent index or a vector database of your code.

4109
05:53:35,278 --> 05:53:37,188
它探索的方式与工程师一致。
It explores the way an engineer does.

4110
05:53:37,774 --> 05:53:44,004
定位相关文件，缩小内容范围，阅读关键部分，然后从那里开始向外追踪关联。
Locate the relevant files, narrow down the content, read the crucial parts, and follow the connections outward from there.

4111
05:53:45,648 --> 05:53:49,476
这个模式包含四个步骤，值得作为四个步骤来学习。
The pattern has four steps and it is worth learning as four.

4112
05:53:50,254 --> 05:53:54,500
使用 glob 定位文件路径，并用 grep 搜索内容。
Locate using glob for file paths and grep for content.

4113
05:53:55,246 --> 05:53:58,596
注意这两者都不会将文件加载到上下文中。
And note that neither of those loads a file into context.

4114
05:53:59,118 --> 05:54:05,088
通过过滤文件类型、收紧模式或在查看前统计匹配数来缩小范围。
Narrow by filtering to a file type, tightening the pattern, or counting matches before looking at them.

4115
05:54:05,614 --> 05:54:14,308
仅读取搜索结果涉及的文件。然后根据你刚读的内容，通过导入、颜色和测试向外延伸。
Read opening only the files the search actually implicated. Then follow, moving outward through imports, colors, and tests from what you just read.

4116
05:54:14,958 --> 05:54:19,844
在“读取”之前的每一步都有一个目的，那就是让阅读范围变小。
Every step before read exists for one purpose, which is to make the read smaller.

4117
05:54:20,078 --> 05:54:21,540
这就是整套技术的核心。
That is the whole technique.

4118
05:54:23,150 --> 05:54:25,412
一旦你意识到这一点，两者的对比就会非常明显。
The contrast is stark once you see it.

4119
05:54:25,998 --> 05:54:29,860
先搜索意味着处理路径和匹配行，这些操作成本很低。
Searching first means paths and matched lines, which are cheap.

4120
05:54:30,734 --> 05:54:34,340
上下文的增长取决于相关性，而不是仓库的大小。
Context grows with relevance rather than repository size.

4121
05:54:34,928 --> 05:54:38,980
因此，无论是在 80 个文件还是 8000 个文件中，它都同样奏效。
So it works identically on 80 files or 8000.

4122
05:54:39,822 --> 05:54:48,608
读取所有内容意味着每个文件都会进入上下文。无论相关与否，上下文都会随仓库规模增长，并在几个问题后导致性能下降。
Reading everything means every file enters context. Whether it is relevant or not, context grows with the repository and degradation arises within a few questions.

4123
05:54:48,848 --> 05:54:53,764
在小型项目中它运行良好，这正是为什么团队直到进入真实项目时才察觉到问题的原因。
It works fine on a toy project, which is exactly why teams do not notice until they are on a real one.

4124
05:54:54,446 --> 05:54:59,972
为了回答关于两个文件的两个问题而加载所有文件，是追求彻底性时成本最高的方法。
Loading every file to answer a question about two of them is the most expensive possible way to be thorough.

4125
05:55:01,646 --> 05:55:03,684
四种工具及其区别。
Four tools and the distinction.

4126
05:55:04,366 --> 05:55:05,700
考试考查这些内容。
The exam tests.

4127
05:55:06,702 --> 05:55:13,028
Glob 根据名称模式匹配文件路径，因此它能找到特定名称的文件并仅返回路径。
Glob matches file paths by name pattern, so it finds files called something and it returns paths only.

4128
05:55:14,350 --> 05:55:21,348
Grep 在文件内部搜索，因此它能找到包含某些内容的文件，并返回路径或匹配的行。
Grep searches inside files, so it finds files containing something and returns either paths or the matching lines.

4129
05:55:22,318 --> 05:55:25,008
这两者都很廉价，因为它们都不会加载文件。
Both are cheap because neither loads a file.

4130
05:55:25,248 --> 05:55:30,980
Read 会加载大量文件内容，这是昂贵的操作，也是你试图减少操作的那个。
Read loads of files contents, which is the expensive operation, and the one you are trying to do less of.

4131
05:55:31,408 --> 05:55:37,220
而 Edit 在原位更改特定文本，这比读取整个文件并写回要省成本。
And edit changes specific text in place, which costs less than reading a whole file and writing it back.

4132
05:55:38,126 --> 05:55:43,620
Glob 用于名称，grep 用于内容，混淆两者是常见的错误答案。
Glob is for names, grep is for contents, and confusing them is a common wrong answer.

4133
05:55:45,294 --> 05:55:47,888
Grep 的功能比人们常用的还要丰富。
Grep has more in it than people use.

4134
05:55:48,368 --> 05:55:54,980
三种输出模式：仅提供文件路径、带行号的匹配行，或者每个文件的匹配计数。
Three output modes giving you file paths only, matching lines with their line numbers, or a count per file.

4135
05:55:55,758 --> 05:55:58,448
先进行计数是一个值得采用的技巧。
Counting first is a trick worth adopting.

4136
05:55:59,022 --> 05:56:06,212
当你不知道规模时，40 个匹配意味着可以继续，而 400 个则需要重新考虑，且计数的成本几乎为零。
When you do not know the scale, 40 matches is a plan and 400 is a rethink, and the count costs almost nothing.

4137
05:56:08,174 --> 05:56:12,996
通过文件类型或 blob 模式进行过滤，在运行前缩小搜索范围。
Filter by file type or by a blob pattern to narrow the search before it runs.

4138
05:56:14,990 --> 05:56:19,172
并请求几行相关的上下文，而不是打开整个文件。
And ask for a few lines of surrounding context instead of opening the whole file.

4139
05:56:20,128 --> 05:56:25,220
当你只需要了解代码结构而非细节时，这已经足够了。
That is enough when you need the shape of the code rather than its detail.

4140
05:56:27,758 --> 05:56:32,516
一旦你读了某些内容，就沿着图谱向外延伸，而不是继续阅读目录中的更多内容。
Once you have read something, follow the graph outward rather than reading more of the directory.

4141
05:56:33,166 --> 05:56:37,508
导入语句告诉你这个文件依赖哪些内容，所以当你需要定义时就去追踪它们。
Imports tell you what this file depends on, so follow them when you need a definition.

4142
05:56:37,968 --> 05:56:42,436
调用者告诉你哪些内容依赖于这个文件，你可以通过搜索函数名称来找到它们。
Callers tell you what depends on this file, and you find them by gripping for the function name.

4143
05:56:43,408 --> 05:56:49,168
测试用例告诉你代码应该做什么，通常比代码本身表达得更清楚。
Tests tell you what the code is supposed to do often more clearly than the code itself does.

4144
05:56:49,328 --> 05:56:56,004
并且有意识地一次跳一跳地追踪，因为每一次跳转都是另一个文件，而每个文件都会增加更多上下文。
And follow deliberately one hop at a time because every hop is another file and every file is more context.

4145
05:56:56,528 --> 05:57:00,420
阅读文件并追踪其导入是一个有界限的策略。
Read the file and follow its imports is a bounded strategy.

4146
05:57:01,294 --> 05:57:02,724
而读取整个模块则不是。
Read the module is not.

4147
05:57:04,398 --> 05:57:08,804
委派是更重型的选项，了解它在什么时候有效是有意义的。
Delegation is the heavier option and it is worth knowing when it pays.

4148
05:57:10,286 --> 05:57:16,708
当任务范围非常广、涉及多个文件以产出简短答案时，交给子代理处理。
Hand exploration to a subagent when it is genuinely broad, touching many files to produce a short answer.

4149
05:57:17,710 --> 05:57:22,404
或者当父级上下文已经变差，而你需要它在核心工作中保持清晰时。
Or when the parent's context is already degrading and you need it sharp for the real work.

4150
05:57:23,246 --> 05:57:26,052
不要为了有针对性的搜索而去调用一个子代理。
Do not reach for one for a targeted search.

4151
05:57:26,766 --> 05:57:32,516
子代理需要一次往返和加载全新上下文，而简单的 grep 命令就能搞定。
A subagent costs a round trip and a fresh context load, and a single grep would have done it.

4152
05:57:33,230 --> 05:57:40,964
Plot 代码会为了这个目的专门派出一个探索子代理，它是处理真正大量阅读任务时的性价比选择。
Plot code ships an explore subagent for exactly this purpose, and it is the cost-effective option for genuinely read-heavy work.

4153
05:57:42,638 --> 05:57:46,756
这里再次提到分叉，因为它很容易与委派混淆。
Forking comes back here because it is easy to confuse with delegation.

4154
05:57:47,088 --> 05:57:56,196
在实验前进行分叉，这样你所在的线程就能保留下来，两个分支都能独立恢复，且原始历史保持不变。
Fork before an experiment, so the thread you are on survives it, with both branches remaining separately resumable and the original history untouched.

4155
05:57:56,608 --> 05:58:00,452
然后对比结果，并从其中一个分支继续。
Then compare the outcomes and continue from whichever branch one.

4156
05:58:01,422 --> 05:58:03,524
重要的限制在第三行。
The important limitation is in the third line.

4157
05:58:04,046 --> 05:58:09,604
分叉会继承父级的上下文，所以它对缓解上下文压力毫无作用。
A fork inherits the parents' context, so it does absolutely nothing for context pressure.

4158
05:58:10,208 --> 05:58:14,916
分叉是为了分支决策，而子代理是为了隔离上下文。
Fork is for branching a decision and a subagent is for isolating context.

4159
05:58:15,648 --> 05:58:22,724
它们在图表上看起来很像，但解决的是不同的问题，这正是考试将它们成对出现的理由。
They look similar in a diagram and they solve different problems, which is exactly why the exam pairs them.

4160
05:58:24,398 --> 05:58:25,508
模式识别。
Pattern recognition.

4161
05:58:25,888 --> 05:58:31,396
同事在智能体闲置时进行了合并，意味着需要一个带有摘要的全新会话或命名刷新。
A colleague merged while the agent was idle means a fresh session with a summary or a named refresh.

4162
05:58:31,648 --> 05:58:37,380
我们要求它重新阅读但它还是搞错了，这意味着仅追加，且两个版本都存在。
We asked it to reread and it still got it wrong, means append only, with both versions present.

4163
05:58:37,648 --> 05:58:42,020
知道哪些文件发生了变化意味着给它们命名，这是廉价且有效的做法。
Knowing which files changed means naming them, which is cheap and effective.

4164
05:58:42,606 --> 05:58:48,324
800 个文件且大多数问题涉及其中，意味着先搜索，然后再阅读搜索结果涉及的内容。
800 files where most questions touch to means search first, then read what the search implicates.

4165
05:58:48,608 --> 05:58:50,528
寻找被调用的文件。
Find files called versus.

4166
05:58:50,848 --> 05:58:53,988
寻找包含内容的项是“块”与“抓取”的区别。
Find files containing is the blob and grip distinction.

4167
05:58:54,670 --> 05:59:00,208
而且大量的探索输出伴随一个简短的答案，意味着子代理或分叉技能。
And huge exploration output with a short answer means a subagent or a forked skill.

4168
05:59:01,454 --> 05:59:02,436
5 行。
5 lines.

4169
05:59:03,648 --> 05:59:07,620
数量和陈旧是两个不同的问题，有不同的对策。
Volume and staleness are different problems with different fixes.

4170
05:59:08,048 --> 05:59:10,128
对话是仅追加的。
Conversations are append only.

4171
05:59:10,288 --> 05:59:13,888
所以重新读取会增加一个版本，且永远不会删除旧的。
So rereading adds a version and never removes one.

4172
05:59:14,702 --> 05:59:18,212
能明确名称变化时就标注出来，不能时就重新开始。
Name what change when you can and start fresh when you cannot.

4173
05:59:19,273 --> 05:59:26,308
定位、缩小范围、读取、追踪，因为在读取之前的每一步都是为了让读取的内容更少。
Locate, narrow, read, follow, Because every step before the read exists to make the read smaller.

4174
05:59:27,182 --> 05:59:30,308
而且 glob 用于匹配名称，而 grep 用于搜索内容。
And glob is for names while glep is for contents.

4175
05:59:30,734 --> 05:59:33,572
而且这两者都不会把文件加载到上下文中。
And neither of them loads a file into context.

4176
05:59:35,342 --> 05:59:36,740
现在有五个场景。
Five scenarios now.

4177
05:59:37,134 --> 05:59:40,292
其中一个完全基于「仅追加」这一事实。
And one turns entirely on the append only fact.

4178
05:59:41,582 --> 05:59:42,528
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

4179
05:59:42,830 --> 05:59:45,188
一名工程师在午餐后恢复了一个会话。
An engineer resumes a session after lunch.

4180
05:59:46,030 --> 05:59:46,916
三个文件。
Three files.

4181
05:59:47,568 --> 05:59:50,788
智能体之前读过的文件后来被同事修改了。
The agent had read have since been modified by a colleague.

4182
05:59:51,374 --> 05:59:55,140
工程师要求智能体在继续之前重新读取这三个文件。
The engineer asks the agent to reread those three files before continuing.

4183
05:59:55,790 --> 05:59:56,516
它执行了重读。
It does.

4184
05:59:57,102 --> 06:00:01,380
随后它生成了代码，但使用的是午餐前的版本中的函数签名。
It then produces code that uses a function signature from the pre-lunch version.

4185
06:00:02,318 --> 06:00:04,964
没有任何内容被截断，也没有发生错误。
Nothing was truncated and no error occurred.

4186
06:00:06,126 --> 06:00:07,076
发生了什么？
What is happening?

4187
06:00:07,534 --> 06:00:11,556
A. 重读失败了且没有报错，返回的是缓存的内容。
a The reread failed silently and returned cached contents.

4188
06:00:12,174 --> 06:00:17,604
B. 两个版本现在都在对话中，没有任何标记显示旧版本已被替换。
B. Both versions are now in the conversation and nothing marks the older one as superseded.

4189
06:00:18,158 --> 06:00:22,768
C. 智能体无法读取在会话期间发生变化的。
C. The agent cannot read files that change during a session d.

4190
06:00:23,168 --> 06:00:26,692
D. 上下文窗口失败了，导致较新的读取内容被丢弃。
The context window failed and the newer read was dropped.

4191
06:00:27,118 --> 06:00:28,356
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4192
06:00:33,710 --> 06:00:34,724
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

4193
06:00:34,928 --> 06:00:40,128
这个场景之所以存在，是因为工程师做了符合直觉的操作，结果反而让情况变糟了。
And this scenario exists because the engineer did the intuitive thing and it made matters worse.

4194
06:00:40,368 --> 06:00:48,836
要求智能体重读一个修改过的文件感觉像是刷新它。但因为对话是仅追加的，并没有替换机制。
Asking the agent to reread a changed file feels like refreshing it. It is not because a conversation is append only and there is no mechanism for replacement.

4195
06:00:49,454 --> 06:00:54,980
新的读取内容出现在旧内容之后，两者都存在，且都没有标记说明哪个是当前的。
The new read lands after the old one, both are present and neither carries a marker saying which is current.

4196
06:00:55,168 --> 06:00:56,964
所以模型可能会从任何一个版本中进行推理。
So the model may reason from either.

4197
06:00:57,408 --> 06:01:01,088
选项 A、C 和 D 都虚构了不存在的机制。
Options A, C and D all invent mechanisms.

4198
06:01:01,408 --> 06:01:06,848
D 被题干明确排除，因为题干说没有任何内容被截断且没有发生错误。
D is ruled out explicitly by the stem, which says nothing was truncated and no error occurred.

4199
06:01:07,342 --> 06:01:12,356
解决方法是声明之前的版本已过时，或者重新开始。
The fix is to state that the earlier version is superseded or to start fresh.

4200
06:01:13,870 --> 06:01:14,948
场景 2。
Scenario 2.

4201
06:01:15,248 --> 06:01:19,716
一个智能体在回答关于包含约 800 个文件的代码库的问题。
An agent answers questions about a repository of roughly 800 files.

4202
06:01:20,128 --> 06:01:25,764
它目前的做法是在回答之前，读取相关顶层目录中的每一个文件。
Its current approach is to read every file in the relevant top level directory before answering.

4203
06:01:26,318 --> 06:01:29,124
这些目录包含的文件数量从 12 到 300 不等。
Directories range from 12 to 300 files.

4204
06:01:29,870 --> 06:01:35,012
在文件较少的目录中，回答质量很好；而在文件较多的目录中，回答明显变差且速度更慢。
Answers on the small directories are good, and on the large ones they are noticeably worse and slower.

4205
06:01:35,328 --> 06:01:38,948
分析显示，大多数问题只涉及一到两个文件。
Analysis shows most questions concern one or two files.

4206
06:01:39,248 --> 06:01:41,088
哪种改变最有效？
What is the most effective change?

4207
06:01:41,408 --> 06:01:46,116
a. 分批读取目录，在继续之前对每批内容进行总结。
a read the directory in batches, summarizing each batch before moving on.

4208
06:01:46,638 --> 06:01:46,848
b.
b.

4209
06:01:47,248 --> 06:01:52,516
使用 grep 查找相关符号，仅读取匹配的文件，然后根据需要追踪导入。
Crep for the relevant symbols, read only the files that match, then follow imports as needed.

4210
06:01:53,102 --> 06:01:57,508
c. 构建代码库索引，并在每次会话开始时加载它。
c. Build an index of the repository and load it at the start of each session.

4211
06:01:58,158 --> 06:02:01,924
d. 按修改时间顺序读取文件，最近修改的优先。
D. Read files in order of modification time, most recent first.

4212
06:02:02,766 --> 06:02:03,844
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4213
06:02:09,550 --> 06:02:11,296
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

4214
06:02:11,982 --> 06:02:17,188
诊断细节是：在小目录中回答很好，而在大目录中表现变差。
The diagnostic detail is that answers are good on small directories and worse on large ones.

4215
06:02:17,710 --> 06:02:23,044
这说明文件读取量是变量，而不是问题本身有问题。
That tells you the volume of files read is the variable rather than anything about the questions.

4216
06:02:23,758 --> 06:02:27,908
目前的策略随目录大小而变化，但它本应根据相关性来变化。
The strategy scales with directory size when it should scale with relevance.

4217
06:02:28,782 --> 06:02:34,084
选项 A 是这个领域中常见的陷阱，因为读取后总结并不能提供帮助。
Option A is the recurring trap in this domain because summarizing after reading cannot help.

4218
06:02:34,416 --> 06:02:40,260
到你进行总结时，每个文件都已经进入上下文了，而总结只是额外消耗 Token。
Every file has already entered context by the time you summarize, and the summary is additional tokens on top.

4219
06:02:40,846 --> 06:02:45,988
选项 D 只是重新排列了阅读顺序而没有减少内容，而且“新近”不等于“相关”。
Option D reorders the reading without reducing it, and recency is not relevance.

4220
06:02:46,798 --> 06:02:51,300
选项 C 为某些功能支付了固定的上下文成本。
Option C pays a standing context cost for something.

4221
06:02:51,536 --> 06:02:53,444
实时搜索并无益处。
A live search does for nothing.

4222
06:02:54,990 --> 06:02:59,972
场景 3，这个题目故意设计得很简单，因为考试中确实会考到它。
Scenario 3, and this one is deliberately simple because the exam does ask it.

4223
06:03:01,262 --> 06:03:09,188
一名工程师需要在庞大的代码库中找到所有仍在调用名为 calculate_tax 的弃用函数的地点。
An engineer needs to find every place a deprecated function called calculate tax is still being called across a large code base.

4224
06:03:10,062 --> 06:03:17,056
他们还需要找出所有符合 config.something.json 命名规范的配置文件。
They also need to find all the configuration files which follow the naming convention config.something.json.

4225
06:03:17,678 --> 06:03:20,612
他们正在决定智能体应该使用哪些工具。
They are deciding which tools the agent should use.

4226
06:03:21,070 --> 06:03:22,628
哪种组合是正确的？
Which combination is correct?

4227
06:03:23,630 --> 06:03:28,228
a. 使用 blob 查找 calculate_tax，并用 grep 查找配置文件。
a blob for calculate tax and grep for the config files.

4228
06:03:29,056 --> 06:03:29,296
b.
B.

4229
06:03:29,776 --> 06:03:33,156
使用 grep 查找 calculate_tax，并用 glob 查找配置文件。
Grep for calculate tax and glob for the config files.

4230
06:03:33,678 --> 06:03:33,936
c.
C.

4231
06:03:34,286 --> 06:03:35,296
两个都用 grep。
Grep for both.

4232
06:03:35,456 --> 06:03:37,540
因为 grep 也可以匹配文件名。
Since grep can match file names too.

4233
06:03:37,856 --> 06:03:38,096
D。
D.

4234
06:03:38,576 --> 06:03:41,892
读取目录列表，然后读取每个候选文件。
Read the directory listing, then read each candidate file.

4235
06:03:42,510 --> 06:03:43,684
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4236
06:03:49,358 --> 06:03:53,456
答案是 B，而这个案例之所以出现在这里是因为选项 A。
The answer is B and the reason this scenario is here is option A.

4237
06:03:53,646 --> 06:03:59,364
它是被反转后的正确答案，而在时间压力下，反转后的答案听起来也非常有道理。
It is the correct answer reversed, and under time pressure, a reversed answer reads perfectly plausibly.

4238
06:03:59,822 --> 06:04:04,576
函数调用存在于文件内部。所以那是内容，而内容交给 grep 处理。
Function calls live inside files. So that is content and content goes to grep.

4239
06:04:04,896 --> 06:04:07,696
文件名是路径，所以那部分交给 blob 处理。
File names are paths, so that goes to blob.

4240
06:04:08,302 --> 06:04:12,772
选项 C 值得思考一下，因为它并不完全错误。
Option C is worth a moment because it is not exactly wrong.

4241
06:04:13,966 --> 06:04:21,316
Grep 可以找到内容中提到的文件名，而 glob 是专门为路径匹配优化的工具，处理起来更高效。
Grep could find file names mentioned in content, and glob is the purpose built tuned for path matching and is cheaper for it.

4242
06:04:22,030 --> 06:04:28,708
选项 D 加载了每一个候选文件，却只是为了回答一个通过两次搜索就能解决且无需加载任何内容的问题。
Option D loads every candidate file to answer a question that two searches answer without loading anything at all.

4243
06:04:30,382 --> 06:04:31,332
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

4244
06:04:32,270 --> 06:04:36,452
一名开发人员正与智能体一起进行复杂的重构。
A developer is deep in a complex refactor with an agent.

4245
06:04:36,816 --> 06:04:43,748
他们想尝试一种截然不同的方法，但如果失败了，也不想丢失当前的思路。
They want to try a substantially different approach, but do not want to lose the current thread if it does not work out.

4246
06:04:44,558 --> 06:04:51,492
另外，智能体的上下文已占用约 70%，且近期的建议准确度有所下降。
Separately, the agent's context is around 70% full and its recent suggestions have become less precise.

4247
06:04:51,776 --> 06:04:57,156
一位同事建议将该实验作为子代理运行，因为这样可以保持上下文隔离。
A colleague suggests running the experiment as a subagent since that keeps context isolated.

4248
06:04:57,536 --> 06:04:58,692
他们该怎么做？
What should they do?

4249
06:04:59,086 --> 06:05:02,308
a. 按照建议，将实验作为子代理运行。
a run the experiment as a subagent as suggested.

4250
06:05:03,214 --> 06:05:08,548
b. 为实验分叉会话，并单独处理上下文压力。
b fork the session for the experiment and separately address the context pressure.

4251
06:05:09,216 --> 06:05:12,964
c. 为实验开启一个没有任何上下文的新会话。
C. Start a fresh session for the experiment with no context.

4252
06:05:13,582 --> 06:05:18,372
d. 在当前会话中继续操作，如果实验失败则撤销更改。
D. Continue in the same session and revert the changes if the experiment fails.

4253
06:05:19,822 --> 06:05:20,836
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4254
06:05:26,496 --> 06:05:32,164
答案是 B，而这个场景的设计核心在于同事的建议混淆了两个问题。
The answer is B, and the scenario is built around the colleague's suggestion being a conflation.

4255
06:05:32,656 --> 06:05:34,276
这里有两个问题。
There are two problems here.

4256
06:05:34,990 --> 06:05:38,308
一是想要分支决策，二是上下文窗口快满了。
Wanting to branch a decision and a context window filling up.

4257
06:05:38,862 --> 06:05:44,836
分叉解决了第一个问题，但对第二个问题毫无帮助，因为分叉会继承父级上下文。
Fork solves the first and does nothing for the second, since a fork inherits the parent's context.

4258
06:05:45,646 --> 06:05:48,868
子代理能解决第二个问题，但对于第一个问题是错误的。
A subagent would help with the second and is wrong for the first.

4259
06:05:49,550 --> 06:05:56,580
子代理不继承任何内容，而一个继续进行的深度重构实验需要保留这些重构的上下文。
Subagents inherit nothing, and an experiment continuing a deep refactor needs that refactors context.

4260
06:05:57,486 --> 06:06:00,836
选项 D 值得注意，因为它呼应了模块 4 的内容。
Option D is worth noting because it recalls module 4.

4261
06:06:01,742 --> 06:06:09,060
还原文件并不会撤销对话，因此被放弃的方法仍留在上下文中，会干扰后续的轮次。
Reverting the files does not revert the conversation, so the abandoned approach stays in context, confusing later turns.

4262
06:06:11,950 --> 06:06:12,996
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

4263
06:06:16,846 --> 06:06:21,188
一个智能体在为期两天的迁移过程中维持一个长周期的会话。
An agent maintains a long running session across a two-day migration.

4264
06:06:21,806 --> 06:06:32,100
第二天早上，工程师知道由于夜间的持续集成，两个目录中的所有文件都重新格式化了，并且有一个依赖项被升级了。
On the second morning, the engineer knows that overnight continuous integration has reformatted every file in two directories and that one dependency was upgraded.

4265
06:06:32,656 --> 06:06:37,476
他们无法轻易列出哪些特定文件受到了重构影响。
They cannot easily enumerate which specific files the reformatting touched.

4266
06:06:38,350 --> 06:06:41,444
该智能体在前一天读过大约 30 个文件。
The agent had read about 30 files the previous day.

4267
06:06:42,318 --> 06:06:45,828
昨天做出的决定仍然有效，而且是经过艰苦博弈才得出的。
The decisions made yesterday are still valid and were hard won.

4268
06:06:46,606 --> 06:06:48,484
最合适的方法是什么？
What is the most appropriate approach?

4269
06:06:49,358 --> 06:06:54,244
a. 继续对话并告诉智能体格式变了但逻辑没变。
a resume and tell the agent that formatting changed but the logic did not.

4270
06:06:54,670 --> 06:06:59,556
b. 开启一个包含昨天决策和当前状态摘要的新会话。
b. Start a fresh session with a summary of yesterday's decisions and the current state.

4271
06:07:00,016 --> 06:07:03,844
c. 继续对话并要求智能体重新阅读所有 30 个文件。
C. Resume and ask the agent to reread all 30 files.

4272
06:07:04,336 --> 06:07:08,708
d. 继续对话，因为格式变化不影响逻辑。
D. Resume and continue since formatting changes do not affect logic.

4273
06:07:17,230 --> 06:07:25,216
答案是 B，而且题干包含了本模块前面提到的判定标准，几乎一模一样。
The answer is B and the stem contains the tiebreaker from earlier in this module, almost word for word.

4274
06:07:25,870 --> 06:07:30,820
他们无法轻易列出哪些变动了，而这种不确定性本身就是答案所在。
They cannot easily enumerate what changed, and that uncertainty is itself the answer.

4275
06:07:31,630 --> 06:07:38,596
结合那些仍然有效且关键的决策，就正好符合“携带摘要并开启新会话”的情况。
Combine it with decisions that are still valid and hard one, and you have exactly the case for a fresh session carrying a summary.

4276
06:07:39,216 --> 06:07:49,136
选项 C 是最差的选择，因为它把 30 个过时的版本和 30 个当前的版本都放进了一个对话里，这是大规模的场景 1。
Option C is the worst choice available because it puts 30 stale versions and 30 current ones into one conversation, which is scenario 1 at scale.

4277
06:07:49,776 --> 06:07:56,932
选项 A 对格式处理得比较合理，但忽略了依赖项升级，而这确实可能改变行为。
Option A handles the formatting sensibly and ignores the dependency upgrade, which can genuinely change behavior.

4278
06:07:57,616 --> 06:08:00,868
选项 D 把那个升级当成了纯外观上的变动。
Option D treats that upgrade as cosmetic.

4279
06:08:02,382 --> 06:08:03,940
模块 17。
Module 17.

4280
06:08:05,006 --> 06:08:06,788
接下来是关于升级的内容。
Next on escalation.

4281
06:08:08,398 --> 06:08:17,380
模块 17 结束了领域 5 并结束了所学内容的讲解。接下来是三个跨领域的实操模块，然后是模拟考试。
Module 17 closes domain 5 and closes the taught material. Three modules of cross-cutting work follow, then the practice exams.

4282
06:08:17,838 --> 06:08:22,596
这个模块是关于系统操作与人工操作之间的界限。
This module is about the boundary between what the system does and what a person does.

4283
06:08:23,246 --> 06:08:28,932
何时进行升级、如何移交，以及如何在不被误导的情况下使用置信度评分。
When to escalate, how to hand over, and how to use confidence scores without being fooled by them.

4284
06:08:30,478 --> 06:08:35,588
这里有一个概念几乎会坑到所有人，它出现在大约一半的位置。
There is one idea in here that catches almost everybody, and it arrives about halfway through.

4285
06:08:36,142 --> 06:08:38,596
留意关于“自信的错误”的那张幻灯片。
Watch for the slide about confident errors.

4286
06:08:39,950 --> 06:08:44,164
首先要明确目标，因为新手经常去优化错误的目标。
Start by fixing the goal because teens often optimize for the wrong one.

4287
06:08:45,216 --> 06:08:48,036
一个从不进行升级的系统不是一个好的系统。
A system that never escalates is not a good system.

4288
06:08:48,782 --> 06:08:55,588
那是一个试图处理所有事情（包括它本不该处理的事情）的系统，而且由于没人去询问，这些失败是隐形的。
It is a system that handles everything, including the things it should not have handled, and the failures are invisible because nobody was asked.

4289
06:08:56,336 --> 06:09:05,156
目标是在智能体把事情搞砸之前在正确的时刻进行升级，并提供足够的信息让人员能够立即接手。
The goal is to escalate at the right moment before the agent has made things worse, and with enough information that the human can pick up immediately.

4290
06:09:06,670 --> 06:09:08,900
升级率并不是衡量标准。
Escalation rate is not the metric.

4291
06:09:09,294 --> 06:09:13,668
以可用的状态将正确的案例进行升级，这才是衡量标准。
Escalating the right cases in a usable state is the metric.

4292
06:09:15,182 --> 06:09:18,816
有六个触发条件，第六个是最重要的。
Six triggers and the sixth is the important one.

4293
06:09:19,296 --> 06:09:25,732
当案例超出政策范围时进行升级，因为智能体不应该决定是否给予例外情况。
Escalate when the case falls outside policy, because an agent should not be deciding whether to grant an exception.

4294
06:09:26,176 --> 06:09:30,884
当操作不可逆或具有高价值时，比如大额退款或删除操作。
When the action is irreversible or high value, like a large refund or a deletion.

4295
06:09:31,726 --> 06:09:39,812
当客户感到焦虑或明确要求人工服务时，因为这个请求本身就是判定标准，不需要额外评估。
When the customer is distressed or explicitly asks for a person, because that request is itself the criterion and does not need evaluating.

4296
06:09:40,718 --> 06:09:48,516
当智能体在同一件事上连续失败两次时，因为第三次尝试很少能成功，或者当它根本就没有处理能力时。
When the agent has failed twice on the same thing, since a third attempt is rarely the one that works, and when it simply lacks the capability.

4297
06:09:49,296 --> 06:09:51,812
第六个是来自模块 4 的兜底条款。
The sixth is the catch-all from module 4.

4298
06:09:52,270 --> 06:09:58,468
任何未能结束或解决的情况都要进行升级，这涵盖了你没想到的那些情况。
Anything that did not end, resolve gets escalated, which covers the cases you did not think of.

4299
06:10:00,142 --> 06:10:01,536
升级准则。
Escalation criteria.

4300
06:10:01,776 --> 06:10:02,816
以同样的方式失败。
Fail the same way.

4301
06:10:03,056 --> 06:10:04,260
提示准则。
Prompt the criteria.

4302
06:10:05,102 --> 06:10:08,100
失败。所以模块 12 的课程内容直接适用。
Fail. So module 12's lesson applies directly.

4303
06:10:09,742 --> 06:10:11,844
描述属性，而不是具体的案例。
Describe the property rather than the case.

4304
06:10:12,526 --> 06:10:15,776
请求对既定政策的例外情况是通用的。
Request an exception to stated policy generalizes.

4305
06:10:16,302 --> 06:10:23,108
询问关于 30 天规则的问题，如果不这样做，就会漏掉下一个询问不同规则的客户。
Asks about the 30-day rule, does not, and it will miss the next customer who asks about a different rule.

4306
06:10:23,376 --> 06:10:28,548
按“为什么需要人工”来对你的准则进行分组，而不是按“客户刚好说了什么”来分类。
Group your criteria by why a human is needed rather than by what the customer happened to say.

4307
06:10:29,296 --> 06:10:36,644
通过询问一个准则会漏掉什么来测试它，而不是去确认它。这样能捕捉到促使你编写该准则的那个例子。
And test a criterion by asking what it misses rather than by confirming it. Catches the example that prompted you to write it.

4308
06:10:38,062 --> 06:10:41,316
最后一个习惯是“规则”和“补丁”之间的区别。
That last habit is the difference between a rule and a patch.

4309
06:10:42,734 --> 06:10:46,916
重试和升级容易混淆，所以值得将它们清晰地分开。
Retry and escalate get confused, so it is worth separating them cleanly.

4310
06:10:47,598 --> 06:10:49,764
当出现瞬时错误时进行重试。
Retry when something transient went wrong.

4311
06:10:51,982 --> 06:10:59,076
超时、速率限制、503，这些情况下的下一次尝试有真正的成功机会，且请求本身没有任何问题。
A timeout, a rate limit, a 503 where the next attempt has a genuine chance and nothing about the request itself was wrong.

4312
06:10:59,950 --> 06:11:03,524
设置尝试次数上限，并在达到上限时无论如何进行升级。
Cap the attempts and escalate anyway when the cap is reached.

4313
06:11:04,110 --> 06:11:10,272
当情况需要判断时进行升级。即超出政策范围或超出智能体的权限。
Escalate when the situation needs judgment. It is outside policy or beyond the agent's authority.

4314
06:11:10,478 --> 06:11:14,756
同样的错误已经发生两次，或者客户要求人工服务。
The same failure has already happened twice or the customer asked for a person.

4315
06:11:15,406 --> 06:11:18,116
模块 6 就错误问题强调了这一点。
Module 6 made this point about errors.

4316
06:11:18,958 --> 06:11:20,992
对于案例来说也是同样成立的。
It is equally true about cases.

4317
06:11:21,232 --> 06:11:24,900
确定性的问题在第三次尝试时不会变得可解决。
Deterministic problems do not become resolvable on the third attempt.

4318
06:11:26,286 --> 06:11:28,900
现在是团队经常忽略的部分。
Now the part teams consistently skip.

4319
06:11:29,472 --> 06:11:31,044
升级很容易。
Escalating is easy.

4320
06:11:31,872 --> 06:11:34,352
有意义的升级才是核心工作。
Escalating usefully is the work.

4321
06:11:34,592 --> 06:11:43,940
如果呈现在人工人员面前的是原始转录记录，你就只是创建了一个工单。那个人现在必须读完全部内容才能搞清楚目前进展到哪了。
If what lands in front of the human is a raw transcript, you have created a ticket. That person now has to read the whole thing to work out where they are.

4322
06:11:44,654 --> 06:11:49,700
如果它带有结构化信息，你就完成了一次交接，他们可以在几秒钟内采取行动。
If it arrives with structure, you have created a handover and they can act within seconds.

4323
06:11:50,032 --> 06:11:58,032
这两者之间的区别体现在处理时间、客户的沮丧感，以及最终导致员工不再信任自动化
The difference between those two shows up as handling time, as customer frustration, and eventually as staff who stop trusting the automated

4324
06:11:58,192 --> 06:11:59,140
路由上。
route entirely.

4325
06:12:00,910 --> 06:12:01,712
六件事。
Six things.

4326
06:12:01,952 --> 06:12:03,204
为什么触发升级？
Why it escalated?

4327
06:12:03,502 --> 06:12:06,592
用一句话说明触发了哪项标准。
In one line, naming which criterion fired.

4328
06:12:06,752 --> 06:12:11,204
清晰且独立地陈述客户的需求，而不是按照他们表达的方式来写。
What the customer wants stated plainly and separately from how they phrased it.

4329
06:12:12,014 --> 06:12:15,844
已经确认过的信息，这样人工人员就不需要重复查询了。
What has already been established so the human does not redo the lookups.

4330
06:12:16,782 --> 06:12:24,196
已经告诉过客户的内容，以免人工人员前后矛盾。如果缺失这一项，会造成严重的后果。
What has already been said to the customer so the human does not contradict it. That is the one that causes real damage when it is missing.

4331
06:12:25,230 --> 06:12:29,028
还有哪些待决事项以及可选方案（如果有的话）？
What remains to be decided with the options if there are any?

4332
06:12:29,678 --> 06:12:36,196
并将转录记录作为附件而非作为交接内容呈现，这样它就在那里供查阅，而不是必须去读。
And the transcript attached rather than presented as the handover, so it is available without being required.

4333
06:12:36,878 --> 06:12:42,788
所有这些信息都可以从会话中推导出来，除非升级流程本身就是为了提取这些信息而设计的。
All of that is derivable from the session and nobody derives it unless the escalation is designed to.

4334
06:12:44,494 --> 06:12:45,732
现在是第二部分。
Now the second half.

4335
06:12:46,112 --> 06:12:49,796
置信度评分确实很有用，但经常被误读。
Confidence scores are genuinely useful and they are routinely misread.

4336
06:12:51,054 --> 06:12:56,516
0.85 的得分并不意味着答案有 85% 的概率是正确的。
A score of 0.85 is not a claim that the answer is correct 85% of the time.

4337
06:12:57,454 --> 06:13:05,284
它是模型产生的一个信号，该模型并非为了输出校准概率而训练的，它的含义完全取决于你的数据告诉你的是什么。
It is a signal produced by a model that was not trained to output calibrated probabilities, and it means whatever your data says it means.

4338
06:13:05,712 --> 06:13:09,540
只要你花点功夫去搞清楚你的数据意味着什么，这就没问题。
Which is fine as long as you do the work of finding out what your data says.

4339
06:13:09,792 --> 06:13:13,508
错误的做法是把这个数字当作自带某种特定含义的东西来对待。
The mistake is treating the number as though it arrived with a meaning attached.

4340
06:13:15,086 --> 06:13:16,196
4 个实践。
4 Practices.

4341
06:13:16,672 --> 06:13:22,820
根据重要程度，在每个记录或每个字段的输出中同时要求提供一个置信度评分。
Ask for a confidence score alongside every output per record or per field, depending on what matters.

4342
06:13:24,462 --> 06:13:32,100
在代码中进行过滤而不是在提示词中过滤，因为让模型去过滤会隐藏它丢弃的内容，这是模块 12 的规则。
Filter in your code rather than in the prompt because a model asked to filter hides what it discarded, which was module 12's rule.

4343
06:13:32,992 --> 06:13:38,884
根据得分计算出一个审查平铺，这样路由就是你流水线中的一条规则，而不是模型中的一个判断。
Compute a review flat from the score so that routing is a rule in your pipeline rather than a judgment in the model.

4344
06:13:39,232 --> 06:13:43,908
并且在信任任何特定数字之前，先针对标注好的数据集校准阈值。
And calibrate the threshold against a labeled set before you trust any particular number.

4345
06:13:44,112 --> 06:13:46,276
需要记住的重点就在这个提示框里。
The line to hold is in the callout.

4346
06:13:47,086 --> 06:13:52,516
得分是你路由逻辑的一个输入，它本身并不是路由逻辑。
The score is an input to your routing logic and it is not the routing logic.

4347
06:13:53,902 --> 06:13:57,444
校准并不复杂，但经常被忽略。
Calibration is not complicated and it is often skipped.

4348
06:13:57,774 --> 06:14:05,124
抽取几百个输出，标注每个是正确还是错误，并观察错误相对于得分分布在什么位置。
Take a few hundred outputs, label each one correct or not, and look at where the errors actually sit relative to the scores.

4349
06:14:05,614 --> 06:14:08,516
这能告诉你给定的阈值能带来什么收益以及会产生什么成本。
That tells you what a given threshold buys and costs.

4350
06:14:09,262 --> 06:14:17,572
阈值本身是在审查量和漏报率之间做权衡，降低阈值意味着增加审核量但减少漏报，提高阈值则相反。
The threshold itself trades reviewer load against misses, so lowering it means reviewing more and missing fewer, and raising it means the reverse.

4351
06:14:17,872 --> 06:14:22,180
仅仅因为 0.8 听起来差不多就选它，本质上是带个数字的盲目猜测。
Picking 0.8 because it sounds about right is guessing with a number attached.

4352
06:14:22,734 --> 06:14:29,604
并且在输入变化时重新校准。因为基于去年文档调整的阈值，恰恰就是这种过时的东西。
And recalibrate when your inputs change. Because a threshold tuned on last year's documents is exactly that.

4353
06:14:30,958 --> 06:14:33,680
这是本模块需要记住的幻灯片。
Here is the slide to remember from this module.

4354
06:14:33,840 --> 06:14:41,924
如果你的审核队列包含所有低于阈值的内容，那么从结构上讲，它只包含模型不确定的情况。
If your review queue contains everything below the threshold, then by construction it contains only cases where the model was unsure.

4355
06:14:42,320 --> 06:14:48,228
模型自信产生的每一个错误，都会直接跳过审核进入生产环节。
Every error the model made confidently sales straight past unreviewed into production.

4356
06:14:48,974 --> 06:14:55,012
而且高置信度的错误并不罕见。它们发生在模型误解了某些内容而非犹豫不决时。
And confident errors are not rare. They happen when the model has misunderstood something rather than hesitated.

4357
06:14:55,520 --> 06:14:58,692
从内部逻辑来看，误解并不带有不确定感。
A misunderstanding does not feel uncertain from the inside.

4358
06:14:59,246 --> 06:15:04,996
因此，仅靠低置信度的审核队列，在系统性地忽略一整类故障。
So a low confidence review queue on its own is systematically blind to an entire class of failure.

4359
06:15:06,478 --> 06:15:07,457
所以要建立两个队列。
So build two queues.

4360
06:15:07,886 --> 06:15:15,360
第一个是所有低于阈值的内容，它能捕捉到模型犹豫不决的错误，且量可预测，是必要的。
The first is everything below the threshold, which catches the errors the model hesitated on, has predictable volume, and is necessary.

4361
06:15:15,600 --> 06:15:21,540
第二个是从高于阈值的内容中抽取的样本，它能捕捉到模型自信心过强的错误。
The second is a sample drawn from above the threshold which catches the errors the model was confident about.

4362
06:15:22,350 --> 06:15:24,836
极小的比例就足以发现某种模式。
A small percentage is enough to detect a pattern.

4363
06:15:25,230 --> 06:15:29,476
它还承担第二个任务：告诉你你的阈值设置是否正确。
It also does a second job, telling you whether your threshold is set correctly.

4364
06:15:29,966 --> 06:15:32,292
要记住这个提示框里的表述。
The framing in the callout is the one to carry.

4365
06:15:32,878 --> 06:15:35,972
第一个队列保护的是你已经怀疑到的情况。
The first queue protects the cases you already suspected.

4366
06:15:36,880 --> 06:15:43,588
第二个队列告诉你哪些地方搞错了，这更有价值，但几乎没人去建立它。
The second one tells you what you are wrong about, which is more valuable, and almost nobody builds it.

4367
06:15:45,230 --> 06:15:48,388
如果你要进行采样，就得规范地采样。
If you are going to sample, sample properly.

4368
06:15:49,006 --> 06:15:55,268
要跨文档类型、来源和置信度区间进行分层抽样，而不是随机均匀抽取。
Stratify across document types, sources, and confidence bands rather than drawing uniformly at random.

4369
06:15:56,654 --> 06:16:01,200
对一个偏斜的群体进行均匀采样，大多只能让你看到最常见的情况。
A uniform sample of a skewed population mostly shows you the common case.

4370
06:16:01,774 --> 06:16:09,380
极小的比例就足以发现系统性问题，虽然不足以精确测量其发生率，但你追求的是检测到它。
A small percentage is enough to detect a systematic problem, though not enough to measure its rate precisely, and detection is what you are after.

4371
06:16:09,742 --> 06:16:17,156
将你的发现反馈到标准、架构或阈值中，因为不采取行动的发现仅仅是一个事实。
Feed whatever you find back into the criteria, the schema or the threshold, because a finding you do not act on is just a fact.

4372
06:16:17,998 --> 06:16:24,260
并且记住，只对简单类别进行采样，只能可靠地告诉你这个简单类别没问题。
And remember that sampling only the easy category will reliably tell you the easy category is fine.

4373
06:16:25,998 --> 06:16:27,620
再来一个关于可靠性的案例。
One more reliability case.

4374
06:16:28,000 --> 06:16:33,476
当工具或后端宕机时，智能体仍必须在某个地方结束交互。
When a tool or a backend is down, the agent still has to end the interaction somewhere.

4375
06:16:34,478 --> 06:16:38,884
说明什么不可用，并用用户真正关心的术语来解释这意味着什么。
Say what is unavailable and what that means in terms the person actually cares about.

4376
06:16:39,598 --> 06:16:44,388
提供你仍能做到的任何操作，因为部分帮助优于直接拒绝。
Offer whatever you can still do because partial help beats a blank refusal.

4377
06:16:44,878 --> 06:16:49,860
记录请求并承诺后续跟进，让交互在明确的节点结束。
Capture the request and commit to a follow-up so the interaction ends somewhere definite.

4378
06:16:50,702 --> 06:16:57,988
永远不要用记忆中的内容来代替工具，因为一个看似合理的虚构答案比诚实的故障报告要糟糕得多。
And never answer from memory as a substitute for the tool because a plausible invented answer is considerably worse than an honest outage.

4379
06:16:58,606 --> 06:17:02,500
优雅降级仍然意味着结束、解决或升级。
Degrading gracefully still means ending, resolved, or escalated.

4380
06:17:03,438 --> 06:17:06,244
宕机并不代表可以无休止地拖延。
An outage is not permission to end nowhere.

4381
06:17:07,822 --> 06:17:08,932
模式识别。
Pattern recognition.

4382
06:17:09,360 --> 06:17:14,244
人类需要阅读整份转录记录，这意味着是结构化交接而非简单的工单。
The human has to read the whole transcript means a structured handover rather than a ticket.

4383
06:17:14,560 --> 06:17:19,204
错误仍能通过审核，意味着也需要对高置信度的输出进行抽样。
Errors getting through despite review means sample the high confidence output as well.

4384
06:17:19,760 --> 06:17:25,700
智能体自信但判断错误，这意味着从结构上讲，置信度阈值无法捕捉到这类情况。
The agent was confident and wrong, means a confidence threshold cannot catch this by construction.

4385
06:17:26,638 --> 06:17:31,236
我们选择 0.8 作为阈值，意味着需要对照标注好的数据集进行校准。
We picked 0.8 as the threshold means calibrate against a labeled set.

4386
06:17:31,520 --> 06:17:34,916
它一直在尝试同样的事情，这意味着要限制重试次数并及时升级处理。
It keeps trying the same thing means cap the retrees and escalate.

4387
06:17:35,440 --> 06:17:43,044
而且后端宕机时它编造了内容，意味着要执行解释、提供选项和捕获，绝不能用记忆来代替工具。
And the backend was down and it invented something means explain, offer, and capture, never substituting memory for a tool.

4388
06:17:44,302 --> 06:17:52,320
关闭领域模块需要五行代码。要在正确时刻提供正确信息时进行升级，因为速率并不是衡量标准。
Five lines to close the domain modules. Escalate at the right moment with the right information because the rate is not the metric.

4389
06:17:52,617 --> 06:17:57,444
将准则写成属性，而不是作为触发这些准词的事件来写。
write criteria as properties rather than as the incident that prompted them.

4390
06:17:58,030 --> 06:18:04,228
交接内容包括：名称、升级原因、已确立的内容、已沟通的内容以及剩余待办事项。
A handover names, why it escalated, what is established, what has been said, and what remains.

4391
06:18:04,910 --> 06:18:15,524
低置信度审核无法识别高置信度的错误。因此，也需要对高于阈值的记录进行抽样。并且在输入变化时，基于标注数据重新校准阈值。
Low confidence review is blind to confident errors. So sample above the threshold as well. And calibrate the threshold on labeled data, recalibrating when the inputs change.

4392
06:18:16,494 --> 06:18:17,924
现在是六个场景。
Six scenarios now.

4393
06:18:18,320 --> 06:18:22,948
接下来是三个横向模块和模拟考试。
Then the three cross-cutting modules and the practice exams.

4394
06:18:24,494 --> 06:18:25,444
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

4395
06:18:26,734 --> 06:18:31,040
提取流水线会将任何评分低于 0.75 的记录路由到人工审核。
An extraction pipeline routes any record scoring below 0.75.

4396
06:18:31,470 --> 06:18:32,996
置信度低则转人工审核。
Confidence to human review.

4397
06:18:33,838 --> 06:18:38,564
审核员能纠正他们看到的内容中约 30% 的错误，所以这个队列显然是必要的。
Reviewers correct roughly 30% of what they see, so the queue is clearly earning its place.

4398
06:18:39,470 --> 06:18:43,920
对从未被审核过的记录进行审计时，发现错误率约为 4%。
An audit of records that were never reviewed finds an error rate of about 4%.

4399
06:18:44,640 --> 06:18:46,960
这些错误集中在同一个文档中。
The errors concentrate in one document.

4400
06:18:47,342 --> 06:18:50,244
模型处理这类内容时表现为「自信但错误」。
Format the model handles confidently and incorrectly.

4401
06:18:50,734 --> 06:18:53,200
团队正在考虑降低阈值。
The team is considering lowering the threshold.

4402
06:18:53,360 --> 06:18:55,204
哪种改变最有效？
What is the most effective change?

4403
06:18:55,982 --> 06:19:00,676
a. 将阈值降低到 0.85，以便审核更多的记录。
a lower the threshold to 0.85 so more records are reviewed.

4404
06:19:01,134 --> 06:19:06,404
b. 对高于阈值的记录进行抽样审核，并按文档格式进行分层。
b. Add a sampled review of records scoring above the threshold stratified by document format.

4405
06:19:07,022 --> 06:19:10,820
c. 重新培训审核员，让他们对已看到的记录审查得更彻底。
C. Retrain reviewers to be more thorough on the records they already see.

4406
06:19:11,758 --> 06:19:12,000
d。
D.

4407
06:19:12,526 --> 06:19:16,260
要求模型在分配置信度时更加保守。
Ask the model to be more conservative when assigning confidence.

4408
06:19:16,590 --> 06:19:17,700
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4409
06:19:23,406 --> 06:19:30,916
答案是 B，决定性的词汇是「自信但错误」，它同时排除了 A 和 D。
The answer is B, the phrase that decides it is confidently and incorrectly and it rules out A and D together.

4410
06:19:31,790 --> 06:19:35,456
降低阈值可以审核更多模型不确定的记录。
Lowering the threshold reviews more records the model was unsure about.

4411
06:19:35,790 --> 06:19:40,096
这些错误不在那个组里，所以你增加了审核员负载，却还是漏掉了同样的 4%。
These errors are not in that group, so you add a reviewer load and miss the same 4%.

4412
06:19:41,358 --> 06:19:49,316
选项 B 要求模型对它误解的内容降低信心，而误解在内部看来并不像是不确定。
Option B asks the model to be less confident about something it has misunderstood, and a misunderstanding does not feel uncertain from the inside.

4413
06:19:51,310 --> 06:19:54,820
选项 C 改进的是一组这些记录永远不会进入的工作内容。
Option C improves work on a set these records never enter.

4414
06:19:55,694 --> 06:20:03,536
只有 B 关注了错误真正出现的地方，并且通过文档格式进行分层，旨在让样本对准集群
Only B looks where the errors actually are and stratifying by document format aims the sample at the cluster

4415
06:20:03,726 --> 06:20:05,700
审计已经识别出的部分。
the audit already identified.

4416
06:20:07,406 --> 06:20:08,388
情景 2。
Scenario 2.

4417
06:20:08,718 --> 06:20:12,096
支持人员会将约 12% 的对话上报升级。
A support agent escalates about 12% of conversations.

4418
06:20:12,430 --> 06:20:17,668
上报的案件进入人工队列时，仅包含完整的对话转录内容，没有任何其他信息。
Escalations arrive in the human queue as the full conversation transcript and nothing else.

4419
06:20:18,158 --> 06:20:23,460
代理人报告称，处理一个上报的案例所花的时间几乎与从头开始处理一样长。
Agents report that handling an escalated case takes almost as long as handling it from scratch.

4420
06:20:24,398 --> 06:20:29,700
在好几个案例中，人类人员反驳了代理人已经告诉客户的内容。
In several cases, a human has contradicted something. The agent already told a customer.

4421
06:20:30,190 --> 06:20:33,124
目前的上报率本身被认为是合理的。
The escalation rate itself is considered appropriate.

4422
06:20:33,838 --> 06:20:34,948
应该改变什么？
What should change?

4423
06:20:35,726 --> 06:20:39,716
a. 降低上报率，让代理人处理更少的案例。
a reduce the escalation rate so agents handle fewer cases.

4424
06:20:40,496 --> 06:20:40,736
b。
b.

4425
06:20:41,390 --> 06:20:48,292
用结构化的交接代替转录内容，提供原因、既定事实、说过的话以及剩余待办事项。
Replace the transcript with a structured handover, giving reason, established facts, what was said and what remains.

4426
06:20:48,656 --> 06:20:48,896
C。
C.

4427
06:20:49,294 --> 06:20:52,996
让代理人在转录内容顶部写一段话的摘要。
Have the agent write a one-paragraph summary at the top of the transcript.

4428
06:20:53,390 --> 06:20:53,696
D。
D.

4429
06:20:54,062 --> 06:20:57,060
培训人工代理人更高效地阅读转录内容。
Train human agents to read transcripts more efficiently.

4430
06:20:57,486 --> 06:20:58,564
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

4431
06:21:04,174 --> 06:21:10,596
答案是 B，而选项 C 是值得思考的干扰项，因为它确实比什么都没有要好。
The answer is B, and option C is the distractor worth thinking about because it is genuinely better than nothing.

4432
06:21:11,342 --> 06:21:13,124
摘要段落确实有帮助。
A summary paragraph does help.

4433
06:21:13,646 --> 06:21:17,380
但它仍然是纯文本，所以作者每次都要决定包含哪些内容。
It is still prose, so the writer decides what to include each time.

4434
06:21:17,838 --> 06:21:20,868
这里遗漏的特定信息可能还会再次丢失。
The specific thing being missed here can go missing again.

4435
06:21:21,262 --> 06:21:22,976
看第二个症状。
Look at the second symptom.

4436
06:21:23,470 --> 06:21:31,524
人类在反驳代理人已经告诉客户的内容，这是因为之前说的话并不是任何地方定义的字段。
Humans are contradicting what the agent already told the customer, which happens because what was already said is not a named field anywhere.

4437
06:21:31,856 --> 06:21:36,708
结构化可以解决这个问题，因为它让必须填写的字段被正确填写。
Structure fixes that because a field that must be filled gets filled.

4438
06:21:37,166 --> 06:21:42,596
选项 A 被题干排除，而选项 D 则会一直消耗人力成本。
Option A is ruled out by the STEM, and option D pays the cost forever in human time.

4439
06:21:44,270 --> 06:21:45,376
情景 3。
Scenario 3.

4440
06:21:45,870 --> 06:21:49,216
退货代理人在其系统提示词中有明确的政策。
A returns agent has clear policy in its system prompt.

4441
06:21:49,870 --> 06:21:57,700
在客户解释了家属去世的情况后，智能体在退货窗口期外授予了一项违反政策的退款。
After a customer explained a family bereavement, the agent granted an out-of-policy refund outside the returns window.

4442
06:21:58,510 --> 06:22:00,804
团队编写了一条新的升级规则。
The team writes a new escalation rule.

4443
06:22:01,454 --> 06:22:04,036
任何提到“丧事”的请求都要进行升级。
Escalate any request mentioning bereavement.

4444
06:22:04,910 --> 06:22:11,204
两个月后，智能体为一名住院客户授予了一项违反政策的特例处理。
Two months later, the agent grants an out-of-policy exception for a customer who was in hospital.

4445
06:22:11,536 --> 06:22:14,116
他们这种做法的核心问题是什么？
What is the underlying problem with their approach?

4446
06:22:14,656 --> 06:22:19,268
A. 该规则应该列出更多情况，包括住院。
A. The rule should have listed more circumstances including hospitalization.

4447
06:22:20,078 --> 06:22:26,660
B. 判断标准是基于个案编写的，而它应该是针对任何要求突破既定政策的请求。
B. The criterion was written from an instance and should be any request for an exception to stated policy.

4448
06:22:27,136 --> 06:22:31,780
C. 系统提示词需要关于退货窗口更强硬的措辞。
C. The system prompt needs stronger wording about the returns window.

4449
06:22:32,336 --> 06:22:32,656
D。
D.

4450
06:22:33,102 --> 06:22:37,216
智能体根本不应该处理情感敏感的对话。
The agent should not handle emotionally sensitive conversations at all.

4451
06:22:37,536 --> 06:22:38,724
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4452
06:22:44,430 --> 06:22:46,016
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

4453
06:22:46,862 --> 06:22:48,708
看看这两个事件的共同点。
Look at what the two incidents share.

4454
06:22:49,038 --> 06:22:57,540
不是丧事也不是住院，而是客户要求破例而智能体准予了请求这一事实。
Not bereavement and not hospitalization, but the fact that a customer asked for an exception to stated policy and the agent granted it.

4455
06:22:58,318 --> 06:23:02,020
这就是核心属性，也是该规则所属的层级。
That is the property and it is the level the rule belongs at.

4456
06:23:02,830 --> 06:23:08,896
选项 A 用更长的列表重复了同样的错误，而且总会有一些人没想到的情况。
Option A repeats the mistake with a longer list and there will always be a circumstance nobody thought of.

4457
06:23:09,136 --> 06:23:13,092
选项 C 虽然值得一提，但因为政策本身已经很明确了。
Option C is worth naming because the policy was already clear.

4458
06:23:13,614 --> 06:23:20,356
清晰的政策在同情心案例面前败下阵来，这是问题的本质，而不是靠增加一个句子就能解决的。
A clear policy losing to a sympathetic case is the situation rather than something a former sentence fixes.

4459
06:23:20,878 --> 06:23:23,524
这也是关于执行力的再次教学。
This is also the enforcement lesson again.

4460
06:23:23,776 --> 06:23:27,108
特例处理应该是一个由人来做出的决定。
An exception should be a decision a person makes.

4461
06:23:28,814 --> 06:23:29,764
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

4462
06:23:30,064 --> 06:23:33,504
一个智能体通过仓库查询订单状态。
An agent looks up order status through a warehouse.

4463
06:23:36,046 --> 06:23:39,940
在长达 2 小时的停机期间，API 的每次调用都返回错误。
During a 2-hour outage, the API returned errors on every call.

4464
06:23:41,006 --> 06:23:49,732
在回顾故障时，团队发现智能体告诉了几位客户他们的订单已经发货。这些表述看似合理，但在四种情况下是错误的。
Reviewing the outage, the team finds the agent told several customers their orders had shipped. Those statements were plausible and, in four cases, wrong.

4465
06:23:50,702 --> 06:23:55,076
系统提示词要求智能体提供帮助并让客户知晓相关信息。
The system prompt tells the agent to be helpful and to keep customers informed.

4466
06:23:55,424 --> 06:23:57,412
最重要的改变是什么？
What is the most important change?

4467
06:23:57,870 --> 06:24:01,028
a 添加一条指令，严禁猜测订单状态。
a add an instruction never to guess order status.

4468
06:24:01,454 --> 06:24:08,804
B. 在工具故障时，说明哪些信息不可用，提供仍可操作的方案，并记录请求以便后续跟进。
B. On tool failure, state what is unavailable, offer what can still be done, and capture the request for follow-up.

4469
06:24:09,678 --> 06:24:09,904
C。
C.

4470
06:24:10,304 --> 06:24:14,084
在停机期间更积极地重试 API。
Retry the API more aggressively during outages.

4471
06:24:14,464 --> 06:24:19,396
D. 缓存最近的订单状态，以便在停机期间提供答案。
D. Cache recent order statuses so answers are available during an outage.

4472
06:24:20,494 --> 06:24:21,668
稍停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

4473
06:24:27,278 --> 06:24:28,544
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

4474
06:24:29,134 --> 06:24:35,140
之所以要明确说明 A 选项较弱，是因为它在其他场景中也同样适用。
The reason A is weaker is worth stating clearly because it applies well beyond this scenario.

4475
06:24:36,238 --> 06:24:42,820
如果只是禁止而不提供替代方案，智能体面对客户时，提示词却要求它提供帮助。
A prohibition with no alternative leaves the agent with a customer in front of it and a prompt telling it to be helpful.

4476
06:24:43,662 --> 06:24:45,316
这样它就无从采取任何合理的行动。
It has nothing acceptable to do.

4477
06:24:46,254 --> 06:24:48,964
在这种压力下，它会胡编乱造一些话。
Under that pressure, it will find something to say.

4478
06:24:49,710 --> 06:24:51,908
B 提供了正确的行为逻辑。
B supplies the correct behavior.

4479
06:24:52,334 --> 06:24:55,524
所以当工具失效时，有一个正确的处理方案。
So there is a right answer available when the tool fails.

4480
06:24:58,574 --> 06:25:01,540
选项 C 误解了 2 小时的停机情况。
Option C misunderstands a 2 hour outage.

4481
06:25:02,702 --> 06:25:06,820
选项 D 有点微妙，因为缓存听起来很稳妥。
Option D is the interesting one because caching sounds prudent.

4482
06:25:07,694 --> 06:25:15,620
但停机期间的缓存状态从定义上讲就是过时的，所以你只是用一个虚构的答案换成了一个过时的答案。
A cache status during an outage is stale by definition, so you have swapped an invented answer for an out-of-date one.

4483
06:25:17,262 --> 06:25:18,532
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

4484
06:25:18,926 --> 06:25:22,404
一个团队正在推出一个文档分类系统。
A team is launching a document classification system.

4485
06:25:23,278 --> 06:25:31,140
他们计划将置信度低于 0.8 的内容转给人工审核，并认为 0.8 是一个看起来合理的数值。
They plan to route anything below 0.8 confidence to human review, having picked 0.8 as a sensible looking figure.

4486
06:25:32,078 --> 06:25:38,308
他们从试点中获得了 400 份带有已知正确分类标签的文档，但他们还没去用这些数据。
They have 400 labeled documents from a pilot with known correct classifications, which they have not used.

4487
06:25:38,926 --> 06:25:43,812
审核人员的人手有限，他们不确定 0.8 这个标准是否会让他们不堪重负。
Reviewer capacity is limited and they are unsure whether 0.8 will overwhelm it.

4488
06:25:44,334 --> 06:25:45,764
他们首先应该做什么？
What should they do first?

4489
06:25:46,704 --> 06:25:51,108
a 先用 0.8 的标准上线，再根据审核人员的反馈进行调整。
a Launch with 0.8 and adjust based on reviewer feedback.

4490
06:25:51,694 --> 06:25:57,252
b 将试点数据运行一遍，并将错误与置信度进行绘图对比，从而确定阈值。
b run the pilot sec through the system and plot errors against confidence to choose the threshold.

4491
06:25:57,934 --> 06:25:58,224
C。
C.

4492
06:25:58,702 --> 06:26:03,492
将阈值设定为任何能让审核量符合人员能力的数值。
Set the threshold to whatever produces a review volume matching reviewer capacity.

4493
06:26:04,334 --> 06:26:07,104
D. 在第一个月里，将所有内容都转给人工审核。
D. Route everything to review for the first month.

4494
06:26:07,374 --> 06:26:08,452
稍停一下，做个决定。
Pause and decide.

4495
06:26:13,902 --> 06:26:20,004
答案是 B，而题目中埋下的关键信息是他们已经有 400 份标注好的文档但还没去用。
The answer is B, and the planted detail is that they already have 400 labeled documents which they have not used.

4496
06:26:20,398 --> 06:26:24,304
能把猜测变成决策所需的信息就在他们的硬盘里。
The information needed to turn a guess into a decision is sitting on their disk.

4497
06:26:24,942 --> 06:26:32,772
运行试点数据并绘制错误与置信度的对比图，可以让他们知道任何阈值在漏报和审核压力上分别意味着什么。
Running the pilot set through and plotting errors against confidence tells them what any threshold costs in misses and in reviewer load.

4498
06:26:34,030 --> 06:26:37,316
选项 C 是那种值得警惕、应当避免的习惯。
Option C is the one worth flagging as a habit to avoid.

4499
06:26:37,870 --> 06:26:42,596
为了匹配人员配置而设定质量阈值，意味着你的质量控制是由你的 roster 决定的。
Setting a quality threshold to match staffing means your quality control is determined by your rotor.

4500
06:26:43,502 --> 06:26:50,244
选项 A 只让系统了解了数量，却从未让它了解漏报情况，因为从定义上讲，这些漏报是不可见的。
Option A learns about volume without ever learning about the misses, which stay invisible by definition.

4501
06:26:51,982 --> 06:26:58,660
情景 6，它特意回顾了模块 4 的内容，以检查你是否掌握了那个概念。
Scenario 6 and it deliberately revisits ground from module 4 to check the idea has stuck.

4502
06:26:59,438 --> 06:27:04,772
一个计费智能体有明确的升级标准和结构化交接格式。
A billing agent has clear escalation criteria and a structured handover format.

4503
06:27:05,262 --> 06:27:13,824
在生产环境中，3% 的对话以最后一条消息结束且没有进行升级，导致客户问题未解决。
In production, 3% of conversations end with a final message and no escalation, leaving the customer unresolved.

4504
06:27:14,414 --> 06:27:19,332
调查显示，这些情况是智能体认为自己已经解决了问题。
Investigation shows these are cases where the agent believed it had resolved the issue.

4505
06:27:19,584 --> 06:27:22,692
团队已经改进了两次升级标准。
The team has already improved the escalation criteria twice.

4506
06:27:23,118 --> 06:27:24,580
什么能填补这个缺口？
What closes the gap?

4507
06:27:25,006 --> 06:27:28,356
a. 第三次改进升级标准。
a improve the escalation criteria a third time.

4508
06:27:29,230 --> 06:27:35,076
b. 在每场对话后进行编排检查，对任何未标记为已解决的内容进行升级。
b. An orchestration check after each conversation that escalates anything not marked resolved.

4509
06:27:35,664 --> 06:27:35,984
C。
C.

4510
06:27:36,334 --> 06:27:39,716
降低智能体触发升级的置信度阈值。
Lower the confidence threshold at which the agent escalates.

4511
06:27:40,304 --> 06:27:40,624
D。
D.

4512
06:27:41,134 --> 06:27:44,704
在系统提示词中加入未解决对话的示例。
Add examples of unresolved conversations to the system prompt.

4513
06:27:45,390 --> 06:27:46,468
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

4514
06:27:52,142 --> 06:27:55,332
答案是 B，而且这个选项应该让你感到很熟悉。
The answer is B and it should have felt familiar.

4515
06:27:56,526 --> 06:28:02,020
除了 B 之外的每个选项都在要求智能体去检测一个它根本不知道自己出问题的故障。
Every option except B asks the agent to detect a failure it does not know it is having.

4516
06:28:02,606 --> 06:28:06,276
题干清楚地告诉你，它认为这些案例已经解决了。
The stem tells you plainly that it believed it had resolved these cases.

4517
06:28:07,022 --> 06:28:11,312
标准是由智能体评估的，所以更好的标准并不会触发。
Criteria are evaluated by the agent, so better criteria do not fire.

4518
06:28:11,886 --> 06:28:16,752
基于置信度的升级需要智能体处于不确定状态，但它当时是很有把握的。
Confidence-based escalation needs the agent to be uncertain and it was confident.

4519
06:28:17,072 --> 06:28:21,604
示例只能提高一个由“智能体没注意到”这一问题定义的故障率。
Examples improve a rate on a problem defined by the agent not noticing.

4520
06:28:22,318 --> 06:28:28,228
只有编排检查是不管智能体的结论如何都会运行的，这就是它成为正确答案的原因。
Only the orchestration check runs regardless of what the agent concluded, which is why it is the answer here.

4521
06:28:28,782 --> 06:28:30,500
还有在模块 4 中。
And in module 4.

4522
06:28:31,310 --> 06:28:33,028
这完成了领域模块的内容。
That closes the domain modules.

4523
06:28:33,454 --> 06:28:37,316
接下来是模块 18，教你如何区分极其相似的答案。
Module 18 next on telling near identical answers apart.

4524
06:28:38,958 --> 06:28:39,940
模块 18。
Module 18.

4525
06:28:41,966 --> 06:28:46,912
这个模块几乎没教你什么新东西，这是故意设计的。
This module teaches you almost nothing new, and that is deliberate.

4526
06:28:47,118 --> 06:28:49,860
到现在为止，你已经理解了其中的每一个区别。
By now you understand every distinction in it.

4527
06:28:50,254 --> 06:28:58,308
你还没做的是在计时的情况下，从一个从未见过的题干中，用 4 秒钟识别出这些区别。
What you have not yet done is practice recognizing them in 4 seconds from a stem you have never seen while a clock runs.

4528
06:28:59,246 --> 06:29:03,620
这是两种不同的技能，而第二种是考试当天容易出错的那种。
Those are different skills, and the second one is the one that fails on exam day.

4529
06:29:04,206 --> 06:29:06,052
所以这个模块是一个演练。
So this module is a drill.

4530
06:29:06,592 --> 06:29:13,764
精简的判定表，然后是 10 个快速情景，唯一的目的就是测试你是否能立刻想到那对关键点。
Compact tiebreaker tables, then 10 rapid scenarios that do nothing except test whether the light pair comes to mind.

4531
06:29:15,438 --> 06:29:17,732
这个模块要解决的问题就在这里。
Here is the problem this module solves.

4532
06:29:17,952 --> 06:29:21,412
你已经看了 17 个模块，内容你也理解了。
You have watched 17 modules and the material makes sense.

4533
06:29:21,712 --> 06:29:25,508
然后你坐在考场上，面对 60 道题和 120 分钟的时间。
Then you sit down with 60 questions and 120 minutes.

4534
06:29:32,654 --> 06:29:35,620
那一刻你需要的不是更多的理解。
What you need at that moment is not more understanding.

4535
06:29:36,032 --> 06:29:41,712
你需要正确的配对能立刻跳出来，以及区分这两个选项的关键那句话。
You need the correct pair to surface immediately, along with the one sentence that separates its halves.

4536
06:29:42,286 --> 06:29:48,676
这就是检索。而检索是通过练习来训练的，这正是接下来 20 分钟要做的。
That is retrieval. And retrieval is trained by retrieving, which is what the next 20 minutes are for.

4537
06:29:50,222 --> 06:29:54,468
识别失败有四种情况，最后两种代价最高。
Four ways recognition fails, and the last two are the expensive ones.

4538
06:29:54,752 --> 06:30:01,552
你认出了主题但没认出配对，所以你知道这是关于会话的，却不知道是哪一个会话问题。
You recognize the topic without recognizing the pair, so you know it is about sessions and not which session question it is.

4539
06:30:01,792 --> 06:30:07,364
你记住了两个选项，但没有区分点，而那个区分点正是决定答案的那句话。
You recall both halves without the discriminator, which is the one sentence that actually decides it.

4540
06:30:08,206 --> 06:30:16,548
你选择了功能更强大的机制，比如因为听起来更强大而选了钩子而不是权限，或者选了智能体而不是工作流。
You pick the more powerful mechanism, choosing a hook over a permission or an agent over a workflow because it sounds more capable.

4541
06:30:17,038 --> 06:30:22,980
或者你接受了一个错误的答案，因为在快速做题时，通过文件名搜索看起来非常合理。
And you accept a reversed answer because grep for file names reads perfectly plausibly at speed.

4542
06:30:23,630 --> 06:30:28,292
最后这两种情况感觉像是能力问题而非失误，这就是它们代价如此之高的原因。
Those last two feel like competence rather than error, which is why they cost so much.

4543
06:30:29,902 --> 06:30:32,292
下面是这些表格的用法。
Here is how to use the tables that follow.

4544
06:30:32,592 --> 06:30:38,020
读出配对，遮住右侧列，在看之前大声说出判别词。
Read the pair, cover the right-hand column, and say the discriminator out loud before you look.

4545
06:30:38,432 --> 06:30:44,452
如果你没能说出来，记录下它属于哪个模块，并在进入模拟考试前回去复习。
If you cannot produce it, note which module it came from and go back before the practice exams.

4546
06:30:45,326 --> 06:30:52,004
判别词是需要记忆的单位，而不是定义，因为你已经掌握了定义。
The discriminator is the memorizable unit, not the definitions, because you already have the definitions.

4547
06:30:52,430 --> 06:30:58,628
六个幻灯片里共有 28 对配对，你应该会发现其中有三到四个你还不太稳。
There are 28 pairs across six slides, and you should expect to be shaky on three or four of them.

4548
06:30:59,246 --> 06:31:01,636
这正是这个模块存在的目的。
That is exactly what this module is for.

4549
06:31:02,126 --> 06:31:04,004
在这里感到不稳是信息。
Being shaky here is information.

4550
06:31:04,846 --> 06:31:07,300
在考试中感到不稳就是扣分。
Being shaky in the exam is a mark.

4551
06:31:08,846 --> 06:31:10,948
领域 1，6 对配对。
Domain 1, 6 pairs.

4552
06:31:11,854 --> 06:31:16,612
工作流或智能体取决于你是否能提前画出流程图。
Workflow or agent turns on whether you could draw the flowchart in advance.

4553
06:31:17,582 --> 06:31:24,708
链式调用或动态分解取决于步骤是每次都一样，还是取决于第二步返回的内容。
Chaining or dynamic decomposition turns on whether the steps are the same every time or depend on what step 2 returns.

4554
06:31:25,614 --> 06:31:31,748
并行化或编排工作者取决于你是否能在看到输入之前写出子任务列表。
Parallelization or orchestrator workers turns on whether you could write the subtask list before seeing the input.

4555
06:31:32,832 --> 06:31:39,748
子代理或更多上下文取决于工作是需要独立窗口，还是父级已经包含了所需内容。
Subagent or more context turns on whether the work needs its own window or the parent already holds what is needed.

4556
06:31:40,512 --> 06:31:44,836
分叉分支决定决策，而子代理隔离上下文。
Fork branches a decision while a subagent isolates context.

4557
06:31:45,742 --> 06:31:52,772
结束轮次代表完成，而达到上限意味着失败，这在大多数试卷中是判定问题的关键。
An end turn is completion while hitting a cap is failure, which decides a question on most papers.

4558
06:31:54,512 --> 06:31:56,964
会话和上下文，6 对配对。
Sessions and Context 6 pairs.

4559
06:31:57,358 --> 06:32:04,996
会话让对话持久化，而检查点机制让文件持久化，而且第一行是大家最自信地做错的那一项。
Sessions persist the conversation while checkpointing persists the files, and that first row is the one people get wrong most confidently.

4560
06:32:05,792 --> 06:32:12,612
继续（Continue）获取最近的，恢复（Resume）获取命名的，分叉（Fork）分支，而恢复永远不会创建新会话。
Continue takes the most recent, resume takes a named one, fork branches, and resume never creates a session.

4561
06:32:13,102 --> 06:32:15,312
是继续之前的，还是带摘要重新开始。
Resume or fresh with a summary.

4562
06:32:15,502 --> 06:32:17,540
显示在你不在场时发生了哪些变化。
Turns on what changed while you are gone.

4563
06:32:18,574 --> 06:32:21,312
原地刷新或重新开始决定了操作方式。
Refresh in place or start again turns on.

4564
06:32:21,552 --> 06:32:28,164
你是否能列出变化的内容，如果你不能，这种不确定性本身就是答案。
Whether you can list what changed, and if you cannot, that uncertainty is itself the answer.

4565
06:32:29,102 --> 06:32:35,300
清除会丢失内容但保留可重新获取性，而压缩保留核心内容但会丢失措辞。
Clearing loses content while keeping it refetchable and compaction keeps substance while losing wording.

4566
06:32:35,950 --> 06:32:40,228
并保留下一次决策所需的要素，记录下后续可能需要的点。
And keep what the next decision needs, writing down what a later one might.

4567
06:32:41,838 --> 06:32:44,432
工具和 MCP，六对。
Tools and MCP, six pairs.

4568
06:32:44,846 --> 06:32:46,672
当一个工具具有三种行为时进行拆分。
Split when one tool has three behaviors.

4569
06:32:46,912 --> 06:32:49,232
当成功总是涉及三次调用时进行合并。
Merge when success is always three calls.

4570
06:32:49,552 --> 06:32:52,964
如果智能体在决策前需要了解某些信息，则视为资源。
Resource if the agent needs to know something before deciding.

4571
06:32:53,454 --> 06:32:55,072
工具效果意味着必须执行某项操作。
Tool effect needs to do something.

4572
06:32:55,598 --> 06:33:00,420
错误意味着工具运行了但失败了，而协议错误意味着请求根本没到达工具。
Is error means the tool ran and failed, while a protocol error means the request never reached it.

4573
06:33:00,752 --> 06:33:05,244
空结果也是一种成功，因为匹配不到任何内容的搜索也回答了问题。
An empty result is a success because a search matching nothing answered the question.

4574
06:33:05,294 --> 06:33:11,364
GloB 用于名称，grep 用于内容，而这个规则最常被考成相反项。
GloB is for names and grep is for contents, and that rule is the one most often tested reversed.

4575
06:33:12,046 --> 06:33:14,596
为通用系统采用一个服务端。
And adopt a server for a common system.

4576
06:33:15,022 --> 06:33:16,516
仅为你个人构建。
Building only for your own.

4577
06:33:18,222 --> 06:33:21,156
配置和强制执行，6 对。
Configuration and enforcement. 6 pairs.

4578
06:33:21,902 --> 06:33:27,780
Cloud.mb 是上下文，settings 是强制执行，且只有 settings 在冲突时有明确的胜者。
Cloud.mb is context and settings is enforcement and only settings has a defined winner on a conflict.

4579
06:33:28,462 --> 06:33:33,604
导入始终加载，而路径范围规则才是真正减少上下文的部分。
Imports always load while path scope rules are what actually reduce context.

4580
06:33:34,190 --> 06:33:37,444
权限是扁平的，而钩子可以评估条件。
Permissions are flat while hooks can evaluate a condition.

4581
06:33:38,414 --> 06:33:42,468
工具使用前防止操作，工具使用后做出反应且不可撤销。
Pre-tool use prevents and post tool use reacts and cannot undo.

4582
06:33:42,912 --> 06:33:51,652
禁用模型调用会移除 Claude 作为调用者，而用户可调用设为 false 会移除你，这是两个名称相似但效果相反的字段。
Disable model invocation removes Claude as the invoker while user invocable false removes you, which is two similarly named fields with opposite effects.

4583
06:33:52,494 --> 06:33:53,472
并且追加。
And append.

4584
06:33:53,872 --> 06:33:59,972
系统提示词添加到默认值中，而替换会将其移除，包括你所依赖的部分。
System prompt adds to the default while replace removes it, including the parts you are relying on.

4585
06:34:01,678 --> 06:34:04,032
提示词工程和输出，六对。
Prompting and output six pairs.

4586
06:34:04,398 --> 06:34:09,632
标准或示例决定了该事物是更容易定义还是更容易演示。
Criteria or examples turns on whether the thing is easier to define or easier to demonstrate.

4587
06:34:09,934 --> 06:34:17,764
一个提示词还是两个提示词决定了我们改进的阶段。一件事变好了，另一件变差了，这是领域 4 中最明确的单一信号。
One prompt or two turns on the phase we improved. One thing and another got worse, which is the clearest single signal in domain 4.

4588
06:34:18,318 --> 06:34:22,852
在提示词中过滤会隐藏模型丢弃的内容，所以采用下游过滤。
Filtering in the prompt hides what the model discarded, so filter downstream.

4589
06:34:23,310 --> 06:34:27,460
模型无法获知的必填字段会导致生成虚假内容。
A required field the model cannot know produces a fabricated one.

4590
06:34:28,494 --> 06:34:33,636
相同的重试失败意味着将错误返回，而不是重新发送请求。
Identical retry failures mean send the error back rather than the request.

4591
06:34:34,574 --> 06:34:38,372
而批处理或同步则取决于是否有人在等待答案。
And batch or synchronous turns on whether anybody is waiting for the answer.

4592
06:34:40,078 --> 06:34:43,012
可靠性和审查，共 5 对。
Reliability and review 5 pairs.

4593
06:34:43,598 --> 06:34:51,524
遇到瞬时错误时重试，需要判断时升级，因为确定性失败在第三次尝试时也不会解决。
Retry when it is transient and escalate when it needs judgment because deterministic failures do not resolve on the third attempt.

4594
06:34:52,494 --> 06:34:57,508
低置信度审查会完全漏掉高置信度的错误，所以也要采样高于阈值的部分。
Low confidence review misses confident errors entirely, so sample above the threshold as well.

4595
06:34:58,478 --> 06:35:05,412
「保证」这个词会排除所有基于提示词设计的选项，这是整个课程中含金量最高的句子。
The word guarantee eliminates every prompt shaped option, which is the highest value line in the whole course.

4596
06:35:06,062 --> 06:35:12,548
同等会话审查会漏掉作者误解的内容，因为审核者也持有同样的误解。
Same session review misses what the author misunderstood because the reviewer holds the misunderstanding.

4597
06:35:13,102 --> 06:35:17,792
而且计划模式是一个边界，而要求提供计划则是一个请求。
And plan mode is a boundary while asking for a plan is a request.

4598
06:35:19,072 --> 06:35:27,108
如果这些表格里你没记住别的，就记住这三个问题，因为它们能解决大部分的配对。
If you remember nothing else from these tables, remember three questions because between them they resolve most of the pairs.

4599
06:35:27,406 --> 06:35:28,420
谁来决定？
Who decides?

4600
06:35:29,678 --> 06:35:32,512
路径是由你的代码选择的，还是由模型选择的？
Is the path chosen by your code or by the model?

4601
06:35:33,070 --> 06:35:35,588
工具是由模型选的，还是用户选的？
Is the tool chosen by the model or the user?

4602
06:35:36,366 --> 06:35:39,236
阈值是在提示词里设置的，还是在你的流水线里设置的？
Is the threshold set in the prompt or in your pipeline?

4603
06:35:40,238 --> 06:35:41,312
它能拒绝吗？
Can it refuse?

4604
06:35:43,598 --> 06:35:49,380
这个机制是说服还是强制执行？是上下文还是代码？
Is this mechanism persuasion or enforcement? Is it context or code?

4605
06:35:50,158 --> 06:35:51,620
还有，发生了什么变化？
And what changed?

4606
06:35:52,750 --> 06:35:56,452
在文件读取后的间隔期间，两次运行之间发生了什么变化。
Between the two runs during the gap since the file was read.

4607
06:35:57,038 --> 06:36:03,168
这个模块中几乎每一对题目，都是这三个问题在用不同的词汇表达。
Almost every pair in this module is one of those three questions wearing different vocabulary.

4608
06:36:04,526 --> 06:36:06,372
这里是作为查询表提供的相同概念。
Here is the same idea as a lookup.

4609
06:36:06,848 --> 06:36:07,812
谁来决定？
Who decides?

4610
06:36:08,238 --> 06:36:15,332
解决工作流或智能体、资源或工具、在提示词中过滤还是下游过滤，以及两个调用字段。
Resolves workflow or agent, resource or tool, filtering in the prompt or downstream, and the two invocation fields.

4611
06:36:16,110 --> 06:36:16,928
它能拒绝吗？
Can it refuse?

4612
06:36:17,102 --> 06:36:25,540
解决 clot.md 对比设置、权限对钩子、计划模式对比要求提供计划，以及任何关于保证的问题。
Resolves plot.md against settings, permissions against hooks, plan mode against asking for a plan and any guarantee question.

4613
06:36:26,062 --> 06:36:33,956
「发生了什么变化」解决了继续或全新、刷新或重启、重试或升级，以及盲目重试与知情重试。
And what changed resolves resume or fresh, refresh or restart, retry or escalate, and blind against informed retry.

4614
06:36:34,768 --> 06:36:41,572
所以当两个选项看起来都对时，搞清楚题干实际上在询问这三个问题中的哪一个。
So when two options both look right, work out which of those three the stem is actually asking about.

4615
06:36:41,998 --> 06:36:44,260
然后应用对应的配对答案。
Then apply the pair that answers it.

4616
06:36:45,518 --> 06:36:51,684
一种特定的防守手段，因为考试中会出现反向答案，而这些低级错误会导致丢分。
One specific defense because reversed answers appear on this exam and their cheap marks lost.

4617
06:36:52,238 --> 06:36:57,476
当你在快速做题时，两个部分对调的选项看起来非常像正确答案。
An option with the two halves swapped leads perfectly plausibly when you are moving fast.

4618
06:36:58,286 --> 06:37:01,124
用 GloB 查内容，用 grep 查文件名。
Glob for contents and grep for file names.

4619
06:37:02,126 --> 06:37:03,556
把紧急的项进行批处理。
Batch the urgent ones.

4620
06:37:04,334 --> 06:37:06,340
使用本地范围，这样整个团队都能看到。
Local scope so the whole team gets it.

4621
06:37:07,248 --> 06:37:16,004
防御策略是：在阅读选项之前先对自己说出区分点，这样你是在进行匹配，而不是从零开始评估。
The defense is to say the discriminator to yourself before you read the options so that you are matching against something rather than evaluating from scratch.

4622
06:37:16,368 --> 06:37:20,708
如果某个选项看起来明显正确，也要花一秒钟检查一下方向。
And if an option feels obviously right, spend one second checking the direction.

4623
06:37:21,008 --> 06:37:23,556
你不能通过更努力地阅读来发现反转项。
You cannot spot a reversal by reading harder.

4624
06:37:24,334 --> 06:37:27,428
只有在你还没看选项前就预知答案时，才能识别出它。
You spot it by knowing the answer before you look.

4625
06:37:28,846 --> 06:37:34,688
5 条。既然你已经掌握了定义，那么区分点就是可以记忆的单元。
5 lines. The discriminator is the memorizable unit since you already have the definitions.

4626
06:37:34,848 --> 06:37:39,524
“谁决定”、“它可以拒绝”以及“发生了什么变化”这些问题能解决大部分的配对。
Who decides can it refuse and what changed will resolve most of the pairs?

4627
06:37:39,888 --> 06:37:43,168
更强有力的机制不是默认答案。
The more powerful mechanism is not the default answer.

4628
06:37:43,408 --> 06:37:47,332
在读选项前先知道答案，这样就不会被反转项误导。
Know the answer before you read the options so a reversal cannot land.

4629
06:37:48,110 --> 06:37:52,740
任何你现在无法回忆的配对，都是在进入模拟考试前需要重温的模块。
And a pair you cannot recall now is a module to rewatch before the practice exams.

4630
06:37:53,088 --> 06:37:59,008
10 个快速场景。接下来这些内容刻意缩短了，所以每个目标是大约 4 秒。
10 rapid scenarios. Next, these are deliberately short. So aim for about 4 seconds each.

4631
06:37:59,278 --> 06:38:02,340
先说配对，再说区分点，最后说字母。
Say the pair, then the discriminator, then the letter.

4632
06:38:03,726 --> 06:38:04,484
快速练习 1。
Rapid 1.

4633
06:38:04,688 --> 06:38:07,140
一个智能体在一次会话中编辑了 3 个文件。
An agent edited 3 files during a session.

4634
06:38:07,568 --> 06:38:11,908
在工程师将这些文件在磁盘上还原后，会话被重新启动。
The session was then resumed after the engineer reverted those files on disk.

4635
06:38:13,006 --> 06:38:16,964
工程师期望智能体知道这些文件已经恢复到原始状态。
The engineer expects the agent to know the files are back to their original state.

4636
06:38:17,742 --> 06:38:19,728
这个预期正确吗？
Is that expectation correct?

4637
06:38:20,128 --> 06:38:20,448
A。
A.

4638
06:38:20,928 --> 06:38:24,196
是的，重新启动会话会恢复对文件系统的视图。
Yes, resuming restores the session's view of the file system.

4639
06:38:24,622 --> 06:38:24,928
B。
B.

4640
06:38:25,198 --> 06:38:30,852
不是。会话保留的是对话内容而非文件。所以它仍认为自己编辑了它们。
No. Sessions persist the conversation rather than the files. So it still believes it edited them.

4641
06:38:31,328 --> 06:38:34,180
C。是的，如果启用了检查点机制。
C. Yes, if checkpointing is enabled.

4642
06:38:34,528 --> 06:38:34,848
D。
D.

4643
06:38:35,088 --> 06:38:38,448
不是。除非工程师先运行 /上下文 命令。
No. Unless the engineer runs slash context first.

4644
06:38:40,142 --> 06:38:40,644
暂停。
Pause.

4645
06:38:45,248 --> 06:38:45,568
B。
B.

4646
06:38:46,222 --> 06:38:53,924
配对是“会话对比检查点”，区分点是“会话保留对话，而检查点保留文件”。
The pair is session against checkpointing and the discriminator is that sessions persist the conversation while checkpoints persist the files.

4647
06:38:56,046 --> 06:39:03,204
智能体的历史记录显示它做了那些修改，而在磁盘上还原文件并不会改变对话内容。
The agent's history says it made those edits and reverting the files on disk does not reach into the conversation to say otherwise.

4648
06:39:05,067 --> 06:39:05,764
快速练习 2。
Lapid 2.

4649
06:39:06,158 --> 06:39:15,332
一个团队需要找到所有文件名匹配 report_*.py 的文件，以及包含字符串 legacy_auth 的所有文件。
A team needs to find every file whose name matches report underscore star.py and separately every file containing the string legacy underscore auth.

4650
06:39:15,662 --> 06:39:16,484
该用哪些工具？
Which tools?

4651
06:39:16,848 --> 06:39:19,908
对文件名用 grep，对字符串用 glob。
a grep for the file names and glob for the string.

4652
06:39:20,526 --> 06:39:23,588
B. 对文件名用 glob，对字符串用 grep。
B Glob for the file names and grep for the string.

4653
06:39:24,238 --> 06:39:24,528
C。
C.

4654
06:39:24,750 --> 06:39:25,860
两者都用 glob。
Glob for both.

4655
06:39:26,542 --> 06:39:29,924
D. 读取目录，然后扫描每个文件。
D. Read the directory, then scan each file.

4656
06:39:30,606 --> 06:39:31,168
稍停。
Pause.

4657
06:39:35,886 --> 06:39:38,448
B 是正确答案，而选项 A 是它的反转。
B and option A is the reversal.

4658
06:39:38,688 --> 06:39:41,572
Glob 用于名称，grep 用于内容。
Glob is for names and grep is for contents.

4659
06:39:42,542 --> 06:39:46,180
如果你犹豫了，这种犹豫比得分更重要。
If you hesitated, that hesitation is worth more than the mark.

4660
06:39:46,670 --> 06:39:50,660
因为它告诉你这对题目在考试前还需要再过一遍。
Because it tells you this pair needs one more pass before exam day.

4661
06:39:52,366 --> 06:39:53,220
Rapid 3。
Rapid 3.

4662
06:39:53,774 --> 06:40:01,124
每当任何工具写入生产环境路径时，规则必须生效，无论智能体是否被告知该规则。
A rule must hold whenever any tool writes to a path under production and it must hold whether or not the agent was told about it.

4663
06:40:01,710 --> 06:40:02,756
这个规则应该放在哪里？
Where does the rule go?

4664
06:40:03,534 --> 06:40:04,928
a 系统提示词。
a the system prompt.

4665
06:40:05,168 --> 06:40:06,048
正式表述。
Stated formally.

4666
06:40:06,606 --> 06:40:10,052
b clot.md，这样每个会话都会加载它。
b clot.md so every session loads it.

4667
06:40:10,848 --> 06:40:11,088
C。
C.

4668
06:40:11,648 --> 06:40:15,236
一个在工具使用前检查路径并拦截的钩子。
A pre tool use hook that inspects the path and blocks.

4669
06:40:15,568 --> 06:40:19,717
D. 一个在工具使用后对生产环境写入发出警报的钩子。
D. A post tool use hook that alerts on production writes,

4670
06:40:23,248 --> 06:40:23,648
稍停。
Pause.

4671
06:40:28,494 --> 06:40:28,752
C。
C.

4672
06:40:29,152 --> 06:40:37,072
这里有两个对立项。上下文与强制执行的对比排除了 A 和 B，预防与反应的对比排除了 D。
Two pairs fire here. Context against enforcement eliminates A and B, and prevention against reaction eliminates D.

4673
06:40:37,312 --> 06:40:44,324
路径条件是它作为钩子而非权限的原因，因为权限是标记式的，无法检查参数。
The path condition is why this is a hook rather than a permission, since permissions are flagged and cannot inspect an argument.

4674
06:40:45,838 --> 06:40:46,820
Rapid 4。
Rapid 4.

4675
06:40:47,310 --> 06:40:50,820
一个审查提示词涵盖了可访问性和性能。
A review prompt covers accessibility and performance.

4676
06:40:51,182 --> 06:40:57,796
强调可访问性减少了性能问题的发现，而强调性能则减少了可访问性问题的发现。
Emphasizing accessibility reduced performance findings and emphasizing performance reduced accessibility findings.

4677
06:40:58,478 --> 06:41:00,228
总的发现数量保持不变。
Total findings stayed flat.

4678
06:41:00,654 --> 06:41:01,872
这预示着什么？
What does this indicate?

4679
06:41:02,318 --> 06:41:05,540
a 最大标记数截断了响应。
a Max tokens is truncating the response.

4680
06:41:06,030 --> 06:41:09,284
b. 一个提示词承担了两项任务，所以把它拆分开。
b. One prompt is doing two jobs, so split it.

4681
06:41:09,712 --> 06:41:12,484
C. 模型需要更大的上下文窗口。
C. The model needs a larger context window.

4682
06:41:13,134 --> 06:41:16,004
D. 标准需要更明确一些。
D. The criteria need to be more explicit.

4683
06:41:16,814 --> 06:41:17,312
稍等。
Pause.

4684
06:41:22,030 --> 06:41:29,412
B. 我们改进了一项，但另一项变差了，这是领域 4 中最清晰的信号。而且平整的总数排除了截断的情况。
B. We improved one thing and the other got worse is the clearest signal in domain 4. And the flat total rules out truncation.

4685
06:41:30,032 --> 06:41:34,468
两个任务在竞争一个注意力预算，所以解决方法是分成两次调用。
Two jobs competing for one attention budget, so the fix is two calls.

4686
06:41:36,110 --> 06:41:36,932
快速 5。
Rapid 5.

4687
06:41:37,390 --> 06:41:44,196
智能体在规划任何查询之前，需要知道有效的状态码和数据库架构，且这两者大约每半年变动一次。
An agent needs to know the valid status codes and the database schema before it can plan any query and both change about twice a year.

4688
06:41:44,622 --> 06:41:45,988
这应该如何暴露？
How should this be exposed?

4689
06:41:46,542 --> 06:41:49,572
a 一个智能体调用的工具来获取架构。
a a tool the agent calls to fetch the schema.

4690
06:41:50,062 --> 06:41:54,212
b 一个包含架构和状态码的 MCP 资源。
b an MCP resource holding the schema and status codes.

4691
06:41:54,702 --> 06:41:59,204
C 用户调用的 MCP 提示词。
C An M CP prompt the user invokes.

4692
06:42:00,110 --> 06:42:03,812
D 一个负责查询架构的子代理。
D a subagent that looks the schema up.

4693
06:42:04,398 --> 06:42:04,992
稍等。
Pause.

4694
06:42:09,518 --> 06:42:15,876
B 在决定任何事情之前就需要知道，意味着资源；需要执行某些操作，则意味着工具。
B needs to know it before deciding anything means resource and needs to do something means tool.

4695
06:42:16,272 --> 06:42:22,692
“稳定”加上“需要预先获取”是资源的特征，而“每年两次”几乎是数据能达到的最稳定频率了。
Stable plus required upfront is the resource signature and twice a year is about as stable as data gets.

4696
06:42:24,302 --> 06:42:25,312
快速 6。
Rapid 6.

4697
06:42:25,552 --> 06:42:33,312
验证失败在三次重试中都返回相同的错误，且失败的字段是一个格式错误的日期。该如何修改？
A validation failure returns the same error on all three retrees and the failing field is a date in the wrong format. What should change?

4698
06:42:33,678 --> 06:42:41,348
a 在重试之间加入指数退避。b 增加重试次数。C. 将验证错误随重试一起发回。
a add exponential backoff between retrees. b increase the retree count. C. Send the validation error back with the retree.

4699
06:42:42,190 --> 06:42:45,572
d 放宽架构以接受该格式。
d loosen the schema to accept the format.

4700
06:42:46,382 --> 06:42:46,912
稍等。
Pause.

4701
06:42:51,392 --> 06:42:51,632
C。
C.

4702
06:42:52,558 --> 06:42:59,972
每次尝试都出现相同的失败意味着是确定性的，这能一次性排除所有与重试相关的选项。
Identical failures across every attempt means deterministic, which eliminates every retry-shaped answer at once.

4703
06:43:00,512 --> 06:43:04,164
把错误发回，让模型有新的信息可以处理。
Send the error back so the model has something new to work with.

4704
06:43:04,622 --> 06:43:09,380
选项 D 是危险的，因为它虽然可行，但会接受错误的数据。
Option D is the dangerous one because it works and it accepts bad data.

4705
06:43:10,574 --> 06:43:11,392
快速 7。
Rapid 7.

4706
06:43:11,632 --> 06:43:18,020
一个包含 3 万条记录的耐克对账任务由团队每天早上审核，财务部门希望减少构建量。
A Nike reconciliation job of 30,000 records is reviewed by a team each morning and finance wants the build reduced.

4707
06:43:18,352 --> 06:43:19,632
第一个杠杆是什么？
What is the first lever?

4708
06:43:20,032 --> 06:43:21,952
a 并行运行这些记录。
a run the records in parallel.

4709
06:43:22,192 --> 06:43:22,432
B。
B.

4710
06:43:22,672 --> 06:43:23,872
通过批处理发送它们。
Send them through the batch.

4711
06:43:24,112 --> 06:43:24,912
API。
API.

4712
06:43:25,152 --> 06:43:27,972
C 减少每个响应的最大标记数。
C reduce max tokens on each response.

4713
06:43:28,592 --> 06:43:28,912
D。
D.

4714
06:43:29,312 --> 06:43:31,620
增加更多子智能体来分担工作。
Add more sub agents to share the work.

4715
06:43:32,078 --> 06:43:32,580
稍等。
Pause.

4716
06:43:37,038 --> 06:43:40,004
B。每天检查意味着没有人正在等待。
B. Reviewed each morning tells you nobody is waiting.

4717
06:43:40,512 --> 06:43:43,940
选项 A 和 D 是同样的错误，出现了两次。
Options A and D are the same mistake. Twice.

4718
06:43:44,398 --> 06:43:50,660
并行性可以节省墙钟时间，但永远不能减少成本。而且选项 D 还会增加上下文负载。
Parallelism buys wall clock time and never buys a discount. And option D adds context loads on top.

4719
06:43:51,950 --> 06:43:52,900
快速 8。
Rapid 8.

4720
06:43:53,230 --> 06:43:54,672
一项技能部署到生产环境。
A skill deploys to production.

4721
06:43:54,912 --> 06:44:01,828
当用户询问关于部署的假设性问题时，Claude 开始自动调用它，而团队仍希望手动运行它。
Troud has begun invoking it on its own when users ask hypothetical questions about deployment and the team still wants to run it manually.

4722
06:44:02,222 --> 06:44:02,912
哪个字段？
Which field?

4723
06:44:03,278 --> 06:44:05,312
a 用户可调用为假。
a user invokable false.

4724
06:44:05,632 --> 06:44:08,132
B. 禁用模型调用为真。
B. Disable model invocation true.

4725
06:44:08,558 --> 06:44:11,428
C 允许工具限制为只读工具。
C Allow tools restricted to read tools.

4726
06:44:11,872 --> 06:44:12,192
D。
D.

4727
06:44:12,526 --> 06:44:13,444
ContextCheck。
ContextFuck.

4728
06:44:14,062 --> 06:44:14,592
稍等。
Pause.

4729
06:44:19,246 --> 06:44:21,796
B 和选项 A 又是反转项。
B and option A is the reversal again.

4730
06:44:22,112 --> 06:44:27,684
「禁用模型调用」移除作为调用者的 Claude，而「用户可调用为假」则把你移除掉。
Disable model invocation removes plot as the invoker while user invocable false removes you.

4731
06:44:28,782 --> 06:44:32,324
题干列出了两个要求，所以要读清楚它想去掉哪个调用者。
The stem names both requirements, so read which invoker it wants gone.

4732
06:44:33,966 --> 06:44:34,884
快速 9。
Rapid 9.

4733
06:44:35,312 --> 06:44:39,940
一个提取系统将任何置信度低于 0.7 的内容转到审核。
An extraction system routes anything below 0.7 confidence to review.

4734
06:44:40,192 --> 06:44:44,388
审计发现有一组评分高于 0.9 的记录出现了错误。
An audit finds a cluster of errors in record scoring above 0.9.

4735
06:44:44,912 --> 06:44:46,052
该如何修复？
What is the fix?

4736
06:44:46,414 --> 06:44:48,832
a 将阈值提高到 0.9。
a raise the threshold to 0.9.

4737
06:44:49,262 --> 06:44:52,132
b 对高于阈值的记录进行抽样审核。
b. Sample records above the threshold for review.

4738
06:44:52,782 --> 06:44:56,100
C 要求模型更保守地打分。
C. Ask the model to score more conservatively.

4739
06:44:56,558 --> 06:44:58,980
d 增加审核员的容量。
d. Increase reviewer capacity.

4740
06:45:00,174 --> 06:45:00,672
稍等。
Pause.

4741
06:45:05,376 --> 06:45:05,696
B。
B.

4742
06:45:06,254 --> 06:45:12,836
从结构上讲，置信度阈值无法识别那些高置信度的错误，所以调整阈值也没用。
A confidence threshold is blind to confident errors by construction, so no adjustment to the threshold reaches them.

4743
06:45:13,166 --> 06:45:15,236
题干中的数字起到了关键作用。
The number in the stem is doing the work.

4744
06:45:15,758 --> 06:45:21,732
这些错误都在 0.9 以上，而选项 A 只把门槛提高到 0.9。
The errors sit above 0.9, and option A only raises the bar to 0.9.

4745
06:45:23,536 --> 06:45:24,644
快速 10 分。
Rapid 10.

4746
06:45:24,976 --> 06:45:30,256
每一次拉取请求审查都按相同的顺序运行这三个独立的检查。
Every pull request review runs the same three independent checks in the same order.

4747
06:45:30,496 --> 06:45:34,564
审核人员无法判断缺失的发现是意味着代码干净，还是漏掉了步骤。
Reviewers cannot tell whether a missing finding means clean code or a skip step.

4748
06:45:34,976 --> 06:45:36,388
正确的结构是什么？
What is the right structure?

4749
06:45:37,198 --> 06:45:41,456
A. 一个包含所有三个检查清单并带有更强提示词的智能体。
a one agent with all three checklists and a stronger prompt.

4750
06:45:41,998 --> 06:45:46,180
B. 采用提示词链，通过三个串行调用，每个调用执行一个检查。
B Prompt chaining with three sequential calls each doing one check.

4751
06:45:46,830 --> 06:45:49,892
C. 一个拥有三个工具的智能体，每个工具对应一个检查。
C. One agent with three tools, one per check.

4752
06:45:50,478 --> 06:45:50,736
D
D

4753
06:45:52,718 --> 06:45:54,948
由协调者运行的三个子智能体。
three sub agents run by a coordinator.

4754
06:45:55,696 --> 06:45:56,292
稍等。
Pause.

4755
06:46:01,070 --> 06:46:09,924
B。相同的三个步骤，相同的顺序，彼此独立，这意味着你可以提前画出流程图，智能体就无需做任何决策。
B Same three steps, same order, independent of each other, means you could draw the flowchart in advance so there is nothing for an agent to decide.

4756
06:46:10,416 --> 06:46:18,176
而且审核者的投诉是关键线索，因为只有工作流才能让“缺失的发现”在逻辑上等同于“代码干净”。
And the reviewer's complaint is the tell because only a workflow can make a missing finding provably mean clean code.

4757
06:46:18,496 --> 06:46:20,516
这结束了第 18 模块。
That closes module 18.

4758
06:46:21,454 --> 06:46:23,300
接下来是第 19 模块。
Module 19 next.

4759
06:46:23,616 --> 06:46:26,660
关于这项考试如何编写题目。
On how this exam writes its questions.

4760
06:46:28,398 --> 06:46:29,508
第 19 模块。
Module 19.

4761
06:46:29,936 --> 06:46:32,772
其他所有模块都在教你相关知识点。
Every other module has taught you the material.

4762
06:46:33,550 --> 06:46:35,300
这一部分是关于试卷本身的。
This one is about the paper.

4763
06:46:35,822 --> 06:46:39,588
题目是如何构建的，以及题干中的限定词起到了什么作用。
How an item is built and what the qualifier in the STEM is doing.

4764
06:46:40,430 --> 06:46:42,596
错误答案存在的四种形式。
The four shapes a wrong answer takes.

4765
06:46:44,046 --> 06:46:48,164
以及如何在 120 分钟内分配时间，而不至于在最后 10 道题时仓促赶工。
And how to spend 120 minutes without rushing the last 10 questions.

4766
06:46:49,102 --> 06:46:53,696
本模块的部分内容是基于 134 道练习题的实测数据。
Some of this module is grounded in measurements from 134 practice questions.

4767
06:46:53,936 --> 06:46:59,140
如果某个数字来自这些测试数据而非 Anthropic，我会明确说明。
I will say clearly when a number comes from that rather than from anthropic.

4768
06:47:00,814 --> 06:47:02,116
试卷的结构。
The shape of the paper.

4769
06:47:02,798 --> 06:47:08,196
120 分钟内做 60 道题，意味着每题有 2 分钟，且没有专门的阅读时间。
60 questions in 120 minutes, which is 2 minutes each with no separate reading time.

4770
06:47:08,878 --> 06:47:21,572
四个选项中只有一个正确答案；在包含 134 道题的练习库中，有 133 道符合这一规律，虽然格式允许要求多个答案的题目，但练习库里没出现过这类题。
4 options with one correct answer, and in the practice bank that held for 133 of 134 items, the format does allow items asking for more than one answer, and none appeared in the bank.

4771
06:47:21,870 --> 06:47:24,260
所以要读指令行，而不是去盲目猜测。
So read the instruction line rather than assuming.

4772
06:47:25,582 --> 06:47:28,964
分数按比例缩放到 1000 分，达到 720 分即可通过。
Scoring is scaled to 1000 with a pass at 720.

4773
06:47:29,774 --> 06:47:33,988
这不是原始百分比，所以不要在考试过程中试图计算自己的得分。
That is not a raw percentage, so do not try to compute your score during the exam.

4774
06:47:34,958 --> 06:47:38,692
在 6 个场景中，你会随机抽到 4 个。
And you get 4 of the 6 scenarios chosen at random.

4775
06:47:40,302 --> 06:47:46,436
每个题目都有相同的五个部分，包括建立生产系统及其限制条件的背景设定。
Every item has the same five parts, a setup establishing a production system and its constraints.

4776
06:47:46,990 --> 06:47:49,668
用可观察术语描述的症状。
A symptom described in observable terms.

4777
06:47:49,936 --> 06:47:56,324
一个埋设的细节，这是决定答案的唯一事实，且通常是题干的最后一句。
A planted detail, which is the single fact that decides the answer and is very often the last sentence of the stem.

4778
06:47:56,976 --> 06:47:58,736
问题中的限定词
A qualifier in the question

4779
06:47:58,736 --> 06:48:06,340
行。还有四个选项，通常有两个看似合理的，一个较弱的，以及一个要么是反向干扰项，要么就是虚构的。
line. And four options, typically two plausible ones, one weak one and one that is either reversed or invented.

4780
06:48:07,086 --> 06:48:13,188
在练习题库中，题干的长度从 34 到 150 个单词不等，中位数为 101。
On the practice bank, stems ran from 34 to 150 words, with a median of 101.

4781
06:48:13,902 --> 06:48:16,164
选项平均约为 19 个单词。
Options averaged about 19 words.

4782
06:48:17,006 --> 06:48:20,484
所以你每道题大约要读 180 个单词。
So you are reading roughly 180 words per question.

4783
06:48:21,774 --> 06:48:25,444
把这笔账算清楚，因为它会改变你对待试卷的方式。
Do the arithmetic once because it changes how you approach the paper.

4784
06:48:25,870 --> 06:48:32,228
101 字的题干加上 4 个各 19 字的选项，大约是 177 个单词。
A median stem of 101 words plus 4 options of 19 each is around 177 words.

4785
06:48:32,942 --> 06:48:39,876
以阅读技术性纯文本的舒适速度来看，这大约需要 45 秒，而此时你还没开始思考任何内容。
At a comfortable reading speed for technical prose, that is roughly 45 seconds, and you have not yet thought about anything.

4786
06:48:40,558 --> 06:48:44,976
所以在你 2 分钟的时间里，大约三分之一就花在阅读上了，还没开始推理。
So of your 2 minutes, about a third is gone to reading before any reasoning starts.

4787
06:48:45,518 --> 06:48:51,940
这就是为什么本模块的技巧是关于如何高效阅读，而不是思考得更快。
That is why the techniques in this module are about reading efficiently rather than thinking faster.

4788
06:48:53,966 --> 06:48:55,620
你没法让大脑转得更快。
You cannot think faster.

4789
06:48:55,968 --> 06:48:57,924
但你可以带着目的去阅读。
You can read with a purpose.

4790
06:48:59,534 --> 06:49:00,836
这是一个可行的分配方案。
A workable split.

4791
06:49:02,190 --> 06:49:04,368
大约 45 秒用于阅读。
Around 45 seconds reading.

4792
06:49:04,608 --> 06:49:12,452
在看选项前，花 15 秒形成你自己的答案。30 秒进行匹配和排除，剩下的约 30 秒作为备用。
15 seconds forming your own answer before you look. 30 seconds matching and eliminating, and about 30 seconds spare.

4793
06:49:13,230 --> 06:49:17,828
那 30 秒的备用时间是你的缓冲，而难题会消耗掉这部分时间。
That spare 30 is your buffer and it is what a difficult item borrows from.

4794
06:49:18,528 --> 06:49:28,196
耗费时间的因素是第三次去重读题干，这通常意味着你前两次只是在被动阅读。注意这里的强调，因为这是核心策略。
The thing that eats it is rereading the stem a third time, which usually means you read it passively the first two. And note the call out because it is the actual strategy.

4795
06:49:28,448 --> 06:49:33,636
平均值不是目标。简单的题目应该花一分钟，这样难题才能有三分钟的时间。
The average is not the target. Easy items should take a minute so that hard ones can take three.

4796
06:49:35,342 --> 06:49:38,788
这个顺序值得在后续的考试中练习。
This order is worth practicing in the exams that follow.

4797
06:49:39,088 --> 06:49:43,556
先读问题行再读题干，这样你就知道为了什么目的去阅读了。
Read the question line first before the stem so you know what you are reading for.

4798
06:49:44,014 --> 06:49:49,156
然后读题干，特别留意那个埋设的细节，通常是最后一句。
Then read the stem watching specifically for the planted detail, which is usually the last sentence.

4799
06:49:50,094 --> 06:49:54,980
接着在看任何东西之前，先在心里把你的答案表述成一个短语。
Then say your own answer to yourself as a phrase before you look at anything.

4800
06:49:55,758 --> 06:50:01,892
然后去读选项，与你已经决定的内容进行匹配，而不是去逐个评估每一个选项。
Then read the options, matching against what you already decided rather than evaluating each one code.

4801
06:50:03,342 --> 06:50:06,628
最后一步的原因是模块 18 的课程内容。
The reason for the last step is module 18's lesson.

4802
06:50:07,470 --> 06:50:13,092
在阅读选项前就先确定答案，这会让反向干扰项显现出来。
Committing to an answer before reading the options is what makes a reversed distractor visible.

4803
06:50:14,766 --> 06:50:17,124
这里有一点需要准确把握。
Here is something worth being precise about.

4804
06:50:17,518 --> 06:50:24,388
在练习题库中，“最有效”出现在 40% 的题干中，而某种形式的“最佳”出现在另外 11% 中。
In the practice bank, most effective appeared in 40% of stems and some form of best in another 11.

4805
06:50:24,846 --> 06:50:29,728
“最可靠”和“最合适”两者合计约占 5%。
Most reliable and most appropriate accounted for about 5% between them.

4806
06:50:30,254 --> 06:50:36,900
“根本原因”、“保证”以及“不论提示词工程”都很罕见，每项仅出现在少数题目中。
Root cause, guarantee, and regardless of prompting were rare, appearing in only a handful of items each.

4807
06:50:38,894 --> 06:50:47,428
这很重要，因为我在整个课程中都强调了“保证”系列，它是最关键的限定词，虽然不是出现频率最高的。
That matters because I have emphasized the guarantee family throughout this course, and it is the most decisive qualifier while not being the most common one.

4808
06:50:48,368 --> 06:50:55,076
你实际会看到的是“最有效”，这意味着那个具有普适性的答案。
Most effective is what you will actually see, and it means the answer that generalizes.

4809
06:50:56,688 --> 06:51:01,444
既然几乎一半的试卷都取决于这一个词，那就花点时间思考它要求的含义。
Since almost half the paper turns on this one word, spend a moment on what it asks.

4810
06:51:01,934 --> 06:51:07,140
“最有效”意味着哪个选项能解决这一类问题，而不是仅仅解决你面前的这个案例。
Most effective means which option fixes the class of problem rather than the instance in front of you.

4811
06:51:07,918 --> 06:51:14,724
那些只针对特定情况的补丁是典型的“险些选对”，因为它们确实管用，但只能管用一次。
Options that patch the stated case are the classic near miss because they genuinely work and they work exactly once.

4812
06:51:15,168 --> 06:51:20,356
比起处理当前情况的选项，更倾向于让下一次情况不再发生的改变。
Prefer the change that makes the next occurrence impossible over the one that handles this occurrence.

4813
06:51:21,390 --> 06:51:28,580
当两个选项都明显可行时，有用的问题是：哪一个在六个月后你依然会满意？
And when two options both clearly work, the useful question is which one you would still be happy with in six months.

4814
06:51:29,248 --> 06:51:31,648
这个问题能解决大部分情况。
That question resolves most of these.

4815
06:51:33,038 --> 06:51:35,568
现在来看错误答案，因为它们不是废话。
Now the wrong answers because they are not filler.

4816
06:51:36,046 --> 06:51:44,548
在编写良好的考试中，每个干扰项都是某人真实持有的特定误区，这意味着它们会以可预测的方式出错。
On a well-written exam, every distractor is a specific misconception someone actually holds, which means they are wrong in predictable ways.

4817
06:51:45,614 --> 06:51:48,708
这篇试卷上的几乎所有错误选项都属于这四种类型。
Four shapes cover almost all of them on this paper.

4818
06:51:49,646 --> 06:51:56,004
一旦你能识别出这些类型，你就可以在不进行完整推理的情况下排除掉某个选项，这就是节省时间的关键所在。
Once you can name the shape, you can eliminate an option without fully reasoning through it, and that is where the time saving lives.

4819
06:51:56,368 --> 06:52:02,500
接下来的四张幻灯片每张讲一个系列，最后的案例会标明每个错误选项所属的系列。
The next four slides take one family each, and the scenarios at the end name the family re for every wrong option.

4820
06:52:04,270 --> 06:52:05,316
这四个系列是：
The four families.

4821
06:52:05,867 --> 06:52:10,884
“正确的想法在错误的层级”，即正确原则被应用在了提示词中，而不是代码里。
Right idea in the wrong layer where the correct principle is applied in a prompt instead of in code.

4822
06:52:11,790 --> 06:52:17,540
“治标不治本”，即选项确实减少了故障，但没有解决故障发生的根本原因。
Symptom rather than cause where the option genuinely reduces the failure without addressing why it happens.

4823
06:52:18,446 --> 06:52:26,308
“过度设计”，即提出的机制比问题所需的更复杂，而且它通常是列表中听起来最高级的选项。
Overengineered, where a heavier mechanism is proposed than the problem needs, and it is usually the most impressive sounding option on the list.

4824
06:52:26,958 --> 06:52:34,788
还有“反向”或“虚构”，指成对的两个部分被互换了，或者描述的功能根本不存在。
And reversed or invented where the two halves of a pair are swapped or a capability is described that simply does not exist.

4825
06:52:35,758 --> 06:52:42,532
本课程中的每个案例都包含至少其中一种情况，现在你可以给它们命名了。
Every scenario in this course has contained at least one of these, and now you get to name them.

4826
06:52:44,110 --> 06:52:50,500
系列 1 是考试中最常见的，它之所以有效是因为选项中的原则始终是正确的。
Family 1 is the most common on this exam, and the reason it works is that the principle in the option is always correct.

4827
06:52:51,534 --> 06:52:56,068
这个规则确实属于某个地方，但该选项把它放在了提示词或记忆文件中。
The rule does belong somewhere, and the option puts it in a prompt or a memory file.

4828
06:52:57,422 --> 06:53:01,828
这个检查确实需要执行，但该选项要求智能体去记住去做它。
The check does need to happen, and the option asks the agent to remember to do it.

4829
06:53:02,766 --> 06:53:07,908
限制确实需要强制执行，而该选项提供了一个参数。模块本身会处理好这一切。
The limit does need enforcing and the option offers a parameter. The module sets itself.

4830
06:53:08,782 --> 06:53:15,716
这种特征是一种特定的感觉：你认同该选项试图做的事情，但它展示的机制实际上无法实现这一目标。
The tell is a particular feeling. You agree with what the option is trying to do, and the mechanism it shows cannot actually enforce it.

4831
06:53:16,064 --> 06:53:18,852
当你察觉到这种感觉时，你就找到了这一类选项。
When you notice that feeling, you have found this family.

4832
06:53:20,590 --> 06:53:25,348
类别 2 在不改变失败原因的情况下降低失败率。
Family 2 reduces the failure rate without changing why the failure happens.

4833
06:53:25,870 --> 06:53:27,844
这些常见的特征是易于辨认的。
The common shapes are recognizable.

4834
06:53:28,270 --> 06:53:33,156
更多的 retry、更大的上下文窗口、更严格的提示词、更短的输出。
More retrees, a bigger context window, a stricter prompt, a shorter output.

4835
06:53:33,710 --> 06:53:34,788
这类测试很快。
The test is quick.

4836
06:53:35,598 --> 06:53:40,384
如果采用这个选项，同样的失败会在不同规模下再次出现吗？
If this option ships, does the same failure come back at a different scale?

4837
06:53:40,942 --> 06:53:46,464
一个能多争取两个问题的更大上下文窗口，是本课程中最典型的例子。
A bigger context window that buys two more questions is the clearest example in this course.

4838
06:53:46,704 --> 06:53:55,268
特别是在“根本原因”和“最有效”这些词语下要警惕这一类，因为这两个限定词明确排除了它们。
Watch for this family particularly under the words root cause and most effective because both of those qualifiers explicitly exclude it.

4839
06:53:55,584 --> 06:53:57,636
“会有所帮助”并不是标准答案。
It would help is not the standard.

4840
06:53:58,190 --> 06:53:59,364
这个问题正在适用中。
The question is applying.

4841
06:54:01,070 --> 06:54:07,824
类别 3 提供的机制比问题所需的更复杂。比如用智能体去解决本可以用工作流解决的问题。
Family 3 proposes a heavier mechanism than the problem needs. An agent where a workflow would do.

4842
06:54:08,110 --> 06:54:10,692
用子智能体去解决本可以用单一上下文解决的问题。
Subagents where a single context would do.

4843
06:54:11,264 --> 06:54:14,624
构建一个 MCP 服务器，而实际上只需采用现有的即可。
Building an MCP server where adopting one would do.

4844
06:54:14,864 --> 06:54:18,596
使用模型分类器，而关键词规则已经能正常工作了。
A model classifier where a keyword rule already works correctly.

4845
06:54:19,344 --> 06:54:26,468
这听起来像是很好的架构，而这正是它被提供的原因。因为复杂性往往会被误认为专业能力。
It sounds like good architecture, and that is exactly why it is offered. Because sophistication reads as competence.

4846
06:54:26,704 --> 06:54:31,396
其特征是为原本不需要做决策的事情增加了一个决策者。
The tell is that it adds a decision maker to something that had no decision to make.

4847
06:54:32,078 --> 06:54:41,104
并记住 Anthropic 发布的官方指南：寻找最简单且有效的方案，只有在需要时才增加复杂度。
And remember Anthropic's own published guidance, which is to find the simplest thing that works and add complexity only when you need it.

4848
06:54:42,350 --> 06:54:44,464
类别 4 有两种形式。
Family 4 comes in two forms.

4849
06:54:44,784 --> 06:54:51,972
反转型，即成对的两个部分互换了位置，比如用于内容的 GloB 或批量处理紧急流量。
Reversed, where the two halves of a pair are swapped, like glob for contents or batching the urgent traffic.

4850
06:54:52,654 --> 06:54:57,024
以及虚构型，即选项描述了一个并不存在的机制。
And invented where the option describes a mechanism that does not exist.

4851
06:54:57,806 --> 06:55:04,932
子智能体之间直接通信，或者是一个根据你的业务政策来对比工具结果的 SDK。
Subagents messaging each other directly or an SDK that compares tool results against your business policy.

4852
06:55:05,582 --> 06:55:10,564
只要你在阅读选项前先形成自己的答案，这两类就很容易识别出来。
Both are easy marks provided you form your own answer before reading the options.

4853
06:55:11,342 --> 06:55:13,316
并注意底部的警告。
And note the warning at the bottom.

4854
06:55:14,222 --> 06:55:20,868
虚构的选项往往听起来最专业，因为具体性会被误认为是权威性。
Invented options often sound the most technical of the four because specificity reads as authority.

4855
06:55:21,518 --> 06:55:23,492
具体并不等同于证据。
Specificity is not evidence.

4856
06:55:25,038 --> 06:55:27,108
关于猜测的一个简短诚实的章节。
A short honest section on guessing.

4857
06:55:27,982 --> 06:55:35,332
在练习题库中，答案字母的分布几乎完全均匀，分别是 35、33、33 和 33。
In the practice bank, the answer letters were almost perfectly uniform at 35, 33, 33, and 33.

4858
06:55:35,886 --> 06:55:37,732
没有所谓的“幸运字母”可以作为保底选择。
There is no lucky letter to fall back on.

4859
06:55:38,702 --> 06:55:44,676
最长的选项正确率为 38%，而随机猜测的概率仅为 25%。
The longest option was correct 38% of the time against 25% by chance.

4860
06:55:45,230 --> 06:55:48,452
这是一个真实的信号，但太弱到不能作为决策依据。
That is a real signal and far too weak to act on.

4861
06:55:49,294 --> 06:55:57,796
所谓有效的工作就是排除法，因为去掉一个选项能让概率从 25% 提升到 33%，去掉两个则能提升到 50%。
What does work is elimination because removing one option takes a guess from 25 to 33% and removing 2 takes it to 50.

4862
06:55:58,464 --> 06:56:04,420
并且一定要填出答案，因为答错没有扣分，而留白肯定是零分。
And always answer since there is no penalty for a wrong one and a blank is a guaranteed zero.

4863
06:56:05,966 --> 06:56:08,196
如果你有纪律性地去使用标记功能，它就会派上用场。
Flagging works if you use it with discipline.

4864
06:56:08,544 --> 06:56:12,900
在第一轮时填出所有题目，即使你不确定，然后再进行标注。
Answer everything on the first pass even when you are unsure, then flag it.

4865
06:56:13,184 --> 06:56:16,996
一个已经填了答案且被标记的题目不会让你损失任何分数。
A flagged item with an answer already in it costs you nothing.

4866
06:56:17,486 --> 06:56:21,124
但如果没填答案，时间一到就得丢掉整分。
An unanswered one costs the whole mark if time runs out.

4867
06:56:21,902 --> 06:56:29,700
基于规则而非感觉来标注，比如两个你确实无法区分的选项，或者一个你不认识的术语。
Flag on a rule rather than a feeling, so two options you genuinely could not separate or a term you did not recognize.

4868
06:56:30,286 --> 06:56:37,732
标记的数量不要超过 10 个左右，因为对 20 个题目进行第二轮审查已经不是在复查了，而是第二次考试。
Do not flag more than about 10 because a second pass over 20 items is not a second pass, it is a second exam.

4869
06:56:38,702 --> 06:56:42,756
在复核时，只有在你能说明理由的情况下才更改答案。
An on review, change an answer only when you can state the reason.

4870
06:56:44,494 --> 06:56:47,748
这 6 个场景以及每个场景真正测试的内容。
The 6 scenarios and what each is really testing.

4871
06:56:48,270 --> 06:56:53,124
客户支持涉及升级、保证的结果和工具限制。
Customer support is about escalation, guaranteed outcomes, and tool limits.

4872
06:56:55,054 --> 06:56:56,624
使用 Claude 进行代码生成。
Code generation with Claude.

4873
06:56:57,294 --> 06:57:01,508
代码相关的内容涉及内存层级、计划模式和强制执行层。
Code is about the memory hierarchy, plan mode, and enforcement layers.

4874
06:57:02,446 --> 06:57:06,052
多智能体研究涉及委派和上下文隔离。
Multi-agent research is about delegation and context isolation.

4875
06:57:06,542 --> 06:57:11,492
开发者生产力涉及内置工具、探索和 MCP。
Developer productivity is about the built-in tools, exploration and MCP.

4876
06:57:11,984 --> 06:57:17,988
CI 和 CD 涉及用于分类运行结果的无头模式标志，以及新会话复核。
CI and CD is about headless flags classifying how a run ended, and fresh session review.

4877
06:57:18,304 --> 06:57:23,300
而结构化提取涉及架构设计、虚构和重试循环。
And structured extraction is about schema design, fabrication, and the retry loop.

4878
06:57:24,430 --> 06:57:25,636
注意这个提示。
Note the callout.

4879
06:57:26,734 --> 06:57:31,268
场景只是背景，所测试的领域往往是不同的。
The scenario is only the setting, and the domain being tested is often a different one.

4880
06:57:33,006 --> 06:57:34,384
一些实操细节。
A few practicalities.

4881
06:57:34,624 --> 06:57:41,476
请自行核查当前的费用、预约路径和访问规则，因为这些内容会变动，本课程无法保证这些信息的实时性。
Check the current fee, the booking route, and the access rules yourself because those change and this course cannot be current on them.

4882
06:57:44,302 --> 06:57:49,220
如果你是参加有监考人员的在线考试，请提前测试你的设备，而不是在考试前半小时才测。
If you are sitting it online with a proctor, test your setup in advance rather than half an hour before.

4883
06:57:49,998 --> 06:57:56,100
记住时钟的位置，每做 10 道题扫一眼，而不是每道题都看，并设置一个检查点。
Know where the clock is and glance at it every 10 questions rather than every question and use one checkpoint.

4884
06:57:56,654 --> 06:57:59,524
到第 30 题时，你应该还有大约 60 分钟左右。
At question 30, you should have about 60 minutes remaining.

4885
06:58:00,302 --> 06:58:04,324
如果你做到第 30 题时只剩 40 分钟，那就加快速度。
If you are at question 30 with 40 minutes left, speed up.

4886
06:58:04,654 --> 06:58:07,556
否则，继续做题并停止盯着时间看。
Otherwise, carry on and stop watching the clock.

4887
06:58:08,782 --> 06:58:09,764
5 行。
5 lines.

4888
06:58:10,254 --> 06:58:15,844
先读题目行，再读题干，然后在阅读选项之前确定一个答案。
Read the question line first, then the stem, then commit to an answer before reading the options.

4889
06:58:16,224 --> 06:58:21,316
“最有效”这个词出现在考卷上近一半的题目中，意味着那个具有普适性的答案。
Most effective appears on nearly half the paper and means the answer that generalizes.

4890
06:58:22,702 --> 06:58:24,864
共有四类干扰项。
There are four distractor families.

4891
06:58:25,358 --> 06:58:26,224
错误层级。
Wrong layer.

4892
06:58:26,414 --> 06:58:30,820
只是症状而非原因，属于过度工程、反向设计或虚构。
Symptom rather than cause over engineered and reversed or invented.

4893
06:58:31,758 --> 06:58:36,676
回答所有问题，少用标记，且只有在有明确理由时才修改答案。
Answer everything, flag sparingly, and change an answer only with a reason you can state.

4894
06:58:37,358 --> 06:58:40,964
并在简单题目上节省时间，为难题留出充足思考时间。
And spend a minute on easy items so that hard ones can have three.

4895
06:58:41,614 --> 06:58:42,980
现在是五个场景。
Five scenarios now.

4896
06:58:43,344 --> 06:58:47,844
每一个场景都会让每个错误选项背后的逻辑失效。
And each one maims the family behind every wrong option.

4897
06:58:49,582 --> 06:58:50,404
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

4898
06:58:50,830 --> 06:58:56,356
支持智能体在未经经理批准的情况下，绝不能发放超过一千英镑的退款。
A support agent must never issue a refund above a thousand pounds without manager approval.

4899
06:58:56,750 --> 06:59:00,452
系统提示词中规定了这一点，且工具描述中也重复了这一要求。
The system prompt states this and the tool description repeats it.

4900
06:59:01,070 --> 06:59:08,384
在四个月内，有六笔超过限额的退款被发放，且每位客户都给出了充分的理由。
Over four months, six refunds above the limit were issued, and in each case the customer had given a compelling reason.

4901
06:59:08,942 --> 06:59:12,804
审计要求团队证明该限制是不可逾越的。
Audit requires the team to demonstrate the limit cannot be exceeded.

4902
06:59:14,670 --> 06:59:16,356
最有效的改进是什么？
What is the most effective change?

4903
06:59:17,230 --> 06:59:22,724
a. 在系统提示词中增加示例，展示如何正确拒绝超过一千英镑的请求。
a add examples to the system prompt showing correct refusals above a thousand pounds.

4904
06:59:23,342 --> 06:59:23,584
b.
b.

4905
06:59:24,144 --> 06:59:26,064
拒绝超过一千的金额。
Reject amounts above a thousand.

4906
06:59:26,734 --> 06:59:30,564
在退款工具中返回一个命名为“审批工具”的错误提示。
Inside the refund tool returning an error naming the approval tool.

4907
06:59:30,944 --> 06:59:31,104
C。
C.

4908
06:59:31,982 --> 06:59:36,708
增加一个“经经理批准”参数。智能体必须在金额超过限额时设置该参数。
Add an approved by manager parameter. The agent must set for amounts above the limit.

4909
06:59:37,166 --> 06:59:40,900
D. 将所有退款通过一个经理审批子智能体进行处理。
D. Root all refunds through a manager approval subagent.

4910
06:59:41,390 --> 06:59:42,468
停下来思考并做决定。
Pause and decide.

4911
06:59:48,206 --> 06:59:52,516
答案是 B，且此项包含了四个错误类别中的三个。
The answer is B and this item contains three of the four families.

4912
06:59:52,814 --> 06:59:59,172
选项 A 是症状而非原因，它只是在提高成功率，而要求是证明无法违规。
Option A is symptom rather than cause, improving a rate when the requirement says demonstrate it cannot happen.

4913
06:59:59,424 --> 07:00:05,988
选项 C 虽然思路正确但属于“长层”，因为智能体自行设置的参数仍由你试图约束的那个智能体来决定。
Option C is right idea, long layer, because a parameter the agent sets is set by the agent you are trying to constrain.

4914
07:00:06,670 --> 07:00:13,636
选项 D 是过度工程，为了监控六笔大额退款而给每一笔小额退款都加一个子智能体。
Option D is over-engineered, putting a subagent in front of every small refund in order to police six large ones.

4915
07:00:14,224 --> 07:00:21,252
一旦你能识别出类别，你就能在两秒内排除掉一个选项，而不是去推敲它的后果。
Once you can name the family, you eliminate an option in about two seconds rather than reasoning through its consequences.

4916
07:00:22,670 --> 07:00:23,492
场景 2。
Scenario 2.

4917
07:00:23,824 --> 07:00:27,300
研究协调员将任务分配给四个子智能体。
A research coordinator delegates to four subagents.

4918
07:00:28,110 --> 07:00:32,772
综合子智能体经常遗漏数据子智能体产生的结果。
The synthesis subagent consistently omits findings that the data subagent produced.

4919
07:00:33,550 --> 07:00:38,628
日志确认数据子智能体已完成任务，并将详细结果返回给协调员。
Logs confirm the data subagent completed and returned a detailed result to the coordinator.

4920
07:00:39,502 --> 07:00:44,164
综合子智能目的提示词是：将研究内容汇总成报告。
The synthesis subagent's prompt reads synthesize the research into a report.

4921
07:00:44,704 --> 07:00:46,180
根本原因是什么？
What is the root cause?

4922
07:00:46,606 --> 07:00:56,164
a. 合成子智能体的轮数限制太低，无法收集所有内容。B. 数据子智能体应该直接将结果传递给合成子智能体。
a. The synthesis subagent's turn cap is too low to gather everything. B. The data subagent should pass its findings to the synthesis subagent directly.

4923
07:00:57,134 --> 07:00:57,424
C.
C.

4924
07:00:58,144 --> 07:01:02,116
协调者未在合成提示词中包含这些结果。
The coordinator is not including the findings in the synthesis prompt.

4925
07:01:02,624 --> 07:01:06,704
D. 合成子智能体需要一个能力更强的模型。
D. The synthesis subagent needs a more capable model.

4926
07:01:07,310 --> 07:01:08,452
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4927
07:01:14,158 --> 07:01:15,696
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

4928
07:01:16,430 --> 07:01:20,068
从这道题中可以学到的技巧是关于引号内的提示词。
The technique to take from this one is about the quoted prompt.

4929
07:01:20,462 --> 07:01:27,856
当题干完整引用某段内容时，那是关键证据而非干扰项，之所以放进去是因为阅读它能决定问题的答案。
When a STEM quotes something in full, that is evidence rather than color, and it is there because reading it decides the question.

4930
07:01:28,416 --> 07:01:35,716
「将研究结果汇总成报告」这一句中不包含任何具体结果，而且提示词是进入子智能体的唯一通道。
Synthesize the research into a report contains no findings, and the prompt is the only channel into a subagent.

4931
07:01:36,096 --> 07:01:41,376
选项 B 是虚构的逻辑，描述了一个并不存在的机制。
Option B is the invented family describing a mechanism that does not exist.

4932
07:01:42,254 --> 07:01:51,056
选项 A 和 D 都只是对症状的处理而非根本原因，即给子智能体更多轮数或更强的能力来处理信息
Options A and D are both symptom rather than cause, giving the subagent more turns or more capability to work with information

4933
07:01:51,342 --> 07:01:52,388
它压根就没收到这些信息。
it never received.

4934
07:01:54,062 --> 07:01:54,976
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

4935
07:01:55,246 --> 07:02:02,180
一个团队每月处理 200,000 份文档进行归档分类，结果将汇总到季度报告中。
A team processes 200,000 documents monthly for archival classification and results feed a quarterly report.

4936
07:02:02,576 --> 07:02:08,736
流水线在收到每份文件时将其作为同步请求发送，且费用逐年翻倍。
The pipeline sends each document as a synchronous request on arrival and the bill has doubled year on year.

4937
07:02:09,294 --> 07:02:12,932
在汇编季度报告之前，没有任何结果被消耗掉。
No result is consumed before the quarterly report is compiled.

4938
07:02:14,478 --> 07:02:16,644
最具成本效益的改进是什么？
What is the most cost effective change?

4939
07:02:17,038 --> 07:02:20,420
a 并行处理文档以减少总运行时间。
a process documents in parallel to reduce total runtime.

4940
07:02:21,038 --> 07:02:25,700
b 通过消息批处理 API 发送这些文档。
b send the documents through the message batches API.

4941
07:02:26,414 --> 07:02:31,364
C 构建一个带有专门分类子智能体的多智能体流水线。
C Build a multi-agent pipeline with specialized classifier sub agents.

4942
07:02:32,174 --> 07:02:32,537
D。
D.

4943
07:02:33,422 --> 07:02:37,188
减少最大标记数，使每次分类响应更短。
reduce max tokens so each classification response is shorter.

4944
07:02:38,606 --> 07:02:39,780
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4945
07:02:45,376 --> 07:02:47,216
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

4946
07:02:47,616 --> 07:02:50,212
选项 C 是一个值得警惕的陷阱。
Option C is the one worth dwelling on.

4947
07:02:50,574 --> 07:02:56,196
它是作为解决成本问题的答案而提供的过度工程，它不仅没用。
It is over-engineering offered as an answer to a cost question and it does not merely fail to help.

4948
07:02:56,558 --> 07:03:00,644
因为它会增加成本，因为子智能体会成倍增加 token 的消耗。
It actively costs more since sub-agents multiply token consumption.

4949
07:03:01,294 --> 07:03:08,996
当问题要求你降低成本，而某个选项提出更复杂的架构时，那个选项几乎总是错误的。
When a question asks you to reduce cost and one option proposes a more sophisticated architecture, that option is almost always wrong.

4950
07:03:09,966 --> 07:03:13,156
它往往会朝着与需求相反的方向走向错误。
Frequently wrong in the opposite direction from what is needed.

4951
07:03:14,062 --> 07:03:21,636
选项 A 对并行性带来的收益理解反了，而选项 D 只解决了账单中很小的一部分。
Option A is reversed understanding of what parallelism buys and option D targets the small half of the bill.

4952
07:03:22,976 --> 07:03:24,228
场景 4。
Scenario 4.

4953
07:03:24,686 --> 07:03:30,496
一名工程师需要智能体找出所有文件名以 .config.ts 结尾的文件。
An engineer needs the agent to locate every file whose name ends in.config.ts.

4954
07:03:30,976 --> 07:03:34,020
然后找出这些文件中哪些引用了已弃用的 helper。
Then find which of those references are deprecated helper.

4955
07:03:34,416 --> 07:03:36,964
该仓库大约有 4000 个文件。
The repository has about 4000 files.

4956
07:03:38,096 --> 07:03:40,132
最有效的方法是什么？
What is the most efficient approach?

4957
07:03:40,814 --> 07:03:44,132
a. 读取仓库中的每个文件，然后再进行过滤。
a read every file in the repository, then filter.

4958
07:03:45,038 --> 07:03:49,604
b. 先按文件名模式搜索，再在这些文件中用 grep 查找 helper。
brop for the file name pattern, then grep those files for the helper.

4959
07:03:50,030 --> 07:03:54,052
c. 用 grep 匹配文件名模式，然后用 drop 查找 helper。
C. Grep for the file name pattern, then drop for the helper.

4960
07:03:54,510 --> 07:03:58,656
d. 派出一个子代理来探索仓库并汇报结果。
D. Spawn a subagent to explore the repository and report back.

4961
07:03:58,976 --> 07:04:00,336
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4962
07:04:05,966 --> 07:04:12,964
答案是 B。如果你先读题干并构思出自己的答案，这道题大约只需要 20 秒。
The answer is B. This item is worth about 20 seconds if you read the question line first and formed your own answer.

4963
07:04:13,262 --> 07:04:18,820
选项 C 是反向操作，选项 D 是过度工程，这两个都可以排除。
Option C is the reversal and option D is over engineering and both are eliminable on site.

4964
07:04:19,726 --> 07:04:27,216
注意 B 的两个步骤顺序正确：先通过名称缩小范围，然后再仅在这些较小的集合中搜索内容。
Note also that B has the two steps in the right order, narrowing by name first and then searching contents only within that smaller set.

4965
07:04:27,376 --> 07:04:35,364
如果你在 C 上犹豫了，那么在做模拟考试前，这个知识点值得再过一遍。它在模块 18 中也出现过。
If you pause on C at all, that pair is worth one more pass before the practice exams. It was also rapid 2 in module 18.

4966
07:04:36,814 --> 07:04:37,988
场景 5。
Scenario 5.

4967
07:04:39,342 --> 07:04:50,948
一个提取架构要求包含保单编号字段。大约 15% 的提交文档没有保单编号，而对于这些文档，提取结果会返回一个看似合理但并不存在于任何系统中的号码。
An extraction schema requires a policy number field. About 15% of submitted documents have no policy number, and for those, extraction returns a plausible number that does not exist in any system.

4968
07:04:51,310 --> 07:04:55,296
提示词中已经指示模型不要虚构数值了。
The prompt already instructs the model not to invent values.

4969
07:04:55,822 --> 07:04:59,428
下游系统已经根据这些号码创建了记录。
Downstream systems have created records against these numbers.

4970
07:04:59,822 --> 07:05:01,348
最有效的修复方法是什么？
What is the most effective fix?

4971
07:05:01,742 --> 07:05:06,116
a. 加强指令并增加一个没有保单编号的示例。
a strengthen the instruction and add an example with no policy number.

4972
07:05:06,606 --> 07:05:06,816
b。
b.

4973
07:05:07,246 --> 07:05:11,524
将保单编号设为可为空，并注明 null 表示不存在。
Make the policy number nullable, documenting that null means not present.

4974
07:05:12,238 --> 07:05:16,932
c. 在接受之前，根据源文本验证提取出的保单号码。
C. Validate extracted policy numbers against the source text before accepting.

4975
07:05:17,696 --> 07:05:17,936
d。
d.

4976
07:05:18,414 --> 07:05:21,124
降低采样温度，让模型减少虚构内容。
Lower the temperature so the model invents less.

4977
07:05:22,510 --> 07:05:23,748
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

4978
07:05:29,390 --> 07:05:31,120
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

4979
07:05:31,440 --> 07:05:40,644
这个干扰项是故意设计的，而且这是你在本课程中已经见过好几次的环节。提示词里已经要求模型不要虚构数值了。
The eliminator is placed deliberately and it is a phase you have now seen several times in this course. The prompt already instructs the model not to invent values.

4980
07:05:41,454 --> 07:05:48,452
每当题干告诉你某个指令已经存在但不起作用时，任何旨在提供更好指令的选项都是错误的。
Whenever a stem tells you an instruction exists and is not working, every option that lights a better instruction is dead.

4981
07:05:50,400 --> 07:05:56,080
选项 C 是最强的干扰项，因为验证确实是很好的实践。
Option C is the strongest distractor because validation is genuinely good practice.

4982
07:05:56,622 --> 07:06:02,404
它只是在事后解决问题，而且由于仍有虚构内容的压力，这并不能从根本上解决问题。
It also catches the problem after the fact on every document forever while the pressure to invent remains.

4983
07:06:04,238 --> 07:06:08,100
选项 A 属于错误的层级，而选项 D 是症状而非原因。
Option A is wrong layer and option D is symptom rather than cause.

4984
07:06:09,102 --> 07:06:11,940
接下来是模块 20，然后是模拟考试。
Module 20 next and then the practice exams.

4985
07:06:13,614 --> 07:06:16,036
模块 20，是最后一个教学模块。
Module 20, the last teaching module.

4986
07:06:16,720 --> 07:06:22,692
在整个课程中，我有十次提醒大家：考试答案和当前的官方文档并不一致。
Ten times in this course, I stop to say that the exams answer and the current documentation disagree.

4987
07:06:23,694 --> 07:06:29,360
本模块将所有这些差异汇总到一起并进行分类，因为它们的权重并不相等。
This module gathers all of them into one place and langs them because they are not equally important.

4988
07:06:29,840 --> 07:06:32,228
其中 5 个会改变你应该给出的答案。
5 will change the answer you should give.

4989
07:06:33,040 --> 07:06:38,720
剩下的内容如果你在不知道它们存在的情况下去读文档，只会让你感到困惑。
The rest will only confuse you if you read the documentation without knowing they exist.

4990
07:06:39,200 --> 07:06:44,868
而且还有相当一部分你预期会变动的内容根本没变，这部分也值得说明一下。
And a good deal of what you might expect to have moved has not moved at all, which is worth saying too.

4991
07:06:46,158 --> 07:06:52,836
认证内容总是滞后于它所认证的产品，而这项考试在某些地方大约落后了六个月。
Certification content always trails the product it certifies, and this exam trails it by roughly six months in places.

4992
07:06:53,678 --> 07:06:59,257
这是正常的，并不是在批评产品，因为每当旗舰产品更新时，考题不可能每次都重写。
That is normal and it is not a criticism because a paper cannot be rewritten every time of flagships.

4993
07:07:00,398 --> 07:07:05,028
这对你的意义是：在少数几个主题上，你需要掌握两种答案。
What it means for you is that on a small number of topics you need two answers.

4994
07:07:05,360 --> 07:07:09,700
一个是考试评分所依据的答案，另一个是你实际在工作中会使用的答案。
The one the exam is scored against and the one you would actually use at work.

4995
07:07:10,222 --> 07:07:13,860
只要你知道自己处于哪种模式，这两者就不会产生冲突。
Those are not in conflict as long as you know which mode you are in.

4996
07:07:14,720 --> 07:07:19,556
本模块的目的就是让你有意识地切换这两种模式，而不是凭感觉去猜。
This module is about making that switch deliberate rather than accidental.

4997
07:07:21,006 --> 07:07:23,396
在进入细节之前先看比例。
Some proportion before the detail.

4998
07:07:24,718 --> 07:07:27,097
在 20 个模块中共有 13 处差异，
13 divergences across 20 modules,

4999
07:07:28,377 --> 07:07:30,297
其中 5 个会改变你应该给出的答案。
5 of them change the answer you should give.

5000
07:07:30,958 --> 07:07:36,548
另外 8 个只有在你阅读文档并发现指南中从未提到的内容时才重要。
The other eight only matter when you read the documentation and find something the guide never mentions.

5001
07:07:37,440 --> 07:07:44,068
考试框架中的几乎没有任何内容变错，只是有几项变得不完整了，这是不同的问题。
Almost nothing in the exam's framing became wrong, and several things became incomplete, which is a different problem.

5002
07:07:44,640 --> 07:07:50,116
只有一种技术被正式撤回了，这也是列表中唯一真正的修正。
Exactly one technique was actually withdrawn, and that is the only genuine correction in the list.

5003
07:07:51,022 --> 07:08:00,260
关于智能体循环、架构模式和强制执行原则的所有内容都没有变，而这些是你学习的核心内容。
Everything about the agentic loop, the architecture patterns, and the enforcement principles is unchanged, and that is the bulk of what you have learned.

5004
07:08:01,710 --> 07:08:05,828
第一层，5 行，这些是必须清晰掌握的。
Tier 1, 5 rows, and these are the ones to hold clearly.

5005
07:08:06,702 --> 07:08:09,252
符合架构的 JSON 是工具。
Schema conformant JSON is the tool.

5006
07:08:10,286 --> 07:08:14,564
考试上用的是架构技术，而在工作中用的是原生结构化输出。
Schema technique on the exam and native structured outputs at work.

5007
07:08:15,470 --> 07:08:20,080
预填充曾是一种推荐的技术，但在最新模型中已被撤回。
Prefill was a recommended technique and has been withdrawn on the latest models.

5008
07:08:20,590 --> 07:08:27,780
这使得它成为唯一一个考试时代的答案现在就是错误的，而不仅仅是不完整的项。
That makes it the only row where the exam era answer is now simply wrong, rather than merely incomplete.

5009
07:08:29,422 --> 07:08:32,560
指令和技能过去是分开的，现在合并为一个系统。
Commands and skills were separate and are now one system.

5010
07:08:33,294 --> 07:08:38,800
委派工具以前叫任务，现在叫智能体，而任务作为别名仍然有效。
The delegation tool was task and is now agent, with tasks still working as an alias.

5011
07:08:39,854 --> 07:08:45,604
而 slash memory 回答了哪些文件被加载，这项任务现在已拆分为 slash 上下文。
And slash memory answered which files are loaded, a job now split with slash context.

5012
07:08:46,510 --> 07:08:49,092
在考试中选择中间那一列。
Give the middle column in the exam room.

5013
07:08:50,414 --> 07:08:54,532
结构化输出值得详细说明，因为它是最大的差异点。
Structured outputs deserves the detail because it is the largest gap.

5014
07:08:55,246 --> 07:08:55,940
有两种形式。
Two forms.

5015
07:08:57,440 --> 07:09:05,920
一种是约束 Claude 回复内容的输出配置格式，另一种是约束 Claude 如何调用工具的严格标志。
An output configuration format that constrains what Claude says and a strict flag on a tool that constrains how Claude calls it.

5016
07:09:06,350 --> 07:09:12,804
两者都使用语法约束采样，所以无效输出是无法产生的，而不仅仅是受到限制。
Both use grammar constrained sampling, so invalid output is unreachable rather than merely discouraged.

5017
07:09:13,120 --> 07:09:19,620
它们解决不同的问题并结合在一起，让你同时获得有效的工具参数和结构化的最终答案。
They solve different problems and combine, giving you valid tool arguments and a structured final answer together.

5018
07:09:20,526 --> 07:09:27,140
支持的架构关键词是一个子集，没有数字范围限制、没有字符串长度限制，也没有递归。
The supported schema keywords are a subset with no numeric bounds, no string length constraints, and no recursion.

5019
07:09:27,600 --> 07:09:32,228
所以你仍然需要一个验证层，因为结构是保证的，但含义不是。
So you still need a validation layer because shape is guaranteed and meaning is not.

5020
07:09:33,870 --> 07:09:35,620
1. 明确修正。
1. Explicit correction.

5021
07:09:36,046 --> 07:09:42,788
这是唯一一个如果你在实际工作中遵循这门课程的考试时代指导，就会导致你使用已弃用功能的地方。
It is the only place where following this course's exam era guidance at work would leave you using something withdrawn.

5022
07:09:44,302 --> 07:09:44,964
模块
Module

5023
07:09:45,678 --> 07:09:46,596
列出了 12 个。
12 listed.

5024
07:09:47,246 --> 07:09:49,764
在技术阶梯中，预填充响应。
Pre-filling the response in the technique ladder.

5025
07:09:50,702 --> 07:09:54,724
作为考试时代的指导，这是正确的，而且它就在试卷上，
That is correct as exam era guidance and it is on the paper,

5026
07:09:55,438 --> 07:09:58,436
但在最新的模块中，预填充不再受支持了。
and prefill is no longer supported on the latest modules.

5027
07:09:59,182 --> 07:10:01,092
所以在新的工作中不要去用它。
So do not reach for it in new work.

5028
07:10:01,486 --> 07:10:08,420
为了控制输出格式，请使用结构化输出或使用示例，后者完全不受影响。
For controlling output format, use structured outputs or use examples which are entirely unaffected.

5029
07:10:09,390 --> 07:10:17,348
而该阶梯上的其他所有内容仍然有效，包括最重要且最大的手段：清晰直接。
And everything else on that ladder remains current, including the first and largest lever, which is to be clear and direct.

5030
07:10:18,926 --> 07:10:23,876
第二层有 6 行，其中没有任何一项会让指导性错误答案变成错误的。
Tier 2, 6 rows, and none of them makes a guide error answer wrong.

5031
07:10:24,398 --> 07:10:29,860
它们只是不完整，这就是为什么当你查阅文档时会觉得有些意外。
They make it incomplete, which is why they read as surprises when you meet them in the documentation.

5032
07:10:30,958 --> 07:10:38,944
整合大型工具集仍然是正确的做法，而且现在还有按需加载定义的工具搜索功能。
Consolidating a large tool set is still right, and there is now also a tool search capability that loads definitions on demand.

5033
07:10:39,598 --> 07:10:46,116
手动总结依然有效，并且上下文编辑和记忆工具现在作为平台原生功能存在。
Manual summarization still works, and context editing and a memory tool now exist as platform primitives.

5034
07:10:47,470 --> 07:10:50,916
除非你传递了裸模式标志，否则 CI 配置会正常加载。
CI configuration loads normally unless you pass the bare flag.

5035
07:10:51,278 --> 07:10:53,124
计划模式有另外三条路径。
Plan mode has three more routes in.

5036
07:10:53,934 --> 07:10:57,700
记忆文件获得了自动记忆和跨工具互操作性。
Memory files have gained auto memory and cross-tool interoperability.

5037
07:10:58,606 --> 07:11:02,916
而且钩子大约有 30 个事件，而不仅仅是几个。
And hooks number around 30 events rather than a handful.

5038
07:11:04,622 --> 07:11:08,708
第三层很短，建议就是不要去动它。
Tier 3 is short and the advice is simply to leave it alone.

5039
07:11:09,518 --> 07:11:13,220
MCP 规范有一个 2026 年的候选版本。
The MCP specification has a 2026 release candidate.

5040
07:11:13,678 --> 07:11:20,452
它提议采用无状态协议，并弃用路由、采样和登录，移除窗口大约为一年。
It proposes a stateless protocol and deprecates routes, sampling, and login with a removal window of about a year.

5041
07:11:21,358 --> 07:11:27,812
子代理嵌套至 5 层已有文档记录，且关于哪些类型的子代理能获得工具的报告各不相同。
Subagent nesting to 5 levels is documented and reports differ on which subagent types actually get the tool.

5042
07:11:28,078 --> 07:11:34,052
而且自动模式已成为付费计划中新会话的默认权限模式，这不会影响计划模式。
And auto mode became the default permission mode for new sessions on paid plans, which does not affect plan mode.

5043
07:11:34,414 --> 07:11:36,292
这三项都要按考试版本回答。
Answer the exam version for all three.

5044
07:11:37,024 --> 07:11:42,384
列出这些是为了防止你在参加考试的前一周被文档内容搞糊涂。
These are listed so the documentation does not unsettle you the week before you sit.

5045
07:11:44,238 --> 07:11:47,556
现在是进入模拟考试前值得注意的部分。
Now the part worth hearing before you go into the practice exams.

5046
07:11:48,430 --> 07:11:51,460
让这项考试变难的所有因素都没有改变。
Everything that makes this exam difficult is unchanged.

5047
07:11:52,238 --> 07:11:59,332
判断决策、架构决策、强制执行原则以及对失败的推理。
The judgment calls, the architecture decisions, the enforcement principles, the reasoning about failure.

5048
07:12:00,270 --> 07:12:05,156
这些都没有偏移，因为它们不依赖于任何标志名称或功能发布。
None of that has drifted because none of it depends on a flag name or a feature release.

5049
07:12:07,950 --> 07:12:09,584
变动的是表面内容。
What has moved is surface.

5050
07:12:09,902 --> 07:12:15,184
哪个命令显示某些内容、某个机制的称呼、或者某种功能是否已经存在。
Which command shows you something, what a mechanism is called, whether a capability exists yet.

5051
07:12:15,566 --> 07:12:20,324
下一张幻灯片列出了没有变动的内容，这涵盖了课程的大部分。
The next slide lists what has not moved and it is most of the course.

5052
07:12:21,614 --> 07:12:24,292
6 个领域，都没有变动。
6 areas, none of which has moved.

5053
07:12:24,910 --> 07:12:32,784
智能体循环和停止原因反馈，仍是循环条件、枢纽与辐条式委派，且子代理不继承任何内容
The agentic loop and the stop reason feed, still the loop condition, hub and spoke delegation, with subagents inheriting nothing

5054
07:12:32,974 --> 07:12:35,428
且同级节点仍无法互相通信。
and siblings still unable to talk to each other.

5055
07:12:36,302 --> 07:12:43,620
「错误」是否与「协议错误」一致且在事实上明确为验证失败时的“错误”。
Is error against protocol error unchanged and in fact clarified in favor of is error for validation failures.

5056
07:12:43,984 --> 07:12:48,132
设置优先级链，其中托管策略处于顶层。
The settings precedence chain with managed policy at the top.

5057
07:12:48,704 --> 07:12:55,108
提示词负责说服，而代码负责强制执行，这是整个课程中价值最高的理念。
Prompts persuade while code enforces, which remains the highest value idea in the entire course.

5058
07:12:55,918 --> 07:13:00,644
以及批处理在 50% 时和必填字段导致的虚构。
And batch at 50% and required fields causing fabrication.

5059
07:13:01,646 --> 07:13:05,316
如果你掌握了这张表，其他地方的变动就只是些微小的注脚。
If you know this table, the drift elsewhere is a footnote.

5060
07:13:06,990 --> 07:13:08,388
如何同时兼顾这两者。
How to hold both.

5061
07:13:09,006 --> 07:13:11,364
在考场上，按照指南来回答。
In the exam room, answer from the guide.

5062
07:13:12,238 --> 07:13:17,860
如果某个选项描述的功能超前于指南，那它就不是他们想要的答案。
If an option describes a capability the guide predates, it is not the answer they are looking for.

5063
07:13:18,542 --> 07:13:24,708
在你的工作岗位上，请根据当下的文档来构建，因为考试并不是生产系统的风格指南。
At your desk, build from today's documentation because the exam is not a style guide for production systems.

5064
07:13:25,584 --> 07:13:32,324
不要试图去调和这两者，因为它们是针对不同人群、出于不同原因提出的不同问题的答案。
Do not try to reconcile the two since they are answers to different questions asked by different people for different reasons.

5065
07:13:32,622 --> 07:13:35,620
只有第一层级的 5 行内容值得真正去背诵。
And only the five tier 1 rows are worth actually rehearsing.

5066
07:13:36,462 --> 07:13:43,876
第二和第三层级的所有内容，你只需在遇到时识别出来即可，这也是本模块要达到的全部目标。
Everything in tiers 2 and 3, you will simply recognize when you meet it, which is all this module needs to achieve.

5067
07:13:45,582 --> 07:13:49,508
有四件事本课程无法保证是最新的，所以请自行核实。
Four things this course cannot be current on, so check them yourself.

5068
07:13:49,824 --> 07:13:52,036
费用以及它是否发生了变化。
The fee and whether it has changed.

5069
07:13:53,102 --> 07:13:59,556
访问规则，因为可用性已限制在合作伙伴组织中，且准入安排会变动。
The access rules, since availability has been gated to partner organizations and gating arrangements change.

5070
07:14:00,238 --> 07:14:07,652
还有考试指南版本，如果 Anthropic 发布了更新的版本，它将完全取代本模块的内容，你应该去阅读它。
And the exam guide version, because if Anthropic has published a newer one, it supersedes this module entirely and you should read it.

5071
07:14:08,334 --> 07:14:15,780
Anthropic 官方的认证页面才是权威，而不是这门课程，更不是博客文章。
Anthropic's own certification pages are the authority on all of this, not this course, and certainly not a blog post.

5072
07:14:16,238 --> 07:14:18,820
课程只能告诉你哪些细节已经过时了。
A course can tell you which details go stale.

5073
07:14:19,662 --> 07:14:21,764
它无法告诉你这些内容的当前值。
It cannot tell you their current values.

5074
07:14:23,470 --> 07:14:24,288
5 行。
5 lines.

5075
07:14:24,590 --> 07:14:31,076
13 个差异点，其中 5 个会改变你的答案，另外 8 个只影响阅读文档。
13 divergences, of which 5 change your answer, and 8 only affect reading the documentation.

5076
07:14:31,566 --> 07:14:37,380
结构化输出是最大的差距，所以请采用工具技术来回答问题，并在实际开发中使用真实功能。
Structured outputs is the largest gap, so answer the tool technique and build with the real feature.

5077
07:14:38,382 --> 07:14:40,964
Prefin 是唯一明确被撤回的内容。
Prefin is the only outright withdrawal.

5078
07:14:41,390 --> 07:14:43,236
所以不要在新的工作中用到它。
So do not use it in new work.

5079
07:14:44,142 --> 07:14:55,140
循环、配置层级以及“说服”与“强制”这两个概念完全没变。考试时遵循指南，而在你自己的工位上则参考文档。所以要清楚你现在身处哪个环境。
The loop, the configuration hierarchy, and persuade versus enforce have not moved at all. An exam room means the guide while your desk means the documentation. So know which room you are in.

5080
07:14:55,790 --> 07:14:56,900
3 个场景。
3 scenarios.

5081
07:14:57,710 --> 07:15:00,708
现在开始练习题。
Now then the practice exams begin.

5082
07:15:02,382 --> 07:15:03,332
场景 1。
Scenario 1.

5083
07:15:04,014 --> 07:15:07,172
这就是整个模块存在的意义所在。
And this is the situation the whole module exists for.

5084
07:15:08,238 --> 07:15:16,836
一道考题要求：如何确保文档提取每次都能返回符合特定架构的 JSON。
An exam item asks how to guarantee that a document extraction returns JSON conforming to a defined schema every time.

5085
07:15:18,062 --> 07:15:24,420
一个选项描述了定义一个输入架构为目标形状的工具，并通过工具选择来强制执行。
One option describes defining a tool whose input schema is the target shape and forcing it with tool choice.

5086
07:15:25,328 --> 07:15:31,332
另一个选项描述在输出配置中传递架构，从而让生成过程受到语法约束。
Another describes passing the schema in an output configuration so that generation is grammar constrained.

5087
07:15:31,968 --> 07:15:33,188
你会选哪一个？
Which do you select?

5088
07:15:33,678 --> 07:15:37,380
A：选择语法约束选项，因为它提供的保证更强。
a the grammar constrained option since it is a stronger guarantee.

5089
07:15:37,902 --> 07:15:42,820
B：选择工具输入架构选项，因为这是考试评分所依据的技术。
B the tool input schema option since that is the technique the exam is scored against.

5090
07:15:43,568 --> 07:15:43,808
C。
C.

5091
07:15:44,448 --> 07:15:48,368
C：两者都不选，而是添加验证和重试循环。
Neither and add a validation and retry loop instead.

5092
07:15:48,688 --> 07:15:49,008
D。
D.

5093
07:15:49,262 --> 07:15:53,328
D：选择题干场景中已经确认为在使用的那个。
Whichever the STEM scenario has already established as in use.

5094
07:15:54,254 --> 07:15:55,568
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

5095
07:16:00,942 --> 07:16:05,860
答案是 B，而且值得承认的是，这感觉不太对。
The answer is B, and it is worth acknowledging that this feels wrong.

5096
07:16:07,968 --> 07:16:08,608
选项。
Option.

5097
07:16:10,862 --> 07:16:12,848
A 描述的是更好的工程实践。
A describes the better engineering.

5098
07:16:12,974 --> 07:16:16,420
如果你明天要构建这个系统，你会选择用 A。
And if you were building this system tomorrow, it is what you would use.

5099
07:16:17,870 --> 07:16:21,380
但在考场上，你的得分是基于已发布的蓝图。
In the exam room, you are scored against a published blueprint.

5100
07:16:21,902 --> 07:16:27,780
描述那些在蓝图发布之后才出现的特性的选项，并不是这门考试要考核的内容。
An option describing a capability that post-dates that blueprint is not what the paper is testing.

5101
07:16:28,174 --> 07:16:34,020
在实践中，这种精确的组合不太可能出现，因为考试不包含较新的选项。
In practice, this exact pairing is unlikely to appear precisely because the exam does not contain the newer option.

5102
07:16:34,766 --> 07:16:43,140
更有可能出现的是：你明明知道一个更好的现代答案，但它不在四个选项中。识别出这种感觉，然后选择指南给出的答案。
What is likely is a stem where you know a better modern answer and it is not among the four. Recognize that feeling and pick the guide's answer.

5103
07:16:44,848 --> 07:16:46,020
场景 2。
Scenario 2.

5104
07:16:46,638 --> 07:16:51,300
一位准备同一场考试的同事阅读了当前的 Claude Code 文档。
A colleague preparing for the same exam reads the current Claude code documentation.

5105
07:16:51,568 --> 07:16:57,604
他们发现斜杆命令和技能是一个系统，而且委派工具被称为智能体。
They find that slash commands and skills are one system and that the delegation tool is called agent.

5106
07:16:58,350 --> 07:17:05,444
他们现在不确定关于子智能体和斜杆命令的课程内容是否错误，而他们下周就要参加考试了。
They are now unsure whether the course material on subagents and slash commands is wrong and they sit the exam next week.

5107
07:17:06,766 --> 07:17:08,004
你应该告诉他们什么？
What should you tell them?

5108
07:17:08,718 --> 07:17:13,188
A. 遵循当前文档中的 trusty 内容，因为它具有权威性。
a resty from the current documentation since it is authoritative.

5109
07:17:14,094 --> 07:17:23,328
B. 原理是一样的，只是名称和包装变了。所以按要求回答任务，并将命令和技能视为指南所要求的。
B. The mechanisms are the same and only the names and packaging changed. So answer task and treat commands and skins as the guide does.

5110
07:17:23,648 --> 07:17:27,268
C. 在考试之后完全忽略这些文档。
C. Ignore the documentation entirely until after the exam.

5111
07:17:27,886 --> 07:17:31,716
D. 联系 Anthropic 确认考试使用的是哪个版本。
D. Contact Anthropic to confirm which version the exam uses.

5112
07:17:33,568 --> 07:17:34,884
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

5113
07:17:40,654 --> 07:17:41,968
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

5114
07:17:42,368 --> 07:17:46,084
让他们感到不安的两件事只是标签，而不是行为逻辑。
Both of the things that alarm them are labels rather than behavior.

5115
07:17:46,448 --> 07:17:49,220
任务仍然可以作为智能体的别名使用。
Task still works as an alias for agent.

5116
07:17:49,648 --> 07:17:52,772
一个技能仍然会产生相同的斜杆命令。
A skin still produces the same slash command.

5117
07:17:53,088 --> 07:17:56,516
命令文件确实是这样，只是在名称冲突时以技能为准。
A command file did, with skills winning a name clash.

5118
07:17:57,454 --> 07:18:02,448
他们学到的关于委派或调用工作流的内容都没有错。
Nothing they learned about delegation or about invoking a workflow is wrong.

5119
07:18:03,374 --> 07:18:06,340
选项 A 是代价高昂的过度纠正。
Option A is the expensive overcorrection.

5120
07:18:06,574 --> 07:18:10,116
在最后一周去重新学习那些并没有改变的内容。
Spending their last week restudying material that did not change.

5121
07:18:10,958 --> 07:18:21,968
选项 C 是另一种方向的过度纠正，而且阅读文档正是他们发现这些问题的途径，这是一个很好的习惯。总的教训是：恐慌带来的代价比版本差异更大。
Option C overcorrects the other way, and reading the documentation is exactly how they found this, which is a good habit. The general lesson is that panic costs more than the divergence.

5122
07:18:23,310 --> 07:18:24,292
场景 3。
Scenario 3.

5123
07:18:24,782 --> 07:18:29,796
一名工程师通过了考试，并被要求在下个月构建一个生产环境的提取流水线。
An engineer passes the exam and is asked to build a production extraction pipeline the following month.

5124
07:18:30,606 --> 07:18:40,484
他们采用了工具输入架构技术、手动上下文摘要，以及用于格式控制的预填回复，因为这些是他们复习过的技术。
They implement the tool input schema technique, manual context summarization, and a pre-filled response for format control because those are the techniques they revised.

5125
07:18:41,390 --> 07:18:43,488
哪一个选择实际上是个问题？
Which choice is actually a problem?

5126
07:18:43,822 --> 07:18:51,968
a 工具输入架构技术，b 手动上下文摘要，c 预填回复，d 全部都是。
a The Tool input schema technique, b manual context summarization, C the prefilled response, D.

5127
07:18:52,334 --> 07:18:54,848
这三项都应该被当前的功能所取代。
All three should be replaced with current features.

5128
07:18:55,150 --> 07:18:56,484
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

5129
07:19:02,062 --> 07:19:09,444
答案是 C，而且它测试的区别也是你要带着离开这个模块的重点。被取代并不等同于被撤回。
The answer is C, and the distinction it tests is the one to leave this module with. Supersed is not the same as withdrawn.

5130
07:19:09,840 --> 07:19:15,236
工具输入架构技术和手动摘要这两项，都已经被更方便的功能所取代了。
The two schema technique and manual summarization have both been superseded by more convenient features.

5131
07:19:16,142 --> 07:19:20,640
两者目前都可用，用它们来构建是合理的，而不是错误的做法。
Both still work, and building with them is reasonable rather than a mistake.

5132
07:19:21,134 --> 07:19:26,340
预填充功能已被撤回，因此在最新模型上无法运行，相关代码也会报错。
Prefill has been withdrawn, so it does not work on the latest models, and that code will fail.

5133
07:19:27,822 --> 07:19:31,780
选项 B 就是本模块旨在防止的过度纠正。
Option B is the overcorrection that this module exists to prevent.

5134
07:19:32,430 --> 07:19:36,804
仅仅因为有新功能就重写原本就能运行的代码并不算是一种改进。
Rewriting working code because a newer feature exists is not an improvement.

5135
07:19:37,486 --> 07:19:39,460
这部分教学模块就到此结束。
That closes the teaching modules.

5136
07:19:40,110 --> 07:19:41,860
接下来是模拟考试。
The practice exams are next.

5137
07:19:43,440 --> 07:19:45,316
4 场模拟考试中的第 1 场。
Practice exam 1 of 4.

5138
07:19:45,614 --> 07:19:52,900
包含涵盖所有五个领域的 20 道题，权重与正式试卷一致。每道题有 9 秒时间。
20 questions mixed across all five domains and weighted the way the real paper is. Each question holds for 9 seconds.

5139
07:19:53,200 --> 07:19:59,908
这远低于考试中给出的 2 分钟。所以把这个停顿当作提交答案的提示，而不是用来犹豫思考的时间。
That is well under the 2 minutes you get in the exam. So treat the pause as a prompt to commit rather than time to deliberate.

5140
07:20:00,480 --> 07:20:07,360
如果你想进行严格计时练习，可以在第一题时暂停，并在计时的情况下在纸上写下你的答案。
If you want a properly timed run, pause at the first question and write your answers on paper against a clock.

5141
07:20:07,758 --> 07:20:09,600
然后再回来听解析。
Then come back for the walkthroughs.

5142
07:20:09,902 --> 07:20:13,060
无论哪种方式，在每一页答案出现前都要确定一个字母选项。
Either way, commit to a letter before every answer slide.

5143
07:20:14,510 --> 07:20:16,160
开始前有 4 条规则。
4 rules before you start.

5144
07:20:16,430 --> 07:20:18,800
在检查任何题目之前先回答全部 20 道题。
Answer all 20 before checking any.

5145
07:20:18,960 --> 07:20:22,788
因为边做边查会虚高你的分数，而且几乎学不到任何东西。
Because checking as you go inflates your score and teaches almost nothing.

5146
07:20:23,246 --> 07:20:29,604
把每个字母写下来，因为记在脑子里的答案往往会在解析结束前就变成你认为正确的那个。
Write each letter down since a remembered answer has a habit of becoming the right one by the time a walkthrough finishes.

5147
07:20:30,542 --> 07:20:35,396
记录每道错题属于哪个领域，因为最后的评分幻灯片会要求提供这个信息。
Note which domain each miss came from because the scoring slide at the end asks for that.

5148
07:20:35,918 --> 07:20:40,132
而且不要去查任何资料，因为有提示才拿到的分数不能作为衡量标准。
And do not look anything up because a score you helped is not a measurement.

5149
07:20:41,294 --> 07:20:48,740
20 道题只是一个快照而非最终判决，而在四套试卷中出现的规律才是真正能告诉你些东西的东西。
20 questions is a snapshot rather than a verdict, and the pattern across four papers is what actually tells you something.

5150
07:20:50,510 --> 07:20:51,236
第 1 题。
Question 1.

5151
07:20:52,142 --> 07:20:55,364
一家物流公司运行一个货物状态查询服务。
A logistics company runs a shipment status service.

5152
07:20:56,494 --> 07:21:00,196
每次请求都按相同的顺序执行同样的三个操作。
Every request performs the same three operations in the same order.

5153
07:21:01,006 --> 07:21:06,500
验证追踪号码、获取承运商记录，并生成面向客户的摘要。
Validate the tracking number, fetch the carrier record, and format a customer facing summary.

5154
07:21:07,630 --> 07:21:11,108
每一步都是独立的，且顺序从不改变。
Each step is independent and the order never varies.

5155
07:21:12,014 --> 07:21:17,476
当前的实现是将这三个任务交给一个智能体，让它决定如何处理。
The current implementation gives a single agent all three tasks and lets it decide how to proceed.

5156
07:21:17,998 --> 07:21:23,108
输出结果不稳定，而且每 12 次响应中大约有一次会完全漏掉承运商详情。
Output is inconsistent and about one response in 12 omits the carrier detail entirely.

5157
07:21:23,854 --> 07:21:25,924
最有效的设计更改是什么？
What is the most effective design change?

5158
07:21:26,574 --> 07:21:31,588
a. 在系统提示词中强调每次都要执行全部三个步骤。
a add emphasis to the system prompt requiring all three steps every time.

5159
07:21:32,320 --> 07:21:32,640
b。
b.

5160
07:21:33,040 --> 07:21:38,372
重构为提示词链，包含三个串行调用，每个调用处理一个步骤。
Restructure as prompt chaining with three sequential calls each handling one step.

5161
07:21:39,200 --> 07:21:39,520
C。
C.

5162
07:21:39,920 --> 07:21:44,240
给智能体提供三个工具，每步一个，并让它调用这些工具。
Give the agent three tools, one per step, and let it call them.

5163
07:21:45,006 --> 07:21:49,764
D。增加最大轮数，让智能体有足够的空间完成所有三个步骤。
D. Increase max turns so the agent has room to complete all three steps.

5164
07:22:00,334 --> 07:22:01,412
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

5165
07:22:01,902 --> 07:22:07,840
相同的三个操作、相同的顺序、彼此独立，这是对工作流的定义。
Same three operations, same order, independent of each other, is a specification for a workflow.

5166
07:22:08,000 --> 07:22:16,548
你可以在请求到达前就画好流程图，这样决策者就没有需要决策的内容了。增加一个选项只会引入变数，没有任何其他作用。
You could draw the flowchart before the request arrives, so there is nothing for a decision maker to decide. Adding one introduces variance and nothing else.

5167
07:22:17,520 --> 07:22:24,548
选项 C 是最强的干扰项，因为三个专注的工具确实比一个综合的检查清单更强。
Option C is the strongest distractor because three focus tools genuinely beat one combined checklist.

5168
07:22:25,934 --> 07:22:29,412
智能体仍然掌握路径，所以它仍可能跳过某一步。
The agent still owns the path, so it can still skip a step.

5169
07:22:30,958 --> 07:22:31,748
问题 2。
Question 2.

5170
07:22:32,160 --> 07:22:38,404
受监管的机构必须确保公司任何地方的恶意代码会话都不能执行 curl 命令。
A regulated organization must ensure no plot code session anywhere in the company can execute curl.

5171
07:22:39,566 --> 07:22:43,556
工程团队控制他们自己的仓库和他们自己的设置文件。
Engineering teams control their own repositories and their own settings files.

5172
07:22:44,462 --> 07:22:52,676
平台工程师在每个项目的设置文件中添加针对 bash curl 的拒绝规则，并通过代码审查来强制执行。
A platform engineer adds a deny rule for bash curl to every project settings file and enforces it through code review.

5173
07:22:53,102 --> 07:22:54,980
这种方法有什么弱点？
What is the weakness in this approach?

5174
07:22:55,950 --> 07:23:00,580
a 拒绝规则无法匹配命令参数，只能匹配工具名称。
a Deny rules cannot match command arguments, only the tool names.

5175
07:23:01,358 --> 07:23:06,692
b 项目设置可能会被本地设置覆盖，且某些仓库可能会被遗漏。
b a project setting can be overridden by a local setting and a repository can be missed.

5176
07:23:07,040 --> 07:23:10,148
C。代码审查无法检测到设置文件的更改。
C. Code review cannot detect settings file changes.

5177
07:23:10,640 --> 07:23:15,396
D。没有弱点，因为项目范围是团队范围内规则的正确层级。
D There is no weakness since project scope is the correct layer for a team wide rule.

5178
07:23:25,806 --> 07:23:29,600
答案是 B，它指出了两个不同的漏洞。
The answer is B and it identifies two separate holes.

5179
07:23:30,000 --> 07:23:33,604
在优先级链中，项目本地设置高于项目设置。
Project local settings sit above project settings in the precedence chain.

5180
07:23:33,920 --> 07:23:37,348
所以任何工程师都可以在他们自己的机器上添加允许规则。
So any engineer can add an allow rule on their own machine.

5181
07:23:37,966 --> 07:23:43,492
而且依赖于每个仓库都有该规则，意味着每个仓库都是可能遗漏的地方。
And relying on every repository having the rule means every repository is a place to forget.

5182
07:23:44,400 --> 07:23:52,100
全公司范围的保证属于企业管理层，这是唯一的层级。任何下层都不允许放宽限制。
A company-wide guarantee belongs in the enterprise managed layer, which is the only one. Nothing below can relax.

5183
07:23:53,550 --> 07:23:54,240
问题 3。
Question 3.

5184
07:23:54,542 --> 07:24:03,044
一个提示词要求 Claude 从申报文件中提取所有监管引用，并对每一个引用评估该申报是否符合相关规定。
A single prompt asks Claude to extract every regulatory citation from a filing and for each one assess whether the filing complies with it.

5185
07:24:04,174 --> 07:24:07,620
当请求进行合规性评估时，会有一些引用丢失。
When compliance assessments are requested, several citations go missing.

5186
07:24:07,920 --> 07:24:10,916
当省略评估时，引用召回率很高。
When assessments are omitted, citation recall is high.

5187
07:24:11,886 --> 07:24:16,900
评估本身逻辑严密，且两种输出都是必需的。
The assessments themselves are consistently well reasoned and both outputs are required.

5188
07:24:17,550 --> 07:24:19,492
最有效的做法是什么？
What is the most effective approach?

5189
07:24:20,240 --> 07:24:25,796
a 指示模型无论评估工作量如何，都不得遗漏任何引用。
a instruct the model that no citation may be missed regardless of assessment effort.

5190
07:24:27,086 --> 07:24:31,844
b 分成两次调用：先提取引用，然后再对提取出的列表进行评估。
b Two calls, extracting citations, then assessing the extracted list.

5191
07:24:32,686 --> 07:24:32,960
C.
C.

5192
07:24:33,520 --> 07:24:38,532
先要求提供引用，然后在同一个回复中进行评估。
Ask for citations first, then assessments within the same response.

5193
07:24:38,880 --> 07:24:39,120
D.
D.

5194
07:24:39,520 --> 07:24:43,300
增加最大标记数，这样就有足够的空间容纳两个输出结果了。
Increase max tokens. So there is room for both outputs.

5195
07:24:53,902 --> 07:24:54,916
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

5196
07:24:55,406 --> 07:25:03,044
当请求评估时召回率下降，而没要求时又恢复，这是两个任务在争夺同一个注意力预算的典型特征。
Recall drops when assessment is requested and recovers when it is not, which is the signature of two jobs competing for one attention budget.

5197
07:25:04,846 --> 07:25:10,212
选项 C 有点帮助，因为它把召回放在前面，但两个任务仍然存在于同一个回复中。
Option C helps a little by front loading recall and both jobs still live in one response.

5198
07:25:11,118 --> 07:25:18,532
排除选项 D，因为没有任何内容被截断，而且题干显示评估过程逻辑严密且一致。
Option D is ruled out because nothing was truncated and the STEM tells you the assessments were consistently well reasoned.

5199
07:25:20,046 --> 07:25:20,900
问题 4。
Question 4.

5200
07:25:21,422 --> 07:25:25,412
一个智能体已经运行了一个持续 90 分钟的客服会话。
An agent has been running a support session for 90 minutes.

5201
07:25:26,286 --> 07:25:32,996
在开始时，用户声明由于法律原因，他们的机构无法接受第三方 Cookie。
At the start, the user stated that their organization cannot accept third-party cookies for legal reasons.

5202
07:25:33,550 --> 07:25:37,572
现在该智能体推荐了一个需要第三方 Cookie 的解决方案。
The agent now recommends a solution requiring third-party cookies.

5203
07:25:38,414 --> 07:25:44,196
约束条件仍存在于对话历史中。没有任何内容被截断，也没有报错。
The constraint is still present in the conversation history. Nothing was truncated and no error was raised.

5204
07:25:44,480 --> 07:25:46,468
最可能的解释是什么？
What is the most likely explanation?

5205
07:25:47,054 --> 07:25:57,700
a. 上下文窗口溢出了，并静默丢弃了早期的轮次。b. 随着窗口填满，注意力会下降，导致早期信息获得的权重降低。
a. The context window overflowed and silently dropped early turns. b. Attention degrades as the window fills, so early information receives less weight.

5206
07:25:58,414 --> 07:26:03,620
C. 该约束是由用户陈述的而非在系统提示词中，因此它不具有约束力。
C. The constraint was stated by the user rather than in the system prompt, so it is not binding.

5207
07:26:04,160 --> 07:26:07,460
D. 触发了压缩功能，并从摘要中删除了该约束。
D. Compaction fired and remove the constraint from the summary.

5208
07:26:18,094 --> 07:26:19,600
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

5209
07:26:20,142 --> 07:26:24,388
题干中的三个细节排除了所有机械性的解释。
Three details in the stem rule out every mechanical explanation.

5210
07:26:24,910 --> 07:26:29,124
约束条件仍然存在，没有内容被截断，也没有报错。
The constraint is still present, nothing was truncated, and no error was raised.

5211
07:26:29,774 --> 07:26:36,580
剩下的只有退化问题，即在窗口内但由于窗口失效而导致信息权重按比例降低的情况。
What remains is degradation, where information technically in the window receives proportionally less weight as the window fails.

5212
07:26:37,518 --> 07:26:42,308
注意选项 D 直接与题干相矛盾，这一点值得留意。
Note that option D contradicts the stem directly, which is worth catching.

5213
07:26:44,014 --> 07:26:44,932
问题 5。
Question 5.

5214
07:26:45,646 --> 07:26:51,428
一个协调者派生了五个子智能体来研究竞争对手分析的不同方面。
A coordinator spawns five subagents to research different aspects of a competitor analysis.

5215
07:26:52,334 --> 07:26:54,468
每个智能体都收到了一行指令。
Each is briefed with one line.

5216
07:26:54,800 --> 07:26:57,604
研究此领域并报告你的发现。
Research this area and report your findings.

5217
07:26:58,318 --> 07:26:59,684
出现了两个问题。
Two problems recur.

5218
07:27:00,560 --> 07:27:10,180
三个子智能体独立研究了相同的定价历史，而客户明确提到的一个市场在任何子智能体的输出中都没有出现。
Three subagents independently research the same pricing history and a market the client specifically named appears in no subagent's output.

5219
07:27:10,990 --> 07:27:12,676
最有效的修复方法是什么？
What is the most effective fix?

5220
07:27:13,134 --> 07:27:16,292
a 添加第六个子智能体来覆盖缺失的市场。
a add a sixth subagent covering the missing market.

5221
07:27:16,910 --> 07:27:17,200
b.
b.

5222
07:27:17,710 --> 07:27:24,516
给每个子代理设定明确的目标、明确的超出范围界限，并要求特定的输出格式。
Give each subagent a narrow objective, explicit out of scope boundaries, and a required output format.

5223
07:27:24,974 --> 07:27:25,280
C.
C.

5224
07:27:25,646 --> 07:27:29,476
让协调者在综合过程中对重叠部分进行去重。
Have the coordinator deduplicate overlapping sections during synthesis.

5225
07:27:30,030 --> 07:27:35,588
d. 让子代理串行运行，以便每个子代理都能看到前一个涵盖的内容。
d. Run the sub agents sequentially so each can see what the previous one covered.

5226
07:27:45,870 --> 07:27:50,820
答案是 B。关键在于发现这两个症状只有一个共同原因。
The answer is B. The move is spotting that both symptoms have one cause.

5227
07:27:51,072 --> 07:27:59,492
没人被明确告知哪些内容属于自己负责，所以明确的目标能解决重叠问题，而明确的超出范围界限能填补空白。
Nobody was told precisely what was theirs and what was not, so narrow objectives fix the overlap and explicit out-of-scope boundaries fix the gap.

5228
07:28:00,270 --> 07:28:11,204
选项 D 是一个具有启发性的错误答案，因为串行执行看起来似乎会有帮助，但无论顺序如何，子代理都无法看到彼此的工作内容。
Option D is the instructive wrong answer because sequential execution feels like it would help, and sub-agents cannot see each other's work regardless of ordering.

5229
07:28:12,430 --> 07:28:13,476
问题 6。
Question 6.

5230
07:28:14,192 --> 07:28:18,432
一个支持智能体有一个被描述为「检查权限」的工具。
A support agent has a tool described as checks entitlement.

5231
07:28:19,712 --> 07:28:23,684
它的输入架构包含一个客户 ID 和一个产品代码。
Its input schema takes a customer ID and a product code.

5232
07:28:24,272 --> 07:28:26,724
在生产环境中，该智能体从未调用这个工具。
In production, the agent never calls it.

5233
07:28:27,632 --> 07:28:34,192
它根据对话内容和通用知识工具来回答权限问题，且回复通常很长。
It answers entitlement questions from the conversation and from a general knowledge tool and is frequently long.

5234
07:28:35,150 --> 07:28:38,032
手动调用时，该工具运行正常。
The tool works correctly when called manually.

5235
07:28:38,382 --> 07:28:39,940
最可能的原因是什么？
What is the most likely cause?

5236
07:28:40,462 --> 07:28:44,228
a 该工具不在智能体允许的工具列表中。
a The tool is missing from the agent's allowed tools list.

5237
07:28:44,672 --> 07:28:44,992
b.
b.

5238
07:28:45,582 --> 07:28:50,340
描述并没有描述一个场景。智能体识别出了它所处的场景。
The description does not describe a situation. The agent recognizes it is in.

5239
07:28:50,912 --> 07:28:51,152
C.
C.

5240
07:28:51,552 --> 07:28:56,004
输入架构要求两个参数，而智能体无法提供这些参数。
The input schema requires two parameters which the agent cannot supply.

5241
07:28:56,832 --> 07:28:57,152
d.
d.

5242
07:28:57,710 --> 07:29:00,996
通用知识工具在工具列表中的排名更高。
The general knowledge tool is ranked higher in the tool list.

5243
07:29:11,406 --> 07:29:12,512
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

5244
07:29:12,942 --> 07:29:21,632
「检查权限」是一个真实陈述但没用的描述。它没有说明何时使用该工具、返回什么内容，或者回答什么问题。
Checks entitlement is a true statement and a useless description. It says nothing about when to use the tool, what it returns, or what question it answers.

5245
07:29:21,792 --> 07:29:26,852
因此，智能体无法识别出权限问题是这个工具可以处理的情况。
So the agent cannot recognize that an entitlement question is a situation this tool addresses.

5246
07:29:27,566 --> 07:29:35,780
选项 D 虚构了一个排名机制，而描述那些并不存在的机制的选项本身就是一类干扰项。
Option D invents a ranking mechanism and options that describe machinery which does not exist are a distractor family in their own right.

5247
07:29:37,230 --> 07:29:38,112
问题 7。
Question 7.

5248
07:29:38,510 --> 07:29:43,392
一个媒体监控服务每月对 30 万篇文章进行情感分类。
A media monitoring service classifies 300,000 articles a month for sentiment.

5249
07:29:44,238 --> 07:29:46,212
有两个用户在使用这些输出。
Two consumers use the output.

5250
07:29:47,022 --> 07:29:51,908
一个是需要在一分钟内获得结果的实时警报仪表板，另一个是月度趋势报告。
A live alerting dashboard needing results within a minute and a monthly trend report.

5251
07:29:52,686 --> 07:29:58,180
大约 6% 的文章符合警报关键词，其余的仅用于月度报告。
About 6% of articles match alerting keywords and the rest feed only the monthly report.

5252
07:29:58,512 --> 07:30:03,652
目前所有 300,000 条数据都通过同步请求处理，成本是核心问题。
All 300,000 currently go through synchronous requests and cost is the concern.

5253
07:30:04,206 --> 07:30:06,308
哪种变动最具成本效益？
What is the most cost-effective change?

5254
07:30:06,672 --> 07:30:09,188
a. 将所有文章转为批处理。
a move all articles to the batch.

5255
07:30:11,312 --> 07:30:11,632
b.
b.

5256
07:30:12,046 --> 07:30:17,392
c. 保留 6% 的同步请求，并将剩余 94% 的内容通过批处理接口传输。
Keep the 6% synchronous and route the remaining 94%% through the batch API.

5257
07:30:17,806 --> 07:30:18,112
c.
C.

5258
07:30:18,414 --> 07:30:21,124
d. 并行处理所有文章以缩短运行时间。
Process all articles in parallel to reduce runtime.

5259
07:30:21,632 --> 07:30:21,952
d.
D.

5260
07:30:22,190 --> 07:30:24,644
e. 对所有分类使用更小的模型。
Use a smaller model for all classifications.

5261
07:30:35,150 --> 07:30:36,832
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

5262
07:30:37,232 --> 07:30:42,020
关键词规则已经对流量进行了分类，因此路由决策不产生额外成本。
The keyword rule already sorts the traffic, so the routing decision costs nothing.

5263
07:30:42,478 --> 07:30:47,460
94% 的工作量成本减半，而警报部分保持不变。
94% of the workload moves to half price and the alerting part is untouched.

5264
07:30:47,952 --> 07:30:57,700
选项 A 违反了要求的延迟要求，而选项 C 是关于并行处理和批处理各自优势的常见混淆点。
Option A violates the stated latency requirement, and option C is the recurring confusion between what parallelism buys and what batch buys.

5265
07:30:59,152 --> 07:31:00,324
问题 8。
Question 8.

5266
07:31:00,832 --> 07:31:04,032
一个夜间智能体负责对账供应商发票。
An overnight agent reconciles supplier invoices.

5267
07:31:04,272 --> 07:31:12,644
它在设有轮数限制和预算限制的情况下被调用，且编排包装程序在调用返回且未抛出异常时标记运行完成。
It is invoked with a turn cap and a budget cap, and the orchestration wrapper marks a run complete whenever the invocation returns without throwing.

5268
07:31:13,646 --> 07:31:19,588
一名审计员发现，有部分标记为“已完成”的对账单中，有四分之一的票据从未被检查过。
An auditor finds reconciliations marked complete where a quarter of the invoices were never examined.

5269
07:31:19,872 --> 07:31:21,284
根本原因是什么？
What is the root cause?

5270
07:31:21,774 --> 07:31:25,392
a. 发票数量相对于设定的轮数限制过高。
a The turn cap is set too low for the invoice volume.

5271
07:31:25,712 --> 07:31:25,952
b.
b.

5272
07:31:26,446 --> 07:31:31,552
包装程序将任何非异常返回都视为成功，包括因达到限制而中止的运行。
The wrapper treats any non exception return as success, including runs aborted by a cap.

5273
07:31:32,512 --> 07:31:32,752
c.
c.

5274
07:31:33,312 --> 07:31:35,844
d. 智能体在未完成时应进行报告。
The agent should report when it has not finished.

5275
07:31:36,366 --> 07:31:40,036
e. 工作应拆分到多个较小的调用中。
D. The work should be split across several smaller invocations.

5276
07:31:50,702 --> 07:31:51,716
答案是
The answer is

5277
07:31:52,416 --> 07:31:52,736
B。
B.

5278
07:31:53,056 --> 07:31:59,940
触发护栏是第三种结果，但由于该包装程序仅区分“通过”和“未抛出异常”，因此无法识别它。
Hitting a guardrail is a third outcome that this wrapper does not know about because it only distinguishes through and did not throw.

5279
07:32:01,294 --> 07:32:04,324
被限制的运行会正常返回并被标记为完成。
A capped run returns normally and gets marked complete.

5280
07:32:05,262 --> 07:32:05,776
选项
Option

5281
07:32:07,502 --> 07:32:15,460
A 是在真正起作用的，它不是根本原因，因为提高上限只会让静默失败在更高的容量下再次出现。
A is genuinely contributing and it is not the root cause because raising the cap only moves the volume at which the silent failure reappears.

5282
07:32:17,134 --> 07:32:17,856
第 9 题。
Question 9.

5283
07:32:18,190 --> 07:32:26,576
一个团队要求：在凌晨 1 点到 4 点的夜间数据加载期间，Claude Code 绝不能对预发布环境执行部署命令。该加载任务从凌晨 1 点运行到 4 点。
A team requires that clot code never runs a deployment command against staging during the nightly data load. That load runs from 1 in the morning to 4.

5284
07:32:26,736 --> 07:32:32,676
在那个时间段之外，预发布部署是常规且频繁的操作。部署命令是通过 bash 发出的。
Outside that window, staging deployments are routine and frequent. Deployment commands are issued through bash.

5285
07:32:33,326 --> 07:32:34,564
什么能强制执行这一规定？
What enforces this?

5286
07:32:34,926 --> 07:32:38,660
a. 对 bash 部署命令设置权限拒绝规则。
a A permissions deny rule on bash deployment commands.

5287
07:32:39,406 --> 07:32:45,136
b. 在 bash 上设置一个工具使用前钩子，检查当前时间并在该窗口内进行拦截。
b a pre-tool use hook on bash that checks the current time and blocks within the window.

5288
07:32:45,456 --> 07:32:50,372
c. 一个 claude.md 规则，说明夜间加载的时间段。
C. A clot.m d rule stating the nightly load window.

5289
07:32:50,736 --> 07:32:51,056
d.
D.

5290
07:32:51,566 --> 07:32:56,068
d. 一个工具使用后钩子，在窗口期间运行部署时发出警报。
A post tool use hook that alerts when a deployment runs during the window.

5291
07:33:06,574 --> 07:33:07,620
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

5292
07:33:08,430 --> 07:33:14,180
这里的两个选项都是真正的强制执行，所以仅靠“不采用强制执行”的逻辑是不够的。
Two options here are genuine enforcement, so persuade against enforce is not enough on its own.

5293
07:33:15,118 --> 07:33:22,436
选项 A 是绝对可靠且永久的，但它会拦截团队在每天 20 小时中依赖的常规部署。
Option A is absolutely reliable and permanent, which blocks the routine deployments the team depends on for 20 hours a day.

5294
07:33:23,054 --> 07:33:28,100
规则是基于时间的，而权限是扁平化的；相比之下，钩子可以进行逻辑判断。
The rule is conditional on time and permissions are flat while hooks can evaluate.

5295
07:33:29,326 --> 07:33:31,492
选项 D 是在造成损害后才做出反应。
Option D reacts after the damage.

5296
07:33:32,896 --> 07:33:33,936
第 10 题。
Question 10.

5297
07:33:34,222 --> 07:33:46,660
一个 MCP 服务器提供了一个货币转换工具。当传入不支持的货币代码时，服务器会抛出异常，并由 SDK 转换为 JSON RPC 错误。
An MCP server exposes a currency conversion tool. When an unsupported currency code is passed, the server raises an exception that the SDK converts into a JSON RPC error.

5298
07:33:47,374 --> 07:33:55,588
追踪显示智能体调用该工具并带入相同的无效代码多达四次，然后才告诉用户无法进行转换。
Traces show the agent calling the tool with the same unsupported code up to four times, then telling the user conversion is unavailable.

5299
07:33:55,918 --> 07:33:57,028
应该做出什么更改？
What should change?

5300
07:33:57,518 --> 07:34:05,216
a. 将不支持的货币作为工具执行结果报告，包含错误信息和列出支持代码的消息。
a report the unsupported currency as a tool execution result with is error and a message naming the supported codes.

5301
07:34:05,678 --> 07:34:05,936
b.
b.

5302
07:34:06,414 --> 07:34:09,376
b. 减少重试次数，让智能体更快放弃。
Reduce the retry count so the agent gives up sooner.

5303
07:34:09,616 --> 07:34:09,856
c.
C.

5304
07:34:10,222 --> 07:34:13,764
c. 当代码不支持时，让工具默认转换为美元。
Have the tool default to US dollars when the code is unsupported.

5305
07:34:14,256 --> 07:34:17,636
d. 将支持的货币列表添加到系统提示词中。
D. Add the supported currency list to the system prompt.

5306
07:34:28,174 --> 07:34:29,376
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

5307
07:34:29,838 --> 07:34:37,540
完全相同的重复意味着智能体在尝试之间没有收到任何信息，而它之所以没收到信息是因为协议错误永远无法传达到模型。
Identical repeats mean the agent received no information between attempts and it received none because a protocol error never reaches the model.

5308
07:34:38,382 --> 07:34:44,964
将同样的失败报告为包含错误和支持代码列表的消息，这样它就能在下一次调用时纠正。
Report the same failure as is error with a message naming the supported codes and it corrects on the next call.

5309
07:34:45,454 --> 07:34:53,252
选项 C 是危险的，因为默认转换为美元会产生一个自信但错误的数字，而不是报错。
Option C is the dangerous one because defaulting to dollars produces a confidently wrong number instead of an error.

5310
07:34:54,766 --> 07:34:55,652
第 11 题。
Question 11.

5311
07:34:55,982 --> 07:35:00,164
一个迁移智能体在两周内跨越三个会话运行。
A migration agent works across three sessions over two weeks.

5312
07:35:00,686 --> 07:35:04,004
第9步需要在会话中做出架构决策
Step 9 needs a schema decision made in session

5313
07:35:04,846 --> 07:35:15,108
1，并在会话2中发现受影响的服务列表。在每个会话中，压缩都会触发多次，且所有内容目前都保存在对话中。
1 and a list of affected services discovered in session 2. Compaction fires several times within each session and everything currently lives in the conversation.

5314
07:35:16,046 --> 07:35:17,296
他们应该采用什么方案？
What should they implement?

5315
07:35:17,616 --> 07:35:21,476
a 提高压缩阈值，让早期轮次保留更久。
a raise the compaction threshold so early turns survive longer.

5316
07:35:22,094 --> 07:35:27,940
b 每完成一个步骤就将决策和结果写入状态文件，并在稍后从中读取。
b Write decisions and findings to a state file as each step completes and read from it later.

5317
07:35:28,366 --> 07:35:32,363
c. 在每个提示词开始时重复之前的会话决策。
C. Repeat the session one decision at the start of every prompt.

5318
07:35:33,006 --> 07:35:33,330
选b。
b.

5319
07:35:34,158 --> 07:35:38,372
将每一步作为子代理运行，以保持上下文隔离。
Run each step as a sub agent so context stays isolated.

